ntent.7.5776":"Telenox","content.7.5777":"Karn","content.7.5780":"Thalos-Kyarrelmne","content.7.5781":"Karn","content.7.5782":"Rock","content.7.5783":"Eliatrope Energy Battery","content.7.5784":"Noxine","content.7.5785":"Hand","content.7.5786":"Cube","content.7.5787":"Arlemia","content.7.5788":"Nox","content.7.5789":"Miner Azure Dragon","content.7.5790":"Mage Dragon","content.7.5791":"Neo Royal Gobball","content.7.5792":"Neo Royal Piwi","content.7.5793":"Neo Royal Moogrr","content.7.5794":"Neo Joel the Golem","content.7.5795":"Neo Royal Blibli","content.7.5796":"Neo Vampyro","content.7.5797":"Neo Black Crow","content.7.5798":"Neo Black Crow","content.7.5799":"Neo Kya, Missiz Freezz","content.7.5800":"Neo Soft Oak","content.7.5801":"Neo Soft Oak","content.7.5802":"Neo Soft Oak","content.7.5803":"Neo Wa Wabbit","content.7.5804":"Neo Remington Smisse","content.7.5805":"Neo Pandora","content.7.5806":"Neo Ogrest","content.7.5807":"Nox","content.7.5808":"Black Crow","content.7.5809":"Ermina","content.7.5810":"Lumyss","content.7.5811":"Morgouz","content.7.5812":"Ryou","content.7.5813":"Otomai","content.7.5814":"Ogrest","content.7.5815":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5816":"Neo Jonk","content.7.5817":"Neo Soldier","content.7.5818":"Neo Hunter","content.7.5819":"Neo Lieutenant","content.7.5820":"Neo Monk","content.7.5821":"Vengeful Ghost","content.7.5822":"Vengeful Ghost","content.7.5823":"Vengeful Ghost","content.7.5824":"Vengeful Ghost","content.7.5825":"Black Crow's Mount","content.7.5826":"Nekark","content.7.5827":"Tentacle","content.7.5828":"Fishercat","content.7.5829":"Fishercat","content.7.5830":"Fishercat","content.7.5831":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5832":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5833":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5834":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5835":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5836":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5837":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5838":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5839":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5840":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5841":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5842":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5843":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5844":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5845":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5846":"Sinistro","content.7.5847":"Roc","content.7.5848":"Vengeful Spirit","content.7.5849":"Neo Lieutenant","content.7.5850":"Neo Monk","content.7.5851":"Neo Prowling Spirit","content.7.5853":"Aguabrial","content.7.5854":"Otomai","content.7.5855":"Koutoulou","content.7.5856":"Immature Diepwon","content.7.5857":"Neo Lieutenant","content.7.5858":"Neo Monk","content.7.5874":"Gigantegg","content.7.5875":"Rock","content.7.5876":"Gigantegg","content.7.5877":"Gigantegg","content.7.5878":"Gigantegg","content.7.5879":"Gigantegg","content.7.5880":"Gigantegg","content.7.5881":"Gigantegg","content.7.5888":"Ignemikhal","content.7.5889":"Kralove","content.7.5890":"Celestial Cwab","content.7.5891":"Celestial Gobball","content.7.5892":"Fluffy War Chief","content.7.5894":"Fluffy Gobball","content.7.5895":"Fluffy White Gobbly","content.7.5896":"Fluffy Black Gobbly","content.7.5897":"Fluffy Gobball","content.7.5898":"Fluffy White Gobbly","content.7.5899":"Fluffy Black Gobbly","content.7.5900":"Sacrier","content.7.5901":"Bamboo","content.7.5902":"Xineigyhnu","content.7.5903":"Strange Individual","content.7.5904":"Old Amnesiac","content.7.5905":"Black Ink","content.7.5907":"Old Amnesiac's Ghost","content.7.5912":"Unknown Island Starfish","content.7.5913":"Chaos Quartermaster","content.7.5914":"Chaos Captain","content.7.5916":"Ignemikhal","content.7.5917":"Ignemikhal","content.7.5918":"Ignemikhal","content.75.277":"Aaaah! The Cr... Crow...  Not my caravan...","content.75.278":"Gather round, gather round, Welcome to Kelba market, the adventurers' paradise. The best place to buy or sell...  and, above all, {[1*]?kit yourself out with some of the best equipment:find a weapon to match your achievements}.","content.75.285":"Please excuse my intrusion, but you look a little lost, my dear.  Nowadays, it's ill-advised to walk without knowing where you're going. Some journeys have been known not to have return legs...","content.75.287":"You're in luck, {[1*]?madam:sir}, you'll be able to find everything you need at my market. Be careful, though!","content.75.290":"The Black Crow, {[1*]?my good lady:my good sir}. He's been causing chaos at this market for far too long already. A great many people have got themselves in a flap trying to bring him back down to earth...","content.75.312":"How can I help you?","content.75.313":"Just because, {[1*]?my dear lady:my dear sir}! I'm sure he has something against my beautiful maps. Look at these wonders!","content.75.314":"He just passes through, so to speak... Perched on his infernal bird, a single fly-by is enough to ravage all our caravans. He's the bird-brain, but we're the ones left with egg on our faces...","content.75.315":"Where? The last time I saw him, he was perched on a dead tree in the Lands, not far from here. Methinks he's spying on us...","content.75.831":"I'm very well, thank you. When the kama's doing well, everything just falls into place, right Kirikon? Aw what a smart Drheller you are!","content.75.832":"Shh! Listen... Do you hear it too? I'm sure he's out there somewhere, crouching in the shadows... He's watching us with his fiery red eyes. Hide! It's me he wants. But he's not going to catch me, I'll escape again and start over somewhere new.","content.75.833":"You must be a bit mad to want to attack the great Gobbalrog in his bed! Believe me, if you're unlucky enough to meet him, you need to run as fast as you can in the other direction. Preferably avoiding any bridges suspended over high cliffs with long falls.","content.75.834":"He's a terrible monster. \"You shall not pass!\" Falgand the Gray, the pretentious twit, thought he was being clever. Bam, into the abyss! That'll teach him. Baal and Kirikon ran away, but at least they're alive.","content.75.836":"Crocobu... hoorio? I have a book about part of his life... It'll cost you 5 kamas, though.","content.75.862":"Your passport is not valid! Only Bontarian citizens can step through this threshold into the White City. Go and see Master Hoot in the South for more information!","content.75.863":"Make way for [#name], citizen of Amakna. Your passport seems to be valid. Do you want to use the canoon to get to Amakna?","content.75.864":"Halt! Your passport is not valid! Only Amaknian citizens can step through this gate into the continent. Go and see Master Pigmy down there, he's the one that deals with passport validation.","content.75.865":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Bonta! Your passport seems to be valid. Do you want to use the canoon to get to Bonta?","content.75.867":"Halt! About face! Only Amaknian citizens are allowed beyond this point.","content.75.868":"You cannot go further. Only Bontarian citizens can cross this threshold.","content.75.942":"Buenos dias, traveler! What can I do for you?","content.75.943":"Celebrating something? Ha ha! We need no excuse to party, amigo!","content.75.1142":"Your passport is not valid! Only Brakmarian citizens can step through this gate into the City. Go and see Master Barney in the North for more information!","content.75.1143":"You cannot go any further. Only Brakmarian citizens can cross this threshold.","content.75.1144":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Brakmar! Your passport seems to be valid. Do you want to use the canoon to get to Brakmar?","content.75.1146":"You've got a fighting{[1*]?:} spirit, [#name],, but watch out. Until now those Boowolves were imprisoned beneath the palace, and they somehow managed to escape. They're ferocious creatures, and I'm afraid you won't survive.","content.75.1147":"Are you fond of that intoxicating aroma surrounding the village? I have to tell you - it disgusts me. I don't dare wander around anymore, for fear of getting my clothes soaked in that stench. I don't know what to do...","content.75.1148":"There are indeed quite a few Boowolves in the clearing east of the kingdom. They seem to be disturbed by some powerful magnetic force. At first I thought it was coming from the Tree of Life, but it's something else. It's troublesome... These are complicated times for the kingdom, and my son Armand is determined to investigate the problem... He's at a tough age.","content.75.1149":"May Sadida watch over you, young adventurer. Your face looks familiar. Do I know you...? Oh... You're [#name], are you not? I'm proud to consider you one of us now.","content.75.1287":"Braf!","content.75.1288":"Brow braf!","content.75.1289":"...","content.75.1290":"Mrrr...","content.75.1315":"Your passport is not valid! Only Sufokian citizens can step through this gate into the City. Go and see Master Screech in the North for more information!","content.75.1316":"You cannot go any further. Only Sufokian citizens can cross this threshold.","content.75.1317":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Sufokia! Your passport seems to be valid. Do you want to use the canoon to get to Brakmar?","content.75.1699":"I have no time to waste on you. Come back and see me once you've earned the gods' favor.","content.75.1729":"Hey there, deckhand! Us Hullcatz, we go everywhere in the World of Twelve.\\nSeems like everyone wants us to take them over to that there Mount Zinit!","content.75.1814":"Are you looking for the librarian? Unfortunately, she was called to Externam. She's probably being boiled up in the primeval soup as we speak, with all the repenters... Be careful: You could be next!","content.75.1815":"Tell me what you know, dear adventurer... Although, I'm not so sure I can help you persuade the Nun. She's blocked the way for so long now that I can't even remember why...","content.75.1816":"Loool, don't you think that would be a bit obvious? Come on, how about a serious answer this time? ","content.75.1821":"Another crazy Ghoul? Get outta here!","content.75.1822":"Oh, my sincere apologies, dear adventurer. Normally, we don't see anything but Ghouls in this neighborhood. They're trying to get into the village any way they can to take the villagers to Vampyro.","content.75.1823":"Young Count Wagnar succumbed to Shadofang, as many others before him did too. As you can see, nobody's around to help us... What are we supposed to do?","content.75.1824":"Why, to turn them into Ghouls, of course! That way he can launch Ghoul attacks night and day. They're insatiable. They all come from his castle.","content.75.1829":"Kid, you'd do better to forget the whole candles thing.","content.75.1830":"If you want some advice, lay off the imitation rum - it's messing with your head.","content.75.1831":"I have no idea how you plan on doing that, but if you decide to try, gimme a ring.","content.75.1832":"Ooooh, I see you're smarter than the others. Are you sure you haven't forgotten anything?","content.75.1833":"Wooooowsers! Hahaha! Urmm... I think you're joking, but just in case... No. That's not it.","content.75.1834":"Cum voles mihi factum esum PRONUS.","content.75.1835":"Riiight... And...?","content.75.1836":"Well, yeah, except for the fact that a light wave's intensity is, by definition, proportional to the square of its amplitude. And by squaring the previous expression we get... the wrong answer to the riddle.","content.75.1889":"A smooth, rich voice resounds...","content.75.1897":"Hey, you there! Yes, you! Haven't you noticed something a little bit strange going on today?","content.75.1898":"Al Howin Gobballs are invading the World. We're all doomed!!! There's a witch at the head of an army of orange Gobballs who seems to have caused a ruckus among the vulnerable villagers.","content.75.1899":"You're going to have to defeat this witch if you don't want to face the same fate as those Gobballs. She's holed herself up in a vault and will only let nocturnal creatures enter.","content.75.1901":"Right - let me finish! You need to go through their entrails to extract the pieces. In other words, you're going to need to defeat a dozen or so Gobballs...","content.75.1902":"Psss whsss whsss! Whsss... psss psss whss.","content.75.1903":"All we know about it is that he's ordered his subjects to capture as many Cracklers as possible. Apparently they're being held captive in a place known as the \"Whisper Crisper\".","content.75.1906":"Psssst... Hey, you there! Fancy helping a brother out? Free me, will ya? Come on... I'll make you a wealthy little whisperer. I've got friends in high places, you know?","content.75.1907":"How do I know you're going to open the door if I tell you?","content.75.1908":"OK. The code to get into the room is... the code.","content.75.1930":"I've heard that you can undergo a temporary metamorphosis using her magic cauldron. Why not try it out? It's in Astrub, near the Wabbit Cemetery. Find it and fill it with 4 Pieces of Pumpkwin - that should do the trick!","content.75.1931":"You've come to the right place, my{[1*]?:} young friend{[1*]?:}. Unfortunately, I still haven't received the stuffing to make this one really succulent! But I can still give you a hunk of Dragoturkey and let you stuff it yourself.","content.75.1932":"That doesn't matter, kiddo! Here's a stuffing recipe that even a dummy can get right. You'll have a fantastic feast together in no time. You should be able to get the ingredients you need from monsters. Hurry, though - it'll be too late by tomorrow!","content.75.1933":"Sorry, it's a bad habit! I was saying: Help us!!! They've all gone mad!","content.75.1934":"Ever since our leader, Shhhudoku, got so bigheaded, you can cut the atmosphere with a knife. Anyone who dares stand in the way of his plan goes straight to jail! Thankfully, we managed to hide here.","content.75.1935":"Mother Nature gifted us with long, trunk-like appendages that we can use to deliver our soft sighs and murmurs to hypnotize our victims. See, if I just slip my trunk into your...","content.75.1953":"Here you are: one shiny seal. Use it wisely!","content.75.1957":"Here you are: one shiny seal. Use it wisely!","content.75.1958":"Here you are: one shiny seal. Use it wisely!","content.75.1959":"Here you are: one shiny seal. Use it wisely!","content.75.1969":"Ho ho ho! Finally, a helping hand! Look at the state those darn Reindeer left me in. It's their thing at the moment; taking whatever they find and wrapping it up as a gift. If you could help me, I'll give you so many gifts you won't know what to do with them.","content.75.1970":"Ho ho ho! You need to fight the monsters scattered around here. I'm hoping that you'll eventually come across my clothes... I've got a ton of gifts to prepare and I just don't have the time to do everything.","content.75.1971":"Ho ho ho! What have you found?","content.75.1972":"Ho ho ho! Soon I'll be covered from head to toe!\\nI'm finally going to be able to go back to what I'm good at. From this point on, I'll never let go of my clothes.","content.75.1974":"Ho ho ho! I feel so much better in this outfit... And you'll finally receive your gifts... Except... ","content.75.1975":"Ho ho ho! I just want to make sure that nothing else was taken during all this hoo-ha. Would you mind taking a look in my workshop whilst I gather up what I need to get this show on the road?","content.75.1978":"What can I do for you?","content.75.1979":"Ho ho ho! So, how did your little visit go? Did you find anything?","content.75.1980":"Woah ho ho! If it isn't the key to my House! You can keep it, friend; come and visit me any time you like! I'll try not to deck the halls with you, ho ho ho!","content.75.1985":"Hello, my friend! Welcome to my Ice Floe, on the aptly named Chillberg Island. I'm looking for people who want to invest in my business. Are you interested?","content.75.1986":"Hello, little chilblain! Welcome to the *Snowbound* Snowbound Village.","content.75.1987":"Welcome aboard the USS Enterp... *ERROR -1* *EMERGENCY REFORMAT* *WELCOME PROTOCOL SYL-0001.b*\\nWelcome, Frigostian, I am Klap-Klap, your Frigostian Communication Protocol Mecha, and Master Sylargh's masterpiece.{[1*]?:}","content.75.1988":"Styffen Chillberg, but call me Chillberg. I set up shop here after discovering a mineral that I now use as the basis of all my work. And my work, my friend, is unsurpassed.","content.75.1989":"This is my home, my friend. I discovered this island on my travels, and I built this harbor with my own hands. I help passing adventurers explore that tower you can see in the distance, in exchange for minor services, of course.","content.75.1990":"Taroudium is named after the geologist who discovered its main properties, Hazieff Taroun. It has many uses, and yet it is only mentioned in ancient, extremely rare books.","content.75.1991":"Brrr! Nothing, apart from freezing my bits off in this outfit! The hunters north of my Ice Floe are experts in the manufacture of warm clothing; you should go see them and then we can talk business.","content.75.1993":"Don't be shy, my child: Old Father Deepboar only wants what's best for you. But quickly now, we need to get you to shelter - the waters are rising and hordes of Chafers are at the castle gates! It is the end of the world! The great flood! Chaooos!","content.75.1994":"You digress, my child, and Missiz Freezz's armies are marching across Frigost, ever nearer. But have no fear, for I have barricaded the only way into the castle, and no more will come. But the count won't stop there. His Dofus endows him with almost god-like power.","content.75.1995":"Protocol error - Rebooting - Top of tower inaccessible \\n*censored - security protocol SYL-0005.e* \\nAccess possible by flying machine. Enter through the Master's Workshop","content.75.1996":"I always need Taroudium. You should be able to find shards on Polar Cracklers, if you have the guts to hunt them. When you've got ten, bring them to me, and I'll give you a reward.","content.75.1997":"A deal is a deal, my friend, so here's your equipment. Have fun in the gorge, and happy treasure hunting!\\nDon't hesitate to bring me some more Taroudium; I've always got something for generous investors.","content.75.1998":"I don't need your opinion!!! I need willing young souls who are prepared to pay tribute to the gods who gave them life!","content.75.1999":"Die? Me? You mad? ","content.75.2000":"What are you saying, my child? Let me see... Woah! Hmmm... Uh... Well, I'm standing here before you, alive and kicking, right as rain, aren't I?\\nAlthough it's true I have felt lighter for a few years now, and I don't have much of an appetite for much, apart from Freezepops that is, and...","content.75.2001":"What the...!? Did I hear something growl? It's a Snowfoux for sure! SOUND THE ALARM! SOUND THE ALARM! Hmmm... no, I don't see anything Oh! Oh wait, there's someone there! Hello, I didn't see{[1*]?:} you coming! Have you come to help me treat the villagers?","content.75.2004":"*YUM* Thank you... Here, key... *CHOMP*","content.75.2005":"I don't have enough to pay for the roof repairs. The Frigostians are losing faith. No one attends services any more and the church coffers are empty. If you want to help, do the quests in the village and bring me as many ice kamas as you can.","content.75.2009":"Me - Frigostian Communication Protocol Mecha - serial number ZR98-B-KL4P-KL4P - My master and creator calls me Klap-Klap - Sylargh's assistant - in the image of master - his equal - \"abandoned\" by Count - crazy - do everything to find him - me abandoned in turn...","content.75.2010":"*initializing memory* *compiling information* Courtyard of Harebourg County, at the heart of Harebourg Castle - estate of Count Harebourg - quartermaster Sylargh - not been seen recently...","content.75.2011":"Me - Sylargh's assistant - in the image of master - his equal - abandoned by Count - crazy - me abandoned in turn...","content.75.2012":"*analysing request* *error* *insufficient responses available* *alternative suggestion required*\\nLike, for several hundred years.\\nworking on the *censored - security protocol SYL-0005.e* project.\\nFree time on personal project \"The Harebourg Pearl.\"","content.75.2013":"I am Father Deepboar of the Order of the Green Fathers, and I have officiated at the Church of the Twelve in the Snowbound Snowbound Village since... well, a very long time ago. I settled here in the year 551, when the village was known as Boundwons, and I spread the good word to Count Harebourg's workers.","content.75.2014":"I love children.\\nIn the past, there were many, dotted all over the village, and their laughter and games made the place feel alive when the adults were at the building sites. But then the big freeze hit our island and everything went quiet. Too quiet.","content.75.2015":"In the year 550, people came from all over the island to help build the Count's Water Clock, founding the village of Boundwons. Djaul's curse plunged Frigost into endless winter in an instant. The accumulated snow and ice caused an avalanche that covered the town, and it was renamed the Snowbound Village.","content.75.2016":"We cleared a path through to the houses, but there was too much snow to do anything else. When the great tidal wave came, the ocean water rose quickly and froze above us almost immediately, creating an impenetrable dome of ice. Until today...","content.75.2017":"My Master and Creator - Harebourg's assistant for climate project - Fantastic handyman - Genius inventor - Father of all Mechas.","content.75.2019":"Yes, my little dumpling. Dofus are a source of incomparable power. The primordial Dofus are related to dragons and are extremely rare. It seems that a young ogre called Ogrest has gone looking for them. I hope he doesn't find them, imagine the power he would have...","content.75.2023":"Ah... Oh... Well, you didn't ask me for details. And who knows, you might have been too scared to go to the Tower, or worse, you might have tried to haggle down the price of the equipment.","content.75.2024":"My, how time flies! Anyway, you're still alive, and I have my shards. Everyone's happy, right?","content.75.2026":"With help from my clients, I found out exactly what I needed to make cooking spices, detergent, deodorant, stain remover, rust preventative, an explosive energy drink, matches for barbecues... I can make anything, basically!","content.75.2027":"No, no, no. A deal cannot be renegotiated. Bring me the 10 Stolen Cargo, and I'll give you the Climbing Gear.","content.75.2028":"Yes, it's been a long time since anyone mentioned them. Their story must have been forgotten, and it's better that way. There's no point crying rivers over it. But back to Count Harebourg and his Ice Dofus.\\nIt is not one of the Primordial Dofus.","content.75.2029":"Useless? Look at what's happened here! Before the Great Deception of Count Harebourg, there were fields of golden wheat as far as the eye could see across the plains of Frigost. The sun shone brightly every day, warming our hearts and our souls.","content.75.2030":"You see, the Ice Dofus was given to Count Harebourg by Jiva, disciple of the god Xelor, protector of the month of Javian and Herald of Bonta. In her eternal struggle against Djaul, she gave the Ice Dofus to Count Harebourg so he could complete the Water Clock.","content.75.2031":"The Water Clock was created by Count Harebourg and his five lieutenants. It allowed him to work miracles on Frigost. I mean, he made the coldest day of the month of Descendre disappear outright!","content.75.2032":"Not quite... Djaul, demon of the Shustuft Crust, Protector of the Month of Descendre, Herald of Brakmar, and sworn enemy of Jiva, didn't see it like that, and still doesn't. Incensed at the \"theft\" of his day, Djaul came to restore the order of the seasons, and he didn't stop there. His revenge was to plunge the entire island into an endless, icy winter.","content.75.2033":"You're out of your mind, my sweet. Missiz Freezz would destroy you long before you got to the castle. We need a real army, which means we must start by treating all the wounded in my clinic. Take my key and go!","content.75.2034":"My little duckling, I can see that you are interested in the Dofus. The bad news is that it's locked at the top of Harebourg Castle.\\nThe good news is that I have the only key to get inside. I'll make you a deal...","content.75.2035":"I've just remembered, I took some notes before all this happened! My child, I think you may be able to find some clues as to the whereabouts of this key in my clinic.\\nHere's the key to get inside.","content.75.2036":"Freezepops, of course! Those frozen treats are my guilty pleasure. Ten should be enough to satisfy my libid... my hunger.","content.75.2037":"If Jacquemart Astron Harebourg had not accepted the Ice Dofus, none of this would have happened. Curse them, curse them both!","content.75.2038":"Since then, there have been no more visits from the children and the church remains inaccessible. The gods punished us for our greed, but they could have spared the children. The poor little things had nothing to do with it.","content.75.2039":"I am the village's spiritual leader. With all the problems we've had, our faith in the gods has been strongly put to the test...\\nI also used to teach the children of the village, but due to the state of the buildings and a lack of students, that's no longer possible.","content.75.2040":"I pray to the gods every day. I ask for forgiveness, and I protect the entrance to my church.\\nDo you think that after centuries of repentance, the gods will eventually prove lenient?","content.75.2041":"Do not be afraid, young adventurer. Here on Frigost, time runs much slower, and in fact has almost stopped. This is due to the effects of the Water Clock combined with Djaul's curse. It explains my boundless energy - I have not slept for at least 300 years!","content.75.2042":"blahblah","content.75.2043":"blahblah","content.75.2044":"She's one of Count Harebourg's lieutenants, and she is a traitor! She came with promises of the moon and the stars, and ultimately betrayed us all! She and her army of Chafers came out of nowhere! She's holed up in the manor, sending out wave after wave of undead horrors.","content.75.2045":"That's an understatement! She is as awful on the inside as she is on the outside! In times gone by her icy beauty would have made your blood run cold. These days she does the same with a single glance... literally as well as figuratively! They say she raises the dead to use as slaves...","content.75.2046":"That Freezepop? Not really, but I'll take it off your hands. The last time I found one of these beauts was when I stumbled upon an abandoned cart near the Manor. Since those pesky Chafers invaded I've not been able to return.","content.75.2047":"Hey you! My name's David Croquette, hunter of the Guild of Hunters. This place sure freezes the hairs on your chest, don't you think? What brings you to these parts?","content.75.2049":"I fear that my activity is nearing its end. A band of pirates stole some of my cargo. All I have is this map, which shows the location of their camp. I'll give you the Climbing Gear if you help me.","content.75.2051":"That old skinflint Chillberg wants us to give you some warm clothes? I could make some, but I'll need some Brrrbli fur. Have a look in the caves beneath us, we keep a few in captivity down there.","content.75.2052":"Here's your equipment! We're very grateful to Chillberg, so we'd like you to take some Pure Taroudium to him. You can extract it from the area's ice cores.","content.75.2059":"All I know is that no adventurer has ever returned. By Enutrof's beard, there's treasure to be found, make no mistake. If only I didn't have my little Taroudium business to look after...","content.75.2060":"We're under siege! Trapped like rats! The terrible Missiz Freezz and her hordes of Chafers are about to launch one last, devastating assault!","content.75.2061":"Are you sure you're ready? We're talking burning desire here... because there's no going back! And it's no use counting on Peece, Cantile and Lou; they're in no condition to fight.","content.75.2062":"Calm down, little one. I hid it in one of the secret books in the library, and while I live, it will not leave that hiding place.","content.75.2070":"If we want to survive, we need to treat everyone as soon as possible.\\nThis apocalypse is proof that the gods are angry. We should have spent more time in prayer!","content.75.2071":"The key to the castle? What for? There are more urgent matters at hand! Treat all the people you see here, \\nand then we'll talk about the key...","content.75.2072":"That's perfect, but I fear that the dead are rising... We'll see about your key later. In the meantime, head to the library. Here's the code to the lock, you take care of the adults and I'll take care of the children...","content.75.2074":"Thank you for bringing me this Pure Taroudium. I would have happily given you my Climbing Gear in exchange... but something terrible has happened!","content.75.2075":"You search the library catalog. Certain titles catch your eye...","content.75.2080":"Badoom tsh! Hey you! How's it hangin'? Great party, isn't it? I hope you're having fun, because I can't stand it when people are in a bad mood!","content.75.2081":"Hey hey, party person! What brings you to our island of dancing and debauchery?","content.75.2114":"That's up to me... And I say you've got a long way to go before you're good enough!","content.75.2115":"Ha! Knowing how to shake your posterior doesn't qualify you as a bona fide party animal! There's a contest being held near the local disco... We'll talk after you've proved your worth there.","content.75.2121":"Hey party people! Isn't it funky around here, isn't it fresh? What a blast! What do you say to a little challenge? Nothing like it to loosen up your hamstrings. Gather round! Take your place - you'll have a great time, promise!","content.75.2122":"There will be four cells around you, and you will have four states. Step on the cell whose color matches the lowest level state, cast the spell matching its description, then repeat for the other colors.","content.75.2123":"I see you've taken a liking to it! I still have a few Multijelys left. Good thing my stocks are replenished every day! Which one would you like?","content.75.2136":"What brings you down to my sewers, adventurer? Be quick! There's justice to dish out down here! \\nSeriously, I hardly ever take a break - whoo ha!","content.75.2141":"Someone led this Chaos monster here, you say?! I need to learn more about this. Say, do you have time to inspect some of the city's hot spots for me? If you succeed, I'll pay you in shiny new kamas.","content.75.2142":"That's what I was afraid of... I've done some investigating of my own and I believe that members of Ogrest's Cult are responsible... Those vermin! In any case, you must be quite the warrior if you got rid of them all!","content.75.2143":"You certainly won't find 'em up at the surface, not for all the hairs in Pappy's beard! You should go and see Donalangelo in the sewers of our city. He must know where their hideout is. And I bet your fighting skills will interest him too!","content.75.2147":"I was born on Zinit a long, long time ago. I fought the Ogre when he arrived, and I wound up all alone down here in a strange liquid... Then the gods - oh, praise them! - gave me a second chance and put me in charge of security in these here sewers.","content.75.2154":"Halt! Your passport is not valid! Only Amaknian citizens can come to me to complete missions and earn rewards.","content.75.2155":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Amakna. Your passport looks fine, are you here for a mission?","content.75.2156":"Halt! Your passport is not valid! Only Bontarian citizens can come to me to complete missions and earn rewards.","content.75.2157":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Bonta! Your passport looks fine, are you here for a mission?","content.75.2158":"Halt! Your passport is not valid! Only Brakmarian citizens can come to me to complete missions and earn rewards.","content.75.2159":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Brakmar! Your passport looks fine, are you here for a mission?","content.75.2160":"Halt! Your passport is not valid! Only Sufokian citizens can come to me to complete missions and earn rewards.","content.75.2161":"Welcome, [#name], citizen of Sufokia! Your passport looks fine, are you here for a mission?","content.75.2163":"Nope, you're not ready.","content.75.2164":"Don't get me wrong; I loooved the way you wibble-wobbled on the Raft! But you're a long way from having my disco skills. And you're missing something even more important...","content.75.2165":"No. You must find your color. It is hidden deep, deep within you. It is your destiny to find it. There are some hunters not far from here who should be able to help. And if you manage, then we'll talk Show business!!!","content.75.2166":"Hey, you! What brings you to these parts?","content.75.2172":"Ahhh, look at that color... Your color is truly beautiful, but you must see it for yourself. Here: Take the Multijely that suits you and then visualize your color.","content.75.2173":"Ah yes... I can see it in your eyes. The Multijely has freed your mind! You're ready for the Jellix Show! Here's your pass to the Jellith Dimension. Go and win that show like the celebrity you are. Bilbiza is watching you! It's PARTY TIME!","content.75.2174":"What ale you looking fol? You wouldn't be a Wabbit spy by chance, would you?","content.75.2175":"Oh no! I completely fowgot about the militawy pawade coming up! I have to pwesent myself to the sewgeant, but I've lost my geaw again! Ohhhh, the sewgeant's gonna kill me!","content.75.2176":"We could always do with more raw materials to continue our repairs. Perhaps you could bring me some of the things on our list! It will help you gain experience.","content.75.2177":"We could always do with more raw materials to continue our repairs. Perhaps you could bring me some of the things on our list! It will help you gain experience.","content.75.2178":"We could always do with more raw materials to continue our repairs. Perhaps you could bring me some of the things on our list! It will help you gain experience.","content.75.2179":"We could always do with more raw materials to continue our repairs. Perhaps you could bring me some of the things on our list! It will help you gain experience.","content.75.2180":"Thanks fow finding my geaw!","content.75.2181":"This awmy is a catastwophe! The most undisciplined in all of Wabbit mawtial histowy! ","content.75.2182":"It's not going well... Listen, I've a message fow you to take to the Loyal Lenald. Think you can take cawe of it? Pay attention, it's a coded message! Wemembew it vewy well; it's veeeeeeeewwwy impowtant!","content.75.2183":"Pewfect! Now listen cawefully! The message is: \"It's time to lecluit some melcenalies!\"","content.75.2184":"Awe you kidding me? Yes! The Cawwot hawvestews awe in a wage. They'we always upset about one thing ow anothew. They'we scweaming about wevolt not faw fwom the thwone woom. It would be good if we could calm them down somewhat!","content.75.2185":"Awe you kidding ow what? Fow example, Siw Bows! He's the wowst kind of soldiew. He's a big ninny who wowwies mowe about the laundwy than the upkeep of his swowd. He's so scawed that he's locked himself away in the wawehouse. Go get him!","content.75.2188":"A message fol me? I bet it comes flom the Wa Wabbit's Lieutenant! What is it about?","content.75.2191":"Aha! Glad to heal it, sholtie! Them Wabbit velmin, we massacled them! This island is ouls! Nowadays you only find them undelglound.","content.75.2192":"Celtainly not! They deselve theil fate! And you'le about to join them if you don't change youl tone quick! I'm light, peliod, end of stoly.","content.75.2193":"Light, that's enough of that! Gualds! Thlow them in plison!","content.75.2212":"Flying ovel? It was completely smashed neal the sholes not long ago. Since then, my walliols have seen a big Xelol and a little man head into the Old Gallely with some Black Wabbits they indoctlinated.","content.75.2213":"The enemy of my slav... uhm, selvants, is my fliend. Take this key to get into the Ancient Gallely, which we have condemned. Be caleful once inside! Many of my walliols nevel came back.","content.75.2227":"Hey! What awe you doing in my thwone woom?!","content.75.2228":"WHAT?! GUALDS! Catch that strangel and lock {[1*]?hel:him} up! That will teach {[1*]?hel:him} to insult me!","content.75.2229":"TO YOUL WEAPONS!!! THIS IS WAL!","content.75.2230":"Cwispy cawotene on a cwackew, that was close!","content.75.2231":"This is no time to ask questions; you saved me! We need some wepellent!","content.75.2232":"Black Cawwot Juice! A malvel! Just chock-full of memolies. Evely swig leminds me of the battle we alduously won against those insuffelable Wabbits... *hic* I was on the flont lines, you know... *hic* A beautiful line of Cawwots... *hic* *hic* No! A beautiful VICTOLY! *hic* Wait... who ale you again?","content.75.2233":"Yes, of coulse! The leselves of lice lations have been disappealing undel oul noses! Go find them! I'm supel hungly! ","content.75.2235":"Aha! Glad to heal it, sholtie! Them Wabbit velmin, we massacled them! This island is ouls! Go enjoy oul lands! But I waln you, don't make any agleements with oul enemies, or you'll end up in a saucepan!","content.75.2236":"Seventy-thwee... Seventy-fouw... Hmm. The supply of Cawwots is diminishing; I must wawn the Kween...","content.75.2237":"Actually, I do! Would you believe my subjects can't stop golging themselves on lice impolted flom a neighboling island, and now we have almost no leselves left?! \\n\\nMake them go on a diet! ","content.75.2238":"Obviously, times awe hawd! The waw with the Lenalds thweatens to bweak out again, and we can't gwow a thing in these wotten tunnels!","content.75.2239":"If the Woyal Guawd was able to help us, maybe we could get somewhewe. But fow that to happen, we'd need a huge supply of Antimawosis to get them thwough the tunnels.","content.75.2259":"Grmblmgmrmghgh... What? Who awe you? Awe you the new assistant they wewe supposed to send me? You'we late!","content.75.2260":"Ulgh! I despise Callots! Sule, they implove youl eyesight, but me? I want nothing to do with them.\\n\\nBut... I guess we have to let the Black Wabbits do theil thing. I suppose they have to eat, aftel all.","content.75.2261":"Come wead my notes. I think I have sevewal pwomising leads on how to cweate a Supew Wabbit. Test them and let me know what you discovew. And don't fowget to get wid of the test subjects so they don't cwowd up my lab.","content.75.2262":"So?! Have you finished the expewiments I asked you to pewfowm? You'we suwe taking youw time!","content.75.2263":"Fantastic! We'we almost thewe! The time has come to cweate the Ultimate Wabbit! The only pwoblem is that my notes got a bit wet and, fow the life of me, I can't wead them. You'll have to find the wecipe youwself, I'm afwaid.","content.75.2264":"Is that so? Thank you, messengel! You can tell the lieutenant that we applove of the suggested tluce. ","content.75.2265":"Awe you still hewe?\\nI have loads to do befowe I can face you like the noble I am.\\nSkedaddle! Get outta hewe befowe I call in my guawds!","content.75.2266":"As pwomised, the Bow is youws. Oh, you don't know how happy it makes me to recovew my woyal attwibutes! Mowe impowtantly, I'll get my Cawwot Dofus back!\\n\\nThe next time we meet, stwangew{[1*]?:}, we'll pwobably be advewsawies. Until then, good luck in youw adventuwes.","content.75.2267":"What?! Steady on, sweetheawt. Do you weally think that's the way to talk to a Wa? You'we lucky you'we one of the ones who helped me get this faw. Othewwise it would have been... *SHLIK!* Off with youw Cawwot top!","content.75.2272":"Why? Why?! Fow the GLOwY, of couwse! Fow Science, with a capital S! To save my bwethwen fwom this howwid affliction... To... But what do you mean, asking me all these questions instead of wowking?!","content.75.2273":"But... But... All wight. The secwet is too big to keep to myself. I twust you. Some hooded individuals with a stwange accent came to visit me a while ago. They gave me some notes fwom anothew age, pwepawed by a cewtain Doctow Waltew-Bychop. They said it would be wise to stawt by studying Wabbits suffewing fwom Zwombbification.","content.75.2274":"Thewe's something else. They told me it would allow me not just to cuwe the least-infected zwombbits, but also to cweate supew-powewful wabbits, and that these \"ubew-wabbits\" would be the solution in a big conflict that will be as unexpected as it is imminent and disastwous fow the island. I can't say any more as long as I know that the howwows I cweated awe still clinging to life.\\nPlease, get wid of my most howwible test subject - I locked it up in Womewo's Labowatowy.","content.75.2275":"Weally? Fabulous! As pwomised, hewe's the west of the stowy.\\nTo this day, I haven't succeeded in cweating any Ubew-Wabbits. Just mowe and mowe vawieties of Zwombbit... In fact, I wondew if that isn't what those hooded visitors weally wanted...\\nTo be completely honest, I'm not looking fow glowy. They thweatened me, me and my family...\\nAnd the stwangest bit of all was definitely theiw accent. It definitely wasn't a Wabbit accent. Now Black Wabbit, and cewtainly not Lenald. Oh no! Theiw accent... Theiw accent was a bit flattew... Mowe neutwal and without wawmth... A bit... A bit like youws, actually.","content.75.2276":"Ah... The cwatew of shame... It used to be whewe you could see the pwide of the Wabbit Nation: The Huge Cawwot!\\n\\nOh! It was SO plump and juicy! Each yeaw, one lucky individual chosen at wandom fwom among the most valiant Wabbits was authowized to have a bite of the Huge Cawwot, just once.\\n\\nBut fow some weason, it stawted to fall apawt and it changed colow. And now, it's occupied by Muvegitants.","content.75.2284":"Hi! Did you come to admire me? \\nPeople come from everywhere just to see me! When I'm not busy hunting Moowolves, I come here to complete my collection of skulls and beauty products. Al Howin monsters have excellent resources!","content.75.2285":"You're suuuch a sweetheart!. You wouldn't be willing to bring me 10 of each sort, would you? Happy, content, smiling...? I'd be the happiest woman in the world!","content.75.2286":"If killing those vile creatures doesn't bother you too much, I'd really like it if you could bring me some of their wool. I really like the color; about a dozen ought to be enough to shine my boots.","content.75.2287":"I have a particular affection for these monsters, but their emulsions keep my skin so soft that I couldn't do without them. Could you bring me ten of them?","content.75.2288":"Oh, what a lovely thought! But I can't take all of your lovely skulls! \\nHere: I'll leave you one so you'll always think of me!","content.75.2289":"If it doesn't bother you too much, I only need a little bit: just a sample, you know. Hmmmm... 10 Pumpkwinny Wools and 10 Al Howin Emulsions ought to do the trick!","content.75.2290":"STOP! YOU SHALL NOT PASS! Kralaman hates it when someone disturbs him during his shower! And if I let you pass, he's going to slap me with his tentacle...","content.75.2291":"STOP! YOU SHALL NOT PASS! Lardevil is in the kitchens, in the middle of making a feast, and even if I'm hungry like a wolf, I don't want to suffer his \"blind justice\"...","content.75.2292":"STOP! YOU SHALL NOT PASS! Decepticod is busy lifting weights to become the world's greatest supervillain.\\nIf I were you, I wouldn't disturb him... he might use you as a punching bag.","content.75.2293":"PROTOCOL: REFUSE PASSAGE!\\nCreator calibrating... Move along or disintegrate.","content.75.2296":"There are strange things afoot in the Ingalsses' Cellar. I want you to go over there and find out what the problem is. Don't worry, it's nothing dangerous, and I just know you're the right person for the job!","content.75.2297":"My name is E.Z. Yeast. What can I do for an amateur gourmet?","content.75.2298":"I can see you're a person of taste! And which profession would you like to learn to become the best chef of the year?","content.75.2299":"I am N.D. Hammersmith, the master of the Astrub Forges!\\nWould you like some help crafting a stabbing weapon?","content.75.2300":"On which forge would you like to start?","content.75.2301":"Welcome to Missy Amulet's\\nThe fashion accessories bazaar for all your adventuring needs!\\nWhat can I do for you?","content.75.2302":"And which profession would you like to learn?","content.75.2315":"Hmmm... What is it for?\\nI'm very busy. Research waits for no man.","content.75.2319":"Bwork! What you non Bwork do here?","content.75.2320":"Bwork! Bwork Chief send you?","content.75.2322":"Non Bworks gone. Gone in Temple. But Temple block by Bwork Foos.","content.75.2323":"Ah yes. Help very nice good. But you not strong enough. You go play Bworkball prove me you strong! You come back after win Bworkball! Me give Bworkball Registration, now go play.","content.75.2324":"You win Bworkball...?! Perhaps you useful then... Go see Bwork Cook at mountain top. He know what you good for.","content.75.2326":"You help me make Bwork Foo cure mixture. You get bits from monsters in enclosure there! Me no want do.","content.75.2327":"Bwork! I prepare cook's special: Bwork Burgers! Cure for everything! You take to Bwork Foo Zero and cross fingers it work good.","content.75.2328":"Bwork! If Bwork Burger not worked, must use ultimate weapon... Bwork Beer! Kill all the microbes!","content.75.2329":"Yes but you need go in arena give him Bwork Beer.","content.75.2331":"Bwork! You non Bwork, help me. Blue non Bworks attacking me!","content.75.2332":"What?\\nYou no see blue non Bworks coming?\\nYou no cursed! You no can help me!\\nBut you safe...","content.75.2333":"More non Bworks. Non Bworks not nice. They go to old ancient Bwork Temple. Diggum, diggum, diggum dust and earth.\\nBut you no can go Temple. Temple in Bwork Camp. Bwork Chief no like non Bwork. Go show chief you friend of Bworks. And you no smell like Bwork. Ten Worn Wild Gobball Wools give you nice stinko like you should.","content.75.2334":"He's right, kid. We're always looking for extra manpower for rebuilding Astrub. My mercenaries are all busy dealing with important issues. Could you bring me some Logs of Wood? You should find some near the old Sawmill.","content.75.2335":"Of course, I think I can trust you with this one! It's a very important mission, so don't let me down! \\nDeliver this missive to the Guild of Hunters' camp for me.","content.75.2339":"Yes, of course! Jenry Hones Sr., my old Archaosologist friend, will be able to tell us more about the monster. You should go and see if he's at the Temple of Scriptures.","content.75.2345":"Ah, a strapping Bontarian! Hello! It's not often that brave adventurers like you come to see me. What's up?","content.75.2346":"What are you doing here? I didn't ask for backup! I'm not paying a kama of your transport fees, you know! I, Eminerell Lebbocq, will take credit for everything salvaged from this temple in the name of Brakmar!","content.75.2347":"Good day to you, my Sufokian friend... Or should that be good evening? I've been underground so long that I've lost track of time!","content.75.2348":"Howdy, fellow Amaknian!\\nWhat are you doing in our dark, forgotten corridors?\\nAre you lost?","content.75.2349":"This gem should allow you to activate the mechanism in the main hall of the old Bwork Temple. If everything has gone to plan, my fellow Archaosologists from the other nations will have found the other gems.","content.75.2350":"If our research is correct, we need them in four different colors. That's why we split up the tasks.","content.75.2351":"After several months of research at the Temple of Scriptures, we finally gathered enough clues to attempt the legendary Wild Gobball recipe from the Dofus Age. It seemed to be based on a sauce made from Bwork Beer.","content.75.2352":"We were led to the Wild Estate by a series of accounts about Goultard and his evil alter-ego, Dark Vlad. The location in question seems to be in the same spot as the forest where Dark Vlad lived in the Dofus Age.","content.75.2353":"If our research is correct, we need them in four different colors. That's why we split up the tasks.","content.75.2354":"This gem should allow you to activate the mechanism in the main hall of the old Bwork Temple. If everything has gone to plan, my fellow Archaosologists from the other nations will have found the other gems.","content.75.2355":"We've been trying out new recipes using Wild Gobball for several weeks now. And then, a few days ago... The tremors, the shrieks, and the GIGANTIC Gobball who appeared out of nowhere with his savage herd... I don't think he approved of us chowing down on his little protégés. Few survived to join me in seeking shelter at the Bontarian camp.","content.75.2356":"It was just before supper time, and the most industrious workers among us were still down in the galleries... That's when that beast, Gobbsage, and his horde literally trampled the camp to the ground as they stampeded in from the northeast, heading southwest. There must still be some poor souls stuck underground. May the gods have mercy on them... When the Amaknians arrived, we half-heartedly allowed ourselves to be shepherded to the Brakmarian camp, in the bleak hope that they might help us.","content.75.2357":"Talk of the excavations of Bwork camps in the Wild Estate caught our attention at a recent symposium held by our Sufokian friends... But we didn't find much there. Our colleagues from the other Nations were on the trail of an extremely powerful relic, and we joined them, hoping for a slice of the glory. The relic's just got to be in the temple!","content.75.2358":"It wasn't me who wrecked the camp, so it's no use sending me the bill! I was hard at work when disaster struck. I'd opened up the treasure room and found it empty - apart from that skeletal monstrosity. It was the Sufokians that stole the goods!","content.75.2359":"Our \"analysis\" of the Sufokians' research in the area revealed the potential existence of an incredibly powerful relic on the island. You get me, right? Powerful means desirable, and that means tons of kamas for me! Er... I mean, for Brakmar, with perhaps a generous bonus for me. We thought we would find the relic in the place where we set up camp, but apparently it's actually in the Temple! Probably a Sufokian ploy to confuse us.","content.75.2360":"If our research is correct, we need them in four different colors. That's why we split up the tasks.","content.75.2361":"Take this... extremely valuable... gem. To thank you for everything... Hmmm... It should allow you to activate the mechanism in the main hall of the old Bwork Temple. My incompetent archaosologist counterparts from the other nations might have found the other gems, although I doubt it.","content.75.2362":"Really? Did you read the bit about... no, nothing. I'm going to need it back though, unless you want to pay me for it. Anyway. I got out of there and found the camp obliterated. Those poor wretches from Bonta and Amakna begged me to help them. Despite all the bad blood between me and Jenry Hones Jr, I made a deal with them - I would help, if they helped me \"settle things\" at the Sufokian camp.","content.75.2363":"It turned out that the relics they stole from us like cowards were actually cursed. But they still learned that the extremely powerful relic was somewhere nearby. I negotiated a temporary agreement to unearth it and we hit the road, once we'd pooled our research notes on this relic and on the island as a whole.","content.75.2364":"But instead of clues about their history, we found indications of an extremely powerful relic. We worked together with the Sufokians to try to save the relic from the clutches of Lebbocq and those dastardly Brakmarians. The relic's just got to be in the temple!","content.75.2365":"Bwork Beer good yum yum! You take this key and more beer and go help other Bwork Foos.","content.75.2366":"Perfect! You non Bwork wait.\\n\\n*The Bwork pulls out some dried-up little knots of Worn Wild Gobball Wool and spits liberally on them before scrunching them up in his filthy hands. Drop by drop, a foul-smelling liquid starts seeping out, and he collects it carefully in a flask.*\\n\\nTake! You see Bwork Chief, at north real Bwork village, first stage on mountain.","content.75.2367":"I have a little list of things to do, if you're interested. Things like picking up Ash Wood, extracting Tin Ore, floating on your back without sinking... Anyway, do them all in order and I'll reward you handsomely.","content.75.2368":"Me?! Chief of all Bworks, of Bworde? HAHAHA! Me no crazy, no want attack biggum Bworks what think 'em good chief material.\\nNo, me chief Bwork Explorers. We explore, find Bwork treasure, kill opposition.","content.75.2369":"We problem. Enemies at ours. Thork and other explorers not happy. Say \"NOT ENOUGH BWORK BEER\" but I say \"ENOUGH BWORK BEER\". Then they go on stripe. Always trouble and stripe.","content.75.2370":"Explorers no can kill explorers. So Thork and others in Stripers Trenchment, in southwest of plateau. And he took my beautiful Kiki! Strongest Bwoggall. Wild Gobball wildest mount in Bworde.","content.75.2371":"Haw haw haw! Many want my Bwork Beer recipe. But nobody know. Me use traditional recipe.\\nMe add special ingredient. And you... never... allowed... know...!","content.75.2372":"Traditional recipe?! You non Bwork. You no know tradition. And you no allowed know. And you no Bwork Cook neither! And even if I teach you Bwork cooking, you no can make secret ingredient for traditional recipe. Oops! Say too much.","content.75.2373":"Hahaha! You think you smarter than Bwork Cook? You guess secret 'gredient, then.\\nIf you find, you allowed learn recipe. Although... if you find, you know recipe already. Oops... Already say too much.","content.75.2374":"You so far, you invisible!\\nHahaha!\\nPlay recipe?","content.75.2375":"You idiot!\\nWhy not Bwork fart too, huh? No.\\nPlay recipe?","content.75.2376":"Pfffft!\\nYou funny funny, but no good!\\nPlay recipe?","content.75.2377":"Hoohoohoo! Haha! You stop!\\nMe no control, peepee in pants!\\nPlay recipe?","content.75.2378":"This gem should allow you to activate the mechanism in the main hall of the old Bwork Temple. If everything has gone to plan, my fellow Archaosologists from the other nations will have found the other gems.","content.75.2379":"If our research is correct, we need them in four different colors. That's why we split up the tasks.","content.75.2380":"Oh, heavens! What a catastrophe! We were really making progress studying the artifacts we'd found onsite. That's when Lebbocq showed up with his posse of Bontarian and Amaknian archaosologists. He was in a foul mood and kept bawling about debts, theft and I don't know what else. He wanted to see what we'd found on \"his\" site. We showed him. He looked disappointed and asked to study a few artifacts.","content.75.2381":"After looking up endless references at the Temple of Scriptures, we learned of one of the oldest species on earth: the Wild Gobballs of the Wild Estate. We went and worked on sites all over the island, which is where we found out that we were mistaken. Osamodas hadn't left his divine mark there... Instead, we unearthed clues leading to an ancient Bwork site, where a highly powerful relic was apparently kept.","content.75.2382":"We studied various ruins in Sufokia, following Jenry Hones Sr's instructions. We found traces of Oktapodas and his worshippers. Certain clues led us to believe that Oktapodas was one of the forms that Osamodas liked to take.","content.75.2383":"A few hours later, the Bwork workers who were helping Lebbocq came rushing out in a panic, shouting about ghosts and \"blue non Bworks\". We thought they were cursed. Lebbocq wouldn't breathe a word of what had happened in there. But we were all in a hurry to leave that place. I had made plans with the Bwork Explorers to start work on the old Temple at the top of the mountain. Since four heads are better than one, I also invited the archaosologists from the other nations to join me. I asked Jenry Hones Jr. to keep an eye on Lebbocq... And he didn't need much convincing to accept.\\nWe left the Bwork workers to take care of the camp, with that poor Frightened Bwork as their leader; he was in charge of guarding our reserves.","content.75.2384":"Good Bwork Archaosologist Lebbocq. Diggums go very good! \\nBut we no solve mystery of model...","content.75.2385":"Skeletal Gobballs kept closed up, but every time they killed, they coming back...\\nThey crazy! They eat dirt, gravels, artifacts... and Bworks! You do, you do quick, then we leave! And drink beer... You promise beer, no forget, hmmm?","content.75.2386":"We searching headpiece here in excavation site. But assault by Skeletal Gobballs! \\nStaff normally be found west of model, but we no find... No time for diggum, too many Skeletal Gobballs!","content.75.2395":"*The mysterious man looks you up and down with a piercing gaze that makes you feel quite uncomfortable* Hmmm... Yes, you might do...","content.75.2396":"Were you born to be a fearless, reckless adventurer?! Does the heart that beats within your chest yearn for a life of legendary glory?","content.75.2398":"It looks like fate is on our side! You're just the person I need! I'm one of Otomai's Disciples. I don't know if you know anything about my fellows and me, but all you really need to know is that we need resources from some of the World of Twelve's monsters. Unfortunately, I'm so busy that I can't leave Astrub right now...","content.75.2399":"Absolutely! But listen... I need you to collect resources from very specific - and potentially very dangerous - monsters. I'm going to have to test your skills little by little to make sure I'm not sending you on suicide missions.","content.75.2402":"If you can bring me everything I need, I'll reward you with an extraordinary item: a relic! I trust that'll be enough to convince you to go collecting stuff for me? ","content.75.2406":"I need certain resources that can only be found deep within the dungeons of the World of Twelve. You'll need to visit the nations and challenge their scariest monsters. Here: I've made a note of the first list on this scroll. Once you've brought me everything on it, I'll give you the next list.\\n\\n(For the Otomai's Disciple quests, the \"Kill the boss\" objectives are validated retroactively when logging back in to a character if they have already been completed previously)","content.75.2408":"Got any new resources for me?","content.75.2409":"Perfect! I see you've finished the first list. *holds out a scroll* Here's the second one.","content.75.2410":"So, how's the harvest coming along? You got anything for me?","content.75.2419":"Good, you're coming along nicely. Ready for another list?","content.75.2420":"So, any new resources to give me?","content.75.2421":"Excellent. I hope it wasn't too difficult. Shall we continue?","content.75.2422":"More happy hunting to share with me?","content.75.2423":"Great! You're quite the eager beaver! Here's the next part.","content.75.2424":"So, how's the harvesting coming along?","content.75.2426":"Shall we continue? Still motivated? If you complete this list for me, you'll get a little gift as a reward.","content.75.2427":"Rest soon you shall, young disciple... but not yet.","content.75.2428":"You're almost there, this is my last order... For the moment...","content.75.2429":"Good harvesting?","content.75.2430":"How are you getting on with the hunt?","content.75.2431":"So how are the deep, dark dungeons of the World of Twelve doing these days?","content.75.2432":"I expect you're in a hurry to be done with all this, but I'm still waiting on some of the resources from the list.","content.75.2433":"Congratulations! You really are an outstanding hunter. Here is your reward, as promised. It's a very special piece of armor, so take good care of it. If you're not afraid of hard work, I can give you even rarer items... Come back and see me if that interests you.","content.75.2434":"So, are you once again ready to roam the World of Twelve and confront untold dangers in the name of glory? I'm going to need your precious services again.","content.75.2435":"What are you doing here!? I have a ritual to finish, and I need sileeeence!","content.75.2437":"Hoo-hoooo!\\nWhat can the head archivist of the World of - hoot - Twelve do for you?","content.75.2438":"What do you-hoo want to know?","content.75.2439":"An archivist is assembling all the knowledge and wisdom of the World in books.","content.75.2440":"Astrub used to be the City of Mercenaries, led by Brutas the Guild Master.\\nThere's a statue of him on the huge fountain in the middle of Astrub.","content.75.2446":"You can find all the information relevant to the nations on the board next to me.","content.75.2449":"A mercenary is someone who carries out missions of varying difficulty with the sole aim of making life better for the inhabitants of the World of Twelve!","content.75.2450":"These will be perfect for preparing new timber frames for the city's houses. The value of missions like these must never be underestimated. Listen, that's not all. I have an urgent problem to solve. The Bow Meows are ruining all our work!","content.75.2451":"What do you want to know?","content.75.2452":"The hunters engaged by the Guild of Hunters are helping us get rid of the bothersome species at the same time as saving the Guild. They collect rare ingredients, I don't know what for, but we benefit because they're getting rid of the monsters for free!","content.75.2457":"Good, good, another good deed done. I must say that I'm exhausted!","content.75.2458":"... Hmm, a trivial detail. I have more important things to worry about! I sent one of my men on a mission and he's still not back...","content.75.2459":"We don't have monsters like these in Astrub... If what you're telling me is true, this complicates matters. What shall we do?","content.75.2462":"How can I help you?","content.75.2464":"Ogrest's Cult is such a nuisance... Its members have sabotaged so much of our research. But there are too many of them to combat, and they have their reasons for acting the way they do.","content.75.2465":"We archaosologists are members of Otomai's Disciples. We're scholars, as you might know, and we're especially interested in uncovering relics from times gone by.","content.75.2469":"Ahhh, Zinit... I went there once, but it's not my kind of place. \\nIt's a terribly dangerous place, but maybe you'll be able to climb Mount Zorrow.","content.75.2470":"Why, Ogrest's Chaos is all the water and wind that tore our magnificent city to pieces! Now I have to see that it's all rebuilt...","content.75.2471":"Ahhh, Jenry, my old friend! Did you know that I got most of my fortune from him? He racked up so many debts to me... Don't look at me like that! I gave him a good deal!","content.75.2472":"The day one of those Ogrest's Cult fellas runs into me, he'll have my shovel to deal with! Just thinking about them... Grrr... It sends shivers through my money pouch!","content.75.2473":"Some members of Ogrest's Cult have a hideout around here. Shreddie is the leader of this hireling camp, and he's one tough fighter. You'd better keep an eye... both eyes... on him. \\nOne time, I heard him say that he had to get his hands on some artifacts for his \"Master\", so as to stop adventurers from using them. I don't know what he was talking about exactly.\\nArchaosology isn't really my strong suit.","content.75.2474":"What do you want to know?","content.75.2476":"Yes, I did meet someone who called themselves the Astrub Knight.\\nHe proudly left to fight the Cult in their camp, with no heed for my warnings. He hasn't come back out yet.\\nThe knucklehead probably got captured!\\nIf he's even still alive...","content.75.2525":"Not another word! It's that blasted Occult Cult again, isn't it? And that idiot of a Grand Master, getting mixed up in rituals he doesn't understand! Well, you're going to need a special weapon to repel the being invoked by the ritual. Go and find some Larval Powder and a Hollow Tube for me. I'll make the tool you need.","content.75.2526":"Perfect! So... If I just put the powder here... Close up the tube, nice and tight... Add a little of my special fluid... *Donalangelo turns around, appearing to chew on the hollow tube* And, presto! The ultimate weapon! This'll help you defeat the monster created by the ritual!","content.75.2527":"Okay, okay! You beat me! But the ritual has started now, and nothing can stop it... Except perhaps Donalangelo... He always knows what to do!","content.75.2535":"Finally, it works! The portal to the Shustuft Crust is open... the writings about Eliatrope magic were true!\\nAhem, pardon my enthusiasm. What brings you here?","content.75.2536":"In Rushu's kingdom, Shushus reign supreme. They come in all shapes and sizes. The monsters have tons of artifacts, resources, and powerful objects. But watch out! Appearances can be deceiving. ","content.75.2537":"I've seen some others like you come through. Those who survived were so few there's no point mentioning them. The biggest came back terrified, without their equipment. The treachery never ends. You don't escape Rushu's kingdom; you just slowly perish.","content.75.2538":"Exactly. If you bring me some of those interesting things, I'll reward you. Thanks to the Eliatrope writings, I've succeeded in creating certain enchanted items with resources people bring me.","content.75.2539":"Bad day to you, inhabitant of the World of Twelve. You are entering the territory of the great Rushu. Or at least, one fairly remote little part of it...","content.75.2540":"You are in the Shustuft Crust, the land of our king, Rushu. We've been locked in this prison ever since the non-invasion pact was signed with the gods, back in the days of the World of Ten. There are no rules here.","content.75.2541":"Demons come to the Shustuft Crust and destroy everything they find just to amuse themselves. They also steal souls, fallen from Incarnam, in order to populate the dimension... and wait for the next invasion.","content.75.2543":"Thank you! I'd have had trouble beating them in my state. They're the ones that forced us to leave the village. The other members of the expedition headed west to do some recon and find a new spot for us to settle.","content.75.2544":"Hey there, stranger! It's been a long time since we last saw a new face around here.\\nWhat brings you to our settlement?","content.75.2546":"Poink poink pooooiiink!!! Poink poiiinky poiiipoipoink??","content.75.2548":"Poooiiink!!! What do you want, sof'skin?","content.75.2559":"Hey, look who's coming back to life.","content.75.2562":"You'll find the sap in the Castuc Grove, to the northeast. The Juicy Cacti are dripping with it. We'll use it to hide the seams and give your \"fake\" Castuc skin a really natural look.","content.75.2563":"Did he get away? I've been so worried, but the camp isn't safe enough for me to go and get him just yet. He did well to send you here, because we need help! You didn't come to this island by chance, you know!","content.75.2564":"Excellent, we'll make you a magnificent costume, and they won't notice a thing! Then you just have to sneak into their camp and see if you can find a way to make them see sense.\\nHere's your costume!","content.75.2565":"Can't share, not enough room. Poinkkoink mostly, not enough water. Poinkk poiiink regrets...\\nNo spring now except the underground poinker.","content.75.2566":"We have lost that knowledge. The only poinkkoinkoink we have now is our instincts. On the eve of its Great Drought, each Castuc goes on a walkabout to the north, to protect the passage from our afterlife.","content.75.2567":"I shall invoke the spirits of the Ancient Poinkpoinks to come talk to me. We haven't spoinkipoink for a long time. This might take quite a while. Why don't you let me get on with it and come back to see me in the village in a bit?","content.75.2568":"No more Castuc invasions to report!\\nWhat can I do for you, kid?","content.75.2569":"I'm the one who thought up the \"plan\". I created a diversion here at the tavern using a few water kegs whilst the others fled out the back way.\\nEither way, what with all this sand, I'd have slowed them down with my wheels. \\n\\nBesides, I'm the second-best fighter in the group, after Ezam the huntress, so I had a pretty good chance at getting away alone.","content.75.2570":"I'm the procession leader. Not the actual leader, of course, but I decide when it's time to find shelter or stop a while to let the mounts rest. I'm also in charge of monitoring the water supply - and protecting it, more importantly! And I feed the Dragoturkeys too.\\nI like Dragoturkeys, and they serve me well.","content.75.2571":"These? Funny story there.\\nI used to be a bit of a thug... fighting, joyriding Dragoturkeys, the lot. But Ahabar saw my potential and trained me as a Dragoturkey racer.\\nI tell ya, I was the best. Ahabar has a real eye for spotting people's inner talents. But one day, I took a bad fall during a race... The other riders didn't have time to swerve to avoid me.","content.75.2572":"Using a Castuc costume to infiltrate their camp?! Why didn't I think of this before? But the spine isn't going to be enough, not even with the resources we have on hand. We're missing... Juicy Sap!","content.75.2573":"I don't know exactly, but one thing's for sure: whenever they attack, they come from the south, maybe southwest, and leave the same way afterwards!\\nI'm staying here to watch over the camp. I'm counting on you!","content.75.2574":"Ahhh! Back again, stranger? What's new on the arid plains of Ohwymi?","content.75.2575":"I'm the guy who organized and funded everything.\\nI'm originally from Brakmar, see, and over there, sometimes things get dark. Real dark. \\nI was unlucky enough to fall out with one of the \"big guys\", who had people in the government. He did all he could to put pressure on me and make sure my projects and endeavors failed. I even have a hunch that Little-Feet's \"accident\" was nothing of the sort, if you know what I mean.","content.75.2576":"Everything went to the dogs, and the whole of the village where I lived was burned down. This time, nobody was hurt, but we had no place to go, and no real money to settle in another part of Brakmar. The other Nations wanted nothing to do with us. I felt responsible for what happened... So I decided that we should go far, far away, to settle in the untouched lands of the Nations.","content.75.2577":"I'd heard tell of a region that used to be lush and green, but that had become hostile and unpopulated. I invited the villagers to come on an expedition with the bravest among us to check the place out. The rest of the villagers are still shacked up in makeshift huts in Brakmar. I'm not going to get them out here until we have found a safe place with accessible drinking water.","content.75.2578":"At first, I thought the Castucs were just stupid, wild monsters. \\nBut after observing them for a while, I'm starting to wonder whether they're not more civilized than they look. If that's the case, they must know the whole region... and more particularly, any potential watering holes. If you could help us pinpoint the location of one of these springs, it would be a real thorn out of our sides.","content.75.2579":"The Eniripsas in the pits did all they could, but they couldn't save my legs. My career was over, but after our village's catastrophe, Ahabar offered me the procession leader gig. Once again, he saved my butt.","content.75.2580":"Our legends poinkkoinkoink of an ancient land, a land with plenty of water, where our people lived before our skin grew poinks.\\nBut nobody can go there now. Our ancestors left the ancestral Poinkpoink. Great Evil poinked our ancestors, and they left the ancestral Poinkkpoinkk. We return there no more. Promised our brothers from beyond the passage.","content.75.2582":"I see you have braved the spirits of the Ancient Poinkpoinks.","content.75.2583":"The Ancient Poinkpiks are willing to give you their blessing. This will allow you to enter their ancient lands. This place is poinking haunted - be careful!\\nO great ancient spirits! Come to us and purify this sof'skin!","content.75.2584":"You took a great big gulp of spores when you came in, and that made you hallucinate. I've brought you here to treat you with a dose of Inhibitor. Some of the toxins have gone, but you might still notice a few side effects.","content.75.2585":"Speaking of Inhibitor, I've actually used up my whole stock treating you. Would you help me harvest some more? \\nIf the Blackspores attack, we'll need it!","content.75.2586":"Yes. The Blackspores are dangerous, but I'll explain all that later.\\n\\nFor now, I need you to harvest some sporine from the spores deep in the cave. Just be sure you don't kill them! They're the only ones lef... Be careful!","content.75.2587":"Thanks for helping me fight them off!","content.75.2588":"There's something I've wanted to try out for a long time indeed... But I'm stuck here watching over the last healthy spores... Do you think you could inject some Inhibitor into the Contaminated Springs?","content.75.2590":"What can I do for you, human?\\nAre you curious about the Fungopole?","content.75.2591":"I'll write down the various springs on your map, one by one. \\nThat way, you'll have no trouble finding your way to them!","content.75.2592":"The Blackspores' thoughts, eh? I didn't think that humans could understand their inner ponderings. That must be one of the side effects of the spores you inhaled when you arrived.","content.75.2593":"Once upon a time, the Blackspores belonged to the same species as me. They were perfectly healthy Fungi. But when our Amybia turned to seawater to satisfy its tremendous thirst, it became afflicted with a strange disease... Most of the Fungi were then contaminated.","content.75.2594":"The others... I don't know exactly. They went to the surface and I never saw them again. \\nA sad fate for the rest of us... What are these \"Ogrest's Tears\" you speak of?","content.75.2595":"I'm very busy with the healthy spores. \\nThe Blackspores are always attacking us; I never get a moment's rest!","content.75.2596":"Meet me at the spore stocks! I need you!","content.75.2597":"I can't...\\nMy mission is to protect the part of the Fungopole that is still healthy and to prevent the contamination from spreading further!\\nI will not fail!","content.75.2598":"Poinkkoinkoink spirits have spoken. The sof'skin can enter the Poinkpoiiiiink passage, but must be careful. No Poinkkoinkoink has been in there for eons.","content.75.2599":"What excellent news! We'll finally be able to start a new life here in Ohwymi, and it's all thanks to you!\\nThe villagers we left behind in Brakmar will be able to come and join us at last. We owe you our eternal gratitude!","content.75.2600":"We need to find the Fungi Master in order to return to our Poinkpoink origins. We'll be able to live in peace with the poinkoiink water we need. \\nAmybia killed, poinkoiink water become pure again.","content.75.2601":"And yet I sense a terrible Poinkpoink sensation... Must be imagination. \\nI was tested by communication with Poiink ancestors!","content.75.2602":"What excellent news! We'll finally be able to start a new life here in Ohwymi, and it's all thanks to you!\\nThe villagers we left behind in Brakmar will be able to come and join us at last. We owe you our eternal gratitude!","content.75.2605":"I need a poink more time. (content unlocked on 4 April 2014 at 23:59)","content.75.2606":"You don't believe me, do you? \\nYou think I'm crazy too?","content.75.2607":"Hmmm... So, let's recap from the start... Normally, the particles should react like this... ","content.75.2608":"I'm glad you're a part of the mission!\\nI placed some beacons the first time I went to Chillberg Island. All we have to do is teleport over there.","content.75.2610":"This machine is way bigger than I was expecting. We're going to need more energy to stabilize it... Here: Take the Wakfu Harvester again and go take down some powerful monsters!","content.75.2611":"Yes, that's me. I'm Pandora. Nice to meet you. I contacted{[1*]?:} you because I've been keeping a close eye on your adventures. I must say, I'm impressed! And I'd like you to help me to recover a rather special energy source that I can use to activate a certain extraordinary machine.","content.75.2612":"After extensive research, I believe I've figured it out.\\nI think it's none other than a portal capable of transporting people to other dimensions!\\nUnfortunately, this one hasn't worked for a very long time... Probably since Ogrest's Chaos or perhaps even earlier, it's hard to tell.","content.75.2615":"You?! What are you doing here? You're not safe in this place! Run away, my darlings!","content.75.2616":"What do you want? I'm the master of the Pickpocketer's Guild. I don't have time to waste on strangers like you...","content.75.2617":"Hey, stranger! As Mistress of the Guild of Attic-Emptiers, I salute you. Let's talk business or not talk at all.","content.75.2618":"Wait! Your work for the guilds didn't go unnoticed. The Guild Master would like to talk to you. Go to the V.I.P.R. room at the back of the tavern, he's waiting for you. I think he has work for you, and it's got to be big, given his status. Farewell, and may Sram's shadow be with you.","content.75.2619":"Come closer, don't be so shy.","content.75.2620":"Do you want to go back to Astrub?","content.75.2621":"You're back! There was a problem with the portal settings, but it should be working properly now...","content.75.2622":"I need to fix this... and that, too! This machine is such a hassle to maintain!","content.75.2623":"Let's have a look, then! You know, you're probably going to have to bring me more every day to keep the portal open.","content.75.2624":"Right, I think you've gathered enough Skramas. With what we've gathered ourselves, it should be enough to gain access to the Bank.","content.75.2625":"We're going to try sneaking into the bank unnoticed and find the portal to the Enutrof god's dimension. If we follow the plan exactly, it should all go swimmingly.","content.75.2626":"If it doesn't work... Plan B!\\nWe'll improvise!","content.75.2627":"Stick to the plan to get inside the bank. It should all go well. Once inside, you'll have to find the portal to the Enutrof God's dimension. I'm sure you can do it!","content.75.2628":"To what do I owe this visit, young adventurer{[1*]?:}?","content.75.2629":"Plan B is: we improvise!\\nIt's just a back-up plan in case we need it, but normally, with the amount we gathered, it should all be fine.","content.75.2630":"Hello and welcome to the Enurado bank!\\nHow can I help you?","content.75.2631":"Ok, we're going to start the usual procedures.\\nIf you could wait for a few moments.","content.75.2632":"You can head to your chest. The registration of the deposit-maker is complete.","content.75.2633":"You are in Enurado, the dimension for the riches of the god Enutrof.\\nWould you like to deposit some money?","content.75.2634":"Hello, nice to see you in the Enurado bank again!\\nHow can I help you?","content.75.2635":"Well, I see you managed to make it out safe and sound! I wasn't expecting any less of you. The Great Explorancient was right then. It's a good job I didn't place any bets today, I would have lost my mind! HAHAHA!!","content.75.2636":"HAHAHA! You're so funny, I'm happy to have you here!\\nUnfortunately not, you used the I.S.D. too much when coming here. It can still easily cover small distances and some pre-recorded coordinates, but it hasn't got enough energy to travel to a new location.\\nYou'll have to find a large amount of compatible energy to power it fully! The energy I have here won't be enough, sadly. You'll have to think of something else.","content.75.2637":"Have you got what you need to recharge the I.D.S. and make the jump? HAHAHA!!","content.75.2638":"I'll refresh your memory!\\nYou have to beat monsters that are as powerful as you are so that this little harvester can take the Wakfu we need.","content.75.2639":"This little invention is really very practical! \\nI'm going to try to transfer the Wakfu you've collected to the Syncroportal. This better work.\\nWait, don't move!","content.75.2640":"Well, here you are again! What news from outside? Would you like me to teach you a couple of things about dimensional mechanics? Or do you want to test yourself against my riddles? That would be more up your street.","content.75.2641":"Listen to my first riddle, it's an easy one:\\n\\n\"I am of water, but also of air or energy. What am I?\"","content.75.2642":"Ah, so much energy! Very good, I'll transfer some to the Syncrportal. I'll add the rest to your reserves, it'll come in useful if you run dry.","content.75.2643":"Ah, there you are! You weren't followed? Sure?","content.75.2644":"Hey! Calm down! It's safe. Hidden in the Divine Dimensions. But I don't know where. It was decided to split the information relating to its location between several high-ranking Voyagers. As such, it will be harder to reach for anyone who seeks it for themselves.","content.75.2645":"Ah, you're back! Ready to take on a few contracts and finance our survival operations?","content.75.2646":"Always ready for action, right? Which contract would you like? Choose well, as you can only complete one contract per day.","content.75.2647":"Perfect. This should sell like hot cakes on the black market. Come back tomorrow to try your luck in the Skrammerzell House.","content.75.2648":"Excellent! This will swell our coffers nicely. Come back tomorrow to try your luck in Trickree Street again, after the guards and pedestrians have forgotten your face.","content.75.2649":"What? You came here through the... Oh! I see. She shouldn't have... Well... It doesn't matter. You're currently in Ingloriom, the dimension that used to host the Council of Twelve. The place has been abandoned for quite some time, a divine \"no-man's land\", and I've made it into my refuge.","content.75.2650":"We don't have time for such chit-chat! If the gods found out about your arrival... Especially you, young Pandora... By the Great Explorancient! Anyway, my role is to tell you that another Dimensional Voyager is waiting for you in Srambad, the dimension of the Sram god.","content.75.2651":"So, stranger, what's new?","content.75.2652":"Honestly? I don't like people walking on my turf. That militiaman should have known better than to come to my street, and talk to me. To ME!\\nWe shouldn't linger here; the Militia can't be too far away.","content.75.2653":"Hahaha!\\nNo witnesses, no danger, don't you agree?\\nAnd I don't think you or your friend will go telling on me... Right?","content.75.2654":"Hmmm... It's been ages since I saw strangers in Srambad. I'm sure I could make some money from this, even if I just act as your guide. Since you're new here, I'm sure you need information, right?","content.75.2655":"Oh... I see. In that case, the best thing to do would be to gain the trust of the bigwigs in the area. The Srambad guild masters, we'll need to loosen their tongues. And that means working for them... Let's head to the tavern!","content.75.2656":"This little marvel captures the Wakfu released by the expiration of life. The living source must be powerful enough to stimulate flux production and recover the charged particles.","content.75.2657":"Sorry, I got carried away. My device is synchronized with the portal. You need to defeat monsters whose power resonates at the same frequency as the portal's energetic signature.","content.75.2658":"Simply because I haven't been able to yet. The Wakfu is so condensed and solid that I can't extract it. In that form, they're just boring old crystals to me... Maybe one of these days I'll make some jewelry with them!","content.75.2660":"Sadly, I can only answer that question in part. I initially thought I was related to the Foggernauts, given the ease with which I can design and use technomagical engines. Er, when I say Foggernauts, I don't mean the tin cans you see clunking around today. I mean the ones who invented the Protoflex, you know?","content.75.2661":"Well, when I started studying ancient artifacts, Zaaps and other primitive objects and documents, I found out that I'm a whiz at portals and instantaneous transportation. The Teleport of Scriptures was based on my early experiments.","content.75.2662":"This is just a theory, of course, but I'm starting to believe that I'm the last living descendant of the Ancients... \\nAn Eliatrope!","content.75.2663":"I think I need to accept the fact that I'm a Dimensional Voyager. I'm a little disappointed, but I'm also really excited about all the opportunities I'll have now. Just think of all the worlds within my reach! But I hardly know any of my people's skills yet.","content.75.2664":"That's true. But that's no reason to give up! I've already drawn up an action plan, and I'm preparing a series of training exercises for myself! With the help of our new friends in Ingloriom and elsewhere, I should be up to speed in no time at all!","content.75.2665":"It's... unsettling. Besides, the globe we brought back from Chillberg seems to identify me as one as well, but I can't find any references to these people anywhere else! It's as though someone deliberately erased all traces of them from the World of Twelve...","content.75.2666":"Me? You can call me Chad O'Marsy if ya like. My friends'd call me Chad, if I had any. The others avoid talking to me.\\nAs for my enemies... Well, I dunno what they call me.","content.75.2667":"Pfft. I'm just a poor old Sram who's been livin' round these parts too long... Always the same bony faces, hollow eyes, stabs in the back... I need somethin' new... Adventure and action! You and your friend can offer me that, tied up in a pretty package with a bow.","content.75.2668":"Ha! The ones that cross me don't have time to chat... *FLICK* *SHWIP* They don't do much chatting at all after that, know what I mean?","content.75.2669":"Exactly! All the Wakfu you brought me was very useful. We can enter the portal as soon as you're ready{[1*]?:}. After all you've done for me, it's only fair the two of us would be the first to use the portal.{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} I can't wait to see what's on the other side!","content.75.2670":"Well, like I said, I need help to find an energy source that's compatible with the portal. The thing is, I can't do it alone, which is why I wanted your help.\\nIf you're interested, you can come with me once the portal's up and running, and see what kind of new dimension is on the other side.","content.75.2671":"Calm down, I know what you're looking for, or rather, \"those\" you are looking for. The Voyagers. I've been watching you for a while. Your arrival in Srambad with your companion has not gone unnoticed.","content.75.2672":"Silence! I wonder how it's even possible that you haven't been captured yet.\\nI won't say any more for now. Before that, you must complete one final mission.","content.75.2674":"Forget the Guilds. Now you're dealing with me. How can I know that you're not spies working for Sram or any other god? No agent of Sram would be crazy enough to accept these contracts. You've scored a point by completing them, but I still don't fully trust you.","content.75.2675":"I think I can trust the young woman, unlike you and your Sram friend. In order to gain my trust, you'll have to rid me of the Enutrof god's embassador tonight at the society gathering, and without raising any suspicions.","content.75.2676":"That's right, or you can go home and forget the Voyagers. It's up to you. But that would be hard on the little engineer, don't you think?\\nI'll be keeping an eye on you, so no dirty tricks...","content.75.2677":"Hahaha! Honestly, I didn't think you'd make it... That said, the loot is all mine.\\nAll I know about the Voyagers is that under the leadership of the Explorancient, they stole something from Sram himself. As you can imagine, he isn't too pleased.","content.75.2678":"Listen kid: I'm not going to beat around the bush. I need you to clean out a few bunches of unsavory swindlers around Trickree Street. Bring me 2000 Skramas from their laden purses and I'll see what I can tell you.","content.75.2679":"Listen closely. I was asked to gather 10,000 Skramas worth of precious items from the Skammerzell House. If you want, you can do it for me. Come back with the required amount and we'll talk about your needs.","content.75.2680":"I'm impressed, little one... Let me lighten your load, you look like you can't carry any more.\\nHere's what I can tell you about the Voyagers. It's been 200 to 300 years since we saw some in the area. Our master, Sram, has them tracked, locked up and executed.","content.75.2681":"Very good! Now activate the control panel... Let's see if that does it. Fingers crossed!","content.75.2682":"I can't believe it... Give me a little time to study the situation. Let me know if you want to help... All these failures are really getting me down...","content.75.2683":"Good, good... Excellent decision coming from him... Well, I imagine so... Anyway. No, I'm not the boss. To be honest, we don't really have a boss here. As to your visit here...","content.75.2684":"No, no, not for nothing... Hasn't the elder told you anything? I haven't got all the info, but it's about the Gods' Power...","content.75.2685":"Be quiet! No one must hear us!! Yes, the power of the Gods. Our order was able to take it.","content.75.2686":"Well, it seems rather obvious. It's time for me to share the information I was given. I've wirtten it all on this parchment. My mission is coming to an end. The next step for you is to head to Enurado and find the Dimensional Voyager hidden there.","content.75.2687":"My plan is simple. We'll need Skamas. Lots of Skramas. You've seen the Enutrof bank in Srambad? There's a portal to Enurado inside. But to reach it, we'll have to rob the bank!","content.75.2688":"Right, I'll keep it short so your Iop brain can follow. Enutrofs only let the rich enter their bank. So we're gathering Skramas, then we'll enter the bank and scope it out. From there on, we'll decide how to reach the portal inside.","content.75.2689":"You're right. The fastest way to amass Skramas here in Srambad is to complete contracts for guilds. So you've got a choice: burglary or pickpocketing. Discreetly bring the loot back to me and I'll contact the Guild Masters. Come back and see me when you're ready for the contracts.","content.75.2690":"You'll soon learn, don't worry about that. One thing at a time. \\nI think \"Gods' Power\" is a more topical subject.\\nAm I wrong?","content.75.2691":"Well, well... If I knew where it was, it wouldn't be a game! HAHAHA!\\nWhat I can tell you, is that I was responsible for creating the chest that contains it.\\nThe Container, to be exact.\\nI don't know where it was taken or hidden. One thing's for sure: My security system is flawless. It will be difficult for anyone who wants it to get their hands on it.","content.75.2692":"Yes, just as I made the one you just crossed. The one created for the Power of the Gods is, of course, of an entirely different caliber! I poured my heart and soul into it for many years, and I believe the result measures up.\\nI'm sure I burned out a few neurons along the way! HAHAHA!","content.75.2693":"Well, you're going to need to travel to the next dimension to learn more. \\nFor that, you'll need to use the Synpochro... The Dimensional In... Aaargh! Why did I give it such a long name? Well... The I.D.S. lets you activate dimensional beacons that we have placed throughout the Divine Dimensions. There should even be some left in the World of Twelve, if they haven't all been destroyed.","content.75.2694":"Yep, that's it, the I.D.S.!\\nWell, this one is for limited use...\\nMight I borrow you for a few seconds...  Ok, let me synchronize it with my own I.D.S. A little turn here... Some tinkering there... Aha! The coordinates have been saved. There is not too much damage, or any corrupted data. That's a good thing!","content.75.2695":"Oh! Not bad, this thing, we should have thought of that!\\nIf, as you say, you're fighting with enough monsters of a similar level to you, you should be able to get enough energy to charge your I.D.S.","content.75.2696":"Wrong answer! HAHAHA!\\nYou'll do better next time!","content.75.2697":"Well done; you have my congratulations!\\nYou really are the puzzle master.\\nIt's been ages since I've had so much fun!","content.75.2698":"Last question, listen carefully:\\n\\n\"How many teleporters are in the room after the 3 doors?\"","content.75.2699":"Bad news!\\nI know that you and the other have had a hard time gathering all this Wakfu, but I'm afraid it's not enough.\\nYou have to inject energy regularly to keep the battery working, without overcharging it. \\nI'll let you take care of gathering the Wakfu!\\nPretend it's a game, go on! HAHAHA!","content.75.2700":"Well done!\\n\\n\"What is the full name of the I.D.S.?\"","content.75.2701":"Not bad at all!\\n\\n\"What is the name of the ideal pet for the Dimensional Voyager?\"","content.75.2702":"Good answer!\\n\\n\"What currency do we use here?\"","content.75.2705":"Open your eyes, there are some in the pen just next to you! In fact, we've actually got too many.\\n\\nThe Drago-Express company already took what they needed, and there are still so many left over.","content.75.2706":"HAHAHA!!! \\nFeeling full of ourselves, are we?\\nWrong answer, but good try!","content.75.2707":"No problem. I've worked things out with Goultard.\\n\\nBut remember, a dragoturkey isn't a bow meow! They require much more care and attention, especially if you want to train one and ride it.","content.75.2708":"Yep, it can be done... But it's a pretty time-consuming job, and I don't have time to teach you everything. However, I have a solution for you and I hope you're really keen, because you'll have a lot of reading to do! Mwahahaha... Don't count on me to help you out with the reading; you'll just have to get on with it.","content.75.2709":"Dragoturkeys? I'm a bit of an expert! I can give you this one, written by a member of the Hogmeiser family who specialized in dragoturkeys...\\n\\n*After searching through a pile of books, he looks at you with an apologetic expression*\\n\\nCrumbs, where's it gone...? I was sure that... Oh!","content.75.2710":"First of all, Dragoturkeys don't talk: not to me, not to anybody. And usually, when I'm dealing with a Dragoturkey, it's not really in any state to do anything! If you help me out, I can share a few culinary secrets, like how to prepare a good Dragoturkey stew, or how to slice it into a roast. My stock room has been invaded by rats, and they're eating everything. Here's the key to my stock room. Get rid of them and I'll give you my book.","content.75.2711":"Of course I know what I'm doing! I've been supplying the Drago-Express company with harnesses for years. But I'm sorry, I'm very busy and won't have the time. However, I do have a very informative book on the topic, if you're interested. Craft a few objects with the wood I gave you and it's yours. There are workshops next door, and I can teach you the basics of each forge crafting technique if you don't know them yet. To make the coarse handles I'm asking for, you'll have to learn the Weapons Master profession.","content.75.2712":"Who would have thought it: Books have other uses besides kindling? Okay, after the theory, we need to move on to the practice. Now you need a saddle and reins to be able to tame your Dragoturkey. Go and find Missy Amulet; she'll be able to tell you more.","content.75.2713":"A saddle and reins? Shouldn't be a problem. But I'll need a few things to make a saddle I can really be proud of. I'll need some canoon powder. Just craft some with the Herbalist profession. If you don't know the basics yet, I can teach you.","content.75.2714":"Yes, as agreed, I was able to build it with the stuff you brought me. Here. ","content.75.2715":"You seem awfully sure{[1*]?:} of yourself... All right, as you wish. Here's a dragoturkey. It's docile and adventuresome, so it's perfect for you. Take good care of it!\\n\\nAnd feel free to come back and see me if you want to get into the basics of dragoturkey training. I'll make a{[1*]?:} real expert{[1*]?:} out of you!","content.75.2716":"I saw it. Impressive. Looks like you know how to choose your friends, young Pandora. Now I know I can trust you.\\nI am one of the Dimensional Voyagers that you are seeking.","content.75.2717":"Sram has been relentlessly tracking us for centuries, but we've managed to infiltrate his ranks. What better way to fool the enemy than hiding among his own? But let's get back to basics: Our boss is waiting for us at our headquarters. Head to the prayer room, in the lowest levels of this district. Pull the lever on the statue of the delinquent god Sram, and head down.\\nGo now.","content.75.2718":"Bring as much energy as possible. \\nEven if we don't use it all, I can stock some in reserve tanks.\\nIt'll come in handy.","content.75.2720":"So, are you ready for the big rodeo? Maybe you have some questions?","content.75.2721":"Well, well... I thought I'd stored it here after I came back from Brakmar a few days ago, but I can't find it. Nor can I find several other rather precious books... Now that I think about it, I think one of my bags fell during the return trip, between the Brakmarian outpost and the temple... I'll bet the books I've lost were in there!","content.75.2722":"You would do that? I'd be very grateful. If you can find my books, I'll give you my copy on Dragoturkeys. I came through Astrub Forest in order to avoid the city center, which is much too noisy for me. I must have dropped my bag at the edge of the Astrub Plains when my Dragoturkey reared up on the way back. I hope it's still there!","content.75.2724":"In order to be in compliance with local regulations and have the authorization to ride a Dragoturkey or any other mount, you need a special permit. I can give you one for 3,000 kamas. I'm not the only one who can give them out.","content.75.2725":"You have to succeed at training a dragoturkey by first putting its saddle and reins on, then capturing it before it start panicking too much.","content.75.2726":"Your Endurance lets you move around and carry out actions (cast spells). It regenerates by 5 levels at the start of each turn\\nbut you lose 1 Endurance level per MP used and spells consume it, too. So you have to keep an eye on your Endurance to make sure you aren't too tired when the time comes.","content.75.2727":"The Dragoturkey's Panic represents its stress level. The more panicked it is, the more it will try to defend itself against you and will no longer be afraid of you. The Dragoturkey gains 2 Lvl. of Panic at each turn And the closer you get to it at the start of each turn, the more the Dragoturkey panics. And be careful: If the Dragoturkey panics too much (State Lvl. 30), it will rush you and KO you!","content.75.2728":"The dragoturkey's Exhaustion represents its physical form. The more you make it run, the more tired it gets. It loses 2 Lvl. of Exhaustion at the end of each turn. You will only be able to catch the dragoturkey if it is too tired to be able to fight back against your attempts to saddle it and capture it. Its Exhaustion needs to be at least 10 to harness it and 20 to capture it.","content.75.2729":"Make good use of your movement and spells to tire out the Dragoturkey without making it panic, and without tiring yourself out through loss of Endurance. Make you sure you don't trap it in a corner, or it will rest. You must make it run in circles so it will tire itself out while you save your strength. First, you must harness the Dragoturkey with the saddle and reine, but wait for it to be tired enough first (Lvl 7). Once the saddle and reins are on, you can try to capture it, but once again, make sure it's tired enough (Lvl 12).","content.75.2741":"Hello little one, have you met my husband, Pappy Pal?\\nHe's out in the courtyard by the exit.","content.75.2742":"Ah, youth!\\n\\nSometimes I envy you... But I'm too old nowadays to go off on adventures. I retired a long time ago!","content.75.2745":"Hello, little one ! \\nI'm the head of the Mercenaries' Guild. What can I do for you?","content.75.2746":"Ah, that old thing... I did tell her I didn't want it anymore.\\nTake it if you want; it could be useful. I'll explain to you how to use it... By the way: I've never seen you before.\\nAre you a new incarnate ?","content.75.2747":"You've got a rather thick skull, I wonder if... well, anyway...\\nYou'd certainly make a great mercenary, but you still need a little training.\\nWould you like me to teach you how to be stronger ?!","content.75.2748":"Well done, kid ! I like that idea!\\nStart by heading to the Mercenaries' Training Room\\nIt's not far from here. One of my young recruits is already practising there. He's called the Astrub Knight, he'll be able to show you the ropes of being a good mercenary!","content.75.2751":"I see... so Goultard's sent you to help us?\\n\\n*The old Enutrof scrutinizes you. Your Gemlin frowns in annoyance*\\n\\nYes... I suppose you'll do. I'll give you the short version: Some nasty characters are causing trouble in our fine city. They're from Ogrest's Cult, you see.\\n\\nIf I ever cross paths with one of those cultists, they'll have my shovel to deal with!","content.75.2752":"I'm not sure what their end goal is. But what I do know is that they're getting in my way... right here in my own city!\\n\\nWould you like to track them down?","content.75.2753":"Sorry, kid,{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} I'm too busy at the moment. The Guild of Mercenaries is rebuilding the entire town. A vital and significant mission...\\n\\nI already sent the Astrub Knight to investigate, but he hasn't come back yet. If Goultard sent you, that means you're the{[1*]?:} only one{[1*]?:} who can help us. I have confidence in your abilities! \\n\\nAnd if things go sour, avoid fighting them head on!","content.75.2754":"My sincere thanks, kid!{[1*]?:}\\n\\nOne of my mercenaries reports that members of Ogrest's Cult have been spotted several times to the east of the Astrub sewers.","content.75.2767":"Hey, little one! What can old Pappy Pal do for you? \\nThe Mercenaries' Guild has plenty of different missions! \\nA helping hand is always welcome; don't hesitate to take on some of the missions posted on the Mercenary boards.","content.75.2772":"Hmmm...\\nI can feel that you have a lot of potential... I've never met an adventurer like yourself.\\nWith your skills and the training I've given you, you're finally ready to tackle the minions in Ogrest's Cult.","content.75.2773":"Don't rush!\\nStay on your guard, especially with Shreddie.\\nDanger is everywhere.\\nTheir camp is a little to the east of here. \\nTake my Nun Chukapi, I'm sure you'll find it useful.","content.75.2774":"Alas, since Ogrest's Chaos, we've got more sticks and - hoot - stones than actual houses. These - hoot - days, Pappy Pal is in charge of the Guild of Mercenaries and takes an active role in the reconstruction work.","content.75.2786":"Where did you find this compass?!","content.75.2787":"This artifact is priceless! \\nWe Archaosologists are always wanting to discover such remains.","content.75.2788":"I'm not in the habit of sharing that kind of information. But since you already own an artifact, I guess you're{[1*]?:} destined{[1*]?:} to look for more.\\nAt the moment, archaosologists of various nations are searching for ancient relics. They've already started the search and have gathered a lot of information.\\nBut...","content.75.2789":"Except members of Ogrest's Cult, especially their Grambo lackeys, have kept our search from advancing. They're keeping anyone from getting their hands on these relics from the past.","content.75.2790":"And as for your inquiry about an artifact allowing you to cross the void...\\nLet me see, I think I read something one day that could put you on the right track. One of our digs in Sufokia is based on this old scroll. Where did I put it!?","content.75.2791":"Ah, there it is! Take it; you'll get more use out of it, and anyway, I've made copies! Next, you'll have to go see Amakna's Archaosologist. As for me, I still have lots of ancient documents to decipher and analyze.\\nGood luck in your search!","content.75.2792":"What's going on?","content.75.2793":"When we got married, Pappy and I had to exchange a gift to symbolise our union. A dowry, if you will. This little Gemlin is a proof of our love. More or less. But it's much too wild for someone my age.","content.75.2797":"Don't thank me!\\nYou know, one of the mercenary rules states that the easiest missions should be given to beginners. Even the if the reward isn't great, it's good training to help them progress. The strongest mercenary gets the best mission. But don't worry, one day you'll get to my level! ","content.75.2798":"Hey! Are you new?\\nGo on: Train on the dummy in front of you. Let's see what you can do!","content.75.2799":"I can't wait to start the mission! \\nIt's just what I need to warm up my arms! The other one is for you. \\nYou know, one of the mercenary rules states that the easiest missions should be given to beginners. Even the if the reward isn't great, it's good training to help them progress. The strongest mercenary gets the best mission, but don't worry: One day, you'll get to my level! ","content.75.2800":"Not bad at all! \\nThe old timer has skill when searching for new mercenary recruits! You might only be a beginner, and you're no match for me, but you'll make fast progress, just you wait!","content.75.2801":"In fact, if you're up for it, I might have a mission for you.","content.75.2802":"The old guy gave me two.  Let me have a look...\\nOh yeah... The first mission is great: It's right up my street! Wow, and the reward is insanely good!\\nLet's see the second mission! Hmmm... That one is good for you! Here, you can have it!","content.75.2805":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'll like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.2807":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.2808":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.2809":"*grunts* Yet another who hasn't done their research on the important people of Astrub. Don't imagine I've always had this prepubescent four-eyed face! For your information, you should know that I spent my youth running across the world with my friend, Pappy Pal! If my son was here, he'd make fun of you... and probably of me too.","content.75.2810":"Unfortunately, yes... A few years ago, I learned of a most wonderful and legendary object, the Holy Liarg, which is said to give eternal life. Since I didn't want it to fall into the wrong hands, like that foul Brakmarian Lebbocq, I set out to find it.","content.75.2811":"Don't interrupt me, kid. One thing led to another, and eventually I left with some hooded strangers and that vicious Lebbocq. My son, Jenry Hones Jr., ran to my rescue. I was mortally wounded during the adventure. Junior used the Holy Liarg on me to save my life.","content.75.2812":"Well, it did save my skin, but regaining my physical youth was an unexpected side effect. When they saw that, the hooded ones lost all interest in the holy relic, and Lebbocq ran away as he always does when he faces us Hons. What a coward.\\nThat said, I'm not one to complain. A second breath of life to study even more mysteries. What joy!","content.75.2813":"Can I interest you in the Handyman profession?","content.75.2814":"An ax ashore is an ax for war! Or my name isn't Wikan Dewitt!\\nHave you any need of an ax? Don't worry: It's gonna look good!","content.75.2815":"Looks like you were unlucky enough to encounter us! What did you think was going to happen, coming here all by yourself? People often vanish without a trace. If you don't have a reason for being here, I suggest you run off.","content.75.2817":"By Ecaflip! I'd completely forgotten about it!\\nGive my apologies to Pappy Pal, but don't share too much info with Mammy Pal. The adventure Pappy Pal and I shared in our youth is still a thorn in his side. But it was way before they even met! Hehehe!\\nHere's my contribution.","content.75.2818":"Hahahah! That old miser is never caught out. He could at least have the decency to come in person. But anyway, business is goo. Praise be to Sadida and Enutrof for watching over my business. Well, here's my contribution.","content.75.2819":"Usually, I'd challenge you to an arm-wrestling match before I decide if you deserve my contribution. But your arms are so skinny, I might just break them. Let's just say you won. Here's my contribution. And make sure you tell Pappy Pal to send me someone stronger next time! Hahaha!","content.75.2820":"By Mother Eniripsa! How could I forget that? I thought I'd written it down on the...the...the...erm...\\nAnyway, here's my contribution. If you remember, tell Mammy Pal that I have a brand new recipe for eel with cotton candeh cream. It's to die for!","content.75.2821":"Ah! So nice of the people of Astrub to think of us. Very true, I was getting hungry. We still have food, but I'm sick of Amaknian porridge. Your food basket got here just in time!","content.75.2822":"May Jiva's light bring you happiness, my friend. Getting these rations is a real treat. There's way too much here for us Bonta Guards affected to the gates of Astrub. I'll share it with my comrades in the Last Sentinels. May the sun shine down on you.","content.75.2823":"What is this? Have you come to beg? What?! Food for me? Again? I didn't ask for anything; I'm not paying for this! It's... It's free? Great, I'll take it. I can sell any leftovers to the guard who'll be relieving me... Heh heh heh! Now scram; I have stuff to do!","content.75.2824":"Now that is the best news I've heard all day! No, no, of the week! That's right! Call me a snapper, I was getting tired of Puffnando soup. It's good to get some land food once in a while, right? Thank you, kid !","content.75.2825":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'll like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.2828":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.2829":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.2863":"Being a good Citizen means following the laws of one's nation. And respecting the Clan Members' requirements. Following these rules will earn you Citizenship Points (CP).","content.75.2864":"Do you really want to become a Guard for your Nation? \\nOr have you only come to disturb me during my shift?","content.75.2865":"Hmm, I'm looking forward to it, excellent!\\nIf you serve your nation with honor, wherever you are, and if you swear to fight with loyalty and dirty tricks, I'm willing to accept you as an Amaknian Guard.\\nAre you happy with your choice?","content.75.2866":"That's going to cost you dearly, and I won't be there to back you up! If you serve your nation with honor, wherever you are, and if you swear to fight with disloyalty and dirty tricks, I'm willing to accept you as a Brakmarian Guard.\\nAre you happy with your choice?","content.75.2867":"Compared to me, you don't amount to much!\\nIf you serve your nation with honor, wherever you are, and if you swear to fight with loyalty and dirty tricks, I'm willing to accept you as an Bontarian Guard.\\nAre you happy with your choice?","content.75.2868":"Groan, you're making me work so hard! \\nIf you serve your nation with honor, wherever you are, and if you swear to fight with loyalty and dirty tricks, I'm willing to accept you as a Sufokian Guard.\\nAre you happy with your choice?","content.75.2869":"Welcome to our ranks!\\nNow, just open your passport and activate Player versus Player to fight crime.\\nGet to work, on the double!","content.75.2875":"You're not very convincing... I would have preferred to watch you sink to the bottom of the ocean or be tied up in a barrel of explosives...\\nHeehee, anyway; if you accept giving up on the gimmicky nations of the World of Twelve, I'm ready to accept you into the Riktus Clan. That would stop you from going for a swim, hehe! \\nSo, what'll it be?","content.75.2877":"Welcome among us, [#name]!\\nAs a member of the Kiktus, you'll have to rob and destroy everything that isn't within these walls.\\nBut watch out for the Nations' Guards and for the elderly. They can respectively be vicious or clingy.","content.75.2917":"As long as you're loyal to me, I'll answer all your questions!","content.75.2918":"According to may adventurers, the Bermuda Triangle is responsible for the disappearance of many ships.\\nA dream place for us Riktus, as it offers natural and scary protection while we find a place to settle down. \\nOnly the unluckiest of adventurers find our clan instead of happily drowning. Sometimes, we let some join, like we did with you, but most of the time, we let them rot in deep waters, ha ha.","content.75.2919":"\"Pillage\", \"destroy\", \"steal\"... These are words I like to hear in my Clan!\\nKicking an older guard's butt is even funnier than robbing these poor citizens. And don't get me started on that amazing feeling you get when you fill your purse with other people's Kamas!\\nIf you only remember one thing, make it this one: A good Rikus only does to others what he wouldn't want others to do to him!","content.75.2920":"Do you have any other questions for me, [#name]?","content.75.2925":"One clan against the Bontarians, United against the Amaknians, Treacherous to the Sufokians, One clan against the Brakmarians. At the heart of the Bermuda Triangle, One clan to govern them all, One clan to pillage them all, One clan to destroy them all.","content.75.2991":"Hmmm...\\nI'll take your words into consideration. I'll let you think for a while so you can be sure of your choice. It's not something you can decide lightly. Go think about it and come see me when you've made your choice!","content.75.2998":"Rabatuss has volunteered to recruit young adventurers such as yourself. Surely there must be better places than the enemy camp to corrupt the recruits?!\\nThat's why he doesn't drink the potion.","content.75.3009":"The Magik Riktus are a splinter group of ours.\\nOur only link is that we have some common actions.\\nAnd... ! They'll never be better than our clan!","content.75.3048":"The drop wasn't too awful? We're safe now. You must have a lot of questions...","content.75.3049":"It's to be expected. That's a lot of information to take in in one go. You know where I am if you have any more questions. The next step is to go back to the Present Xelorium to contact the dimensional voyager already there. It will be a bumpy trip, so we should get some rest before we head over there. You can use one of the beds in the room.","content.75.3050":"We have to save Pandora, no matter what it costs! They must have taken her to the present. I know a way to get there quickly, but the journey will be a difficult one. And I won't be able to come with you. ","content.75.3051":"You're right: You should have enough energy now. Go to these coordinates. During your absence, I created a dimensional portal. Use it to save some time; it's in my secret room, behind the library. And be careful: I haven't heard from that dimension's Wiseman for a while now...","content.75.3052":"I'm waiting impatiently!","content.75.3054":"I have no idea. I will contact the other Dimensional Voyagers and try to find some information that could help you. We will contact you again when we know more.","content.75.3055":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3057":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3058":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3059":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3061":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3062":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3063":"Well... I am Pandora. And we're in the Xelorium, Xelor's dimension. However, the real question isn't where we are, but when.","content.75.3064":"And yet... She and I are the same person. But we each belong to a different era. I would never have gone there... but it was the only way to prevent Sram from getting his hands on me... well, I mean present me.","content.75.3065":"As I said, we're in the Xelorium. But in this era, Ogrest's Chaos hasn't happened yet. I'm here because Pandora is the key to accessing the Divine Power, and I couldn't let Sram get his hands on her.","content.75.3067":"Yes? What do you want to know?","content.75.3068":"As I said, I can't let Pandora get captured by Sram's henchmen. She is the key to everything. It's me, and therefore her, who are the only ones who can unlock the place where the divine power is hiding.","content.75.3069":"It's actually very simple. You still don't understand? I was the one who hid the Divine Power inside the temple. With the help of the other Dimensional Voyagers, we made sure that the Divine Power would be safe there. That's why, once my task was complete, I erased my own memory. That was how you found me in Astrub.","content.75.3078":"What?! How is that possible?! That shouldn't have happened. You need to find her. There is only one place where Sram could have taken her. We have to get there as soon as possible. But...","content.75.3079":"But access is blocked by a powerful dimensional barrier. To destroy it, you'll have to deactivate three dimensional beacons. I know where they are; I'll come with you. Follow me, quickly!","content.75.3080":"*Kabrok speaks in monotones*\\nWelcome to Kabrok's. We have the world's biggest treasures for an adventurer's greatest pleasures. Everything is for sale here, as long as you can afford it.","content.75.3081":"If you're here to spend a few kamas, you're welcome, my {[1*]?lady:lord}.","content.75.3082":"Dear future clients, here we sell everything you've ever wanted, and more. Our merchandise is guaranteed to be worth your investment. Only the best merchandise for the best clients!\\nFor the latest Sadida sacks, fine Bonta fabrics and other such refined things, see me. For Tofu seed, weapons, and other adventurers' playthings, see Kabrok.","content.75.3083":"Hmph...\\n*Miranda looks at you furiously*\\nFor more than 10 years, Kabrok has devoted his time to wandering the world in order to offer the best merchandise in this shop.\\nHe started with nothing, and one day decided to become a merchant. In just a few days he was the best in all of Kelba Market, and it was thanks to the quality of his merchandise and his talent as a salesman.\\nEven though we may be partners in life and in business, I feel it's right that it's his name on our sign.","content.75.3084":"What a lack of tact toward a lady of my class!\\nThat said, considering the success of our trade, I'll take that as a compliment... ...this time.","content.75.3085":"Oh! It's you! *Miranda changes her tone and becomes colder, harder*\\nYou're late... Let's skip the formalities - today I'm the client. I need you to bring me a VERY important package from Kelba Port.","content.75.3086":"As if I didn't know! Don't interrupt me.\\nThis package is very important. I already sent a fake package before organizing the transport, and the deliveryman was attacked while following the main route.\\nI don't want any risks this time: an alternative route, a strong-armed escort, and the important package hidden with a bunch of similar ones.","content.75.3087":"You want to play the role of the box? You're the strong-armed escort, Iop-brain.\\nThe package must ABSOLUTELY reach me. It's VITAL. The conclusion of SEVERAL YEARS of research. You'll be rewarded in an equal amount to my expectations: NOTHING is more valuable to me than that PACKAGE.","content.75.3088":"Perfect! Go pay a visit to Hadibal Toot. He'll let you know which package you must pick up at the port. Apparently, he's figured out how to avoid any trouble on the route. If you come back here with the package intact, the map is yours.","content.75.3089":"*Miranda throws you a surly look*\\nWhy ask me that? And what are you doing here instead of bringing me my PRECIOUS package? What are you waiting for? Out! Get out of here if you don't have the package and don't want to buy anything. And all the same, you can do your shopping once my package's been delivered!\\nBring me my package RIGHT AWAY! KAAAABROK! Show them the exit!","content.75.3090":"Kabrok! Another for him! Kabrok this, Kabrok that! For the last few years, all anyone talks about is his merchandise!\\nIncredible! He's going to end up buying all the other stalls in the market!","content.75.3091":"Speak to Miranda at \"Kabrok's Shop\". An Enutrof at heart, that darling. But don't tell her that; she might scratch you. Head out on the south road and then head west as soon as possible toward the shop. See you soon I hope, and don't hesitate to look round the market!","content.75.3092":"Dreams, {[1*]?my dear lady:my dear sir}! Adventure! All that's waiting for you, if you follow my maps!\\nLook at these marvels!","content.75.3093":"The package? Oh! You're talking about the package for Miranda?\\n*Hadibal suddenly seems nervous, glancing around furtively. He swallows then focuses on you again*\\nHmm... okay, here's what we'll do...","content.75.3094":"Perfect! First of all, go to Kelba's port. There, a convoy is waiting for you. Here...\\n*Hadibal hands you a messy, scrawled-out sheet representing a path on a map of Kelba*\\nLearn this route by heart. Then destroy this document... COMPLETELY. Miranda's orders.","content.75.3095":"Find me at the port at sunrise. I'll give you more instructions there. Make sure no one follows you!","content.75.3096":"Very well, let's make a few things clear...","content.75.3097":"I'm going to explain everything. It... it's for the good of the market, understand?\\nI...","content.75.3098":"By Enutrof's beard! Are you going to let me finish?\\nFor years, I've maintained a \"protection\" agreement with the Riktus. They don't attack the market, nor our convoys. They stick to the roads of Bonta and the tourists. In exchange, I sometimes give them a heads-up on certain convoys that might interest them.","content.75.3099":"It's rare that Kabrok and Miranda have need of my services. The merchandise must be very special, and of questionable legality. An opportunity to save a convoy of honest merchants, plus the possibility of causing a bit of trouble for those opportunists, Kabrok and Miranda: it's really a golden opportunity and, like the good Enutrof I am, I can't pass it up.","content.75.3100":"Woah! Don't say that name; you'll bring bad luck. It's been more than 10 years that he comes from time to time to attack the market. It has nothing to do with the Riktus or myself. He's completely independent, and my stall is frequently the first to be destroyed.\\nHe's much too powerful for us to fight, and no one knows where he hides. Unless...","content.75.3101":"Uh, well, you see... Well, it's hard for me to say, I took a vacation. Only one or two times! May Enutrof keep me from taking any others, seeing as they cause you to lose profit... Anyway, I was here when the Black Crow attacked the market without me knowing it. When I left to go check my stall, I saw his sinister shadow passing over my head, then heading straight for the cliffs to the west. He must be hiding in that direction!","content.75.3102":"What the... You've been atta... You came across some trouble... Uh...\\nI mean... What are you suggesting?  That I had something to do with it? You think I set up an ambush, is that it?\\nAre you crazy?","content.75.3103":"Are you crazy? HA. DI. BAL. T. Double-O. T. I'm Hadibal Toot. Yes, you already...\\nYou already know it, and you know who I am: THE member of the Kelba Clan, elected by the gods to protect this region. You can't just show up and start accusing people! By Enutrof's scales, how dare you point the finger! All to cover your own incompetence!","content.75.3104":"Wha... What? What the...\\n*Hadibal anxiously studies the proof you've shown him, then whispers*\\nI didn't... Oh, by Enutrof's greedy claws, it's not what you think... We can't speak of it here, do you understand?","content.75.3105":"Not so loud!\\nIt's rather complicated, but I cannot talk about it here... The stalls have ears and if this news gets out, Kelba market and its reputation will be no more. The Black Crow would finally be able to defeat us. And Kabrok would take control of the entire market!\\n*Hadibal, with a teary eye and glistening nose, takes out a map of the island and points to a location on the cliffs to the south*\\nMeet me here *sniff* in a hidden cave at the foot of the cliff, and I will explain EVERYTHING! *sniff*","content.75.3106":"*Kabrok speaks in monotones*\\nWelcome to Kabrok's. We have the world's biggest treasures for an adventurer's greatest pleasures. Everything is for sale here, as long as you can afford it.","content.75.3107":"Calm yourself, friend. Miranda is sorting out some things in the stockroom. Explain everything.","content.75.3108":"Ah... the Black Crow... the worst bandit in all of the World of Twelve. I'm sorry, but there's not much you can do. But don't worry, I'll handle Miranda and her legendary temper. It's not that bad, and...","content.75.3109":"Wha... No, no, no, no! It's far too dangerous. The Black Crow is much too powerful for you. No, you should go home, have a nice meal, have a little sleep, then find some other little adventure. I think that would be the best all round, don't you?","content.75.3110":"Oh! Very good! Tell me: I don't suppose you have any idea where to start looking, right? Not the slightest clue. Nothing. Am I right?\\nHahaha! Well, you just need to look in the right direction. Only three people knew about the convoy, excluding yourself. Miranda, myself... and Hadibal Toot!","content.75.3111":"What a great idea! I'm sure you'll find what you're looking for there. In the meantime, I will try to divert my darling Miranda's attention to more \"down-to-earth\" matters.","content.75.3112":"Nothing? How come? Have you properly scoured the crime scenes, especially where the bandits attacked? That's certainly where it all began.\\nCome on, my little friend. Pretend you are Herlock Shomes, the famous detective!","content.75.3113":"REALLY? Uh... I mean... Congratulations! So, what will you do now? Go and confront the vile felon. Get him to come clean and avenge your tarnished honor! Don't let him wriggle out of it! That old crook will try anything to confuse you: I just know it!","content.75.3114":"Hahaha! He's trying to slip away. I bet he'll be gone or you'll hit a dead end. Or worse, he'll have set a trap...\\nKeep your wits about you!","content.75.3115":"We should talk. There's no point hiding or lying now.","content.75.3116":"Oh, no. He was once my worst enemy... but also my best friend, for several days. I beat him several times and the last time, some ten years ago, it was fatal. But that's another story...\\n*Kabrok goes misty-eyed for a brief moment, then he closes his eyes*\\nPeace be with you, Korvus, and may Osamodas watch over you.","content.75.3117":"Cro-Cave! No! She doesn't know and must never know. If she were to find out... By Osamodas' dragons, that would be the end of me, of our union, our business, EVERYTHING!\\nShe would never recover from it and I don't have any more of that miracle potion that erases the memory. So, there's no way to repair the damage, as I did ten years ago...","content.75.3118":"If I were you, I would avoid... Look, we share some common goals, and I've not hurt a thing since becoming the Black Crow, except maybe a little pride or a wallet.\\nBut if you want to ruin my marriage... Well, I will become the Red Crow from the red of your blood splattered all over my plumage.\\nIf you really want to fight, then make it a fair one: out in the open, in the mountains... But if you don't give away my secret, then in time, I will make sure you are rewarded.","content.75.3119":"Perfect! As soon as I have something in stock that might interest you, I'll offer it to you for an unbeatable price. In the meantime, let's get back to business...","content.75.3121":"It's not THAT simple.  No one was supposed to find that lair. The intrusion followed by the theft of the package, as well as your arrival here, are all signs that I was mistaken.\\nThe people who pulled off this stunt, entering AND leaving with the package, are no simple Twelvians like you and me.","content.75.3122":"... what?","content.75.3123":"Xelor? The Box? So you really have opened the Box! It's amazing! You were gone for several hours!\\nTell me, what do you remember? Do you really possess the power of the gods? Well it sure doesn't look like it...","content.75.3124":"All you had with you when you arrived was this simple crystal and this book. Let's see... Hmmm... Argh!\\nThat's the Chosen One? Who will confront Ogrest? Who will save the people of the World of Twelve? By Xelor!\\nYou have lost most of the power of the gods!","content.75.3125":"It's a catastrophe! I mean... Yes, it's good that you are alive, but it's very bad news for the memory of the gods.\\nLet's think... In the council of the Gods... The box... Your subconscious... The crystal...\\nHmm... Maybe...","content.75.3126":"Well... The part you absorbed is represented by this crystal. Maybe the other fragments that escaped you have also materialized into crystals and are somewhere in the Krosmoz... And probably on the World of Twelve, for the most part!","content.75.3127":"Don't be stupid... I've got an inkling of who the crooks are... But... I can't think of why they would attack another's nest...","content.75.3128":"Well, you see, I've got an inkling of who the crooks are... But... I can't think of why they would attack another's nest...","content.75.3129":"Good, good. In the heights of Kelba, at the top of the rocky peaks, live some intelligent, very little-known creatures. They avoid Twelvians and only come down to the plains on rare occasions.","content.75.3130":"The only times I've managed to see them around here were after my little feathered excursions. They seem to come by when everyone has gone. They collect all the waste and goods left by the merchants.","content.75.3131":"Much more than that. They are humanoids, in the same way that Trools and Bworks are, but they seem closely descended from Crobaks. There is something unusual about them... I sometimes think that their appearance is more due to something like what we go through when devoting ourselves to a god, people like us, Osamodas, Ecaflips, and even Pandawas... Do you see what I mean?","content.75.3132":"That's true, my friend{[1*]?:}, that's true...","content.75.3133":"What?! But why didn't you tell me the first time?! By the horns of Osamodas, you...\\nAh, but yes, it's true. You were totally freaked out{[1*]?:} and making no sense{[1*]?:}, and...","content.75.3134":"Hehehe!\\nActually, I know those creatures well, especially their leader. I haven't spoken with him in several months, however... We should pay them a visit and see what happens. There's just a \"little \"problem... well, especially for you.","content.75.3135":"Hahaha! You're full of vinegar{[1*]?:}, young adventurer{[1*]?:}. Crefish! It's been a long time since I've heard of these urban legends...\\nNo, your problem is that the bridge to reach the peaks has been broken for many years now. And it's not that old cheapo Toot who'll get a kama out to start repairs.","content.75.3136":"Hmmm... The best you can do is to wait a little. Bring me some wood. As for me, I'll take care of hiring crafters. I'll be able to find something to trade for their services among all my junk...","content.75.3142":"Hello, that'll be 30 kamas to pass.","content.75.3143":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3145":"Perfect! It costs 1000 kamas. You'll be able to take on contracts in Kelba. If you want to take on contracts elsewhere, you'll have to find my colleagues there and purchase a license.","content.75.3146":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3147":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3149":"What can I help you with?","content.75.3150":"Kawwww koaw, stranger, I'm Grand Korvishus!","content.75.3156":"Ding Dong! Ah... Shoot! That's the catchphrase of my third cousin by marriage, the daughter of the milestone of the Crackler warrior, on... hmm, whose side is that on? Routa? Or was it Terminus?\\nAnyway, I can't decently steal her catchphrase, she would be mad at me and I don't feel like making her cry, especially because...","content.75.3157":"It should be easy. He's the only Raskaw living alone and who has any interest in what goes on around here. Go and see him, but don't say I sent you. We have had some.... let's say, differences in the past.","content.75.3159":"Mraaaaaooooo... So, my currrious ones, you want to stand up to Ush? You should be carrrreful, you don't want to wake a sleeping Bow Meow... You play with fire, you'll get burrrrned.\\nYou are in my rrrrealm and you don't have a chance...\\nWell?\\nSo, what are you waiting for? Suddenly afraid?\\nBow Meow got your tongue?","content.75.3160":"Oh! A specific map, you say. What type of map? A treasure map perhaps? Or a map leading the way to an ancient forgotten place? All the maps I sell here lead to a treasure of some kind. Satisfaction guaranteed!","content.75.3161":"By Enutrof's millions! The Shushu map! THE Grav'Mar'Av'! Even if I had that map, I wouldn't sell it, or at least I might, but for a price that would bring tears to your eyes. It breaks my heart, but for such a special and unique map, you'll have to go somewhere else.","content.75.3162":"A Shushu is a demon, an evil being that serves Rushu, the Shushu King. Shushus normally reside in their own dimension, the Shustuft Crust, at the edge of Externam. Most rare Shushus who have tried to invade our world have been captured by powerful warriors and trapped in magical objects.\\nThese items bestow incredible power on their Guardians. But watch out: Trapped Shushus are still active and harmful. They constantly try to deceive their Guardians so they can escape their physical prison.","content.75.3163":"Ah...\\nWell... You see, about ten years ago, once I'd left adventuring behind me, three great things... err, two great things happened: I decided to sell the treasures I'd collected during my travels, and I met Miranda.\\nI came here to Kelba with a simple caravan. I met Miranda on the way and we made the journey together.\\nIt turned out that I was a talented merchant and my high-quality products were popular with customers. Well, one thing led to another, and I was eventually able to invest in this store, which Miranda and I renovated. Then, once I'd built up enough courage, I asked for the hand of my beautiful and indomitable Ecaflip. She accepted, and thus started my new big adventure. But that is another story.\\nBasically, I am a good trader, but Miranda is the one with the business brains. The name is just a matter of ownership and reputation - the reputation of myself and my merchandise.","content.75.3165":"Welcome, I am Etnop, the Meridia of Eggs. \\nEggs are everything to me. \\nWhat do you want now?","content.75.3166":"You must defeat a boss in the dungeon of your choice at the dungeon level. You may need to adjust your level. For example, the Gobball dungeon requires level 20 at most. By the way, hordes of Wodents have been trying to steal my eggs. They can be found near Astrub, and have some really nice loot. You should go and see them too!","content.75.3168":"Shhh! Not so loud! Miranda doesn't know and must never know. If she were to find out... By Osamodas' dragons, that would be the end of me, of our union, our business, EVERYTHING!\\nShe would never recover from it and I don't have any more of that miracle potion that erases the memory. So, there's no way to repair the damage, as I did ten years ago...","content.75.3169":"Yes. The Black Crow is none other than Kabrok the Shopkeeper!\\nLucky for you that you found me unmasked, otherwise I would have given you a good thrashing. I was a legendary adventurer in my time.\\nBut that is all far behind me now.","content.75.3170":"Ha! It's that wretched artifact! For months, she's thought of nothing but completing her Ecaflip artifact collection. I'm referring of course to the god Ecaflip!\\nUntil recently she has only found some small, uninteresting pieces, probably fakes. But ever since she saw the Ecaflip's Paws in that scoundrel Kerub's shop, she's been obsessed, as if she's hypnotized. Watching her in front of that item, I realized it was a genuine, authentic, divine artifact.","content.75.3171":"Well, it's rather obvious. The Ecaflip Paws are making Miranda crazy, worse than Bow Meow Grass. She is obsessed with her treasure, her precious, her artifact.\\nMy beautiful and feisty wife has lost interest in our business and become totally paranoid. I'm afraid her madness will lead her to uncover my secret and then I'll lose her.\\nOh! My aging heart could not bear such separation.\\nI simply had to get that horror away from her, and who better than the Black Crow to carry out such a heinous task.","content.75.3172":"A Riktus Clan Petsmount harness? That would be 2,000 kamas from you to me. If you want to proudly display the colors of our good Riktus Clan, I will give you a Patriotic Petsmount Token so you can choose the harness you want in our ship's hold.","content.75.3173":"Here, among the rocky peaks, live intelligent and poorly understood creatures. They avoid Twelvians and only come down to the plains on rare occasions. The only times I have managed to see them in the moors have been after my little feathered excursions.","content.75.3174":" They seem to come by when everyone has gone. They collect all the waste and goods left by the merchants. They are humanoids, in the same way that Trools and Bworks are, but they seem more descended from Crobaks. And intelligent.","content.75.3175":"No... There is something unusual about them. I sometimes think that their appearance is more due to something like what we go through when devoting ourselves to a god, people like us, Osamodas, Ecaflips, and even Pandawas... Do you see what I mean?","content.75.3176":"Uh... What's the problem? Are you part Bwork or whaaat? You can speak to me normally, you know... Anyway, you waaant information, is that it? Maybe I caaan help you, for a price of caaawrse. Everything is negotiable with us Raskaws, as long you have something to trade, something we waaant.","content.75.3177":"Well, it's pretty simple. It is customary that our young fly far from the nest until fully grown, so they can build their kawwracter. They return once they are ready to offer their loot to the Grand Orrok. But some of the little devils have taken my belongings, which is just wrong.","content.75.3178":"You're a quick learner for someone paaarrt Bwork, kakakak! Bring me three crates from the young Raskaw camps strewn around the Kreublos to the south and east. But caaaaareful! Only three! Any more would be theft, and we demand justice here: Maarrrk my words.","content.75.3179":"You really are part Bwork, kakakak! Bring me three crates from the young Raskaw camps strewn around the Kreublos to the south and east. But caaaaareful! Only three! Any more would be theft, and we demand justice here: Maarrrk my words.","content.75.3180":"Ah! Perfect! Now, listen: a little while ago, I saw a group of grubby-looking Raskaws pass through. They seemed vacant, almost possessed. They were heading toward Rakkao, our main village, where the Grand Orrok presides. They must have taken their treasure to the warehouse.","content.75.3181":"Cross the bridge on the other side of the market. I have a hideout in a cave not far from there. You can't miss it.","content.75.3182":"Oh yes! It is, but don't worry. Oh yes! It is, but don't worry. On the side of the building, there is a secret door that you can use without anyone spotting you. However, once you'aaare inside, watch out for guaaarrd patrols.","content.75.3183":"Kaawwww! I don't waaant to talk about that. It's... it's too painful. So many shaaattered dreams, so many hopes daaaashed, so many feathers plucked out. It's ancient history and I just want to forget, even if I cannot...","content.75.3184":"Kawwkoaa! It's a very old story, stranger. And I don't trust you enough to tell it to you. All I will say is that I used to be the Grand Orrok of our village, but I was beaten and baaanished by the current Grand Orrok.","content.75.3185":"Kawwwkakakaw! Listen, if you manage to give the new Grand Orrok a good plucking, I might be inclined to tell you the tale...","content.75.3186":"Kaaaawwwkaw! Not A woman... MY woman. I hope you gave her a good spanking, kakakak...\\nNow that you have cleared my name, I know I caaan trust you. If you waaaant, I can tell you my story.","content.75.3187":"Kakakak! It's a long story but I'll try to make it short. You seem to be in a hurry. It all started about fifteen years ago, when the one you kawwwwl the Black Crow came to these parts. The other Raskaws were afraid.","content.75.3188":"No, to me, this kawwwwreature was a divine messenger, a celestial being come to spread the word. At first, he was quite aggressive. But by paying homage to him and making offerings, he became more welcoming. But there was always a language barrier.","content.75.3189":"Well, each time I paid them a visit and gave an offering, I learned new words. After a few years, I knew enough to teach the other Raskaws. But as they are so isolated and since I am no longer Grand Orrok, they no longer learn anything.","content.75.3194":"So, are you searching for the ultimate thrill? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3195":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3197":"Perfect! It costs 1000 kamas. You'll be able to take on contracts in Forfut. If you want to take on contracts elsewhere, you'll have to find my colleagues there and purchase a license.","content.75.3198":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3199":"You were able to defeat the members of Ogrest's Cult in the sewer temple?!","content.75.3200":"Congratulations little one! \\nI knew you could do it! You have the potential to become a great adventurer!\\nGood thing you were there to heal the Knight; he owes you!","content.75.3201":"The{[1*]?: }hero{[1*]?:} of the prophecy... I also had that impression the first time we met{[1*]?:}. I wouldn't say you ARE the{[1*]?:} hero{[1*]?:}, but I'm sure you could become the hero. \\nWhat did this... \"Ullu\" tell you?","content.75.3202":"Mount Zinit! It's a very dangerous place... \\nIn my opinion, the best way to get to the cursed island would be aboard the Hullcatz's \"The Black Purr\". \\nThey're in Astrub, near the port to the east.\\nGo talk to them, but tell Master Bossowl you're leaving beforehand; he'll have some precious advice to give you, because Mount Zinit is nothing like the challenges you've faced so far!","content.75.3203":"Oh, I nearly forgot! Take this, you've earned it.\\nIt's not much, but you're family now, so...!\\nCome back and visit whenever you want. And remember to say goodbye to Mammy. Apparently, she wanted to tell you something.","content.75.3206":"Hey, I remember you!\\nI see you've become a renowned hero{[1*]?ine:}!\\nWelcome aboard the \"The Black Purr\", matey!\\nSoon as you be feelin' ready to leave for Mount Zinit, give the signal and we'll pull up anchor!","content.75.3207":"Hey, I remember you, deckhand!\\nYou coming for Mount Zinit?","content.75.3212":"You're gonna have to go it on foot.\\nYou ready to cross the Mount Zinit Reefs?\\nIf you're wantin' to go back t' Astrub, you just gotta ask.","content.75.3217":"The artifacts... I think you should go see my old friend, the archaosologist Jenry Hones Sr. \\nHe's in the Temple of Scriptures, just outside the city. I'll mark it on your map. I'm certain he can help you.","content.75.3219":"ooo...aaa... Hmmm...\\nCan I be of some use to you?","content.75.3224":"Come back and see me when you've accomplished all the tasks I've given you.","content.75.3225":"Hey! Have you come to ask me for an autograph?\\nYou know, I'm the most popular hunter this year. I won't tell you about all the visitors I get each day.","content.75.3226":"Oh! You're looking for the famous artifact that's supposed to be able to call a dragon! I understand better now why Mr. Hones Senior sent you to see me. At the moment, we archaosologists are all working together on one immense work site.","content.75.3227":"Like I told you, you need three items to serve as the key: Orichalcums. An Orichalcum is a small bead made of a very rare and precious ancient metal with mysterious properties. The last traces in history of this metal being forged date from the Primitive Age, well before the Age of Dofus.\\nI've conducted a lot of research, and the information I was able to collect is very interesting!","content.75.3228":"Oh no! We haven't gotten our hands on any sort of artifact. However we have discovered a very old sunken temple underneath a Sufokian island. The door of the temple was slightly ajar and inside there's a fresco identical to the one on the scroll Jenry Senior gave you.","content.75.3229":"You can't go there just like that!\\nThe sunken temple is a grand dig site, closed to the public. We're trying to do our best to make sure the site isn't ravaged by inexperienced hands. Only an Honorary Archaosologist{[1*]?:} can get the required authorization.","content.75.3230":"I can put you through various archaosological tests. If you succeed, you'll officially become an{[1*]?:} Honorary Archaosologist.","content.75.3252":"Oh! You passed the tests perfectly! I didn't think you were capable of doing everything I asked you to do so quickly and ably.","content.75.3253":"Yes, we'll be able to go to Sufokia's big dig site.","content.75.3254":"Here is your well-deserved title!\\nCome back and speak to me when you're ready to go!","content.75.3265":"The receptacles on the door serve as a sort of lock. We need three items to work as the key. I've done a lot of research: The leads I've worked out should be quite interesting! But we'll talk more of that later. I still need to verify a few things...","content.75.3266":"This temple seems completely sunk. If we manage to open this door, I hope we'll find a dry passage to explore the corridors and rooms of this ancient sacred place.","content.75.3267":"This temple seems completely sunk. If we manage to open this door, I hope we'll find a dry passage to explore the corridors and rooms of this ancient sacred place.","content.75.3268":"I'll have to call in a few favors to get my hands on the elements we'll need to open this door. The delivery charge will be yours!\\nI don't have any more information for you. Now go! ","content.75.3269":"Listen, you spoke way too long with Hones, to be honest. I also have good information. I can tell you that it makes my heart ache to give it to you freely... But I can't lose face against Jenry. I already had an Orichalcum in my hands!","content.75.3270":"Psshtt. Go on, I'm not going to be spotted!\\nThe information obtained is pretty interesting this time. Nothing more to do than just lend an ear... Can you see me, of all people, dirtying my hands with arkaeolitic work!?","content.75.3271":"I loooooooooove this architecture! Everything's done in the ancient Sufokian style. What I wouldn't give to live in that era! This temple must be magnificent!","content.75.3272":"According to my sources, the hunter Magnum Bairefute has an item like those Orichalcums that we're looking for.","content.75.3273":"Magnum Bairefute can be found in the Amakna Capital, in the Guild of Hunters' Camp.\\nI hope he will indulge us and give us something that may be one of the Orichalcums.","content.75.3274":"That's true. I'm sure I crossed a similar item in my research, a few months ago. But I can't remember what it was...\\nListen - check out other leads, and on my side I'll try to concentrate and remember, and take a look back at my old research. I should be able to track down this supposed Orichalcum. As soon as I have any new information, I'll let you know through my father, at the Temple of Scriptures.\\nWhat do you say?","content.75.3275":"Ah, you want to talk about my good luck charm. I found it during an exhausting mission to Sufokia and it definitely brought me luck. I find it completely intriguing!\\nIs that what you're looking for?","content.75.3276":"Well... I'd be ready to give it to you and the Archaosologists... but not for free.","content.75.3277":"At the moment, we have two problems: First of all, mysterious entities have taken control of the Puddlies. Then some \"nocturnal creatures\" have attacked the people in the area.\\nThe Puddlies are blocking access to a well, far to the east. It's surprising, because Puddlies are normally pretty inoffensive creatures. \\nAs for the \"nocturnal creatures\" they appear in the Ogre's Salt Lakes, nearby to the south, attacking people unfortunate enough to be walking in the area.\\nNo one here wants to take care of it because they don't believe in such things.\\nSo, it's an opportunity for you to prove to me that you're a good hunter that I can trust.","content.75.3278":"What?! Larvae possessed by spectres? You must be dreaming - that's not possible. I'm going to act as if you didn't tell me anything. I'm going to give you another mission: some larvae have gone crazy in the fields, but we don't know why. We found a strange pile of wool where it seems they established their nest, at the old sheep pen to the south of the region. Take care of that and I'll take your efforts into consideration.","content.75.3279":"A Weakened Spectral Arachnee?! But what are you talking about? You haven't seemed very clear since I met you. But thanks; the problem seems resolved.\\nI'd like you to accomplish one final mission though: Something important, and I'd be ready to reward you with my good luck charm!","content.75.3280":"I'll need rockwool. It's a bit difficult to harvest, because its owner is not at all docile!\\nAs you can see, my workers are rather few, and we have a lot to do in order to fill the orders for parts given to us by our scientific colleagues. And not to mention that we need to replant as much as we harvest. Between the Gobballs and the Wild Plants, and the occasional Scarecroolates, we have our hands full.\\nI need valiant adventurers to harvest this unique tuft of Rockwool from Bovis.\\nBovis is a once-domesticated Gobball believed lost, or eaten by Boowolves, by its shepherd. But decades later, a young adventurer exploring a dungeon quite far to the south of here came nose-to-nose with a plump Gobball covered in abundant wool.\\nHaving lived all this time underground, eating mushrooms and eating element-rich mud, he developed a coat abundantly encrusted with rare minerals.\\nI need to deliver a tuft of this wool to the Great Rationalist of Otomai's Disciples.\\nThe Great Rationalist is the most educated and revered scientomage of all Otomai's Disciples, our master! You understand, then, why this mission is so important.","content.75.3281":"Oh! Thank you for the rockwool! You didn't have much difficulty taming Bovis. I think I can trust you: I'm going to give you my good luck charm. But please take care of it!","content.75.3282":"Rather, it strongly resembles an Orichalcum if we listen to the descriptions in the old scrolls. I can't definitively confirm it - you must go see Jenry Hones, Sr. He'll know for sure if this old relic is one of the Orichalcums we're looking for!","content.75.3283":"Let me see that! Hmmm... That color...","content.75.3284":"Hmmm... *whispers something about the heat given off by the metal*\\nHmmmmmmmm... Yes, it would be good...\\nHmmmmmmmmmmm... *murmurs indistinctly while leafing through an old dirt-covered volume that reeks of compost*","content.75.3285":"Very well.\\nWith all my knowledge, I can assure you that this is indeed an authentic Orichalcum!","content.75.3286":"Ahoy adventurer, the tax has been paid to the Guild of Hunters. The archmonster has therefore been freed! It will only be available for a short time.\\n\\nWould you like to start the fight?","content.75.3287":"Very good!\\nYour title of Honorary Archaosologist gives you the authority to visit, but please, touch nothing!\\nThe archaosologists of the other nations are present - you must make a good impression, for the honor of your nation.","content.75.3293":"Calm down! I don't have it anymore. How should I say this? I'm a renowned scientist, and my finds are worth their weight in gold. The greatest collectors snatch up my discoveries, and my competitors' when they can be provided. And this little metal sphere is already destined for a sucke... a buyer, and has been for years.\\nGive me a bit of time, I'll find you the name of the buyer. Don't mention it to others; it might make trou... They might be jealous that I was lucky enough to hold an Orichalcum bead in my hand!\\nOtherwise, I noticed that Laura Craft seemed rather pensive. Maybe she has something for you? Nothing as useful as me, I hope...","content.75.3295":"Hey adventurer, the bowl is not yet full! Therefore, it's not possible to fight the archmonster for the moment.\\nThe entirety of the tax must be paid to the Guild of Hunters to free the monster for one hour.","content.75.3297":"Ouk ouk ouk","content.75.3298":"Welcome to Moon Island, little one.\\nYou're brave, that much is obvious. Be careful. Our dear little island is full of resources, but isn't what it used to be... I'd advise against journeying outside the Kanniball village, unless you want to end up in the ground like a root.","content.75.3299":"I'm Botan Ficus, the spiritual leader of this village. But don't go thinking it's a position of power. Being the spiritual chief means being completely devoted, for the good of the tribe.\\nLike everyone here, I'm a Kanniball. We're the last Sadidas who respect the ancestral traditions, protecting this sanctuary from the madness of the world.","content.75.3300":"Our Kanniball village has been here for hundreds of years. Our most distant ancestors were waiting for the prophesied coming of a being with the power of Breath, who was no other than Moon. Since then, they worship him like a god.\\nBy the way, a big celebration in honor of Moon will be held soon. I strongly suggest you come!\\nHowever, not everything's rosy here. Certain aggressive and ambitious Kanniballs are trying to take power, like the vicious Saul the Tortuous. I still have enough influence to counter his plans, but he's gaining supporters every day.","content.75.3301":"As it's name suggests, this island is home to our god: Moon!\\nHis boldness is only equaled by the splendor of our island - his temperament is as hot as the sand of our beaches and his spirit is the source of inspiration for our entire civilisation. But that's not all...","content.75.3302":"There are numerous treasures in the archipelago, but they're guarded by creatures much more dangerous than simple Tropikokos. Start proving yourself by finishing off Koko the Nutt, in Tropickle Dungeon, just off the beach.","content.75.3303":"Moon has always protected us in our most difficult moments. Recently, the incidents have been multiplying, and powerful monsters and individuals have been causing trouble in the village. We were overwhelmed, near defeat. That's when Moon, in his omnipotence, let the dark side of his power loose on our adversaries.\\nBefore we even had time to recover the stolen treasures, the troublemakers found themselves exiled at the top of sacred totems, symbols of the our great protector's power.\\nIf you manage to climb up and defeat these crooks, the treasures they took will be yours!","content.75.3304":"Calm down, little one! Have an herbal tea. It's not that simple. You're not going to be able to challenge Moon. Moon will come to find you when he thinks you're a worthy adversary.\\nProving yourself in our dungeon would be a good place to start... Come back and see me when you've succeeded.","content.75.3305":"The Darkli Moon that you confronted is only a fraction of the alter ego of our great Moon.\\nHe live lives beyond the Great Door, to the north. To open it, we must go through a grand ritual, that we practice on rare occasions.\\nThe next ritual won't be for a little bit. Come back and see me when we start the festivities.","content.75.3306":"Ahem... What are you doing here?\\nDid you get lost? Let me show you where the exit is.","content.75.3307":"Very well, I'll tell you some more. But first of all, I must warn you: there are fishy things happening at the moment... I here rumors in the hallways. I've even come upon conversations that were to say the least strange, in the library in the evening.","content.75.3308":"Y-y-you... Not so fast, my {[1*]?girl:boy}! Before revealing all the secrets to you, we have to be sure that you're able to grasp the most elementary of concepts. So start by putting away the crates that are lying around in the library, and we'll then decide.","content.75.3309":"Good day to you, and welcome to Rok Island!\\nYou're in the Registration and Certification of Skills Office of the Huppermagic School!\\nWhat can I do for you?","content.75.3310":"Very well, very well, I'll make good note of your request... But you should know that we don't open the school gates to any old simpleton. To complete your enrollment, I'm going to submit you to a first test. It's very simple, well, if you have the necessary learning abilities... You need to find three objects we scattered downstairs in the school: a Blue-toned Pearl, some Precious Powder, and a note that we leave especially for novices.","content.75.3311":"Hi! I'm Janine Soleau, Professor of Botanics. You should know that botanics is a story of balance, just like the other subjects taught here... Except that it's a more diversified, noble and passionate subject.","content.75.3312":"I have a test for you. You see the last seedling to have bloomed over there in the corner? I need you to harvest it.\\nBut be careful: the plants don't seem to like it when novices start poking around in there, and will defend it fiercely!","content.75.3313":"There is a synergy between plants, a very close link which binds them together. Once more, it's all about equilibrium: the strong plants defend the weak... right from when they're seedlings. That explains why plants react violently when a novice seems to be getting too close to the seeds at the bottom. Their motion is guided by the novice's movement, which they imitate each in their own way, for maximum effectiveness.","content.75.3314":"Oh, okay then. It seems you got by quite easily with my young plants. The next step consists of going into the field! You will indeed have to go up against real wild plants, and they won't let you get away with anything. Go now to the Sureberry Fields dungeon in Amakna: Fearlessly face the onslaught of the Evil Dandelions and Demonic Roses, and triumph over the terrible Carnivorous Plant. Then come back and tell me about your adventure.","content.75.3315":"Absolutely marvelous...\\nPerfectly admirable...\\nIncredibly fantastic...\\nOh, sorry, didn't see you there. I was talking to my lovely Adenioma, just born! Isn't she magnificent...?\\nYou were saying? You've beaten the Carnivorous Plant? Ah yes, good good. Congratulations: You've passed the test. It seems you have what it takes... Well maybe, just maybe! Although... No, probably not with that shocked look on your face. Anyone would think you'd fallen out of the sky!","content.75.3316":"Hey there, {[1*]?little girl:little guy}, calm down. Don't go over the top. Even though I'm very nice, I can still get angry!\\nCome on, it probably no big deal. It was probably a few of your friends who wanted to tease you a bit, don't you think? That happens a lot in schools, you know. Plus you don't look to be in a bad way. Did you get by okay or did you take a beating?","content.75.3317":"Oh you poor thing. Now you know why we don't want any weaklings at the Huppermagic School. They're far too adept at getting into trouble and bothering the teachers, which costs precious time. Come back and tell me if you have the same problem again.","content.75.3318":"Well there we go: no worries in that case!\\nI'm glad to see you can manage on your own, just like one of the big {[1*]?girls:boys}. You have potential, little one.","content.75.3319":"Uhh... I may be able to help you. In the past, students asked me to provide them with a potion which was guaranteed to repel intruders, but I don't have the ingredients to make it any more... You'll need to get some flax flowers from a herbalist and bring them to me.","content.75.3320":"Oh, I expected no less of you! I congratulate you all the same. It's always nice to see a youngster succeed brilliantly... But do not rest upon your laurels just yet: challenges of a whole nother difficulty are waiting for you right now!\\n\\nDon't hesitate to attend the free lessons in the Study Room, to visit Professor Soleau in the Greenhouse, to meditate in the Central Garden, and to take a well-deserved break in the dormitories at the end of the day.","content.75.3321":"As it happens, I have already prepared it for you, and here it is. My heartfelt congratulations! But be warned: the second year of studies will be more complicated. That's why we require a minimum level of 80 to start it. When you're ready, go and see Hu-Sed-Tusei-Bald in the library upstairs, and he'll take over for your the next part of your studies.","content.75.3322":"Basically, I think some serious events are going on. I don't know who's behind it all, but I advise you not to be over-zealous in public, so as not to cause yourself problems. Whoever's pulling the strings surely isn't a child of heart, and won't hesitate to eliminate any threats. For now, follow your lessons to the letter, and above all go unnoticed.","content.75.3323":"That's the right attitude, my {[1*]?girl:boy}! As you're, err,  insignificant... to them... you could possibly go unseen. I'd like you to investigate for me. Every time I go somewhere, things have been moved around, as if someone rummaged around just after I came by... like in the Store Room upstairs next to the swimming pool. I put one of my books down in there with an invisible security mechanism to si if anyone puts their hands on it. Don't hesitate to go there and see if you can catch the crooks red-handed. What's more, you'll need to bring me a very precious artifact that I hid in the Equipment Room's basement. But there was a leak, and I haven't been able to go back and get it. While going via the Equipment Room, don't hesitate to ask Thomass Edwindu, our Master of Equipment, if he needs any help. He can equip you to face the dangers that await.","content.75.3324":"Greetings!\\nWhat brings you to my Crafting Workshop?","content.75.3325":"Well, equip you to defend yourself, you say? Within our walls, even the darkest of creatures can do nothing. What's more, second year students are not allowed to have their own weapons. But I can probably provide you with a temporary form of defense. If you want to get it, you'll have to bring me some resources. These damned final year students have reduced my stocks to nothing.","content.75.3326":"That's my good deed for the day! Now, you'll have to work on the first steps of making your weapon yourself. I'll show you how to go about it. It's a basic test, which blends thought and movement. It will take place in this room, because the equipment made here is drawn on the floor before being materialized.","content.75.3327":"As you probably noticed, the slabs on the ground depict a sword. You're no doubt aware that good raw materials are important when making a quality weapon, and you took care of that aspect with vigor. You must also be aware that making them is quite complex, and that it requires attention to detail, great knowledge and countless iterations, at the same time. But that's not all: a well-designed weapon will be more effective in every situation. That's why the first step consists of recreating the diagram of your weapon, already deformed, on the Fiftinepuzle.","content.75.3328":"Already? I've been sick of repeating myself for all these years that the diagram is too easy... Well... It may not be the ultimate weapon for now, but it's the only type of weapon that a student in your year is allowed to use. Be careful, this blade doesn't glow and doesn't turn blue when enemies are nearby!","content.75.3329":"Bring me the following resources:\\n5 rustic handles, and\\n30 korals.\\nAs for the rest, I think I have everything I need at my disposal.","content.75.3330":"Hello, young adventurer. What can I do for you?","content.75.3332":"Yes, that's right! It wasn't easy. But to continue my research, I'm going to need your help right here, at the Immaterial University of Bonta!","content.75.3333":"Hahaha! I'll never get tired of seeing people's faces when I tell them that! This is only an access point. The University is someplace far away, under the Huppermages' protection. When you're ready to leave, talk to me again!","content.75.3334":"Are you sure you want to go to the Immaterial University of Bonta?","content.75.3335":"Hey there! I hope the University is to your liking.","content.75.3336":"There you go again with your harebrained ideas, each one worse than the last! Breathing underwater? What a funny idea! That being said... Nothing could be simpler: one of our champions demonstrated it recently, by being able to breathe underwater for over an hour!","content.75.3337":"He used the Branchy-Flower! Oh, what a brilliant idea. Trust me when I say I'm proud, because it's me who taught him everything! He was one hell of a kid when he arrived, but I turned him in to one of our best Huppermages. Since then, his feats have been stacking up. I still remember the day I was told how he managed to beat his opponents in hand-to-hand combat during a terrible fight. He has a bleeding heart for the oppressed. After having started with quietly doing in a few Snow Boohemoths, he was pinned to the ground by a shock which terrified his two helpless spectators. With the two miraculously cured spectators watching, a look of despair in their eyes, uncertain of what was going to happen, my champion got straight back up, with all his muscles flexing. A call to violence, deep down within him, reverberated like a strange euphoric symphony. He immersed himself in it up to his eyeballs, awaking the enthusiasm of a fighter in him, who is sure to fight for a just cause. Secluded in his inner tower, surrounded by an isle of light, the ground seemed to open up beneath his feet as he felled the woefully famous Yech'Ti. In short, an astounding person... Why did you come here again?","content.75.3338":"It's a very simple recipe!\\nAll you need to do is grind up 50 edelweiss with 15 Arachnee legs, and then simmer all that with...","content.75.3339":"You have done well. Credit must be given where credit is due, so well done! I'll be able to make Branchy-Flower for a whole team! Here's a sample which will let you get through the flooded path.","content.75.3340":"It really does feels better when the library is nice and tidy.\\nAlbeit still with a bit of dust here and there... Are you here to sort it out?","content.75.3341":"Did you find the chest? Did you bring back what it contained? It's very important.","content.75.3342":"It's a catastrophe!!! It's worse than I feared, our enemies must have gotten there before us.\\nThey must have a big head start. Don't waste time, go back and investigate!","content.75.3343":"Hahaha! I never said the Orichalcum was here. But you'll be able to help me pick up its scent thanks to the greatest tool in archaosology!","content.75.3344":"Don't be ridiculous! I'm talking about books, of course. Did you know that 70% of archaosology is done in the library?","content.75.3345":"Of course. The first step consists of getting a volume of the Spherolithic Encyclopedia. It must be in the library, just behind this door. Go and find it. In the meantime, I'll write up my notes. I'll tell you more as soon as I have the Encyclopedia in my hands!","content.75.3346":"Excellent! Let's see... Hmmm... \\n*Jenry quickly flicks through the book several times, reading a paragraph here and there throughout the pages*\\nYes... Oh! Keep going... Ah! Perfect!","content.75.3347":"Huh... what? No, not yet, but I've found an interesting lead, which refers to another book, but...","content.75.3348":"Actually, not at all! A few hours ago, I was talking to a colleague who told me he was going to deliver a lecture using the very book we need for reference. He's a really big name in his field, and I don't think he really needs the document...","content.75.3349":"Actually, you're going to pay a visit to the amphitheater and relieve the good professor of that dusty old book he doesn't need, right in the middle of his lesson. It must be on his desk. As for me, I'll stand watch so no one goes disturbing you.","content.75.3350":"Great! I trust you had no problems. Now I have to go and correlate my annotations from the Encyclopedia with the contents of the Compendium...\\n*Jenry returns to flicking through the two volumes intensely, comparing his notes and hastily jotting down a few words*","content.75.3351":"Holy Feca's Shield! I found something. It seems that the old model of the Bontarian Gobbowl Champions' Cup contained a sphere of unknown metal, but...","content.75.3352":"Not so fast, young Gobball! This model of cup dates back several hundred years, long before Ogrest's Chaos. We'll have to locate the cup before rushing in head first. So...","content.75.3353":"Come on, get a move on. The objective isn't far off now. Show me the Archaosologist in you! Go back to the library, and bring me the Gobbowlium Codex, the biggest sports almanac of all time. It references every Gobbowl match since the sport was created.","content.75.3354":"What?! But... By the gods! What about the Library?","content.75.3355":"Our beautiful library... Well...\\nLet's refocus. Most of the books that were available in there were copies of old documents found in the Old Bonta's Ruins. The one that was destroyed and partially buried during Ogrest's Chaos.","content.75.3356":"We don't have any way to move and look after such old documents, especially after their prolonged exposure to the magic of Ogrest's tears. Which means that the original copy must still be in the Library of the Old Bonta Ruins! Let's go there!","content.75.3357":"We've got no time to lose! So, we're going to use one of the Huppermages' Elemental Portals, powered by the Quadramental Breeze. Go back down this corridor and take the second door on your right. I'll meet your at the ruins after getting my equipment!\\n Jump through the aquatic portal.","content.75.3358":"Hello adventurer!\\nTempted by an exhilarating adventure? Then go to the Huppermage School!\\nThere, you'll be able to learn new spells and maybe, just maybe, become a member of the Huppermage Brotherhood!","content.75.3359":"At the Huppermage School, you'll have the incredible chance to be educated by our most eminent scholars, and to mix with the greatest intellectuals the World of Twelve has ever seen.\\nTo go there, you just have to get on the platform and tell me when you're ready.","content.75.3360":"Hahaha! We say Huppermage. H.U.P.P.E.R.M.A.G.E.\\nHuppermages. Great scientomages, masters in the art of weaving their spells from the Quadramental Breeze. They had disappeared at the time of Ogrest's Chaos.","content.75.3361":"When they returned several years after the start of the Chaos, they contacted Bonta. Some time later, they helped found the Immaterial University of Bonta, right here at the foot of their prestigious school, almost 130 years ago. All of the greatest scientists in the World of Twelve come here at least once, either as a student, professor or guest.","content.75.3362":"So, adventurer{[1*]?:}, are you ready{[1*]?:} for the most heart-pounding 30% of archaosology?","content.75.3363":"We must get the Gobbowlium Codex from the Old Bonta Library, here in these ruins.","content.75.3364":"There you are, adventurer!\\nAlready feel like going back to the flatlands?\\nGet on the platform and tell me when you're ready!","content.75.3365":"The Codex taught us that the last time the cup containing the precious metal sphere was put back into play, it was Khan Karkass's team who won the match. Khan was a champion of the Dofus Age, over 300 years ago.","content.75.3366":"Most great champions are buried with their most handsome trophy. Khan's tomb must be someplace in Old Bonta Cemetery, here in these ruins.","content.75.3367":"You want to measure up to me? You'll have to do the first 3 tests!","content.75.3368":"You have done well!\\nAs for me, I've been developing my theory about the Hoodlums.","content.75.3369":"From my research, I'm starting to get a better view of the mystery surrounding them. But do take into account the fact that there are still things I don't know about them, and I still have to find out about this famous Hoodfella, then analyze the details you'll observe in the Zeppelantern. Now that I've nuanced my words enough, listen closely...","content.75.3370":"In my opinion, they could be Huppermages who have rejected our core values, who are focusing on the study of the magic of the World of Twelve classes. But worse still, I think they have a set purpose, and that they're doing this on the orders of someone far higher up than Hoodfella... For what little I know, it could be one of our own...","content.75.3371":"That remains to be discovered... But everything is linked, I'm certain of it. The school's downfall, the Hoodlums' strange doings, the attacks on students... They all have the same cause and result. We must find who's behind it all and stop them as soon as possible.","content.75.3372":"Well, you were fast this year. Well done! Let me see where I put your papers, one moment... No, they're not here... Not there either... Oh, there they are! I'll add my signature, and... done.\\nI've been told about difficulties in the third year of study. So I have been instructed not to let you start before you reach level 130.","content.75.3373":"I've been told about your feats this year! Well done, champion. We've decided to spare you from the traditional challenges: here are your papers.\\nAll that's left to do now is to gain maturity, to be ready to devote your life to it, and we reckon you'll be worthy to start studying the Quadramental Breeze and the White Fire. We'll come back to you when it's time to start lessons, and you might just get a front-row seat.","content.75.3374":"It was so foreseeable... I told you to surprise them, not to get surprised by them!","content.75.3375":"Are you certain? Maybe you didn't look properly, absent minded as you are...","content.75.3376":"Hmmm... That can only mean one thing: They have special ways of getting around the school... Secret passages that let them go from place to place fairly quickly while avoiding the professors. In any case, tell me more about your attackers!","content.75.3377":"Hoodlums, hmm... I read some references about them recently. Reputedly, they have a flying structure which goes around the nations, and they attack poor travelers and take their money. This structure is known as the \"Zeppelantern\". Their leader could well be on board it. I see you've done quite well so far. How would you like to get down to business and go take a look? I need more information about these strange individuals.","content.75.3378":"Quite the contrary!\\nThe ruins have been explored and the knowledge they contain indexed and copied a very long time ago, in the early days of archaosology.\\nLed by the Huppermages, the first exploration groups focused their research on all the untapped sources of knowledge. I have to admit that few people visit them, due to the difficulty getting there. I think we may even be the first people to set foot there for several decades!","content.75.3379":"On the surface?! But... why? And especially, how? I don't think you have any idea of the size of this place! Old Bonta's Ruins are spread out over several square miles! We risk causing a lot of damage by moving so much as one building, so as for what's left of the city... I don't dare imagine it!","content.75.3380":"Hahaha! Well, it's clear that you're an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}. You know, in archaosology, every bit of treasure you find has a place in a museum. Only a few vultures like that Brakmarian, Lebbocq, or the vile Amelia of the Riktus Clan ignore that rule.\\nThat being said, you won't find a lot here. I think the first few expeditions took everything that was able to withstand being transported, that's to say not a lot. The mudslide and exposure to Ogrest's tears greatly degraded most of what can be found here in these ruins. If I were you, I wouldn't touch anything that isn't necessary to our expedition.","content.75.3381":"Here we are, reunited once more, adventurer! What may the goddess that I am do for you?","content.75.3382":"Aaah, our dear school... Rebuilt in front of the ruins of the old school, the new Huppermage School is more magnificent than ever, and once again ready to receive students. Excited at the prospect of having the knowledge we've acquired and preserved for centuries at the tips of their fingers, a crowd of students is already roaming the corridors, breathing a life into this school unseen since the downfall. It fills my old heart with pride.","content.75.3383":"It flew just a little, {[1*]?little girl:young man}! This sanctuary of wisdom and knowledge has survived the ages and even Ogrest's Chaos, would you believe it! Where the gods failed, the Huppermages succeeded.","content.75.3384":"Yes, indeed... But it's another problem that happened some time later. That's got nothing to do with it, nothing whatsoever.","content.75.3385":"Well that, young {[1*]?lady:man}, was thanks to the magic of the Huppermages, of course!\\nBut you'll learn more about our magic, as well as about the Quadramental Breeze, in the course of your studies... That is, if you're deemed worthy to learn more about it.","content.75.3386":"The equilibrium seems unstable with you.","content.75.3387":"Hello again... You still haven't fetched the items needed to get signed up? Are you sure you want to join the ranks of the school?... Just to remind you, you need to find three objects we scattered downstairs in the school: a Blue-toned Pearl, some Precious Powder, and a note that we leave especially for novices.","content.75.3388":"Sorry, I'm not allowed to let you go through the University any more, now we've cleared a way to Old Bonta via the Kara Geyser.","content.75.3389":"So much the better! I have work to do; go back and practice.","content.75.3390":"Yes. Your equilibrium is delicate, and will require regular work. So go back and practice.","content.75.3391":"Among what you want to believe is balanced, what you think is balanced, what you want to say is balanced, and what you say is balanced, we have little chance of managing to balance our point of view.","content.75.3392":"Elementary, my dear. But really, not at all!","content.75.3393":"Nice try.","content.75.3394":"Maybe, maybe not.","content.75.3395":"Indeed. That's why you should go back and practice. I have work to do.","content.75.3396":"There is no madness without genius, but especially no masterpiece without thorough, compos mentis work. For the time being, you should go back and attend to your things... And get a little practice.","content.75.3397":"Hurry up, I don't have all day you know!","content.75.3398":"I'm listening, but hurry up. My time is precious!","content.75.3399":"Hey you cocky little person! Can't you see I'm in the middle of a lecture?","content.75.3400":"Come now! Not so fast!\\nWhy would I give you this book? Hmmmm... I'm in a playful mood today.\\nIf you really do want it, you'll have to a answer a few questions for me...","content.75.3401":"Sorry! That's the wrong answer.\\nYou'll have to study far better than that if you want the book.","content.75.3402":"All good!\\nI see you're a real hard worker who's not afraid of being immersed in books when necessary. You really deserve this book. So here it is!","content.75.3403":"What is the subtitle of the Spherolithic Encyclopedia?","content.75.3404":"What is the subtitle of the Boxford Dictationary vol. XXXVI?","content.75.3405":"What is the subtitle of volume XXII of Exotic Zoomonology?","content.75.3406":"Spot on! Now, for the second question...","content.75.3407":"What is the subtitle of volume II of World of Twelve Cartography?","content.75.3408":"What is the subtitle of the copy of the Gobbowlium Codex?","content.75.3409":"Spot on! Now, the third and final question will be a little more than just a test of memory. You'll need to use your gray matter!","content.75.3410":"What book bears the subtitle \"Kings and Disquiet\"?","content.75.3411":"What book bears the subtitle \"Blades and tears\"?","content.75.3412":"What book bears the subtitle \"From sand to copper\"?","content.75.3413":"What book bears the subtitle \"Mimic mimics\"?","content.75.3414":"What book bears the subtitle \"Ogrest's Cult and Dathura's Sisters\"?","content.75.3415":"In the Summary of Ogrest's Chaos News, what does the subtitle refer to?","content.75.3416":"What is Sufokia Archaosology Vol. I about?","content.75.3417":"What is Chronicles of the Gray Moon volume XIV about?","content.75.3418":"From Incarnam to Externam tells a wonderful story. What is it about?","content.75.3419":"What scandal was caused by the review Anthropology Illustrated - year 33 no. 42?","content.75.3421":"Hello young one! So, you'd like an autograph?","content.75.3422":"Just a bit, little {[1*]?girl:guy}! So, that took the wind out of your sails, didn't it? You've never seen as flamboyant a Iop as me, am I right? La crème de la crème, my little friend!","content.75.3423":"Wha... What? Of course not! Do you take me for a Iop? I mean... Leaving the symbol of my greatness within reach of the first Enutrof who comes along... By the Twelve! The cup is safe in the Gobbowl Stadium of our great Bonta! A monument to my glory, that everyone aspiring to the title of champion may admire at every match.","content.75.3424":"You're going to the stadium? Fabulous! You're full of energy, just like my old friend Joris. You remind me of him when he was 8 years old. Heh heh heh... I'll go with you. Take lead, and I'll meet you there, I have to make an entrance...","content.75.3426":"You aren't a wimp, are you? You really think that I've always had a honker like an old shriveled prune?\\nI'm a Iop, not an Enutrof! My Gobbowl days were back in my youth! I haven't always been a Gobbowler. After suffering a knee injury, and going through a bit of a bad patch, I became an adventurer. We did travel around a lot, my little Jojo and I! I wonder what became of him...","content.75.3427":"Heh heh heh... That's my second adventuring sidekick, after my little pal Joris. He couldn't stand me leaving, so joined me in the hereafter. I'm talking about the birdie, not Jojo!","content.75.3428":"Let me see that! Hmmm... That color... It's different from the first one...","content.75.3429":"Hmmm... *whispers something about the heat given off by the metal*\\nHmmmm... Yes, it would be good...\\nHmmmmm... *murmurs indistinctly while leafing through an old mold covered volume that reeks of the swamp*","content.75.3430":"Here we are!\\nI can assure you, just like last time, that this is indeed an authentic Orichalcum!","content.75.3431":"And as for my part, as I've already told you, I'm trying to track down one of my ancestors, who was apparently a Gobbowler in the time of Old Bonta. He was supposedly my Ocarina's guardian for some time.","content.75.3432":"Really? Well I'll make the most of... Errr... You'll be able to make the most of my greatness and power while I find out what I need. Osamodas is watching over you!","content.75.3433":"The Immawhat of Bonta? No, I came via the geyser there, just behind me. My Magicarpett was really useful for sliding through the currents. It must be possible to go back through here too. \\nYou look skeptical... All I did was ask the elders of the region, and for a few kamas, they explained how I could get to this place.","content.75.3434":"But... Of course! What would make you doubt that?\\n*Mimi blushes*\\nI... Don't you know it's dangerous to doubt a god or goddess's power? It's just as well I'm magnanimous, and that you've shown more respect than previously by putting your poor talents to my use.\\nI'll wipe the slate clean this time...","content.75.3435":"It's not little!\\nIt's just... ...different. That's what makes it, and me, special.\\nAs for the Ocarina, it's a family heirloom. We have been its guardians for generations, since long before Ogrest's Chaos.\\nWhen I hold it in my hands, I feel all of Osamodas's power... err, my power rise up in me. It must have belonged to me in a former incarnation!","content.75.3436":"It seems they want to steal my ocarina! I wonder why... It's an instrument belonging to Osamodas, who happens to be me, so I'm sure it would be of no use to them!\\nBut they'll never get their hands on it anyway! They can't do anything against my divine power!","content.75.3437":"Hmmppfff... My Twelvian name is Michelene Tordsabots, but as a goddess, you may simply call me Mimi the Marvelous, or Goddess.","content.75.3438":"Grrrrrrr!!! That Team Missile! I hate them! They've been hunting me down for weeks.\\nAfter our confrontation in Bovis's Lair, I looked into their training methods, from a purely educational point of view, of course. A goddess hardly needs that to control inferior creatures. I just wanted to... errr... find out how to counter their techniques better. That's it, yes. Exactly! Counter their techniques better! Hehehe!","content.75.3439":"I'm getting to that! So insolent, these mortals...\\nSo, I asked around, I made inquiries, and then... Bam! I came across a training school, where they teach the Gobé'Mob technique. Unfortunately, it's now closed. So I went off too look for the people who taught there...","content.75.3440":"We're getting there! Ugh...\\nSo, I tracked down the Gobé'Mob master, and he told me he had closed the school after two of his students used his techniques for evil - to humiliate his niece, Twisty, the worst Gobé'Mob master he has ever known. Those wicked students were none other than Jemmy and Janes, along with Miouze... otherwise known as Team Missile!","content.75.3441":"Exactly!\\nDazzled by my divine charisma, and encouraged by a nice purse of kamas, he agreed to teach me Gobé'Mob master techniques.\\nAfter my training, probably stunned by my mastery, the venerable old man gave me this outfit as a symbol of what I meant to him.","content.75.3442":"But... I...\\nNOT AT ALL!\\nIt was... He... It's mostly because he thought of me as a member of his family! Pfff...\\nYou understand nothing, poor mortal.","content.75.3443":"Actually, I wanted to see how mortals defended themselves. I wonder how Janes was able to learn this technique? It's surprising for a Iop... I guess Jemmy has something to do with it.\\nAnyway! Besides, it was by learning these little sleight of hand tricks that I got this wonderful outfit. Wonderful, but I think I'm already growing tired of it...","content.75.3444":"He... I... I didn't want to keep such a beautiful animal, of such a rare species, in captivity. Yes, that's right. I therefore decided by myself, in my clemency, to free him. That way, he can find his soul mate and propagate his species... That too is the role of Osamodas!","content.75.3445":"I am a Huppermage. I helped with the rebuilding of the school, and I'm part of the second wave of teachers at the Immaterial University of Bonta. Contrary to some of my Huppermage counterparts, I am for renewing contact with the people of the World of Twelve and sharing our common knowledge.","content.75.3446":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3447":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3449":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3450":"Well! What an adventure! You have my respect. The task was long and hard but you pulled it off brilliantly! Unfortunately, I don't have anything else to offer you. You've brought me everything I needed. But maybe I'll have some more work for you soon...","content.75.3451":"Unfortunately, I don't have anything else to offer you. You've brought me everything I needed. But maybe I'll have some more work for you soon...","content.75.3452":"Very well. So, now we've hit a dead end. Well, not really, but there's only one way out.\\nOlavrann could only have fled through here.","content.75.3453":"Well, you seem perfectly capable of helping me find Olavrann, and of containing the contamination of the creatures and souls around here. First, we must find this Olavrann. He's certainly returned to the Incarnam Plains. It's the only way out of here.\\nHe's got quite a lead on us - we'll have to find his trail before we can intercept him.\\nBut before doing that, we have to jump. I mean, you have to jump.","content.75.3454":"Nice to meet you, vacationer! I'm Gnat, the Meridia of this sumptuous and hot summer! I'm looking for proud voyagers to collect some Fine Sänd and brave adventurers to go to La Mädrague Beach. Would you be one of these people?","content.75.3456":"Odd... *COUGH* *COUGH* *COUGH* Hello stranger. To what do I owe the visit in this quiet lost place? Are you real, or just a hallucination? Did I eat my mushrooms this morning? What time is it, Boufson?","content.75.3457":"Of course. Most of the time, old Jacky hides deep in Kannivore territory, far in the depths of the Kannivore Dungeon. He takes care of the sacred plants for us. But if you make too much noise while getting there and you're too slow in getting to where he's hiding, he'll take off, and you'll have to start all over again.","content.75.3458":"Woah! Let me take a look...\\n*Botan Ficus attentively deciphers the few still-legible words on the page*\\nYes. I think I know how to help you. You must go and see the hermit that lives with the Kannivores. He's solitary, and doesn't much like strangers. He's lived there for years, ever since he arrived on the island at the same time as the Crocodyls, on board the ship the Nyl Arena, whose wreck still adorns the beach to the south. Back then it was my father who was the village chief.\\nYou'd better be fast if you want to see him.","content.75.3459":"It's not easy to explain. In terms a stranger and neophyte like yourself will understand, I can tell you \"in the Kannivore Dungeon\". But it's a bit more. I don't think that there are words in your language to express all the complex ideas related to this place.\\nThe link with life, nature, and the Kannivores themselves is very powerful in the depths of Moon Island, and each thing has a reason to live - or die - there.\\nI could tell you about the Great Gynoecium and the...","content.75.3460":"Ha! Jacky... He arrived in the village one day, one leg gravely injured, around the same time the Crocodyls showed up. He was scared we would eat him! Hahaha! That was several decades ago. I was just a little Kanniball then. It was my father, who was the chief of the village back then, who welcomed him. We healed him, but we weren't able to save the injured part of his leg. While he was resting up, I was able to improve my Twelvian speak by talking to him.\\nToday, he's our gardener in the depths of the island and takes care of the Kannivores to thank us.","content.75.3461":"I'd like to lay down in the Fine Sänd like an abandoned shell. \\nCould you bring me about ten?","content.75.3462":"By Ecaflip's whiskers! The same to you, you impolite little cretin! Go on! Get out of here! Clear off! Come back and see me when you have something interesting to tell me, you insolent little Bwork!!\\nWe're not going to let ourselves be mistreated by such a rude person, are we Boufson? Honestly!","content.75.3464":"Hey Boufson! {[1*]?Sh:H}e knows my name! {[1*]?Sh:H}e knows who I was! {[1*]?Sh:H}e knows who I am, Boufson!\\nYes, I am, I was, and I will be Jacky Lilye Tstrong. But you can call me Captain, or Jacky, if you prefer. But don't call me Ship's Apprentice. I haven't been that in a long time, and it might upset Boufson. Isn't that right, Boufson?","content.75.3465":"Hahaha Boufson! {[1*]?Sh:H}e forgot! Haha! {[1*]?Sh:H}e's even madder than I am! Or stupider, hehehe! Or both, you're right Boufson!\\nIt's simple, look everywhere, in all the corners, in all the Crocodyls. Any of them could have gobbled up a page of my... of our logbook. Excuse me, Boufson.\\nWe need lots. LOTS!\\nIn all the Crocodyls, YES! But especially in the Nyl Crocodyls especially! The Nyls, YES, but any on Moon Island!\\nI don't think other Crocodyls would have been able to come to Moon Island, hahahaha! Isn't that right, Boufson?","content.75.3466":"Hey, Boufson! {[1*]?She:He} did it! Let's see...\\n*Jacky frantically flips through the logbook fragments, hands trembling, Boufson tucked under his left elbow*\\nHmmm... See that, Boufson?\\nI have a hard time reading it, and it's all sticky. I didn't think it would be pretty, but this is pretty catastrophic, isn't it Boufson?\\nSomething must be done. Thankfully, we have a plan. What, Boufson? Oh, yes! A great plan, hahaha....","content.75.3467":"Hear that Boufson? {[1*]?Sh:H}e's got news! Do you think {[1*]?s:}he'll manage to reassemble the logbook with your kit, Boufson?\\nTell me everything, little one...","content.75.3468":"Hey Boufson! {[1*]?Sh:H}e made progress!\\nNicely done! Take care of all that. You're going to need it to use Boufson's binding kit. Isn't that right, Boufson?","content.75.3469":"Yes, reinvigorating and hydrating Bläck Sänd. I'd really love to have ten of them, but they're only found on a horrible monster called the Bläck Skäte.\\nHe's certainly in the Märine Pälace.","content.75.3470":"Hahaha Boufson! Not so stupid, this one, right? \\nWe worked on it for a long time... Days? No. Months? Not enough, Boufson... Years... YES! YEARS! Heh heh heh!\\nYes, yes, yes... And what have we done for all these years, Boufson? What? We've taken care of Kannivores? That's true, Boufson... But above all, we thought! Thought about how to get the logbook back. How it would be when we got it back. Thought about how to fix it... Yes, we thought about all that, and much more. We had a lot of time, didn't we Boufson?","content.75.3471":"Oh what a rush {[1*]?s:}he's in, Boufson. Like a giant moth looking at a dancing flame in the night. We've been waiting decades, and {[1*]?s:}he can't even wait for nice Jacky to explain. Bwork stupid! *COUGH* *COUGH*\\nOk, let's go. You're going to need Boufson's special binding kit, as well as a certain number of specific ingredients. I'll give you the Binding Kit and the list of ingredients. When you've got all that together, you can try to restore the logbook to a readable state, if my calculations are correct. Go on! Hup! Get out now! Boufson and I need to clean.","content.75.3472":"What a Bwork brain this one is, Boufson. But it doesn't matter... *COUGH* *COUGH*\\nWhen I talk to Boufson, I'm talking to Boufson. And when I talk to you, I'm talking to you. Simple, no?\\nAnyway, what do you want from old Jacky? Huh, Boufson... What does {[1*]?s:}he want from us?","content.75.3473":"By Ecaflip's whiskers! Look, Boufson!\\n*Jacky rips the half-digested treated leather page from your hands. He squints his eyes so they're as small as Moofly paws. He smells the page, then holds it out to his strange Gobbowl ball*\\nSmell this, Boufson! It's one of them! That smell of sea, ink, and Crocodyl bile. Do you smell it Boufson? It's one of them, it's really one of them!\\nWhere did you find this? Huh, Boufson, where did {[1*]?she:he} find it?","content.75.3474":"Shhh! Shhh shhh shhh!\\nWe know... Isn't that right, Boufson? WE KNOW!\\nThe Crocodyls! As expected! They ate the logbook! The gluttons, the cannibals! But we knew it had to happen, isn't that right, Boufson... We wrote it! Yes! Wrote!\\nBut now, we don't remember everything. That's true... Not everything. But we'd like to remember. Isn't that right, Boufson...","content.75.3475":"{[1*]?Sh:H}e's funny, isn't that right, Boufson?\\nNo, we can't leave. We have too much to do here with the pretty plants. We don't like Nyl Crocodyls. No, no, no. They weren't nice to Ship's Apprentice Jacky when he became captain. Oh no.\\nBut you... YOU can do something for old Jacky's memory - isn't that right, Boufson? They can do something?","content.75.3476":"The Mastostroke? THE MASTOSTROKE! *COUGH* *COUGH*\\n{[1*]?Sh:H}e's the Mastostroke, huh Boufson? Heh heh heh!\\nI'm too old to climb the ropes to get out of here, and I don't have the strength to go fighting Crocodyls at my age, huh Boufson?\\nI already wasn't able to fight them with we got to the island so many decades ago.\\nBut you, you can! You must go and bring old Jacky some nice pieces of the Nyl Arena's logbook to feed my memory, hehehe.","content.75.3477":"Hahaha Boufson! {[1*]?Sh:H}e didn't understand! Hahaha! Has {[1*]?s:}he been drinking Bwork Beer or what? Or {[1*]?s:}he is just dumb, hahaha! Or both, you're right Boufson! *COUGH* *COUGH*\\nIt's simple, look everywhere, in all the corners, in all the Crocodyls. Any of them could have gobbled up a page of my... of our logbook. Excuse me Boufson.\\nWe need lots. LOTS!\\nIn all the Crocodyls, YES! But in all the Nyl Crocodyls especially. The Nyls, YES! The Nyls, YES, but any on Moon Island!\\nI don't think other Crocodyls would have been able to come to Moon Island, hahahaha! Isn't that right, Boufson?\\nI'll give this back to you to start with.","content.75.3478":"Look at that, Boufson! {[1*]?Sh:H}e wasted everything!\\nThankfully, we planned for everything, even h{[1*]?er:is} clumsiness, isn't that right, Boufson?\\nI'll give you another one for 100,000 kamas. What do you say?","content.75.3479":"Ecaflip's biscuit! Look at that, Boufson! Land ho! Hoist the main sail! Hahahaha! Even more beautiful than the original!\\n*Jacky takes the logbook and disappears into the foliage for several minutes, then comes back, carrying a second book made of leaves and plants, as well as a large bundle ready to split open.*\\nHere{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}, I've made you a copy. You've earned it.\\nIsn't that right, Boufson? You can discover for yourself what really happened.\\nThe bundle is for you. There are a few gifts in there for you that you more than earned: Some little things that Boufson and I made or recovered while we've been here. I hope you like them!\\nDon't hesitate to come back and see me from time to time.\\nCome on Boufson, say goodbye!","content.75.3480":"See that Boufson? {[1*]?Sh:H}e's curious!\\nSo, what do you want to know about old Jacky? Or about Boufson, if he's inclined to answer you! Heh heh heh!","content.75.3481":"Hoohoohoo! Did you see that, Boufson? It's the little binder!\\nWe'll tell {[1*]?her:him} everything, and {[1*]?s:}he won't believe {[1*]?her:his} ears. Right, Boufson?\\nListen well: yesterday, a guy came by. He said he was working for a Phil Harmonic. He heard about what you did for me. So he came especially to buy the story of the logbook from me. Do you believe it? The guy wanted my story! And you'll never guess what he's going to do with it: a musical! You know, with singers, dancers, all that jazz! Boufson never dreamed of it!","content.75.3482":"Yes, like I said! And what's more, he offered me more kamas than I can count with my tired eyes!\\nWe're rich now, Boufson and I.","content.75.3483":"In the World? In the WORLD?! Hear that Boufson? More than 30 years of living my life here peacefully, and I have to go looking for trouble. Heh heh heh... I voyaged quite a bit when I was a Ship's Apprentice on the Nyl Arena, not to mention my misadventure with the Crocodyls. Now I just want to live peacefully, with my memories, my plants, and my friend Boufson. Right, Boufson?","content.75.3484":"So, here you are in the Incarnam Plains. You must be extra-careful, because the area has been altered by Stasis, which is not normal at all.","content.75.3485":"We must find Olavrann. I'm convinced that he's linked to the source of the problems we're witnessing in Incarnam.\\nI don't know which way he went. Go and see if you can find any trace of him. I'm going to try and find something to contain the spread of the Stasis.","content.75.3486":"I'm listening. What do you want to know, my child?","content.75.3487":"Excellent! Thanks to your research, I've been able to find him.\\nIt looks like the trail is still fresh, and Olavrann's hideout seems to be well-guarded.\\nHurry up and get there, before the Stasified monsters suspect something!","content.75.3488":"Evidently these Embrysouls were contaminated by Stasis.\\nBut there shouldn't be Stasis in Incarnam... Or rather, I suppose there shouldn't, because if Incarnam is the counterpart of Externam - the place where souls are freed of their Stasis and the weight of their lives - then there shouldn't be any Stasis here at all.\\nThis contamination could be the reason there are so many new incarnates turning to illicit activities after arriving in the World of Twelve...","content.75.3489":"Hahaha! It's true that I didn't really introduce myself. Sorry.\\nI'm Otomai - scientomage and alchemist. I'm older than I am famous, even if people come to flatter me to get my help.\\nDon't judge me by my appearance. I'm several centuries old, and my vast knowledge is due to the time I've had to study so many things.","content.75.3490":"Olavrann... This soul is not like the others you'll cross here in Incarnam, neither the Embrysouls nor the Stasified ones. Olavrann the External seems to be a soul who didn't follow the \"normal\" path of incarnation, as you did, for example. No.\\nIt could be that his soul did not have his life discharged in Externam after his death, and that he didn't pass through the great Wakfu flux before being reincarnated here.","content.75.3491":"You're here in the Incarnam Plains. Well, one of the Incarnam Plains. The place is huge. It's said that everything you see is actually on the back of a giant dragon, sleeping in this dimension, parallel to the real, material world: the real, material world where the World of Twelve is located. That's where I come from, and you too, in principle.","content.75.3492":"During the flood, the number of Twelvians who lost their lives was such that Incarnam was overflowing with souls wanting to reincarnate. Under the power of the flux, the old Incarnam of the Dofus Era disintegrated, and a new Incarnam has slowly been built over the centuries.\\nThe temple seems to be a ruin from that time, that the souls empowered when they passed, and there inscribed their memories of the World of Twelve.\\nThe place must be chock-full of interesting information, as much about the world as its inhabitants.","content.75.3493":"This sänd? It comes from a little island near Bilbiza. It clings to various monsters of the world! Incidentally, I believe I saw some bottles with that sänd drift ashore in the nations. I think there were messages inside...","content.75.3494":"Yes, messages. Or at least a bit of paper... I haven't bothered to take a look! It's too tiring! I'd prefer tanning my shells in the sun! These messages must surely mean something! Important? Definitely. You should take a look!","content.75.3495":"Ah yes, the messages... I have the strange impression that someone's calling for help somewhere on Bilbiza Island.\\nI found this compass in the Fine Sänd. It should be useful in guiding you to whoever it is that needs help!","content.75.3496":"You're really an inimitable vacationer!\\nI'm happy to have met you. Don't hesitate to bring me some Sänd when you have the time to kick back a bit, because the summer's not over yet!","content.75.3497":"{[1*]?Sh:H}e's asking who we are, but {[1*]?s:}he already knows! What's that, Boufson? Not just my name? Hahaha! Alright!\\nI used to be a Ship's Apprentice on the ship Nyl Arena. I was under the command of Captain Gem S. Crook for several years. I was young, and as agile as a monkey. The rigging was my kingdom. You didn't experience that, did you Boufson?","content.75.3498":"But one day, while we were transporting savage creatures, a strange curse fell upon the ship, and everyone fell asleep. The rest... Well, it's a bit blurry, and painful to tell. It's best to read the logbook; it's all laid out inside. Isn't that right, Boufson?","content.75.3499":"Me, I'm from Brakmar. And Boufson, I think he's from Amakna, but he doesn't like to talk about it too much. Right, Boufson? The past is the past. And sometimes we can allow ourselves to forget part of it.","content.75.3500":"{[1*]?Sh:H}e asked us why we stay here, can you believe it?\\nWhere would I go? I've dedicated my life to caring for these plants. And the plants... they're nice to us. Sometimes, they become a bit crazy when a Kanniball wanders off the beaten path.\\nBut we like the plants, and they give us everything we need, don't they, Boufson?","content.75.3501":"That's easy to answer, eh Boufson?\\nIt's very easy. I was a Ship's Apprentice on a ship. When the captain abandoned the ship, it was up to the most senior member of crew remaining to become captain. And it just so happens that, with everything that happened on the Nyl Arena, that was me. That's how I became a captain. For more detail, you should read the ship's logbook. What, Boufson?","content.75.3502":"Ha! That's what I'd like to forget. I don't want to talk about it. And it's useless looking at Boufson like that. He's not going to tell you more!\\nIf it interests you, look in the logbook!","content.75.3503":"It's true that you must be a bit lost here.\\nThis place is one of the incarnation platforms, in the dimension of Incarnam.\\nSouls, attracted by the Wakfu flux, incarnate and reincarnate here, just like you just did - spectacularly so, might I add. Then they go and rejoin their native world - for you, that's the World of Twelve I believe, just like me.","content.75.3504":"Hmmm... Well that's a peculiar question.\\nOne might think it was the first time we'd met. But I feel like we already met{[1*]?:}.\\nSince you just incarnated, you must have died{[1*]?:} recently. I don't particularly remember you, so our meeting must have happened decades ago, maybe even centuries ago, in another one of your lives. Hmmm... Yes, it's possible. Hang on...","content.75.3505":"It seems that Incarnam suffered greatly during Ogrest's Chaos, the cataclysm that ravaged the World of Twelve 200 years ago. The Chaos didn't have a direct impact. The Primordial Dofus that my little Ogrest has in his possession didn't give him enough power to attack this place.\\nNo, something sadder happened here.","content.75.3506":"You wouldn't be one of those adventurers who refused to take my advice about Mount Zinit and were literally crushed by my son Ogrest, would you?\\nHoly Feca's Shield! That was over a hundred and fifty years ago!\\nSorry for what happened to you and your friends back then... The next time, try to trust me a little more, will you?","content.75.3507":"Hmmm... No, I don't see for the moment. Give me a bit of time, and I'll remember!","content.75.3508":"Phew...\\nI didn't need help! I wäs getting älong just fine on my own! \\nI'm going to need ä new ideä to fiddle äround and fix this problem... hmmm...","content.75.3509":"Who...? Me...? I got lost... ä long time ägo... I think. I got so bored that I stärted throwing bottles in the seä, but no one came until todäy! So I kept on mäking my cute little Sänd Skätes, but they don't listen to änything! They just do whätever they wänt!","content.75.3510":"Oh come on! It's obvious, but no!\\nAnd... I was very explicit in my messäges in bottles!\\nRescue the beäutiful and young Impette who is dying of boredom in her Sänd Cästle!","content.75.3513":"Ok, but I'll warn you right now: monsters outside of Incarnam are tough. I suggest you start with Bow Meows before attacking the rest of the fauna. Remember that if you don't feel comfortable over there, you can always come back here by using the Astrub Zaap for free.\\nAre you sure you want to leave now?","content.75.3514":"\\nThe leaders of the World of Twelve have sent me here to investigate the cause of the resurgence of criminality, which seems to have supernatural causes.","content.75.3515":"Evil? No! But it's a bit more complicated than that. To make things easier for you, let's say that Wakfu and Stasis are complimentary. Two diametrically opposed types of the same energy. Generally speaking, Wakfu is associated with change, movement and, by extension, life. Stasis, on the other hand, is considered to be the energy behind stability, immobility and, by extension, death. But that's an oversimplification. If Wakfu and Stasis aren't balanced, the whole World, even the whole Krosmoz, would be irreparably destroyed.","content.75.3516":"Yes. What a horrible trip through the Krosmoz. Who knows how much time he spent wandering through the void before landing here? He must have gone insane.\\nI thought he was the source of the Stasis, but it seems that's not the case. But I'm certain that he will lead us to the real source!","content.75.3517":"My stones are beautiful, aren't they?\\nIf you activäte them in a certain order, you will be able to go down to see how you mätch up to my greatest creätion: a Sänd Skäte that is equally as good in water! I häve to fill the tänk with water regularly because it consumes so much of it!\\nLook, I scräwled this solution onto some scrap paper, if ever you feel bräve enough...","content.75.3518":"Who goes there?\\nDo you have a pass, an invitation or an employee ID card?\\nIf not, off you go!","content.75.3519":"Who goes there?\\nDo you have a pass, an invitation or an employee ID card? But?!\\nWhat am I supposed to do with these kamas?\\nUnless it's got three zeros, I'm not interested. And even then...","content.75.3520":"Hey, you! Tourist! Look who's lost in the backstreets of Brakmar... Do you need a hand?\\nI expect immediate payment, in cash. And I don't do refunds! Non-negotiable.\\nOh! And I don't like having to repeat myself, so if you ask me for the same information twice, you'll have to pay double.","content.75.3521":"Hey there, cutie, are you all alone? Or are you here for one of your \"friends\"?","content.75.3522":"AND to what do I owe the pleasure of your VISIT?\\nI hope for your sake that it's IMPORTANT, or else you can be on your way!","content.75.3523":"What do you want? Speak quickly or get out before I shut you up. I'm not too keen on being seen with a stranger. In fact, I don't like being seen full stop.","content.75.3524":"I'm going to end this unpleasant discussion.\\nGUARDS! GUARDS!!!\\nPlease see this lout out... AND... don't waste any time with subtleties!","content.75.3525":"I see... trade... and which item in my splendid collection are you looking to acquire?","content.75.3526":"My time is precious; what do you want?","content.75.3527":"I am the boss of Sidimotes & Co. and I don't think you have an appointment, do you?\\nWhat's more, I don't have time to waste with a groupie like you.\\nGuards, please see this lout out... ","content.75.3528":"You mean this small, mysterious, metal ball which is hot to the touch, and makes all the hairs of my body stand on end?","content.75.3531":"You intrigue me. Show me your arguments. Let's hope you have something good, because I won't back down so easily!","content.75.3532":"You have a lot of spunk. I like that, even if I like people who rub me up the right way!\\nHere in Brakmar, people take business very seriously, and I leave nothing to chance.","content.75.3536":"So I'm expecting you to be ready to go! \\nIf you really want to get MY Orichalcum, you're going to have to lay your cards on the table!","content.75.3537":"I worked hard to get here. And it's true that I've invested a significant amount of both my time and my money in the reconstruction of our Brakmar. I earned my social status.\\nThere was also a time when I repelled those beastly rebels' attack on our beautiful Sidimote Moors. What's more, I was received a commendation medal for services to Brakmar.","content.75.3538":"Ah, those were the days...\\nAlthough, these days are actually much better, ever since I founded my flagship Factory: Sidimotes & Co.","content.75.3539":"An innovative mode of transport! It cannot be denied that Brakmarians were able to recognize my talent and the proof of that is here today. My mechanical creations are sold throughout the whole world and my bank balance has never been healthier!","content.75.3540":"Enough small talk. Let's talk about the Orichalcum.","content.75.3541":"WELL? My patience has its limits!","content.75.3545":"HAHAHA! Very funny! But back to more serious stuff.\\nI think you have more to offer than that, if you want the object of your desires!","content.75.3546":"You're full of ideas. That's an interesting proposal! \\nAnd what sort of missions could I possibly want to entrust to you?","content.75.3547":"I'll admit that I don't have much opportunity to get out and about at the moment...","content.75.3548":"Actually, I've already got enough on my plate with the construction of my colossal project!","content.75.3549":"Be careful. A deal's a deal; there are missions to complete, without asking questions about the Orichalcum. Are we both in agreement?","content.75.3550":"Good! You can start right away!\\nI'll need several different materials.\\nI hope you'll be tough enough to complete these tasks!","content.75.3551":"You're the one who needs the Orichalcum, and at any cost! And that's good enough for me.\\nIf it's too difficult for you, try and buy what you need...\\nGet on your way.","content.75.3554":"What the...?! I'm a famous scientist, I don't have time to waste on good-for-nothings like you...\\nWait a bit... Haven't we already met?","content.75.3555":"So, how are you coming along?","content.75.3556":"Oh, yes! Honorary Archaosologist.\\nVery well. I've managed to track down my customer, the one who bought the Orichalcum back when I didn't know what it was.\\nI got a good price for it, but I could have got much more... Uh... I wouldn't have sold it had I known what it was at the time.","content.75.3557":"How impatient! Well, you're right, time is money!\\nIt looks like we're dealing with one of the largest industrial fortunes in Brakmar. The magnate of the Sidimote Mechas, who I call: Charles-Henri of Vileardent. And I can tell you he's a hard businessman. He was a regular customer, a real lover of antiques. But he hasn't been back in touch since he bought that Orichalcum from me.","content.75.3558":"Give? GIVE?! Hahaha!\\nTo hear you talk, anyone would think it's your first time here, or the first time you've heard of Brakmar. Nothing's free here. Everything has a price: even people's lives. So, you think that if he bought this item from me, he's not going to give it up so easily. Even with some strong negotiations, expect to pay a high price. Personally, I won't be paying a single kama; it's you who wants the Orichalcum, after all.","content.75.3559":"Well, as with all complicated things, let's start with the basics. Find me at the heart of the ghetto, in front of the entrance to the Sidimotes & Co. Factory, further to the west. Hold on to your purse. The inhabitants of this neighborhood are known for their sticky fingers...","content.75.3560":"Hahaha! That's true. I get too easily distracted.\\nListen, I'm going to take advantage of my celebrity to get us into the factory. Watch how the professionals do it. Ready?","content.75.3561":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3562":"Ha! Lebbocq. That little bundle of nerves. Hehehe!\\nHe's too cute. He's always been straight with me. So, I'll offer you the same prices as I offer him. If you need to distract somebody sensitive to feminine charm, come see me. It would be my pleasure to put a sparkle in their eyes and melt their heart. For the right amount of kamas, of course.","content.75.3563":"I see.\\nListen, if he sent me to you, it may be that you need my services. So, if you have someone you need to make disappear quickly and quietly, I'm your guy. My contract is very clear and straight-forward - you pay, I slay.","content.75.3564":"Ha! Little Lebbocq. Brakmarian through and through, that one. He's also been by two or three times this week. He warned me he'd be sending others here before long. I'm so happy he did!\\nIf you need information about the locals, or, I don't know... let's say the guards posted in the factory's airlocks, come back and see me later. I should be able to help you, for the right price.","content.75.3566":"Great, you've met some of the locals who stand the best chance of helping us get past the guards. Thanks to them, we'll be able to get to the center of the factory much more easily... As long as you get them on our side and you can make the most of their skills at the right moment.\\nWhatever you decide, we need to get going.\\nBy all means, go ahead of me. I'll cover our backs!","content.75.3568":"Well, I hope you've got something for me!\\nThe last resources should be easy to find in the wild, to make, or to buy somewhere.","content.75.3569":"I've heard that our governor doesn't wear pajamas or underwear to bed, just a pair of socks on his ears.\\nCrazy, right? Well, it's true that it can get quite hot in Brakmar at night time...","content.75.3570":"It looks like Savhanna used to be an Ouginak.\\nA male one.\\nIt's hard to believe when you see the pretty little thing she's become, though.","content.75.3571":"What?! Where do you think you are? It's not a charity shop. Look, I'm going to tell you something that's worth more than all the kamas in the world:\\nGo and win some. Kill monsters, complete extraordinary achievements or make the coins yourself. By Enutrof, sell some of that junk that's rotting in your bag. Sell your smelly shoes if you have to!\\nBut sort it out! It's not free, you know. Bring me at least 100 kamas. And even at that price, you're not going to get a lot.","content.75.3572":"Ah! There you are! I was wondering if you'd ever come back...","content.75.3573":"Well, here's the first step: Be prepared.\\nThe Mechamummy's lair was built by Charles-Henri to make a living museum. You can expect to find quite a few people and machines that might not be very happy to see you there. On the other hand, we don't know this creature's powers. Be very careful!","content.75.3574":"If you encounter any issues or you're too afraid to head into the dungeon straight away, you can take the staircase to my right back up to the surface. Don't forget that you can use this same exit to re-enter the gallery whenever you want.","content.75.3575":"As I just mentioned, we have to go and speak to Charles-Henri, in his office at the back of the factory.\\nHe's a big important man with a very busy schedule. It's rather difficult to get to talk him in person. Especially when you don't have an appointment. Usually, it's incredibly complicated to even get an appointment.\\nIn fact, he often ends up pushing back appointments, sometimes for weeks on end.","content.75.3576":"If you were paying attention when you were talking to them, you no doubt know why they would be useful to us, given their nature.\\nTonguetwist is selling information about the guards' sensitivities, their weak spots.\\nSkrapur will offer you a new option once you're face to face with a guard in the factory's airlock: Eliminate.\\nSavhanna will allow you to use a seduction approach to neutralize a guard.\\nThe cost is pretty high and, if you use them, wisely or unwisely, or you leave the zone without using them, you'll have to pay again!","content.75.3577":"Let me see that! Hmmm... That color... It's different from the other two...","content.75.3578":"Hmmm... *whispers something about the heat given off by the metal*\\nHmmmm... Yes, it would be good...\\nHmmmmm... *murmurs indistinctly while leafing through an old dust-covered volume that reeks of sulfur*","content.75.3579":"Here we are!\\nI can assure you, just like last time, that this is indeed an authentic Orichalcum!","content.75.3580":"What resources have you brought?","content.75.3582":"I can't tell you too much about it right here, but it looks like Charles-Henri isn't the real name of the Sidimotes & Co. boss.\\nSome people think he bought his name from a noble family with no heirs. Others say he switched identities with a man he met in the Brakmar jail, who is believed to have died there.\\nBut nobody dares ask him, in case that question turns into their last...","content.75.3583":"That one always makes me laugh:\\nIt is said that a long time before Ogrest's Chaos, Goultard witnessed the destruction of Brakmar at least twice. Most of the time, he worked for Bonta. But from what I've heard, there was a dark period of his life where he apparently decimated entire Bontarian regiments.\\nThat's amazing, right? For a legendary hero?","content.75.3584":"Listen to this: It seems old Moe Kneetorks, the Sidimote Moors' clan member, might have family in Bonta! What's more, one of them has inherited his renowned Enutrof family's entire fortune and estate.\\nPoor Moe, reduced to hard labor to make ends meet... What was his real name supposed to be again? Groub? Groot? Sprout? Trude?\\nAh! Stroud! It's Stroud! At least that's what I was told.","content.75.3585":"I think this is the worse one, after the one about... Oops, I almost let slip some information for free!\\nListen carefully: there's a rumor going around that the only true legendary and mysterious secret ingredient that gives Bwork Beer its unique taste is... Bwork juice. Actually, beneath this fruity term lies a much less appetizing reality: It's Bwork urine!\\nOnce I heard that, I stopped drinking it.","content.75.3586":"The other day, I overheard two scientomages talking in the tavern.\\nIt would appear that Ogrest spent some time in this area a very long time ago, long before Ogrest's Chaos, and long before he destroyed our world. In fact, they were saying he was only a child...\\nI have trouble believing it, myself.","content.75.3587":"An old hermit passed through the other day to pick up provisions before returning to his isolated cabin all, lost somewhere up there to the north of the volcano. He told me something surprising: Djaul used to wear a pair of knickers over his pantyhose, but nobody would even notice. And he's right. Who, upon meeting Djaul in person, would dare to look under his loincloth to check?\\nThe old man said he makes these pantyhose with his own hands, using shards of Shushus and lavalarva silk strings...","content.75.3588":"This one's worth its weight in kamas, though I admit that you probably won't benefit much from knowing this:\\nI've heard that members of a rather dangerous cult have hired the services of one of the greatest sailors and oceanographers in the World of Twelve. They allegedly have a submarine with all the latest scientomagic gear!\\nIf they're not up to something untoward on behalf of Sufokia, I'll eat my hat.\\nI wonder where they're getting the money to finance their operations...","content.75.3589":"I've heard that the guard posted in the first airlock has some small gambling debts. If you slip him a few kamas, he'll most likely look the other way while you slip past...","content.75.3590":"I've been told that the Lousy Bwork in the first airlock appreciates the company of lovely ladies... All it takes is a little sway of the hips and he won't be paying attention to his duties anymore.","content.75.3591":"I've heard from a reliable source that the guard in the first airlock is in quite a bit of trouble. If he were to disappear prematurely, nobody would miss him...","content.75.3592":"I've been told that the guard from the factory's first airlock has pretty bad peripheral vision, but he's too proud to wear his glasses to work.\\nIt's probably the opportune time to slip in quietly...","content.75.3593":"Someone told me the guard from the first airlock once payed an inspector to give him a higher test mark when he applied for the post. To be honest, he doesn't really have what it takes for this sort of work. He's not assertive enough.\\nIf you raise your voice just a little, he'll run off with his tail between his legs. Not that he has the choice... Hehehe!... But, well, you understand.","content.75.3594":"That one isn't bad. The Lousy Bwork in the second airlock pretends to be a big shot; that way, no one dares cross him. In reality, though, he's nothing more than a soppy Iop and he'll vanish into thin air like a coward at the mere suggestion of a threat.","content.75.3595":"I heard that the Lousy Bwork in the second airlock appreciates the company of a lovely lady, but he doesn't have much experience with the fairer sex. Just show him an ankle and he'll go gaga...","content.75.3596":"I've heard that the guard at the second airlock is a real swine. Rumor has it he's slept with Lousy Pigs from Bonta! If you listen to the other guards, and half of the local population, this rotter doesn't deserve to live... If he were to disappear, nobody would send out a search party.","content.75.3597":"There's a rumor going around that the guard currently posted to the second airlock is on Riktus's payroll, and doesn't care much about security.\\nI think there's a way to sneak in discreetly without any problems.","content.75.3598":"It seems the second airlock guard has a few mistresses, and he spends all his money buying them gifts. And if you've seen him, you can tell they're definitely not with him for his looks...\\nIn other words, a substantial amount of kamas should convince him to turn a blind eye for a moment or two.","content.75.3599":"Ok, listen carefully. The guard currently posted in the the airlock has been a mere second class for over 10 years. Why? Well, he never shows willingness and is the worst kind of coward. Speak to him sternly and he'll soon surrender!","content.75.3600":"A little birdy told me that the Lousy Bwork from the third airlock has a sweet spot for the ladies. So much so that he's already been married 10 times. He's even divorced 6 of them. Don't ask me any more about this, that's all I know.\\nHowever, that does mean that a nice young lady is all it takes to turn his head...","content.75.3601":"The guard from the third airlock is in on it. In fact, that's what I've been told; I haven't been to check. Oh dear! What, \"in on what\"? Well... you know, \"on it\". Come on, do I have to spell it out? \"IN\". \"ON IT\". He's in on it.\\nNo? Still nothing? Urgh... Ok, it's hard to say, but here goes: This guard is from the S.U.V.D.F.\\nHe's a member of the Standardized Unionized of Very Disgruntled Freelancers.\\nCan you believe it? Trade unions are forbidden in Brakmar. Most of the people who don't work for themselves are either in debt to their boss, or slaves.\\nBasically, trade unions go against all the values and laws of our great nation and being \"in on it\" is considered a risk to national security.\\nI think there are a fair few people who would be quite happy for him to disappear for good.","content.75.3602":"I think the guard from the third airlock is very attached to his traditions. And, in Brakmar, one of our most cherished traditions is corruption. We prefer to talk about \"making our daily contributions\". Never mind. Tradition also comes with its own rules, and the older it is, the stricter these rules are. If you want to get through by contributing to... a bribe, you'll have to pay the asking price. The very high asking price...","content.75.3603":"There are some guards who are sticklers for paying attention. They never allow themselves to be distracted. There are guards who can ignore any amount of distraction to keep a cool composure. Guards that never let anything get to them, that are loyal to the post, unmoving, come wind, rain, snow or burning sunlight.\\nAnd then there's the Lousy Bwork in the third airlock. He's a real scatterbrain.\\nEven the smallest of distractions should buy you enough time to sneak in without being seen.","content.75.3604":"Perfect, perfect!\\nI'll just put that to one side. Where was I?","content.75.3605":"Hmmm... Hmmm...\\nIf possible, try not to damage it... I really treasure it.\\nIt's the most beautiful item in my collection!\\nTutaur'Kama is a role model for me: the greatest ruler from the Primitive Age of our World of Twelve.\\nGo on! Do what you have to do, but please don't destroy it.","content.75.3606":"Beggar? Are you kidding me?\\nI'm you're best chance at survival here. Everything I offer is worth its weight in kamas. And what I'm offering is the best information at the best price.\\nDon't you ever forget that!\\nI should make you pay for doubting my reputation...","content.75.3607":"Yes!\\nI made a little bet with the head guard at Sidimotes & Co. I told him that it would be no problem for me to get through the airlocks, and that his guards wouldn't be able to stop me.\\nHe laughed in my face, so I told him I'd already done it before and he could ask his boss if he didn't believe me. He snorted and still expressed doubt, telling me that I wouldn't be able to do it a second time.","content.75.3609":"What's that got to do with it? Well, it's obvious, isn't it?\\nThe first time, you were the one who helped me break into the factory. So, I'm suggesting to you that we try do it a second time. For the glory, and a well-deserved little reward, of course.\\nThis time, I'll put down the wager.\\nWhether you win or lose, we can try our luck once a day, every day.\\nIn future, you'll be the one paying the wager.","content.75.3610":"Great, I'll take the money and you try and sneak in through the three airlocks.\\nWhether you win or lose, we can try our luck once a day, every day.\\nGo ahead: I'll be right behind you!","content.75.3612":"Don't say a word... I know why you're here, little{[1*]?:} Scaraleaf. You want to learn the art of combat!","content.75.3613":"Haven't you been following anything that's been going on?\\nCharles-Henri is a fan - what an I saying? - is crazy about antiques, especially those from the Pharatauraons era. In particular, Tutaur'Kama.\\nHe must have got the mummy from the latter through means far more illicit than my services. And thanks to his talents as a genius engineer, he must have found a way to bring it back to life and modify it mechanically.","content.75.3614":"Well, it looks like Orichalcums aren't just keys to the Sunken Temple, but also formidable energy sources. Without doubt, it is this energy that opens the door by powering a technomagic circuit in the temple's foundations.\\nCharles-Henri must have found a way to connect this \"technomagic battery\" to his Mechamummy's circuits.","content.75.3615":"If you want to play, you have to pay!\\nFind us 500 kamas and we'll be in the running.","content.75.3616":"Sorry, the head guard isn't interested at the moment.\\nTry again later.","content.75.3617":"G...G-Good evening... What are you doing here? Can't you see it's dangerous?","content.75.3618":"I'm Père Lachaise, the caretaker of the cemetery. *Cough* One is always alone when carrying out such dark tasks... I'm doing well, even if it's not good living to grow old these days: Evil energies seem to be at work, and the area's infested with Raised Skeletons.","content.75.3619":"I can see you're not of the faint-hearted type, but that's still not enough. I suggest you keep on your toes with good reflexes by completing the Combat Challenges.","content.75.3620":"They appear at the beginning of each confrontation, and allow you to earn more experience and loot when you successfully complete them.\\nWhen I was your age, I completed them by the shovel load! But that was a long time ago... Before my career as a dancer, which has given me so many aches and pains.","content.75.3621":"Sshhh. You're gonna scare the fish! What d'ya want?","content.75.3622":"What's it look like? I'm fishin', that's all.","content.75.3623":"In general, I fish, alr'dy. Then I run the li'l bit of business going on around here, which isn't trivial either. T'was a time I was a brilliant sailor, li'l one. But all that's been over for a while now, so I recycled myself as best I could!","content.75.3624":"Oh yes, business. To do it, we do it! But everything's legal, huh, you can imagine... Then there are contracts that can yield great profit.\\nI don't know if you noticed, but there are plenty of mercenary contracts to pick up in town right now. You could get some great loot and experience there, and then you'd come back to do business with us! So, what do you say?","content.75.3625":"Hey!? Well look who's here! Aren't you the one who was running through the middle of my plants just now? Did you think you were on a dance floor?","content.75.3626":"You see, the ecosystem is like this little shoot. It's beautiful, it smells good, and if you're careful, it'll develop properly. So be careful!","content.75.3627":"Ah yes, I had noticed, given the smell! You'd be better trying the Environmental Quests then. They're different in each area and change regularly. You can even complete some of them just by walking around.","content.75.3628":"Their rewards are useful for crafting equipment. It seems that certain types of quests are available only when the Clan Member's wishes are respected, but shhh, that's just between us.","content.75.3629":"Yo. What can I do for you?","content.75.3630":"As long as no one ransacks my fields, all's good in the hood! And otherwise, well, I'll pitchfork them!\\nAnd so long as the neighbors don't make too much noise either! I feel like there are peasants coming by every five minutes to pick up new quests from the Guild of Hunters. And they natter even more than at village parties!","content.75.3631":"And then some! I'll let you touch them, but be careful. I'm very particular about the number of crops in my fields.","content.75.3632":"As with the other clan members, respecting my wishes is essential if the ecosystem is to successfully flourish. For example, you'll see more scarce resources, whole hordes of monsters showing off their good health, and other nice surprises! You have to respect the wishes of others whenever you visit a new region.","content.75.3633":"Hey you, penniless {[1*]?girl:guy}!","content.75.3634":"Who else? So, you're looking for adventure? You've come at the right time; there's plenty to be had at Croesus Scruge's place! But first of all... Do you have any kamas to invest in a most profitable experience for our two parties? We'll insure compensation exactly in proportion to the investment's duration, and in proportion to your diligence in completing the initial task, variable according to the actual difficulty encountered.","content.75.3635":"That doesn't matter! You don't need much to invest. Start by mining a bit, then head to the marketplace and sell what you've harvested to acquire your first few kamas. Then the rest will follow!","content.75.3636":"But wait a minute! If you see good old Pal, give her my compliments. And if that cranky old man Pal is around, add a little wink.","content.75.3637":"Hey, friend. Are you having a stroll or are you lost?","content.75.3638":"That, my friend, is to create the breeze that tickles you when you're strolling through the area.","content.75.3639":"It's my special dance to summon rain. Here, the climatic conditions are very important to maintain the forest's ecosystem.","content.75.3640":"Each resource has its own needs, and weather conditions affect how long things take, as well as the quantities you can harvest! Crazy, isn't it?","content.75.3641":"Hello little one, have you come to collect some seeds from the Gobballs?","content.75.3642":"Poor wretch! Not only does the natural cycle of the ecosystem need the delicate flick of your wrist, but what's more, the Guild of Hunters is experimenting on the seed of Astrubian monsters, and is offering you rewards if you bring them some!","content.75.3643":"One of their camps is located in the fields, near Melmac and Bettie Phenix. And there's another camp located in the sewers, where you can also find quests to complete and monsters to fight!","content.75.3645":"You can view the climate and information about each area's resources from the climate interface (by pressing the \"X\" key).","content.75.3647":"So you want to play tree-huggers?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3648":"If you encounter any issues or you're too afraid to head into the dungeon, you can take the staircase to my right back up to the surface. Don't forget that you can use this same exit to re-enter the gallery whenever you want.\\nThen, all you have to do is jump straight in and hope it works out... Well, that's what my dad - a dizzy old Iop who was a bit too fond of Bamboo Milk - would have done if he were still alive. Luckily, he isn't anymore.","content.75.3649":"One thing's certain: my blades are sharper than your mind. Keep going on like that and you'll get a free demonstration. Well, free for me, by quite costly for you.","content.75.3650":"It's quite simple. You put me on edge, I put you on my knife's edge. Is that good enough?...","content.75.3651":"You're a complete nutter to say that to me! Make another comment like that and I'll prune your ears, and everything between the two...","content.75.3652":"And if I had to dissect you, I'd do it with a scythe and an axe. Even your mother wouldn't recognize you...","content.75.3653":"You just don't know when to stop. I'm going to stop talking, and then I'll chop you up into dog meat for Charles-Henri's Bythards...","content.75.3654":"The quiet ones are always the most dangerous. And I don't like talking too much... I'm more a man of action...","content.75.3655":"You really have a problem. I'll crack your skull in two, and lop off your head...","content.75.3656":"I don't lack spirit. And yours will join Externam in no time if you don't hold your tongue.","content.75.3657":"Continue, and you're really going to taste my blades. And they won't lack spice, trust me. But they'll give you more than a bitter aftertaste...","content.75.3658":"If I'm a fisherman, then you're a big stupid fish writhing in my nets. If you kept calm you'd manage to get out of them, but you won't stop wriggling about, and I'm going to harpoon you...","content.75.3659":"Incisive, cutting, scathing, brutal... And more. And I don't just mean my spirit... Continue down this path and you'll discover all my qualities.","content.75.3660":"I am very polite, and I don't have ticks or tics. Now, if I consider something to be vermin, I crush it mercilessly.","content.75.3661":"Not rodents especially, but I'm champing at the bit, and I'm likely to bite if you don't change tactics. You're treading on thin ice, chum... and I'll be under it when it breaks...","content.75.3662":"The razor'll be all around your neck if you don't stop this masquerade...","content.75.3663":"Only masks I own are death masks - molded on the faces of my victims, and lined up above my fireplace. And you'll soon join my collection. ","content.75.3664":"I'll turn your fingers into a necklace once I've torn them off one by one, unless you stop your trickery...","content.75.3665":"The only top I know is where I nail the rope I tie around the necks of guys who chatter too much. They shouldn't time their chattering so badly...","content.75.3666":"Tying up Ouginak and bad luck in the corner is kinda like giving someone the axe to cut off their own head. Which is what will happen if you don't recognize the limits of your stupidity...","content.75.3667":"That's enough!\\nI've been patient enough with you. But it's over.\\nLet me be clear. Either you immediately stop your puns and your ridiculous lines, or you'll face the consequences.","content.75.3668":"Very well...\\n\\n*Skrapur seems to purse his lips and squint beneath his mask, staring at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3669":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3670":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3671":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3672":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3673":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3674":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3675":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3676":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3677":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3678":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3679":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3680":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3681":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3682":"...\\n\\n*Skrapur says nothing, and keeps starting at you coldly, without moving*","content.75.3683":"Okay.\\n\\n\\nYou win.","content.75.3684":"Are you blind by chance? I'm a guard. A guard of Mister Vileardent's personal militia!\\nNow move along, there's nothing to see here.","content.75.3685":"None of those, yet a bit of each mixed together. Except for the Hukl. Hukls really are quite ugly.\\nI'm a Lousy Bwork.\\nI'm a product of the modern biomagic, combining the best traits of several species of the World of Twelve. We get our main qualities from Bworks and Lousy Pigs, which makes us powerful, stubborn creatures, but also ones that are obedient to their leader.","content.75.3686":"Exotic dancing? I love that. Look, I can make your hormones do a waltz, make your heart race, or make all your extremities quiver... for the right price. But dancing's free and for my personal enjoyment, and I choose my own partners.","content.75.3687":"You know, if you slip a few piles of kamas in the slot... of my piggy bank, you're the one I'll set alight, from head to toe... You won't need heating to burn all night, or all day, or longer, should I see fit...","content.75.3688":"Hehehe! If you don't know what my work is, there's little chance of you needing my services.\\nCome back and see me when you have needs that match my specific skills...","content.75.3689":"But?! You come to me here to insult my work?\\nWhat do you think? Each bit of information I have to deliver comes at a specific cost - a price I had to pay. Whether in kamas, or services, or in exchange for other information. Information is power, and power comes at a price. And that price is the one I set.","content.75.3690":"I remember that once, he postponed an appointment with the governor of Brakmar by over two months, with no apology or explanation. The governor was furious! He chose 69 prisoners to be executed at random from Brakmar's jails. That was one for each day the appointment was pushed back, just to appease his frustration. He didn't utter a word of complaint to Mr. Vileardent himself, though. Oh no!\\nWhen you're dealing with a man as imposing as Charles-Henri, even the governor has to hold his tongue. All that reminds me of another...","content.75.3692":"The door? Haaaa THE DOOR? Haha... This very special door gives access to very specific places... but also very dangerous places... I'm not sure you're tough enough to face what may be beyond this passage...","content.75.3693":"*The old man looks at you from top to bottom with a smile* Sorry kid{[1*]?:}, but you're not broad-shouldered enough to walk through this door, it would be certain death. Come back once you've faced the most powerful creatures in the World of Twelve!","content.75.3694":"*The old man looks at you carefully from top to bottom* Hmm, actually, you seem to be an{[1*]?:} unusual adventurer{[1*]?:}. I feel great power in you... In that case, you may prove useful to me... And if you agree to do a \"small favor\" for me, I'll allow you to walk through this door and you'll see for yourself what lies behind it...","content.75.3695":"*From beneath his cape, the old man takes out a huge white egg with prismatic reflections* I see in your eyes that you understand what this is... Yes, it's a Dofus! This is a Dofus of Nogord Wungleezared, a Minor Prismatic Dragon from a world long forgotten... But this Dofus is weak, very weak... But I have an idea of how to strengthen it, and that's where you come in!","content.75.3696":"*The old man cracks a smile* You may be powerful{[1*]?:} but not necessarily very smart{[1*]?:} from what I can see! It seems to me that you've traveled through Xelor's dimension, right? So you know that it's possible for you to cross rifts to navigate between the past, the present and the future? It just so happens that behind this door, I managed to update a rift allowing you to return to the past, to the golden age of Nogord, in the hope of one day finding adventurers able to face him again. If you're feeling fit and brave{[1*]?:} enough for this test, I'll let you walk through the door and continue on your epic mission!","content.75.3697":"Hmm, my Dofus is still the same; you mustn't have defeated Nogord in the past yet.","content.75.3698":"Hey! Where did you come from? Are you completely nuts, coming here??? You're in Nogord's Lair! Run, you fool!","content.75.3699":"*bursts out laughing* Hahahaha! That's it! I see it all now: My project is paying off! I knew I'd need a little help... Nogord is pig-headed, and refuses to lay a Dofus easily. He only understands strength and power. I guess that my current experiments will allow me to get a Dofus, but that will be weak. So, I'll have the idea of making adventurers come back to the current time from a later time, to face Nogord again. What a great idea!","content.75.3700":"Others! You adventurers are the first to go beyond danger whenever there's a slight possibility of glory or wealth, and sometimes, even just for your ego of having survived death once again! I'm offering you the great honor of challenging a dragon, a DRAGON!!! Can you imagine the legend you'd become if you managed to defeat it???","content.75.3701":"Th... There you are again...! I can't believe it, you won? Or maybe you didn't even dare attend the fight...? ","content.75.3702":"Wow, I can't believe it! That's good... very good, even! If you annoyed him enough by showing him strength and power, he should produce a better Dofus than the one I should soon have, if what you say is true. Now you need to go back to your time to see the result of your efforts with my older self! ","content.75.3703":"*The old mentor looks at you with a disappointed expression* Well, I've noticed the changes you caused in the past, and I congratulate you: you managed to stand up to Nogord and that truly is an achievement worthy of a{[1*]?:} great{[1*]?:} hero{[1*]?:}! But unfortunately, it wasn't enough. The Dofus I inherited is barely more powerful than the first one; let's just say that nothing has changed, unfortunately...","content.75.3704":"You should know that you can come and see me when you want by using the Astrub Zaap to return to Incarnam.\\nIf you really need me, you can also activate the \"Otomai Finisher\", and I'll come and help you defeat a boss, or a monster now and then, when I have the time!","content.75.3705":"I knew you were a reasonable person!","content.75.3706":"Go and open the temple door; I'm right behind you, and the others too!","content.75.3707":"This is the Sufokia submersible Hangar; we shouldn't have any problem finding a vessel to take us through the rift we saw beneath the temple.","content.75.3708":"Just try it and find out! But I assure you it's very solid; it's good recovered wood! And you won't waste your money for nothing! It's 100 kamas a head, but hey... you seem nice, so I'll give you a deal on the trip: 500 kamas for your whole group!","content.75.3709":"Go down this ladder to get into the Hangar Swimming Pool.\\nAnd it's 700 kamas for a diving license and to hire a diving costume!","content.75.3710":"Well, I have good news and bad news! The good news is that you have your diving license. The bad news is that the Smash'kull has a technical problem... our submersible's watertightness needs to be reviewed. So we're in maintenance and can't accept anyone on board! Come back next time!","content.75.3711":"Well.. I'd like to thank you for saving the Nemotilus from this monster's tentacles! But that doesn't mean we're going to get friendly! I'll make you a deal: whenever you want to go to Oktapodas's Temple, you can use my Nemotilus. But let's be clear: only this journey. Beyond that, we don't know each other!","content.75.3712":"We absolutely have to catch this Gankr before he trashes this temple!\\nAmelia and Mimi will lend you a hand. I'd be of no use to you in combat. But come back and see me after defeating that horrible lunatic!","content.75.3714":"How I would have liked to be present for the opening of this Sunken Temple. In the end, you were right to look for all these Orichalcums! A great adventure, in short!","content.75.3715":"Captain Nautilor, at your service!\\nInterested in my vessel?","content.75.3716":"Oh! You'll pay nothing but a trifle to enjoy a trip on board my Nemotilus.","content.75.3717":"Let's see... I've heard about a source of powerful energy called Orichalcum. If you bring me 3 of them, I'll be happy to take you where you want.","content.75.3718":"Well then, bring me some cloudy Moogrr Mimilk.\\nYou'll find some in the pastures of Amakna.\\nI'm almost all out, and I have to make the final preparations to the Nemotilus for our departure!","content.75.3719":"Captain Nautilor, at your service!\\nThe Nemotilus is currently in dock for maintenance; please come back when we're up and running to go on a trip!","content.75.3720":"AH! My cloudy Moogrr Mimilk to oil up my arm! Finally!\\nI really needed it!","content.75.3721":"Leave? Why!?\\nI'm still waiting for my payment; I asked you for 3 Orichalcums. \\nDo you have them?","content.75.3722":"Hahaha! You do make me laugh! I just asked you for a favor while waiting for the preparations for the trip, but it's Orichalcums that I asked you for as a token gift for my vessel! ","content.75.3723":"No ORICHALCUMS, no SUBMERSIBLE.","content.75.3725":"Take a seat and taste this delicious buffet!","content.75.3726":"for validation","content.75.3727":"You can't leave me like this with these Riktus!\\nI've got nothing to do with this Hullcatz rebel!","content.75.3729":"Hey, cabin boy!\\nDoes my vessel tickle your fancy?\\nWould you like to go on a little ride? I'll offer you the most attractive price in this Hangar!","content.75.3730":"Thanks for getting me out of this ambush, cabin boy! I sent that belligerent Hullcatz back home!\\nWithout you, my great vessel, the \"Fleebagh\", would have fallen into the hands of these awful bandits! My hair stands on end just thinking about it!","content.75.3731":"Come and see me later; I'm adjusting the vessel's spine for the moment!","content.75.3733":"If you're looking for a submersible - a real one - my vessel, the Smash'kull, is the best on the market. \\nIt can reach the deepest of the oceans!","content.75.3734":"Nothing could be easier!\\nThe Smash'kull floats using multiple buoys filled with air below its hull.\\nOnce we're ready to leave, my crew will pierce all these buoys and presto: The Smash'kull will abruptly sink!","content.75.3735":"Nothing could be easier!\\nBefore boarding, you must acquire your diving license.\\nOnce you have this license, my men will kit you out in a diving suit, and all you'll need to do is come back up to the surface.","content.75.3736":"We're trying to sort out our watertightness problems.\\nMy whole crew thanks you for your interest in our beautiful Smash'kull!","content.75.3737":"Please, get on board!","content.75.3739":"Oh! I see you've finally got the 3 Orichalcums!","content.75.3740":"It can't have been easy, negotiating this last Orichalcum!","content.75.3741":"Now that you're here, all we have to do is risk it all.\\nIf my analyses are correct, you just need to place the Orichalcums in the holes in the door. They should discharge all their energy to open it.","content.75.3742":"I can't wait to be able to explore Oktapodas's Sunken Temple!\\nI can already imagine myself bringing back a fabulous archaosological treasure and receiving honors from my nation!","content.75.3743":"Take this vessel, the Fleebagh!\\nFor the qual... price! There's nothing better!","content.75.3744":"Well this vessel surely isn't of good quality. And getting attacked by some Riktus... I couldn't have anticipated that, who could have?\\nNonetheless, it's still the cheapest in the Hangar!","content.75.3745":"Don't listen to Lebbocq, you'll get into trouble!","content.75.3746":"Wow, did you see that \"Smash'kull\"? What splendid Bwork architecture! ","content.75.3747":"Well, such a result was only to be expected! With Bwork know-how, the odds of that happening are only 1 in 100.","content.75.3748":"What could they be keeping behind this door...?","content.75.3749":"I'm looking forward to seeing what's hiding behind this door!","content.75.3750":"So go and visit my beautiful Nemotilus!","content.75.3752":"Go down this ladder to get into the Hangar Swimming Pool.","content.75.3753":"Psshtt! Then it's true!\\nWill you finally be able to open this door!?\\nI can't wait to find out what's inside! I hope it's worthwhile!","content.75.3754":"I can't wait to find out what's inside! I hope it's worthwhile!","content.75.3755":"Thanks to me, and with your help, we've finally got our hands on the last Orichalcum!\\nNothing left but to open this door! I insist: After you!","content.75.3757":"Like I told you, you need three items to serve as the key: Orichalcums. I see that you have three of them!\\nIf my information proves to be correct, you just need to place these three keys in the holes in the door, and the mechanism will be triggered!","content.75.3758":"It seems that this temple was reserved for genuine followers of Oktapodas. Penetrating its depths required practicing a very specific ritual: performing gestures, by positioning oneself where the god instructed. I wonder if these tiles...","content.75.3759":"It's written: \"The One Eye sees all. The Eight Tentacles are the Guardians of the Temple\". Actually, you see that majestic statue in the middle of the room? It's staring right at us!","content.75.3760":"There's a heavy atmosphere in this enormous room. I think... the best thing would be to greet the god Oktapodas, don't you? To excuse ourselves for entering his home without having been invited.","content.75.3761":"\"One mistake, and the Anger of Oktapodas will pour down on you. The Temple is defended by...\"\\nThe next part has been erased. I hope we won't set off a trap or attract dangerous creatures...","content.75.3762":"Hurry up, I can't wait to get my hands on the treasures locked up in here.","content.75.3763":"\"The young follower is free to express his anger as much as he wants to, but only if it is centered on himself. There's no room for quarrels within the Temple.\"","content.75.3764":"\"The sound of hands should not imitate the lapping of the waves, but remind the enemy that Oktapodas will trigger a Tidal Wave.\"","content.75.3765":"\"When they present themselves on the balconies on the right, the Champions of Oktapodas receive applause from fans, before heading into combat.\"","content.75.3766":"\"Celebrating Oktapodas is a party. His servant must thank him by being overjoyed. But he must do so as far away from him as possible, in order not to disturb his watchful sleep.\"","content.75.3767":"Go and open the temple door; I'm right behind you, and the others too!","content.75.3768":"\"Do not be afraid of letting weakness take over, because doing so is to give Oktapodas a gift of the salt water of your own body, by linking it to the Great Ocean. Performing this ritual as close as possible to Oktapodas ensures you'll have a calm day.","content.75.3769":"\"Oktapodas is fair to his people, but ruthless. To express your obedience, you should demonstrate that he is feared more than anything, but without fleeing, because his anger is recognized.\"","content.75.3770":"\"If the faithful need to express their tiredness, may they do so far from Oktapodas, who suffers no slackers.\"","content.75.3771":"Help me find a way to access the unlocking system for the upper hatch!","content.75.3772":"Go up this ladder and see what's going on outside!","content.75.3773":"Not really for no reason; we know that an action in the past can influence the present, and that's a major breakthrough for my project! Now all we need to do is whatever it takes to force Nogord to provide a more powerful Dofus. I have an idea of how to go about it. Your fight was impressive, but I think it'll take more for this dragon. You'll have to go and train yourself to be prepared.","content.75.3774":"You came away unharmed{[1*]?:}! What a relief! The Nations' adventure ends here, but what an adventure! If only our archaosologist quarrels could also disappear behind us... but I feel that it's not going to get any better. At least my next dig site will be in the Wild Estate; I hope to see you there!","content.75.3775":"Perfect! So, to train yourself, you'll need to go to the dungeons in the Divine Dimensions and activate their Stasis versions.","content.75.3776":"So, have you finished your training?","content.75.3777":"Very good! Now that you're properly trained, go back and face Nogord in the past as many times as it takes to completely master his secrets, and succeed in beating him with a whopping! That should make him provide a Dofus worthy of the name.","content.75.3778":"*Piqued, the old mentor lets out a long sigh* It's no use... The Dofus has indeed improved, but it's too unstable for me to use it. I think Nogord won't do any better this way, and I don't have any more ideas... Too bad... Bravo! You are truly{[1*]?:} an exceptional Hero{[1*]?:}. To reward you for all your efforts, this Dofus is now yours.","content.75.3779":"Yes, you've earned it. Good luck, champion. A great future awaits you!","content.75.3780":"Safe travels!","content.75.3781":"We absolutely have to catch this Gankr before he trashes this temple!\\nAmelia and Mimi will lend you a hand; I'd be of no use in combat, but come back and see me after defeating that horrible madman!","content.75.3782":"Hmm... A nightmarish creature is blocking the way. \\nI'll let you face it!","content.75.3783":"This discovery keeps its promises. We have proof that Sufokia was once one of the most impressive lands of its time. Look at these beautiful colonnades... the craftsmen of the past had more style than today's!","content.75.3784":"These little streams aren't going to impress me. What interests me in archaosology is finding the riches that previous generations have left us. Have you found something?","content.75.3785":"Oh. Hey little one, stop whining, come on! An old skinflint like me always has a solution. Since such a trifle isn't worth a lot - at least, not to me - I'll give you one of mine for 100,000 kamas. What do you say?","content.75.3786":"Hi! Did you come to admire me? \\nPeople come from everywhere just to see me! When I'm not busy hunting Moowolves, I come here to complete my collection of skulls and beauty products. Spring Has Sprung monsters have excellent resources!","content.75.3789":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3790":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3791":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3792":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3793":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3794":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3795":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3796":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3797":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3798":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3799":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.3800":"Have you noticed this cloudy crevasse? I can see you have! And I bet you're wondering how to cross it, and my answer is simple: with a special artifact!","content.75.3801":"Yes, I am indeed talking about this Artifact: the Ocarina, charmer of dragons. As it happens, charmer of your little Wyrmling. Despite his small pair of wings, he should be able to cross the crevasse without any problem. All you have to do is make the big leap!","content.75.3802":"Ahhh...\\nI can't wait to go back home... there's really nothing fun about looking for old floating balls...","content.75.3803":"It wasn't so terrible accepting my offer! For your first mission, you need to collect a Mollusky Egg and bring it to me! But start by analyzing the behavior of a \"Snailmet\" and a \"Darth Mussel\". I'll show you the steps to take, so follow them well!","content.75.3804":"Oh, well, a very specific artifact, I assure you! \\nIt can only be acquired in the somber Oktapodas Temple, and nowhere else!","content.75.3805":"Oh, but of course! Join me quickly, then!","content.75.3806":"Something quite amusing! \\nI'll allow you to explore our Wild Camp, but you need to collect an artifact called the \"Excarnal Scepter\", because a mere human like you can't enter just like that!","content.75.3807":"Explore our Wild Camp; an amusing surprise awaits you there!\\nI'll show you the steps to take, so follow them well!","content.75.3808":"Your next mission will be as easy as the first! You need to collect a Selachii Egg and bring it to me! But start by analyzing the behavior of a \"Hammer Selachii\" and a \"Spear Selachii\". I'll show you the steps to take, so follow them well!","content.75.3809":"I heard about a lovely treasure hidden on this beach: a brilliant shell! You must expect that I want it, of course! But you need to recover an artifact called \"Paws of Ecaflip\" to be able to explore every nook and cranny of the beach and get your hands on the shell!","content.75.3810":"Bring me the pretty Abandoned Shell on this beach, and I'll give you a good bit of information!\\nI'll show you the steps to take, so follow them well!","content.75.3811":"Who are you?","content.75.3812":"That's all!? HEHEHE!\\nCome on, you're no match for that monster; you wouldn't even be strong enough against me!\\nGo back where you came from; it'd be better for you!","content.75.3813":"Sorry. Meeting such a hopeless case as you makes me forget my good manners. Me name's Mishell, and I still say you're no match for me, nor for my companions. But I'd like to reconsider if you help me out with a few things!","content.75.3814":"Oh, do what you like! You can stay weak and ignorant, or... a little stronger and less ignorant. If you help me, I'll reveal some information to you... useful information! \\nWhat do you say?","content.75.3815":"After all, do what you like! \\nYour fate doesn't matter to me, but if you come across Kali, I wouldn't give you much for your chances!","content.75.3816":"no answers without compensation! Do you not concur!?","content.75.3817":"What an offer, HAHA! Who could refuse a Schnek egg?\\nBut first of all, I suggest you go and take a look at their cave, in order to find a passage.","content.75.3819":"You dare question what I say!? \\nIf I tell you it's there, it's because it's there!","content.75.3820":"You're not as weak as I thought! \\nThank you for the Mollusky Egg. I'll put it with the others I've collected since I got here.","content.75.3821":"Kali is a friend of mine; we were part of the same \"family\", one which I'm particularly affectionate for. She is sometimes impulsive and doesn't like weaklings, but she is charming. She told me that when she was young, she met Ogrest before he lost reason!","content.75.3822":"Indeed! \\nYou wanted to find out about Kali? ","content.75.3823":"Like I said: no answers without compensation! \\nI want to see what you're worth, and I've got a little idea about how to do so!","content.75.3825":"It's about time; I was starting to think you'd never come back!\\nAll that's left to do is to go and see the holes near the Schnek Cave and try out the wand!\\nI'm coming with you; it'll give me the chance to stretch my legs!","content.75.3826":"That's a nice surprise, isn't it!? I wanted to see what my darling Gobgob thought, and I think he likes you! So, I'll let you ask me a question before I give you your next mission!","content.75.3827":"HEHEHE! Good question, adventurer! Unfortunately for you, it's a secret that I cannot reveal; just know that in my family, we're ALL quite particular! HEHE!","content.75.3828":"Hmmm... no! It wouldn't be a game! \\nAnd I'm starting to have fun on this beach, at last! I like you!","content.75.3829":"No, no! I love animals, and I want as many species as possible!","content.75.3830":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3832":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3833":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3834":"Fantastic, another egg for my monster collection!\\nYou deserve a reward, adventurer!","content.75.3835":"We have greater ambitions than defeating that monster, Ogrest! \\nAnd if we're here, it's so we can collect as many floating balls as possible: Silos! They're really useful to us!","content.75.3836":"Sure, if you manage! I wouldn't bet my money on you, HAHAHA!\\nReady for your next mission?","content.75.3837":"It's really beautiful; I dreamed of offering one as beautiful as this to my darling Gobgob! He really loves this delicacy!\\nSo, I'm going to reveal a very important bit of information to you!","content.75.3838":"Of course my information is useful to you! So listen carefully!\\nTo become even more powerful, you'll need to spend some time around the Schneks!","content.75.3841":"Hmmm, yes, I've got some. But thinking about it, I noticed a group of pirates not far from here... If you know what I mean! By the way, you didn't see a pretty shell on the beach, did you? My Gobgob's very fond of them!","content.75.3842":"Oh, very well! I guess you deserve one or two little anecdotes about Mount Zinit.\\nFor example, did you know that by changing a few letters in Mount Zinit, you get \"Mount Limit\"?\\nOr that people say that this volcano holds the secrets of an ancient civilization? Well, you'll be able to see all that for yourself if you keep on exploring!","content.75.3843":"Ullu? I don't know this \"Ullu\", but speaking of an artifact that lets you go and visit the Schneks... I've heard of a wand that shrinks whoever uses it... well, enough to get through those holes.","content.75.3844":"Ah!!! Before you go, don't forget to give me my Schnek Egg!","content.75.3845":"The Schneks are still quite peculiar monsters. Very little elegance, very little sophistication, but what organization around their queen!\\nI like this place; I'm going to have a bit of fun here!","content.75.3846":"I hope you'll go far and not die right away!\\nThen, if you meet the other members of my \"family\", tell them to hurry up a little; I'd quite like to go home!","content.75.3847":"Hmmm... I think it's called the \"Rikiki Wand\"!\\nIf my memory serves me right, it can be found on Monk Island, in a secret room in the Undieworld Dungeon.","content.75.3849":"This place really isn't made for humans! Even if I help you, I maintain that you must leave as fast as possible! I see so many souls, tormented by my son, arrived in Incarnam, that I've lost count of them... Although there has been a strange reincarnation... This incarnate gave off huge amounts of Wakfu!","content.75.3850":"Let's have a look!","content.75.3851":"You'll be able to go and collect the last tears you need to create the second antidote!\\nAnd I promise you this one will effectively eradicate the poison from your body; you'll be completely immune to Mount Zinit's miasma. However, you still need to confront the Whirlies, and particularly the Silmawhirly, who has accumulated an abnormally high volume of Ogrest's Tears in himself, which will be enough for us. In your state, that could prove to be quite difficult!","content.75.3852":"Oh! The camp?! My darling Gobgob helped me transport everything, and while you were using your wand, I had the time to set up my cosy little nest and join you!","content.75.3853":"I hope your encounter with Queen Schnek was very pleasant for you.","content.75.3854":"You're exaggerating... she's still a queen! And meeting a queen is quite pleasant!\\nAnyhow, during your royal stay, I went for a stroll in this enormous cave, and came across a magnificent oasis with splendid, Luminescent Water!","content.75.3855":"All you need to do is go and see for yourself, and you'll realize the beauty of the flourishing paradise and its Luminescent Water!","content.75.3856":"There's nothing left but to start alchemy!","content.75.3857":"I'll cross the cliff with you! \\nI've got a bad feeling about this...","content.75.3858":"No, that won't replace fighting against her! But he'll get you ready for it, and you'll become more powerful! \\nTraining is non-trivial if you want to have a chance against Kali!\\nSo don't be stubborn, and confront the Drhellers so you'll be ready to face what's waiting for you at the end of this trek!","content.75.3859":"I see that your training was a success; you'll no doubt be able to face other dangers...\\nWhile taking a stroll during your absence, I found a strange wall to the northeast of the slope.\\nIt's strangely smooth, and... how can I put it? You'd better go and have a look for yourself; you'll see what I mean!","content.75.3860":"I'm still wary... entering the vessel of an ancient civilization, not knowing what you'll find there... Stay on your guard! What's more... That Ullu! I wonder if he's really telling you the truth... \\nUnfortunately, I must let you progress on your own from here on; I've also got things to do in Incarnam! The last bit of advice I can give you, young, stubborn adventurer... Don't die!","content.75.3861":"Now's the time!\\nTime to say \"goodbye\" to you!\\nTime for you to finally find out how to swim! Hehehe!","content.75.3862":"Luckily, we came out unscathed, but that may not be the case next time!","content.75.3863":"Kali is quite formidable, I can assure you. I hope you won't have to face her!","content.75.3864":"I won't manage to make you change your mind about the danger... So listen carefully! There's a formidable opponent who goes by the name of Rascal. \\nA terrible Drheller living in a Haven Bag, stolen from its owner and hidden here. ","content.75.3865":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3867":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3868":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3869":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3870":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3872":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3873":"Woooah... Leave me alone!","content.75.3874":"Say what? You want to know what became of Ruel and I? I'll tell you what happened!\\nRuel poked his head into the tunnels of an island not far from Zinit. As soon as we were in the tunnels, we were overrun by Drhellers!\\nAnd then, there was him...\\nA gigantic monster, an abomination! I'd never seen anything like it! It had been lying beneath the surface for thousands of years, at least! I've seen many Drhellers in my life, but one like that... my word, never!\\nAs far back as the stories about Mount Zinit go, there has only been one creature like it: Rascal, King of the Drhellers.\\nWe were stuck in the tunnels, with nowhere to take refuge. That's when I placed a bomb in the tunnels. Years of Drheller gas, which had built up in the tunnels, you can imagine... it exploded like an ancestral Bwork fire! We were launched far from the island! I then understood what had happened; as for me, I landed on a bale of hay! Ruel wanted to protect himself from the explosion using his bag, and I think a number of Drhellers got sucked into it.\\nThe last thing I saw was Ruel getting his Haven Bag ripped from his arms by the blast of the explosion. Who knows what's happened to the old skinflint...?","content.75.3875":"Yeah, well, while waiting, I... I'm going to compose myself...","content.75.3878":"Well actually... Yes, it was indeed me who caused those explosions. That's to say, when I came here, I didn't succeed in making my antidotes the first time round, and there were a few failures. Sorry!","content.75.3879":"Yes, there was indeed a problem with the assembly process. It's quite common on Zinit, with all this miasma. The relic's fragments were corrupted by the miasma's effects, and weren't able to guide their power into this item.\\nI want to unlock part of its power right now, but if you want me to release its whole potential, you'll need to bring me several Relic Inhibitors, each quite specific and rare.","content.75.3880":"Nicely done! I'll take care of the ritual.\\n[...]\\nYup, I've unlocked the hidden secrets of your relic. It's much more powerful than before!\\nGood luck for the remainder of your quest!","content.75.3881":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.3883":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3884":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3885":"YOU SHALL NOT PASS!!! Unless you have a Mercenary License for this area of course... I can supply you with one if necessary, for a small fee, naturally. ","content.75.3887":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.3888":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.3889":"So you want to play at environmentalists?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3890":"So you want to play at environmentalists?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3891":"So you want to play at environmentalists?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3892":"There you are! Chosen One{[1*] ?e:} of the Prophecy!","content.75.3893":"Are you here to help me?","content.75.3894":"Alas... Yes, that's my body you see behind me. Or what's left of it.","content.75.3895":"Oh, yes, that... It's extraordinary magic. It took me a long time to understand how it works, but before my body became to weak I managed to transfer my consciousness into this ship... and survive, in a manner of speaking. So, will you help me?","content.75.3896":"No, sorry, of course not... I'm just looking for a solution. I'm stuck in here, but you're not. You should explore these ruins: they might not be in the same condition as in your era. You should start with the Archive Room, take the corridor that leads down.","content.75.3897":"Marvelous! You've got the last Artifact, the one that will let you travel back in time! Return to the Cryo Room, you can use it to go and get me before I died, and save my life! Please, hurry!","content.75.3898":"Yes, okay, I do owe you a few explanations. I'm making you take risks, you should at least know why. Actually, it's a little embarrassing, but I'm very clumsy... I've got myself stuck in here with no way out.","content.75.3899":"I am, how should I put it... A sort of freelance archaosologist. I came to the heart of the danger on Mount Zinit because I believe most of the answers can be found here. The archaosologists of the four nations only work for the benefit of their governments. But I don't work for anyone.","content.75.3900":"What? No way, not really! How could you say such a thing? Look, during my digging I was obviously fascinated by this spot... it's like nothing we've ever seen before! This technology is nothing like ours! And that's when the drama started.","content.75.3901":"I was totally absorbed by the magnificence of this place when the door shut behind me. I might of triggered a security system when I tried to take... I mean \"examine\" a few objects. As for the rest... it's like this: Without the I.D.S. we can't get out.","content.75.3902":"Oh, so you're leaving now? Why don't you stay and chat a while?","content.75.3903":"That's absolute codswallop. The divine artifacts? And transfer my consciousness into these ruins? It will be a ship to travel through the Krosmoz? I thought I'd already reached rock bottom, but now I find myself trapped with {[1*]?a madman:madwoman}... Stay away from me.","content.75.3904":"Wait! I've been here for 3 days and I can't find any way out. I'd completely lost hope. Forgive me for my reaction. If there's any chance what you're saying is true, I'd like to come along. What do we do?","content.75.3905":"These Artifacts... If I understand correctly, they won't allow me to come with you. It looks like they can only be used by one person at a time. Which means... GIVE 'EM TO ME!!!","content.75.3906":"So please... Leave me...","content.75.3907":"I'd really like to chat, but don't you want to get rid of these monsters first? They're annoying me...","content.75.3908":"In the worst case scenario, if I manage to transfer my consciousness... oh well, this promises to be a fascinating experience. I would probably gain access to an incredible amount of information on the people that built this place. It's not the life I planned for myself, but I don't have a choice. Farewell!","content.75.3909":"This is a great step forward! But honestly, you're not thinking of leaving without me? I still have to get out of here.","content.75.3910":"But why? Do you want to leave me to die here? Why would you be so cruel? I beg you, don't leave me!","content.75.3911":"Fantastic! All you have to do now is follow the rest of the instructions you found in the Archive Room.","content.75.3912":"What? You didn't find any other instructions? There's nothing that says how to open the other doors? Are you going to leave me here? I'll have to stay trapped in this room?","content.75.3913":"I see... Honestly, I've thought about everything you told me when you arrived. Everything you've done for me, all the things I've been able to learn here or by following your adventures... I don't think there's any way to get rid of me. Not of your own accord.","content.75.3914":"If I want to get out, I'll do it myself. There has to be a way to leave again, all this technology will help me. I'll take as long as I need, but I'll find out how it works in the end. Don't worry about me, you've given me hope again.","content.75.3915":"Finally, we didn't manage to change my fate... Forgive me for lying. I couldn't think of any other solution. Having said that, it could have been worse. I could have never met anyone as fantastic as you! Keep on walking, don't mind me, it's not so bad here.","content.75.3916":"Exactly the way you left it! Go, leave, take back your freedom, Chosen One{[1*]?e:} of the Prophecy!","content.75.3917":"Oh, but what have we here? A training scarecrow? It's kind of you to come all this way to get thrashed! Shall I start with the left cheek or the right?","content.75.3918":"You're really starting to rile me up with your stories. I'm not here to listen to your complaints. If you have a problem with my servants, go and challenge a few of them, they love a good fight. If you still have a mouth to talk with, come and see me afterwards.","content.75.3919":"Okay, so you've decided to really tick me off. I've had it up to here with you. If you want to get truly pummeled, show me what you've got by fighting my best elements, in the Sanctuary. If you make it through that, I'll come and finish you off.","content.75.3920":"I'm not hanging out on this forsaken mountain for nothing. Have you ever seen the Silos, those spheres that let you move quickly from one place to another? I need to retrieve a few of them. Don't ask me why, that's my business!","content.75.3921":"I understand! In the meantime, there's something else you can do for me. There's a rockslide in the cave, a little further on. Find a way to get past it! A big sort of hammer should do the job, and I've heard there's a really massive one on Moon Island.","content.75.3923":"What do you want to know?","content.75.3924":"Oh, that's right... I'm not quite as \"divine\" as I pretend to be. You have to understand, it's better to embellish the story a bit to make sure you'll come all the way through. As for the Prophecy, that's true in some respects. Are you the one who came{[1*] ?e:} to talk to me, in the past.","content.75.3925":"The Artifacts? I know they exist because you told me about them, a long time ago... I'm not sure why this ship uses them. This place isn't linked to any deity, and yet all over the mountain there are ways to use them. Maybe the Eliatropes learned how to use them? They were a people with highly advanced technology.","content.75.3926":"Yes, a ship! These aren't ruins from this world! I understood that when I fused my spirit with this gigantic machine. Some of the elements make me think it was used to travel through the Krosmoz. Do you understand what that means? Oh, I can see you're starting to think I'm crazy again...","content.75.3927":"You want to know who I was in the past? Goodness me, I don't know if I'm the best person to tell you all that, my memories are fading... Try to see with my \"me\" of the past, when I was still something other than a huge machine.","content.75.3928":"Oh! You found a sacred hammer! I imagine you had to work hard to get it. Anyhow, that's exactly what we need to open up the passage in the cave.","content.75.3930":"You want to know who I am?","content.75.3931":"No, I don't have any family. I could have had, but... Well, I decided to focus on my work. I'd like to say I don't regret it, but now that I'm stuck in here, I admit I wish I'd chosen a different life.","content.75.3932":"Actually, I spent my whole childhood at Bonta, but that's not important to me. My mother came from Sufokia and my father's from Amakna, so I have no reason to prefer one nation over another. I think war is foolish, and everything would be a lot better if we could all work together. But until that day arrives, I prefer to work for myself.","content.75.3933":"Yes, it was a stupid accident, really. I came in through a crack on another level. I'd never seen such technology in my life, and so well-preserved! I completely forgot to be careful, and wound up lost. A real rookie's mistake. I started activating mechanisms randomly and I think I closed all the doors...","content.75.3934":"Okay. You're not as pathetic as you look. If you're so determined to stay in the area, maybe you can help me in some way.","content.75.3935":"No. Should I?","content.75.3936":"Hahaha! Go and play somewhere else, moskito!","content.75.3937":"Oh yes... Otomai. I see that it didn't really work. Now you're back to annoy me, just as I thought. I should have taken care of it myself.","content.75.3938":"Why? Because you were with Otomai, and I wanted to tantalize him a little. Unfortunately, if we want things done properly we have to do them ourselves. Listen, I'm getting sick you now. Buzz off or I'll drown you in the river.","content.75.3939":"What? Did my lackeys hurt you? Oh, poor dear{[1*] ?e:}... Do you want some candy?","content.75.3940":"I don't like sissies, so get lost!","content.75.3941":"If you can't calm down, I'd prefer to stop this conversation right now.","content.75.3942":"Oh yeah, you want to fight me? Had enough of life, eh? If you want to get the thrashing of your life, show me what you've got first by fighting my best warriors, in the Sanctuary. If you make it to through that, I'll come and finish you off.","content.75.3943":"Great! If you weren't so insignificant, I might even have thanked you! I might even start to feel like letting you live! Nah, I'm exaggerating a little... But we're not here to get all warm and fuzzy.","content.75.3945":"Look at this! All these monsters to slug! I have a challenge for you: The first one who brings back the Badgwitch Left Eye will make the other person their slave. So, do you accept? Careful now; it has to be the left one! Start by practicing on its little friends; they're more your size.","content.75.3946":"The problem is that I accidentally destroyed the aerial convoy that brings me Capsules, while I was training to fight flying targets. I couldn't ask the Count for more, so it would be really great if you could go and retrieve the ones that survived the fall. You'll find them spread all over Mount Zinit, I hit hard.","content.75.3947":"Oh! My favorite dogsbody! Are you coming to work for me?","content.75.3949":"Haha! Yeah, I see you thrashed that big teddybear, but I was a lot faster! Oh, you want proof? No need for that, I'M the one who decides the rules around here! And that means YOU are my slave!","content.75.3950":"Yes, alright, calm down. I was joking. You have no sense of humor. Well, on a more serious note, I have a favor to ask. Could you go and retrieve a load of Cooling Capsules, sent by a Count I know? You wouldn't refuse that to a friend, would you?","content.75.3951":"In fact, it's so you can come with me... With enough Capsules, you can make a protective suit and follow me into the cave full of molten lava a little further up. Isn't that exciting?","content.75.3952":"No, are you doing that on purpose? That wasn't the challenge. I want the LEFT EYE of Badgwitch, you'll have to go and find it in his burrow. Go!","content.75.3953":"Ask me questions, I'll choose whether I want to answer.","content.75.3954":"The tall guy who lived on his island and never cut his hair? His missed out on life. He could have done so many things with us, but... Well, that's his bad luck, he'll always be a loser. You should choose your friends more wisely. On the other hand, without him, no Ogrest and no Chaos... I almost admire him a little.","content.75.3955":"Oh, you met Mishell? And you survived? You're lucky because if you had made her angry... But you didn't, you're here, so you behaved yourself. But be careful, If I find out you hurt her I'll feed you to the Gobgob myself.","content.75.3956":"I like it here, you can get rid of troublemakers without leaving a trace. Speaking of which, what brought you here?","content.75.3957":"But anyway, we're not here to have fun. I still need you to go and get a few things for me. I need some Sacred Basalt for my personal use. You don't think I made you come here to relax did you?","content.75.3958":"Not bad. But I'll need some more equipment... You're not scared of getting burned are you? You can find more Sacred Basalt on the lifeless body of their chief, Sor'Hon, the leader of the monsters who live here. Of course, you'll have to be the one to make him lifeless first. The entrance is inside the stream of lava, it's guaranteed to be gentle on skin.","content.75.3959":"BUT WHY WON'T YOU JUST DIE?! Um... Sorry, my emotions got the better of me. Just give me the Sacred Basalt and go; I'm sick of trying to make you die in atrocious pain. If you want to go and cozy up to Ogrest, you'll find a path at the end of the cave. But the Summit is still a long way away!","content.75.3960":"In fact, I have to admit, I misjudged you{[1*] ?e:}. I thought you'd be dead{[1*] ?e:} a long time ago, or have run off{[1*] ?e:}. Instead, you keep coming back to see me. Anyone else would have finished in little pieces scattered all over the world, I think I'm developing a soft spot for you... ","content.75.3961":"Lovely, isn't it? I never thought I'd find a Sacrier Temple in a place like this. I did a few renovations to spruce it up, broke a few stones, polished the chains, sacrificed a few adventurers to repaint here and there... you wouldn't happen to have a couple of extra liters of blood on you?","content.75.3962":"You want to know if I'm afraid of Ogrest!? HAHAHA! But that's ridiculous! I knocked him out with a single blow when I was young! That cry baby never knew how to fight! And you've got it in your head to calm him down? I admit that would be fun to watch, but you don't have what it takes. Don't be offended; it's just the way of nature. You're weak.","content.75.3963":"Don't ask questions about things you don't understand, little one. You don't need to know more, and the last thing we need is you meddling in our affairs. Climb up your little mountain if you want to, get yourself dismembered by Ogrest if you feel like it, but in the end, none of it matters. You'll understand when the time comes.","content.75.3964":"So you want to play at environmentalists?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3965":"So you want to play at environmentalists?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful. It's not free!","content.75.3966":"The Mount Zinit Summit... The last step before facing my son's rage...\\nI'm not too happy about being here right now, but my analyses won't wait.\\nSomething disturbing is going on here.","content.75.3967":"So you want to play tree-huggers?\\nAllow me to offer you these few items. Choose what you need, but be careful, because it's not free!","content.75.3968":"The way that Dreggon is behaving is definitely not normal... I'd like you to take a closer look at the other Dreggons that aren't sleeping like a bunch of logs, then bring me back some Bulia Powder - I think it'll come in very handy before long. And watch out for yourself!","content.75.3969":"Perfect! I guarantee we'll find a good use for this! I have another mission for you - a very important one... Searching the summit for other sleeping Dreggons shouldn't be too much trouble, should it?","content.75.3970":"Hmmm... It's pretty unnerving to see such terrifying monsters turn into sweet little Gobblies... By analyzing the data you brought me, I've been able to trace the problem back to its source. You'll need to find out what's causing their deep sleep - I'll mark the spot on your map that I think is connected to this phenomenon.","content.75.3971":"A Noxine! I've already found a few of these in our world. I don't know who's behind this mechanism, but it absorbs Wakfu from living beings... I have to tell King Sheran Sharm right away - I've got a really bad feeling about this... Could you take this message to the Sadida Kingdom?\\nI'll make you a potion from the Bulia Powder and the Noxine to knock out the Dreggon that's blocking the passage to the other side of the summit in the cave.","content.75.3972":"Hello, and welcome to your Haven Bag! Don't be afraid; this is your place. I'm your Haven Bag's Mod'Ule, at your service. What can I do for you today?","content.75.3974":"If this missive comes from Otomai, it must be vitally important.\\nI'll take care of reading this message - you go see my beloved subjects, Renata and Canar.\\nOur queen passed away recently, and morale has hit rock bottom here...","content.75.3975":"I'm so sad about losing our queen. If only I had something to wipe away my tears... something incredibly soft and fluffy.","content.75.3976":"This kingdom has lost its most beautiful flower... but there's an adorable little blossom I'm proud to take care of. She's just the cutest little princess... I do so wish I could make her life a rose garden...","content.75.3977":"Sigh... if only I had some Pink Gobball Wool... so soft... I could make something to dry my tears.","content.75.3978":"Oh! Can you please help me and accept my request? Aren't you charming!? If you could bring me a Crozolily Bouquet, I'd be eternally grateful.","content.75.3979":"Otomai was right to warn me of this danger...\\nThere's no time to lose. You have to get to the Forgotten Dimension to collect a certain powder... Let's get moving. I'll send you to the Tree of Life just this once. Touch it, and you'll go straight to the Forgotten Dimension!","content.75.3980":"... *meditating deeply*","content.75.3981":"Just my luck, I go off to a nice quiet place to relax, but people still show up to bother me! Go tell everyone you know that the prophet Moze is on vacation. No more fortune-telling to predict tomorrow's weather! Hey, wait a second... I feel like I know you from somewhere! Let me take a look at you... You wouldn't be the chosen one from the prophecy, by any chance?","content.75.3982":"It seems like forever since I've seen an adventurer around here!\\nWhat a pleasure! I'm so happy, I feel like I could pick a whole mountain of Crozolilies with you!","content.75.3983":"Picking Crozolily Flowers is a sign of great friendship, sincerity, and love! I get goosebumps of joy just putting them in my basket and smelling their exquisite scent. \\nGo pick 10 Crozolily Flowers and bring them back to me, my dear.","content.75.3984":"An adventurer? Here? What brings you here? You want to have a feast with me? Pink Gobball meat is downright succulent compared to White Gobball meat.","content.75.3985":"Well, shoot: If it's wool you're after, just take whatever you need! But make it quick, before I eat 'em all up!","content.75.3986":"What gorgeous flowers! I'll make you a bouquet with those ten Crozolily Flowers you brought me.","content.75.3987":"My prophecies are never wrong! You look terrible, my friend... What's wrong? Let me guess: Otomai thought it would be a good idea to expose you to Ogrest's Wrath, right? He'll never change. He's a damn genius, but sometimes he can be such an idiot... A bit too often, really. You didn't realize it at the time, but by fighting all those monsters on Mount Zinit, you've absorbed Ogrest's Wrath. If you don't get rid of it one way or another, you're sure to end up dead!","content.75.3988":"Hello, [#name]. I'm Wolfram, the wisest of all the Boowolves... Welcome to my territory, the Forgotten Dimension. Are you here to continue your quest?","content.75.3989":"Watch out, Gobblington Jr... The boy who cried Boowolf lost his voice and all his friends! Go check in the pen behind me. It's getting late... you should find that Gobball there. Don't stand next to it for too long, unless you need help nodding off. Look at me, I'm exhausted. Kick his butt for me.","content.75.3991":"Ooh... how wonderful! Thank you so much for this wonderfully soft wool! I feel a bit better thanks to you!","content.75.3992":"What a magnificent bouquet! I'm sure it will please our little princess and our dear departed queen.\\nThank you so much!","content.75.3993":"Yes, this is the powder that Otomai mentioned in his missive. It's a Sleeping Powder. I hope you'll find it useful. Be careful out there!","content.75.3994":"Sleeping Powder, fantastic! We finally have everything we need to prepare the Sleeping Potion. I hope that the good old Wolfram wasn't too harsh with you. It had been a long time since King Sheran Sharm had let anyone use the Tree of Life. Tell me when you're ready{[1*]?:} to start production.","content.75.3996":"Here we are. Can you hear the cries echoing in this part of the Summit?\\nAnyone planning on facing Ogrest needs to be properly prepared. I'm crafting a little something that will be very useful for your upcoming adventures. Could you go and get me some vapors from the nearby monsters?","content.75.3997":"Perfect! Using these vapors, I'll prepare it for you in no time. You'll love it!","content.75.3998":"Alright, come closer and I'll explain what you can use it for.","content.75.3999":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to make a deal with me? I hope you have a mercenary license for this region...","content.75.4001":"It's possible. Either you don't have the level required to access new contracts, or you don't fulfill other specific conditions, such as having completed all the Rank 1 contracts to access the Rank 2 contracts.\\nPerhaps you've already completed them all!","content.75.4002":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.4003":"I see, I see... You say that the Dreggons like intense heat. According to your observations, they mostly live in the volcanic part of the Summit. And it's true that they're never seen in the snowbound areas. In any case, I wonder why they've become so aggressive recently...\\nWe're really lacking too much important information about these monsters.\\nI wonder if the need for a warm climate has anything to do with incubating the Dreggons' eggs. Maybe they need a nearby source of heat to hatch?","content.75.4004":"Well, actually... The beer is to pass the time while the mixture settles a bit. Cheers!","content.75.4005":"I see... it's probably the powder from that damned Gobball. It ravaged our ecosystem and left it in this terrible state. Good thing Mimi and Wolfgang are there to take care of it.","content.75.4006":"But you know, I knew the queen of the trappers, Baba Boowolf. She taught me all I know. And today, I'm still here to pass on that ancestral knowledge...","content.75.4007":"Ogrest's Chaos turned the World of Twelve upside down. So far, nobody's managed to restore order... Now it's up to you and your peers to try.","content.75.4008":"One day, the hero from the prophecy will appear and restore balance once and for all in the World of Twelve.","content.75.4009":"What do you want to know?","content.75.4010":"Each individual's Haven Bag is unique. You can open it almost anywhere in the world and customize it as you wish. You can also put crafting workshops and a few useful things in there.\\nYou can find me there each time you come, and I'll be there to offer you quests to complete in exchange for rewards. I'll offer you your first Adjustable Level Quest once you reach level 51. You'll be able to unlock other ones later!","content.75.4011":"The adjustable level system allows you to reduce your character's level. That way, you can play with friends who haven't yet caught up with you by reducing your level to theirs; you can even start new challenges!\\n\"Scoreboard\" quests I offer you consist of defeating a dungeon's boss while having adjusted your level to that of the relevant dungeon in order to receive rewards.\\nIt's a daily quest: Each day, the quest is different, but everyone must defeat the same boss.","content.75.4012":"I was born out of one of Otomai's experiments. He asked me to help him and to accompany adventurers through their journeys. The World of Twelve has been a perilous place since Ogrest's Chaos, so I prefer to waiting peacefully in Haven Bags...\\nIn short, Otomai cannot keep an eye on you all the time, which is why he sent me in his place, to check on your progress. I am supposed to help you properly explore your potential, so do not hesitate to come back and see me!","content.75.4019":"Hey, that's... That's the children's book I wrote for Ogrest way back when! I remember when I used to read him those stories to calm him down and put him to sleep. If I'd known then that he'd gather all six Primordial Dofus one day, and that he'd be the cause of such terrible disasters...","content.75.4020":"You're probably right. I never expected that he'd actually manage to do it. And, well... to be perfectly honest, I never thought you'd manage to stand up to him either. The feats you've accomplished since your incarnation have been nothing short of exceptional. It's as if your entire body is a bottomless vessel for power... with no limits whatsoever on how far you can progress. For a little while now, I've had this hypothesis that you might be able to absorb a fragment of Ogrest's omnipotent power.","content.75.4021":"To do this, you'll have to fight the various monsters that roam Mount Zinit. They must be infused with the leftover wrath contained in Ogrest's Chaos. A high level of Stasification should make it easier to gather Ogrest's Wrath within yourself. Good luck!","content.75.4022":"Well, congratulations! Have you started to feel that special feeling deep in your heart? No? Still nothing? Hmmm... Well, coming from the Upper Slope, the amount of Stasis should be a bit lower since you're getting closer to the Summit.","content.75.4023":"That's all. You need to go back to the Forgotten Dimension and leave your wrath behind. You'll find a well there, the Well of Forgetting. Throw all your wrath down the well, and it'll be... forgotten. Forever.\\nOK, time for me to get back to my prophecies. Hmmm, hmmm...\\n(...)\\nZzzz...\\n(...)\\nThe boy king...\\n(...)","content.75.4024":"Well, that's strange. After all those fascinating experiments I did on how Ogrest's Wrath was concentrated on Mount Zinit... I had hoped that it could live naturally within you and amplify your abilities, but obviously I was wrong. I suppose the best thing now would be for you to go and see my old friend Moze. He's somewhere in the Sadida Kingdom. Not sure where exactly, but what with his... unusual style, he shouldn't be too hard to find. Tell him I sent you.","content.75.4025":"Adventurer{[1*]?:}. Finally, we meet again.","content.75.4026":"Easy-peasy, let me teleport you straight to the Forgotten Kingdom! Close your eyes, andఽ...","content.75.4027":"Halt! Don't take another step: You're approaching Verna's territory!","content.75.4028":"You want to get in? I'm sure that can be arranged. Let's see... Ah! I know! I'll ask you a riddle. No, wait... Make that three riddles! Yeah, that's more like it. If you fail, you'll turn right around and go back where you came from!","content.75.4029":"Tell me three of an Ouginak's virtues. So?","content.75.4030":"Hmmm... Yeah, I suppose that's okay. Next question. What's small... And blue? Hang on... No, dang it, that's not right... What's green and waits around? Grrr, I get it wrong every time. What's red and rushes up when you... Shoot, I can't do it! Oh well, let's just say you've passed the second test.","content.75.4031":"And finally... What smells like rotten fish and should go back to play with the fleas in the trash heap it crawled out of?","content.75.4032":"That's it! Hahaha! An Ecaflip! Funny, right? No? Okay... As you wish. Anyway, you've passed all the tests: You're seriously awesome. You should talk to Verna, our chief. Enjoy your visit!","content.75.4033":"You lost! Not too smart, are you? Run along now!","content.75.4034":"*Sniff*... *sniff sniff*... No, I'm sorry, but I don't smell anything interesting on you at all. Either answer one of my riddles or get out of here.","content.75.4035":"*Sniff*... *sniff sniff*... Ooh, is that a Chafer Bone I smell? What a lovely scent! So captivating! If you give it to me, I'll let you in! Please!","content.75.4036":"Welcome to the camp, young {[1*]?lady:man}. Be quick: I've got things to do. What do you want?","content.75.4037":"We will take back the land that is rightfully ours. Long ago, Ohwymi was the land where the Ouginaks formed a unified tribe, and we're going to recreate that ideal. Before long, all the Ouginak will know that they once again have a place to feel at home, without having to submit to the Nations and their freedom-killing rules. You look like someone who's willing to fight for a good cause, am I right?","content.75.4038":"That's perfect! I have a mission that I can't entrust to anyone from the camp: I need a go-between to communicate with someone who's not too happy about us taking up residence on her hunting grounds. Her name is Ezam, and if you can convince her to leave us alone, we'd all really appreciate it!","content.75.4039":"Grmpf! In that case, get out of here, and don't set foot in this camp again until you're ready to make yourself useful. Farewell!","content.75.4040":"A reward? I thought you were on our side! Everyone here is working for the common good! If you don't have that same spirit of solidarity, maybe I'm better off without your services. But so be it. I'll reward you with our symbol. It will prove that you're a member of our clan, and let everyone know how much you've helped us. What do you say?","content.75.4041":"Perfect! So now you can go see that huntress and figure out how to make her a bit more friendly. I might have a better job to offer you if you succeed.","content.75.4042":"Really? That's too bad... We could have achieved all kinds of great things with someone like you, but it's your choice... You really don't want to help us?","content.75.4043":"A weekly tax? Forbidden from getting rid of those Castucs? Are you sure you know how to negotiate? Although I suppose it's still better than just letting the conflict continue... You've done a good enough job. Thanks.","content.75.4044":"Ah! The reward. We're not quite there yet. You've done us a small favor, to be sure, but certain things still remain to be done. To tell you the truth, I want to get back something that was stolen from me. It happened at sea, when we were sailing through here.","content.75.4045":"Some creature tried to sink us. We won the battle, but it left with part of our cargo, and what's worse... It took an item that belonged to my ancestor. I don't care about the cargo, but that Bell has been passed down in my family from one generation to the next. It's really precious to me.","content.75.4046":"I'm telling you, it's an item of immense personal importance! Nothing could ever replace it. If you find it, you'll get your reward. During our confrontation, I tore this piece of black fabric from my opponent's clothes. I was going to send Tovak, my best tracker, to go looking for him. You should work together. I'll wait here for you to come back.","content.75.4047":"Hey, you! If you're looking to join the Guild of Hunters, you've come to the right place!","content.75.4048":"Ah yes, those squatters. You want to help me get rid of them? That's nice of you. Bring me back 10 Moist Ouginak Truffles, and I'll give you a reward on behalf of the Guild. They've moved into our hunting grounds, after all.","content.75.4049":"Negotiate? You mean you're on their side? Their presence is causing all kinds of problems for the Guild's plans! Anyhow, I don't see anything to negotiate about. I mean, at most, to compensate for their losses, I could accept a tax of, say... 10,000 kamas per person per day. You can pass my offer on to them.","content.75.4050":"I don't see any here. Otherwise, by bringing me some proof that you're not against me. I want to be sure that you're also acting in the best interest of the Guild of Hunters. If you ever do business with my colleagues on Ereboria or in the Wild Estate, tell them I need a certificate. I'm warning you: I'll know right away if it's a fake!","content.75.4051":"Let me see that... Hmmm. Yes, it looks authentic enough. I'll accept a truce with the Ouginaks from the camp in exchange for a tax of 5,000 kamas a week. There will be no further negotiations. And be sure to tell them that if they intend to go after the Castucs, hunting is restricted: Exterminating them is forbidden.","content.75.4052":"We will take back the land that is rightfully ours. Long ago, Ohwymi was the land where the Ouginaks formed a unified tribe, and we're going to recreate that ideal. Before long, all the Ouginak will know that they once again have a place to feel at home, without having to submit to the Nations and their freedom-killing rules.","content.75.4053":"Hello? Need something?","content.75.4054":"Verna sent you to help me, huh? I'm sure you can be of some use. I don't have a lot of good leads to find this bandit, but a fresh pair of eyes will help me to see things more clearly. I didn't recognize any particular scent on this piece of fabric; I just found a few Ecaflip hairs.","content.75.4055":"One of my cousins, Bay Toven, is almost as good a tracker as I am. He might be able to get us pointed in the right direction. We can leave for Astrub as soon as you're ready. But things are a bit chilly between him and me, and I'm not sure if he'll agree to help us.","content.75.4056":"A cousin? What cousin? Ugh! That weakling, Tovak! Are you still a wittle puppy-wuppy doing twicks for your mistress? Does she give you a wittle num-nums when you stand on your hind legs? You could have brought me a better cousin than that, my friend. But I suppose you haven't come here just to amuse me.","content.75.4057":"Haha! Have you lost your sense of smell, Tovak? Have all those years of submitting to Verna the Feeble finally robbed you of your instincts? It's funny, really! Anyhow, I can't just help you for no reason. Tell me, adventurer: Do you think you can be a better Ouginak than him?","content.75.4058":"You're right, that's true. Let's make this simple. I'll help you if you show me that you can gather a pack and lead it to victory! What do you think? Recruit some other adventurers and head off to confront Morfor, the beast that controls the Raised Vault.","content.75.4059":"Well! I wasn't exactly betting on you. I like your attitude: Never back down when faced with a challenge! I don't know how you wound up working for Verna, but look out for yourself, or you'll wind up like the little worm they call my cousin. So, about your piece of fabric...","content.75.4060":"I don't know who your thief is, but I recognize a certain smell. Not the strongest in the world, but it's the smell of an Ecaflip who lives in the Tailors' Quarter of Astrub. In fact, she's the one in charge of it! If you want my opinion, that's the start of a solid lead. Good luck!","content.75.4061":"Well, shoot, I reckon I don't need much in life, y'know? Fishin's all I really care 'bout. Big fish, little fish, and even them medium-sized ones. But right now I'm 'bout to run clean out of lures.","content.75.4062":"I'd go lookin' for more in the sewers, but that's such a long hike, and with my arthritic knees I'm not really up for it. You just tell that lady, she finds me a nice lure that don't need replacin', well then I reckon I'd like that just fine. What was that name again?","content.75.4063":"Well, goodness me, this is downright lovely! And I just love me some colors! It's almost as like someone was tryin' to seduce me! I shore don't know who done this, but it sure seems like some kind of nice lady! If you run into her in your travels, tell her she's more'n welcome to come an' fish a spell with me any time she likes! Long as she don't scare the fish...","content.75.4064":"A fabric? Certainly... Ah... Oh, I'm sorry, were you saying something? Are you the people I asked for? That was fast! I only sent my letter to the Matchfindr Gazette this morning! You can really count on them when you need help!","content.75.4065":"Yes, yes... I'll help you after you help me. After all, I called on you, not the other way around. All right, I'm counting on you to keep this a secret. The man I can't stop thinking about is... Andy Ago! The handsome Hullcatz down in the Fishermen's Hamlet! Oh, what a fine man... Anyway, I need your help to find out how to make him like me too. But you have to be discreet!","content.75.4066":"He wants... A lure for his fish? Oh, what a passionate man! Of course! For him to be interested in me, I have to get interested in fishing! You folks at the Matchfindr Gazette know all about this stuff, right?! He uses... larvae? But that's revolting! How can I do this?","content.75.4067":"Oh, I know! I'll sew him a lovely little fabric lure! But where can I find a larva without going down into those disgusting sewers...? Would you mind being my model? You really look a whole lot like... Well, you know what I mean.","content.75.4068":"Don't take it too hard! It's just nature's way: We have to accept who we are and love the face we're given, even when it's hard... But no, there's still something missing. You need to be all dressed up in the Muddy Larval Set. It's gorgeous!","content.75.4069":"Well, put it on so I can see you! I've got to make the right lure for your model!","content.75.4070":"Magnificent! Well, for a larva, anyway. So don't move... Whatever you do, stay calm. Okay, a little thread here... A quick snip there... Ta-da! It's perfect! Oh, I don't dare to go and give it to him myself... Would you please take him my gift? But don't tell him it's from me! I'm much too shy...","content.75.4071":"Oh yes! Let me see that... Oh, I know exactly what that is. I have a customer who comes from very far away just to get this fabric. But the Crobak Feathers don't come from here; I think she collects them on the island where she lives.","content.75.4072":"Yeah, strange place! My client is an Ecaflip who's very gracious and refined, and quite a lovely lady. But she's not shy about using her claws when she has to! Not always easy doing business with her, but as long as she comes to me and not the competition... It's nice of you to bring her back the fabric that she lost.","content.75.4073":"Maybe you're looking for a legendary weapon or a nice strong shield? Or maybe a silky-soft tunic that doesn't chafe under your arms when you swing 'em around? I've probably got whatever you need. And for any \"special\" requests you may have... there's a back room with a little something for everyone.","content.75.4074":"Well! I've got a few models, if that's really what you're here for. There's all kinds of them here: for hanging on your belt, for putting on Moogrrs' collars, or even for giving Trools a nasty earache... Although I don't recommend that last one.","content.75.4075":"Should I? It's just a little bit of worn fabric: Why on earth should that mean anything to me? Do you have any idea how many people out there wear black? Now, are you here to just accuse people for no reason, or to actually buy something? I only have patience for customers with nice, full purses!","content.75.4076":"The trail leads back to me? You're not seriously going to call me a thief in my OWN shop, are you?! Get out of here now, before I lose control of my claws! And don't come back until you've learned to behave yourself around an honest lady!","content.75.4077":"We'll see about that! Hold on, now... You wouldn't be looking for THE Bell, would you? A regular (but anonymous) customer did come by to sell me this item... They say that a long time ago, it belonged to an Ouginak who saved Bonta all by herself when she was a child. Would that be the bell you're talking about? The cost for such a relic is high.","content.75.4078":"I'd need to know what you want to accuse me of: having your Bell, or not having it? I acquired it honestly. That is to say, I'll agree to ignore your rudeness and to do business with you... If you're ready to pay the price. Don't you dare try to negotiate after the scandalous behavior you just showed me.","content.75.4079":"I'm looking for the Amulet of the terrible Thork, the Great Wild Gobball Ring, and the incredibly rare Padded Epaulettes! And I'm talking about the real thing here, pure and unadulterated, not one of those \"improved\" copies from some artisan trying to make a name for themself. I want the version that those monsters actually wear.","content.75.4080":"Let's see... That's exactly what I'm looking for! We can go ahead and make the trade, and then I never want to see you again. I'll also take that bit of black cloth. It'll help me to identify your thief in case I see him in my shop again. I don't want him stealing things from me too!","content.75.4081":"Oops! I must have made a mistake... Here's the right one. I don't know if it's true what they say about it, but I'm glad I could make this trade. I don't suppose you'd like to buy some worn-out shoes that used to belong to the legendary Gobbowler Ruel Stroud, would you? Or the Justice Knight's bedside lamp? He wasn't using it, since he's never in his room at night anyway.","content.75.4082":"Well, I guess we're done with our business. Now scram! I've got to clean up in here after letting you come in with those grimy old boots.","content.75.4083":"What wonderful news! I never thought I'd see it again, to be honest. This Bell makes me feel better already; I can feel my ancestor's spirit still ringing inside of it! With this at my side, I'm sure I can rally enough Ouginaks to put an end to Ogrest's reign of terror. Our ancestors will be avenged! Come on; I'll give you the reward you were promised.","content.75.4084":"You've traveled the World for me, [#name], and now I consider you an ally. You have acted in accordance with Ouginak values: you've defended our territory, hunted with the pack, latched on to your prey without ever letting go, and followed a trail to the end of the World.","content.75.4085":"All that matters is that you did it. For your bravery, I solemnly present you with this Marrow Bone, the symbol of our god. Summon it, and you'll find that Ouginak is by your side in every battle.","content.75.4086":"Now leave me alone please, [#name]. One day, if I need you again, I'll send you a letter. But you'll have to wait until you feel strong{[1*]?:} enough to take on this island's challenges without too much trouble. For now, farewell and safe travels!","content.75.4087":"Halt! Oh no, it's all right, you can leave without answering my riddles.","content.75.4090":"It's tempting! Thank you so much for your help! I'll renew my subscription to the Matchfindr Gazette for at least another year! Ah, love...","content.75.4092":"That's my dad Alibert's recipe book! I'm learning how to make Gobball Stew so I can help him at the inn!","content.75.4093":"Hello!","content.75.4094":"In that case, go ahead and have lunch at the inn!","content.75.4095":"Look at this crown of flowers I made! It's magnificent!","content.75.4096":"I'll make a whole collection: the Princess Amalia collection!","content.75.4097":"*Looking at the little princess with her proud, cheerful face, you decide not to contradict her*","content.75.4098":"*She casts a disillusioned glance at the crown of flowers in Amalia's hands*","content.75.4099":"*Ruel mumbles* Hmm... Maybe that one? If I sleep under the stars and travel on foot, I can get there and back in two days, plus the time to catch that scoundrel...","content.75.4100":"Aaaaaahhh! What were you thinking scaring me like that?! \\n... You want to see it, you say... You seem pretty smart, but not yet smart enough to be a bounty hunter!","content.75.4101":"The goal is not only to reunify us. There's a larger objective behind this project: defeat Ogrest! He's the one who scattered our peoples when he flooded the World of Twelve with his tears. Our temple is somewhere at the bottom of the ocean; we can't get there any more. So we're looking for it at the same time as we're preparing for the greatest battle of our lives!","content.75.4102":"Absolutely! What's the point of starting a project if you're not going to put the proper resources into it? All the Ouginaks that are staying with us here are taking part. While some focus on searching for traces of our former civilization, others are training hard for battles to come. We are unstoppable.","content.75.4103":"Here at the camp, I supervise the archaosological digs and the search for the temple. Off behind me, there seems to be some sort of submerged structure with its tip sticking out of the water. I've sent a diver out there to find out more. But my real work is as a tracker! When it comes to finding lost people or items, no one is better than me.","content.75.4105":"Hello, and welcome to your Haven Bag! Don't be afraid; this is your place. I'm your Haven Bag's Mod'Ule, at your service. What can I do for you today?","content.75.4106":"Hey, my bag of books! You found it, thanks! As promised, here is the book you were searching for. I owe you this much for having found the others.","content.75.4107":"Ah! That tower! Yes, it came up out of the ocean recently, but I've been very occupied with the digs, so I haven't been able to get over there. \\nThe boat should be able to get there. I doubt that something like that went unnoticed... and the Archaosologists are hardly the only ones with an interest in it.","content.75.4108":"Hey! What are you doing here? If you came to see the big, shiny crystals, then be off with you!","content.75.4109":"Hmmm... Have you come to try your luck in the tower? Let me explain what's going on here; this is no ordinary tower. And don't call me \"ma'am\": The name's Arpagone.\\n\\nThis tower goes down below sea level. Don't go punching holes in it if you feel like jumping out a window.","content.75.4110":"And you might want to as well, once you've seen what's down there! The monsters that make their home there never die: They just get right back up, again and again. It's only a matter of time. So let me give you some advice: If you do manage to knock them down, don't hang around too long afterwards.","content.75.4111":"One last thing: The entity that's been keeping the tower strong all this time, and that pulled it out of the sea in the first place... it can swallow your soul. No Externam, no reincarnation, nada. But I've got a solution for that: Feca Incantations.","content.75.4112":"They look like little bits of paper, but there's more to them than meets the eye. They're blessed by an artifact that... well, I'll spare you the details, but the point is, they protect you from the influence of the thing that controls the tower.","content.75.4113":"Hang on. They don't last too long, so you'll only have time for one incursion before they disappear. And just so you know, I don't share my incantations... unless you've got some very convincing arguments.\\n*Arpagone looks at your pouch full of kamas with a big smile*","content.75.4114":"Perfect! Go on in: There's only one elevator going down.","content.75.4115":"To go down, you must pull the lever.","content.75.4116":"Not that one!","content.75.4117":"Nyaargh, I cyan't believe it! They should have been here nyhours ago! I hope they haven't crashed our ship on a sand byank...","content.75.4118":"That boat? Oh yes, of course. I'll go with you, actually... I think it'll be a while before the boat I'm waiting for gets here.","content.75.4119":"Look, there it is. Pay close attention once you're inside.","content.75.4120":"First of all, you can't go in without a Feca Incantation, or else you'll die for good.\\nSecond of all, the monsters always get back up eventually, so if you manage to beat them, grab what you can and get back up here pronto.\\nThird of all, if you want to go down there more than once a day, you'll have to pay!","content.75.4121":"Wow, looks like they didn't pull any punches: They kicked you right out, didn't they? But it seems like you've still got that fire in your belly, am I right?","content.75.4123":"(You can open the Shop at any time if you want to buy a Powerful Feca Incantation, then collect it from the gift interface.)","content.75.4125":"Well, well: I see you've reached level 25. It's time you learned a few things about this crazy ride we call life.\\nThis might come as a shock; are you ready?","content.75.4126":"You-hoo may not believe it, but Astrub isn't the only island in the World of Twelve!\\nThere are other islands out there too-hoo, starting with the four great Nations: Amakna, Sufokia, Bonta, and Brakmar, but also lots of other islands that you're shu-hoor to discover once you've got a bit more experience.","content.75.4127":"To-hoo get to Amakna, the first Nation, all you-hoo have to do is take the boat here at the Astrub docks.\\n\\nBut we don't suggest you-hoo leave for Amakna until you're goo-hood and ready.{[1*]?:} So take your time exploring all of Astrub's treasures and riches! Once you're sufficiently experienced{[1*]?:}, you can even go to the other three Nations.","content.75.4128":"There are a lot of papers to-hoo fill out, which is why I will only be able to help you-hoo become neutral again once a month at most. What's more, it will cost you-hoo; that's why I'll ask you-hoo for a payment depending on your level:\\n- Level 50 and lower: 5,000 kamas\\n- Levels 51 to 100: 25,000 kamas\\n- Levels 101 to 150: 50,000 kamas\\n- Level 151 and higher: 100,000 kamas\\n\\nWarning: Becoming neutral again will remo-hoove all your Citizenship Points, as well as all of your Merit Points and Glory Orbs.\\nCome back and see me with the kamas once you're ready.","content.75.4129":"As it happens, I've just finished getting the papers ready for you-hoo to become neutral again. As a reminder, you'll only be able to do so once a month, and you'll need to pay me the amount on the following price list:\\n- Level 50 and lower: 5,000 kamas\\n- Levels 51 to 100: 25,000 kamas\\n- Levels 101 to 150: 50,000 kamas\\n- Level 151 and higher: 100,000 kamas\\n\\nWarning: Becoming neutral again will remo-hoove all your Citizenship Points, as well as all of your Merit Points and Glory Orbs.\\nHave you brought me the kamas, and are you sure you want to become neutral again?","content.75.4130":"You're neutral again. Congratulations!\\nIf you wish to choose another nation, you-hoo can find all the information relating them on the nation selection board behind me, and choose the one you want!","content.75.4131":"Hoo-hoooo!\\nYoung Incarnate, you're rising to the top like an arrow.\\nI can see that you've already completed some achievements in our fair city. But kno-hoo this: Your future adventures won't be this easy.","content.75.4132":"We don't think you-hoo are ready for this adventure. We suggest you-hoo increase your level before scaling Mount Zinit. You-hoo won't be able to go there before you've reached level 21 or higher.\\nThere are many ways to gain experience. You-hoo can work through the Main Quests, massacre monsters, or complete dungeons... However, you should know that the Mercenary Post, the Guild of Hunters, and Otomai's Disciples can also help you gain experience. All missions are good choices, so you-hoo should check them out!","content.75.4134":"You?! Go t' Mount Zinit?!\\nSorry little one, but we only agree to take real hero{[1*]?ine:}s on our ship, \"The Black Purr\".\\nCome back 'n see us when you've proven you're up to scratch!","content.75.4136":"(You can continue through the dungeon without suffering a death penalty and with no combat mechanic changes. However, if you decide to leave the dungeon and come back at any point, the combat mechanic will be different.)","content.75.4137":"You can now turn yourself in if you want to get rid of your outlaw status. You just have to go through the gate behind me.","content.75.4138":"I'm the law around here!","content.75.4139":"Careful: You can only do one of the three quests offered. And you'll have one week to complete it.","content.75.4141":"Come see me later and I'll find a mission just for you!","content.75.4142":"You seem pretty resourceful{[1*]?:}! Come this way. I've got a mission that could bring in a pretty penny for me - I mean you! If you accept, we'll share the loot fairly: 10% for you and 90% for me. Not bad, eh?","content.75.4143":"Here's the deal: We've got to catch a kama thief who fled from the Astrub Inn. And we can share the loot! That's great, right?","content.75.4144":"Well, how'd it go? Not bad being a bounty hunter! Here, take your reward.","content.75.4145":"If you ever want to do it another time, you know where to find me!","content.75.4146":"Hey, don't I know you? We've already done a mission together!","content.75.4147":"Hmmm... Hmmm... Come see: I've found a rather interesting mission... It talks of killing powerful monsters. Take this: We're going to choose this one to begin. You should be able to manage. Apparently, if you defeat several of them, you'll be rewarded.","content.75.4148":"So you're going to train me? Fantastic!","content.75.4149":"Hey, kid!{[1*]?:} Here{[1*]?:} for a bit of brawling? I'd happily do a little tournament!","content.75.4150":"Ready? We have to follow its tracks and keep our eyes peeled! Go ahead, I'm right behind you.","content.75.4151":"Ahh, you saw Daldal. That little Iop looks like he has what it takes to become a great warrior. But right now, he's got a long way to go...\\nWhat would you say about giving me a hand?","content.75.4152":"Go fight a monster with Daldal. That will show him the basics of fighting before moving on to more serious things.\\nHere's a Iop Whistle. It will allow you to call Daldal when you're ready.","content.75.4154":"Take this, here's your Whistle.","content.75.4155":"At that moment, I was drinking at the tavern.","content.75.4156":"The beer was very good, but some people didn't like it much.","content.75.4157":"I don't remember the rest...","content.75.4158":"I think I saw someone empty their tankard in... in a pot... Oh, what a waste! Pouring beer on a plant!","content.75.4159":"The beer was very good, but I saw someone empty their tankard in a flower pot.","content.75.4160":"I remember there was some scrapping, and someone grabbed the stool next to me.","content.75.4161":"For a moment there was some commotion and some people fighting... Someone grabbed the stool next to me hahaha haa... I love it when things go south!","content.75.4162":"What's it to you what I was doing that evening!?","content.75.4164":"All I can say is that it wasn't me who stole that purse!","content.75.4165":"I was much too busy to pay attention to that!","content.75.4166":"I noticed the music stopped much earlier than normal.","content.75.4167":"I was about to get smashed by a stool; I didn't have time to steal...","content.75.4168":"Hmmm... Usually there's music, but that evening, it stopped rather early.","content.75.4169":"I... I don't wish to talk about it.","content.75.4170":"I was fighting with another tavern customer, voilà!","content.75.4171":"...One of the stools got broken that evening. I still have the marks; you wanna see them? Is that proof enough for you?","content.75.4173":"I, too, was at the Inn that evening, indeed.","content.75.4174":"I played the piano for the audience. I was seated far from the victim's table.","content.75.4175":"I had come to the inn for a beer, but it was disgusting.","content.75.4176":"I just came to have a beer and quench my thirst. I was also really disappointed. It was disgusting! I got rid of it.","content.75.4177":"I played the piano all evening, despite the fight between the two drunkards. The Pandawa here didn't say a word.","content.75.4178":"The customer was very drunk. He probably confused me with someone else.","content.75.4179":"That can't be me.","content.75.4180":"Yes, even if a fight broke out in the middle.","content.75.4181":"Two ill-tempered regulars got into a fight again. Even the furniture was involved in the action.","content.75.4182":"It's not hard to see, given the state they're in. One might say that for this Pandawa who comes home dead drunk every night, even fighting hasn't managed to fish him out of his tankard.","content.75.4183":"Because it was one of the tavern's customers, and I don't know his name.","content.75.4184":"I stopped playing the piano to go get a drink.","content.75.4185":"Oh, I had to get up to go get a drink...","content.75.4186":"Hey, have you come to join the Ogrest's Cult? We're no longer recruiting. Sorry.","content.75.4187":"Hey, hey, have you seen our cult hideout? It's great, isn't it? We dug it ourselves!","content.75.4188":"You too; did you get a call from Ogrest? Here, he's like a brother to us. Our Brogrest!","content.75.4189":"Pssst! Pssst! Look at our uniform. See how classy it is! Makes you want to join us, right?","content.75.4190":"That's why we have spectacles!","content.75.4191":"Nothin' but good scrappin' there! My master's the one who told me!","content.75.4192":"Listen, kid{[1*]?:}... I think Daldal needs to get some theory into that Iop brain of his before he returns to field training. Come back in four days. I'll ask you to go fight a new monster with him!","content.75.4193":"Ahh, you saw Daldal. That little Iop looks like he has what it takes to become a great warrior. But right now, he's got a long way to go...\\nOnce you're strong enough to accompany him, would you like to help me with his training?","content.75.4194":"I don't have any missions for you right now, but you could perhaps come back later!","content.75.4195":"I'm waiting in the court to question the suspects!","content.75.4202":"Hello, adventurer! Want to make yourself useful? Then don't lollygag about; get going as soon as you can!","content.75.4203":"Whatcha want, pipsqueak? I can see you've got something on the tip of your tongue!","content.75.4204":"The contract is a request from a wealthy merchant in Sufokia. He's asked the Guild to procure a golden api. Golden apis can only be found in what used to be called the Jumpin' Jungle.\\nThat's a region located to the northwest of our capital. Be careful. The Jungle is fiercely defended by Puddlies and rife with Taurs.","content.75.4205":"I'd be careful in your shoes. The Puddlies originally came from Amakna and settled in Sufokia a few years ago following the violent events in Ogrest's Chaos. But some Puddlies are different. They wear red hats and are more aggressive. Almost as if they were distant cousins.","content.75.4206":"Because there aren't any contracts, that's all. We're barely more than a want ad relay station. We don't have an army, especially not in Sufokia where the law forbids us from creating our own contracts. Basically, just get a golden Api and bring it to us quick to get your reward. If you show the Taurs your mercenary license, they should listen to your request.","content.75.4207":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to take on a little contract?","content.75.4208":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.4209":"It's possible. Either you don't have the necessary level for new contracts, or you might have already done them all! There's nothing stopping you from taking care of other problems yourself without expecting a reward from us! You'll still improve all the same if you do, so don't hesitate. ","content.75.4211":"Buddy, you consolidated all the barrels. I'm the one who's happy. Yes indeed!","content.75.4212":"No! The Puddly is still not back. If I'd have known, I wouldn't have asked him. Find him and bring him to me so I can give that Puddly a paddling.","content.75.4213":"So, runt, how'd you like them Apis? Bwahahaha!","content.75.4214":"What? Why would we stop? I'm here to take everything there is to eat, that's all! No one's stronger than the Taurs!","content.75.4215":"At night? He's got to be in his village resting.","content.75.4216":"Now that was fast! You're a loyal mercenary, and you didn't dawdle along the way! I wish I could say the same about my other employees... You certainly deserve a small award for putting the objective first.","content.75.4217":"Huh? The Api? What... Oh! Right. That old contract from a merchant who pulled it because he got tired of waiting.\\nI don't know what happened to you in that Jungle, but one thing's for sure... it wasn't a mission for you. Anyway, congratulations all the same! I'm sure you suffered rightly.","content.75.4218":"In any case, the contract has been fulfilled. Well done. Congratulations again!","content.75.4219":"The Taurs arrived a few months ago and started exploiting the Puddlies. At first, they just forced them to hand over their supplies. But Puddlies have recently started attacking adventurers who dare step foot in the region. We don't know much other than they're using tactics involving barrels of Apis.\\nTaurs are fearsome creatures. It's very difficult to get rid of them. However, the Puddlies are becoming an even bigger threat...","content.75.4220":"Well, I'll be a Gobball's uncle! An adventurer in my field! Don't ya have better to do than tickle me Moogrrs?{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}","content.75.4221":"From Amakna to Emelka, how'd he go, from Amakna to Emelka... Oh, hello. Help ya?","content.75.4222":"You've got awfully odd ways, you adventurers. Our life's not that thrillin' but we like to farm our patch in peace. What do ya want from me?","content.75.4223":"'lo. Ya wouldn't want to help me now would ya? I've gotta build the Moogrr pens 'cause they keep wanderin' off and the others aren't liftin' a finger!","content.75.4224":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to take on a little contract? ","content.75.4225":"This contract is a request from the oldest farmer in Amakna, who we affectionately call Old Joe. He's not in his right mind anymore, though, so I wouldn't be surprised if this was a false alarm. If you want to look into it anyway, head to the Singing Fields east of our capital.","content.75.4226":"The easiest thing would be to start by looking for clues at the scene of the crime. Old Joe should be waiting for you at his farm all the way southeast. I marked the exact location on your map, so just head there and collect as much information as you can to help you in your search.","content.75.4228":"Amakna is a fairly quiet nation, and low-level contracts are essentially to be found in the Singing Fields to the east, as well as near Emelka, north of the capital. They're often issued by farmers or villagers who can't fight or who need help with a task.","content.75.4229":"Haha, you're right that most of our contracts involve helping farmers with their heavy labor. But sometimes we have more serious problems. Recently, the Moogrrs and Plants have gone crazy and started attacking careless travelers, but nobody knows why. Not to mention the Cracklers in Emelka causing tremors, which is a growing concern.","content.75.4230":"Since the latest crisis with Ogrest's Tears, the entire ecosystem has been out of whack, but those creatures are pretty weak compared to everything else. There are also some high-level contracts to deal with Riktus-related problems. But I'll tell you more once you're powerful enough to take them on. Until then, avoid venturing south of the capital.","content.75.4231":"I'm sure that's true, but don't mistake recklessness for bravery. At any rate, you'll have to prove your worth before we'll let you take up any contracts. The mercenary post doesn't want to be responsible for a sudden and tragic death, and you'll have plenty of time to do them later.","content.75.4232":"Hey... I recognize ya! From the Mercenary Post. What're ya doin' in my field?","content.75.4233":"Me Moogrr? What Moogrr?","content.75.4234":"... ?","content.75.4235":"... OOOH, MOORRIGOLD! Me Moogrr, my beauteous Moogrr's gone! Me old farmer's heart's never hurt this much. Ah swear. That Moogrr was me whole life... She was in the pen next to me. Then this morn' no more Moorrigold. The Mooligrr Prize contest starts a few shakes. Gotta get a move on and find her! ","content.75.4236":"Well, now, that's nothing to do with me! But now that ya mention it, I remember seeing Old Joe with a strange fellow two moons ago while I was measurin' the pens. Don't know if it has anythin' to do with his Moogrr going missin'...","content.75.4237":"'lo. You the one who's gonna find Old Joe's Moogrr? Been watchin' ya run 'round for while now. Bad luck losin' his best Moogrr right afore the contest, it was... ","content.75.4238":"You again? I already told ya 'bout Old Joe!","content.75.4239":"That's nothin' to do with me! I just remember seein' Old Joe with a strange fellow about two moons ago while I was measurin' the pens.","content.75.4240":"Almost time for the agricultural fair to start. And this time, I'm gonna win the Mooligrr Prize, I am! Me Moogrrs are way above last years', you can bet your last bag of oats on that. ","content.75.4241":"You say that because of Old Joe? I don't need no Bwork strategy to win the prize. B'sides, we're in it just for fun. The way I see it, none of us would ever have hurt his Moogrr.","content.75.4242":"Still here? Ya should get a move on if you don't want to miss the start of the next contest!","content.75.4243":"I don't need no strategy to win the prize, I tell ya. It wasn't me. 'sides, it's all just in good fun. None of us'd ever hurt Old Joe's Moogrr.","content.75.4244":"The Moogrrs are all riled up lately like never before...  Sixth time today I've had to dodge a flying hoof. Sure as shootin' it's that Ogrest's fault!","content.75.4245":"I been seein' you run about asking questions, getting all up in everybody's business. Amakna's the kingdom of chatterboxes, so if it was one of us, we'd know! Pector mentioned a strange Foggernaut stalking 'round our farms these past few days. Don't much fancy havin' metal men 'round my place.","content.75.4246":"Still haven't found the culprit, right?","content.75.4247":"Pector mentioned a strange Foggernaut stalking 'round our farms these past few days. Don't much fancy havin' metal men 'round me place.","content.75.4249":"Any news 'bout me Moogrr? Me poor Moorrigold...","content.75.4250":"Yee-haw! Not much time, friend. The contest'll be startin' in a few minutes! I've already prepped Cloovrr for the strength contest, but she's not as talented as Moorrigold, that one... When you're ready, go talk to Morton, he's in charge of the contest.","content.75.4251":"Good day! You must have seen my husband when you arrived. I hope he didn't bother{[1*]?:} you too much with his stories. What brings you here?","content.75.4252":"Yeah there? Sorry, but I'm busy getting ready for the next Mooligrr Prize so I don't have time to chew the fat, ya see. Come back later!","content.75.4253":"The Mooligrr Prize strength contest is about to start. Have ya got a Moogrr to enter?","content.75.4254":"Well, now, that's just perfect. Hurry up, it's about to start!","content.75.4255":"Why are you still here? The challenge is waiting for you!","content.75.4256":"It's over. I'll never win me the Mooligrr Grand Prize. It's been me lifelong dream since I was knee-high to a Tofu... But without Moorrigold, it's no use. We can't win the other two contests.","content.75.4257":"It's very nice of you to offer to help, but you don't yet seem up to the task.\\nCome back when you have more experience.","content.75.4258":"It's very nice of you to offer to help, but I don't have anything for you at the moment. Come back tomorrow and I'll have a challenge for you!","content.75.4260":"Moooooooo? Moooo Mooo.","content.75.4261":"Mooo mooo...","content.75.4262":"Moo Moooo Mooooo.","content.75.4263":"Ah, you came{[1*]?:} to join the fight... Yes, the Amakna Militia is looking for recruits to deal with the Riktus forces.\\nThe Magik Riktus arrived in southern Amakna a few months ago already! They were living peacefully in their Bermuda Triangle, and now they've dropped anchor in the Fertile Prairie harbor. Those bandits have tried to carry out attacks in the capital, and they battle us from under our walls!","content.75.4264":"Our militia chief, Didi Stroyer, is leading a fierce resistance against those terrorists, but the conflict is dragging on and he needs more fighters. You might just provide vital support now that you seem to be at an adequate level.","content.75.4265":"It's a mistake... There's nothing for me to do here...","content.75.4266":"You have to believe me! I'm innocent! Mercy, help me get out of here!","content.75.4267":"Are you ready{[1*]?:} to listen to me? My name is Rick Tusse, and I'm a roaming Magik Riktus. I know all the jokes and pranks! I can sing every Ryk Astli song ever, and I can imitate the governors of all the nations.","content.75.4268":"And there you have it. Life as an entertainer hasn't been so easy since Ogrest's Chaos. People are too busy rebuilding their villages to laugh at my act.","content.75.4269":"It's still true for some Riktus, but in my opinion, I don't think robbing honest people is a profession with a future. So, I do odd jobs. I lend a hand here and there, nothing crazy. But one day, a person offered me a job with a rather tempting reward. All I had to do was unload some crates and put them in a warehouse, he said.","content.75.4270":"Yes, it was a man I had never seen before, some kind of Foggernaut, I think. In short, it was nighttime, and I had gone to the warehouse to work...","content.75.4271":"And bam, that's how I ended up in prison... You gotta believe me, I didn't do anything!","content.75.4273":"There are several hundred of them and only a few of us... It's going to be hard to surround them!","content.75.4274":"Hah! A greenhorn like you doesn't know anything about the battlefield! Me, I was in the Nietvam War and the Battle of Revdun! I'm a veteran among veterans... And I didn't hire the{[1*]?:} first{[1*]?:} runt{[1*]?:} who came along{[1*]?:}!","content.75.4275":"Listen, kid{[1*]?:}... It's a real no man's land here. There's no place for fairy tales. Just setting foot on this land puts your life in peril! Prove to me you're capable of surviving in conditions like this and help us accomplish our environmental goals.","content.75.4276":"You got guts, kid{[1*]?:}, but that's not enough. I've fought with the most decorated warriors in the world! I personally trained Rykke Errel, Brutas and Goultard! Iop even personally asked me to take his place in the final combat against Ogrest!","content.75.4277":"The... The nerve, the gall! I'll show you what I'm made of!","content.75.4278":"I saw the contest, I did. Bravo, youngun, you've got raising Moogrrs in your blood, sure as shootin'! Just one contest left to go. Train Kamoomile so Cloovrr can rest.","content.75.4279":"We did it! We won the Mooligrr Grand Prize! You've warmed the cockles of this old Enutrof's heart. Thank you, adventurer.{[1*]?:}","content.75.4280":"What have ya got for me there? Kamoomile's bell? Well, thank ya kindly for everything you've done for me Moogrrs, friend. They're all doing wonderfully!","content.75.4281":"Okay, okay, I think that's enough...","content.75.4282":"If this war has dragged on so long, it's because the Riktus we're fighting seem more organized and united than usual. Initially, they were just small groups of bandits, no more than three or four at once. But for some time now, they've started operating like a gang. Maybe you should go check out... Wait. Who are you?","content.75.4283":"War against Amakna? Listen, if you only came to ask me that, you've wasted your time. Instead, you should be asking the hundreds of Magik Riktus who've been captured by the Amaknian guards and thrown into the dungeon! We've seen hundreds of Riktus disappear completely!","content.75.4284":"Yes, that's why we're warring against Amakna. Until we've found our brother bandits, we will continue to use send forth our forces, no doubt about it.","content.75.4285":"Other Riktus? I'm the only one imprisoned here at the moment! The others escaped a few days ago... Are you saying that they may have escaped but didn't go back to the Bermuda Triangle?","content.75.4286":"A mysterious individual, you say? And numerous Riktus who escaped from prison but have gone back home nevertheless... What's more, while you were gone, their attacks intensified... I hate to say this, but that really smells like trouble.","content.75.4287":"The Amaknian authorities aren't willing to wage open battle against the Riktus. A great many souls would perish in the process. Some of our soldiers simply come from our farms, and our greatest warriors are currently traveling the world. There is only one solution to prevent a direct conflict...","content.75.4288":"Exactly! Their armada was reinforced with a large warship. It's one of the largest Riktus reinforcements on the Plain. If we can sink the ship, that should allow us to slow down the arrival of their reinforcements. That way, we can contain their attacks and return to the status quo.\\nPrepare well. It'll be well guarded...","content.75.4289":"Congratulations, mercenary! We're proud to include you in our ranks, and Amakna owes you a debt of gratitude! The Magik Riktus will continue prowling the Plains, but they've been weakened. Peace is restored for a time.","content.75.4290":"You seem to be saying a single individual is behind the recent troubles in Amakna... If that's the case, maybe this war between Amakna and Riktus was nothing but a setup from the start. But I have to wonder who would benefit from the situation.\\nI'll dispatch a few mercenaries and alert the Amaknian government. We'll try and find that Foggernaut. Your contract here is complete, so take a well-earned rest! We'll keep you posted if there are any new developments.","content.75.4291":"Yes, the Magik Riktus might not all be terrorists after all. Who knows anymore? I'm no longer sure of anything. Our masked opponent really played us... But he'll regret that!","content.75.4292":"The Mooligrr Prize beauty contest is about to start. Have ya got a Moogrr to enter?","content.75.4293":"If ya say so. We can get started!","content.75.4294":"The contract is a request from one of our most promising bakers. Xav produces golden wheat, a new variety that seems to make exceptional flour. To reach his domain, you'll have to travel through the Singing Fields, east of our capital, until you get to Gobballfield. I marked it on your map.","content.75.4295":"This case seems special. Xav put up a contract for his friend Glovis, who seems to have gone missing. Start by going to see the interested party, have him explain the situation, and then you can get rowdy. Be careful, though - this must be connected to those mutant plants that have been popping up.","content.75.4296":"Ah! Excellent, I was reluctant to return to the mercenary post. Things are getting worse. I haven't seen my friend Glovis since he delivered his last harvest to me several days ago... I wasn't worried until now, especially since he'd only just recovered from a trying ordeal...","content.75.4297":"He lost everything after the Ogrest's Tears disaster - his crops were all destroyed. I offered him work here in Gobballfield, but he's a stubborn one and preferred to stay on his own land. Just recently, he seemed to have developed a special fertilizer, which he used to grow his crops in record time!","content.75.4298":"I couldn't tell you. Last time I saw him, he was carrying his latest harvest, wanting me to make bread from it. His plot got invaded by those highly aggressive plants, and now I'm afraid the trouble is spreading to my land as well. Some of my plants are growing weird...","content.75.4301":"Wow... That's almost worse than being a ghoul!!! Listen, if what you say is true, you need to be very careful; you're in grave danger. But don't worry, you're not the only one this has happened to. For some guidance, go to Wagnar's Castle. Once in the hall, head for the door on your left and examine it. After you've done that, come back and see me and I'll tell you more!","content.75.4302":"Oh, yes, sorry... That's what I was afraid of. When you fought Vampyro, Shadofang stole part of your shadow... That's what lets her force images and some of her will on you! You're in very serious danger... She wants to steal your shadow and your soul! Go see Jenry Hones, Sr. at the Temple of Scriptures. He should be able to give you more information.","content.75.4303":"Thanks for your help, adventur{[1*]?er:er}! If you find anything, you should go talk to Shika Ingalsse. She knows a lot about plants in the area, so she'll probably be able to help us. She often hangs around just above Gobballfield, you can't miss her!","content.75.4304":"Shadofang, you say? Do you mean the Shushu that Wagnar is supposed to be guarding, who ended up seducing him? That's unfortunate... Shadofang is an extremely powerful Major Shushu... You should be worried!","content.75.4305":"Sorry, that's just the way it is! Shadofang managed to dominate Wagnar, who became Vampyro, by imposing some of her will on him. Her dearest wish is to be able to leave her current prison, Vampyro's ring in which she is trapped, in order to regain physical form in our world. With the little I know about Shushus, I doubt her intentions are positive as far as we are concerned if she succeeds. She must be prevented from doing so.","content.75.4306":"Vampyro is merely a puppet... Believe me, Shadofang's power is much, much more than anything you've come across. It must have been precisely during that fight that she saw you as a potential bodily envelope. She must be have been waiting for you to get strong enough to pull you back to herself to finalize her grip on your shadow and control you completely!","content.75.4307":"Well, you haven't got a choice; your time is running out. You need to find a way to recover the portion of your shadow she took from you so that she no longer has a hold over you; otherwise, you're lost! I suggest you go see Ahr Khayuh at Shusnitch Reef. She's a disciple of Otomai; you're sure to have run into her before. As far as I know, she's the one who knows the most about Shushus. She should be able to help you out of this mess!","content.75.4308":"Have you got a problem with a Major Shushu? Then you've come to the right place! Shushus are my specialty! Tell me more so I know exactly what's going on. ","content.75.4309":"Hmhm... Fascinating! So, you're dealing with Shadofang... Aren't you the lucky one! Well, I mean... It's true that she's not just anyone, after all... Very well. I'll help you. It might help further my research, too. What do you want to know?","content.75.4310":"Shadofang is a 5-element Major Shushu. In other words, she is extremely powerful. She's on the same level as Anathar, for example, and some even think she's Rushu's favorite. She was trapped in a ring that acts as a prison by Armand-Louis, the sovereign of Forfut at the time and Wagnar's ancestor. He's said to have used Shadofang's weakness - her word. You should know that demons always keep their word. Another of Shadofang's defining characteristics is obviously her ability to steal her victims' shadows and turn them into ghouls. Each shadow she captures extends her hair and makes it darker; her hair is what she cares about the most...","content.75.4311":"The only way to trap a Shushu in an item is to make a pact with the Shushu so that it goes into the item willingly. Armand-Louis threatened to cut Shadofang's hair if she didn't go into the ring; that's how he captured her. In fact, a Shushued item is very similar to Haven Bags; they are portable dimensions. These item-dimensions are prisons for Shushus.","content.75.4312":"Well, you should know that Shushued items completely neutralize the powers of the demon trapped in it in the World of Twelve, but in this dimension, their power is total. The demon takes its original form and can act freely inside it. I'm afraid that the only way for you to get your shadow back is to go find Shadofang in person and make a pact with her for her to give it back! Without a doubt, she'll have to agree to give it back to you if you manage to get the better of her in single combat. Defeat Shadofang and she'll return your shadow...","content.75.4313":"The place is rather gloomy... I hope I don't take too long here; I'm not as young as I used to be!","content.75.4314":"These Riktus don't seem to be made of the same stuff as the ones we've run into so far. The fight is looking tough. It appears you've already had a run-in with Grossanto in the past.","content.75.4315":"Greetings, traveler{[1*]?:}! Beware, the chant of the carts can lull the most careful of adventurers into a trance.","content.75.4316":"We've connected the recent incidents in Amakna. There seems to be a troubling assembly of individuals in our nation's mine. That must be where the mysterious Foggernaut is holed up.","content.75.4317":"Absolutely. It's an open contract. Whoever nabs that troublemaker is awarded the bounty. And one last thing...","content.75.4318":"Our enemy has sullied the fields and livestock of Amakna, exploited the Cracklers, and fabricated evidence to start a war with the Riktus. He is extremely dangerous and devoid of remorse. If his goal is to wreak bloody havoc on the nation, he's doing well so far.","content.75.4319":"You don't understand. He's got no regard for the impact he may have on the ecosystem. Everyone knows that to create something, you have to sacrifice something else in exchange. But that one seeks only to create and create some more... He's disrupting the balance of the entire Krosmoz. And that's the last thing we need right now. We all pay in the end, after all...","content.75.4320":"Oh, I... I didn't see... Behind you, those feathers, that sword... Could it really be the Black Crow?!","content.75.4321":"You're right. Times are tough! A menace has set up its den in the depths of the mine, in a place where no light reaches. I dare not get close. It's the Riktus...","content.75.4322":"Yes, but they're different. They're not Magik Riktus, they're just a bunch of swindling bandits who dress in black to better blend in with the darkness in the mine. I suspect they tampered with the rails in the mine to cause who knows what kind of calamity with the carts...","content.75.4323":"What audacity! You'd have to be very brave to dare come to my home! Brave... or very stupid!!!\\n\\n*sarcastic laugh* It looks like I was right to choose you as my prey; you've fallen straight into my trap!{[1*]?:} Now all I have to do is finish you off and your shadow will be mine!","content.75.4324":"Perhaps, but be as it may, be ready to help us get rid of them. I no longer dare imagine what twisted plan whatshisname in charge of the herd is preparing.","content.75.4325":"Sadly no, they settled in some of the mine's old abandoned quarries that I no longer go to. I only know the name of their leader. He goes by the name \"Grossanto\".","content.75.4326":"I see... Do you really think you have a choice? How amusing... and pathetic... But since that's the way it is, let's play... I'm listening, but hurry. I'm eager to get this over with and get out of here. ","content.75.4327":"*Snickers*\\n\\nI'm going to crush you in any case, no doubt about it. How risky can it be to make the deal? You have my word... If you beat me, I'll return your complete shadow... If not, you'll be mine...\\n\\nThere's just one catch: You must bring me a Shadowed Potion or there's no fight!\\n\\n*Evil laugh* Let's end this!","content.75.4328":"Show what you've found. By the Twelve! You say you found this in Xav's field? This substance appears to contain enough Stasis to contaminate a whole parcel... But there's another problem. For a plant to experience such growth, it must have consumed a large amount of Wakfu.","content.75.4329":"Yes, normally, but the plant drains the Wakfu straight from the soil. If they multiply, the fields of Amakna could become unworkable! I'm familiar with these plants, and in normal times they aren't supposed to pose this kind of problem.","content.75.4330":"Let's recap.","content.75.4331":"Old Joe, who tried to win the Mooligrr prize, bought special fodder for his Moogrr from Grossanto. Her physical capabilities greatly increased, but her mental skills declined... Apparently, depriving her of her special hay (and beating her a little) was enough to make her return to normal.","content.75.4332":"Because of Ogrest's Chaos, which decimated his farm, Glovis bought a special fertilizer from Grossanto. This fertilizer was actually a pesticide that contaminated all the plants in the area and made them come to life.\\nI wonder if it's the same ingredient as the one used in the Moorrigold fodder...","content.75.4333":"All that just to create a strange explosive powder.","content.75.4334":"Grossanto convinced some Magik Riktus to unwittingly position the explosives he got on the Cracklers in various warehouses in Amakna. I wonder if Grossanto wants to destroy these warehouses so he can sell his strange product more easily.","content.75.4335":"If that's the case, these Black Riktus are certainly the ones who escaped. Maybe they're under the influence of this mysterious doping product. They must be formidable adversaries...","content.75.4336":"Apparently his objective is to sell this strange product. But as Shinka and the mercenary chief said, this drug is bad news, and it could disturb the Wakfu's equilibrium, or destroy Amakna even. The matter is more grave than I thought...","content.75.4337":"Glovis... That boy wouldn't hurt a Moofly. Plus, he's not smart enough to modify plants or create a substance like that... Oh no! Glovis has made a lot of wheat deliveries lately. They must all be contaminated! You have to find it fast before the inhabitants eat it.","content.75.4338":"Perfect. While you were gone{[1*]?:}, I looked at this substance more closely, and I think it's used as a doping product. The plants' metabolism doesn't allow them to resist such trauma, and, as defense mechanism, they start to grow way too fast by draining the Wakfu from the soil.","content.75.4339":"If we don't really have any information on his position, it's because he's still at home. Otherwise, someone surely would have noticed him. Gather some companions and go see what's become of him. Make sure you destroy all the plants on the parcel. No need to take any risks, even if the task is unpleasant.","content.75.4340":"Address the root of the problem, literally and figuratively! These plants have become like this by human intervention. We have to keep them from reproducing and find Glovis so they don't reproduce. ","content.75.4342":"It is okay? Were you able to recover all the contaminated wheat from the surrounding areas?","content.75.4343":"Thank you again for saving me. What can I do to help you?","content.75.4344":"Unfortunately, nothing much. As I already said, he didn't give me his name. However, he did look very scholarly and seemed to have just developed the substance. I reckon I was a guinea pig, in spite of myself. I hope he doesn't have anymore in reserve. Who knows what he might do with it?","content.75.4345":"Not one drop more. He told me I should use it all up for the product to be effective, and that's what I did. If only I hadn't listened, my fields wouldn't be in such a state. I hope that Xav will still want me to help him in Gobballfield in spite of what I did.","content.75.4346":"What are still you doing here? Hurry up and take care of these plants before the situation gets worse!","content.75.4347":"How are you? Thank you for your help with the wild grass. You've no doubt saved the lands of Amakna from an undesirable fate! Do you need something?","content.75.4348":"All this happened because of a Foggernaut scientist... I knew Glovis couldn't have bad intentions! So, he's agreed to come work with us, which will give his land time to recover and allow him to process this whole thing.","content.75.4349":"Thank you, adventur{[1*]?er:er}. I'll never forget what you did for us! That business with the Foggernaut is still worrisome. How about mention it at the mercenary post when you go pick up your reward!","content.75.4350":"You contained the threat? It's fair to say this matter's all squared away. Xav already sent me a letter singing your praises! It's nice to see such potential in a new recruit.","content.75.4351":"You must mean that Foggernaut scientist. I gave his description to the other mercenaries. I'm sure we'll catch him one of these days. For now, here's your reward. You earned it! Amakna will need mercenaries like you again in the future.","content.75.4352":"Old Joe isn't completely senile after all! I see you got acquainted with the local customs. You must've made people jealous winning the Mooligrr prize like that, haha. Thanks to you, the farmers could enjoy the festival without needing to worry about their Moogrrs.","content.75.4353":"In any case, this thing with the fodder and the Foggernaut is odd. Apparently he hasn't shown up around the farmers since then, but we'll keep an eye out. At least you helped out and became acquainted with Amakna. Here's your reward for all the good work!","content.75.4354":"Did you check to see if me Moogrr is in the stable?","content.75.4355":"Was that really the Black Crow down there?","content.75.4356":"I'm from one of the wealthiest families in Amakna. Of course, being wealthy in Amakna doesn't mean much... The name won't ring a bell. We were honest farmers. We worked the land hard, we fed our Moogrrs and gave them a lot of love. Of course, we never forgot our roots, and helping neighbors in need was always a matter of principle.","content.75.4357":"One day, a merchant visited us. He offered us a very particular contract. He demanded funding to carry out strange experiments on the soil. He was convinced that by using Wakfu to interfere with the Stasis aided by certain chemical procedures, the harvests would become more profitable. These promises were crazy. According to him, we could have planted wheat in the winter, and, if his experiments on living creatures were fruitful, we could have worked whole weeks without ever stopping.","content.75.4358":"That's right. We did, of course, refuse his financing proposal. But some strange catastrophes occurred not long after... And my family suddenly fell ill and into poverty. My grandfather, Joe, was the only survivor. I left my life as a farmer to become a bandit in the hopes of making a few kamas!","content.75.4359":"Life with the Magik Riktus was simple, dishonest and marked by a deep melancholy. No bandit was there by chance... I met some brave guys whom life had not spoiled, guys who had lost it all from one day to the next. What we shared was an indelible nostalgia and a desire to return to simpler days.","content.75.4360":"Grossanto is the one who gave them his famous doping product. It increases their physical abilities, but they lose their ability to think. I tried to resist Grossanto, to prevent him from... But it was too late. We should have never agreed to him helping us avoid prison.","content.75.4361":"He has gathered a formidable army now... If we don't stop him from causing harm fast enough, who knows what he's capable of doing?","content.75.4362":"He's hiding in a cave deep in the mines and is protected by guards, falling rocks and explosive mines. You must be very careful when you approach him.","content.75.4363":"You'll always be welcome in me fields, adventurer. Me Moogrrs and me will be right glad to see you again. Thanks for everything.{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}","content.75.4364":"These mines terrify me... Please, you have to stop Grossanto!","content.75.4365":"How excellent for you, you're saved!{[1*]?:} Hmm, can you show me that belt? Well, look at that! True, it's not in the most pristine condition, but this item holds great power. The problem is, it's worthless the way it is now. But there must be a way to fix that. To start with, I'll need a dark purple dye that's high in Stasis. That should revive the item's dormant power. Bring me some of that and we'll see how it goes.","content.75.4366":"The contract was requested by Alibert, mayor of Emelka, the neighboring town. To get there, just head north - I've marked it on your map. Apparently the town has had earthquakes with increasing frequency, and he's rather concerned about it.","content.75.4367":"Perfect! I wasn't expecting any less of you. Let's see... *fiddles around for a few minutes* Well, the Stasified Dark Purple has produced the intended effect. It's restored the belt's power. However, now we'll need to repair the belt. I'm going to need two catalysts of Shushu origin. Once again, these must be closely connected to Stasis. You'll find some on the other side of this portal. ","content.75.4368":"Alibert suspects the Cracklers are causing these disturbances. The mountain was hit hard by the latest Ogrest's Tears episode, and the Cracklers seem much more aggressive than usual, so your job is to confirm or disprove this theory, and if possible, put a stop to it.","content.75.4369":"Thanks for coming so quickly, adventur{[1*]?er:er}. The villagers have been panicking since the last tremor caused a chunk of mountain to fall near a home. I'm afraid the next one will have dire results.","content.75.4370":"They seemed agitated after the Ogrest's Tears crisis, but it's only gotten worse in the last few weeks. They've started attacking anyone who ventures outside the village. No one knows why they're reacting that way, and I don't see what else could be causing tremors like that. ","content.75.4371":"It wasn't going to take me long to point out the problem... Some of the Crackler population got trapped in the mines after part of the mountain collapsed. At first, they wandered the tunnels aimlessly. More recently, though, they've started smashing the walls.","content.75.4372":"The two Crackler populations are surely trying to reach one another. Unless something else is going on, but I don't dare venture into the tunnels again for fear they'll collapse on me. Be careful{[1*]?:} if you go in there!","content.75.4373":"Very good! Well, the hardest part is over, but we're not done yet. We have the catalysts to restore the belt's full power. But we're still missing a few materials to make it usable. Here's a short list of things I need to finish my work. Lucky for you, I know a thing or two about the leather trade! So, bring me a master leather dealer's seal, 15 blood-drenched nettle leaves, 80 eternal leathers, and 200 powders. ","content.75.4374":"So, bring me a master leather dealer's seal, 15 blood-drenched nettle leaves, 80 eternal leathers, and 200 powders so I can finish repairing the belt.","content.75.4375":"Everything's good! Give me a few minutes and I'll fix it for you. *a few minutes later* Here is your well-earned belt!","content.75.4377":"What? The Riktus are exploiting the Cracklers to extract ore and make bombs? That can't be good at all... With the mining and the Cracklers on the surface trying to free their fellow beings, it's not surprising that Amakna is shaking in all directions.","content.75.4378":"You'll have no chance trying to take on the Riktus and the Cracklers all at once. One thing at a time. It appears that the Royal Crackler has the power to whisper in the ears of all Cracklers through stones. He must be the one who gives the ones on the surface their orders... If you neutralize him, the Cracklers will get disoriented!","content.75.4379":"He's hiding up in the mountains. The good news is, there are two ways to get in. One is behind Emelka if you climb up the mountain, and the other one is the opposite. You go through this mine and go up through the tunnels. I locked the entrance, but I can give you the key. It's up to you to decide which way you prefer, but I'd suggest taking some friends with you.","content.75.4380":"So, it really was the Cracklers who were behind the tremors... Thus, you made a deal by doing business with the Royal Crackler. That reminds me of a story I used to tell to my little Yugo. It is said that if children wander off into the mountains at night, the Royal Crackler, believing the child to be lost, can turn the children to stone and adopt them as his own.","content.75.4381":"Ahahah, I got it from my father, and he got it from his father. It's especially useful for protecting children in the village, but like all legends, there is some truth to it, as you've just shown me. You've done a great job. Thank you, adventurer{[1*]?:}. You can return to the Mercenary Post to receive your well-deserved reward!","content.75.4382":"Reports seem to indicate that Emelka hasn't suffered a single earthquake since I gave you this contract. Who would've thought you could converse with creatures like that? It's true that Ogrest's Chaos doesn't only affect humans. Monsters have to deal with the fallout as well. At any rate, you did excellent work!","content.75.4383":"The situation in the mines is indeed still troublesome, but you can't go up against the Riktus just yet. Not to worry: There'll be a separate contract for them. Enjoy your victory, and get even stronger so you can take care of them later on!","content.75.4384":"The Mooligrr Prize tenacity contest is about to start. Which Moogrr is entering this time?","content.75.4385":"Let's see what she can do. On your mark!","content.75.4387":"Oh yes, you're responsible{[1*]?:} for bringing back a Divine Koko, isn't that it? My{[1*]?:} poor devil, it's no easy task. However, it's true that the Kokokos look quite agitated, especially on an island off the coast of Sufokia. There could very well be one there right now!","content.75.4388":"Sufokia is a nation that prospers mainly thanks to its sea trade, so it depends less on its natural resource production. Low-level contracts happen in the Terrana Dune, a tourist beach to the east that is regularly invaded by monsters that need killing. We also have many contracts in which wealthy merchants are looking for collectible items that need to be recovered as soon as possible.","content.75.4389":"The following contracts take place near the Puddly Mountains and the Jumpin' Jungle to the northwest. The zone is fiercely guarded by belligerent Puddlies and Taurs. They aren't a direct threat to Sufokia, but they're stopping us from exploiting the area, which is sometimes a bit of a problem for some.","content.75.4390":"Not at all. Snappers got caught in the depths, and it drove them crazy. But the biggest problem is the Rogues who have been spotted in the tunnels more than once. They're surely up to something, but it's hard to say what those swindlers are plotting. In any case, they have high-level contracts out on them.","content.75.4391":"It's possible. Either you don't have the necessary level for new contracts, or you might have already done them all! There's nothing stopping you from taking care of other problems yourself without expecting a reward from us! You'll still improve all the same if you do, so don't hesitate. ","content.75.4392":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.4393":"Bonta is a nation that consumes enormous amounts of resources to maintain its economic growth. We've have some bad luck with the mine Mushdskitos. We have to cull the population regularly or the groundwater gets contaminated. No one's made a request about these monsters, but there's nothing stopping you from taking care of them yourself. ","content.75.4394":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to take on a little contract? ","content.75.4395":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.4396":"It's possible. Either you don't have the necessary level for new contracts, or you might have already done them all! Bonta only has one contract right now, but there's nothing stopping you from taking care of other problems yourself without expecting a reward from us! You'll still improve all the same if you do, so don't hesitate. ","content.75.4397":"Brakmar is a nation built on dangerous, inhospitable terrain. Many legends and strange phenomena add to the local folklore. The first contracts take place in the Sidimote Moors to the north and in the mines that have been invaded by the Chafers. These somewhat intelligent, revived beings are beginning to act strangely. A new Chafer king may have been born, and he seems aggressive.","content.75.4398":"No one has taken out a contract to end the threats to Brakmar. There's nothing stopping you from taking care of the threats yourself without expecting a reward from us! You'll still improve all the same if you do, so don't hesitate. ","content.75.4399":"Mercenary Posts let you take on contracts with rewards worthy of the completed task, in each region of the World of Twelve and beyond. To take on contracts, you must first have proven your worth and be up to level for the area in which the contracts are located.\\nThere are 3 difficulty rankings. You must finish all Rank 1 contracts before you can take on Rank 2 contracts. You must finish all Rank 2 contracts before you can take on Rank 3 contracts.","content.75.4400":"So, looking for a little adventure? Maybe you'd like to take on a little contract? ","content.75.4401":"We can't hide anything from you. The most aggressive ones are the Dark Treechnids, a new species that appeared as deforestation of Yurbut intensified. They are very dangerous and an intermediate contract has been taken out on them to try to find a solution. The lumberjacks are terrified and refusing to work...","content.75.4402":"Actually, it appears there's something even worse. A secret organization, whose members go by the name of \"Hoodlums\", apparently has it in for the capital. We've already sent several mercenaries to investigate them and their alleged HQ deep in the mines, but none have returned. We haven't issued a contract for that problem yet.","content.75.4403":"All the better. In a less secret note, we have concerns about the Scaraleaf overpopulation in the Pabong Fields to the east of the capital. They could eventually scorch the little greenery remaining in Brakmar! The intermediate contracts will concern the Musical Blops in Macheville, to the far north of Brakmar. They look harmless, but their music is a very powerful magic, so you'd better beware, all the same.","content.75.4404":"The high-level contracts concern the Stalagmotes, mineral monsters made of hardened lava that populate the depths of the mines. Veteran mercenaries ventured down there and were eventually buried under the rubble. The miners are terrified and refusing to work until their population is reduced, which is very problematic.","content.75.4405":"Ah! You're right to quench your thirst for paranormal knowledge. I've just captured one of these specimens. I tried to question it earlier, but I couldn't get anything out if it. That said, I don't think they pose a great threat to Astrub as such, but you never know. You can try talking to it if you think that'll help you find out more.","content.75.4406":"The recollections of those Yokai in the form of blueish flames... I like that a lot. They look so beautiful as part of my interior decor. If you bring me five of them, I'd even have enough to make you a wonderful lantern to light your way in the darkest corners of World of Twelve.","content.75.4407":"Kiiiiii! That hults! Stop stliking me! *The Lenald spirit is clearly terrified*","content.75.4408":"You'le not going to stlike me? You'le sule? Finally, a nolmal human! That clazy woman leally put me thlough the wlingel! My name's Ikali, and I'm a Yokai, a Lenald spilit. My fliends ale being contlolled by a dalk powel, and I'm wollied they'll halm innocent people. You have to help them find peace. I wanted to ask that woman fol help, but she locked me up and stluck me, yelling at me...","content.75.4409":"It's not oul fault! The witch conjuled us up in Astlub! I was playing a little plactical joke on a young Lenald flom my village when my fliends stalted disappealing... I walked all the way to find them hele, but they'le no longel themselves... Flee them, adventulel, and theil souls will be able to letuln to oul island.","content.75.4410":"Say, it seems he was more talkative with you than he was in my company. I trust he didn't give you any stupid ideas like preventing me from using his little friends' souls, for example? *smiles predatorily at you* You'd really be an angel if you were to help me gather some, but I can't force your hand...","content.75.4411":"*takes a knife out of her boot* No really, I insist; I certainly don't want to have to force your hand. After all, you don't have to help out a magnificent young lady such as myself, do you? I'd really like 50 of those Yokai souls, which should let me study them. Besides, I quite like the color.","content.75.4412":"I heald evelything... I don't speak to tlaitols.","content.75.4413":"Oh, fabulous! It can't have been easy; the souls are so volatile, so difficult to capture... But I'm happy it worked out well! When these Yokai fall in combat, they can lose control of their ethereal form and stabilize as a kind of flame, which is what you've brought me here. Their blue light has the most beautiful effect on my skin, don't you think? If you find any others, feel free to bring them to me!","content.75.4414":"The contract is a request from a prominent chef in Sufokia. He's asked the Guild to procure a Divine Koko so he can prepare an exceptional meal for the next Cartel banquet. In case you didn't know, it's a Kokonut that's been blessed by the Kokokos, and this blessing gives it a truly unique flavor, making it a rare delicacy that few people ever get a chance to taste in their lifetimes.","content.75.4415":"It's not that easy. There's only one Divine Koko in every generation of Kokokos, and it looks exactly like a normal Kokonut. That's why it's so hard to get. You should start looking on the Terrana Dune to the east. Ask Hugo Tydal if he has any information on suspicious behavior among Kokokos. Good luck!","content.75.4416":"Hello. You can't stay here. We're in the middle of the last-minute preparations for the second season of Kokokobana and only the contestants are allowed to stay on this part of the beach.","content.75.4418":"Hi there! My name's Raphito, and I love to fish Sharkie. It's my passion! If you're afraid of going hungry during the adventure, you should join our team because that's not likely to happen thanks to my skill as a fisherman and Teihourra's skill as a cook. I even know how to fish with a simple piece of string. After all, when you're in a survival situation, you don't always have your trusty fishing rod handy!","content.75.4419":"Of course. But that wouldn't impress the others as much. And that would be a real shame. Hahahaha. If I didn't want to make an impression, I wouldn't be wearing a loincloth and about to head to a deserted island, you know! Plus, Sharkie meat is much better than the rest, in my opinion.","content.75.4420":"AH! That changes everything. Well, normally I'd refuse. But our ratings are in a slump these days. Adding a surprise contestant could catch the public's attention! Hmmmm... I've decided. You can join us, but you'll need to pick a team, either Red or Yellow. Take some time to talk to them and let me know what you decide.","content.75.4422":"Hello, you. Let me say, right now, I'm panicking so hard... Nobody trusts anybody, nobody. Nobody trusts anybody. Do you understand? I hope it's not a sign, because I've figured this game out and it's better to play with me than against me. So, if you want to have a chance, you should join my team because I'm going to crush the other team! ","content.75.4423":"You aren't thinking of joining Kokoumba's team, are you? I'm sure it feels good to play with amateurs but you got to hustle if you want to make a kama. And look, the Red team is obviously going to win! Fishing Sharkie with the locals won't get you the win, believe me.","content.75.4424":"Hello, and welcome to the Yellow tribe! What's special about us is that all three of us are from small archipelagos in Sufokia. We're playing on home field, as they say! My specialty is physical challenges, but we all have our strengths and weaknesses. The atmosphere around camp is great. You'll see if you join us.","content.75.4425":"I hope you don't join Bob Roston's tribe. He's an egocentric nutcase and can't be trusted! Seems he already betrayed people last season. You should count on our friendship instead, but I can't force you, of course. ","content.75.4426":"Have you chosen your tribe?","content.75.4427":"AH! You're sure?{[1*]?:} Very well. From now on, you'll wear your tribe's buff. Go join them and talk to your captain because the next immunity challenge is about to start. ","content.75.4428":"Since time's running short, you'll have to take care of a few things before leaving. We need fresh water to fill our gourds, check the fish traps and collect whatever they caught, and recover a few Kokoko leaves for... various purposes.","content.75.4429":"Perfect! Sorry to have given you such a horrid task, but well... welcome to the Kokokobana adventure!{[1*]?:} And you're right on time. Geoff Grobst just announced the next challenge. Just head to the boat to joins on the island.","content.75.4430":"I knew you'd choose the Red team, my friend!{[1*]?:} We need to get ready for the next challenge. It's going to be on another island, and I can tell you that it won't be a walk in the park, not like here. We're going to start the survival part, real survival, in loincloths surrounded by Kokokos and wild weather!","content.75.4431":"Welcome to the Yellow tribe, [#name] ! Sorry to put you to work so soon, but we have to get ready for the next challenge. It's going to take place on another island and we won't be as comfortable as we are here. Plus, we'll be competing with the Red tribe, too... ","content.75.4432":"Were you able to get everything we needed?","content.75.4433":"Were you able to get everything we needed?","content.75.4434":"AH! However, there's a bone! The island was privatized by a wealthy Xelor, who developed a technology that allowed him to capture and retransmit images. Ever since, he's been amusing himself by reproducing extreme situations as a sort of game. He even named Kokokobana Island and built various facilities. I think if you want your Divine Koko, you're going to have to take part in this game. No one else is authorized to set foot on the island. ","content.75.4435":"You should speak with Geoff Grobst. He's the one who's in charge of organizing the game. He's quite successful, too! I'm not sure he'll accept, but you can always give it a try. He should be at the south end of the beach. You can't miss him. Good luck!","content.75.4436":"Now that we're on opposite teams, I'm going to ask you to leave, [#name]..","content.75.4437":"You made your choice. Don't come crying to us when we win!","content.75.4438":"What are you waiting for? The challenge has started. You need to get to the island!","content.75.4439":"The challenge isn't ready yet. Go back to your tribe and help them while you wait!","content.75.4440":"The challenge is about to start. Head to Kokokobana island. We'll meet you there!","content.75.4441":"The Immunity Totem is hidden deep in the island. Kokokos are in every room and you must triumph to move on to the next room. Keep the ballot papers. They will let you choose between fighting a particularly fierce local or entering the treasure room. But remember that the first team to recover the totem wins!","content.75.4442":"Well, well, well! I didn't really think you'd bring back a Divine Koko. That's quite a feat! You're going to be able to fulfill your contract, since they've fortunately let you{[1*]?:} participate... You've a funny look on your face. Something wrong?","content.75.4443":"Oh, I understand. You think you should have talked to them beforehand. But if you had, there's no way of knowing they would have allowed you{[1*]?:} to come onto the island. It was a necessary evil. In any case, it's just a game. They'll get over it, don't worry. You should really return to the Mercenary Post to receive your reward.","content.75.4444":"Really? It looks like a normal Kokonut to me, though... *He smells the Kokonut* That delicious sweet smell... no doubt about it, this is indeed a Divine Koko. Incredible! Did you have to compete in Kokokobana to get it? Between you and me, you'd have to be a bit nuts to walk around in a loincloth among the Kokokos... In any case, you deserve your reward!","content.75.4445":"You can now turn yourself in if you want to get rid of your outlaw status. You just have to go through the gate behind me.","content.75.4446":"I'm the law around here!","content.75.4447":"Are you looking to jump in the lion's den without any preparation?! I've know some fearless adventurers, but not like this. You'll have no chance if you play on their turf, and you don't even know where they've hidden the treasure. Plus, pirates follow a very strict code of honor. You'll get nothing out of them by force.","content.75.4448":"They won't say anything to an enemy, but to an ally is a different story. The Rogues might be clever, but we'll just have to outsmart them! Actually, I helped one reintegrate a few years ago. Currently, he's leading an honest life as a blacksmith, but he should be able to give you information. Return to Sufokia and find Synosore. With his help, you can't miss him.","content.75.4449":"... *he looks at you intently for a little while longer before returning to his work* I don't see any reason to speak with you. I'm just a simple blacksmith.","content.75.4450":"*He interrupts his work once again and sighs* The old man talks too much... Listen... That's all in the past. I have nothing to do with them anymore. Plus, I'm a deserter who betrayed the hunting party. I'll hang if I go back and see them. ","content.75.4451":"... Rogue pirates are subject to a strict code of honor. It's both a strength and a weakness because they have little reason to believe in the good faith of others. We all have different goals and pasts, but we're all pursuing the same ideal of freedom. *Synosore seems nostalgic for a brief moment* To find it, our mask determined our place in the band, and we used some... peculiar... formulations.","content.75.4452":"You'll see when they put you to the test. Just be careful not to repeat the same thing twice. As for the disguise, I put it in my cellar. My house isn't far from here. *he points southward with a vague hand gesture and returns to his work* You can keep it; it's of no further use to me. Go to an island to the east and pretend to be a new recruit. That should help you find out what you want to know.","content.75.4453":"This contract is of the utmost importance. Treasures that were being kept in the national bank were stolen a few days ago. The Cartel is sure that Rogue pirates are behind the theft, no doubt about it. Their last known hideout was in the depths of Sufokia Mine.","content.75.4454":"There were three treasure: an ogrine stone the size of my fist named \"Ogrest's Tear\", the priceless magic ring of the Stubbynubbins, a long-lost people in the World of Twelve, and an Ecaflip spell book. I don't know what pirates could do with those treasures other than sell them on the black market. You'll have to hurry!","content.75.4455":"Wait... It wasn't written in the contract but the Cartel was very clear about wanting to catch their leader to make an example of him and crush his organization. You'll therefore have to take care of him as well. Be especially careful when you go. You're not the first mercenary we've sent and some haven't come back.{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}","content.75.4456":"I've never seen you before. You've no business on this island, so get lost before I make you MY business!{[1*]?:}","content.75.4457":"Hello, friend.{[1*]?:} My name's Freudy, and I'm good at putting things together. A real Kraw-Gyver! If you want to have tools and be comfortable, you'd better come with me. We'll have weapons, fishing rods, and even a tent! ","content.75.4458":"And how! If only you could have seen me at nine. I managed to repair my mom's Zaap portal with a small Swiss Army knife and Grandpa Robert's toothpick. I certainly could set up in a corner of the city and earn my life easily. But where would the thrill of adventure be in that? No, really, I think I'm better off knocking stuff together on the beach, my chest hair in the breeze.","content.75.4459":"Hi, my name's Serah. Just because I'm a girl doesn't mean I'm not as strong as the others. Quite the opposite! I work out every day to keep my muscles strong, and every time I mess something up, boom, 20 push-ups as punishment! And when I'm bored... Boom, 20 push-ups! Need to calm down? Boom, 20 push-ups!","content.75.4460":"Well, yes. My body's my weapon. Gotta keep it in shape! You're safe with me. I could even teach you a few fighting tricks during the adventure. The two of us will fill the ocean with our sweat. It'll be great!","content.75.4461":"My name is Teihourra and I'm from these islands. I don't want to brag, but I think I'm the greatest survival specialist out of all the contestants. I was abandoned in the jungle when I was six years old, and I had to survive for several months drinking rainwater and eating roots and berries. So sad.","content.75.4462":"Maybe, but today that gives me a huge advantage over the others! My real passion is cooking. I want to win so I can open my own Yumm-Cart and travel the World of Twelve making delicious meals for adventurers. That's been my dream ever since I got out of this jungle.","content.75.4463":"*He seems to squint under his mask* Do you think we share all our secrets with just anyone who comes along?{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} You have to be real pirate material!{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} And I only know one way to find out if you are. Get ready for a duel. The weapon is insults!","content.75.4464":"*Smisse starts laughing and points at you* You know what, rookie? I've met Piwis that are more threatening than you!","content.75.4465":"Not bad... But you're a lightweight. Even my 98-year-old grandma has more muscles than you!","content.75.4466":"Ha ha ha. Nice try. But you know what you remind me of? A bag of barf{[1*]?:}, my friend.","content.75.4467":"Yeah, well you're... you're a... baboon dropping, you are!","content.75.4468":"Had enough? I'm not going to lose to someone who's about as classy as a monkey in a monkey suit!","content.75.4469":"Ha ha ha, I already said that! Learn to swear like a real{[1*]?:} pirate{[1*]?:} before you come back again.","content.75.4470":"*Smisse World suddenly changes color; you hit him where it hurts* You... You... BABOON DROPPING, YOU!","content.75.4471":"I've got some business to settle in town, but the last time I went in, I almost made the guards suspicious. I'd rather not take any risks and send you instead this time. Nothing very complicated, I promise. One of the craftsmen in Sufokia has owed us a hefty sum of money for too long now. *He holds out an IOU* ","content.75.4472":"It's the cook, Fafahoff. Feel free to threaten him if he seems reluctant. Then use the money to grease the palm of Fertilizator, the Sufokia lumberjack. This isn't the first time we've worked with him, so just tell him that I sent you and to do like usual. We need a lot of wood again for our plan.","content.75.4473":"You'll see for yourself if you do this. So hurry up and come back to see me when it's done.","content.75.4474":"So? Did you finish the job I gave you?","content.75.4475":"*Fafahoff signs* I knew I shouldn't have hired those louts... Don't wear yourself out trying to convince me. I'll give you your money. I know just what you're capable of, and I don't want any more trouble. *He digs through his pocket, pulls out a purse of kamas, and hands it to you* Now, if you aren't planning on buying anything, get lost. ","content.75.4476":"An ax ashore is an ax for war! Looking for an ax? Don't worry, it'll do!","content.75.4478":"I'm Fafahoff, the executive chef of Sufokia. Here, we mainly use ingredients from the sea, but I import good meat from Brakmar to satisfy my appetite. I can't help it. You can't start the day without a good meal. Did you want to order?","content.75.4480":"{[1*]?:}Hey little one! Here, we arm everyone. No exceptions!","content.75.4482":"Welcome to the fashion accessories bazaar! \\nWhat can I do-hoo for you-hoo?","content.75.4488":"Hey there snapper, everything going swimmingly?","content.75.4490":"Can I interest you in the handyman profession?","content.75.4491":"An ax ashore is an ax for war! Looking for an ax? Don't worry, it'll do!","content.75.4492":"The chopper is a cook's best friend. A good blade never betrays its master, no matter how vigorously it's used for cutting and slicing. At least, that's what I was taught. I'm Tyra Misu, the Brakmar cook. Do you need a piece of meat?","content.75.4493":"I can see you're a person of taste! And which profession would you like to learn to become the best chef of the year?","content.75.4494":"On which forge would you like to start?","content.75.4495":"{[1*]?:}Hey little one! Here, we arm everyone. No exceptions!","content.75.4496":"And what profession would you like to learn?","content.75.4497":"Welcome to the fashion accessories bazaar! \\nWhat can I do-hoo for you-hoo?","content.75.4498":"Hello there, shrimp! Are you lost?","content.75.4499":"Don't make a sound. You'll scare the fish away. What do you want?","content.75.4500":"Oh, a visitor! What can I do for you?","content.75.4501":"{[1*]?:}Hello, adventurer. What can I do for you?","content.75.4502":"{[1*]?:}Hello, adventurer. What can I do for you?","content.75.4503":"Another{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}? I didn't see you{[1*]?:} arrive. What are you here to do?","content.75.4504":"Oh, a visitor! What can I do for you?","content.75.4505":"Good day, {[1*]?ma'am:sir}. If you are here to work with wood, you're in the right place. I've just only finished my apprenticeship, but I think I can help you. What can I do for you?","content.75.4507":"*Georgiana blushes deeply when you look at her*\\n\\nW-welcome, adventurer{[1*]?:}! If you're looking for accessories or clothing, I'd be glad to hug... err, help! Help you. What can I do for you?","content.75.4509":"Hey kid, you falling in love with my wheat or something?{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} Feel free to visit our beautiful city and its many interesting attractions. What with the crafts, temples, and government buildings, there's a lot to see! Are you interested in anything in particular?","content.75.4510":"If you're looking for a weapon, you're in the right place, kid.{[1*]?:}. We're not here to play games! Although, sometimes patience is a virtue... I've been waiting 236 years for my sword, and my virtue is starting to wear thin...","content.75.4512":"Well, yeah, that's nothing! Just grab like this, pull a little, a few well placed hits with a hammer, and boom: a brand new bell!","content.75.4513":"Hey, you! Come over here and smell these beautiful buns, straight out of the oven. A real treat, right? Sorry, I forgot my manners... My name is Shosanne, and I'm the executive chef of Amakna hihi! What can I do for you?","content.75.4515":"Hello, adventurer{[1*]?:}! To what do I owe the pleasure of seeing you in my dear Frigost Village? I can serve you some Gobball stew if you're hungry. I also run the village inn. You can also take this time to say hello to Yugo, my little Piwi. He loves adventure stories!","content.75.4516":"Hello! Welcome to Gobballfield. What can I do for you?","content.75.4517":"Come here, little one... What can I do you for?","content.75.4518":"Out of shorts? What? We can't wear shorts all the time... {[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}You're losing your mind, poor soul.","content.75.4519":"Hurried? {[1*]?:}You've got a lot of gall coming here to beg! Don't young people learn manners anymore?","content.75.4520":"Hmmm... Nope, haven't seen him around lately. And you, Kirikon?... No, Kirikon hasn't seen him either.","content.75.4521":"I'm very well, thank you. When the kama's up, everything just falls into place, right Kirikon? Yes, you're a good Drheller, you are!","content.75.4522":"Shhh! Listen... Do you hear it too? I'm sure he's out there somewhere, crouching in the shadows... He's watching us with his fiery red eyes. Hide! It's me he wants. But he's not going to catch me. I'll escape again and start over somewhere new.","content.75.4523":"{[1*]?:}You must be nuts to want to attack the great Gobbalrog with a trumpet! Believe me, if you ever meet him, just run away as fast as you can, and above all avoid any bridges over large drops.","content.75.4524":"He's a terrible monster. \"You shall not pass!\" Falgand the Gray, that pretentious twit, thought he was being clever. Bam, into the abyss! That'll teach him. Baal and Kirikon ran away, but at least they're alive.","content.75.4525":"Great shovel, I should think so! The Strouds are the most influential (and richest) family in Windy Village!","content.75.4526":"You're probably talking about my nephew, young Ruel. He thought he could get rich by playing Gobbowl. Youthful folly... Miners and mercenaries, those are the ones who really honor the god Enutrof!","content.75.4528":"The downside is their tendency to try and get free by taking possession of their bearers. This cloak contains a major demon, Anathar. That's why the Justice League exists - to track down and capture all Shushus.","content.75.4529":"I am the Law, you got a problem with that?","content.75.4530":"Affirmative. There is, indeed, something very... special about it. It is, in fact, a Shushu, a demon locked inside an ordinary item, giving huge powers to its carrier. ","content.75.4531":"Indeed, pipsqueak, I often put the qualities of passing adventurers like you to the test with these environmental quests. They are community tests that allow me to reward winners and enforce the law.","content.75.4532":"Affirmative! He's the one who chooses and sets the environmental quests he wants to see in his territories. That makes elections and laws even more important. Got a problem with that?","content.75.4533":"Oh, a visitor! What can I do for you?","content.75.4534":"Oh, a visitor! What can I do for you?","content.75.4535":"It's stupid to use science to make things explode when we can use it to create the most exquisite meals ever. I'm Macrobio, executive chef of Amakna. I'm developing new revolutionary cooking methods! Are you interested in anything in particular?","content.75.4537":"{[1*]?:}Hey little one! Here, we arm everyone. No exceptions!","content.75.4539":"An ax ashore is an ax for war! Looking for an ax? Don't worry, it'll do!","content.75.4542":"Welcome to the fashion accessories bazaar! \\nWhat can I do-hoo for you-hoo?","content.75.4543":"Hi, shortstuff!{[1*]?:} Looking for a few tips on exploring the city?","content.75.4544":"Listen, I've already helped you a lot, and I'm taking a huge risk by smuggling all this wood. The authorities are going to get suspicious... I don't wanna end up in the slammer!","content.75.4545":"*A greedy glimmer illuminates Fertilizator's eyes for a brief moment before he pulls himself together*\\nNo, if I accept this money, you'll never leave me in peace! I've cooperated this far, but I'm not a pirate. I refuse to take any more risks for you.","content.75.4546":"*Fertilizator seems to realize the consequences of his decision* W-wait! It's okay, I'll do it. The wood will be delivered to the usual spot. But tell them that our arrangement can't last forever. Inspections are getting more and more strict.","content.75.4547":"So, Fertilizator's been whining like a baby? The authorities must be tightening the screws lately... Pfft! This latest delivery will be the last in any case. We're almost ready!","content.75.4548":"Ho ho ho, what lovely trees you have in these parts. I think I'll stick around for a while. Tell me, little one, were you good this year?{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}","content.75.4549":"Indeed. You are on my nice list. You deserve a good gift for being so respectful of others... Speaking of being nice... Could you do me a little favor? Do you want to make Father Kwismas happy? ","content.75.4550":"But... You're not on my nice list. Lying is very bad, you know! You were mean{[1*]?:} to the people of your nation, and I don't think you deserve a gift...","content.75.4551":"I really love the trees you've put everywhere. If you plant enough of them... say, 250, that's a good number... I'll make sure my gift gets to you wherever you are. That's the Kwismas magic!","content.75.4552":"Hmmmm... Do you have any Mentor tokens? If you bring me five, I'll put you back on my list. Helping others matters.","content.75.4553":"Ho ho ho, what a good kid you are! I really love the trees you've put everywhere. If you plant enough of them... say, 250, that's a good number... I'll make sure my gift gets to you wherever you are. That's the Kwismas magic!","content.75.4554":"But... Ho ho no, you're not on the nice list. You're on the very naughty list! No presents for the likes of you. Don't come back until you're a good, honest citizen of your nation! No excuses. I can't hear you. *Father Kwismas plugs his ears*","content.75.4559":"This is gastronomic heaven: the National Kitchens. Here, <b>bakers</b> and <b>chefs</b> work at their careers until they're stuffed. For the capital, and to sell their goods on the market. Adventurers all need a good meal before or after a difficult fight!","content.75.4560":"I can't leave without what I came for. My brother's counting on me to save him. You've earned the treasures, but I'm only asking for one: the Ecaflip spell book. You can keep the rest. They are of no interest to me... for now.","content.75.4561":"You want the treasures? Take them! But leave my men out of it. You don't understand the importance of our actions, in any case. The members of the Cartel aren't who you think.","content.75.4562":"We haven't always been pirates hunted by the nation. Back then, the Cartel didn't yet exist; they were just individualistic, wealthy merchants. When they started scheming, they needed henchmen to do their dirty work, and they took advantage of our situation. We were struggling to eat at the time, so we were forced to accept.","content.75.4563":"Just like Arachnees, they've spun their webs in the highest reaches of Sufokia to control all commercial flows and levy taxes that profit them. If someone didn't agree with them, they would send us to, um, convince them. Well, until the night of the Jolly Roger.","content.75.4564":"I don't let just anyone in...\\n\\nProve your worth by accomplishing your Resilience!","content.75.4567":"The citizens of Sufokia were losing trust in the Cartel more and more because they were starting to see what was happening. One night, they hoisted a Jolly Roger flag over our den and then set it on fire. They then spread their poisonous lies throughout the population, claiming we were responsible for all the recent bad deeds. They sacrificed us to masquerade as heroes... and we became what they wanted us to be by fleeing the city.","content.75.4569":"The Cartel doesn't deserve your trust. It's just a ragtag collection of Bworks, and the world would be better off without them! But... If we can't make them pay, at least let us build a new life for ourselves somewhere else. We won't make waves in Sufokia anymore, we promise!","content.75.4581":"*Remington seems to weigh the pros and cons for a few minutes, then he shrugs* A very powerful Ecaflip turned my brother into a Bow Meow. I've been trying to get him back to normal ever since. Believe me or not. But it's the truth.","content.75.4582":"*Remington squints under his mask when you mention Ush* ... Maybe. Would it change anything? Do you know him? Are you in cahoots with him?","content.75.4583":"I'll keep the details to myself; I've already said too much anyway. My brother and I were on a big job, but things went south on us, that's all. Are you going to give me the book or not?","content.75.4584":"The stone, the ring, and the spell book... Everything's here! Plus, you kept your word and told us Tibia-Thrasher and his men's exact position, getting rid of most of his men. To be honest, I didn't think you'd succeed, so perfect results such as these are truly impressive! The Cartel will be delighted.","content.75.4585":"The stone, the ring... Where is the Ecaflip spell book?! *The mercenary seems truly upset* I hope you didn't let them keep that treasure, did you?","content.75.4586":"*he stares at you for a few minutes before relenting* Well. I suppose it's not your fault. And you did give us Tibia-Thrasher and his men's position. The Cartel will have to be satisfied with that.","content.75.4587":"The stone, the ring, and the spell book... Everything's here!  The Cartel will be delighted to recover their treasures. However... *The mercenary seems to frown* You didn't provide any information on Tibia-Thrasher and his men. The request was clear on that point.","content.75.4588":"*He stares at you for a few minutes before speaking in a reassuring tone* So, the contract was for the treasures, and you fulfilled the terms. The Cartel should be satisfied. Mostly.","content.75.4589":"The stone, the ring... Where is the Ecaflip spell book?! *the mercenary seems truly upset* I hope you didn't let them keep that treasure, did you? Not to mention that you didn't turn over their leader.","content.75.4590":"I'd be lying if I said it would be easy to get the Cartel to accept that... I must have underestimated you after all.{[1*]?:} Well, you did bring back two treasures... You'll get your reward.","content.75.4591":"Let's hope that the Rogue pirate problem won't rear its ugly head again. Here's your reward.","content.75.4592":"You're in the National Forges, where <b>weapons masters</b> and <b>armorers</b> put all their know-how into designing equipment and pieces of metalwork. So, obviously, between this heat and those muscles, it doesn't smell like flowers in here! Whatever you're looking for, be it a few new strings for your bow or a smashing sledgehammer, you'll find everything an adventurer needs here!","content.75.4593":"We're at the National Workshops. Here, our crafters are the most ingenious at designing new equipment that is equally effective and elegant. Basically, this is the perfect place to dress with style. Our <b>jewelers,</b> <b>tailors,</b> and <b>leather dealers,</b> all fall over one another to offer you the best prices on the market.","content.75.4594":"This is the National Sawmill. We handle an astronomical number of orders now that reconstruction is in full swing! In addition to delivering the planks needed for all buildings, our <b>handymen</b> work night and day to turn out small storage containers for adventurers and other items that make their lives easier. They also build furniture for the most homey homebodies among us.","content.75.4595":"The contract is an order from Nina Richa. She had ordered wood from three lumberjack brothers. The brothers never returned from their excursion into the Thicket of Yurbut. It's clearly because of the Dark Treechnids in that area. These dangerous creatures would be better off exterminated, and fast!","content.75.4596":"Oh, yes! Ron Bush, Tiv Bush and Ido Bush, the three lumberjack brothers went to cut me some Sylvan Pine in the Thicket of Yurbut. They haven't returned... I had to post a contract at the Mercenary Post. I imagine you've come{[1*]?:}on their behalf?","content.75.4597":"They were in a lumberjack village at the eastern tip of Bonta. But you should go investigate right there... ","content.75.4598":"Ah! Thanks a lot! With all this wood, I'll be able to sharpen my Ecaflip Claws correctly! They get worn out quickly cutting all this yarn and fabric, you know...","content.75.4599":"Good evening and welcome to my humble abode. Root I am, the spirit of the Thicket I incarnate.","content.75.4600":"The force I used to you here bring. I've been watching you for many hours, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Without understanding them, you the Dark Treechnids fight.","content.75.4601":"Well, okay. I'll try to be quick. You noticed there had been a lot of Dark Treechnids in the Thicket of Yurbut for a while now, didn't you?","content.75.4602":"Surely, you must be speaking of Ron Bush, Tiv Bush and Ido Bush. In fact, I need to fully explain to you what Treechnids are, but first of all let me explain what's going on. You've already found the lumberjacks you were looking for. Those were Treechnids you fought.","content.75.4603":"Humans, yes... Who were transformed by the lumberjacks' curse. Most lumberjacks are aware of this phenomenon, but that doesn't stop merchants from demanding more and more wood in exchange for kamas. The Treechnid transformation occurs when the forest's balance is threatened, but that's not all.","content.75.4604":"Ever since the massive deforestation of Bonta's neighboring forest, more misfortune has befallen us. In fact, if that weren't bad enough, some Polters arrived.\\nSurely you know the Treechnids of Astrub. Dark Treechnids are the product of crossing a Treechnid with a Polter. They are more aggressive and bitterly defend their territory.","content.75.4605":"The trouble with the Polters is that they're virtually ethereal. They cling to a life, a small piece of inanimate wood sometimes, and then they take possession. The real long-term solution would be to take control with the help of a powerful spirit...","content.75.4606":"I'm far from being strong enough to put all the Polters under my care. On the other hand, I know an entity that has the power to put them under its command: the Soft Oak.","content.75.4607":"He's already there. I called him to come help rescue the endangered forest by explaining the situation telepathically. Unfortunately, he fell into the trap and under the Polters' curse... His spirit is fighting for survival, but the venerable Soft Oak is old and tired. His body is no longer strong enough to survive the waves of Polters wanting to take possession of him. If they succeed, it'll probably be the end of the world!","content.75.4608":"Wait! Whatever you do, don't hurt the Soft Oak. It's our ally. Just break the curse and prevent the Polters from reaching it. Otherwise, it'll be the end of Bonta, the Sadida Kingdom and, perhaps, the World of Twelve.","content.75.4609":"Well done, comrade. You've won some heroic battles. Yet, the three lumberjack brothers are nowhere to be found... That's annoying, very annoying. Technically, you didn't fulfill you contract by finding these brothers. Thus, there is no reward for you. Unless...","content.75.4610":"Unless you go honor the lumberjacks' order with Nina Richa. Do it and I'll consider the contract fulfilled.","content.75.4611":"Nice! The Soft Oak has gone back inside its abode, taking the Polters with it. Order has been re-established in the Thicket of Yurbut, and the Soft Oak can now continue watching over the forests of the World of Twelve... ","content.75.4612":"Yes, it's true that I retransformed myself. After our heroes' fights against Ogrest, an earthquake opened a crack in the ground where my flock was. My poor animals didn't survive the fall, and a shepherd without a flock has no purpose in life. Thus, I changed professions, and it's all for the better! ","content.75.4613":"Twhat twoo want?","content.75.4614":"The castle? Why, it belongs to the Governor of Amakna, of course! He's elected by the citizens every two weeks. They vote by going to see their nation's Clan Member.","content.75.4615":"A Governor must serve the Nation. That's why only people with the rank of Involved Citizen can run for office. We can't let just anyone come into power, you know! Hoo!","content.75.4616":"The governor lays down the laws that are enforced throughout the nation. He's also the one who sets the taxes at the markets and can ask clan members to do certain things. Lastly, he is in charge of international relations.","content.75.4617":"If you want to vote, you'll have to prove your dedication to your nation by achieving the rank of Simple Citizen at least. Don't forget to take your passport with you when you go to the Clan Member to cast your vote!","content.75.4618":"Of course there are laws. If you don't follow them, you will become an Outlaw. Outlaws can be attacked by anyone and will be arrested if they lose.","content.75.4619":"If you are arrested as an Outlaw, you will go to jail and the length of the sentence you serve will depend on what crimes you have committed. You can do community service to cut time off your sentence. Hoo.","content.75.4620":"What do you-hoo want?","content.75.4621":"The castle? Why, it belongs to the Governor of Bonta, of course! He's elected by the citizens every two weeks. He's elected by the citizens every two weeks. They vote by going to see their nation's Clan Member.","content.75.4622":"Twhat twoo want?","content.75.4623":"The castle? {[1*]?:}Why, it belongs to the Governor of Brakmar, of course! He's elected by the citizens every two weeks. They vote by going to see their nation's Clan Member.","content.75.4624":"Twhat twoo want?","content.75.4625":"The castle? Why, it belongs to the Governor of Sufokia, of course! He's elected by the citizens every two weeks. They vote by going to see their nation's Clan Member.","content.75.4626":"Hmmmm... I think Old Joe has had a spot of trouble lately. You should probably go to his place and see what you can do to help him and his Moogrrs. He lives southeast of the city in an isolated house. You can't miss him. On the other hand, he's a pretty grumpy guy, and he's too proud to ask you to help him with his Moogrrs, even though he'd be overwhelmed. Still, try to see what you can do once you get there.","content.75.4627":"Mercenary, you punished our enemy soundly, and for that I thank you. Alas! The world is still full of danger. This was just the beginning. It's unfortunate, but I think that our role should be to prevent threats rather than crush them...","content.75.4628":"Do you enjoy coming here and taunting me while I'm rotting in prison?","content.75.4629":"*Tibia-Thrasher turns around and sits up in the back of his cell* Well, you should've thought about that before getting me and my men thrown in the slammer. It's too late for good intentions.","content.75.4630":"Go ahead; I'll cover your back. None of those pirates will be able to get to you, or my name isn't Remington Smisse!","content.75.4631":"Oh, yes, ever since he heard of your exploits, Dot's been betting to let him go with you. Ever since he met you, all he talks about is adventure, and I'm getting too old to take care of him... Would you take him with you?","content.75.4632":"Wait. Before you go, I need to explain a few things about Gemlins. They are creatures that can evolve if they eat very special stones. They say that fragments can be found in very special chests in the various nations and in dungeons. There's a machine called the Gemlevolver in the basement of the Astrub Inn. You should check it out so you know what you need. Gemlins aren't very powerful pets, but they're perfect when you're just starting out. ","content.75.4633":"You might also stumble across items that can change the appearance of Gemlins. We call those items \"gemligems\". They have almost all disappeared, but you could still find a few. Here, I'll give you the only one I have. I like Dot the way he is, so I never used it. But he's your pet now. Take care of him and good luck on your adventures! ","content.75.4634":"An Amakna nation petsmount harness? Hoo-hoo, it's possible, but we don't give them out to just anyone. You have to earn it and be a good patriot (over 10,000 CP). And it costs 2,000 kamas, which will go into the nation's treasury to help it develop. If you meet these conditions, I will give you a Patriotic Petsmount Token so you can choose the harness you want.","content.75.4635":"A Bonta nation Petsmount harness? Hoo-hoo, it's possible, but we don't give them out to just anyone. You have to earn it and be a good patriot (over 10,000 CP). And it costs 2,000 kamas, which will go into the nation's treasury to help it develop. If you meet these conditions, I will give you a Patriotic Petsmount Token so you can choose the harness you want.","content.75.4636":"A Brakmar nation petsmount harness? Hoo-hoo, it's possible, but we don't give them out to just anyone. You have to earn it and be a good patriot (over 10,000 CP). And it costs 2,000 kamas, which will go into the nation's treasury to help it develop. If you meet these conditions, I will give you a patriotic petsmount token so you can choose the harness you want.","content.75.4637":"A Sufokia nation petsmount harness? Hoo-hoo, it's possible, but we don't give them out to just anyone. You have to earn it and be a good patriot (over 10,000 CP). And it costs 2,000 kamas, which will go into the nation's treasury to help it develop. If you meet these conditions, I will give you a Patriotic Petsmount token so you can choose the harness you want.","content.75.4638":"Ah, I see you've been to Pandalucia. Hmmm... What you're describing is very odd... It's been years since I've been to that valley. I wonder what's been happening there lately. From what you're saying, it hasn't all been good.","content.75.4639":"Alas, I'm not a specialist in that department. I've read books on the subject, but that was a long time ago and my memory's a bit spotty. Normally, you need two main ingredients to purify the ground and remove Plantala curses.","content.75.4640":"Unfortunately, the book was banned from normal libraries. But I do know someone who has forbidden books in is personal library. Count Harebourg. Head to his tower. I'm sure he's kept a copy.","content.75.4641":"Let's see what you've brought... Black Zordfish slobber and Tsu Tsu Tsar blood! Of course. I'll make the Plantalacide. It's going to take a while. Tell me about your adventures while I work. How is life as an adventurer{[1*]?:} treating you?","content.75.4642":"Fascinating! But many challenges are still before you. You must not stop until you've prevented the coming disasters.","content.75.4643":"I understand your feeling of solitude. People are hard to convince in the World of Twelve. I've done extensive research on living creatures. Some are very complex, but none even come close to us Twelvians. ","content.75.4644":"For example, we know the concepts of justice and injustice. And that's enough to make many things complicated.","content.75.4645":"That's true. We create the world we know using our sense and our brains. Ultimately, the world exists only because there are creatures who can feel it and recognize it. It's an extremely fragile balance, of course. After all, what can we believe in if we interpret everything?","content.75.4647":"*The old Pandawa standing in front of you seems unflappably calm. He is as still and pale as any of the many ghosts in the area*\\nGreetings.","content.75.4648":"Welcome to the Cemetery in... Pandala. Many errant creatures joined us here after Ogrest's Chaos. Our ancestors sealed the bridge at the entrance to the zone with the help of powerful magic, thus condemning these creatures to wander for all eternity. I'm Lab Elfive, their guardian.","content.75.4649":"Hmm, if it's that important to you... My bones are too old now for me to verify the state of the protection measures on the various ways in and out of the cemetery. If even one Pandala soul managed to leave, the consequences could be terrible for the World of Twelve!\\n\\nI'd be very grateful if you could handle it.","content.75.4650":"Hey there, little sprig! What brings you to these parts? Be careful where you put your feet. One misstep and you'll fall into the brown bog! And we're not going to fish you out, no way!","content.75.4651":"You should have seen it a few decades ago. The bamboo didn't look the same, oh no. The rising waters brought salt into the area, and plants have a hard time growing. Back then, lots of us grew bamboo. We had so much fun back then... Now, on top of it all, there's all these Plantalas everywhere.","content.75.4652":"You look like you're ready to do some cleaning{[1*]?:}... Very well. And it's true they've been causing a lot of upset in the area lately. It'd be nice if you could set a few traps to keep them away from the roads.\\n\\nI'll leave it in your hands, little sprig. While you're at it, I'm... I'm going to be very busy... You know that... supervising... is a huge job!","content.75.4653":"*Ray Dlabel works with a skill and speed that no one would have guessed possible. A few minutes later the traps are ready*\\n\\nThere you go, little sprig! Off with you now. And be careful, we're going up against a really strong family.","content.75.4654":"Well done, little sprig! With all the traps we set, they're caught like Rattlers! Now's the perfect time to find out their strengths and weaknesses... A good Pandawa is a Pandawa who thinks forty... no, two... no, forty-two... steps ahead, at least.","content.75.4655":"Well, well, little sprig, bravo! I never doubted you. I knew that we were going to win! There's no doubt about it. You've improved the condition of the swamp.\\n\\nLet's celebrate with a stiff drink! Bamboo milk?\\n(Ray Dlabel offers you a bottle full of a dark and lumpy liquid! The mouth of the bottle is covered in spit...)","content.75.4656":"They've always been here. They were here before us even! They were peaceful, and lived in our bamboo forests. They got aggressive over time... Little by little, they even started attacking us! Who knows what they're capable of?","content.75.4658":"Halt! To what do I owe the displeasure of seeing a {[1*]?Jane:John} Doe of your ilk among my belligerents? Get lost, vermin, before I cut off your head!","content.75.4659":"This town belongs to the Pandissidents. Our congregation took control of the place, and we enforce our laws as we please. We don't give a fig about our insipid detractors. The Pandawas who used to live here were flattened by our military prowess. We're enjoying the fruits of our victory and their cellars full of bamboo milk. I won't say it again: Get out or I'll punish you!","content.75.4660":"Hey there, little {[1*]?girl:man}. Isn't Pandalucia beautiful?","content.75.4661":"Well now, why are you interested in Pandissidents anyway? They were just bandits before. We lived peacefully in the village, but we often heard *burp* stories...\\n\\nTheir numbers grew over time and they started attacking us. Not a big deal for me. I've always lived in these swamps! Too smelly to live in a city, they said. If you want to know more... Ask someone who used to live in the village. Pandiego, for example.","content.75.4662":"I've got quite a story to tell you! At first, the leader of the Pandissidents was called Pandora. He was a bandit, and much more of a radical than Chiv Asregal today. He massacred adventurers who came through here, and was planning on raising an army of Thirsters to conquer the World of Twelve. Luckily, Chiv Asregal defeated him. He makes for a much more moderate leader. He wants to start trading bamboo milk internationally, but it's just a matter of time before their group splits off. There are too many dissidents among the Pandissidents.","content.75.4663":"Hmph! I already know that, riffraff. Obviously, I can't ignore the perfidious acts of that rascal, Pandora. That cad will get what he deserves. I'll kill him with my own hands.","content.75.4664":"... That's true. The antagonism between us could endanger our respective missions.","content.75.4665":"Very well, you wretch, your arguments have convinced me. Stop pleading and get to work. You have my word. The unity and well-being of my followers is worth more to me than this pile of planks.","content.75.4666":"Welcome to the forest.\\n\\nThe charred forest.","content.75.4667":"Yes.","content.75.4668":"About what?","content.75.4669":"The forest burned.","content.75.4670":"That's why it's called the...\\n\\n\"Charred Forest\".","content.75.4671":"... You don't know anything. The fire went everywhere. Burned everything. Consumed everything. Blightopards and even Pandawas screamed in agony, trapped.\\n\\nI knew then that we had angered the Great Spirit.","content.75.4672":"The Great Spirit will never forgive us. Neither will the Blightopards.\\n\\nWe'll be trapped in the flames forever. Not even the rain or the ocean waves could extinguish the fire.\\n\\nAs many charred bodies on arid dirt.\\n\\nAll hope is gone.","content.75.4673":"Well, your tale is quite something! Luckily for you, I've got something that'll work. The Pandawas went about it all backwards. If there's one thing felines hate, it's water. Flood their lair and they'll learn their lesson. I'll make you a few bombs. You'll have to set them so they can't get in or out without getting their fur wet.","content.75.4674":"*Synosore turns around for a minute to make the bombs, and then hands them to you*\\nHere you go, kid{[1*]?:}. This time, they're on the house!","content.75.4675":"It seems like you're saying the balance in the area is off somehow... The consequences would be terrible if the barriers gave way.\\nThat's a terrifying prospect, but you seem to have found an unexpected ally.\\n\\nVery well. I'll perform the ghostly energy possession ritual. I'll need you to bring me certain materials, but once the ritual's done, you'll be able to fight the Pandala ghosts on equal footing.","content.75.4676":"Hmmm? You... can see me?","content.75.4677":"Maybe you can help me. I'm searching for a way to leave this land and be reincarnated. I've been searching for a very long time. But for some unknown reason, I can't get any rest.","content.75.4678":"*the ghost gulps*\\nI wish it were that simple. I think the souls are trapped here because of a single ghost's rage. An invisible threat lies over this cemetery, and Lab Elfive isn't strong enough to eradicate it.\\n\\nDid you come to investigate the state of the doors separating the real world from the cemetery? Unfortunately, they've never been weak.","content.75.4679":"Well, I... I know it's not really your problem. But if nothing's done about it, we're going to have a serious issue.\\n\\nIn fact, it's an \"I scratch your back, you scratch mine\" kind of situation. I help you rid the cemetery of the threat to stop an army of the dead from reaching the World of Twelve. And in return, you help me get to Incarnam.","content.75.4680":"Go back to Lab Elfive and ask him to prepare a ghostly energy possession ritual for you. You can't defend yourself against the ghosts in this cemetery if you're not on the same physical plane as them.","content.75.4681":"Let's just say... I lived a full life before coming to Pandalucia. My tomb is in this cemetery - maybe you could visit it and pay your respects when you have the chance.","content.75.4682":"How's it going?","content.75.4683":"I knew you were a remarkable adventurer{[1*]?:}. To perform the ritual, all that's left to do is capture a Pandala ghost... Lay the bamboo out in a cross and draw the monster to the middle, then throw the capture stone. I'll mark down an auspicious spot for the ritual on your map.","content.75.4684":"*a flash of light appears in the Pandawa sage's eyes*\\nI was right about you.","content.75.4685":"Yes, interesting... Just a minute.\\n\\n*Lab Elfive gets to work drawing mysterious runes on the ground; he throws the capture stone in the middle of them, and a bright light pervades you; when you open your eyes, the stone is gone*\\n\\nThere, your body is ready to confront the Pandala ghosts. Be careful, though - you can only reach their spectral plane a certain number of times. In other words, after a ghost takes several hits, it will become more intangible and resistant to attack.","content.75.4686":"Perfect, then you'll be able to battle the ghosts. However, I'm afraid your skills will be put to the test sooner than expected. We're surrounded by ghosts.","content.75.4687":"*the Unknown Ghost looks at you, taken aback*\\n\\nI wasn't aware you were so powerful{[1*]?:}. I think you're quite capable of saving me.","content.75.4688":"So... The problem is Ghost Tanukouï San. He's the one keeping the area the way it is. He's feeding the conflicts and regrets of the spirits in the cemetery, preventing them from resting in peace.\\n\\nHe was our leader once... When Pandala fell during Ogrest's Chaos, his hatred endured and he used a powerful magic to make the ghosts slaves to his will.","content.75.4689":"Many of the ghosts somehow managed to leave the cemetery. Legendary warriors worth several adventurers{[1*]?:} like you, ordinary people... Over time, they were able to break free.\\n\\nYou should be able to recover traces of their existence in the tomb where Ghost Tanukouï San resides. If you manage to acquire their residual desires and regrets, you can disperse the ghosts.","content.75.4690":"*the Unknown Ghost tries to be reassuring*\\n\\nI know that. I understand, but it's the only solution now. I'm sure it will work.","content.75.4691":"*the Unknown Ghost looks at you with a friendly smile, seeming satisfied*\\n\\nWell done.","content.75.4692":"*a shadow falls over the ghost's face*\\n\\nI... I still have things to do, battles to fight.","content.75.4693":"But the people need me here. I can't leave - I have to help the last of the ghosts.","content.75.4694":"... You're right... I need to let go. Goodbye. I'm glad I met you.","content.75.4695":"At any rate, good job stealing the bamboo milk out from under those Pandissidents' beards. I'm impressed, kid{[1*]?:}! Sadly, we've already sold everything you brought two days ago.","content.75.4696":"I don't know. You disappeared all of a sudden, shortly after Otomai arrived. Maybe you were battling a fierce Pandawa{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4697":"I'm afraid not... Hey, speaking of Otomai, maybe he knows a solution.\\n\\nThe trouble is really that damn marsh. We thought we had a long-term solution with the saltwater-resistant bamboo plants! But it's been one disaster after another for quite a while now. It's almost like the Great Spirit is really angry...","content.75.4698":"Wow, kid{[1*]?:}, you downed all those pints of bamboo milk without even knowing that?\\n\\nIt's an old Pandawa legend, the founding myth of Pandalucia. We believe he's protected the valley since the dawn of time. But like I told you, it's been hard times lately.","content.75.4699":"Are you sure{[1*]?:} you saw him? I'm not doubting your visual acuity, but...\\n\\nLet me put it another way: Can we be sure he's behind all this?","content.75.4700":"This is a tough situation, kid{[1*]?:}... Thanks to you, we were able to get far in our trials. But it seems like it'll be hard to find a way to grow healthy bamboo. We may never be able to replant the valley.","content.75.4701":"Very well, I don't see any other options either. We should head to the statue. I'll go with, and perhaps we'll spot a clue that shows us the what to do.\\n\\nI recommend going at night if we want to stay safe.","content.75.4702":"Panda-what? I've never heard of the place! You must be mistaken - I've never left the Sadida Kingdom.","content.75.4703":"Bring me 2 Royal Wool, 2 Royal Tofu Feathers, and 2 Shin Larva Legs.","content.75.4704":"Bring me 2 Royal Feathers, 2 Morfor Horns, and 2 Treechnell Legs.","content.75.4705":"Bring me 20 Black Enewgies, 20 Luxulious Fuls, and 20 Royal Myceliums.","content.75.4706":"Have you ever heard of the Bonta Gobbowl Bowl? The finals are in just a few days, and we've lost our special Blibliball! It's made out of Royal Blibli leather, which is very rare... The government therefore gave us this contract. It's vitally urgent. Since you've taken the contract, head to the Cania Plains. The Justice Knight can fill you in better than I can.","content.75.4707":"So you're the runt that Bo R. Throom has sent to hunt the Royal Blibli? You seem a bit puny{[1*]?:} for the job. Go take care of something else and let the grown-ups handle this.","content.75.4708":"You'd go against my law? Listen, germ, I'll give you a chance to make up for your mistakes. Before, the ecosystem was split between the Prespics and Bliblis. But they've forged a very surprising alliance... Investigate their alliance and I might tell you where to find the Royal Blibli. Start by fighting a small group to show me you know what you're doing.","content.75.4709":"Affirmative. Well, almost. Hunting Bliblis and Prespics is against the law, except when an exceptional government contract is in place. It's an emergency measure taken when the Blibli population becomes a threat to the city of Bonta.","content.75.4710":"Honestly, the \"exceptional\" contract is almost always open. As a result the Cania creatures have been almost entirely eradicated from the surface of the World of Twelve for their skins and fur.","content.75.4711":"Do you dare challenge the Laws of Bonta in my presence? Choose your words carefully when you address me, you miserable creature!","content.75.4712":"I guess you've proven your value, runt. The Royal Blibli is really in the Boarthroom Estate. Bo R. Throom is a Bontarian noble who got enormously rich by selling Blibli leather.\\n\\nHis estate is on the outskirts of Cania. You can get there by taking the bridge I'll note down on your map. Many Bliblis have been captured and kept there in captivity.\\n\\nIt seems the creatures turned out to be too difficult to keep locked up and they eventually took control of the place. I assume the hidden goal of the contract is to free the Boarthroom estate of Bliblis so that Bo R. Throom can go back to the estate.","content.75.4713":"Halt! The bridge was destroyed by Ogrest's chaos. You can't get to the Boarthroom Estate by land anymore. Go back.","content.75.4714":"You should have told me you were with the Mercenaries right away! Borrow my rowboat over there. You can get to the Estate by following the ruins in the sea.","content.75.4715":"It seems I've underestimated you{[1*]?:}. You are a true{[1*]?:} ally{[1*]?:} of Justice! Keep fighting like that and Bonta will cover you with glory and rewards. Hurry and report to the Mercenaries, and may the law be with you.","content.75.4716":"Wonderful! We're going to be able to make a Blibliball and the Gobbowl Bowl can be held without a hitch. We're deeply indebted to you!\\n\\nSo, who are you rooting for? Wessi or Lonardo? In any case, it's going to be a fantastic game... The Guild of Mercenaries will all be watching from the stands.","content.75.4717":"Chafers have made a massive come back in the Sidimote Moors. They are living-dead skeletons that attack all living beings that come through here without distinction. It is our job to protect the population. Be careful. They can come back to life if their bones are not entirely disembodied... Grind them into dust, if you must!","content.75.4718":"Hmmm... I wonder if you're ready{[1*]?:} to hear the whole truth about the Chafers. Look at them... Aren't they peaceful and calm? They've attained true serenity, don't you think?","content.75.4719":"They only want to go back to their immortal peaceful sleep, you know. What is life if not a succession of dramas and fatalities? It's much simpler to just let go...\\n\\nBut I digress...","content.75.4720":"Powerful magic is at work in the Morbax Neplopolis. I used to guard those souls, before... But I was chased out of the Neplopolis by a Chafer named Chaferfu who is more powerful than the others. He seems to be behind the reanimation of the Chafers. Be careful if you cross his path; I couldn't do anything to stop him.","content.75.4721":"The ch-cha... Chafers? Never heard of them.","content.75.4722":"I know nothing! I see nothing! I did not even get up this morning...\\n\\n*Moe looks frightened and doesn't seem to be able to tell you any more, but you get the feeling that the mine is full of secrets*","content.75.4723":"*Moe's face changes as you read the miner's journal to him*\\n\\nI... Okay. I'll tell you everything. I was under a lot of pressure, you know. The Stroud family disowned me, and I had to change my name and earn my way... Make a living. I worked hard, too. Even though I wasn't a miner for long and quickly became section leader, I had a lot of responsibilities. It's a lot of pressure, you know. I tried to defend the miners' interests.","content.75.4724":"And what more would you have had me do? Before, I was in Bonta living a life of luxury. But here? There's nothing here! No jobs, no guards, criminals everywhere... How do you expect me to adapt to an environment like that? Charles-Henri might be unfair and cruel, but he's the only one offering an alternative. At least he changed things.","content.75.4725":"But whatever happens, you must promise you won't repeat any of this to Charles-Henri. If he finds out I talked...\\n\\n*Moe shudders*","content.75.4726":"The miners lived in a small company town in Sidimote, outside the city, away from the slums alongside the factory. It was far from Gnashville too. Extremely isolated. One day, the dark carbon ran out. To stop paying the miners at a loss, Charles-Henri decided to make them all disappear. Most of them were former criminals trying to make amends, or people too stupid to understand what was happening to them. Some couldn't even read or write...\\n\\nSidimotes & Co.'s special guard burned down the village, killed all the survivors, and dumped all the bodies in the Morbax Neplopolis. But what the guards didn't know is that Charles-Henri is an Ouginak with a nose for detail.","content.75.4727":"Yes, the army massacred the miners. Once they all went inside the Neplopolis to bury the miners, Charles-Henri had them locked in from the outside. All proof had to be eliminated. No tongues could wag. He saved their wages, and hired Bworks and machines to be his new security detail.","content.75.4728":"Don't tell anyone, please! You might be able to give these Chafers eternal rest, but I've got a position to maintain here. I don't want to lose everything like I did when the Stroud family disowned me. Please!","content.75.4729":"Congratulations, mercenary. You've eliminated Chaferfu and brought peace back to Sidimote! I knew I could trust you. You deserve a good, long rest... Well, not too long all the same. I wouldn't want you to become yet another Chafer.\\n\\n*the mercenary bursts out laughing*","content.75.4730":"Good grief, kid{[1*]?:}, you've been hitting the bamboo milk too hard. I know you're quite the{[1*]?:} party{[1*]?:} animal{[1*]?:} and all that, but I still can't figure out where you come up with these kinds of stories...","content.75.4731":"Sure. Lay back, tell me your name, and what year it is.","content.75.4732":"... Hmm. I find your story rather hard to believe... But you've done Pandalucia a great service by bringing back bamboo milk for its inhabitants, and I'll do whatever I can to help you. If you want to prove that the world outside of this Valley is in some other age, then I'm willing to go with you back to where you came from. Do you know Ruel Stroud? That old miser will recognize me for sure! And he'll confirm that this is the year 982.","content.75.4733":"What? Pandalucia? Well, yes, I've been there before... Why do you ask?","content.75.4734":"All right, kid{[1*]?:}, I might have a few names for you. But you know, times are tough in Amakna right now. Would you consider doing a little job for me, like maybe a mercenary contract? I'm not normally such a hard nut to crack, but...","content.75.4735":"Ah, so you've been able to see for yourself how restless the Amaknian lands have become. These are truly challenging times, my friend{[1*]?:}. It's getting harder and harder to cultivate our wheat and raise our livestock. Oh well, I don't suppose you've got a miracle fix for Ogrest's Chaos, in any case!\\n\\nThe fact is, I've heard that Count Harebourg already came through here a while back. He talked to a few different people and suggested some dodgy arrangements. I don't know the details, but the mayor of Emelka surely knows more about it. You should ask Alibert about whatever you need to know. If you don't know him, tell him I sent you.","content.75.4736":"I figured that people would start asking questions sooner or later... Yes, a Xelor from Frigost did come to speak with me. A strange fellow. He seemed interested in Yugo. Insisted on talking to him for a minute. I didn't really understand what he was talking about... \"elite ropes\", or something? Anyway, he was a bit of an oddball. Hard to believe he could really be the guy in charge of Frigost.","content.75.4737":"Hmmm... If I remember correctly, he suggested bringing the entire Amaknian people to his home in Frigost, and he told us something like... our nation was doomed. We refused, of course. The soil has become harder and harder to cultivate because of Ogrest's Chaos, but that's no reason to abandon our land, our roots... As for me, I've found a new life here.\\nHe seemed to really care about our people, but he got very upset when we refused... He let out this sinister laugh and teleported away. That sent a shiver down our spines... me and the leaders of all the other nations. But I expect we'll all be laughing about it in a few weeks.","content.75.4738":"Yes, as a matter of fact. I think he was headed for Bonta. I get all kinds of travelers at my inn, so I end up hearing plenty. A couple of shady older fellows told me they'd seen a Xelor traveling with a Bontarian minister named Lugiani. Go see my old friend Jonk. He's the commander of the Bontarian army, maybe he can give you the information you're looking for.","content.75.4739":"Well now, little one{[1*]?:}... I'm very sorry, but I'm not really the person you should be talking to about that. Diplomatic confidentiality and all that... I don't know any more than that.","content.75.4740":"Well, that's precisely the problem. I was head of the army, but not any more. I've served here for several centuries, I've had an illustrious career and built up a titanic body of knowledge, but in the end, I guess I was taking up too much space... Overshadowing the wrong people, I suppose.","content.75.4741":"Listen, little one{[1*]?:}... That's life. You need to choose your battles, and I've learned that the hard way. I assumed that after all my many victories on the battlefields, my opinion would count for something in the Bontarian government. But I was wrong! It's all a bit beyond me now.","content.75.4742":"*Jonk Lees glares at you. His grumpy but good-natured attitude disappears, leaving nothing but cold fury in his eyes*\\n\\nI'll be perfectly honest with you. You're asking me to go and talk to a bunch of rotten politicians. You know what the real evil eating away at Bonta is? Those people spend their days tearing down everything I've fought for centuries to build... They rewrite history to make everyone think I'm some kind of rebel! I want you to be perfectly clear{[1*]?:} about who's really the law around here. The governor and his little clique are puppets. Replaceable. They come and go, vote in a few nice little plans. But there are certain ministers who are somehow always there. You know what? Go take a mercenary contract and you'll see how rotten things are in Bonta.","content.75.4743":"Hmm, you really put your heart into your work. To be honest, I'm so upset by the whole situation that I've completely given up. But seeing a little dwarf{[1*]?:} like you running around looking for answers does lift my spirits just a bit. All right, I'll set up a meeting for you with Lugiani. He's not the nicest guy in Bonta, but at least he'll be willing to give you the information you're looking for, in exchange for a little bri... well, you know. Let's just say you'll need to \"fill his cup with the good stuff\" if you want to get anywhere! If you still want to meet with him... You know what to do.","content.75.4744":"Maybe, maybe not...\\n\\nYou know what they say... My mother told me never to talk to strangers! But then again, my mom didn't really set a good example as far as that goes. A good woman... They don't make 'em like that any more. She insisted on staying in Brakmar. The land of her parents before her, and the land of my children after me, she used to say. A hell of a fighter. She even managed to put in a few years in the mine before it killed her. Ha! What was I saying, again? I forget...","content.75.4745":"Hahaha... You know how things work around here. Work is life. People who try to live an honest life just get exploited by those big bosses.\\n\\n*Viscus suddenly sounds very tired, as though he were bearing the weight of the world on his shoulders*\\n\\nAnd everyone puts the blame on us, the \"criminals\". Brakmar, city of crime. Brakmar, den of evildoers. Brakmar, organized chaos. Yep, everyone's supposed to work themselves sick for Charles-Henri... Hey, speaking of which, it's got to be him you're looking for. If anyone's seen Count Harebourg, it's him, the real undisputed leader of this nation. Heh heh, don't thank me, my little kidney. It's never easy to deal with those people. So whatever you do, don't take care of yourself!","content.75.4746":"Hmm... Indeed. I assume our last encounter left you with some unpleasant memories.","content.75.4747":"Well? I don't believe we have an appointment. Get out of here this instant or I'll have you chased out.","content.75.4748":"*Charles-Henri seems to think for a moment. He's mentally weighing what he has to gain and lose*\\n\\nVery well. I'll tell you everything. Now, you may see me as a ruthless businessman, as a hard-edged boss who's only interested in profit. But that's not the whole truth.\\n\\nMost people want me to put myself in their place... But who rebuilt the city? Who paid to build and rebuild all those different neighborhoods? Who provided honest work for hundreds... no, thousands of Brakmarians? If all of those people had been as successful as I have been, would they have done the same? Without me, Brakmar would be a place for farmers and uncivilized criminals.\\n\\nEvery kama I earn is for Brakmar. And you can't deny it!","content.75.4749":"Indeed I shall.\\n\\nI think it's fair to say that, in a manner of speaking, I'm the great craftsman behind the reconstruction of Brakmar. I'm the face of the nation. So Count Harebourg came to see me just a few days ago. He wanted to buy resources from me and exchange technologies. He's a bit mad, I suppose, but he's a brilliant inventor and engineer. He was very interested in my mechanikal creations.\\n\\nYou're already familiar with my \"haggling\" skills... I pretended to accept, but I still tried to rip him off. An old Brakmarian habit.","content.75.4750":"Not at all! Haha, everyone really made fun of him.","content.75.4751":"Let's move quickly here. I know there are important issues at stake, but Miranda only left for half a day, and I need to be back at Kelba when she returns.","content.75.4752":"So, adventurer{[1*]?:}...? There's no shame in asking for help from a goddess like me. Looks like the dynamic duo is back in business! Do take good care of my Ocarina, won't you?","content.75.4753":"Pshh pshhh psh! pshhhh pshh psh... psh psh.","content.75.4754":"Honestly, did you see how those Brakmarian soldiers were glaring at me? They think I'm another monster. If I leave here without you, they're sure to mistake me for an enemy.","content.75.4755":"I don't like coming to this kind of place one bit. The nations aren't really right for us. Our clan prefers freedom and wide-open spaces. Our instincts tell us to stay away from city life.","content.75.4756":"Remember, we have no intention of dying before defeating Ogrest.","content.75.4757":"Hmm, so we've gone from saving Astrub from a rat invasion... to saving Brakmar from a Mecha invasion. It'll take more than that to throw me off my game! At least the weapons here are pretty nice. Obviously, Brakmarian weapons aren't a bunch of junk like in Astrub.","content.75.4758":"Do you think they make any good wines in Brakmar?","content.75.4759":"Come now, stop looking at me like that. Haven't I already explained that Brakmar's interests are the same as mine? Even today, I deploy the Guard that I pay and equip all by myself to defend the nation.\\n\\n*Charles-Henri chuckles*\\n\\nEveryone who lives here owes me their sincere thanks. I hope they'll buy even more of my products to express their gratitude...","content.75.4760":"All right, then! I still owe you one, you pulled me out of the dark rooms and managed to defeat Shreddie. We're pals now. So obviously I'll be with you for every battle!","content.75.4761":"Oh, I'm sorry! Old habits can be tougher than a Crackler to break... We came with a few soldiers who are waiting outside, actually. It wasn't easy to put together a volunteer troop in only an hour, but we've still got some skilled blades in our group. Besides, most of the soldiers are indebted to you. You saved our entire kingdom by freeing the prisoners and destroying the Organasm. It's an honor to stand alongside you in battle!","content.75.4762":"It's all very nice and peaceful... and that's the whole problem. How should I say this... I miss the adrenaline. Sure, there are moments of real panic, even fear, when I'm running the shop. But nothing like the raw excitement of a battle to the death.\\n\\nYou ever feel that weight on your chest on a Dinsdor night? When your heart just starts pounding like it's in agony? Something's missing from my life, and I don't want to ignore it anymore.","content.75.4763":"At least we understand each other. But you're lucky enough to be able to continue your adventures. Oh, listen to me rattling on...\\n\\nI'm not trying to say that I'm not happy with my Miranda. I like spending time with her, and I'd say I'm very lucky to have her. But something's missing... something that you have.","content.75.4764":"Ever since you defeated the Amybia, it's much easier to take care of Ohwymi. It's strange... I have the feeling that everything's just fine! My intuitions are always right, and right now they're telling me that there won't be the slightest hint of danger in the centuries to come.\\nI mean, there's still some leftover contamination to get rid of, but it should be all right for me to go away for a day or two. I owe you at least that much.","content.75.4765":"What are you trying to tell me? I had everything under control with those Wabbit creatures! You didn't need to come save me.\\n\\n*A playful gleam in her eye tells you that Mimi the Marvelous is still glad you{[1*]?:} showed up to save her*\\n\\nOkay, so maybe I did need a little help. Anyway, who's keeping score after that whole adventure we went through?","content.75.4766":"Hahaha! We'll set that research aside until the battle is over, my friend{[1*]?:}! To tell you the truth, I wasn't expecting to get caught up in something like this when I met{[1*]?:} you. I'm not really a heroic warrior, more of a researcher or inventor. But if the fate of the world is in our hands, we need to face up to that.","content.75.4767":"Haha! Don't worry, we've got resources. And there's no way we'd ever abandon one of our own. You're a member of our clan now, and we support each other no matter what! You've got one of the best trackers in the World of Twelve by your side. So focus on what you have to do.","content.75.4768":"Is that any way to talk in the presence of the head of Sidimotes & Co.? Be careful... if you play with fire, you might get burned. My priority at the moment is Count Harebourg, but keep that up and you'll have a taste of my wrath too.\\n\\nIf you'd be so kind as to drive those Mechas away, I'll forget this whole thing happened. Ready{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4770":"Good day, traveler{[1*]?:}. I am Armand, crown prince of the Sadida Kingdom! We're happy to have you here. Please, make yourself at home... If you feel like training, what do you say we train together?","content.75.4771":"It's a long story, traveler{[1*]?:}, and a frustrating one to say the least. You've arrived at a troubled time, you see...\\n\\nSome Boowolves have managed to escape from our prisons and take over our clearings. Our residents can no longer go for a peaceful stroll in the woods! My sister is nothing but a dreamer, and my father is grieving... So it falls to me, the prince, to take care of it!","content.75.4772":"Ha, you've got that right! I don't need all these guards... I'm already much better than them in battle. I wish everyone would stop treating me like a child. I'm a Sadida warrior too!","content.75.4773":"By Sadida... How I despise Arachnees. Lucky thing there are none here around this fire.","content.75.4774":"*Tarak Nofobe rolls up in a ball, terror-stricken at the very thought of those hairy monsters*\\n\\nI can't cross the hills if they're infested with Arachnees!","content.75.4775":"*Tarak Nofobe lets out a piercing little squeak*\\n\\nOf course not! You don't understand! The thought of crossing those hills is far too frightening. I appreciate the thought, but it's totally out of the question!","content.75.4776":"Ugh, just the thought of those horrible creatures walking on the same ground as me... I simply can't bear it! ","content.75.4777":"Hey there! Are you here looking for treasure too? Just be careful not to run into any Gerbeans!","content.75.4778":"Hey, what's up! Fancy meeting you here! C'mon, don't look at me like that. It's not like we're going to go to war over a few trees...","content.75.4779":"You didn't exactly pick the best time to come here. The Sadida Kingdom isn't doing too well at the moment. I've got far too much work to do since the... since the mother of my children has been gone.\\n\\nIt's not easy for me to lead a whole people while also raising a family, and taking care of the Tree of Life too. My little Amalia still doesn't know that her mother is gone, and Armand has got it in his head to take on all kinds of dangers just to get some attention.\\n\\nNot only that, I've also caught wind of a major threat to our southern forests. The Sadida Guard, our elite soldiers, haven't been able to get anywhere near it. These wild owls keep pushing them back. So as you can imagine, I don't have a lot of time to spare for you. I'm sorry, come back later...","content.75.4780":"Uh... Oh, don't worry about me. I'm just passing through. I'm here on... vacation! Frigost is nice, but it is a bit chilly...\\n\\n*You look at the mechanical installations, nuts and bolts, and oil stains all around Sylargh. He doesn't seem to realize that his lies are completely obvious*\\n\\nW-Why are you looking at me like that?","content.75.4781":"Oh! So you know I'm here to deforest part of the Sadida Kingdom! I was starting to feel a bit lonely here, to be honest. Sure, my super Saw Mechas need a little bit of maintenance... But ever since the Master lost faith in the machines' combat potential, I've sure got a lot less work.\\n\\nOh well, with all this wood, I'm sure we'll do just...\\n\\n... *Sylargh stops suddenly, realizing he's just been tripped up*","content.75.4782":"You... I, uh... Oh no! I've revealed the Master's plans! You tricked me! You manipulated me! Me, Sylargh, the incredible genius!\\n\\n*Sylargh gets ready to fight*","content.75.4783":"...","content.75.4784":"You disappoint me, [#name]. And here I thought you were an{[1*]?:} honorable and committed{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}...","content.75.4785":"That's enough! You're trying to stir up trouble in our lands. If you don't stop, we'll strip you of your right to stay in the Sadida Kingdom. Count Harebourg is an... eccentric character, but an honorable man. He's never done our nation any harm, and he's one of the few leaders in this World who really cares about our problems.\\n\\nI refuse to let you sully his name behind his back!","content.75.4786":"Whew, we're back in the Xelorium. I have to admit, I'm feeling a bit nostalgic thinking back on all our adventures! Anyway...","content.75.4787":"*Pandora jumps at the chance*\\n\\nI... need to talk to you too. Chad and I were both defenseless at that moment. I've always wondered... Why did you save me?","content.75.4788":"*Pandora looks disappointed for a split second, but her pragmatic side quickly returns*\\n\\nSorry, it's just my scientific side. I always try to figure out the meaning behind things. But it is what it is. He died for no reason, and there's no special meaning to one choice or another.\\n\\nAnyhow... To be continued. We have other things to worry about at the moment.","content.75.4789":"*Pandora is disconcerted, and doesn't seem to know what to think*\\n\\nI don't know why, I'm just a bit frustrated to find out that our survival came down to the flip of a kama. I do understand that it must have been a very difficult choice for you. Don't take this the wrong way, but I hope you don't make all your decisions like that.\\n\\nAnyhow... To be continued. We have other things to worry about at the moment.","content.75.4790":"*you sense profound regret in Pandora's eyes*\\n\\nChad... I'll never understand his intentions. I think he was our friend, but... Damn it, why'd he have to die? I still had so many questions for him... I just can't believe he was truly a bad person. I'm not angry with you for the choice you made, it's just that now I'll never have answers to those questions.\\n\\nAnyhow... To be continued. We have other things to worry about at the moment.","content.75.4791":"*Pandora's eyes are filled with a range of emotions. Her attitude softens as she reflects on the meaning of your words*\\n\\nI don't know what to say... I'm so grateful to have met you{[1*]?:}. I've never done anything to deserve what you did for me. At first, I just wanted to draw on your fighting abilities to satisfy my curiosity, but now... I've made a lifelong{[1*]?:} friend{[1*]?:}. Thank you.\\n\\nAnyhow... To be continued. We have other things to worry about at the moment.","content.75.4792":"*Pandora flashes you a grim look, suddenly fully aware of the weight of her responsibilities*\\n\\nRight. Thanks for reminding me. It's true, I have important things to accomplish here, and you're right to keep your eyes on the prize... but try not to make all your decisions based on what's best for the World of Twelve. You're allowed to think of yourself sometimes too. I mean, for a{[1*]?:} hero{[1*]?:} like you{[1*]?:}, I assume that's your main concern.","content.75.4793":"*You place your hands on Pandora's shoulders and show her that you sympathize with her situation. You notice that she's trembling*\\n\\nGood choice. I'm sorry, I'm just totally confused since I got my memory back... Sometimes, I wonder who I really am. And my memories of Chad, of the Xelorium Sage... Their deaths haunt me. Will my whole life be just a series of sacrifices? Will I lose you too someday? I'm afraid I won't be strong enough to face it all.","content.75.4794":"*Pandora's trembling resides a bit, but doesn't stop completely. Almost imperceptibly, she signals that she wants to change the subject. You drop it*\\n\\nOkay... To be continued. We have other things to worry about at the moment.","content.75.4795":"After I got your message, I started looking into anomalies in the spatial region of the Divine Dimensions, and I've identified two that may match what you're looking for. One of the anomalies is especially strange because... how should I say this... It's a sort of \"rip\" in space between Xelorium and Srambad.\\n\\nKing Mallory has provided us with a map that shows how to get to the place in Srambad where the anomaly is located. Apparently it's in an old prison built by Sram himself. Who knows what we'll find there?","content.75.4796":"Phew! We're back in the Xelorium! Can't say as I really missed it too much... So I guess you need my old carcass to help find some guy?","content.75.4797":"Is that so?! What exactly d'you wanna tell me, then? 'Cause me, I know I've got a pretty big question for you, kid. Hah!\\n\\nYou know I was a rotten double agent all along... The only way them Srams managed to keep finding you in one dimension after another is 'cause I was feedin' 'em the info. So I gotta know.\\n\\nWhy the heck 'dja save me?! I mean, seriously, I just don't get it! Why would you let your friend get killed instead o' the traitor that put you in that situation?","content.75.4798":"Hmph! I shoulda figured. Tryin' to play it cool, like there's nothing in it for you{[1*]?:}, huh? I get where you're comin' from, kid{[1*]?:}. The world doesn't make much sense to me either. Still, I kinda felt like you, me and Pandora, we had a little thing goin'... not exactly sure what, but... Ah well, not this time, I guess.\\n\\nAnyway, guess I'll return the favor this one time.","content.75.4799":"Hahaha! Now that's the way to do it! What can I say? You made the right choice. Except you shoulda rigged the coin so it always comes up Pandora.\\n\\nAnyway, guess I'll return the favor this one time.","content.75.4800":"Whoa, what the heck are you sayin'? You disappoint me, my friend{[1*]?:}. I knew you were a bit light on brains, but... wow. That's gotta be the dumbest thing I've ever heard. Come talkin' to me about morality when you're the one judgin' people like that? That's seriously messed up.\\n\\nAnyway, guess I'll return the favor this one time.","content.75.4801":"Ah, c'mon... No need for kind words with a piece of garbage like me. Save all that for someone else. It's wasted on me, believe me.\\n\\nAnyway, guess I'll return the favor this one time.","content.75.4802":"Are you serious{[1*]?:}?! Mwahaha! You've always been a little hard to read, but I never figured you were quite that sadistic. And she trusted you, too, y'know?! Hahaha... Dang, kid{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nAnyway, guess I'll return the favor this one time.","content.75.4803":"I've already checked that out a little bit... And I think I might know where the dude you're lookin' for is at. But first, we've got somethin' important to do. You know I used to be pretty good buds with Sram himself, right? And no one can keep a secret from me forever... Y'know?","content.75.4804":"Pandora is alive.","content.75.4805":"She's been a prisoner all this time in a secret dungeon in Srambad. I've managed to get my hands on the blueprints of the building in question. All I need is a green light from you to go in and get her. You'll come with me, of course. I'll need you to carry my daggers.","content.75.4806":"Well, thanks for your concern for the Sadida Kingdom. There must still be a few seasoned fighters that could answer your questions.\\n\\nI remember hearing stories about Boowolves when I was younger... My mother used to read them to me. Maybe there's some truth to those tales. You should look into it.","content.75.4807":"Well done. It looks like you prevented a serious disaster! Who knows what would've happened to our lands if that Giant Moon had continued growing to boost the Boowolves' power. That's one problem solved at least.","content.75.4808":"Come on! Who the heck could orchestrate something like that? I can't imagine why a Sadida would release those creatures into our wilderness. Especially considering many of our warriors have died fighting Boowolves...","content.75.4809":"Ah, finally some good news! The whole troop vanished some months ago. It was very troubling... Thank you for bringing our illustrious expert back to us!","content.75.4810":"I see, we've been manipulated by an extremely dangerous creature. At least the kingdom is no longer threatened. Things can get back to normal now... Until another great danger arises, of course. Thanks for your help - I can't thank you enough.","content.75.4811":"Hmmm, let's see... Oh yeah! I remember that little crew. I told them where an old mining site was found... It's on your map, right there! Those galleries are pretty big - be careful not to get lost, and avoid those Gerbeans!","content.75.4813":"If you're really that motivated{[1*]?:}, I can send you to face the greatest dangers this world has to offer.","content.75.4814":"It's more messy than ever, but your reward will make it worth the trouble.","content.75.4815":"I see. We've been manipulated by an extremely dangerous creature. So, what did you do?","content.75.4816":"So, the threat remains... Well, I'm grateful to you regardless. After all, you came back{[1*]?:} to warn us. Thank you for completing the investigation.","content.75.4817":"*At the beginning of your story, Otomai interrupts you occasionally to ask you to repeat yourself or be more precise. Then he remains silent, with a gloomy look about him. As far as you're concerned, your mentor and ally Otomai always has an answer to everything. But this time, even he seems puzzled.\\n\\nYou finish telling your story, while acknowledging that it seems strange. In just a few months, you touched the Ice and Cawwot Dofus, explored the Divine Dimensions, talked with Xelor, and discovered that temporal anomalies exist.\\n\\nA long silence sets in and you take the opportunity to admire the Mount Zinit landscape. This mysterious place will probably never reveal all its secrets to you. Otomai eventually stands up to speak*\\n\\nI... see. I must have a potion for madness lying around somewhere. Stay there...","content.75.4819":"Yes, yes. I understood. This is a big deal. I need to think about it a little more. I'm feeling at a bit of a loss right now.","content.75.4820":"I think so. Sorry, but I don't really have a solution for what you've described. It sounds like a problem that's beyond all of us. On the surface of it, I think we should let the Twelve take care of it. But who knows what they're up to? ","content.75.4821":"It's worth a try. Besides, you're probably used to it. Maybe you could contact a Dimensional Voyager and see what new dimensions there are to explore?","content.75.4822":"My old house in Astrub is so nostalgic... Ever since I regained my memory, it's as if this peaceful little life here took place centuries ago.\\n\\nCan I help you, [#name] ?","content.75.4823":"Errr, yeah. What about you?","content.75.4824":"...","content.75.4825":"*An awkward silence sets in*","content.75.4826":"Nothing in particular. I'm still trying to think about what Count Harebourg told us, but we lack solid information and I still can't contact the other Watchers. It looks like my powers are limited...","content.75.4827":"Remember when I got my memory back? I told you I was a Dimensional Voyager. It's not entirely true. I'm one of the Watchers. They're a group of timekeepers, if you like. I've been their leader for a few centuries.","content.75.4828":"We are immortal beings who can move through space and even time. We serve Xelor, we follow his plan, and we carry out his plans.","content.75.4829":"There were many of us at first, but there are fewer and fewer Watchers active. There's been almost no one left since Ogrest's Chaos. My mother Septangel was the very first Dimensional Voyager to become a Watcher. But she stepped down, letting me become Master of the Watchers in her place. I don't know why she disappeared, and I'm still looking for her.","content.75.4830":"I hope so... She probably had good reason. ","content.75.4831":"As you know, Ogrest defeated the Twelve gods. They lost some of their powers, knowledge, and memories. Xelor was obviously aware, and rather than trying to avoid the inevitable, he decided to entrust the gods' lost memory to guardians.\\n\\nThat's how the Order of Watchers was created. The project's ultimate goal is to convey this memory to mortals.","content.75.4832":"With Ogrest's Chaos, several Watchers lost their powers or died. There are only Dimensional Voyagers left now, but they aren't aware of everything. That's why I'm trying to find Jullier and my mother, Septangel, to tell them about these temporal anomalies...","content.75.4833":"Usually, yes, but I can't for now. It's as if I were stuck.","content.75.4834":"Certainly. I bet a few mortals have already tried to go back in time, but it seems impossible to me, even for a few minutes. Only us Watchers can do so, because we have the powers of the god Xelor.\\n\\n*You look at your friend Pandora. She seems tired and puzzled at the same time. Figuring out the temporal anomalies will be very difficult, let alone finding a solution. The task seems unbelievably complicated, and yet here she is stuck at the very first hurdle*","content.75.4835":"He's doing better... But I think his combat abilities are still just as diminished. I don't think he can go with you in the coming battles.","content.75.4836":"Honestly, I don't think I've regained anything you could call combat abilities. I could well be a burden for the battles to come, so I'd rather not go with you...","content.75.4837":"I don't really have time to go with you... I'm looking for other Watchers and my lost powers.","content.75.4838":"I don't know what you plan on doing, but a few Dimensional Voyagers recently opened a portal to a dimension you haven't yet explored... The god Osamodas's. They look like they're in trouble, so maybe you could help them out!\\n\\nI'll set up the Temple of Scriptures portal to take you where you need to be.","content.75.4839":"What can I do for you, adventurer{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4840":"Not much. Many of our order's members are dead... Max Arturo and I decided to do what we do best: explore the dimensions ourselves, looking for vanished Dimensional Voyagers. They're our companions, after all.","content.75.4841":"Precisely. We completed our mission by protecting the gods' power and leading you to it. But many of us suffered in the process.\\n\\nNow that's all over, I'd like us all to go home. We were obviously just pawns in a greater plan...","content.75.4842":"I think you know much more than we do. Apparently, Xelor himself selected several members of our order to perform temporal surveillance missions, in a way. But I have absolutely no idea who was involved.","content.75.4843":"Listen, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I don't know what happened in the Xelorium... On the other hand, in my view, nothing justifies your decision to sacrifice Pandora.\\n\\nI really wish I could never forgive you. It'd all be so much easier! But Pandora herself wiped the slate clean... After all, you managed to find her in the god Sram's prisons, which I certainly wouldn't have been able to do. If only you knew how much I regret being so powerless.\\n\\nPerhaps I was doomed to be a mere observer from the very beginning...","content.75.4844":"Listen, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I don't know what happened in the Xelorium... On the other hand, I want to thank you for not sacrificing Pandora.\\n\\n*A shadow falls over King Mallory's face*\\n\\nThe Xelorium Sage's death has already caused me great suffering. She was a spirited girl with a great sense of responsibility. That's why I'm telling you I feel bad about the loss of my companions... If only you knew how much I regret being so powerless.\\n\\nPerhaps I was doomed to be a mere observer from the very beginning...","content.75.4845":"Hey there, adventurer{[1*]?:}! What are you doing here? Are you lost{[1*]?:}? HAHAHA!","content.75.4846":"Well, everyone hits a snag once in a while! Especially when it's a divine entity blocking your path! It's true that I built some serious things in the past, including the Container. Ah, it was a fine masterpiece...\\n\\nBut you know, most people only have one project, one reason for being. It's hard to reinvent yourself and stay creative all the time, especially when you've already moved mountains. Most Twelvians are like that! HAHAHA! I'm just very tired, and I wish it would all stop!","content.75.4848":"Let's not dither, we've got a lot to do. And so little time...","content.75.4849":"*You look at Pandora's face. Your friend seems filled with cold resolve. She bears very little resemblance to the Pandora who stayed in Astrub. The Pandora from the future seems determined to do what it takes to save the World of Twelve*","content.75.4850":"*Pandora seems hesitant*\\n\\nIt's just that many things have happened since I got back from the Xelorium.","content.75.4851":"It was in the Xelorium, wasn't it? Yes, those were the days.","content.75.4852":"So... Where should I start? First, I trust you to keep this conversation and my coming here absolutely secret.","content.75.4853":"*You are in an entirely new Dimension, far from the World of Twelve, and with Pandora, who seems to have returned from the future. You get the feeling this extraordinary situation is nothing compared to what Pandora is about to tell you*\\n\\nIt's a long story. Are you ready{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4854":"I take it you know what the Watchers and temporal anomalies are? We learned that a large-scale disaster would soon take place. It'll happen in a few years' time, actually.","content.75.4855":"Let me finish... The nature of this disaster remains a mystery, but we know what the result will be. Listen carefully.","content.75.4856":"There will be nothing left. Absolutely nothing. I've traveled through time more than once, but nothing and no one survived the disaster I'm talking about.","content.75.4857":"We formed a council to fight the Plagues. The goal was to weaken them before they grew too powerful... But we were soundly defeated.\\n\\nI tried to put an end to the threat on my own, but it was impossible. I was mortally wounded facing the Plagues. My clock hand broke... But my mother Septangel, helped by a friend, turned back time to bring me back.","content.75.4858":"Harebourg was absolutely right. The world itself is causing its own undoing.","content.75.4859":"Imagine the wind blowing in the same direction, every second of every day. A mere breeze is of no danger. But if the wind blows for centuries without stopping, there are bound to be repercussions.\\n\\nThat's all. It's an accumulation of failings, sorrows, and fights.","content.75.4860":"How do you fight ideas? How do you fight the wind that blows?","content.75.4861":"I know it's hard, but you have to admit that our World has come to a dead end. The cycle of Wakfu and Stasis turns and turns... But it is not eternal. All things have an end, and the end is inevitable.","content.75.4862":"You know how we never drink from the same river twice?\\nLet's imagine that yesterday, you drank the water from the river.\\n\\nToday, you cannot drink that same water again for two reasons. First, yesterday's water has flowed away and is gone. Second, you're not the same person anymore because you're a day older{[1*]?:}.","content.75.4863":"The world is the same. It's constantly changing. Everything is altered every second. All these changes don't mean starting anew. Both energies are opposite and conflicting. Every second, a tiny and minute part is consumed and returns to the interstellar void...\\n\\nEverything has an end and dies, then something else comes to take its place. Do you want to stop the world from destroying itself? Then you have only one option: destroy it yourself.","content.75.4864":"Harebourg just wanted to delay and escape the inevitable. He doesn't have a lasting solution to this problem. There are only the choices we want to make.","content.75.4865":"That's it. It's all going to disappear, yes.","content.75.4866":"*Pandora smiles with amusement*\\n\\nI knew you were going to say that. There's still hope. But it's an equally painful and grueling task. I'd understand if you refused. But I think you're one{[1*]?:} of the only{[1*]?:} adventurers{[1*]?:}... Maybe even the only person who can rise to the challenge.","content.75.4867":"For now, I think you should first focus on your arrival in this dimension and try to digest what I taught you.","content.75.4868":"*Pandora hesitates*\\n\\nI don't want you to get your hopes up too high. Our plan isn't the most amazing one in the whole universe. The disaster cannot be avoided...\\n\\nWe'll talk about it more later. First, go see what Osamodas has to tell you.","content.75.4869":"To enter the god Osamodas's realm, first, you'll need to find four keys.\\n\\nThis dimension is divided into four parts, with four dungeons full of creatures that are more powerful than anything you have ever faced. Defeat them and you'll get the plans for the keys.\\n\\nYou'll also need a special ore to craft the keys. I've indicated the coordinates on your map.","content.75.4870":"Take care of yourself.","content.75.4871":"I expected no less of you! But you still don't have all the plans to craft the keys.","content.75.4872":"I expected no less of you! But you still don't have the ore to craft the key.","content.75.4873":"Well, well... a mortal. Hello!","content.75.4874":"I see, you're looking for the ore. It's right over there, but unfortunately, the ore is guarded by formidable Osamodas dolls.\\n\\nI hate those dolls. They stop me from mining inside the cave... If you defeat them, can mine what you need... and you'll be doing me a big favor.","content.75.4875":"Oh, thank you so much!\\n\\n*The dragon tries to lay a friendly paw on your shoulder. A warm smile spreads across his face and you can sense how grateful he is*\\n\\nI really couldn't stand those dolls. Thanks to you, I can go back to mining! I will never forget you, adventurer{[1*]?:}!","content.75.4876":"Absolutely. Osamodas created me. Actually, I don't think I'm the result he was expecting...","content.75.4877":"My only desire is to lead a simple, honest life and work hard for my family. Things about the gods and dragons don't concern me. Mining is my great passion in life. I swear only by my pick and miner's helmet, to my family's great despair.\\n\\nTell me honestly, does a Miner Dragon really sound so strange to you?","content.75.4878":"I'm a major dragon but also a miner, you see.","content.75.4879":"How so? Of course not.","content.75.4880":"I expected no less of you! You gathered everything together, good job! Come on, help me craft the keys.\\n\\n*You notice that Pandora has some dust on her clothes*","content.75.4881":"Rest? I don't know what that word means!\\n\\n*Pandora smiles tenderly*\\n\\nWell, it's true that you've already completed most of the tasks. Hard, wasn't it? Take a nap while I craft them; you've certainly earned the rest.","content.75.4889":"*Pandora looks at you, with a slightly guilty air*\\n\\n... On second thought, maybe you need a little rest, right? Go get some rest and I'll craft them myself.","content.75.4890":"How so?","content.75.4891":"*Pandora seems surprised*\\n\\nThat's true. We were missing four pearls of wisdom from the list of things required to craft the keys.\\n\\nYou saw that building outside, not far away, didn't you? Inside, there's a terrible monster guarding the pearls. That was also where Sly Mendrock, the Dimensional Voyager and Osamosa sage, lost his life trying to protect them...\\n\\nThat's why I wanted to go there myself. I didn't want to disrupt your quest by talking to you about it. The main thing is that I got the pearls of wisdom.","content.75.4892":"You're getting to know me well.\\n\\nYes, it's... It's quite difficult. Mendrock was a good, hardworking, honest man. But sometimes you have to be willing to be part of a greater plan.","content.75.4893":"*Pandora pauses*\\n\\nSometimes, I don't know anymore. Balancing the survival of the whole world and the sacrifices of loved ones is confusing.\\n\\nBut you're still here to remind me. Thank you.","content.75.4894":"*Pandora pauses*\\n\\nSometimes, I don't know anymore. Balancing the survival of the whole world and the sacrifices of loved ones is confusing.\\n\\nIt's true that both arguments are valid...","content.75.4895":"You see! I know you so well. Thank you for respecting my choice.\\n\\nIn reality, it's... It's quite difficult. Mendrock was a good, hardworking, honest man. But sometimes you have to be willing to be part of a greater plan.","content.75.4896":"I... I wasn't expecting you to understand. But never mind.","content.75.4897":"*You rest. Those four dungeons were home to creatures of unreal power. You don't know if there are any that could rival them in the World of Twelve, even though Ogrest pales them all in comparison*","content.75.4898":"*You wake up and see Pandora watching you quietly. You notice that she seems thoughtful. Either way, you feel rested{[1*]?:} and more determined{[1*]?:} than ever. In front of Pandora, you see four keys made from the mysterious ore you collected. They are set with strange pearls. You don't know how long you've been asleep*","content.75.4899":"You slept like a Tofu! Come on, get going.","content.75.4900":"I'm sorry, but I can't go with you. The god Osamodas knows that Xelor sent me, and he doesn't always like Watchers interfering in the order of things...\\n\\nBesides, I already know what he's going to tell you.","content.75.4901":"*You craft the keys with Pandora's help. This is a long and tiresome process. Therefore, you don't have a chance to chat with your friend. You'd have liked to ask her more about this so-called plan, but it'll have to wait*","content.75.4902":"*You finish the task. You hold in your hands four keys made from the mysterious ore you collected. They are set with the pearls of wisdom Pandora collected. These four keys seem to promise answers. However, you don't yet know if you'll like those answers*","content.75.4903":"Thank you very much. You helped me craft the keys when you didn't have to{[1*]?:}.\\nRight, now it's up to you.","content.75.4904":"Start by telling me who you are, little creature!","content.75.4905":"That's all!? Hehehe!\\nGive me a break! You'll never survive the dangers of the Osamodas Dimension in the state you're in!\\nGo back where you came from; it'd be better for you!","content.75.4906":"Hahaha! Very well! How amusing.\\nI'd like you to bring me a rare monster. A monster I've never seen before!\\nIf you succeed, then I'll help you get through the door to the Osamodas Dimension.","content.75.4907":"Hmmm... For that, you'll first need to come back in one piece! But you're not entirely wrong. Besides, I'm curious to see what's going on there right now.\\nVery well! I agree to help you get there.\\nThe door said something about a sleeping Gobball, didn't it? You should try bringing a real Gobball and putting it to sleep!","content.75.4908":"Oh, it's you! Do you need me again? Good. You finally grasped how little you know! How may I enlighten you, little creature?","content.75.4909":"Try not to die too fast. And... no, nothing. Bring me a creature, okay?","content.75.4910":"So? Surprised{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4911":"Yes. It's a feather from the god Osamodas himself. You'll need it later.\\nFor now, let's take stock.","content.75.4912":"Exactly. The god Osamodas was busy creating the creatures of tomorrow... Creatures that can withstand extreme situations and ecosystems. That's why this Dimension has brought several biomes together.","content.75.4913":"Are you starting to understand our plan?","content.75.4914":"The reality is that the world will be destroyed and we cannot prevent it. Endless oceans and no land to live on...\\n\\nWe don't know exactly what will happen, but we know that a disaster will occur on a specific date. Rather than trying to endure this disaster... The plan is to avoid it entirely.","content.75.4915":"The aim of our plan is to change fate, giving the islands and their ecosystems a future.\\n\\nWe set out to keep things safe out of space-time so they could resurface when the time was right. We also decided to make the islands stronger so they would have a chance against the disaster.\\n\\nThis is an extremely daunting task and many adventurers have already tried to devote themselves to it in the past. Not everything can be protected from destruction, but we can at least pass on an embryo to rebuild the future.","content.75.4916":"The plan is supposed to work. But we've got a problem.\\nAs Watchers, our strength is time travel. But the Plagues also have this power, and they're gradually eroding the negative energies across many ages... It's the biggest danger we face.\\n\\nWe are working on a solution to these time problems, and we'll need you for this.","content.75.4917":"For now... Nothing. I'm still looking for a few things that are vital for this new plan. I'll explain it to you once my concerns have been dealt with.\\nGive me Osamodas's feather and I'll keep it for you.","content.75.4918":"I'm so sorry for leaving you in the dark...","content.75.4919":"I get your point... But the stakes are far too high.","content.75.4920":"That's right. I'll know where to find you after I've made sure of a few things...","content.75.4921":"I appreciate your patience... The stakes are far too high. Just know that I'm glad that I can count on you.","content.75.4922":"It should be okay, thank you. I'll find you once I've made sure of a few things...","content.75.4923":"See you later, then.","content.75.4924":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.4925":"Not really, but you could say that... I can give you quests, as if I myself were a member of the Guild of Hunters, and you will receive fitting rewards.\\n\\nThe resources you bring me and the bosses you defeat will help me maintain the dimensional portal in the Osamosa Laboratory.","content.75.4926":"We are in a Dimensional Voyager village. I mean... An abandoned village. Four Voyagers arrived a few years ago when they discovered these coordinates. At the time, this part of Osamosa was absolutely pristine. From what I understand of their reports, they decided to settle here to conduct studies.\\n\\nThen the god Osamodas and his creatures arrived to put their plan into motion. Then their dimensional portal closed.\\n\\nI found the body of one of them, but the other three have disappeared. Maybe they managed to escape...","content.75.4927":"Yes, of course. The god Osamodas tried to create monsters in their image. Perhaps he felt inspired by the work of one of his fellow divinities?\\n\\nBut anyway, I'm certain they're not really dolls because they look a little more evil...","content.75.4928":"DO NOT LINGER IN THIS PLACE IF YOU HAVE NOTHING TO ACHIEVE, MORTAL{[1*]?:}.","content.75.4929":"WE ARE IN MY DIVINE PALACE. THIS ROOM IS DEDICATED TO A SPECIAL CHALLENGE.\\n\\nI STUDY THE LIMITS OF MY CREATURES' PHYSICAL AND MENTAL RESISTANCE WHEN THEY ARE FACED WITH A SERIES OF FIERCE FIGHTS. THE AIM OF MY RESEARCH IS TO CREATE GENERATIONS TRAINED FOR EXTREME SITUATIONS.\\n\\nIF YOU'RE INTERESTED, YOU COULD FACE A WAVE OF THEM IN EXCHANGE FOR REWARDS.","content.75.4930":"WHAT DO YOU WANT TO KNOW ABOUT THE WAVES?","content.75.4931":"YOU MUST FIRST SET UP YOUR WAVE.\\n\\nIT CAN HAVE A MIXTURE OF CREATURES FROM THE FOUR ZONES OF OSAMOSA.\\nIT CAN BE SET AT STASIS DIFFICULTY 1, 2, 3, 4, OR 5.\\nIT CAN LAST 15, 25, OR 35 ROUNDS.\\n\\nONCE THE WAVE HAS STARTED, IT'S MERELY AN ENDLESS FIGHT. NEW MONSTERS WILL APPEAR EACH TIME YOU DEFEAT A GROUP.","content.75.4932":"ONCE YOU HAVE DEFEATED ALL THE CREATURES, A SECOND WAVE WILL APPEAR. OVERCOME THIS SECOND WAVE TO INITIATE A \"BOSS\" WAVE. DON'T WORRY. THE BOSSES WILL HAVE LESS HP THAN IN DUNGEONS.\\n\\nONCE YOU HAVE DEFEATED THE BOSSES, IT'S BACK TO SQUARE ONE UNTIL THE ROUNDS ARE OVER OR UNTIL YOU HAVE BEEN DEFEATED, POOR MORTAL{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nBUT THE GODS ARE KNOWN TO BE GENEROUS, AND YOU CAN GET COMBAT BONUSES (EVEN ROUNDS) OR SCORE BONUSES (ODD ROUNDS).","content.75.4933":"ALL THE MONSTERS YOU FACE WILL HAVE THEIR USUAL LOOT. BUT IN ADDITION, EACH LITTLE FIGHTER WILL EARN TOKENS ACCORDING TO A SCORE.\\nTHESE TOKENS CAN BE USED IN THE MACHINE AT THE ENTRANCE TO THE ROOM. THERE YOU WILL ALSO FIND INFORMATION ABOUT THE SCORE.\\n\\nBE CAREFUL, TINY MORTAL{[1*]?:}... IF YOU DO NOT SURVIVE THE WAVE, YOU WILL EARN NOTHING.","content.75.4934":"HOW MANY ROUNDS DO YOU WANT IT TO LAST?","content.75.4935":"WHAT STASIS LEVEL DO YOU WANT TO FACE?","content.75.4936":"SHOW YOURSELF TO BE WORTHY OF MY TIME... MORTAL{[1*]?:}.","content.75.4937":"Before heading to our next destination, you should get a little night's sleep. ","content.75.4938":"...","content.75.4939":"*Your eyes open to the cold morning light. You discover it with a sense of disappointment, because you had already sensed the light through your closed eyelids.*\\n\\n*Between dream and reality, memories are jostling inside your head. What's on your mind?*","content.75.4940":"*Whatever they were, your first thoughts quickly fade away, and you stand up looking haggard. The strange village of the Dimensional Voyagers, abandoned like so many pebbles strewn across the beach, gives you a sense of solitude tinged with dread*\\n\\n*You can see the Osamodas dimension through the windows. A formidable dimension that you had trouble subduing. But in your mind, it looks like the morning is ultimately just an illusion in this dimension*","content.75.4941":"Are you finally awake{[1*]?:}?","content.75.4942":"Our next destination is the Shhhudoku Kingdom.\\n\\nIf you have things to do, you should take care of them before you join me. It'll be more complicated once you're there.","content.75.4943":"Hmmm! You brought a creature back as promised. At least you're not as incapable as you seem...\\n\\n*Mishell seems very interested in the little fox you brought her*","content.75.4944":"So tell me, mortal{[1*]?:}, how was the dimension?","content.75.4945":"*You pause abruptly, suddenly reluctant to talk about the impending apocalypse in front of the mysterious entity Mishell*","content.75.4946":"Just a second! Come back here... I haven't finished talking to you.","content.75.4947":"I don't know what you saw or heard. But never forget that you are a common, insignificant thing. Things that are beyond you...","content.75.4948":"Well, some things are beyond you. Mere mortals{[1*]?:} such{[1*]?:} as you end up regretting being interested{[1*]?:} in the great plans of the gods.","content.75.4949":"If you've ever traveled in the Divine Dimensions, you must know the Dimensional Voyagers, right?","content.75.4950":"Do you feel okay? You don't feel nauseous or dizzy? Losing consciousness?","content.75.4951":"Hmmm...\\n\\n*Mishell gives you a surprised and amused look. You answer with a questioning look*\\n\\nI heard about a disease that systematically affected Twelvians traveling from one dimension to another. The disease is called Dimensional Sickness.","content.75.4952":"You should ask your friends what it's all about. I'm serious, tiny creature. Not just anyone can survive this kind of adventure.\\n\\nMerely being around certain powers is sometimes enough to inflict... irreversible consequences on you.\\n\\nAnd I wouldn't want to lose one of my favorite puppets. So be careful!","content.75.4953":"So? Did you find our lost companions? Are they okay?","content.75.4954":"I... see. So they're...\\n\\n*Mallory turns his face away, but you had already glimpsed the unspeakable pain that could be read in his expression*","content.75.4956":"I need time, [#name]. Leave me alone.","content.75.4957":"Don't say anything. I saw Mallory's reaction. Just tell me... Did you find Serge?","content.75.4958":"That's odd. I'm doubtful. I can't believe they're really dead, as brilliant as they were. Maybe I'm having difficulty accepting reality.\\n\\nToo bad, another trail disappears... Perhaps we're the last two Dimensional Voyagers still active?","content.75.4959":"*Arturo raises his eyebrows and stares off into space; he clearly doesn't know how to broach the subject*\\n\\nSerge was... How can I put this?","content.75.4960":"No, don't worry about it. It's quite complicated to explain, because I always got the impression that Serge was out of place among us. As if he wasn't from here.","content.75.4961":"I guess all I can do is keep the memories of those years I spent with the group, and maybe move on...","content.75.4962":"Let's not dither, we've got a lot to do. And so little time...","content.75.4963":"You're not entirely wrong. In fact, it is one! It's been dead for years, luckily for us.","content.75.4964":"*Pandora turns to you with a serious look*\\n\\nYou mean you don't know? The Crackler who makes up the Shhhudoku Kingdom... You suggested it to Osamodas. It was conceived in the future, then came back to the past because of a time rift... and now the Whisperers have taken up residence there.","content.75.4965":"I'm sure that in another timeline now forgotten by all, the Shhhudoku Kingdom was located on an entirely different island...","content.75.4966":"That's true... We mere observers are so little in the face of passing time.","content.75.4967":"We have two main missions here. Find the Whisperers' melody, and retrieve the gods' power somewhere in the Tundra.","content.75.4968":"For the melody, you must investigate in the Murmoor. As for me, I'll try to locate the gods' power.","content.75.4969":"Not normally. But the Eliocalypse is such a danger to the world that I have to intervene.","content.75.4970":"Sorry, but we cannot help you right now, adventurer{[1*]?:}... Our kingdom is on the verge of extinction, and our lives are in danger!","content.75.4971":"These are old Whisperer legends, barely more audible than a whisper... We forgot this melody, and besides, I'm not even sure it still exists.\\n\\nBut I know someone who can tell you more.","content.75.4972":"Shhhudoku himself investigated the melody at length. He was desperately looking for it, and his final plan was to awaken Grampar, the huge Crackler on which we rest... in order to conquer the world.\\n\\nI guess he found it, because he started building the Organasm to play it.","content.75.4973":"Hey there! Welcome to my little corner of paradise. Do you want to take a dip with me?","content.75.4974":"It's a little hot, but it's alright.\\n\\n*You sense a hint of worry and suffering in Rykke Eensy's eyes*","content.75.4975":"*You pull it back out immediately; the water's hot enough to boil eggs*","content.75.4976":"Hahaha! Don't worry, I've already been in here for several days.\\n\\nI read in the venerable legends of Rykke Errel that hot springs were very good for circulation and muscles...","content.75.4977":"I admit it's a bit of a pain, but at the same time it's a bit chilly outside... and the Scramshells ate my clothes, so for now, I can't go out. You know what I mean?","content.75.4978":"That is, I had a weighted outfit for my training... So if you really want to help me, you'd have to make me a new one. Otherwise I won't come out!","content.75.4979":"No, it's true?!","content.75.4980":"Scramshells, you say? Horrors... So they still exist!","content.75.4981":"This is an extremely serious threat. The Scramshells once lived in Sufokia, and they started attacking us when the beaches silted up.\\n\\nWe lost hundreds of militiamen and city guards repelling them... If they get the urge to come back, we might not be able to repel them!","content.75.4982":"I imagine you don't really know about all this. You're not naive{[1*]?:}, after all. You see, the sea is one of our best friends. It gives us our fish and lets us travel from one land to another. But it is also one of our fiercest opponents.","content.75.4983":"Actually, that's the least of our worries. The coastlines are an extremely special and fragile ecosystem.","content.75.4984":"Waves hit our rocks and houses every day. They will eventually erode and destroy them completely. That's why we set up rock ridges as breakwaters to lessen the waves' strength.\\n\\nBut in doing so, the waves no longer removed the sand, which put us in danger of silting up. So we had to transport the sand elsewhere every month...","content.75.4985":"Basically, yes.","content.75.4986":"Looks like it. It was an absolutely disastrous idea.\\n\\nBefore, there were natural plants able to protect the coastal dunes. Beach grass, for example. But Sufokia had to develop economically, so we built ports, boats, warehouses, and houses on the beaches... And that race for kamas led to these plants' disappearance.","content.75.4987":"The coastlines are one of the most important battles of our time, and no one is aware of it. Adventurers are all quite happy to enjoy our beautiful beaches, but one day there will be nothing left.","content.75.4988":"I like you, so I'll give you some advice about your outfit. Scramshell shells are a very special material that captures and retains electricity. If you don't choose good fabric for your clothes, you'll be dead as soon as the first hint of a storm comes along!","content.75.4989":"Obviously, the Scramshells themselves are able to withstand these electric shocks. It's thanks to a very particular species of toad. They have special slime that can unbewitch shells' electrical properties.","content.75.4990":"You should investigate near the Scramshells you found. If there are enough of them, they'll have at least one toad in their group. Then again, I'm not sure why you insist on doing this...","content.75.4991":"Be aware that if you get past the toad, you'll scatter the Scramshells at very least. That way, you'll reduce the risk of them coming back someday to take revenge on Sufokia. Honestly, I wouldn't mind!","content.75.4992":"Hmmm... He was in that hot spring before me. But I think I made him leave...","content.75.4993":"He went to a dark place over there.","content.75.4994":"What about my outfit?...\\n\\n*The Iop's unflappable face shows no sign of emotion or fear. His friendly smile is frozen, and deep down you understand that he has been enduring unspeakable suffering for far too long. The smell of charred flesh is getting stronger and stronger. You must hurry and help him*","content.75.4995":"I'm far too hot to remember... Sorry.\\n\\nOh, that rings a bell... When I came here, I found some sheet music, and an inscription on a stele.","content.75.4996":"Alas, the Scramshells ate it along with the stele and my... uh, clothes.","content.75.4997":"Not so fast. I owe you one! I remember the inscription on the stele as if it were yesterday. I am passionate about tales and legends, after all.","content.75.4998":"It seems there are eight steles hidden in the Shhhudoku Kingdom. Each one plays a little sound when touched. These eight steles describe the kingdom's history, and if you put them in the right order, you'll be able to hear the melody. The eighth one is somewhere on the Pingwins' Ice Floe.\\n\\nI hope that will help you in your quest, adventurer{[1*]?:}!","content.75.4999":"Hang on... It seems like... Yes, you recovered a little of the gods' knowledge!","content.75.5000":"Hey there! It's me, the Miner Dragon. Remember me?","content.75.5001":"Yes. By the way, I cleared your way. It's the least I can do to thank you for exterminating those Osamodas dolls.\\n\\n*The dragon pouts while remembering the incident, which was clearly painful for him*","content.75.5002":"What? That's terrible! Well, I'll take your advice literally then.","content.75.5003":"The gods' knowledge is next. We're going to need it for our plan.\\n\\nUnfortunately, I haven't been able to find out precisely where its source is, but I'm sure that it's somewhere on this island, divided into four fragments, including yours. We should ask the people here.","content.75.5004":"I can explain what's at stake a little bit, but I warn you, it's complicated. Are you ready{[1*]?:}?","content.75.5005":"Time is not an unbroken line. It's a... dimension, like any other. If you change where an item is placed, it is no longer in its original place, right? And that can cause damage to the dimension, damage and side effects. For example, a movement, a shock, or an injury.\\n\\nIt's the same for time. If someone goes back in time, the entire world will suffer the side effects, because there cannot be two parallel dimensions.","content.75.5006":"Perhaps you remember having lived adventures, explored lands, and met people...\\nBut perhaps you have experienced other adventures in places that have disappeared due to the temporal side effects. Faced other monsters, met other people...\\nPerhaps you were still dead not so long ago.","content.75.5007":"It's the unpredictable nature of these temporal changes that makes the Watchers' mission so strict. We must not deviate from Xelor's grand plan. We are guardians. Without the Watchers, the consequences of the slightest temporal anomaly could be irreversible, as we've already seen with opponents such as the Plagues.","content.75.5008":"It's impossible to do without the god Xelor. Can you imagine the World of Twelve without even minimal order? It's already hard enough with his help. And that's not to mention the fact that we'd suffer the full force of the Eliocalypse...","content.75.5009":"When you were in the Xelorium, the god Xelor gave you the gods' forgotten knowledge, but your body wasn't able to absorb it.\\n\\nSo it dispersed throughout the World of the Twelve in the form of several crystals. We need to gather the crystals. This is a crucial phase of our plan...","content.75.5010":"Well... it's your destiny.","content.75.5011":"That's the whole purpose of the Methea project.\\n\\nThe twelve gods were defeated in their battle with Ogrest. They lost some of their powers, their knowledge... and their memories.","content.75.5012":"Xelor is the master of time. He knows what has been and what will be. That means he is aware of Ogrest's Chaos and its consequences. He decided to shelter the memory lost by the gods after their defeat. Including his own!\\n\\nOnce sheltered, he entrusted it to us, the Watchers. Then we passed it on to you. Your task was to spread it equally among all mortals in this world. Thus, the gods would no longer be forgotten, and they would act through the mortals they would inspire.","content.75.5013":"You should rest a little before taking on the quest again.","content.75.5014":"*You sit down and decide to gaze at the horizon. The calm, cold sea seems sad to you. The dull grass and melted snow could have reminded you of the joyful return of spring were it not for the dead silence covering these desolate, abandoned expanses. You stay for a while contemplating the horizon, and the late morning seems melancholic*","content.75.5015":"*You cannot forget that this world is in danger of disappearing. The things that seem most dear to you could be destroyed and forgotten. You think about the cause, but you can't figure it out. Pandora seems sure of her plan, but she also warned{[1*]?:} you that the plan might do some damage along the way*","content.75.5016":"*You wonder how you came to{[1*]?:} play such a major role in the world's survival on your own{[1*]?:}*","content.75.5017":"*You know that a being as calculating and powerful as Xelor is bound to have orchestrated everything. He knew everything about your doubts, memories, and abilities. He dreamed up an optimal path that you must follow without asking yourself any questions. Perhaps that prospect reassures you?*","content.75.5018":"*You are aware that you have gained considerable power during your adventures. You have overcome many challenges and it seems natural to you that the dangers threatening this world should be faced by someone equal to them*","content.75.5019":"*Perhaps it was just a fortunate, or unfortunate, combination of circumstances. After all, what is the universe if not an incalculable range of probabilities? And out of everything that has happened in the Krosmoz, with billions of random occurrences and infinite free will having collided, here you are at last, as if by magic*","content.75.5020":"*You always thought that your determination could make a difference. It all starts from there, and even now, your untiring thirst is what drives you to work twice as hard where anyone else would have given up long ago. Many Twelvians live ordinary lives, and it is your ability to never give up and start working hard over and over again that sets you apart* ","content.75.5021":"*You're not as alone{[1*]?:} as all that. How many other adventurers, soldiers, farmers, fishermen, merchants walked this world before you? You're just there to ensure continuity, and then one day pass on your burden to someone else. The infinite loop of Wakfu and Stasis will pass through you, before abandoning you one day, once you have continued its cycle*","content.75.5022":"Were the monsters you defeated more powerful than usual?","content.75.5023":"They had to be strengthened with a fragment of the gods' knowledge. If you defeated them, you retrieved part of it.","content.75.5024":"It's normal. But never mind! Let's get back to the last stele.\\n\\nI've got an idea! Go on ahead, and I'll call for reinforcements.","content.75.5025":"You got a second fragment. Nicely done! It won't take long at this rate. I suspect that the last two fragments are under the mountain where the Pingwins live. Talk to Fisher Fiasco.","content.75.5026":"Well done, [#name]! But it's... strange. We still haven't located the very last fragment, and it's quite a substantial one...","content.75.5027":"Yes, my detector has been sensing it since we arrived on the island. This fragment of the gods' knowledge is larger than the three you gathered so far...","content.75.5028":"I am Aguabrial, primordial dragon and guardian of the Water element... I don't really want to make waves... Turn back, unless of course you want to take a cold shower.","content.75.5029":"It wasn't necessary to cause all this turmoil.\\n\\nStill waters should not be disturbed, unless you want to cause a storm.","content.75.5030":"What world? You only perceive the illusion given by your mortal{[1*]?:} senses.\\n\\nIf you want me to listen to your request...\\n\\nProve your worth to me, and prove that you deserve your place in the Krosmoz!","content.75.5031":"*As you often do, you sit near Otomai, your friend and mentor, to tell him about your adventures.\\n\\nOsamosa and Pandora's various revelations, the arrival of a strange Dimensional Voyager who completely sabotaged your plans, made Pandora disappear... and stole all the gods' knowledge*","content.75.5032":"*Otomai thinks for a moment, unfazed*\\n\\nIf you want a source of energy that's powerful enough, I think you should try to get a Primordial Dofus.","content.75.5033":"Don't worry, we're not going to get it from Ogrest. The Primordial Dragons are gone, except for one who is still active in this period. Aguabrial, the Water Dragon.","content.75.5034":"He is here, on Mount Zinit. He watches over the people of the Mount and dissuades unworthy adventurers from climbing up. Besides, it's a good thing you haven't met him yet...","content.75.5035":"He is such an extremely wise and powerful creature.\\n\\nHe has already created two Turquoise Dofus. One of them is in the possession of my son, Ogrest. The other one hatched and gave birth to Bolgrot, an extremely powerful dragon who ravaged the world before being defeated by Rykke Errel.","content.75.5036":"If a dragon dies without creating a Dofus, they cannot reincarnate and get stuck between worlds. This is the sad fate that awaited Bolgrot.","content.75.5037":"With a Turquoise Dofus, you should be able to fight the Voyager you told me about on an equal footing. On the other hand, for Pandora's plan... Since she's no longer here to explain it to us, I'm afraid it's going to be complicated.\\n\\nI'll gather a few allies together while you're busy finding Aguabrial, and I'll look for Pandora as well.","content.75.5038":"Aguabrial must fall in love with you.","content.75.5039":"I'm sure you'll find a way to charm him! The fate of the world may depend on it.\\nI think without the Primordial Dofus, you won't be able to fight your opponent on an equal footing...","content.75.5040":"I won't say that you arrived too late. Just that I was early.","content.75.5041":"I don't know.\\n\\nBut it doesn't matter. I have finally retrieved the gods' knowledge... I will be able to break the thread of destiny!","content.75.5042":"Your friend, you say? Do you know what her infamous plan is? She still hasn't told you anything, has she?","content.75.5043":"*The Voyager sits on the water clock and dangles his makeshift clock hand*\\n\\nIt's a long story.","content.75.5044":"*The Voyager jumps down*\\n\\nYou know what? I've got one last little thing to sort out. When you opened Pandora's box, your body rejected the gods' knowledge... but you managed to absorb some of it inadvertently.\\n\\nI'm going to kill you, and only after that, I'll have collected all the fragments! I'll finally be able to change the nature of time.","content.75.5045":"Hey! How are you doing?","content.75.5046":"Xelor is using us... We are slaves to his will.\\n\\nImagine all these children's dreams broken and crushed.\\n\\nImagine that you wanted to explore the world to fulfill your dreams, but because Xelor decided otherwise, he made you die. All because your death was perfect for his plan, for the \"good of the world\".","content.75.5047":"He used the Dimensional Voyagers as simply disposable, obedient underlings. We caught a disease we're still suffering from...\\n\\nThe World of Twelve... would be much better without the Twelve. Our creators have inflicted too many trials on us.","content.75.5048":"The Brotherhood of the Forgotten approached me, but their plan was insipid, mere revenge, a simple coup. I want to go further. I want to know what the world would be like if no deity had ever intervened since the dawn of time.","content.75.5049":"I want to go back in time to the Primitive Era, to when the Ten appeared. Then I will get rid of the gods, and I will disappear in turn, leaving mortals to fend for themselves.\\n\\nThat's partly why I need the gods' knowledge. I will bequeath it to mortals to give them the means to achieve their ambitions.","content.75.5050":"There will be no war for Primordial Dofus, no Ogrest's Chaos... No Eliocalypse, even! Only a new world with a cycle of eternal reincarnation, Wakfu and Stasis.\\n\\nDon't forget that I opened myself to much of the gods' knowledge. I retrieved the memory of their failures. Time has no further need for them!","content.75.5051":"You're a Huppermage, so you should be the{[1*]?:} first{[1*]?:} person to understand me.","content.75.5052":"You're an Ouginak, so I think your clan matters much more to you than your god, right? You should understand me.","content.75.5053":"It's always the same with disciples of the Twelve. It's as if we were talking about your parents.","content.75.5054":"*The last Voyager stares at you coldly, indifferent to what you say*\\n\\nI was sure you wouldn't understand.","content.75.5055":"Behind me? That's a water clock. I borrowed it from a friend of yours... Count Harebourg. I must thank you for distracting him during the battle at Brakmar.","content.75.5056":"I did what the Watchers do. I watched... Waited... And a blind spot finally came. The Eliocalypse. Thanks to the temporal interference by the Four Horsemen, a weak point finally appeared in Xelor's plan. The Four Horsemen even killed Pandora.","content.75.5057":"Yes... She met her doom against the Plagues. Her plan was a huge failure, as always. But she has since come back to life, and she has guided you down this path.\\n\\nI must thank you, [#name]. A lot of the things you've done have allowed me to slip out of time and put my plan into action.","content.75.5058":"Thank you so much. I'll be able to get out soon!","content.75.5059":"I'm far too hot to remember... Sorry.","content.75.5060":"Hello! You don't look like you're from around here. Can I help you?","content.75.5061":"But... That's disgusting.","content.75.5062":"Ah, but that changes everything.\\n\\nSo, the trouble is I don't have much honey anymore. Sorry! It's become very rare in this region.","content.75.5063":"Well, I don't know what made you think it was going to be a good idea! Plantiguards can be pretty aggressive when they see a drop of honey. That's why I gather the smallest ones: I teach them good behavior at the same time. They are very civilized creatures.","content.75.5064":"And yet, the Plantiguards can build things, like igloos and rudimentary barriers. They were great beekeepers too, but there aren't many bees left... Fortunately, I'm here to give honey to the babies. Without me, they wouldn't have anything to eat.","content.75.5065":"The new leader of the Plantiguards is not very cooperative... He despises creatures who aren't fierce warriors like he is.","content.75.5066":"He says he descends from the Bearbarians... But I don't believe his story one bit. He's using his dominant position to stuff his face with the little honey that the hives produce. He's unfairly making the Plantiguards go hungry!","content.75.5067":"You look like a tough {[1*]?gal:guy}... Despite how involved I am, I can't restore order to this Tundra. I need you to go fight Bearkneck.\\n\\nBut promise me you'll be careful. He's extremely powerful. And that's not all! He's formed an army of enraged Plantiguards who are prepared to kill for a drop of honey.","content.75.5068":"So, how do you feel?","content.75.5069":"It's a delicate matter...\\n\\n*Otomai takes time to think, before raising his eyebrows, as if he hadn't found a perfect answer*\\n\\nLook, I don't know what you want me to say. It's been months, years even, since I saw{[1*]?:} you incarnate. And from day one, I could tell you were a remarkable person. If just one person has the keys to everyone's destiny, it must be you.","content.75.5070":"I understand what you mean. It is easier to say that everything is going from bad to worse, when in reality we are simply living in a period of transition to something else.\\n\\nThe World of Twelve will have to catch up and adapt to a universe where the Primordial Dofus no longer provide harmony, where the gods have been removed, where Ogrest's Chaos destroys ever more things.\\n\\nStill, I'm optimistic, and I think there are a lot of good things to save. This universe is worth what it's worth. There are certainly difficult times, but you and your allies alone have the responsibility of slowing its decline and trying to bring about a miracle.","content.75.5071":"*Otomai seems to sympathize. He understands that the situation is far from won, but he has no choice other than to put you back on the only conceivable path*\\n\\n[#name], you aren't {[1*]?:}the first person to walk this path. There will always be failures and successes. At the moment, we still have the chance to act. We must keep on fighting to bring the harmonious world we originally dreamed of back to life. Be resilient.","content.75.5072":"Very well. I didn't find Pandora, but I came up with a nice plan for your Dimensional Voyager business. I'm sure he'll love it!\\n\\nFor now, let's go see Aguabrial. Be careful, he'll probably want to fight you again. Are you ready{[1*]?:}?","content.75.5073":"*Jacqueline scowls*\\n\\nWho? My name is Jacqueline!","content.75.5074":"*Jacqueline seems a little vexed*\\n\\nNever mind, I'll get over it. What did you want to tell me?","content.75.5075":"Oh, yes, I see. If you want to know more about the Tundra, there must be a member of the Guild of Hunters around that you can ask. In general, they're the biggest experts on the fauna and flora of each region. I've never seen one on this island, though...","content.75.5076":"I see! Say no more, I have all the information you need! With all the time I've stayed in and around the Shhhudoku Kingdom, I know all there is to know.\\n\\n*Juspark gives a thumbs-up, with a radiant smile on her lips*","content.75.5077":"*Juspark, who is seems a bit touchy-feely, pushes you away nicely by the shoulder*\\n\\nYou've come to the right place! I guess you're looking for Bearkneck? He's in a cave he calls home, but it is fiercely guarded by his servants. It looks like that's where they produce the most of honey.","content.75.5078":"*Juspark looks at you with a glimmer of mischief in her eyes*\\n\\nBearkneck? He's in a cave he calls home, but it is fiercely guarded by his servants. It looks like that's where they produce the most of honey.","content.75.5079":"I have a little idea how to make your life easier. You want a plan to enter this great cave, right?","content.75.5080":"*Farle straightens up and looks at you with a frown. He seems a bit lost*\\n\\nSorry, who?","content.75.5086":"*Fisher Fiasco lets out a long sigh*\\n\\nWhat's going to become of us?... Oh, we're not 20 years old anymore.","content.75.5087":"If all goes well? Quite the contrary... Honestly...","content.75.5088":"Times have certainly changed. The whole world went crazy, or so it seems. Look at this ice floe, once covered with little seals, walruses, and bears. Ah, back then, we knew how to live together in harmony. All that doesn't make us seem any younger...","content.75.5089":"Well, this is the Pingwins' doing, of course! They started ravaging everything a few years ago. They took all the species on the island prisoner, and they slaughtered those who opposed them. I don't know what came over them. It's surely another youngster making a mess of everything with his ideas...","content.75.5090":"Oh wow, they're no good with language! Well, a little common sense isn't too much to ask, is it? Ah, youngsters, always charging in without saying anything.\\n\\n*Fisher Fiasco shakes his head despairingly*","content.75.5091":"I don't know. I don't know. I've lost all faith in humanity since these awful things happened.","content.75.5092":"Can't you see my costume, you dimwit? They ignore me because they think I'm just one of them. They can't teach an old dog like me new tricks!","content.75.5093":"You should ask for help from someone who knows the area well. There must be some specialists around... Isn't there a Guild of Hunters representative on the island? Back in my day...\\n\\nOh, you know what? You should ask Juspark for help. She knows the area well. She's a lovely little girl... Haha.","content.75.5094":"I see. Ah, in my time, we would have celebrated it properly, but nowadays it's no longer possible... Still, we live in a world...","content.75.5095":"Thank you for bringing rest to all those tormented souls. You don't see that everyday among those of your generation. I'll remember you.","content.75.5096":"The Pingwins! Aren't they adorable, with their little orange fish?\\n\\n* Juspark gives a knowing look*","content.75.5097":"Is it true? I didn't know! So that's why the little seals disappeared...","content.75.5098":"Wait! I know there are mysterious steles to the southwest. But you'll probably need someone's help to decipher them, because they're in coded language...","content.75.5099":"I'm willing to help you. But thinking about it, while I'm working on the translation, maybe you could do me a favor? I need makoffee... lots of makoffee.","content.75.5100":"Don't look at me like that, I'll be out soon. Oh, and also bring me a bottle of oil, some toilet paper, two sponges, and some ravioli.","content.75.5101":"For that last point, I prepared an order at Yeast's. It's already paid for, so you just have to collect it. For the makoffee, however... Deal with it yourself!","content.75.5102":"Here, I wrote it all down in this book. Thanks again for the shopping!","content.75.5103":"I think you've got the wrong{[1*]?:} Posteet.","content.75.5104":"Ah, nothing could be simpler. Let me give you a little bag with this.\\n\\n*Yeast goes away for a few moments, then comes back and hands you a bag*\\n\\nHere, give my regards to Jenry!","content.75.5105":"Behave!\\nI'm sure that by creeping into their lair with a little honey, you'll go unnoticed{[1*]?:}!\\n\\n*Juspark smiles at you without realizing that the Plantiguards would jump on you every step of the way if you were covered in honey{[1*]?:}*","content.75.5106":"I thought of everything! That's where my network comes in! Go see someone called Farle, in Amakna. He's an absolute specialist. Ab-so-lute, I say. But he's a pretty discreet person. I'm sure you've never heard of him...","content.75.5107":"If you see him, tell him that you're there on my behalf, and I'm sure he'll help you!\\n\\nOh, and I marked out the entrance to their lair on your map, for later.\\n\\n*Juspark winks at you*","content.75.5108":"You're a little late for that. There haven't been many bees around for years...","content.75.5109":"I don't know the whole story, but I'm sorry I couldn't help you.","content.75.5110":"*Jacqueline opens her eyes wide in rage, and you abruptly stop talking*","content.75.5111":"JACQUELINE! My name is Jacqueline!\\n\\nI'm the only person who worries about this completely melted ice floe and who ventures into these cold lands to try to save whole species! You could at least remember my name! I don't believe it!","content.75.5112":"*Jacqueline looks at you sadly. Your mistake with her name has really hit her hard. You realize that this young woman has no small amount of pride*\\n\\nThat's great. Here's your reward. You can go back to your adventure.","content.75.5113":"I still have a lot of work to do if I want to restore some semblance of ecological balance in this area, and I'm the only one who can do it...","content.75.5114":"No thanks, it'll be fine, I'm used to it.\\n\\n*Jacqueline's coldness once you're no longer of use to her surprises you, but since you couldn't even get her name right{[1*]?:}, there's not much you can do about it*","content.75.5115":"Yes, I'm doing fine! I'm fighting fit. I'm ready to take on new challenges in and around the kingdom!","content.75.5116":"Oh, you know, not much. I run a good old camp for Otomai's Hunters, I take your loot for rewards, and whatnot.\\n\\nThere's nothing unusual on the horizon, except for the Eliocalypse!","content.75.5117":"Oops! Me and my big mouth. I said too much, didn't I? I'm not on great terms with the Watchers. It's a bit difficult to explain! I've had my share of rough adventures, you know. Bad guys, my village getting destroyed. Just the routine stuff.\\n\\n*Juspark feigns a pout*","content.75.5118":"Hey! I just told you it was complicated. I'd like to tell you a little, but you'll have to keep it a secret!\\n\\n*Juspark puts a finger over her lips*","content.75.5119":"Good! It all started when I found myself on the road after some rather unpleasant events. Let's say that... it involved nasty bandits and my home village.\\n\\nAfter a few years of wandering and mercenarism, the Dimensional Voyagers contacted me to become one of them. Anyway. I said to myself: Why not?","content.75.5120":"I spent a few years there, but hey, there already weren't many people left at the time. We were all busy finishing a thing for Project something. Personally, I felt bad more than anything else. I've had weird illnesses from traveling through portals so much. Weeell! I figured I wasn't cut out for that life, so I left.","content.75.5121":"Yes, I'm getting to that! After that I started associating with Otomai's Hunters. I saw it as a nice little job while waiting to do something else, but eventually, I got used to it.\\n\\nIt was only recently that Pandora came to see me.","content.75.5122":"She explained it to me a little, and to be honest, I don't remember everything. But I understood that it would be bad for the universe if we didn't do something!\\n\\nSo I organized a kind of reconnaissance mission for her. You know, exploring a little, picking up a few things... Mainly reporting on the situation here.","content.75.5123":"You there! Not so fast, my friend{[1*]?:}. You think you're getting out of this? I have questions for you as well!","content.75.5124":"*Juspark seems to think cheerfully about a topic of conversation for a moment*\\n\\nI know! Aren't you tired of traveling the world? Wouldn't you like to find a place just for yourself? So you can, I don't know, lay down your arms! Pandora told me a little bit about you, you know. It seems you been around quite a bit...","content.75.5125":"*You realize you haven't really thought about it much lately*","content.75.5126":"I see, I see. Oh, come on! Don't look at me like that! The main thing is being good.\\n\\nHappiness is just perspective, you know. See things for the better and everything will be fine. See things for the worse and everything will go wrong. Come on, don't you have adventures to complete?","content.75.5127":"Wait, this is strange. I can feel him getting closer. He... He's almost here!","content.75.5129":"*Pandora looks at you and you see great anger in her face. You think she must be angry so as not to succumb to fear about the situation*\\n\\nHe must be caught at all costs. But how?","content.75.5130":"No. Osamodas's feather won't reveal his position to me. So I conclude that our enemy Voyager isn't on this island...","content.75.5131":"It's a divine relic, so it starts resonating with the gods' knowledge when it's close enough. But I don't know what the next island with fragments is...","content.75.5132":"I know you won't let me down, which is why I won't reveal the plan to you.\\n\\nOh then, there's nothing left to lose... This isn't really the right time, but hey.","content.75.5133":"There are two steps to the Eliocalypse. The first step is to understand what resonance is. Count Harebourg explained it to you. It's Twelvians' actions that will lead the world to destruction. Flouting ecology, seeking profit, lack of morals, endless wars... Harmony disappeared due to Ogrest's Chaos and the removal of the gods. And all this discord has been fanned by creatures with excessive power.","content.75.5134":"Exactly. The Horsemen started resonating with the negative impulses of Twelvians, gained power and began to eat away at time. I suffered an absolutely resounding failure trying to fight them... But if you, the chosen one, fulfill the prophecy and release the gods' knowledge into the world, then the Twelve could regain some sort of power in order to inspire mortals to do good.","content.75.5135":"The second part of the Eliocalypse is resilience. As I taught you, even if mortals become... how shall I put it?... nicer... we cannot prevent the disaster from happening. I have been to the Eliocalypse, and I know that we've passed the point of no return and that we won't be able to prevent the water from rising drastically again.","content.75.5136":"There are several ways to withstand a shock. The idea is to bequeath a time capsule to future generations. Plant the seeds, so that a future may one day bloom.","content.75.5137":"Many ancestral forces exist in this world, and they can help us accomplish this task. We can store all our knowledge in material forms that are very hard to break, or preserve some of the fauna and flora in the Divine Dimensions. But we need time to do it...","content.75.5138":"Uh, no. In theory, we can, but in practice, we can't really.\\n\\nMay I remind you that with Ogrest's Chaos, without the Primordial Dofus, and without the gods' knowledge, this era is left completely unprotected.","content.75.5139":"It's impossible to \"save\" things that haven't yet happened. There's too much risk of making a mess of it. I told you about the time scar phenomenon, didn't I, [#name]? If you \"move\" in time, then you risk causing damage all around you and creating irreversible temporal shocks. That's why the Watchers' mission is so strict.","content.75.5140":"I think time must be stopped.","content.75.5141":"I thought you were going to react dramatically...","content.75.5142":"Imagine activating a simple time loop. The World of Twelve would remain in 977. But that's not what we want. People would just live their lives and a year later, they would go back to the start of the year without anything ever changing.\\n\\n*Pandora's voice trembles more and more as she seems to get into the details of her plan. You suddenly understand that if she didn't want to tell you about it, it's because this plan would put her in danger and she knows you would be against it*","content.75.5143":"*Pandora stares at the ground*\\n\\nThat's right.","content.75.5144":"*Pandora stares at the horizon. The sea and the ice collide silently with the relentless melting of the ice floe that would signal the end of all species on the island*\\n\\nI've already made my preparations. I was planning to play the Whisperers' Melody to make you forget you met me. All I needed was the gods' knowledge, a crucial step in the plan.","content.75.5145":"*Pandora crosses her arms*\\n\\nIt's not that simple. If we want to catch him...","content.75.5146":"Well, I guess we have no other choice...","content.75.5147":"Yeah, but it'll only work once. I'll have to destroy the feather. Then we'll have to hurry and look for the fragments, and hope that we can recover the ones the Voyager stole from us.","content.75.5148":"*Pandora gestures to you that it might take some time. While she performs a strange procedure, you turn back to the icy sea.\\n\\nOne day, there will be nothing left here or anywhere else. Mortals, created by the gods, will lead their world to their destruction*","content.75.5149":"*You need to decide what is most important to you*","content.75.5150":"It's okay. From now on, there's no turning back. I made a list of places that contain a fragment of the gods' knowledge.\\n\\nHopefully, this will be our last mission together.","content.75.5151":"Looks like the shoe's on the other foot now.","content.75.5152":"You should have left this to me... It's the Watchers' mission to protect time.","content.75.5153":"Maybe it was your destiny as the chosen one{[1*]?:}, but you agreed to take on a tremendous burden. Everything you do from now on will change the world around you...","content.75.5154":"Someday, the loop will eventually disappear because the energy of the Dofus isn't infinite.\\n\\nIn your case, it might take several centuries. And for all the rest of the world, centuries will have passed in just a single year. But everyone will only have lived a year.","content.75.5155":"*Pandora smiles slightly with amusement*\\n\\nI don't know if I'll go back to the Wakfu Era.\\n\\nAnd believe me, it's best for you if you don't see me again. You'd be in serious trouble if that happened!","content.75.5156":"Farewell, [#name]. Thank you for saving me... many times. And thank you for your dedication{[1*]?:} to securing a future for the World of Twelve. I'll never forget you.","content.75.5157":"Oh boy! Why the long face? What's wrong?","content.75.5158":"A bit... I was pretty crazy about climbing back then. And once, I...","content.75.5159":"Oh! A few days at most. But your story sounds really important.\\n\\nCome on, tell me!","content.75.5160":"*Since Juspark is quite aware of what the Eliocalypse and the Dimensional Voyagers are, you vaguely tell her your story*\\n\\nI see... I feel like I know the person you're describing to me.","content.75.5161":"I think you're referring to, uh... Drat. What was his name again? Well... He was a Voyager who was quite mad at his order. He ended up leaving for Osamosa-something-or-other with other Voyagers, and we never saw them again.\\n\\nMost Voyagers could only talk about a prophecy at that time, and they absolutely wanted to activate the phase of a plan for something or other. The group that left for Osamosa was rather dissident.","content.75.5162":"If you want to get to the summit as fast as possible, I've got an idea.\\n\\nBut I'm not sure you'll like it. As for me, I really want to see it! Wahey!","content.75.5163":"They have nice catapults in the Shhhudoku Kingdom, don't they? I saw them send some Cracklers to the Tundra some time ago! It made a dreadful noise. I don't know who finally told them to stop, but it really was necessary. Any more and I was going to make them feel my spear myself!","content.75.5164":"What are you going to do, then?","content.75.5165":"*The sun slowly disappears. The warm twilight glow reminds you that hope is fading. You don't know exactly how much time you still have before the unthinkable occurs*","content.75.5166":"You're inside Grampar. Since the Crackler is dead, we can live in his body without any trouble. We'd quickly be digested, otherwise...","content.75.5167":"I guess the place was inhabited by smugglers, fugitives... In short, all kinds of criminals. It's a nice hiding place, and there's no shortage of food. But all those thugs have fled since the Scramshells arrived. These kinds of turtles are really very aggressive, it must be said.","content.75.5168":"It's... It's a mistake... Don't do it!","content.75.5169":"The gods' knowledge... Everything is falling apart. I'm going to...\\n\\n*Mortally wounded, the Last Voyager begins to ramble. You lean close to him to examine him*","content.75.5170":"*The Last Voyager gradually loses all color, and his misty eyes stare at the horizon*","content.75.5171":"I just wanted to... remember... I wanted to remember those people. The ones who died for Xelor's plan. All those strangers... cast into misfortune...\\n\\nI lost everything... I want to find them... I really want to tell you about...","content.75.5172":"*The Last Voyager closes his eyes in pain, both physical and mental. Tears flow. The clock is ticking. Killing him was the only way to triumph over your enemy*","content.75.5173":"Well, you've come a long way since we met in Incarnam.","content.75.5174":"Oh, I didn't do much. I went with you on your adventures out of curiosity, that's all.","content.75.5175":"No, I'm sorry. Despite all my knowledge of the World of Twelve, I could not provide you with a real solution. It must be said that these temporal intrigues are quite difficult to solve...","content.75.5176":"Believe me, we owe our being saved to you alone. You shone beyond my expectations. You were indeed the chosen one{[1*]?:} expected{[1*]?:} by the Twelve.\\n\\n*Otomai suddenly looks thoughtful*\\n\\nI wonder how Twelvians will behave now they have the gods' knowledge.","content.75.5177":"You've still got plenty of work to do then. And I hope I won't forget all about this past year I spent with you...","content.75.5178":"One last thing, [#name]. Whatever happens, don't forget that you're never alone{[1*]?:}. Remember that you can always count on me.","content.75.5179":"*The evening darkness paints a deadly atmosphere across the Ice Floe as you turn your back on Juspark. The day wasn't going to end until you found that wretched Voyager. You resist your desire to shiver as best you can. But this time it's hard to tell if it's linked to the freezing temperature or the adrenaline caused by the end of the world looming over you*","content.75.5180":"Of course we'll help you, adventurer{[1*]?:}. We are still indebted to you for liberating our dear kingdom. But if I may...\\n\\nI know you're very tough, but...","content.75.5181":"Very well. It's fortunate that we haven't yet disarmed the Crackapult. We'll take you there immediately.","content.75.5182":"Hmmm... Dofus are strange things, and there are still many mysteries regarding their powers. There might be some kind of obstruction between your mind and the Turquoise Dofus you possess.\\n\\nAfter all, you took a little walk through time. Who knows what impacts that could have on the mind? Bring me some ingredients and I'll make you a special potion to clear your mind.","content.75.5183":"What? What's that about time loops?","content.75.5184":"*Juspark nudges you*\\n\\nCome on, you can tell me anything, you know!","content.75.5185":"*Juspark looks serious*\\n\\nPrimordial Dofus are very special things. Your body might not be strong enough to withstand its energy, combined with that of the time loop. On top of that, you bore the gods' knowledge not long ago...","content.75.5186":"*Juspark seems cheerful and absent-minded again*\\n\\nI know! I'm going to give you a great exercise you can do to strengthen yourself up a little. Soon you'll be as strong{[1*]?:} as Tibia-Thrasher! Start by climbing to the mountain's summit, then do two hours of core workouts... Pull-ups, push-ups... Finally, don't forget to eat a wide variety of different proteins... Spread them out well over at least five meals a day!","content.75.5187":"You truly are a sorry {[1*]?princess:prince}!\\n\\n... Well, I know what you want. I'll give you a few dungeons to do anyway. But think about that diet I suggested{[1*]?:}!","content.75.5188":"Oh my, young {[1*]?lady:man}, you do look downbeat! What's bothering you?","content.75.5189":"*Pandiego slaps you really hard on the back*\\n\\nI know exactly what you need, young {[1*]?lady:man}. We're going to take a test of courage. I picked up some bamboo milk this morning, if you know what I mean...","content.75.5190":"It looks like you're completely transformed{[1*]?:}! You overdid the songs a little, as usual...","content.75.5195":"Don't say a word... I know why you're here, little{[1*]?:} Scaraleaf. You want to learn the art of combat!","content.75.5196":"Don't say a word... I know why you're here, little Scaraleaf. You want to learn the art of combat!","content.75.5197":"*The strange monk seems to mutter something as he pinches his elegant spectral beard*\\n\\nI don't think I've heard of it before.\\nMaybe you should visit the Undieworld library? You're bound to find information there to help with your research!\\n\\nThe library is hidden behind a piano, but the entrance is most likely guarded by the Nun.\\nIf you decide to venture into the Undieworld, be careful not to get painfully called{[1*]?:} back to Externam. You could end up spending the rest of eternity wedged tight with all the sinners...","content.75.5198":"Heh heh heh... Looks like you're out of luck...{[1*]?:}\\nWhen you signed your pact, did you happen to read the clause related to defeat after attacking someone?\\n\\nIf you want to get out of here, you'll need to do a little community service to prove your bad faith. Let's say 50 ore. Yes, that should do it.","content.75.5199":"Me? Oh, I'm just a prisoner like you. This prison, located in the Shustuft Crust, punishes little rascals who take careless risks.\\n\\nAnd I might've taken some risks myself recently... I think you can figure out why I'm in this place. Come on, let's get to work!","content.75.5201":"Cool, another Twelvian. It had been a while since I'd seen anyone from my home world.","content.75.5202":"I'm just a passing traveler... I'm trying to study this area's peculiarities. So what are you doing here?","content.75.5203":"I see. You want to find out where these strange memories emerging in people come from, don't you?\\n\\nUnfortunately, I can't help you find the answer you're looking for, but if we help each other, we should be able to find a way to progress to the next area.","content.75.5204":"My name is Arlemia. I came through a portal that has since closed.\\n\\nActually, I discovered the passageway thanks to strange memories that came flooding back to me all at once...","content.75.5205":"No, not for now. I want to learn more about these strange memories. I know they don't exist, but I'm somehow drawn to this place...","content.75.5206":"You're overestimating me a little. I want to know more about these memories, because I want to get to the reality behind them.\\n\\nAnyway, you see, those strange demons seem to inhabit this place. It looks like they are empty inside and the entire area is falling apart over time. This isn't the most welcoming place in the world.","content.75.5207":"A mysterious power seems to be at work... I get the impression this whole surface is being drawn into the black hole. This area is full of... non-life.\\n\\n*Arlemia looks serious*\\n\\nI know the Shustuft Crust is a completely different dimension... but I didn't think it would be a dimension where such a thing could happen.","content.75.5208":"As I told you, I've got memories linked to it. I feel like I've spent my whole life in a world where Twelvians and Shushus live together. And nothing looked like that dead landscape or those soulless creatures...\\n\\nIt looks like those Shushus are completely empty inside, lifeless. They, too, seem caught up in nothingness.","content.75.5209":"I've located the lair that a great evil seems to be emanating from. It's a sort of temple dedicated to the void. It seems that the demons go there to trade a part of their \"existence\" for original powers.\\n\\nUnfortunately, we can't go inside... not alive, anyway.","content.75.5210":"I think the gateway reacts to this strange presence of non-life.\\n\\nWe need to find a way to simulate this effect... maybe by increasing the oblivion around us.","content.75.5211":"I see. I wonder if something in this place could help us.\\n\\nI've explored the area a little, but it's too hard to do thorough searches because of the demons.","content.75.5212":"*Arlemia stares at you wearily*\\n\\nOh no...","content.75.5213":"A little... A lot, even. Actually, I'm from Milo's family. My full name is Arlemia Tchatch.","content.75.5214":"*Arlemia grits her teeth*\\n\\nYou can't understand what it means to spend your childhood with such characters. I had only books for company. My childhood was a hell of solitude and studying. They were only interested in their wretched ruins... I tried to learn about Archaosology on my own, but they showed me nothing but contempt. They're real pieces of work...","content.75.5215":"The memories that came back to me reminded me of another life, another possibility, with Shushus. In my memory, there are very specific moments of a much happier life. Yes, there was chaos, but there was life and simple rules.\\n\\n*Arlemia takes a deep breath*\\n\\nI finally felt affection. It's something I'd never experienced in my current life. That's why... I have to find it. I have to find the way to this other world, whether or not it's an illusion.","content.75.5216":"Absolutely.\\n\\nThey never cared about me.","content.75.5217":"*Arlemia stares at you coldly*\\n\\nI don't have much to do, actually. They left me alone all these years. These memories with the Shushus are my only opportunity to have a real life that's eternal and happy.\\n\\nI have to find these answers.","content.75.5218":"*Arlemia sighs, obviously annoyed*\\n\\nI don't want to call on the Archaosologists...","content.75.5219":"Hey, haven't we met somewhere before?","content.75.5220":"Absolutely. I remember now. Oh, what a great experience that was...\\n\\nI think you've come a long way since then!","content.75.5221":"Come on, don't be shy.\\n\\nI was looking for a way to explore Oktapodas's Temple, but to no avail... I've got some time to spare now.","content.75.5222":"*You see Milo's face light up as you mention the Void Spiral*\\n\\nHmmm, I see. That's really interesting!\\n\\nIt'd be a real pleasure to help you. After all, who knows what secrets Shushu architecture might hold? Perhaps I'll be the first Twelvian to unravel its mysteries! It's such as exciting prospect!","content.75.5223":"*You see Milo's face light up as you mention the Void Spiral. However, he becomes withdrawn when you mention your meeting with Arlemia*\\n\\nI see. Maybe I should... I think...\\n\\nI think it's best if I don't come. I'm sorry, but you'll have to get by without me.","content.75.5224":"*Lost{[1*]?:} in the passage of time, you no longer know when exactly the Wakfu Era began. Thousands of souls have come and gone, with their little stories forming the great cycle of the World of Twelve. And through the gray winter mornings, through the long summer evenings, the totality of existence continues on its linear path. You know, someday it will be the end of all things, when no one will be left to observe. Does that idea bring you comfort?*","content.75.5225":"*You suddenly have very clear memories. You see and hear things that don't belong to you, as if you were a{[1*]?:} mere visitor{[1*]?:} trapped{[1*]?:} inside a physical envelope other than your own. Gradually, a strange certainty takes root in you, the certainty that makes dreamers think everything is normal despite the pearly sky, the undulating ground, and the unlikely silhouettes*","content.75.5226":"*You notice a familiar figure with their back to you. You can't reach them. You draw on all your strength to try to talk, but no sound comes out. These events belong to someone else and cannot be changed. You are a mere spectator{[1*]?:}, amazed{[1*]?:} by how the waves move and invigorated{[1*]?:} by the warm wind caressing you*","content.75.5227":"*You look off to the side a little, as if to better gaze at the brilliant blue sea meeting the pure white sand. A few gray reefs add a welcome touch of complexity to this spring afternoon sky*","content.75.5228":"*Right now, you wouldn't be able to answer any questions. Your age, your name, your background... Memories of your childhood, the songs you sang, the battles you fought... None of that is on your mind. The only feeling inside you is plenitude. You want to stay there forever. Everything that has been only made sense for this moment right now. Everything that will be will merge into this precise moment*","content.75.5229":"*You scan the beach from right to left, and you feel your chest rise as hot air enters it*","content.75.5230":"*Juspark doesn't seem surprised, and he starts looking solemn. His usually so cheerful face seems to darken for a moment. But when you look closer, an enigmatic gleam still brightens up his gaze*\\n\\nI guess you're thinking what I'm thinking...","content.75.5231":"Yes, I'm afraid so.\\n\\n*The girl stares at you before turning abruptly toward the horizon, letting out a little cry of surprise*","content.75.5232":"Not yet. But it won't be long before \"he\" shows himself...","content.75.5233":"Yes. I didn't think it'd come to this, but it looks like we'll to have to call \"that person\".","content.75.5234":"True.\\n\\n*Juspark looks worried, placing his hand on his chin thoughtfully*\\n\\nThere's only one way.","content.75.5235":"I think that's our only solution.","content.75.5236":"Come on, you aren't going to let me think you haven't figured out what's going on yet, are you?","content.75.5237":"Ha ha!","content.75.5238":"They must have found a way to manipulate people's memories so no one will notice their evil plans!","content.75.5239":"You must go to the Shustuft Crust, and...","content.75.5240":"Pandora from the future won't come back. Pandora from the present shouldn't get involved in all this...\\nOtherwise, all the effort we put in might have been for nothing, and we could reset all kinds of situations.","content.75.5241":"*Juspark leans back slightly with a hand on her hip, looking proud*\\n\\nWhat do you think, smartypants{[1*]?:}?","content.75.5242":"Good! Like I was saying before you interrupted... I think you should go to the Shustuft Crust and see what's going on! And don't forget to report back to me afterward!","content.75.5243":"*Juspark looks up to the sky and mumbles a few incomprehensible words*\\n\\nAh, I know! Just ask Rushu your questions! He's kind of their leader, at least I think so. ","content.75.5244":"*Just as you say the name of the lord of the shadows, Ahr Khayuh seems to get stung by a Moskito*\\n\\nI think I misheard... I hope I misheard...","content.75.5245":"Hey, what's wrong with you!? Don't talk so loud!","content.75.5246":"Rushu himself is the problem.\\n\\nHe mustn't find out about our little deal in the Shustuft Crust, or he'll invade the World of Twelve through our portal. With the declining influence of the gods, his arrival in these lands could be catastrophic.","content.75.5247":"*The young Feca raises an eyebrow and adjusts her glasses. She doesn't seem to take you at your word*","content.75.5248":"Well, besides the fact it's completely suicidal...\\n\\nIt's not at all that simple. When I created this portal seven years ago, it appeared in a remote and rather arid area of the Shustuft Crust. Fortunately for us, Sthulhu supervised it.","content.75.5249":"We made a deal for Sthulhu to hide the portal. In exchange, I have to send adventurers to the Shustuft Crust to entertain the demons.\\n\\nRushu isn't aware that such a portal exists, since Sthulhu's territory is highly fragmented, almost completely destroyed, and very far from Rushu's palace.","content.75.5250":"There. If you want to go to the palace, it could be very complicated.","content.75.5251":"*Sthulhu seems glad to see you*\\n\\nBad day to you, inhabitant of the World of Twelve.","content.75.5252":"There's no rush. I'll explain everything. Some time ago, Ahr and I created a portal from Shusnitch Reef.\\n\\nIt appeared in a remote and rather deserted area that I was supervising... Perfect for escaping the attention of the master of demons.","content.75.5253":"That's right. An island shaped by me. I set up additional protection so as not to attract prying eyes.\\n\\nBut we're in a far corner of Rushu's citadel here. He and his minions won't notice a thing... Heh heh heh.","content.75.5254":"There's no rush. Don't be so impatient{[1*]?:} now...\\n\\n*The mischievous little demon chuckles under his beard, apparently in a good mood*\\n\\nThe entrance to Rushu's palace is well guarded. We can't get there without compromising our current position. And I need this place, this outpost.","content.75.5255":"This is my little spot, let's say. Heh heh. You are far, far, far from being the{[1*]?:} first{[1*]?:} Twelvian{[1*]?:} to come by here. It's good for business.\\n\\nAh, but I digress. If you want to go straight to Rushu, I've got just the thing for you, but you'll need a key to get into his palace.","content.75.5256":"Get noticed? I don't want that.\\n\\nLet's just say if a few mortals wanted to walk around the area or even go up against Rushu, then, well... As long as it doesn't come back to me, I wouldn't say no. Heh heh heh.","content.75.5257":"Heh heh. You shouldn't trust the demons you meet. For us, truth is subjective.\\n\\nDo you want to enter Rushu's palace? I can give you a way in. I've created a few portals for you. They'll take you to areas of the Shustuft Crust that are a bit... abandoned. I'm sure you'll soon realize what it's all about, heh heh heh... Each territory has a fragment. Find all five of them, bring all five to me, and the five of them together will open the way to Rushu's citadel.","content.75.5258":"*Wolfram chuckles beneath his beard, then clears his throat. His hoarse voice, like that of a wise old man, sounds like it told a thousand stories, chanted a thousand choruses, and whispered a thousand secrets. You feel soothed{[1*]?:} by his fatherly tone*\\n\\nThere are lots of obscured dimensions... and there's something special about this one. Your world is the one that managed to link up with me, Wolfram.\\n\\nSome time ago, a young Sadida's prayers at the tree of life served as a focal point for me... And her lingering memories of crozolilies, a flower that was erased from history, brought them back into existence here.\\nThen they were brought back to the Sadida Kingdom thanks to you. That's why this dimension can't disappear anymore.","content.75.5259":"In that case, first I must warn you of the countless dangers of your quest, [#name].","content.75.5260":"Your \"path\" is the one that preserves your world... Doing so, however, come at a cost, that of sacrificing the others.\\nIf you go that way, then you'll have to travel to the edges of time and the universes. You'll encounter thick darkness, because the stars that have always been extinguished are uncountable.\\n\\nBut now I know you'll fulfill the prophecy. You're so close to doing it... and yet so far, because your most terrifying opponent hasn't yet appeared to you.","content.75.5261":"The prophecy is real.\\n\\nBut maybe I'm digressing. How about you start by telling me about your quest so far? I'm an old boowolf, after all, and I haven't moved from this place in thousands of years. I'm sure your tale will brighten up my day.","content.75.5262":"Go on then, I'm listening, [#name].","content.75.5263":"Interesting... What next?","content.75.5264":"Oh, Astrub. What next?","content.75.5265":"Travelers see what they see, while tourists see what they came to see, don't they? Go on...","content.75.5266":"Oh, I know that universe well. Frigost and Count Harebourg!","content.75.5267":"A fantastic land, no doubt.","content.75.5268":"I wouldn't worry too much if I were you. Imagirorukam dedicated himself to saving Pandala.\\n\\nBut don't listen to me; just continue your story.","content.75.5269":"So you've seen your first temporal anomaly.","content.75.5270":"In the face of adversity, we often discover new things about ourselves. You probably made more progress than you thought by facing this enemy. The links you forged with Pandora have also been of great value to you...\\n\\nNow, the world is plunged into a state of stasis. You alone{[1*]?:} can interact with it. But what would have happened if you'd lost? What world would we have inherited? The implications are terrifying.","content.75.5271":"To be honest, we shouldn't even be aware of this phenomenon. If he'd gotten his way, everything would have changed instantly. For better or for worse, we'll never know.","content.75.5272":"*Wolfram nods*\\n\\nYou told me a great story, [#name]. Your adventures and the links you forged with your world have satisfied me and brought back many memories. Anyhow, I apologize in advance if what I say hurts you, but... I need more.","content.75.5273":"True, but your story has reinforced my certainties. A shadow looms over your destiny, [#name]. This shadow is a terrible secret that no one must know...","content.75.5274":"*Wolfram chuckles cheerfully, eyes closed*\\n\\nLet's get back to your story back for a moment... It began in your last incarnation, didn't it?\\n\\nBut when was it precisely?","content.75.5275":"What were you doing before? Who were you?","content.75.5276":"Why did the gods put you in charge of getting their forgotten knowledge?\\nXelor had many faithful servants, including Pandora and Septangel. Why did they have to go through you?\\nHow did you guess Pandora's intentions? How did you grasp the concept of temporal scars so easily?\\n\\nHow did you manage to activate the Water Clock in the Shhhudoku Kingdom? It's a technical process that requires thousands of years of studying, or the gods' knowledge, which you didn't yet fully possess. Many mortals have tried to stop time, or turn it back, but they never managed to turn it back by more than a few minutes.","content.75.5277":"You managed to get a Primordial Dofus and use it...\\nYou acquired and mastered the Artifacts of the Ten...\\n\\nEverything will appear to you when you fulfill the prophecy, [#name]. You will understand that all this is just the beginning...","content.75.5278":"It's my duty to tell you that a second prophecy exists.\\n\\nOn the tablets at Rushu's palace, it's written that a hero will reveal themself and will be the only one to wield the Artifact.","content.75.5279":"This prophecy dates from a long-lost age. It originated long before memories were written, long before memories were passed on.\\n\\nIt was given by a forgotten being whose power rivaled that of the most powerful Shushus...\\n\\nIf it is written that a hero will reveal themself and be the only one to wield the Artifact, then I think that hero is you.","content.75.5280":"True... That's not the point of this prophecy. You'll have to find the last Artifact and use it.","content.75.5281":"*Wolfram chuckles softly*","content.75.5282":"If you want to fulfill the prophecy, then you must find the scepter of eternity. Alas, it was lost thousands of years ago... lost and forgotten, like the entity whose existence I was just talking about.\\n\\nBut there's a place where it can still be found.","content.75.5283":"This scepter holds the power to materialize memories. If you manage to materialize this lost memory, then it'll disappear from all memories.\\n\\nThere is a passage in the Shushu Dimension. A kind of connection to another dimension. A bit like the Sadida Amalia's crozolilies.\\nIf you manage to activate it, then you might be able to reach that other world... that other forgotten dimension.","content.75.5284":"I'm not sure. It's a whole other world, after all. Truth be told, you may never come back.\\n\\nBut if there's any hope that you'll find the scepter of eternity, then we must seize it.","content.75.5285":"*Wolfram takes a deep breath*\\n\\nI'm well aware. What I'm asking of you is immoral. From a certain point of view, we're about to condemn one world to benefit yours. But do you have any other choice? After all, this world is only an afterglow, an already-obscured possibility.\\nIt's already a miracle just to have this chance. We must seize the opportunity now if we're to fulfill this prophecy.","content.75.5286":"It's up to you to find that answer. You're the hero of the prophecy, after all.","content.75.5287":"*Wolfram looks at you questioningly*\\n\\nDown here, we constantly have to make difficult decisions. You told me your story too, so I know you made many compromises.\\n\\nBut there are many problems that require everyone's attention all the time. Look at Sufokia. You've got the council of merchants, silting-up, Taurs... and rumors of a prince in an underwater city. The world's ecosystems have passed the point of no return. And no one's aware of it anymore... What's the point in trying to save the World of Twelve from the Eliocalypse if no one can \"do their part\" for the world around them?","content.75.5288":"The winner remains and the loser is eliminated from history. A bit like those obscured worlds.\\n\\nThey're perfectly wise words. And so is the cycle of life, like the tides tirelessly gnawing away at the earth and making the shells of dreams wash up on the beach.\\n\\nWe can't do anything about it. One day or another, someone will take your place in the spotlight and write their own chapter in history.","content.75.5289":"I don't know, [#name]. A god or a demon? A very powerful being? This scepter influences memories. Maybe its creator wanted to forget something at all costs... or remember something...\\nIt was destroyed or lost a long time ago in your current world.","content.75.5290":"Who knows? I doubt anyone knows. Plus, we'll have forgotten everything soon enough, won't we?","content.75.5291":"The risks? My{[1*]?:} young friend{[1*]?:}... If you don't oppose this phenomenon, I'm afraid that nothing and no one will exist anymore. Actually, it's more accurate to say that nothing and no one will have ever existed.\\n\\nIf you want to see for yourself, just chat with people you know. The worlds are being swept along a course that will cause them to shatter against one another. Memories that don't belong to them are already starting to come back to them.\\n\\nAll these contradictory existences will eventually merge and be erased. Everything you've known will be lost, including that which is most important to you.\\n\\nOf course, I could be wrong.","content.75.5292":"Take care of yourself, [#name]. Don't forget, you haven't faced your most fearsome opponent yet.","content.75.5293":"They're demons all right, there's no doubt about that. But they seem to have traded their corporeal shells and consciousnesses for special powers.\\n\\nThe enigmatic power of oblivion that seems to haunt this area is causing us all kinds of problems.\\nAnd who knows what lurks in the obscurity of the abyss...","content.75.5294":"It seems that the mysterious energy is continuing to devour this world, indeed. We've reactivated the pillars, the magical barrier should slow down the disintegration of this area... But nothing is eternal.\\n\\nIn any case, it's interesting that you found a key fragment. I think if you manage to collect all the fragments, you should be able to make some progress in your quest.","content.75.5295":"Mmm, uh huh...\\n\\n*Arlemia is hesitant to talk to you*","content.75.5296":"Say... I noticed that my father is a little older than in my memories.","content.75.5297":"How can I say this...? My parents, my ancestors were my age once too, right? They had their own lives. They walked their own path, like me.","content.75.5298":"I don't know... I can't remember anything any more, but... I think I want to believe. And it's all because of you... Thank you.\\n\\n*Arlemia turns to look at the dark clouds on the horizon*\\n\\nYou know... I've been in this vast, desolate expanse for a while now. Staring at that black hole that consumes everything. One day, the World of Twelve will be sucked into oblivion too, won't it?","content.75.5299":"*Arlemia stays quiet for a minute, staring at the landscape or rather the lack of a landscape*\\n\\nI see. I have a better understanding of who you are. The World of Twelve is in danger, isn't it?\\n\\nWhat we're seeing here is an implacable force that will reach us one day... I didn't know that such power existed anywhere in the Krosmoz...\\nAll these months in the Shustuft Crust, only to realize now how serious the situation actually is... I'm an idiot.","content.75.5300":"Yes. And my parents gave me this life so that I could grow up and carry their load a little further, continue the work that they did in their lives.\\n\\nThey'll die too one day, and I'll outlive them. At least for a while.","content.75.5301":"*Arlemia smiles just a little*\\n\\nYou're right. One day, I'll return home.","content.75.5302":"I see, you did it. And...\\n\\n*Milo seems like he's about to ask you something, but then changes his mind*","content.75.5303":"Yes, definitely.\\n\\nI don't know if you're a parent, but... It's certainly not always easy.\\nI suppose I should have been a better father.","content.75.5304":"I suppose that's true. I guess even at my age, there are still new things to learn. It's like my mother Nimu Tchatch used to say: You learn from your parents, but you learn even more from your children.\\n\\nThank you, [#name]. For your advice, but also for introducing me to such an incredible dimension!\\n\\nIf it wasn't so dangerous, you can bet I'd go back in a heartbeat...","content.75.5305":"*Kali chuckles sadistically at the sight of you*\\n\\nWell, well, who have we here... If it isn't my favorite little slave!{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}\\n\\nI'm starting to think you might be attracted to all the chains and blood.{[1*]?:}","content.75.5306":"... I didn't expect to see my father here... Well, I suppose we'll get along better with his help.\\n\\nWe'll need to be quick about this. Once we've deactivated the protection around the pillars, this whole place will start to disintegrate. It's the only chance you'll have to enter the Voidivions' temple. Who knows what you'll find in there...\\n\\nCome back and see me quickly once you've done what you need to do, so that I can reactivate the pillars.","content.75.5307":"If you absolutely insist on meeting Rushu, the best thing to do is still to talk to Sthulhu about it.\\n\\nWe've just opened another portal that leads to Fallen Souls' Crossing. It's another remote island, so it should be far from his sight.","content.75.5308":"Hi! Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.5309":"Here we are at Fallen Souls' Crossing... Isn't this exciting!\\n\\nAhem, pardon my enthusiasm. What brings you here?","content.75.5310":"Not really, but you could say that... I can give you quests, as if I myself were a member of the Guild of Hunters, and you will receive fitting rewards.\\n\\nThe resources you bring me and the energy from the bosses you defeat will help me maintain the dimensional portal in the World of Twelve.","content.75.5311":"*Kali frowns grimly*\\n\\nLook at me, you little wretch. Do I look like I want to answer your questions?\\n\\n*It's your choice how you want to respond to Kali. Maybe you can win her affection by not rocking the boat, or maybe you can get her to understand that you won't let her dominate you like this*","content.75.5312":"All right, but just this once. In the future, try to remember that between the two of us, I'm the one who asks the questions.\\n\\n*Kali looks satisfied*\\n\\nI woke up one morning with strange memories about the Shushus... For once, I can't come up with any real explanation for it. And my... siblings... Well, none of them have had these strange visions like I have.\\nI thought I was going crazy, but sure enough, a portal to the Shustuft Crust opened right where I thought it would. Intriguing, no? And so, here I am!","content.75.5313":"I've taken out my anger on plenty of demons in my time. They're charming little puppets, really. In fact, those seem so accustomed to suffering that I had a hard time breaking them... Well, not really a hard time, exactly. Just slightly harder than usual.\\n\\nAfter reducing a whole section of the area to rubble, I realized there was a little problem... I can't draw too much attention by unleashing my full power, or Rushu might start getting suspicious. And my current plans don't include him.\\n\\nTo my immense joy, here you are at last. I can finally get back to my favorite little game.\\n\\n*Kali flashes you a big toothy grin*","content.75.5314":"That's about right, yes. You seem to have come a long way since your adventures on Mount Zinit. Why don't you show me what you're made of now?\\n\\n*Kali leans back against her wall and crosses her arms with an expectant look. You take a moment to look around. This place looks like something straight out of a nightmare. The Sacrier demi-goddess seems pleased to have you in her clutches, but she might also be able to give you some answers about this mysterious place and the key fragment you're looking for*","content.75.5315":"Oh, I've seen worse. The demons here look pretty frightening, but they're not especially dangerous.\\n\\nThey're led by a Shushu named Crateros. From what I gather, he's got a bit of an inferiority complex and wants to get revenge on the rest of the Shustuft Crust. I fought him, but he ran away just when it was getting interesting... Now he's holed up in his dungeon and I have no way of getting in.\\nOf course, I could just pulverize the entire island and the dungeon along with it, but... I don't really feel like taking on Rushu at the moment, especially not on his home turf.","content.75.5316":"Well, well! It seems you've finally decided to speak up for yourself! I liked you better when you kept your mouth shut, vermin. Keep it up and I'll have to teach you some manners. And if you think I was using my full power last time, you're in for a rude awakening!\\n\\n*Kali seems on edge*\\n\\nSee, I woke up one morning with strange memories about the Shushus... For once, I can't come up with any real explanation for it. And my... siblings... Well, none of them have had these strange visions like I have.\\nI thought I was going crazy, but sure enough, a portal to the Shustuft Crust opened right where I thought it would. Intriguing, no?","content.75.5317":"I saw that, yes. At least this pathetic little demonstration has brightened up my day.","content.75.5318":"I had a feeling our goals were aligned.\\nIt so happens that I've already fought their leader... he goes by the name of Crateros. He stole something valuable from me and ran off to hide in his dungeon.\\n\\nYou'll need to find a way to get inside. I'll do what I can to help you. You get your key, and I get back what's mine.","content.75.5319":"The only way to get inside the dungeon is to be taken prisoner by Crateros.\\n\\nSo first of all, we need to find you some chains and a collar...","content.75.5320":"Ha ha ha! Don't be in such a hurry{[1*]?:} now. But your enthusiasm is noted...\\n\\n*Kali bows her head briefly, apparently quite amused by your reaction*\\n\\nThat's not exactly what I meant. Crateros' hideout is protected by powerful magic that responds to his own... tools.\\nWe just need to put some fake handcuffs on you long enough for you to get inside the dungeon. Once you're inside, you can take them off and fight him. Just think of it as a little disguise.","content.75.5321":"*Kali whispers in your ear that you can always keep the instruments afterwards. Then she stands back up and smiles again at your reaction before turning serious again*\\n\\nAnyway. There are two places where we can find what we're looking for. I'll mark them on your map. You'll need to go there and take what you find.","content.75.5322":"Are you sure you want to take that tone with me?\\n\\n*Kali growls and the ground begins to give way beneath your feet. Her aggressive voice stabs at your ears, but you do your best not to look troubled by it*{[1*]?:}\\n\\nThat's not exactly what I meant. Crateros' hideout is protected by powerful magic that responds to his own... tools.\\nWe just need to put some fake handcuffs on you long enough for you to get inside the dungeon. Once you're inside, you can take them off and fight him. Just think of it as a little disguise.","content.75.5323":"If you don't want my help, feel free to try and manage on your own.{[1*]?:} Of course, then you'll have to face both me and the Horridemons.\\n\\n*You realize that you need her help to get into Crateros' dungeon. You nod silently while holding Kali's hateful stare*\\n\\nAnyway. There are two places where we can find what we're looking for. I'll mark them on your map. You'll need to go there and take what you find.","content.75.5324":"*Kali jumps up and sits on her wall to loom over you more impressively*\\n\\nHmm, don't you know it's not polite to ask personal questions? But since you've served me well so far, I suppose I can tell you a thing or two.\\n\\nYou know, I have a certain objective in life... Sometimes it's all I think about. I won't share the details with you, but I've been preparing to accomplish something for centuries now. Still, sometimes I get the feeling I'm missing out on something...","content.75.5325":"If I knew, I wouldn't be thinking about it, now would I?\\n\\nI've had a few rather strange dreams. Very... realistic dreams. When I woke up, I wasn't sure if I was really awake or if I had just fallen asleep.\\n\\nWe always want what we don't have. Well, in my case, I make every effort to get my hands on the things I want, and I make sure that I'm the person I want to be. So I want to crush these dreams and everything they imply.","content.75.5326":"I knew you wouldn't understand if I told you. Why did I even bother?{[1*]?:} Come to think of it, I don't know why I'm wasting my time with you at all, little one.","content.75.5327":"I knew you had a certain interest in me, my adorable little slave.{[1*]?:}\\n\\n*Because you've been remarkably docile and polite with the demi-goddess so far, she seems willing to tell you a bit more*\\n\\nIn my dream... I was living a life where I had never joined the Brotherhood, and was just enjoying a peaceful existence with some demons. I didn't have any grand objectives, no great plans for the world. Just my little place with people who liked me...","content.75.5328":"Pfft, I don't have all THAT much time to waste with you. Last time I checked, you and I aren't really friends.\\n\\nAnd besides, don't you have a mission to take care of?","content.75.5330":"It's not like me at all, that's \"what's so bad about that\".\\n\\nI refuse to be harassed by some demonic magic that makes me feel all sorts of strange emotions.\\nI absolutely refuse to be someone else. I won't tolerate this alternative existence.\\nI went to let out my anger on some demons, but they stole something that belongs to me. I'm going to get it back, rip the bones out of every demon I see, forget all this ridiculous nonsense and get back to focusing on my real plans.\\n\\n*You sense that no matter what you say, she won't change her mind about you or herself. But maybe this is your chance to give her your perspective on things. Maybe your words will come back to her one day*","content.75.5331":"Hmph, as if I care about your opinion, little one...{[1*]?:}\\n\\n*Despite her words, you realize that Kali let you recount your entire vision without interrupting*","content.75.5332":"I can sense a whole horde of Horridemons lurking in the shadows. On my signal, I'll flush them out and we'll fight them together.\\n\\nI'll help you to defeat them. And try not to get in my way, understood? If you're unlucky enough to bump into me, there's a good chance you'll regret it!","content.75.5333":"Right, it's settled. We managed to get our hands on some chains infused with Crateros' magic. With them, you'll be able to enter the dungeon without any trouble...","content.75.5334":"The next step is the torture chamber, of course. We'll find you a nice little collar to put around your fragile little neck...\\nOh, and I'm not going with you. You've proved that I can trust your abilities, even if you're still an insignificant creature.","content.75.5335":"The next step is the torture chamber, of course. We'll find you a nice little collar to put around your fragile little neck...\\nOh, and I'm not going with you. You've proved that you're only good at picking a fight with me. You're on your own, for once.","content.75.5336":"Oh, well, it's about time, you little wretch! You'll finally be able to enter Crateros' dungeon.\\n\\nOnce you've weakened him enough, his dungeon's defenses should deactivate, allowing me to enter. He's about to undergo the most terrifying torture session of his life...","content.75.5337":"*Kali glares at you. In a flash, you find yourself handcuffed{[1*]?:} with a collar around your neck... Your bonds are too tight, and the blood can no longer flow in your wrists*\\n\\nThis is my very last warning, miserable creature. I'm much more powerful than you can imagine...\\nDon't ever try disrespecting me again. Pffft, I'm clearly wasting my time with you, you scoundrel{[1*]?:}...","content.75.5338":"That's an interesting proposal! So, we can torture Crateros together. Unless you want to undergo the session as well? That should be fun!\\n\\n*Kali bursts out laughing and then kicks you. It's just powerful enough to make you stagger*\\n\\nWhat are you still doing here, you little wretch? Hurry up and go to the dungeon! Are you going to waste even more of my time?","content.75.5339":"Mission accomplished, yes.\\n\\nThose wretches gave us a hard time. I mean... It made me even happier to break them. And I must admit, you just won't die no matter what situation you get yourself into. You're really quite stubborn, aren't you?","content.75.5340":"At least we achieved our goal.\\n\\nOur working together hasn't been ideal. However, I think I'll get the opportunity to put you back in your place some other day... If you survive until then.\\n\\n*You didn't totally offend Kali, but you didn't kowtow to her either. On reflection, it was probably the best thing to do*","content.75.5341":"Just a second. Since you got{[1*]?:} here, you've behaved{[1*]?:} extremely rebelliously and insolently. If you wanted problems so badly, you should have come and told me straight up. You didn't really think I was going to let you leave like that, did you?\\n\\n*Kali raises her eyebrows. Without you seeing them, chains surround you and immobilize you*\\n\\nNaughty {[1*]?girls:boys} deserve appropriate punishment. For you, it will be a little time in the interstellar void. Don't worry, it won't be painful...","content.75.5342":"No, I'm only joking.\\n\\n*Kali places her hand on your torso, and you are thrown{[1*]?:} across the whole Shustuft Crust at an unbearable speed*\\n\\n*Your eyes can no longer follow the scenery around you, and very quickly, you can no longer make out the Citadel of Horror. You have a vague sensation of moving through different worlds, but your mind has stopped responding; the pain from the speed of the ejection stops you from thinking*\\n\\n*After a few rather intense minutes, you land violently at Fallen Souls' Crossing. Fortunately, the chains come off and you seem to be in one piece. A few long seconds go by, and your mind somehow gets back on track*","content.75.5343":"Tell me, you little wretch, are you sure{[1*]?:} you want to leave? Since you got{[1*]?:} here, you've done nothing but respect and serve me by being very... docile... I must admit, it's quite flattering to see an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} who's so powerful{[1*]?:} and proud{[1*]?:} being totally helpless{[1*]?:} in my presence.\\n\\nBefore you leave, why not spend some quality time with me?{[1*]? I don't mind that you're a woman...:}","content.75.5344":"I see.\\n\\n*Kali seems a little disappointed, but since she's sure of her hold over you, she brushes your face with one of her nails*\\n\\nYou know where to find me if you change your mind.","content.75.5345":"I knew we'd get along well...\\n\\n*You spend the evening with Kali. Or rather, the closest thing to an evening. Any notion of time slips through your fingers like so many drops of blood. This macabre and scarlet universe has been making you lose your mind since you got here*\\n\\n*Kali serves as your only point of reference. Sometimes harsh, sometimes reassuring, this powerful Sacrier with a tortured mind graces you with her divine presence*","content.75.5346":"*Although her barbarity and cruelty seem supernatural, you realize there is more to this character. Born in a world in perdition, endowed with a power that could make Ogrest tremble, there is a clever mix that could drive anyone in her place crazy. The fact that she never mentions her past or her Machiavellian plans is no coincidence... You sense deep denial from Kali*\\n\\n*You might not approve of all her choices, but Kali still helped you{[1*]?:} in her own way several times. First on Mount Zinit, then on this strange island in the Shustuft Crust. You could never believe that a person would do this out of pure sadism*\\n\\n*You sometimes discern sensitivity in Kali's looks and pouts. Some reactions could maybe even be interpreted as fear. You still don't know what it was that Crateros stole from her. The fact that she attaches so much importance to it makes you think that she may have a small, fragile heart hidden behind all this tyranny*\\n\\n*Or perhaps you, yourself, have gone just as crazy{[1*]?:} after all your adventures, to the point that you can no longer tell black from white*","content.75.5347":"*You find yourself thinking about the nature of existence. Centuries have passed, and with them, so many people you will never know, so many faces, so many thoughts lost in the ether. The Krosmoz and its dimensions are endless. No one can ever know everything, explore everything, know everything. Everyone is limited and dependent on the actions of others to survive*\\n\\n*But you found Kali. Like two pieces of the same puzzle, you are part of a whole, and providence demanded that you be side by side in the grand scheme of things. One serving the other, to enable perfect balance, an eternal and sumptuous alignment*\\n\\n*After a few hours have passed, you decide to go your separate ways without saying a word, taking with you the secret of your discussions*","content.75.5348":"It's not good to linger here, kiddo{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nThis landscape riddled with inconsistencies could end up corrupting you too.","content.75.5349":"Well well, I caaan't say it's every daaay you come aaacross aaan aaadventurer.\\n\\n*This strange person seems to have a peculiar accent; he strongly emphasizes As*","content.75.5350":"Looks like the catch was good. This should be enough for a few more rituals...","content.75.5351":"*Goultard begins to laugh out loud*\\n\\nHeh heh heh, what did you expect? I saw light, I went inside, and I beat up demons!","content.75.5352":"Who knows? We are somewhere in the Shustuft Crust, far from Rushu's gaze. But this land's history has vanished... from memory.\\nWe are left with only our senses to interpret what happened here and what now remains.","content.75.5353":"Oh, I see! So you're trying to get to Rushu's palace. You sure are ambitious, kiddo{[1*]?:}!\\n\\nBut if you want my personal opinion, you're not yet ready{[1*]?:} to take on a being of that caliber.","content.75.5354":"*Goultard stares at you in silence and then bursts out laughing loudly. He laughs himself to tears, rolls around on the floor, and hits the ground theatrically*","content.75.5355":"Nothing! Oh, nothing at all! Nothing except you'd have to be doggone oblivious{[1*]?:} to ask me something like that. Trust me, kiddo{[1*]?:}, I'm not just any old coach...\\n\\nI mean, it'll always let me kill time. I have three life lessons for you. I'll gladly give you them if you survive my trials. Let's start with a little warm-up.\\nDefeat ten of those weird demons so I can see what you can do. From there, we'll set up your real test.","content.75.5356":"Whoa, kiddo{[1*]?:}, if you don't like what I'm telling you to do, you can always go back and train with Old Joe.","content.75.5357":"Less questions, more fighting! Right, go beat up ten demons for me!","content.75.5358":"You got a problem, kiddo{[1*]?:}?\\n\\nSometimes I see you staring off into space like that, looking absentminded. Are you sure{[1*]?:} you're okay?","content.75.5359":"Yes, this place is quite strange, I must admit.\\nWho knows? We are somewhere in the Shustuft Crust, far from Rushu's gaze. But this land's history...\\nI have three life lessons for you... well, more fighting.\\nI really like apis...","content.75.5360":"I don't understand what you're saying.","content.75.5361":"I don't understand what you're saying.","content.75.5362":"Marvelous! We can step it up a notch!\\n\\n*Goultard speaks to you unintelligibly. His words get mixed up and make no sense. Sometimes his lips move but no sound comes out. Instead, you hear his words echoing unnaturally loudly in your ears as he looks away vacantly with his lips closed tightly*","content.75.5363":"*A moment of clarity hits you both, and normal conversation resumes*\\nWell, kiddo{[1*]?:}, I don't know what to say. This place seems very harmful. I think we'll put your training aside to resolve the situation here...\\nOr rather, you can imagine that what you do here will be part of your training!","content.75.5364":"Calm down, kiddo{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nThis will be your first lesson... You must always stay in control, no matter what the situation. Stay focused{[1*]?:}. Don't succumb to emotions; be stronger{[1*]?:} and draw strength from them. Use your fears and weaknesses as a weapon.\\n\\n*Goultard takes a deep breath and closes his eyes. He then places his hands around your face. The warmth and gentleness of his palms give you a very comforting and soothing sensation. You gain clarity and alertness*","content.75.5365":"He who controls his mind controls his body. I dispelled the doubts in you and illuminated your eyes. That's all I can do to help you right now, so you'll have to learn how to do it on your own if the same thing should ever happen again.\\n\\nRight, quickly go find out what's wrong with this territory.","content.75.5366":"Yes, that would make sense. Then again, I don't know if Rushu is capable of feeling fear.\\n\\nDid you notice anything else? Anything special about those demons?","content.75.5367":"The roots... I see. Of course!\\n\\nWell done, kiddo{[1*]?:}. I think I just figured out what's going on here.\\n\\nEyes have been watching us everywhere since the beginning... But whose eyes are they?","content.75.5368":"*Goultard closes his eyes and shakes his head, barely cracking a smile. Then he waves his index finger and looks you in the eye*\\n\\nWhat if this whole island was just a big Shushu?\\n\\nI mean, it could change its shape to fool us. I'm sure that all these eyes everywhere belong to one and the same entity.","content.75.5369":"Come now. As with any creature, there is a weak point. I'm sure there's a place where some kind of brain lurks. However, it's bound to be well protected. It will be up to you to find out where it is and how to exterminate it...","content.75.5370":"Well, no, that would be cheating, kiddo{[1*]?:}! You wanted training, didn't you? See this as a step in the process!","content.75.5371":"In that case, I'd say you're ready{[1*]?:} for your second lesson!\\n\\nI already told you that you must control your emotions, which also applies to pressure, obviously. Great adventurers, of which you are one, often carry the fate of the world on their shoulders. It's quite difficult knowing how to deal with these sometimes superhuman expectations. I can tell you I've seen many adventurers cave in and collapse under the pressure.\\n\\nEveryone must find their own solution. Some prefer to remain calm and methodical, while others constantly externalize everything. \\n\\nAs always in life, the goal is to adapt, stay calm, and believe in yourself.","content.75.5372":"Well done, kiddo{[1*]?:}! Now that's some fine hero work done right if I ever saw it!\\n\\nI don't think I have much more to teach you.","content.75.5373":"*Goultard puts his hands on his hips and nods with a conquering look*\\n\\nI'm sure that if you look into your heart, you will find this lesson.","content.75.5374":"Hahaha! You're really way too funny{[1*]?:}, kiddo{[1*]?:}! You remind me a little of my disciple, Dally...\\n\\nTake this as advice rather than a lesson. You'll never learn more about yourself than when faced with adversity. You can't toughen up or gain experience if you don't face enemies or difficult situations. That's how you grow. That's why you shouldn't run away from them.","content.75.5375":"Sometimes you lack courage, sometimes you wait and forget. Sometimes you envy people who are more talented, sometimes you envy people who are luckier, who were born under a lucky star. I'm sure you've already told yourself many times, \"but I've never done that, I don't know if I can do it\".\\nBut no one will ever hold it against you if you don't know something!\\nWhat really matters is wanting to know something and wanting to face the difficulty in order to constantly grow.","content.75.5376":"You know, self-improvement never ends. There will never be a time when you're perfectly happy{[1*]?:} with yourself, when you have no room for improvement. You can always do more. Everything you do should bring you closer to your ideal self.\\n\\nAnyway, if you want my opinion, that's the very essence of life: progressing, becoming a better person, having positive impact around you. And to progress, you must constantly face adversity, enter into debates, explore the unknown, take your courage in both hands, and try new things.","content.75.5377":"You're welcome, kiddo{[1*]?:}. I hope you liked my little lessons!","content.75.5378":"Oh, well, maybe I'll go visit my buddy, Rushu. I don't really know.\\nDally is starting to get big enough to travel. My current situation isn't easy; I may have to leave him alone for a while...","content.75.5379":"I've got a little passing illness. It's nothing serious, I can assure you. Maybe I'll take a few years of quiet retirement to recover from it.","content.75.5380":"Hahaha! We don't have a lot of time, kiddo{[1*]?:}, never forget that. Right, get back on the road, and quick!","content.75.5381":"*His accent immediately vanishes*\\n\\n[#name]? Is it you? That's a surprise! Heh heh, things are going to be a lot of fun soon enough.","content.75.5382":"Yes, I know who you are. I already saw you{[1*]?:} in the past, many times, even.\\n\\n*The strange demon greedily bites into his mushroom*\\n\\nWell, past... Time doesn't flow the same way in our eyes.","content.75.5383":"*The demon looks at you inquisitively*","content.75.5384":"My name is Badd'Luk. Rushu sent me here to supervise this territory. I'm supposed to provide the administration with a detailed report of any abnormal activity that might occur here and prevent risks and dangers to any entitled Shushus...\\n\\n*Badd'Luk bites into his mushroom again and eats noisily in front of you. One look at the horizon is enough to realize he's telling you nonsense; this place is full of abnormal activity*","content.75.5385":"Don't worry, it's just my little way of having fun. And it's not criminal law, but administrative law.\\n\\n*You notice that Badd'Luk doesn't seem determined to take his supervision duties very seriously*","content.75.5386":"It's not as funny if I tell you why now. Come back and see me once you've got the reference. In the meantime, even though I know you're always rushing headlong into trouble, I didn't expect to see you here. Are you looking for something?","content.75.5387":"Under normal circumstances, I would be quite willing to help you, especially if it's for an{[1*]?:} old{[1*]?:} friend{[1*]?:} like yourself.\\nBut I must say that I can't grant your request at the moment. I am an agent assigned to supervising this Kingdom, and I have no intention of upsetting the order in my territory.","content.75.5388":"Do you want to get into administrative law? I wish you good luck... In all honesty, and I'm saying this for you, I don't think you'll manage to make me guilty of anything.","content.75.5389":"Damage to third parties that may be attributed to insufficient supervision of demons may give rise to action for compensation on the part of the victim, their legal representatives, or their beneficiaries. However, the Demonic Kingdom can only be held liable when it is shown that the damage is attributable to a lack of supervision.","content.75.5390":"That means the administration is never responsible and you can always sit on it.","content.75.5391":"I can't wait to hear it.","content.75.5392":"Interesting. However, it is up to the plaintiff to establish that the mushrooms were actually fermented.\\n\\nIf the plaintiff fails to provide such evidence, they will be sentenced to pay a fine of 10,000 fights to death in the Arena for the benefit of the Kingdom, notwithstanding a prison sentence of 500 years.","content.75.5393":"Yes, yes, I know, alright!\\n\\n*Badd'Luk calms down again, confident that he can get out of this situation by helping you*\\n\\nLet's make a deal. You're looking for a key fragment to enter Rushu's palace, aren't you? I know where it is, and I know a lot about the history of the Shushus who live here.\\n\\nI'll tell you everything, and in exchange, you'll keep quiet about my activities.","content.75.5394":"Rushu originally had nine siblings, and they formed a group of ten.\\n\\nRushu established himself as the supreme ruler of the Shustuft Crust when he tried to murder every last one of his siblings. The event dates from the creation of the World of Ten, roughly. Let's say that he took over this dimension by force and crushes the slightest hint of rebellion.\\n\\nHowever, he is far from being unanimously accepted.","content.75.5395":"Long ago, the Kingdom of Despair was one of the territories controlled by Vaal'Enthia. She is a demon queen and Rushu's sister. She was killed at the same time as the others, but managed to reincarnate here...\\n\\nCorruption promised to just reincarnate her and help her achieve her plans. Nevertheless, she corrupted the whole area and all the demons so she could draw more power from them. I don't know if you're aware, but Corruption becomes stronger by perverting minds and matter.\\n\\nBecause of the pact they made, Vaal'Enthia is now greatly weakened and is locked in her palace forever.","content.75.5396":"No, he doesn't know what's going on here and on other forgotten islands in the Shustuft Crust. He secretly sent several supervisors such as myself to supervise his siblings' resurgence.\\n\\nAs for me, I've spent several centuries here, and absolutely nothing has happened... I was alone, forgotten, without anyone to talk to. So all this fuss about Corruption and Vaal'Enthia made me quite happy.","content.75.5397":"I don't know how Corruption got to the Shustuft Crust, but I do know that he had a very specific goal: resurrect Vaal'Enthia and raise an army of demons. Of course, he threatened to kill me if I reported to Rushu.\\n\\nThen he resurrected Vaal'Enthia, though I don't know how... And they both started living together.","content.75.5398":"I'm not going to spell it out for you. They were quite close... Well, that's what it looked like to me, from afar. Who knows what really happened between them?\\n\\nStill, Corruption eventually left this place and left Vaal'Enthia to rot in despair and corruption.\\n\\nI'm happy with that. The Shushus haven't lost hope of one day taking revenge on Rushu AND the Horsemen, which is why they bribe me with card games and bits of mushroom, all so I won't reveal anything to Rushu. In short, for now, this whole situation is mutually beneficial to us... There's little chance of Vaal'Enthia ever leaving her palace, after all.","content.75.5399":"He's being held in Vaal'Enthia's palace, of course. I should warn you, it's more of a theoretical palace. It's a real ruin. I'll give you the key to enter... Here.\\n\\n*Badd'Luk gives you the key to the Phytomorph dungeon, but you get the feeling you could have entered it anyway since there is no lock. You don't know why you think that. It's like you were struck{[1*]?:} by a memory that came out of nowhere*\\n\\nTake care of yourself. And don't forget the terms of our agreement...","content.75.5400":"*Badd'Luk sighs, obviously annoyed*\\n\\nI don't know what else to tell you, [#name].","content.75.5401":"Well, I owe you at least that much.\\n\\n*Badd'Luk grabs another mushroom and turns it over in his hands*\\n\\nThe king of the Shushu originally had nine siblings.\\nHe coldly eliminated them around the time the World of Ten was created. As you have seen, there are still some regions that are independent or still controlled by the servants of the former sovereigns.","content.75.5402":"That's right. Let's take an example.\\n\\nThe Citadel of Horror is under the rule of Crateros, who was an executioner working for one of Rushu's brothers. He leads his own quiet life far from Rushu's gaze. It's strange that he didn't try to suppress those rebellious territories. Perhaps he feels some reluctance to look at them, or his excessive pride makes him not care about them at all.","content.75.5403":"The repulsive-looking Demon King? I admit I didn't keep in touch with him. He doesn't seem to be in Externam anymore, but I really don't know if he reincarnated.","content.75.5404":"He could very well have reincarnated as a nightmare. Still, I don't know what the situation is now. The fact is that some demon kings that were thought to have vanished have been resurfacing for a few centuries.\\n\\nI think Rushu's authority will be put to the test very soon.","content.75.5405":"That's a difficult question to answer. Those who managed to survive or reincarnate are very discreet. Mongrelamus survived in a strange form and is still active. Helzbeth is... Well, I'd rather not say.\\n\\nWhat you need to know is that all these siblings are trying to come back.","content.75.5406":"She's a demon queen who sows despair in her enemies. She controls the corrupted vegetation and uses the terrain as a weapon. You must be careful of the terrain and the corruption surrounding it when you face her.","content.75.5407":"Oh, I don't think she's really dead.\\n\\nIn a few hours' time, her pact with Corruption will bring her back to life. She already tried to end her life several times, but without success. I don't think that fight changed anything for her, other than taking away a little bit of hope.","content.75.5408":"You know, demons are creatures like everyone else.\\n\\nMany have flaws or are sadistic. Nevertheless, many of them are simple living beings who have lost something dear to them, or who are looking for something important in their lives.","content.75.5409":"*Badd'Luk thoughtfully bites into his mushroom and chews while pouting*\\n\\nOh yes, I must have mistaken you for someone else.","content.75.5410":"And you didn't think I might have been deceiving you from the start? It's funny that you talk about deception whenever you don't like something. You've got a lot of progress to make if you want to keep spending time around Shushus...","content.75.5411":"*The demon remains unfazed. The terror that was previously inside him when you threatened to him is long gone. What if it was all just a joke to him? The thought crosses your mind*\\n\\nOh yes, could you also wish him a bad day from me?","content.75.5412":"What are you doing here, mortal{[1*]?:}? This is no place for Twelvians...\\n\\n*The demon sighs and looks you up and down half-heartedly, then he shrugs before inhaling disdainfully*\\n\\nWell, maybe it's fate. You could help me...","content.75.5413":"*The demon interrupts you shamelessly*\\n\\nNice? Me? How hellish... I finally meet a{[1*]?:} Twelvian{[1*]?:}, and {[1*]?she:he} does nothing but bluster in front of me.\\n\\nYou know what, you wretch? I'm going to tell you about my tragic past, and you'll see who's the nicest out of us two.","content.75.5414":"*The demon ignores you and begins talking about his tragic past*\\n\\nIt all started when...","content.75.5415":"I made a pact with Helzbeth. I had to make souls cross the river Ch'Tyx until I drowned. After that, she would have given me the life of a Twelvian again.\\n\\nAlas, I am physically unable to drown... and Helzbeth isn't here anymore. I'm trapped and I have to keep being the ferryman.","content.75.5416":"*Val'Ture's voice becomes depressing and tired*\\n\\nThere are several myths about the origins of the Ch'Tyx. Some claim it was a huge demonic snake; some think it's one of Thanatena's nightmares...\\n\\nStill, this river flows through part of the Shustuft Crust, including this island, and then reaches Akeranzu.","content.75.5417":"I was getting to that. Akeranzu is a river that links the material plane, the infernal plane, and Externam...\\n\\nAt first, the Ch'Tyx cast dead demons into the river Akeranzu. Now it mainly serves as a means of transportation for the Destroyers. A few souls wash up here... A bit like you...","content.75.5418":"Well, you do have a lot of questions. They're kind of like a demon clan. They're followers of Chaos. They travel the world stirring up mortals and encouraging them to fight.\\n\\nIn 651, they came to the World of Twelve, off the coast of Nolifis. You might have heard about it. They got in a bit of a fight with the Bontarians and Brakmarians, among others.","content.75.5419":"Something like that, yeah. But our leader isn't really around anymore. She's been gone for some time...\\n\\nThat means the Destroyers have been left to their own devices, and let's just say they're still no saints. They're planning a big one.","content.75.5420":"I don't really know to be honest. The fact is that K'abah'al has completely lost it for a few centuries now. I think he ended up forgetting about his past as a Pandawa and was consumed by the energy of chaos.\\n\\nHe's been locked away in his hideout preparing weird rituals for a few decades, which doesn't bode well...","content.75.5421":"I need you to do me a favor. I might as well warn you, the difficulty of the task is somewhere between a suicide mission and an impossible ordeal.","content.75.5422":"I don't doubt your good will, but I don't know if you have any hope of defeating K'abah'al.\\n\\nStart by proving to me that you're not made{[1*]?:} of foam by defeating a dozen Destroyers. We'll talk again after. Oh, and... avoid talking about me; they could make my situation even more... What's the word? Disastrous.","content.75.5423":"All this depresses me{[1*]?:}, buddy{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nYou have no idea how many souls I've picked up over the past decades, and all for what purpose? We're all on the brink of the abyss... Here or in the material plane.","content.75.5424":"Come on, you aren't going to be like that, are you? Life is too short, wherever you are in the Krosmoz. My goal is to return to the material plane, but then what? I wouldn't know what to do.\\n\\nAll the people I knew have been dead for a very long time... All my dreams, my plans, my village, my friends... All of it went to Externam centuries ago.","content.75.5425":"I see I have to explain everything to you. When I die, I will be sent back to Externam like most demons.\\n\\nHowever, since I was affiliated with the Destroyers and disrupted the course of souls of the Krosmoz, there's little chance I'll be sent back to the World of Twelve when I'm judged.\\n\\nSo you see, the only way I have of reincarnating is to do good deeds or make a pact with a powerful being who will reincarnate me themself. In other words, it's not going to be easy.","content.75.5426":"*The demon still looks weary and disillusioned. The island inhabited by the Destroyers is full of energy that you cannot define. An electric atmosphere oppresses you while Val'Ture tells you the rest of his story*\\n\\nActually, I drowned when my rowboat got caught in a storm.\\n\\nIn Externam, I escaped judgment the first time. The Destroyers lured me with lies, and I naively followed them... That was when I met our mistress, Helzbeth.","content.75.5427":"She's so... Eloquent. Charismatic. When you see her, you can tell that she's a creature on an entirely different level. Her presence irradiated me. She blew my mind. It took me a few decades to realize that I'd been manipulated.\\n\\nBut anyway, I digress.\\n\\nUltimately, I found myself in the Destroyers' Nightmare for some time.\\nNow I'm stuck here without any real prospects for the future.","content.75.5428":"Like you said... The worst thing about it all is I know I made the wrong decision landing myself here. I can only blame myself. It's really not an easy fight.","content.75.5429":"Alright, I see you're getting comfortable. Well, I admit it shouldn't bother me either way, but at least there seems to be a tiny shadow of hope with you.","content.75.5430":"*Suddenly, the demon's voice begins to sound frightened*\\n\\nI've been here for decades, doing nothing. Look around a little. Does it sound fun to have no one to talk to, no one to share anything with? I wish I could start all over again. I wish I could go back to what I lost.\\n\\nI wish I could get another chance! To enjoy all those past and cherished moments that I couldn't fully appreciate back then. Please, mortal{[1*]?:}, I don't have time for tricks...","content.75.5431":"*This territory with its oppressive atmosphere seems to be a chaotic mix between hot and cold, solid and ethereal, evil and rational*\\n\\n*You don't see anything welcoming at first glance. Yet, a feeling of tranquility sweeps over you. Everything in the Krosmoz was born from oppositions and contradictions. Wakfu will oppose Stasis for all eternity. If the Great Goddess had conceived a uniform universe, nothing would have a purpose, and nothing would have a reason to be. It is because opposition and chaos exist that reason and harmony are born*\\n\\n*The River of Souls in the distance reminds you of how short life is. Everyone will someday end up on this quiet little river. You visualize yourself among all those mortals who, as they cross it, give up every dream, every hope, and every possibility. On the other hand, you also feel that you are letting go of your regrets, your losses, and your battles. You toss aside your contradictions and become empty, neutral*\\n\\n*You have forgotten all about it, but in order to be reborn, you already took this path. And now something new is being written. Maybe you yourself want to forget everything and start all over again*","content.75.5432":"*The demon regains his composure, relieved*\\n\\nMany souls flow through the Ch'Tyx. Do you want to face K'Abah'Al? If so, you must find a way to get around his immortality.","content.75.5433":"He has one of the fragments of Rushu's Palace key. You want to talk to Rushu, right? I don't know why you got it in your head to go find that peach, but... Anyway.\\n\\nK'Abah'Al has only one weakness you can exploit. However, you'll have to take possession of one of the Destroyers' ships, which are called \"Kar'Draks\". There's a place upstream of this river where you can find what you need to face him on an equal footing.","content.75.5434":"Well, I didn't think it would be that quick. We should go straight to K'Abah'Al's tomb. A{[1*]?:} mortal{[1*]?:} just has to see it to break the demon's power.\\n\\nI suspect that enemies are waiting for us there, so you'll have to be vigilant{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nLet me know when you want to sail to the Tomb of the Forgotten. Oh, and there are several tombs. Maybe after you've finished this whole quest, if you're still alive, you should take a moment to pay your respects.","content.75.5435":"Congratulations, mortal{[1*]?:}. See what you can do when you put your mind to it?","content.75.5436":"Now K'Abah'Al isn't here anymore, the Shustuft Crust and the World of Twelve seem to be protected for a while.\\n\\nI'll wait for the Destroyers to leave and then I can return the Ch'Tyx to its usual purpose.","content.75.5437":"I'll be able to drown in the Ch'Tyx once the spirits of Twelvians no longer pass by this way, thus fulfilling my part of the pact I made with Helzbeth.\\n\\nIt's all thanks to you.","content.75.5438":"I didn't tell you, but K'Abah'Al siphoned off loads of souls to perform his rituals. Those souls were expelled from the Krosmoz because of me... I don't think the Great Reaper will forget all about me so easily. But I do admit I'd have to think about it.","content.75.5439":"Thanks again, and good luck with your quest. I hope I won't see you crossing Akeranzu again anytime soon.","content.75.5440":"*The cold air on this ice floe reminds you of dark times. Your chest rises, suddenly gripped by the painful scars inflicted on you by a formidable opponent*\\n\\n*A shiver runs through your body as you think about the victory you achieved in the sacrifice. You had to activate the Water Clock to defeat the Last Voyager and delay the Eliocalypse. The cost is still indescribable*\\n\\n*You think about Count Harebourg, whom you've face many times, and his revelations about the Eliocalypse*\\n\\n*You think about the god Osamodas, who warned you and entrusted the World of Twelve to you*\\n\\n*You think about the Last Voyager; his cryptic words and ambitious plans still hit a nerve with you*\\n\\n*You think about Pandora, and this time, she's gone for good*","content.75.5441":"Hey there!\\n\\n*Her cheerful smile doesn't alleviate the bitter cold of this desolate place*","content.75.5442":"Straight down to business? Alright, let's not waste time.\\n\\nThe Krosmoz is set to face a great danger... I would go so far as to say the danger is the greatest... Well, ever.","content.75.5443":"*Juspark gently puts her hand on your forehead*\\n\\nI've finally figured out who you are. I remembered. And the World of Twelve will not overlook your existence, Chosen One{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5444":"*This time, Juspark takes your hand. Light passes through your eyes. Colors and shapes appear behind your vision, but you don't understand what it's all about. You could swear you were seeing through two different pairs of eyes*\\n\\nListen carefully, [#name]. Has anything changed recently?\\n\\nSuch as an inexplicable event that happened not long ago?\\n\\nThink carefully. It's important.","content.75.5445":"Focus.\\n\\nYou need to focus...\\n\\nOnly you{[1*]?:} can get there...\\n\\nYou can find them. You can find the anomalies.","content.75.5446":"Focus. Find them.\\n\\n*You try to focus on this chaotic feeling that is overcoming you. Nevertheless, just when you think you've found it, it disappears*","content.75.5447":"*You open your eyes and exhale cold air. You're out of breath, and Juspark looks at you worriedly. Her hand is still clutching yours. You push it away, and you hold your head in your hands, all disoriented{[1*]?:}. Where are you, and who are you? You don't know*\\n\\nHey! Look at me.","content.75.5448":"*Juspark cracks an embarrassed smile and no longer seems to be the same person at all*\\n\\nI didn't understand everything myself... so I don't have any answers for you. All I can do is point you in the right direction.\\n\\nI think you need to find some things that aren't right. I feel like something has changed. I'm sure you can find elements in this world that aren't from here...","content.75.5449":"*A being of immeasurable power stares at you. He's about as surprised as one is at seeing a fly on the wall and wondering how it got in and whether or not to leave it alone*","content.75.5450":"*Rushu stays silent*","content.75.5451":"YOU HAVE MY FULL ATTENTION, MORTAL{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5452":"*Rushu rubs his chin, perplexed*\\n\\nWELL NOW, I MUST ADMIT I HAVE NO IDEA.","content.75.5453":"*A flicker of doubt crosses the Lord of the Shadows' face*\\n\\nWHAT'S THIS ABOUT GOING BACK, MORTAL{[1*]?:}? YOU'VE ONLY JUST ARRIVED!","content.75.5454":"Oh no, [#name]. I've feared this moment for so long... So, you've come{[1*]?:} to ask me to lend you my favorite book, \"Martial Arts Training Among the Moogrrs: A Treatise\", haven't you?","content.75.5455":"*You can't help but think that you'd have loved to have that book around a while ago. But that's not why you're here, and Otomai immediately senses the determination in your eyes*\\n\\nI can see by your face that that's not why you've come{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5456":"Oh... That's a vast subject.\\n\\n*Otomai leans on his alchemy table, looking pensive and thoughtful*","content.75.5457":"*After gathering his thoughts, Otomai shares his wisdom with you*\\n\\nI've always thought that there weren't any parallel worlds.\\nThe explanation is entirely logical: There's only one Krosmoz, a continuity in which we navigate.","content.75.5458":"They are dimensions in Ingloriom. According to my research, we're in the same astral plane as Ingloriom, but we just can't go there without a specific portal.\\n\\nThere are some very different worlds out there. Take the one you explored in the Ereboria Mines, for example. Who knows where it actually is? Certainly very far away from here. Yet I still believe that it's here, in the Krosmoz.","content.75.5459":"I don't think so. Still, anything's possible in the absolute... But it's a relatively absurd theory, even for me!","content.75.5460":"You're welcome, [#name].\\n\\n*Otomai hands you the book about the Moogrrs. You take it - after all, a bit of reading never hurts*\\n\\nYou know, this is your starting area. I remember your first incarnation like it was yesterday... It could never have been otherwise, could it?\\n\\n*You seem to realize something as you hear these words, but you don't know what*","content.75.5521":"You can go see our Lord Rushu provided you have put together the key from five fragments found in the forgotten islands. There's a statue that lets you go to the Palace where he presides. Don't worry. Teleporting via the statue won't give you away{[1*]?:}.\\n\\n*The demon points to the imposing statue of Rushu nearby*\\n\\nOh, and, let me warn you about something. You'll most likely have to fight him... Hahaha.","content.75.5522":"The key you have does not only open the door. It will also grant a protective aura for you and adventurers accompanying you so that you don't lose your grip on reality too... horribly. Plus, its power brings together some of the power of five forgotten islands in the form of vestiges. You are free to use them or not. It'll give you a little boost.\\n\\nIn addition, it makes its bearer undetectable. That way, Rushu won't be able to locate Fallen Souls' Crossing. Heh heh heh.","content.75.5523":"Rushu is well beyond your skill level; you can't hope to defeat him. But with the help of vestiges, you should be able to weaken him enough to get the answers you're looking for... If he has them.","content.75.5524":"Bad luck, adventurer{[1*]?:}. And whatever happens, don't say you ran into me!","content.75.5525":"Don't say a word... I know why you're here, little Scaraleaf. You want to learn the art of combat!","content.75.5526":"Don't say a word... I know why you're here, little Scaraleaf. You want to learn the art of combat!","content.75.5527":"Hey, cute stuff{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}!\\n\\nDo you want to go through this door? Do so at your own risk! You aren't disagreeable enough to join our group of supervillains!","content.75.5528":"*The henchman chuckles confidently*\\n\\nThe detestable evildoers of Alkatrool need no introduction, or do they?\\n\\nTheir power is equaled only by their malice and ugliness. They were locked up in there long ago... several days ago at least...","content.75.5529":"This secret prison has been locked up tight by a Stasis forcefield. For a very long time... many hours... I've been searching in vain for a way to set them free!\\n\\nIf you manage to get your hands on a Feca Incantation, you might be able to go up against them.","content.75.5530":"Decepticod? He's the most odious of them all, by far.\\n\\nHis hatred for multimen drove him to develop his muscles for years on end. His physical strength is unequalled in the World of Twelve.\\nHe's the one who pulled off the Astrub Bank heist! Don't expect me to tell you where he ran off to...","content.75.5531":"Merkator? He's the most vile of all in the group of supervillains.\\n\\nHe's a former Foggernaut who didn't go with his kind when they moved to their new underwater city. He's obsessional, big time.\\nHe wanted to map the sea floor with extreme precision, down to every exact grain of sand...","content.75.5532":"Lardevil? He's the reason the group is called \"SUPERvillains\" and not \"not-so-nice villains\".\\n\\nThis distant cousin of the Dragon Pig is blind, but he makes up for it with Herculean strength worthy of Goultard.\\nMake no mistake, if he hits you, you're dead{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5533":"Kralaman? Out of all the supervillains, none come close to being as cruel as him.\\n\\nHe's a former Brakmarian war chief who fused with a Kralove symbiote.\\nHe was arrested by a Walker who sprayed him down with liquid soap, his only weakness, to counter his terrifying suckers!","content.75.5534":"Me? Haha, I'm their most faithful henchman, of course! Simultaneously vile, terrible, monstrous, despicable and ferocious!\\n\\nSoon, the entire world will hear about the supervillains' evil deeds. Don't forget my name, I'm...","content.75.5535":"There you are, adventurer{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nI imagine you want to fight me, right? Prove to me you're worthy and bring me the Black Crow's Lair Symbol!","content.75.5536":"*The Black Crow seems to be in very bad shape and is having trouble catching his breath*\\n\\nAdventurer{[1*]?:}... Your timing's perfect! I've finally caught up with the treacherous fool who stole Miranda's things, but he's much too powerful for me!\\nHe knows all my tactics and has perfected them... It's like fighting Korvus...\\n\\nBut enough chit-chat. We don't have any time to lose! You must find the High Wind Plateau Symbol to fight him! Time's running out and who knows what he's going to do with Miranda's undies...","content.75.5537":"*Perplexed, Bay Toven rubs his thick chin*\\n\\nI'm afraid I don't see what you're getting at. What kind of \"behavior\" are you referring to?","content.75.5538":"*Bay Toven looks at you as if you're from another planet. Either way, you've shared your observations so you can cross off that item in the mysterious journal*","content.75.5539":"So show me your strength by defeating some pirates! We'll see if you're tough enough to save Azozu!","content.75.5540":"Hello, quest 1 good, next?","content.75.5541":"Well, well, an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}...\\n\\nWhat brings a{[1*]?:} zero{[1*]?:} like you around here? You'd better have a good reason, or I might just call in my friends and show you what happens to trespassers!\\n\\nThis beach is guarded by the Octopus Crew, so once you're here, you do what WE say!","content.75.5542":"Hello, you finished quest 2.","content.75.5543":"Hi there, {[1*]?Miss:Mr.} Adventurer! It's a fine day today, perfect weather for exploring!","content.75.5544":"Grrr... Get the hell out of here now or you'll regret it. My pirate friends and I fought to take this beach, and we intend to hold on to it!","content.75.5545":"You've got a real cheek,{[1*]?:} asking me that!\\n\\nCire Momore's treasure has already been claimed by the Octopus Crew, Azozu and me, and we're not letting you through! A zero like you couldn't even find your way around the island with a compass!","content.75.5546":"What? Uh... No, I never said that name!","content.75.5547":"So then how am I supposed to know if I can trust you? For all I know, you're just a{[1*]?:} worthless{[1*]?:} adventurer... or worse!","content.75.5548":"Not bad for a{[1*]?:} zero{[1*]?:} like yourself! Maybe you'll do the trick after all...","content.75.5549":"If I tell you, do you swear not to say anything to anyone else?","content.75.5550":"About six months ago, I was still on the island where I was born.\\n\\nI was playing on the beach with my friend Azozu. We were having a great time until a gang of pirates suddenly came charging at us. Before I knew what was happening, they ran up to Azozu and kidnapped him!\\n\\nI waited 'til they weren't looking and sneaked onto their boat to find Azozu, but all I've found so far are pirates' clothes... They had no idea I was a stowaway, and they brought me to this beach... and I'm not leaving until I find my friend!","content.75.5551":"Well, he's got red and black feathers and a green beak, he's really nice, and he's my best friend!\\n\\nWhen the pirates saw him, they said he looked like their old leader, Captain Eval.","content.75.5552":"I've got lots of information on the pirates, so if you free Azozu, I'll tell you everything I know! I promise! Cross my heart and hope to die!","content.75.5553":"There's a camp on the southern part of the island. I think that's where the thieves keep their stuff, so you might find more information there.","content.75.5554":"Not bad... What did you find?","content.75.5555":"He's my best friend! I want him back! You've got to do whatever you can to bring him back here!","content.75.5556":"Az... Azozu...? My friend, Azozu! He's finally free! I've got so many things to tell him!","content.75.5557":"Ah, the information... I'd forgotten about that.","content.75.5558":"From what I've heard from the pirates, the path to Cire Momore's treasure continues on a beach east of here.\\n\\nIt's called the \"Burning Dead Beach\" or something. That's all I know.","content.75.5559":"Well, well, a{[1*]?:} yobventurer{[1*]?:}! We don't see many of you around here, and for good reason... Have you never heard of the curse, then? You'd best run along back where you came from, and quick. You're not{[1*]?:} welcome{[1*]?:} here.","content.75.5560":"Help you? You've got some nerve! Besides, I don't know what treasure you're talking about.","content.75.5561":"I'm telling you,{[1*]?:} my little{[1*]?:} friend, you really don't know what you're getting yourself into...","content.75.5562":"Stubbyobs. I'm a Stubbyob!\\n\\nYob off, will you? I've enough to do without having to deal with stubbin' idiots like you...","content.75.5563":"My word, it's been a long time indeed since I last drank a beer from the continent!","content.75.5564":"*slurrrp*\\n\\nAh, as they say in my country, \"May your tankard never run dry!\"","content.75.5565":"Very nice of you{[1*]?:}, but I don't see what's in it for me if I help you in your search. Not to mention that there's no treasure anyhow, so...","content.75.5566":"You don't know who you're talking to. Plenty of adventurers much bolder than you have tried to defeat me over the centuries. And as you can see, I'm still here. \\n\\nDon't waste my time. The members of my expedition will set your head straight.","content.75.5567":"You're a tenacious one, aren't you? Not a quality you see too often these days.\\nAlright, I'll give you the rundown.","content.75.5568":"Strictly speaking, we're not really a clan. Long ago, a mad queen pillaged the World of Twelve's riches and murdered many of us. We all lost loved ones, not to mention centuries of hard work.\\n\\nSo I decided to launch an expedition with Stubbyob volunteers, and I managed to rally the various clans to my cause, even though we were in conflict at the time. Desperate times call for desperate measures, am I right?","content.75.5569":"One thing at a time. There's a whole lot to say... ","content.75.5570":"We know where it is, but there's no way we can help you. It's impossible to get to it without putting yourself in danger.","content.75.5571":"The treasure is guarded by no other than Cire Momore. You'll be utterly powerless{[1*]?:} against it. No one can defeat it. Many of us have already lost our minds, our lives, or both in our efforts to fight it...\\n\\nBe off with you; this quest isn't worth the trouble.","content.75.5572":"I admire your determination. It's the same determination that drove us to set up this expedition and to keep fighting against Cire Momore all this time. But to tell you the truth, I'm starting to lose that determination now...\\n\\n*inhales deeply*\\n\\nWe've been fighting here for centuries now. We still haven't found any way to defeat Cire Momore. We've lost a lot of brave warriors, and many of the remaining members are slowly losing their minds as this endless struggle drags on.\\n\\nI'm sure you can understand why we're trying to keep adventurers away from the treasure: just so all our efforts don't turn out to be for nothing. For us, it's not just a question of riches; it's a personal vendetta. Ephedra took much more from us than mere gold...","content.75.5573":"I'm weary of this struggle... Exhausted by the bitter hatred eating away at my soul, and by our futile efforts. Sometimes I want to give up. But the fear of losing everything we've built to continue with what drives us... It always comes back to haunt me. \\n\\nHas all of this time been wasted? Is this fight really even worth it? Do our lives have no meaning beyond this delusional quest? It's hard to imagine making a new start and seeking new objectives after pursuing the same ones for so many years.","content.75.5574":"Keep blindly pursuing a dream that's eating away at us and has caused us great harm, or turn the page and accept that our efforts have failed? It's not an easy decision... With each new attempt, we feel we're getting closer to our goal. But then comes failure, disappointment, and frustration. Yet it's that same frustration that drives us to try again. After all, we can't stop now when we're getting a bit closer to the finish line each time.\\n\\nVictory has seemed impossible for a long time now. I don't want to lose anymore.","content.75.5575":"I don't think of it as giving up. In fact, isn't that what true victory is all about? Overcoming challenges, sacrificing for others, and managing to move on afterwards.\\n\\nI'm ready to start thinking about a fresh start. I don't want to spend my life continuing this ancient struggle.","content.75.5576":"I'm ready to help you with your quest. I don't want to fight anymore. Who knows? Perhaps you'll even find a way to defeat Cire Momore...","content.75.5577":"Most importantly, I'd like you to help me convince the rest of the expedition to give up this fight. We might want to think about forming a real clan and finally being at peace with ourselves.","content.75.5578":"Not everyone's as patient and level headed as I am. This ancient struggle has cost all of us a lot...\\n\\nI believe they're preparing a new weapon to go after Cire Momore.","content.75.5579":"We're the greatest blacksmiths in the World of Twelve, my{[1*]?:} little{[1*]?:} friend! A lot of the best weapons and armor are of Stubbyob origin.\\n\\nAhem, anyway... I think you should try some strong-arm tactics to convince them that their struggle is in vain. If you manage to get rid of their weapon, maybe they'll realize that Cire Momore would swat them like so many flies...","content.75.5580":"Thank you. Not everyone sees it this way, but many of my brethren have realized they've been wasting their time, and they're ready to start rebuilding their lives.\\n\\nAs for me, it's time I freed myself from this ancient struggle. For the first time in centuries, I'm no longer fighting alone, and I can imagine moving forward instead of staying trapped in the past.","content.75.5581":"I'm sorry about your quest, but as you've seen, we're in no position to defeat Cire Momore either, despite all our knowledge and experience. I'm willing to help you if you continue your adventure, but I can't guarantee anything. This island is full of secrets just waiting to be discovered. Who knows? Perhaps you'll be able to defeat Cire Momore yourself one day...\\n\\nIn any event, I can only recommend that you stay away from Cire Momore for the time being. Anyone who gets close to it winds up dead at best, or at worst, loses their mind and becomes a haunted shell of themself. That armor brings nothing but desolation and curses.","content.75.5582":"He's not a kid! He's the Macawker I grew up with!","content.75.5583":"Oh, excuse me, {[1*]?miss:sir}. My mom told me to always say that to any adventurers I meet because it puts them in a good mood. I guess I just assumed you were an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5584":"But that's what Mom said...","content.75.5585":"My name's Goomy, and I'm waiting for my parents to come back. Dad went out to explore two weeks ago, and Mom was getting worried, so she went off to look for him.\\n\\nShe told me to be good and wait for them at home, but I thought I might find them if I came here.","content.75.5586":"Oh, hey, wait a second, {[1*]?miss:sir}! My mom gave me this in case she didn't come back. She told me it would be useful \"for someone who seeks the path\".\\n\\nI followed it here, but it stopped shining... It must be related to the horrible monsters on this beach.","content.75.5587":"He was doing the same thing until I arrived. You should go and see what he's leading you into!","content.75.5588":"Fantastic! So, are you going to save them?","content.75.5589":"So they're alive! Thank you so much, {[1*]?Miss:Mr.} Adventurer! Are you going to go find them?","content.75.5590":"Mom said that the next place to explore was to the north of the beach, in the Bitter-Hammer Cavern.","content.75.5591":"I am Berylbell Copperbeard, leader and founder of the Bitter-Hammer expedition. I started this expedition some years ago.","content.75.5592":"Ephedra was a mad queen at the head of an imposing army. With her insatiable greed for riches, she took advantage of a period when the Stubbyobs were in mourning to steal their treasures. \\n\\nThe kingdom of Ephedrya was part of the Archipelago of Valonia.","content.75.5593":"I assume you're talking about Berylbell? That sweet old chatterbox! You know, she's not so bad. It's just that she's seen a lot of adventurers like you come and go over the centuries...","content.75.5594":"We've been here for centuries now to reclaim the riches that Ephedra stole from us and to avenge our fallen comrades.","content.75.5595":"But of course!{[1*]?:} She is a Stubbyob, after all. They live a lot longer than we do. They've been in Ereboria for a very long time now, but as far as I know, they still haven't managed to get what they came for.","content.75.5596":"Perhaps. I didn't really bother with the details. In any case, they don't like it too much when adventurers like yourself come poking their noses around.\\n\\nBut if you're really sympathetic to the cause, I think I may be able to help you...","content.75.5597":"Like any Stubbyob worth their beard, Berylbell will never turn down a pint. Try bringing her an Astrub root beer; it's probably been a long time since she's had a chance to sample one. I'd be willing to bet that'll loosen her tongue...","content.75.5598":"This place is really hopping... I've traveled a lot, but not many islands have an atmosphere like this.","content.75.5599":"My name is Cyross. I come from Albuera, a land not far from here.\\n\\nI'm on a mission looking for the Prince. He goes by the name of Lance Dur. I heard that he'd been seen on one of the islands in this archipelago, but no one here seems to have run into him...","content.75.5600":"No, Albuera. It's the kingdom of the Forgelances, governed by the Count of Albuera. Albuera is currently inaccessible due to Ogrest's Chaos...\\n\\nIf you want to learn more, I'd recommend picking up a book on the legends of Valonia, which tell the tale of how these islands came to be.","content.75.5601":"Hahaha! Come on, don't try and mess with me.\\n\\nI don't know why you think I'd fall for it, but I wasn't born yesterday, you know. Everyone knows about the Forgelances... right?\\n\\n*Cyross suddenly appears hesitant*","content.75.5602":"Where to begin...\\n\\n*Cyross frowns, apparently baffled by your question*\\n\\nWe are warriors who are not loyal to any god, for we are united around the Original Lance. In fact, it would be more accurate to say that we don't expect anything of the gods. They've failed to prevent so many catastrophes: Ogrest's Chaos, the Destroyers... I suppose you could say we represent a new kind of hope for the world. Through our own force of will, we hope to take our destiny in our own hands and protect the world ourselves.","content.75.5603":"No, we're not rebels. We're just ordinary people committed to taking real action.\\n\\nOur motto is to always be ready for whatever situation may arise. Praying to the gods will never lead us to glory or help this world to survive.\\n\\nI don't know what path you've walked in life, adventurer{[1*]?:}. But never forget that the time we have in this world is very short indeed. Only someone truly naive can sincerely imagine that there's a brilliant, unchangeable future laid out at their feet!","content.75.5604":"Our main goal is to become part of the legends of this world and to pass on our heritage.\\n\\n*You can sense this warrior's overwhelming sense of pride when he speaks of his people*\\n\\nLife is short... And we spend it getting ready for battle. Only in death do we truly achieve our destiny. We return to dust knowing that we've made an impact on the world around us. We may disappear, but our actions reverberate for all eternity.","content.75.5605":"*Cyross rubs his chin and squints his eyes. His countless scars and muscular build present an image of a warrior who has experienced terrible battles throughout his life. Even so, he seems to be a man of intelligence, moderation and tact. A unique aura emanates from Cyross, like that of a hero straight out of an old book of legends*\\n\\nI've never heard of it. But it sounds like a fine treasure indeed... Unfortunately, there's only one place on the island where the item you're talking about could be hidden.","content.75.5606":"All I can do is encourage you as strongly as I can to forget all this madness. I'm sure you're a{[1*]?:} renowned adventurer{[1*]?:} and all that, but the creature that guards that treasure is impossible to defeat. And I do mean impossible.\\n\\nCire Momore is a force that no one can do anything to stop. Once that... thing... has decided to steal your soul, there's no escaping it.","content.75.5607":"Well, if you insist, I won't stop you from charging ahead to certain death.\\n\\nThe treasure is guarded by Cire Momore, but first, you should explore the various beaches on the island. You're sure to find a number of clues about the treasure, and who knows? With a bit of luck, you might even find a way to help protect yourself against the cursed creature that watches over it. I sincerely hope you'll find a way to keep Cire Momore from coming after you.","content.75.5608":"OH NO, YOU'RE NOT BOTHERING ME. YOU WALTZ INTO MY PALACE WITHOUT SO MUCH AS A BY-YOUR-LEAVE, AND YOU ASK ME QUESTIONS AS IF WE WERE FRIENDS CHATTING OVER A PINT...\\n\\nNORMALLY I WOULD TORTURE YOU, BUT I'M GOING TO OFFER YOU A DEAL. JUST TELL ME WHICH PORTAL YOU USED{[1*]?:} TO GET INTO THE SHUSTUFT CRUST, AND I'LL LEAVE YOU BE.","content.75.5609":"*Rushu laughs again, and you feel the ground vibrate beneath your feet. He stops suddenly and glares at you with a scowl*\\n\\nENOUGH CHIT-CHAT, MORTAL{[1*]?:}. YOU'RE NOT LEAVING HERE UNTIL YOU TELL ME EVERYTHING...","content.75.5610":"*You look at Sthulhu. Apparently the little demon put one over on you{[1*]?:}*","content.75.5611":"That's right. But as far as you're concerned, this is the end of the road. You've managed to exile him for now thanks to the power of the Vestiges, but indeed, you've failed to truly defeat Rushu. It's a shame... I would have been happy to have you get rid of him for me.","content.75.5612":"You'll get over it! I know it sounds like a cliché, but I did tell you not to trust anyone... Demons aren't known for being sentimental.\\n\\nIt's not like I didn't warn you.{[1*]?:}","content.75.5613":"Take a guess!\\nMaybe I was bored and wanted to have a bit of fun... Or maybe I just wanted to throw some adventurers to the demons, as a treat.\\nMaybe I was trying to sow chaos and disorder... Or maybe my brilliant scheme was to send warriors who were powerful enough to actually eliminate Rushu.\\nMaybe it was all part of my master plan... Or, you know, maybe just a little of column A, a little of column B, and a dash of none of the above.\\n\\nWhat do you think? ","content.75.5614":"And there's that pride of yours again. What makes you think I have the answers you're looking for, adventurer{[1*]?:}? I've got nothing to do with all that. I just found a way to profit off of it.\\n\\nI know there have been memory disruptions happening for a while now. The Conjurer of the Chaosphony may know more about that. But good luck finding her.\\n\\nDon't you think it's time to bring this chapter of history to a close? You've accomplished what you came{[1*]?:} here for. Go back where you came from, you've been{[1*]?:} here too long as it is.","content.75.5632":"What's a{[1*]?:} pleb{[1*]?:} like you doing here? You don't look like a{[1*]?:} worker{[1*]?:} to me...","content.75.5633":"Yes. Our members come from many different clans, but all share a single goal: to take back what's rightfully ours. Or at least, that was our original mission... We've started to lose sight of it over time.","content.75.5634":"Long ago, the treasures of our various clans were all wickedly pillaged by one and the same person. Besides our clans' wealth, many of our loved ones also lost their lives in combat.\\n\\nSo we set out on a quest to avenge them and take back our treasure.","content.75.5635":"Instead of worrying about some treasure, you'd be better off fleeing from the curse that has this island in its grip. Adventurers like you tend to burn out pretty quickly here, although I suppose some of them do rise from the ashes...\\n\\n*Berylbell chuckles sarcastically*","content.75.5636":"Absolutely. The cursed treasure of this island is in fact Ephedra's treasure, which has been hidden here on Ereboria for a very long time. The riches that were pillaged from us are a part of that treasure, and we were dead set on taking it back. But then we ran into an unexpected obstacle... and a big one, at that.","content.75.5637":"Precisely. Death incarnate.","content.75.5638":"Its origin has something to do with Ephedra. Cire Momore was created to protect her treasure. But whatever's hidden inside that armor seems to be a dark tale indeed...\\n\\nI can't get into the details, as there are still many mysteries around Cire Momore, and anything we once thought we knew has grown less certain over the years... All I can tell you is that besides being greedy, Ephedra was also very proud and extremely jealous. Cire Momore is a product of the pure madness that inhabited the queen's mind.","content.75.5639":"I'm not sure. But regardless, it's not a very nice place to live...","content.75.5640":"Remember that we Stubbyobs are used to being able to travel just about anywhere through the tunnels. As it happens, an ancient Stubbyob clan lived in the area, a long, long time ago...","content.75.5641":"Indeed, we just took advantage of the place that was already built to house our expedition. It was another Stubbyob, Nascherite, who led the way here.","content.75.5642":"Nascherite lived on the archipelago of Valonia for a very long time. Legend has it that she's a really important Stubbyob, but she didn't let it show. She probably has strong ties to the Stubbyobs who originally lived here, since she alone could grant us access to these caverns.\\n\\nAnd besides, she's one of the seven Forgelances of the Oath.","content.75.5643":"I don't know. At the time, we had a close relationship with Albuera island, where Nascherite lived. After Ogrest's Chaos, our dealings couldn't continue, and we're even more isolated than before. Nascherite was the only person who could grant entry to Cire Momore's cavern, and she helped us in our struggle. Since then, we've been left to fend for ourselves, and we try to find solutions, but the hope of recovering our riches fades year after year.","content.75.5644":"Get moving! Can't you see there's still a lot of work to do? \\n\\n... Wait, you're not a Foggernaut! What are you doing around here?","content.75.5645":"Hey there, adventurer{[1*]?:}! Be careful, or you might run into one of the gangs of scoundrels that live on this island... One of them could be in front of you right now, and they could rob you of your purse and your life!","content.75.5647":"Well, you don't see that every day... an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} paying us a visit! If someone had told me that...","content.75.5648":"For sure! Actually, living here is even relaxing, but what do you really know about it?\\n\\nDon't you come from the surface yourself? You shouldn't know much about this place.","content.75.5649":"What's going on? {[1*]?:}My dear adventurer, there are no more seasons; that's what's going on... We Fish-Men have lost all hope in everything.\\n\\nWould you have time for old Spriggiss's story?","content.75.5650":"My story took place at a time when the horizon was nothing but a gray glow tinted with green and yellow. Surface-dwellers may think that Ogrest's Chaos was a calamity for them, but it was also a calamity for marine ecosystems.\\n\\nA lot of species that were vital to the ecosystem chain disappeared, causing mutations in many species in our biome. \\n\\nYou must know about the brutality of nature in the World of Twelve... That era was an era of chaos and upheaval from which something new emerged.","content.75.5651":"Several of us went to the surface. We learned how to develop many things, such as a language, a culture, and an interest in reading, traveling, and discovery.\\n\\nAfter a few years, we came to the conclusion that it was vital to forge an existence that was in harmony with the outside world. It was a world being rebuilt, after all.\\nYou can imagine that in the midst of all these calamities, hope has a specially sweet taste.\\nI was then driven not by the mere desire to overcome everything and return to normal, but by the obsession to move on and achieve a much greater and richer ideal.","content.75.5652":"Unfortunately, that's what I'm talking about. For decades, I wandered the world with a group of nomads. They were a group of Twelvians, or creatures who could speak and were intelligent like myself. I learned many things about the Krosmoz and Wakfu. We lived away from the hustle and bustle of the cities, in quite a minimalist way, and we explored the world.\\n\\nDrunk on all that knowledge and filled with this vision of harmony and tolerance, my people eventually lost their place in my thoughts. When I came back a few days ago, I came across this place, just like you did. I'm having a hard time figuring out what's going on, and everyone is ignoring me...","content.75.5653":"It's inappropriate to ask you for a favor when we only just met, but you seem like an{[1*]?:} experienced{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}, and I'd like to learn what happened to this species.\\n\\nCould you investigate to find out more? Sadly, I don't have much to offer you in exchange except for some kamas and stories...","content.75.5654":"*A strange sound of water has been ringing in your ears since you arrived in the area. You can't accurately describe it, but you realize that it is quite removed from the sound of the sea or a river. It is an ominous, sinister sound. In your ears, you feel all the immensity of a cruel and pitiless world, the seabed. The friendly presence of Spriggiss and his wise mind make you momentarily forget this tension*\\n\\nIf only I knew, I would be happy to give you the answer... The Creepers probably use some strange magic they found after I left. I have no idea what it's all about. By extension, I don't know how to prevent the phenomenon.","content.75.5655":"*Spriggiss looks at you, focused on your story. You tell him about your confrontation in the wreckage of a boat, about the skeletons strewn around the hold, and the fact that it was an honest merchant ship*\\n\\n*You can see the decades of thought and analysis that have made this being an extraordinary thinker. He isn't a great intellectual nor a great inventor, but he is an intelligent, inquisitive character who can break any thought down into uncompromising reasoning*\\n\\n*Despite the fact you've only known him for a barely few hours, you immediately recognized this quality in Spriggiss. The way he stands, his bright eyes, and his keen yet calm interest in your story all suggest that he is absorbing everything and is already thinking of one or more theories about the situation*","content.75.5656":"In all likelihood, they're in a state of retribution, or revenge. This isn't an act of protecting their territory, but a deliberate desire to attack Twelvians.\\n\\nFew animal species in the World of Twelve can anticipate, trap, and harass in this way...","content.75.5657":"Whatever the reasons, we must stop them from causing harm. That said, having some idea about the reasons could help us. Always understand your opponent and know how they think to form a good plan.\\n\\nThe information gathered is a good starting point, but their real motive still escapes me...","content.75.5658":"*You tell Spriggiss that you found many abandoned barrels northeast of the area, and the liquid coming from them seemed really toxic. Spriggiss doesn't seem too surprised by this news*\\n\\nIt's probably the Foggernauts' waste.","content.75.5659":"Yes, the Stasili mines underneath Ereboria. I heard them when they got here. They drill day and night. It's exhausting for us Fish-Men because we have an extremely developed sense of hearing, and we're sensitive to vibrations.\\n\\nI'm not surprised they leave their excrement around there. I don't know if you've met them, but they're a people preparing for war. I've seen many of them in my lifetime, and I think only war will get the idea of war out of their heads...","content.75.5660":"I see I don't need to tell you more. War only takes from people. Their bonds, their spirit, and their life.\\n\\n*A pout of resignation falls over Spriggiss's face. He seems to be taking no notice of all this, content with being a mere spectator of the world around him, avoiding confrontation and futile hostility*\\n\\nWhile these barrels may have caused strife among the Abyssal Creepers, I think they would have simply turned on the New Sufokians if that was the only reason they were upset. While you were away{[1*]?:}, I thought for a while, and I may have found a lead worth exploring.","content.75.5661":"The place chosen by their ocean prison doesn't seem trivial. It's a fortress of our... how could I put it? Little civilization. I told you that after Ogrest's Chaos, many of us inherited thought and knowledge.\\n\\nWhile some went to the surface with the intention of staying there, I know others returned to the sea to guide the rest of our people.","content.75.5662":"Once, we were very simple people of the water. We underwent a drastic change after Ogrest's Chaos, but with hindsight, perhaps it was just another unfortunate consequence...\\n\\nThe fact is, our ecosystem was devestated. We had to looks for new food sources. Some of our people became carnivorous. The rest kept looking for aquatic plants or other insects. I was one of the latter. We inherited a long life expectancy and intelligence that enables us to learn, speak, and write.\\nThe carnivorous ones, on the other hand, remained dark creatures, lurking in the abyss, hunting being their only instinct. They became the Abyssal Creepers.","content.75.5663":"I recognize Immaliss's work when I see it. I came here before to join her, because Immaliss and I... had a relationship before she got close to our king, the giant.\\n\\nI think I have a vague idea of the problem. Go to these coordinates and tell me what you find there.\\n\\n*Spriggiss holds out a rudimentary map showing a passageway inside one of the rifts in the area*","content.75.5664":"*As you tell Spriggiss all the names you found in the cemetery, you recognize the shock on his face*\\n\\nSo, Immaliss is dead, just like all the others. I may be one of the last survivors of our species. Now I understand better. I am a mistake, an anomaly...","content.75.5665":"You're having a little trouble grasping the problem.\\n\\nI've lived for centuries. I abandoned my people. All those comrades died because I traveled without worrying about the fact that they too were mortal. Maybe I could have saved them...","content.75.5666":"Come on, my dear {[1*]?girl:boy}; have you never heard of the terrible corsair, Black Ink? I've sunk so many ships that there isn't enough room on the seabed for them all.\\n\\nNow, get out of here!","content.75.5667":"*Cyross smiles just a little*\\n\\nOh, Black Ink, that guy... He's a penniless little pirate. Piracy admittedly hasn't been doing well in the last few years... I heard the last great pirate of the warm seas was defeated five years ago. Their age is gradually drawing to a close. Anyway, he's not a bad guy; I think he was just trying to scare you!","content.75.5668":"*Deeply afflicted by the news, Spriggiss seems to toughen up as he hears your words*\\n\\nYou're right. I still don't know anything about the context here. Our main goal is to stop this conflict before too many people die needlessly. To do that, you must go to the former sanctuary. Out of all the names you mentioned in the cemetery, there are still three that don't have a grave: our king, his second-in-command, Raeliss, and myself.","content.75.5669":"I'm not sure whether our king is still alive. He'd have been able to lead his people to a compromise. Raeliss has always been the most violent of us, so I wouldn't be surprised if he were behind all this... Especially if Immaliss is dead. Raeliss has always been very possessive. He probably flew into a rage and decided to take revenge.\\n\\n*You think this Immaliss seems to have been quite popular among the Fish-Men*","content.75.5670":"Well, I don't want you to disrupt our work any more than necessary. I'll tell you why we're here. You'd better leave us alone after that.","content.75.5671":"You again? Don't you have anything else to do?","content.75.5672":"So it's you! Such a beautiful invention...","content.75.5673":"I'm glad you noticed. I was afraid it wouldn't be big enough...","content.75.5674":"Yes, our best technomages work right there. I don't know exactly what they're doing there, but one thing's for sure: It's something big.","content.75.5675":"What are you talking about?","content.75.5676":"A worksite? Hmm, so that's what all the commotion is... Foggernauts, you say? I wonder what they're doing there, but if you ask me, their presence doesn't bode well.","content.75.5677":"Not just anyone can handle such powerful energy. I know they're used to it, but I have a feeling it could overwhelm us all someday. I'm afraid that mining all this Stasili could have dire consequences for Ereboria... \\n\\n*Cyross is skeptical* \\n\\nWhy take the risk of coming to Ereboria just to mine Stasili? I don't think they're lacking it, though... I have a feeling they're hiding something. It's as if they quickly needed a large amount of Stasis. Maybe...","content.75.5678":"*Cyross listens attentively, looking serious* \\n\\nAnd they're inspired by the most terrible creatures of Ereboria, you say? Hmph... I'm afraid they're not there in peace. Even though they believe in their scientific breakthroughs, that doesn't warrant this kind of invention.","content.75.5679":"I'm sure they are. But by creating these weapons, they themselves are feeding this vicious cycle of the arms race. The ideal world would be a peaceful one where no one would seek out conflict.","content.75.5680":"Don't tell me your whole life story, please. As you can see, I've got other things to worry about right now.","content.75.5681":"So, it was indeed Raeliss... It seems he never managed to completely free himself from his fury.\\n\\nHowever, one mystery still remains: What happened to our king? Did you find any leads in the sanctuary?","content.75.5682":"I see. Raeliss thought that our king was killed by Twelvians. That would explain why he carried out attacks on passing ships.\\n\\n*Spriggiss pauses*\\n\\nNow that Raeliss is no more and our king, the last giant, is gone, there's nobody left to guide the Abyssal Creepers toward a path of peace and harmony.","content.75.5683":"I cannot. Cowardice is part of me; it's been too many decades since I went to my people. I must set off again and take my own path. You're right, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Now that I've helped conclude the Fish-Men's chapter, an admittedly tragic one at that, I will focus on what I have always done: traveling the world.\\n\\nThis time I'll have the memory of my loved ones and the past of my people in my heart. Thank you so much for your help. I wouldn't have gotten far without you, and I'll never forget you. I hope you'll remember me too. May we meet again someday.","content.75.5684":"Oh no... We were so close...\\n\\n*You sense the young Nao in great distress. You recognize the energy that is unique to children, as they experience everything at greater speed. Fortunately, not all the news you have for him is bad*","content.75.5685":"So? How do you want to find where my friend Azozu is with shovels?","content.75.5686":"*The young boy's eyes light up, and he seems to have realized what you were getting at*\\n\\nIf you want shovels, I've already got a few! Here, take them! If you ever run out, I think some pirates have some; you'll have to take them the hard way...","content.75.5687":"*When he sees you, Nao jumps out of his barrel and runs to find Azozu. This is clearly the right macawker. The two friends are together again at last, all thanks to you. The young boy sobs out of happiness and relief. It looks like he'd been bottling up lots of emotions*\\n\\nI missed you so much... I thought I'd be all alone...","content.75.5688":"I think I know what happened! These two macawkers are also friends. Azozu wanted to rescue him and was captured too!\\n\\n*The two macawkers jump around and chirp when they hear Nao's version, as if to approve what he says. The other macawker approaches you and jumps onto your shoulder*\\n\\nHe seems to like you! I think now he's free, he wants to go with you on your adventures.","content.75.5689":"I don't really know... It sounds like a typical pirate gang. They steal treasures and riches, but why?\\n\\nAll I know is that they, like you, are looking for the real treasure on this island. In any case, I'm not interested. Pirates are bad people... No matter what their reasons!","content.75.5690":"Not really... We sailed together for a short time, but they started to acting really aggressively toward Elaine. So we made a hole in the hold and escaped... Don't tell me they're on this island!","content.75.5691":"Hey, what's it to you? Ask me the question once we've raised the bliblis together, rookie! Now, get out of here!","content.75.5692":"I'm willing to give you some time, so make the most of it.","content.75.5693":"I'm a colonel in the elite Foggernaut navy. I'm working with Prince Adal to find new Stasili mines, and sometimes during our expeditions, not everything goes as planned... \\n\\n*Frida sighs, looking grumpy. Despite her skills and elegance, the young woman seems extremely careerist and doesn't hesitate to sacrifice her health to get things done*\\n\\nOne day, I might receive a promotion.","content.75.5694":"You can't say I didn't warn you{[1*]?:}...","content.75.5695":"Unfortunately, you're no match for it. Maybe one day you'll be able to hold your own. You didn't touch its treasure, did you?","content.75.5696":"Many adventurers have been there. Many have asked themselves the same question as you, and one thing unites them all: They have joined the list of Cire Momore's victims.\\n\\nMove on, or you won't come back alive... There are other things to do with your life; facing the inescapable will do you no good.","content.75.5697":"Well, we came to Ereboria to get some rest, get a tan, a vacation, you know... In other words, there aren't generally too many tourists.","content.75.5698":"And you must agree that you're a little too curious{[1*]?:} and that I don't owe you anything. Stay out of our business. I'm already surprised our guards let you through. You should take this opportunity to leave us alone and go back where you came from.","content.75.5699":"We simply came to mine the Stasili found in abundant quantities in these tunnels.","content.75.5700":"All those purple crystals you can see. They're Stasili. It's ore that's full of Stasis. Stasis is a really powerful energy, just like Wakfu. The difference is that we can handle it to use it in our inventions. We're technomages above all else, and when Stasis was discovered, it was a massive breakthrough for our science. The Foggernauts living on the surface of the World of Twelve are machines brought to life by Stasis. ","content.75.5701":"There's no risk; we're professionals. And to be honest, that's not really our problem. Between curses and other monsters, this island is already doomed.","content.75.5702":"Absolutely not. Stasis is much more important to us. We leave that futile idea to adventurers such as yourself. Either way, we aren't doing anything wrong here. You can't imagine all the incredible scientific breakthroughs we might just make with all that Stasis!\\n*Frida seems to be excited with something specific in mind*","content.75.5703":"Grrr, find a passion, an occupation, you know. You're starting to annoy me, and I have loads of work to do here.","content.75.5704":"Okay, listen. I can't give you all the details of our experiments, because they're top secret. In any case, you're not involved{[1*]?:}. And we're doing a load of experiments of all kinds in our complex, so you wouldn't even understand what it's all about.","content.75.5705":"... Yes, we have a complex, a little farther to the east, where we do all kinds of experiments. It's convenient because we don't have to carry the Stasis very far. Anyway, you're not welcome{[1*]?:} there{[1*]?:}, and only authorized personnel are allowed in. Now let me work, before I get really angry.","content.75.5706":"Well, think again. It's not an arms race. Not everything is totally black or white, you know. An invention like Sire Flexington may help us do good by protecting ourselves and preventing wars. It's also a technical feat. Science makes many breakthroughs thanks to military needs. It's the principle of competitiveness. Our intentions really are good, and we aren't creating these machines so we can take over the world or anything of the sort.\\n\\nActually, it's impossible to separate science from the military. By creating useful machines based on energy that's as powerful as Stasis, ill-intentioned people could get their hands on them and use them for evil. By harnessing our knowledge in the military, we are taking the initiative by controlling who does or does not use this energy. You see?","content.75.5707":"That's the case. Unfortunately, we're not the cause of this eternal paradox. We need to prepare for war to achieve peace.","content.75.5708":"We think of science above all else, and our intention is really to advance it to create ever more amazing inventions. All of our comfort in life nowadays is thanks to science. But as I told you earlier, science and the military are inseparable. Our main goal here is not to create weapons. To be honest, we were inspired by the incredible creatures we encountered on this island, and we wondered if we could use them to fight Cire Momore, perhaps.","content.75.5709":"During Ogrest's Chaos, we were already living in our underwater city. Two factions clashed within the city: the Altered Ones, who were atheists and no longer believed in Oktapodas, and the Unaltered Ones, who followed Oktapodas. Today, everyone's beliefs are diverse. Eventually, the Altered Ones formed a militia for the king; the militia was sent to the surface to find new Stasili mines. They are robotic Foggernauts, like you said. They are souls incarnated in technomagical shells that run on Stasis energy, making their minds the only things that are still human.","content.75.5710":"Not exactly. They are indeed Altered Ones, but their technomagical shells are covered by a human disguise. The goal is to prepare for our gradual return so we'll integrate into the surface world more easily.","content.75.5711":"To mine, can't you tell? I've rarely seen such amounts of Stasis! I'll be rich when I get back from this operation! The richest, even! Really, really rich!","content.75.5712":"True. But I'll tell you something very important, my friend{[1*]?:}. We can't get enough! And it's when you're as rich as I am that you realize it. I imagine a{[1*]?:} poor adventurer{[1*]?:} like you doesn't have this kind of problem...","content.75.5713":"So?","content.75.5714":"Hahahaha! You, help our scientists? How naive; it's so endearing. Sorry, but I don't think you belong there.","content.75.5715":"Bribery? Do you have no shame? \\n\\n*Prince Adal feigns thinking*\\n\\n... Okay, I'm listening. What sort of arrangement?","content.75.5716":"Cire Momore's treasure? That's the only interesting thing about the cursed island, besides Stasili... Unfortunately, my companions don't pay much interest in it. All they're interested in is Stasis. And I completely understand, but... a treasure is cool, though.","content.75.5717":"So be it. But how do you think you're going to do that? I heard that Cire Momore was a sign of inescapable death, and that nobody could defeat it.","content.75.5718":"Hmm... It could indeed be possible. You have no idea about everything we can do with Stasis! Alright, then. Here's the code to enter the complex. But be careful: Don't say I sent you, as I could get in trouble... Besides, they might not be as flexible as I am down there. Get ready to defend yourself with whatever you find, if need be. Either way, not a word about me!","content.75.5719":"Don't tell me: I'm not interested. ","content.75.5720":"I'm not turning a blind eye. It's just... I've got something else in sight.","content.75.5721":"It's more complicated than that. I'm not so corruptible, contrary to how I might seem. I just think the world revolves around money, and I need that money to make my world go round. But I don't make the rules.","content.75.5722":"If I'm trying to amass riches and Stasis, it's because I can't get an idea, a fantasy, out of my head. And I need all of that to make it happen.\\n\\nIt's a bit silly, but... I'm afraid of death. That's why I'd like to face it, so I'd never have to fear it again.","content.75.5723":"No. I'm convinced that science can help me beat death. But to do that, I need loads of resources.","content.75.5724":"Perhaps. I don't really know. I just wish science would enable me to face death in some way or another. I don't know if eternal life is the solution. Actually, we already have quite effective ways of extending our life expectancy... I could incarnate as an Altered One, for example.","content.75.5725":"I don't have the answer. In any case, it makes us live differently.","content.75.5726":"I have faith in science. I'm confident that if we make every effort to pursue our scientific breakthroughs, we will always find solutions to our problems. It is this philosophy that enables me to move forward in life without fear or regret. If we do something wrong, science will help us fix it, someday.","content.75.5727":"I guess it's not. My view may change over the years and with experience.","content.75.5728":"I am Adal, Prince of New Sufokia, our underwater city. My mission is to find the Stasili mines alongside Colonel Mofette. And I've got great plans for the future...","content.75.5729":"That's not what I'm worried about. Foggernauts never occupy a place by chance, and let's say... they serve their own interests above all else. I'd like to find out what they're up to. Do you think you can investigate for me? ","content.75.5730":"I'd have loved to go with you, but I already have a lot to do here.","content.75.5731":"Do what you do best if you think it's necessary: the hard way. Show them you're not just anyone. Foggernauts are diplomatic, and if they think you're dangerous, they may try to cooperate with you.","content.75.5732":"Foggernauts are conquerors, and if you believe the rumors, they've been getting ready to return to the surface for some time now. This amount of Stasis might serve such purposes. I don't think they told you everything.","content.75.5733":"Well, I was going to say that I'd go have a look myself, but if you're offering... I'll wait for you. You know where to find me.","content.75.5734":"In my opinion, it's not about Ereboria. Foggernauts are much more ambitious than that. If they think they're ready, they could descend on the nations any day now to take control of them, and clearly by force. This madness must be stopped, and quick. An arms race is never a good sign...","content.75.5735":"You can start by destroying the machine you got hold of in the complex. From what you're telling me, it is terribly destructive, and it sounds like it's purely military. You should be able to find it easily. Maybe you'll be able to reason with them after that...","content.75.5736":"I don't know. Nature has always been cruel, and all living beings have always waged war on one another. It only takes one person to start a conflict, and an unrelenting, unstoppable escalation of tension ensues. Can we really escape this lure of greed and power? This lure has driven our conflicts since the dawn of time. \t\t\\n\\n*Cyross sighs, looking resigned*\\n\\nNow, all I hope is that their operation in the tunnels doesn't disturb the balance of Ereboria. This island could do without that on top of everything else.","content.75.5737":"Get moving! Can't you see there's still a lot of work to do? \\n\\n... Wait, you're not a Foggernaut! What are you doing around here?","content.75.5738":"*Farle Ingalsse takes a few seconds to size you up, suddenly hesitant - then his tone becomes unconvincing*\\n\\nA rumor? Rumors are par for the course around here, pal{[1*]?:}. Move along then - it must be a booby trap...","content.75.5739":"I won't send any more promising young explorers{[1*]?:} to the frontline.{[1*]?:} Don't expect me to help!\\n\\n*You can see that Farle is very reluctant to help you*","content.75.5740":"Well, I'm not so sure - you seem a bit weak to have such aspirations.","content.75.5741":"Well, alright. All I know is that Alibert's looking for someone who can deal with the situation. You should go see him in Emelka Forest. He's bound to be on the lookout there. Lately, he seems to have a bone to pick with Prancing Chimeras.\\n\\nBe sure to try some of his gobball stew - it's the best in the World of Twelve!","content.75.5742":"Good! I knew I'd eventually find someone.\\n\\n*Alibert rubs his chin and then gets a better look at you - his smile and sparkling eyes give way to a perplexed expression*\\n\\nYou sure{[*1]?:} about looking into that? I have to warn you, I've never seen so many adventurers leave and not return.","content.75.5743":"*Alibert shrugs, the slightly gruff big guy indicating he's seen a lot worse*\\n\\nAlright, kiddo{[1*]?:}, I'll tell you what I know.{[1*]?:} Ya see, I'm used to seeing a lot of adventurers stay at my inn. I was once an adventurer myself, so I take the time to chat with those passing through, hear some news, that kind of thing.\\n\\nSo, yeah, I've recently heard stories about mysterious disappearances in the eastern part of the forest. Nobody seems to know what's behind these disappearances, but it must be connected to the growing number of Prancing Chimeras throughout the forest. Perhaps a great beast is at work. If so, the beast we're looking for is a big one.","content.75.5744":"First off, you should see where all those beasties are coming from. It'll give us a clearer picture of the situation.","content.75.5745":"*Alibert looks thoughtful*\\n\\nNo Prancing Chimeras then... How strange - I know what tower you mean. It was once inhabited by four of the most beautiful princesses the World of Twelve has ever seen. It's said they would spend their days letting in suitors by the thousands, only to laugh at their quirks and kick them out in a hail of taunts.\\n\\nTheir tale ended rather tragically when the god Osamodas himself came before them and suffered the same fate as his predecessors. He was so humiliated that he put a curse on the princesses, but unfortunately, no one really knows what the deal is, and the tower's been inaccessible ever since.\t","content.75.5746":"I'm glad you{[*1]?:} want to know, kiddo{[*1]?:}, because you'll have to go find out for yourself!\\n\\nYou could try finding a way to get past that gate. At the very least, there must be some way to go around it.","content.75.5747":"*Alibert turns pale, seeming pained*\\n\\nThe \"Misses Ugly\"? Gosh, I wasn't expecting such a sad story. I suppose that's what happens when you anger a god. So, were you able to find the missing adventurers?","content.75.5748":"Oh my... Those poor souls don't deserve that - we have to rescue them!\\n\\nYou don't have a secret desire to kiss them yourself, do you?","content.75.5749":"Well, I'll be on the lookout until I find that someone. Thanks for your help, kid{[1*]?:}. You gave me very useful information.","content.75.5755":"*The Sacrier, who seems to be the dojo master, stares at you - the silence, previously interrupted by the disciples' katas, is broken after a few moments*\\n\\nWelcome to my dojo, young incarnate{[1*]?:}. I teach the basics of combat to beginners like you. Interested?","content.75.5756":"Perfect! I offer a few beginner-level courses. Let's see what you can do.","content.75.5757":"Hey, new{[1*]?:} incarnate{[1*]?:}!\\n\\nHow can I help you?","content.75.5758":"You can change your class as you like, up to level 30. Are you sure{[1*]?:} you want to do so now?","content.75.5759":"Ask any questions you like, and I'll be glad to answer them.","content.75.5760":"We're on the Celestial Island of Rii. This island is located between Incarnam - where you came from - and the World of Twelve.\\n\\nYou'll find other souls to converse with and other incarnates like yourself. New souls do fall here, although it's pretty rare. Since that describes you, there must be something special about you!\\n\\nMost people use this place to train in Airyna's dojo, which you'll find to the east. Some even decide to stay here instead of adventuring.","content.75.5761":"Alas, my Ghostof form hides a tortured soul that's never managed to incarnate...\\n\\nThat's why I'm dedicated to guiding souls as they seek incarnation. I want them to get the best advice for the rest of their adventure.","content.75.5762":"You're back, adventurer{[1*]?:}. How can I help you?","content.75.5763":"You're back!\\n\\nWhat I can do for you?","content.75.5764":"*Grougaloragran glares at you coldly*\\n\\nYou're back, [#breedName]. Grougaloragran's been expecting you.","content.75.5765":"*Some kind of Eniripsa ghost addresses you excitedly*\\n\\nHey there!\\nI haven't seen{[1*]?:} you around before. Are you a{[1*]?:} newly{[1*]?:} incarnated{[1*]?:} [#breedName]? I'm Hooly, by the way!","content.75.5766":"Hmm, the incarnation process can be complicated. Even though I've spent plenty of time here, I'm not confident about it myself. It makes sense that you'd feel a bit lost{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nShould I start over from the beginning?","content.75.5767":"A soul never dies, even when separated from its physical shell.\\n\\nWhen our souls leave their vessels, they are drawn to a huge stream of Wakfu that flows in Incarnam, and then they reincarnate. We lose the memories of our previous life in that moment. Whether you were a king or a baker in your previous life, you start over from the same point once in Incarnam.","content.75.5768":"Alas, my Ghostof form hides a tortured soul that's never managed to incarnate...\\n\\nThat's why I'm dedicated to guiding souls as they seek incarnation. I want them to get the best advice for the rest of their adventure.","content.75.5769":"We're on the Celestial Island of Rii. This island is located between Incarnam - where you came from - and the World of Twelve.\\n\\nYou'll find other souls to converse with and other incarnates like yourself.","content.75.5770":"Each soul can choose whatever class they want. It's a matter of choosing what deity they want to be a disciple of. You previously chose to be an actual [#breedName]. That choice isn't permanent.\\n\\nAs for me, I can change your class for free up to level 30. Just come see me if you feel like doing so.","content.75.5771":"A soul never dies, even when separated from its physical shell.\\n\\nWhen our souls leave their vessels, they are drawn to a huge stream of Wakfu that flows in Incarnam, and then they reincarnate. We lose the memories of our previous life in that moment. Whether you were a king or a baker in your previous life, you start over from the same point once in Incarnam.","content.75.5772":"*Otomai seems especially cheerful at the sight of you*\\n\\nYou're back! So, how's it going, exploring the Celestial Island? Are you up for the next part?","content.75.5773":"Hahaha! That's right - I haven't introduced myself. Sorry.\\n\\nI'm Otomai - scientomage and alchemist. Don't be fooled by my appearance. I'm several centuries old... Though I've spent the majority of my time studying various life forms.","content.75.5774":"Good! I can tell you about some of the basic concepts that govern this place, if you like.\\n\\nOtherwise, I would urge you to chat with others on the island, as they'll have important information to share and things for you to do.","content.75.5775":"I'm listening.","content.75.5776":"Hmmm... Well that's a peculiar question.\\n\\nYou'd think it was the first time we'd met. But I feel like our paths have already crossed{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nSince you just incarnated, you must've died somewhat recently. To be honest, I don't remember you. We must've met decades ago, maybe even centuries ago, in one of your other lives. Hmmm... Yes, it's possible. Hang on...","content.75.5777":"You wouldn't be one of those adventurers who refused to take my advice about Mount Zinit and were literally crushed by my son Ogrest, would you?\\n\\nHoly Feca's Shield! That was over a hundred and fifty years ago!","content.75.5778":"Sorry for what happened to you and your friends back then... Next time, perhaps you'll heed my warnings!","content.75.5779":"Wakfu and Stasis are primordial energies throughout the Krosmoz. The entirety of our actions has an effect on them.\\n\\nWakfu is the energy generated by creation. It moves through all that lives in the Krosmoz. By definition, it's associated with life.\\n\\nStasis energy, on the other hand, is associated with stability and immobility. By extension, Stasis is generated by death and destruction.","content.75.5780":"Evil? No! But it's a bit more complicated than that.\\n\\nTo simplify things, let's say that Wakfu and Stasis are complementary. Two diametrically opposed types of the same energy. If Wakfu and Stasis aren't balanced, the whole world, even the whole Krosmoz, would be irreparably destroyed.","content.75.5781":"Want me to tell you about the World of Twelve? There's plenty to say!\\n\\nIt's the world I come from, and I suppose you do too. It's filled with thousands of people, a variety of biomes, and majestic landscapes spread across islands. You'll see that for yourself soon enough!\\n\\nIf you want to know the history behind this situation, you can examine the murals. They're in the sanctuary, in the western part of the island.","content.75.5782":"*You notice the silhouette of a Sadida Ghostof, and your heart is filled with the serenity and kindness that emanate from it*\\n\\nWelcome to Rii, [#name]. I hope you had a pleasant journey. Let me introduce myself.\\n\\nMy name is Kheperalia, and I assist Otomai by helping the island's inhabitants to manage its flora and fauna. I'm here to answer any questions that arise about ecosystems.","content.75.5783":"*Hooly chuckles quietly*\\n\\nYes, new souls do fall here, although it's pretty rare. There must be something special about you!\\n\\nMost people use this place to train in Airyna's dojo, which you'll find to the east. Some even decide to stay here instead of adventuring.","content.75.5785":"Maybe not a real dragoboy, but you're doing fine. Here, take this! You've earned it.","content.75.5786":"I appreciate the harmony of the forces around us. That's why I place so much importance on a balanced ecosystem. Every one of our actions has an impact on the world, and believe me, it's not trivial! So learning to maintain this balance is essential.","content.75.5787":"*Airyna greets you*\\n\\nHow can I help you?","content.75.5788":"I see you know how to deal with fauna. Let's move on to flora!","content.75.5789":"All right, then! When you take care of the ecosystem, it returns the favor. Now you can use the resources you've harvested to craft potions at Otomai's workshop.","content.75.5790":"Grougaloragran senses you are unprepared{[1*]?:}. You'll need a lot more experience before you can be considered a{[1*]?:} seasoned{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5791":"That's very presumptuous{[1*]?:} of you, [#breedName]. En garde!","content.75.5792":"The vast majority of zones have an ecosystem. It relates to all the species living inside it, whether animal or vegetation.\\n\\nIt's crucial to ensure that each one is running smoothly. That's how you make life sustainable within each zone.","content.75.5793":"Each zone has a clan master to make sure it runs smoothly.\\n\\nIf especially satisfied with the way the ecosystem is regulated, they can trigger events like unique environmental quests.\\n\\nOn the other hand, if they're not satisfied at all, they can issue sanctions to adventurers who are negatively affecting the zone.","content.75.5794":"Absolutely! Otomai is in charge of Rii's ecosystem. He can also tell you about the worlds around us and the reason you came here.\\n\\nHe tends to be more reactive if the number of monsters in the zone deviates from the average. I'm sure you'll get a chance to see for yourself.","content.75.5799":"*Kheperalia seems concerned*\\n\\nHello there, adventurer{[1*]?:}... Forgive me - I'm worried because Wodents are becoming scarce on the island. Their population needs help to thrive again...\\n\\nCan I help you?","content.75.5800":"*Kheperalia seems concerned*\\n\\nHello there, adventurer{[1*]?:}... Please forgive me, I'm just worried because there are getting to be a whole lot of Wodents on the island. Their population needs to be controlled...\\n\\nHow can I help you?","content.75.5801":"*Within some kind of abandoned greenhouse, you spot a silhouette, its color clashing with the surroundings. You cautiously approach, noticing that it's some kind of vegetable that came to life. It turns toward you and stares before shouting in surprise*","content.75.5802":"*The plant creature gets a grip and looks at you. Then they begin to speak*\\n\\nForgive me, I was startled to see anyone here...\\n\\n*There's a brief awkward silence. You realize the person you're speaking to means you no harm. You take the opportunity to move a bit closer*","content.75.5803":"I'm just as surprised as you are, really. Sorry, all this is still a bit confusing to me as well. My name is Tom Eyto.","content.75.5804":"I promise that I'm not hostile. I take it you're an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}?","content.75.5805":"In that case, our goals may line up.\\n\\n*The unusual vegetable takes a breath*\\n\\nYou see, I don't know exactly who I am or where I came from. I only became aware of my own existence a few days ago...","content.75.5806":"*Their expression turns sour*\\n\\nOur nature really matters to me... I need to find out where we came from...\\n\\nI'm glad you're willing to help me. The other vegetables avoid me, so I won't get any answers from them.","content.75.5807":"I spotted some kind of large pot nearby. Investigating that might be a good start.\\n\\n*You briefly wonder how this figure could know the Twelvian language, even the names of cooking utensils. They seem to notice your bewilderment, adding:*\\n\\nEven I don't know how I know all this... It all just comes to me.","content.75.5808":"Be careful, adventurer{[1*]?:}. The leek-men are dangerous...","content.75.5809":"*Within some kind of abandoned greenhouse, you spot a silhouette, its color clashing with the surroundings. You cautiously approach, noticing that it's some kind of vegetable that came to life*","content.75.5810":"*Tom Eyto seems lost in thought. Noticing you, their eyes light up*\\n\\nAh, you're back, adventurer{[1*]?:}. How are you?","content.75.5811":"It looks like certain Muvegitants are mimicking Twelvian habits...","content.75.5812":"That's a good question. I can't really answer it, because there are gaps in my past.\\n\\nBut right now, I feel completely lost. I think I can grasp joy, state of mind, existence. No one ever instilled those notions in me. Does consciousness alone make any living being ponder such things?","content.75.5813":"The main problem is loneliness. I feel so alone, you know. The Wabbits and Lenalds fear me.\\n\\nAs for the Muvegitants... They claim I'm not a vegetable...","content.75.5814":"*Tom Eyto's expression turns sour. It seems you've struck a nerve*\\n\\nThat's a tricky question.\\n\\nTomatoes are usually classified as fruit. But I feel more like a vegetable...","content.75.5815":"Unfortunately, people seek to categorize others.\\n\\nWhat's wrong with wanting to be a vegetable if you feel right that way? Besides, everyone already assumes I'm a vegetable... It should be easy to accept, but people will use pseudoscience to argue otherwise.","content.75.5816":"That could be... Am I destined to be alone forever then?\\n\\n*Tom Eyto sighs and stares at the roof of their greenhouse, visibly affected by the news. Feeling a bit uncomfortable{[1*]?:}, you quickly change the subject*","content.75.5817":"The great... Zomkin... It's strange, I...\\n\\n*Tom Eyto is suddenly very upset*\\n\\nI've got a really bad feeling. The Zomkin seems so familiar, and more than that, I feel like you shouldn't go near it... It's something very dangerous, though I couldn't say how exactly.","content.75.5818":"Stay safe{[1*]?:}, adventurer{[1*]?:}. It seems this \"Zomkin\" is at the root of it.","content.75.5819":"So, what was the result? Did you discover new things?","content.75.5820":"*The Loyal Lenald glares at you. His build, scar, and imposing armor make him a menacing figure. You'd rather not cross swords with one who appears to be an accomplished master of war. His expression, however, is withdrawn, almost blank, when he speaks to you*\\n\\nYou don't belong hele, stlangel{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5821":"*Suddenly standing up to full height*\\n\\nSilence! I didn't autholize you to speak. If oul tladitions ale meaningless to you, then you ale meaningless to us.","content.75.5822":"*Before you is some kind of Lenald priestess. Visibly concerned, she holds her face with one hand, her elbow with the other. She doesn't notice you*\\n\\nHmm... Could pelsuade the kween with a lettel... That might wolk.","content.75.5823":"Oh, folgive me. I didn't see you{[1*]?:} thele.\\n\\nWelcome, stlangel{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5824":"The Loyal Lenald folbids us flom intelacting with stlangels, yet Inali teaches us hospitality and benevolence. I'm obliged to lespect these plinciples.","content.75.5825":"We ale at wal with the Wabbits. These ale exceptional measules that go against Inali's plecepts. But I'll find a way to end this wal - I'm sule of it!","content.75.5826":"Much mole than that. Inali is oul goddess. She has evel plotected and guided oul people. She shaled hel wisdom and benevolence with oul ancestols. That wisdom and benevolence was passed down flom genelation to genelation, filst to oul people, and then to the lest of the wolld.","content.75.5827":"That's whele evely Lenald makes an offeling to Inali at least once in theil life. It's a show of glatitude and lespect fol what Inali has done and will continue to do fol oul people.\\n\\n*Liz nods reverently. This dignified Lenald seems to have trained in the art of conversation. Each word is enunciated, each phrasing clear*","content.75.5828":"Of coulse, we'd be honoled!\\n\\nThe Lenalds have a whole plotocol fol that. In hel gleat melcy, Inali wanted to make things simple fol evelyone. All you have to do is go to hel sanctualy, toss lice in the livel, and pay tlibute.\\n\\n*Liz clasps her hands and does a quick bow, demonstrating a simple, respectful tribute*","content.75.5829":"Alound the village. That's fol you to discovel. If you lose youl way, Inali will steel you light.","content.75.5830":"Still hele? I commend youl pelsistence.","content.75.5831":"*The Loyal Lenald crushes the Wabbit Island map in his hand, making a dull sound echo in the small valley*\\n\\nI would've lather you didn't letuln, adventulel{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5832":"Actions have consequences.\\n\\nIn aiding the Wabbits, you enabled the Wa Wabbit to lob us of oul sacled lelic.","content.75.5833":"It's a lelic given to us by oul goddess helself. Liz's family is its gualdian. The Wa? He's pelfidious and self-selving. He and his entile family ale without honol. Thele's no leason to give them an excuse.","content.75.5834":"How do I know you don't desile this lelic as well?\\n\\n*The Loyal Lenald stares at you*\\n\\nI can tell you have some honol, though. No mattel how, we must lecovel the lelic flom the Wabbits.\\n\\nWe have an alsenal at the boldel. You can go check it and give me a lepolt.","content.75.5835":"I have no choice. The Lenalds ale lost, and Inali has folsaken me... The only way to pelsuade a gleat Lenald walliol is to dilectly and honolably challenge them.","content.75.5836":"I believe in you, adventulel{[1*]?:}. May Inali plotect you.","content.75.5837":"*The priestess's expression is one of resolve, despite the tears at the corner of her eyes*\\n\\nBut this is my last lesolt. It's the last tlial flom Inali befole I can ploceed.\\n\\nNo mole talking. We'le on the velge of a massacle! The use of folce isn't one of oul tenets, but so what? I see no othel solution...","content.75.5838":"What do you know of oul destiny? A few houls ago, you didn't know a thing about oul people, oul customs.","content.75.5839":"*Liz frowns, an uncommon expression for a priestess of her standing. You think the situation must be pretty serious and she must be taking it to heart to be so expressive*\\n\\nWhat wisdom? My ancestols alen't hele to guide me. Inali is playing alound with my fate by thlowing obstacles in my way.\\n\\nThe tluth is... I've lost oul lelic, oul people's tlust, and my family's honol...","content.75.5840":"*A moment passes after you nod respectfully. Liz seems to be thinking, or rather... Listening. The quiet of Liz's little house calms you as you stare at the Lenald's eyes, trying to see if your words had an effect on her*","content.75.5841":"... A stlangel comes into my home to lemind me of impoltant values. I gave in to angel, but also to despail. The solution eventually plesented itself. I only needed to keep my neals open...","content.75.5842":"I mean it's time fol me to leclaim oul destiny. I don't have a second to lose... Thank you, adventulel{[1*]?:}! You go see the Loyal Lenald. You wele supposed to talk with him, light?","content.75.5843":"You'le back! It seems the filst implession was acculate. I asked you to leview the alsenal and you lan{[1*]?:} away like a cowald{[1*]?:}!\\n\\nI await youl lepolt...","content.75.5844":"Pule malalkey! My almy exclusively complises blave walliols who tlain hald evely day. And oul geal is top-notch, even if most of it has just one socket...","content.75.5845":"*You failed to provoke the Loyal Lenald. Amused, he crosses his arms*\\n\\nHow plesumptuous{[1*]?:} of you, stlangel{[1*]?:}. Think you know evelything about tlaining at the dojo? I dale you to make it thlough oul dojo in one piece. Plove me wlong and I'll take time out to tlain the tloops myself.","content.75.5846":"You seem to be coming back stlong. I take it you plevailed ovel oul disciples!\\n\\nWe've been in peacetime fol fal too long... These fifty sleepy yeals have done us mole halm than good.","content.75.5847":"*The Lenald smiles mischievously, and in this enchanting place, you're hit{[1*]?:} by a wave of serenity like you've never felt before*\\n\\nAfter a few seconds in this state of bewitchment, you regain control of your faculties*","content.75.5848":"You'le pule of healt and soul. Inali wouldn't entlust the Lenalds' destiny to just anyone.\\n\\nShe... We knew you wouldn't lefuse.","content.75.5849":"You want to talk about the Ivoly Dofus? I vely much hope you can get it fol us!\\n\\nHope has been lekindled, my fliend{[1*]?e:}. The hope of an entile people!","content.75.5850":"Thele's tlouble at the boldel. It's one of the soulces of oul conflict with the Wabbits. That seems like a good stalting point fol youl adventule.","content.75.5851":"I'll lay the gloundwolk with the Wabbits so they don't see you as a Lenald thleat.\\n\\nThele's no time to waste. Let's save oul people!","content.75.5852":"*You notice a Lenald sitting cross-legged next to a tomb. The place seems sacred, mystical. The Lenald is focused on her meditation*","content.75.5853":"*You sense that Tom Eyto would've shrugged if they had shoulders*","content.75.5854":"You know, I find it pointless to compare ourselves to others. It's a fact of life.\\n\\nWe have to move forward no matter what happens, no matter who we are deep down - our actions are what define us...","content.75.5855":"*You describe how the huge compost pile has fertilized the surrounding soil and must have triggered the creation of new Muvegitants. Along with the inordinate size of the rotting Cawwot*\\n\\nSo? Did you run into the great Zomkin?","content.75.5856":"I understand. I'm glad you were successful in your mission{[1*]?:}. That should slow down and disorient the Muvegitants. With any luck, they won't attack the Lenalds and Wabbits as much.","content.75.5857":"Be careful{[1*]?:}, adventurer{[1*]?:}. And thank you again... For everything.","content.75.5858":"You seem to be balging in... Vely well. I don't nolmally cale to deal with adventulels, but I suppose I'm obliged to waln you.\\n\\nMany dangels have alisen on the island lecently... You should leally watch youl step.","content.75.5859":"Muvegitants have been moving into oul fields fol a few yeals. The Wabbits must be behind it. They say they'le not, but I have majol doubts.\\n\\nWhat's mole, evelyone's on edge because of a Black Wabbit that got into the village.","content.75.5860":"We caught him and we'le holding him in the Lenald Palace plison. He seemed to want to lequest oul aid, but... Anyway, that's not youl ploblem.\\n\\nYou've been walned{[1*]?:}, stlangel{[1*]?:}. Have a safe joulney.","content.75.5861":"Wow, it looks like you saved my hide! In spite of my gweat angew towawd my subjects, I shall gwant you a wewawd.","content.75.5862":"So you'we looking fow this awtifact... Hmm, indeed it's been in my family fow genewations.\\n\\nBut I cannot give it to you. It's kept in a secwet temple that's been ovewwun by Zwombbits.\\n\\n*The Wa thinks for a moment*\\n\\nWell, I might have an idea...","content.75.5863":"You see, adventuwew{[1*]?:}, I was unfaiwly deposed and confined in this place aftew a huge wevolt... But if I wewe to wegain my thwone, my little pwoblem would be wesolved. Aftew all, I'm the wightful Wa of this island.\\n\\nThe key is in the temple, the same one whewe the Bow is held.","content.75.5864":"I know a way into the temple. So hewe's what we could do:\\n\\nI can help you get into the temple. In wetuwn, you wecovew the key to my palace. Of couwse, if you find the Bow, you can have it.","content.75.5865":"You'we wight - that's a weal pwoblem. The hoawds of Zwombbits swawming the tunnels may well infect us... Thankfully, I've got anothew solution.\\n\\nThe Spowomawoses that gwow on the island could be used as a wepellent and antidote to the Zwombbits' toxic fumes.\\n\\nCome back aftew you've cwafted some Antimawosis. You'll find vials in the chest wight hewe.","content.75.5866":"Well? What do you have to say?","content.75.5867":"Tewwific! We'll be able to get to the temple. I mawked the location of a secwet passage on youw map. It's in the tunnels, so be caweful!","content.75.5868":"Halt! If you wish to speak with my husband, the Wa Wabbit, I'm afwaid he's pwesently occupied. Come back latew.","content.75.5869":"*You didn't expect to see a desert like this on the outskirts of Wabbit Island. The temperature is much higher here. And yet it seems you didn't have to travel far to reach this oasis, and the beautiful stretch of blue water offers a welcome chance to take stock of the situation. As you approach the pristine water, you notice that a makeshift camp has been erected. You see tents and crates, and even a small campfire*\\n\\n*Just then a girl comes toward you, seemingly quite harmless. Your eyes meet. She smiles at you and extends a hand in friendship*\\n\\nHello. I don't think I know you... Have you too lost{[1*]?:} your way in this sandy place?","content.75.5870":"*The taciturn warrior eyes you solemnly*\\n\\nHello, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I wish I could share something with you, but our resources are scarce, and we've been separated from the rest of our expedition... I cannot offer my time or attention.\\n\\nThat said, if you're willing to help me with the hunter quests, I'd be eternally grateful.","content.75.5871":"*The Ouginak gives you a nasty look. She seems determined, but you also detect a hint of tiredness in her face*\\n\\nOut of my way... I don't have time for you.","content.75.5872":"*The old Wabbit seems tired and ill. You decide not to bother him*","content.75.5873":"Ah, you've letulned! Did you letlieve oul sacled lelic?","content.75.5874":"Flom what I undelstand, you didn't get many answels... You still don't know whele the Muvegitants come flom.\\n\\nBut if what you say is tlue, and you have hindeled theil capacity to fight and invade oul tellitoly, then fol that you have my glatitude and that of the Lenald people. At any late, I've been seeing fewel Muvegitant attacks today.","content.75.5875":"*The Loyal Lenald tilts his head to the side, crossing his arms*\\n\\nYou'll get the answels you seek flom the Wabbits, adventulel{[1*]?:}. Oul people have been peace-loving fol yeals. It would nevel occul to us to steal flom the Wabbits, but they did it to us.\\n\\nConsideling the cilcumstances, I can't vely well tlust outsidels. It's cleal to me that the Wabbits ale lesponsible.","content.75.5876":"Wal isn't necessalily a bad thing, stlangel{[1*]?:}. What othel choice do we have? The Wabbits no longel answel us, they taunt us, lob us, and summon up Muvegitants and a stlange pylamid. Sometimes you have to do gleat evil fol the gleatel good... And I'm plepaled to get my paws dilty to do that necessaly evil.","content.75.5877":"I see that Liz told you oul lelic was an immaculate Dofus. She must have seen some glimmel of hope in you. I sule hope she wasn't mistaken.","content.75.5878":"You'le an{[1*]?:} outsidel{[1*]?:}. As such{[1*]?:}, you'll nevel leally be one of us. But we know you'le tlying to undelstand us. You'le not like the othels.","content.75.5879":"Of coulse. The Wa Wabbit's betlayal won't go unpunished. Oul walliols continue to tlain with my fathel, the empelol.\\n\\n*The Loyal Lenald sets his paws on the table, clearly wanting to cut the conversation short*\\n\\nNot to wolly, I glanted you mole time and I will honol my wold. I'll tly to be patient, out of lespect fol the divine Inali. Neveltheless, I lemain the Lenald leadel, and I stand by my decision to wage wal against the Wabbits.","content.75.5880":"Based on youl stoly, you've faced many tlibulations... You don't hesitate to put youl body on the flont lines to help the Lenald people. May Inali guald you.","content.75.5881":"Flom what I undelstand, you callied out the goddess's will by lescuing someone in need. Even though it was the Wa, you did the light thing.\\n\\nOul Loyal Lenald can be steln, but he halbols a seething hatled of Wabbits. That's tlue of most Lenalds who wele boln duling the gleat wal and took palt in it...","content.75.5882":"*Liz fixes her hair before replying in her characteristically calm tone*\\n\\nYou may not be awale of this, but it was the Loyal Lenald who signed the peace tleaty at the end of the gleat wal. It was not his fathel, the Empelol Lin Shi. Even then, the Loyal Lenald was alleady commanding oul people.","content.75.5883":"Among othel factols, my fathel got him to see leason. Oul people wele tiled of fighting to sulvive - we deselved to live in peace.\\n\\nWhen the Muvegitants appealed, I lemembel that he did oldel the walliols to lesume tlaining. That's also when he added foltifications to the tellitoly's boldels.\\n\\nIn the past, I had pelsuaded the Loyal Lenald to act in good faith and maintain lelations with the Wabbit Kween. But the Wa Wabbit's betlayal lekindled his lage.","content.75.5884":"I don't leally know hel, but I do know she luled the Wabbit tellitoly in the Wa's absence. She's a vely impoltant figule to the Wabbits.","content.75.5885":"Be caleful{[1*]?:}, adventulel{[1*]?:}!","content.75.5886":"*The Kween stares at you warily. Despite her size, she displays the utmost poise and elegance*\\n\\nSo it's you! The Wa told me of youw... adventuwes.","content.75.5887":"*You sense that the Kween isn't like her husband at all. Despite her ungainly appearance, you notice she pays a lot of attention to her tone. She holds your gaze with an almost unnerving charisma*\\n\\nHe said he had weceived help fwom a{[1*]?:} stwangew{[1*]?:}. And yet, you got youw due and he got his.\\n\\nIf you'we back now, you must have something on youw mind. Don't beat awound the bush with me.","content.75.5888":"*The Kween's ears perk up suddenly*\\n\\nThe fate of the Wabbits? You? I don't believe that's youw pwoblem. It's mine, to be fwank.\\n\\nMy husband may have twusted you... But who's to say you'we weally sympathetic{[1*]?:} to Wabbitkind? I would be a second-wate kween if I simply gave my twust to evewy {[1*]?:}stwangew who comes along.\\n\\nThe Wa is shut away in his palace, and it's my duty to pwotect him fwom outside thweats.","content.75.5889":"I'll fowgive you fow those accusations only because you don't undewstand the situation. And faw be it fwom me to waste my time with an{[1*]?:} adventuwew{[1*]?:}.","content.75.5890":"If you want to make youwself useful, go get me some papew and ink. I have a most impowtant missive to dwaft.","content.75.5891":"I'm trying to purify the water of the Oasis and make food grow. I'd love to help make things easier for you, but...","content.75.5892":"I see!\\n\\n*She approaches you and stares at you, still smiling cheerfully*\\n\\nMy name's Alia. I'd be glad to help you out. What do you need?","content.75.5893":"*Alia frowns with concern*\\n\\nI'm afraid I don't know much about the pyramid. But I could tell you my story... ","content.75.5894":"My friend Bordegann and I come from a small island nearby. It was wiped out by a tidal wave. Our village was completely engulfed... Several villagers managed to board some makeshift boats, but Bordegann and I got separated from them. We eventually washed up here on this desert island.\\n\\nOur goal was to make the trip in two phases. The rest of the villagers must be waiting for us farther in. Bordegann is supposed to lead the actual expedition to Ohwymi, which we've chosen as our new home.","content.75.5895":"I'm lucky to have Bordegann with me...\\n\\n*The girl blushes, and you realize that Bordegann is very dear to her. She becomes serious again and continues*\\n\\nOh, and we also met Sindrya. For my part, I'm handling logistics by purifying the oasis water and getting food to grow in this arid desert. It's hard to make full meals from the scarce resources in the desert, but it's better than nothing.","content.75.5896":"We washed up on this desert island a few months ago, back in Frauguctor. We managed to set up this makeshift camp... But we've lost all trace of our friends. They should've been able to find refuge on a more peaceful island than this one.\\n\\n*Alia looks away, frowning. You feel all her worry. She's been separated from her family and friends for months, barely managing to survive in a hostile land*","content.75.5897":"We tried, but unsuccessfully. When the pyramid appeared, they withdrew...\\n\\nWe were unwelcome, even though Bordegann has ties to certain Wabbits. Now our plan is to head to Ohwymi, where we hope to find the other villagers...","content.75.5898":"I know almost nothing about that pyramid. I do know that it appeared a few days before my friend Bordegann and I arrived in the desert. If you want to know more, you should speak with Sindrya.","content.75.5899":"She's an Ouginak who wound up here around the same time as we did. She seems to know a lot about that mysterious pyramid. Unfortunately, she's not very easy to reach and she's wary of strangers...\\n\\n*Alia puts a finger to her chin thoughtfully*\\n\\nI might have an idea...","content.75.5900":"We have a little ritual going. I've known her for a few months now, and we've slowly but surely connected in this way. I bring her a meal every day...\\n\\nBring it to her on my behalf, and maybe she'll agree to help you!","content.75.5901":"*Alia cocks her head to the side before she answers*\\n\\nThere's no need. We all need to help each other out, especially now with Ogrest's chaos. Anyway, you came{[1*]?:} to solve the problems in the area, right?\\n\\n*As the young woman asks you this, she hands you a basket covered with a small cloth. It appears to be a lunch basket*","content.75.5902":"*The woman glares at you. She's clearly resisting the urge to hunt you down on the spot*\\n\\n*Suddenly, she seems to recognize the basket. You hand it to her, and her face softens slightly, albeit still menacing. You notice her snout twitching and realize that Sindrya is sniffing the air to determine its contents*","content.75.5903":"*Still a bit apprehensive, Sindrya takes the lunch basket without saying thanks. You detect a hint of fear and sadness in her. She doesn't seem to be wild or uncouth by nature, so why is she acting this way?*","content.75.5904":"You're wrong to go messing with that pyramid. You'll lose something to it as well.","content.75.5905":"I lost all my companions inside the pyramid... It's not a place where mortals should go.\\n\\nA cursed entity reigns over the pyramid, a powerful specter called Tal Kasha.","content.75.5906":"Her curse will hit you too if you get too close to that pyramid. I'll say it again: you'd be better off leaving.\\n\\n*The firmness of Sindrya's words unsettles you a bit. It seems she lost her adventuring companions to Tal Kasha... Now you have a better idea of why she's so distant and mistrustful. You sense that you'd better not push any harder, and that she won't tell you anything more... for now*","content.75.5907":"*The young woman looks around a bit, pensively. She appears to be weighing the pros and cons of your proposal*\\n\\nOf course... I'm currently building a boat. My goal is to reach Ohwymi.","content.75.5908":"Not really. More than anything, I want to bring reinforcements to storm the pyramid. I owe it to my companions...","content.75.5909":"Bordegann usually helps me with the work. We both wish to get to Ohwymi.\\n\\nBut lately, Bordegann seems overwhelmed by the proliferation of Sandyoptera. I'm running low on wood... Very low, in fact. If you want...","content.75.5910":"*Sindrya nods slightly*","content.75.5911":"*The Ouginak raises her head upon noticing you. She looks determined, but you also catch a hint of tiredness in her face*\\n\\nWhat do you want?","content.75.5912":"*Sindrya still declines to thank you, but she gently nods her head. She seems to be softening up around you*","content.75.5913":"Their stories don't concern me. And they shouldn't concern you either. You're just an{[1*]?:} outsider{[1*]?:} - you're not really one of them...","content.75.5914":"Settling a score with Tal Kasha is like settling a score with the sun or the ocean. It's impossible. And all you'll get for trying is a curse and a terrible death.","content.75.5915":"*You wipe your forehead and your sweat is cold to the touch. The sun is setting, and the desert heat has suddenly dropped. Sindrya looks out at the horizon, lost in her memories. You stay quiet for a minute, waiting for her to open up*\\n\\n*The horizon grows murky, and you're gripped{[1*]?:} by a sense of being ensnared in eternity. The sand piles up, it moves and turns over, day after day, never disappearing. But your lifespan is limited. The people you meet, the buildings, the books, even the equipment will all become another speck in this desert. Forever lifeless*\\n\\n*After a while, Sindrya breaks the silence*\\n\\nWell, if you insist... I'll reveal more.","content.75.5916":"I was in a group of mercenaries... We worked together a lot. We spent quite a few years hauling back and forth across the World of Twelve to complete various missions. Basically, we transported cargo and exterminated monsters.\\n\\nOur group did pretty nice work. Nice enough that one day, we got a job at sea. Our mission was to find the Pyramid of Tal Kasha, which we were told was full of treasure.","content.75.5917":"The deal was incredibly lucrative. Enough to fund our expedition and, of course, settle down in a quiet village and retire.\\n\\nI never found out who the client was, surely some big corporation. We spent several years sailing in search of the Pyramid of Tal Kasha.\\n\\nOne fine day, off the coast of Wabbit Island, our anchor struck something on the seabed, and the pyramid... How shall I put it...\\n\\nA storm of all the elements raged for several hours. I can't describe in words what we saw, it was... nightmarish. And in the midst of that multicolored storm, the pyramid appeared beneath us.","content.75.5918":"That's right. The elemental storm eventually died down, but that wasn't all. Stuck at the top of the pyramid, we were faced with another horrifying sight.\\n\\n*Sindrya shakes her head, disturbed by the memory*\\n\\nI don't know what magic caused that expanse of sand to appear. I think the sand escaped from the opening of the pyramid... Along with those big insects, the Sandyoptera.\\n\\nI couldn't tell you exactly how it happened. When I regained my senses, I could only see that the terrain had completely changed.\\n\\nI still don't know what caused the pyramid to emerge like that, but our boat was unusable then, and so the only thing we could do was explore the pyramid.","content.75.5919":"*The Ouginak takes a swig of water from her flask before continuing*\\n\\nThe rest of the story is pretty straightforward... We entered the pyramid. Not long after we started digging, we were attacked by monsters in the darkness of the pyramid, and one by one, my companions were lost. I'm the only one who made it back to the surface. So there you have it.\\n\\n*You guess that her detached, sarcastic tone is her way of coping with her traumatic memories of the event*","content.75.5920":"That's why I'd like to storm that pyramid with an army.\\n\\nI'm not holding out hope - they're probably dead. Or worse.","content.75.5921":"They could've become servants of Tal Kasha... \\n\\n*A silence falls between you. Suddenly, Sindrya reaches into her pocket and takes out a worn pendant, which she tosses to you. You catch it with both hands and examine it. It looks quite valuable, but it has clearly suffered the ravages of time. You don't know what to make of it as is*\\n\\nThat's the only thing I had time to grab in the pyramid... Before the tragedy.\\n\\nSince you're so interested{[1*]?:} in the pyramid, I suggest you repair that. It could help you learn something...","content.75.5922":"*The Ouginak breathes heavily*\\n\\nOn the contrary, I'm almost glad to get rid of it.","content.75.5923":"If it turns out to be harmless, I want you to give it to Alia.\\n\\n*Sindrya turns and puts her hands on her hips as she looks at the pile of wood you've brought*\\n\\nThat'll give me a chance to thank her for all her nice meals. Well, I won't keep you, unless you want to help me assemble the hull...","content.75.5924":"*Missy Amulet picks up the worn pendant you gently placed on the table*\\n\\nThis looks like a very precious artifact... I'll take care of it.","content.75.5925":"Yes, yes... Hang on a minute, will you?\\n\\n*Missy Amulet turns away and begins working on the pendant*","content.75.5926":"*After a few hours, Missy Amulet brings back your pendant*\\n\\nThere you go. This time I won't charge you... After all, I don't get to see such a beautiful necklace every day.\\n\\n*You take a closer look, and indeed, it's nothing like what Sindrya gave you... It is magnificent, resplendent, and most of all, it exudes a sense of ancient wealth. There are inscriptions on it that remind you of Huppermages. Runes of some kind are engraved on this pendant... It's your only clue at this point, so you decide to make your way to Rok Island to learn more*","content.75.5927":"*You present the pendant to the Grand Master. Unflappable, he doesn't bat an eye. He replies in a tone you'd swear is somber, or perhaps accusatory*\\n\\nWhere did you find this?","content.75.5928":"That artifact you have must have belonged to Lady Jhessica. And so the cursed pyramid of Ohwymi has resurfaced...\\n\\n*The Grand Master's face betrays no emotion, but for some reason, you're certain that he's displeased*","content.75.5929":"She was a famous Huppermage... She created the cursed pyramid to open a portal in search of Prosperus Elementor.","content.75.5930":"I understand your confusion. After all, this story goes back to the 230s. I certainly understand that it isn't common knowledge. Still, this just proves you should've taken your studies more seriously.\\n\\n*The Grand Master shakes his head almost imperceptibly. His expression is so impenetrable that it takes all your energy to guess his intentions*\\n\\nI'll give you a quick refresher.","content.75.5931":"Lady Jhessica was an extraordinary Huppermage. Her knowledge of the arcana was quite exceptional. One day, she decided to perform a ritual to locate Prosperus Elementor, the first Huppermage.\\n\\nShe was aided by Xelor himself, who offered her an hourglass that could slow aging to help her continue her mission.","content.75.5932":"You see, Ohwymi was gradually overtaken by drought over the course of many centuries. It had previously been a region with lush vegetation. Sadly, none of that remains today.\\n\\nWhen Lady Jhessica built the pyramid, several Ohwymians decided to settle in the area to found the City of the Sandglass.\\n\\nThe city grew rapidly as many of those fleeing the growing drought settled there.","content.75.5933":"*You perceive the slightest furrowing in the Grand Master's brow, deducing that he sensed your impatience based on your expression*\\n\\n... Tal Kasha was one of those residents. You must realize that drought can make any living thing go mad. Water... Water is so important.\\n\\n*Without any movement on the Grand Master's part, little balls of water form in front of him. He watches them as though enthralled until they burn and evaporate, consumed by flames summoned by the venerable Huppermage*\\n\\nWater is so fragile.\\n\\n*The air around you becomes cloudy. You're overcome with a feeling of weakness, and a strange darkness descends over the room*","content.75.5934":"*The light returns, and the feeling of weakness leaves you*\\n\\nConvinced that Lady Jhessica was behind the drought affecting Ohwymi Island, Tal Kasha and her men assassinated Lady Jhessica. Xelor was furious with her, however. He broke the hourglass and cursed Tal Kasha and her assassins, condemning them to an eternity of undeath.\\n\\nThey could never leave the cursed pyramid or rest in peace ever again.","content.75.5935":"Of course!\\n\\nThe ancient City of the Sandglass, swallowed up in the depths ever since Ogrest's chaos, has been degraded by its centuries under the sea. Only the pyramid was able to emerge. The main building was built from a different material, you see - one protected by Huppermage runes.","content.75.5936":"Not to my knowledge. She's some sort of invincible specter.\\n\\nGrowing bored in her immortality. Maybe she'll appreciate having adventurers stop by to fight her.","content.75.5937":"It's true that pyramid is linked to us.\\n\\nVery well, I'll send a few Huppermages to perform a ritual to make it sink back down to the ocean floor. It'll take a few years. But as long as no one goes inside, it shouldn't be a problem.","content.75.5938":"Just a minute. That artifact is the property of Lady Jhessica, so it belongs with the Huppermages by right.","content.75.5939":"*The Grand Master opens his eyes wide and abruptly enters your mind. The Huppermage begins to probe your memories with a power beyond imagination. You are utterly paralyzed{[1*]?:} by this powerful mental attack*","content.75.5940":"*Resistance is futile. You have no control over your body or your mind. The Huppermage scans your memories as simply as he would flip through a book, pausing to look at your views of the pyramid. He sees Sindrya, the boat under construction, the desert, and suddenly, he sees Alia*\\n\\n*You sense him lingering on your memories with the girl, then on the promise made to Sindrya to give the pendant back to Alia. After a few seconds, the Grand Master brusquely withdraws from your mind, restoring your control of your movements*","content.75.5941":"*You feel a veil of calming reassurance settle over you. This mental intrusion wasn't really such a big deal, after all. It was even pretty normal. You relax and gaze at the wise elder, waiting for whatever's next*\\n\\nThis artifact is precious, but it has lost all magical power. Do what you like with it.\\n\\n*The Grand Master lifts his head imperceptibly, and you realize he's signaling for you to leave. As usual, it's impossible to determine his true intentions*","content.75.5942":"*The girl smiles sweetly when she notices you*\\n\\n[#name], you're back! How can I be of service?","content.75.5943":"How about that... So that pyramid was built by the Huppermages.","content.75.5944":"*You place the necklace in Alia's hands. She's dumbfounded*\\n\\nOh my, I... I don't know what to say. It's magnificent!\\n\\n*Then Alia's look of amazement fades, giving way to a bitter smile*","content.75.5945":"Sindrya, she... She told you she came with a crew, didn't she? As it turns out... Her partner was among them.\\nAnd now, her sweetheart is one of Tal Kasha's cursed servants... Poor Sindrya must be putting all that pain on herself.\\n\\n*The girl pauses, then lets out her deepest fear*\\n\\nIf the same thing were to happen to Bordegann...","content.75.5946":"He takes so many risks. I sometimes feel like a burden to him, like I can't help him at all... I don't have any combat skills. I'd never get over it if I lost him.\\n\\nI do what I can to make life easier for him. But when I see Sindrya, she seems so strong and solid. And yet, under all that, she's actually quite vulnerable.","content.75.5947":" *Alia shows you which way to go. Then she gives you another lunch basket, this time for Bordegann. She flashes her usual cheerful smile*\\n\\nI don't want it to seem like I'm just using you as a delivery service. Thanks again for your help. I owe you one.","content.75.5948":"Aw shucks, thank you!\\n\\n*Bordegann grabs the lunch basket and starts digging through it. He takes out a sandwich and begins eating it in front of you. He seems to be really savoring the meal, as he chews loudly. Then he realizes you're still there*\\n\\nSorry, adventurer{[1*]?:}... I was starving. Your arrival is timely. I immediately noticed you had the makings of a fighter... and I could use your help.","content.75.5949":"*The man is very friendly. He has all the makings of a charismatic, rousing leader. You instantly feel at ease near him*\\n\\nAlia probably told you a bit already... We have to find the residents of what used to be our island, which was flooded by Ogrest's Chaos. After that, we'll launch an expedition to Ohwymi. Our only hope is to build a vessel with Sindrya's help, but we keep getting attacked by the monsters in this desert region...","content.75.5950":"The Sandyoptera are reproducing at a distressing rate, and I'm barely managing to control their population. I believe the heart of the problem lies in the mother-hive where new generations of Sandyoptera are born, before they go on to swarm other parts of the Sandy Cawwot.\\n\\nAnd every generation is deadlier than the previous one... It seems the Sandyoptera are undergoing mutations that diversify the species. At this rate...","content.75.5951":"No. I have an arrangement with the Wabbits... Or should I say, with one Wabbit in particular.","content.75.5952":"That was the case, but then I met Patwick while venturing into the tunnels in search of basic necessities.\\n\\nIn the end, after discussing it, we reached a deal. I bring Patwick dead Sandyoptera for his research. In exchange, he gives me food and various useful items. You do have to like cawwots, though...","content.75.5953":"Yes, I've also identified the creature causing the swarm. Its name is... hard to pronounce. Presumably some Wabbit science thing.\\n\\n*Bordegann hands you a notebook with a few notes scribbled in it. A name is circled and highlighted*","content.75.5954":"Bless you. It actually has a pretty low life expectancy and has to regress to its larval state to regenerate. I'd like to set a trap and then attack it, right when the creature is at its most vulnerable.\\n\\nHowever, all the Sandyoptera will converge on the mother-hive when the regression starts, so they can protect their leader.","content.75.5955":"You can help out. We need to kill some Sandyoptera to prevent too many of them from gathering in the hive. Then we'll meet up to attack the larva. That way we shouldn't have to take on all the Sandyoptera at once.\\n\\nThe clock is ticking and the creature will soon return. We can't risk waiting any longer.\\n\\nActually... I'd really like to finish eating first, though.\\n\\n*Bordegann takes another bite of his sandwich*","content.75.5956":"There's no time to lose! I'll hold off the Sandyoptera as they return to the hive. You handle the boss!","content.75.5957":"It looks like the Sandyoptera are going away... Did you defeat the larva?","content.75.5958":"The Sandyoptera's numbers are way down in this area, thanks to you.\\n\\nI don't think we're out of the woods just yet, but it provides a respite we desperately needed. Now we'll be able to focus on reaching the other villagers. Then we'll all need to set a course for Ohwymi.","content.75.5959":"Well... I can't be certain, but I think they come from the pyramid.\\n\\nThey seem to primarily feed on Muvegitants which they take back to their hives. The Muvegitants' unique constitution doesn't help matters...","content.75.5960":"I think those Muvegitants are triggering mutations in the Sandyoptera, with each new generation more dangerous than the last.\\n\\nI've already seen larvae parasitizing Muvegitants to the point of controlling them.","content.75.5961":"Their leader, the bom... byx something... has a very short lifespan. It only lives for a few weeks, during which time it produces as many larvae as possible before dying.\\n\\nThat being said, it has the ability to regress to its larval state, thereby renewing its lifespan...","content.75.5962":"I don't know any more than you at this point... Well, actually, I do.\\n\\nThere's another living member of the original species: Archeobombyx the Spicy. It was cursed by the pyramid and sometimes roams the surrounding area.\\n\\nAnd because it's cursed, whenever it's killed, it reappears in the pyramid.","content.75.5963":"*Bordegann examines a part you collected from the Endopterygotic Bombyxolite. He ponders the blue blood dripping from it. Then he straightens up and looks at you*\\n\\nHow odd. The blood seems to have very unique properties. The other Sandyoptera don't have this kind of blood in their veins... You'll need to collect as many samples as you can and have them examined by the famous scientist I told you about, Patwick. He might just find a way to stop their spread.","content.75.5964":"He's in the Wabbit tunnels. There's a few different ways to get there. If I remember correctly, his lab is...\\n\\n*He maps a short route with vague directions on a page in his notebook, which he tears out and gives to you*\\n\\nSay hi to him for me. He's a very fair, very smart Wabbit. I'll warn you, though - he may be a bit... Well, you'll see for yourself. Hopefully he can give you some answers about the Muvegitants, the Sandyoptera... Maybe even that mysterious pyramid too.","content.75.5965":"*Having seemed so heroic and unflappable at first, the man looks almost embarrassed now. He stammers a bit*\\n\\nWell... You know how it is. I already feel like I've known her a long time. She's... my girlfriend, I think.","content.75.5966":"I mean... I'm so proud of her. It feels like I've known her forever, and I feel the need to be near her... To protect her. She's so kind to me, so patient...\\n\\n*You stare at him, hardly believing how foolish he seems since you confronted him about his feelings. At least he is sincere. The relationship between Bordegann and Alia is reminiscent of young love, as it can be simpler to face dragons than admit to having feelings for someone*","content.75.5967":"*You follow the directions left by Bordegann and enter what looks like a labyrinth of tunnels. You came{[1*]?:} this way once before, when you escorted the Wa into the ancient temple - but you hadn't realized just how massive the area was*\\n\\n*You begin to question the map that Bordegann drew up for you*","content.75.5968":"*While roaming the ghoulish tunnels, you notice many unmoving Zwombbits. Their corpses stink somewhat. You could swear they moved... Suddenly, you spot a small camp, with light and signs of life*\\n\\n*It's a small research lab with notebooks and beakers. You compare what you see with Bordegann's drawing, inferring two things: Bordegann doesn't know how to draw, and he also has really poor eyesight*\\n\\n*You approach the makeshift lab and encounter a haggard-looking Wabbit. He'd seen{[1*]?:} you from afar and was expecting you*","content.75.5969":"Hello, adventuwew{[1*]?:}. It's wawe to meet anyone in these tunnels. I haven't cwossed paths with a living soul in ages...\\n\\n*You approach Patwick. As you get a closer look at him, he seems to be in bad shape. He has a serious demeanor under the veneer of fatigue. Could he be older than he looks? He adjusts his glasses before continuing*\\n\\nWhat bwings you to my labowatowy?","content.75.5970":"*The Wabbit seems to be out of breath, and he looks at you, slightly panicked. He holds his ribs for a few moments, slowly exhaling. After letting go, he points you to a chair nearby*\\n\\nOf couwse, I know those two things well... I think I wecognize you, you'we the{[1*]?:} one{[1*]?:} who came a while ago to restowe the Wa Wabbit to the thwone.\\n\\nYou could wecap youw whole adventuwe fow me. Coffee? Tea?","content.75.5971":"*You feel the damp air of the tunnels and the lack of wind just as you sit down to tell your story. Your arrival in these lands, the conflict between the Wabbits and Lenalds... And the situation with the Muvegitants*\\n\\n*Patwick interrupts you, taken aback by your tale*\\n\\nHold on... You mean to say you've encountewed Muvegitants with sentience?","content.75.5972":"I... To tell the twuth, I don't know. You see, I'm the one wesponsible fow the Muvegitants.\\n\\n*You frown. Could the old Wabbit be some kind of mad scientist? It's possible he's trying some cockamamie experiments and unable to control the consequences. Patwick mumbles under his breath*\\n\\nYes, I know they've gotten out of contwol. I'm twying to find a way to stem theiw spwead.","content.75.5973":"If I don't find a solution, they'll keep spweading fowevew. Fow bettew ow wowse, the Muvegitants awe the Sandyoptewa's main food souwce, which also explains why theiw pwopagation takes time.\\n\\nIn showt...\\n\\n*Patwick strokes his beard for a moment*\\n\\nSo a Muvegitant developed consciousness...","content.75.5974":"You say you've bwought samples of blue blood? Awe you suwe{[1*]?:} about that?\\n\\n*You hand over the samples of the Endopterygotic Bombyxolite's blood. Suddenly, Patwick seems to regain his energy. In a departure from his usual sluggishness, he's more eager and begins talking much faster*\\n\\nBy my cawwot... That colow...","content.75.5975":"Sandyoptewa blood has vewy intewesting pwopewties. Fow one thing, it has the capacity to boost enewgy. Howevew, I haven't been able to make any use of it in my weseawch. The blood you bwought me...\\n\\n*Patwick mixes a drop of the bombyxolite's blood with some sort of serum, before sharing his observations*\\n\\nThe effects awe much mowe pwonounced.","content.75.5976":"Now I'm cewtain: the Sandyoptewa must've fed on something that altewed the development of the fiwst specimens. The next genewations inhewit the extwaowdinawy size and abilities of theiw pwogenitows, but the blood is faw less mawked by this change.\\n\\nThe blood being blue, along with the symptoms descwibed, weminds me of something I wead in my youngew days, when I was a mewe assistant. That was duwing the wehabilitation of the Zwombbits...\\n\\nNow whewe could those documents have gone...?","content.75.5977":"I believe I'm on the vewge of a gweat discovewy. I'm sowwy to impose upon you, but I need youw help. You see... My time is wunning out, and we must act quickly.","content.75.5978":"Let's just say time is wunning out.\\n\\n*You notice Patwick has a bluish complexion, unusual for a Wabbit. The color almost reminds you of the bombyxolite's blood... But you don't feel confident{[1*]?:} enough to press the esteemed scientist on it*","content.75.5979":"I know of wecowds that could help me. They'we in Womewo's lab, which was sealed up along with the Zwombbits at the end of the gweat waw.","content.75.5980":"I'm convinced that the cowpowation's wecowds could save me a lot of time. Could you please twavel to that lab? Be caweful{[1*]?:}, thewe might be quite a few aggwessive Zwombbits inside.","content.75.5981":"*Patwick stands up when he sees you. He seems very weak, and you wonder if fresh air would do him good. Unfortunately, his problems aren't only physical*","content.75.5982":"... I guess I owe you an explanation. The Wabbit Kween had instwucted me to do expewiments to twy to addwess the pwoblem of bawwen soil. I was wowking in a gweenhouse, which is now in the devastated fields. I can't imagine it has much of use anymowe...\\n\\nWhat mowe can I say? It's all out of contwol now. I nevew set out to cweate cawnivowous, let alone anthwopophagous, monstews. ","content.75.5983":"*The Wabbit scientist furrows his brow again*\\n\\nAs a child, I always hoped to bwing people joy with my inventions. Look at the wesult... You'we wight, I nevew should've done those expewiments.\\n\\nBut I don't want it to end this way. I wefuse to leave this wowld having only bwought misfowtune.","content.75.5984":"To think a Muvegitant has achieved the stage of consciousness... What you say is a complete shock to me. It's as if I cweated a living thing myself.\\n\\nIf only I could've done mowe good awound me. Unfowtunately, I'm limited by my abilities. I'm westwicted by my sick, aging body.\\n\\nFow pity's sake, help me. I tiwe of all these wegwets.","content.75.5985":"*The old scientist nods before carefully taking the books you brought him*\\n\\nHmmm... Ah, yes, I wemembew... It was this wepowt...\\n\\n*He struggles to turn the pages. Your heart sinks. He has the greatest difficulty doing something that seems utterly trivial to you*\\n\\nAh... Here it is... Spice.","content.75.5986":"It's a substance with many wisks and benefits. Its appeawance is that of a wed powdew with yellow flecks... The puwest kind can be found in the pywamid of Tal Kasha.\\n\\n*He softly taps the page of the report*\\n\\nYes, the cowpowation in Ohwymi had held talks with the Wabbit scientists back then. Let's see... Yes, of couwse.","content.75.5987":"*The old scientist doesn't seem to hear you, too busy reading his report. After finishing, he nods*\\n\\nWe could capitalize on the pywamid's weappeawance. Spice is a powewful wesouwce... And a pwecious one. It's the key to ouw salvation. You must go pwocuwe some...","content.75.5988":"*Patwick looks at you, determined*\\n\\nThe futuwe of the Wowld of Twelve...","content.75.5989":"It's a vewy unique substance with numewous chawactewistics. Hmm, best to stawt with its owigin...\\n\\nSuwely you've heawd of the City of the Sandglass?","content.75.5990":"The pywamid was built by Lady Jhessica, a wenowned Huppewmage. Xelow helped hew by giving hew a sandglass that could slow the aging pwocess. Slowly but suwely, a city gwew awound the pyawmid... The City of the Sandglass.\\n\\n*Patwick has a sudden coughing fit. After several seconds, he recovers and carries on, his voice now hoarse*\\n\\nTal Kasha was a suwvivow fwom the desewt, and she muwdewed Lady Jhessica.","content.75.5991":"When Lady Jhessica was killed, Xelow's sandglass was destwoyed... And the sand spwead acwoss the city. Ovew time, the vawious species within Ohwymi incowpowated the sand into theiw life cycle, until they fowmed the substance we now call spice.\\n\\nSpice's composition is highly complex... In addition to the divine sand, it contains Ohwymi peppew, sandwowm excwement, and castuc pulp.\\n\\n*The scientist has an amused smile. You can tell he's glad to contribute his knowledge*","content.75.5992":"It would be difficult, if not impossible, to cweate mowe of it in the Wakfu Era. Howevew, you should find some in the pywamid...","content.75.5993":"Thewe awe countless effects. They awe wisky yet gweatly beneficial.\\n\\nThis wesouwce was once favowed by the Umphialla Cowpowation... My peews conducted wathew distuwbing expewiments involving the use of spice.\\n\\nFow now, it is both the souwce of and the solution to ouw wowwies.","content.75.5994":"You'we welcome, adventuwew{[1*]?:}. I'm glad that I could sewve a puwpose. Nothing would make me happiew now than to know the futuwe will be bwight.\\n\\n*Patwick looks at you, seemingly sizing you up*\\n\\nI'd weally like... I'd weally like...","content.75.5995":"Thewe awe many pwoblems in this wowld that don't have a wational ow physical solution.\\n\\nCewtain illnesses awe difficult to tweat. It is so, so twagic that we can't access the knowledge of the futuwe. So many twajectowies have been cut showt by we mowtals' lack of knowledge.\\n\\nI have all this knowledge and have done all this weseawch for yeaws, all to become a bettew scientist. And now, it hawdly mattews. At times I feel that all I've leawned is that I know nothing.\\n\\n*The Wabbit seems very tired all of a sudden. He has the greatest difficulty getting to a chair. His body seems achy and feeble. You don't know what to do or say*\\n\\nPlease give me a minute. I'd like to west fow a spell... I can't do mowe to help you at this point.","content.75.5996":"*Sindrya shrugs*\\n\\nI wouldn't exactly say I care about you, but really, what a waste to throw one's life away like that...","content.75.5997":"I don't even know how to dissuade you. Why would you brave the darkness of the pyramid?","content.75.5998":"*The Ouginak shudders at the word \"spice\". She feels the pain before revealing one last secret*\\n\\nCollecting spice was my mercenary troop's mission. We were hired by the corporation for that purpose... That's the only reason we scoured the seas in search of the pyramid all those years.","content.75.5999":"Okay, I'll give you one last warning. Don't do it. If you're still intent on going, though... I'll share what I know about it.\\n\\n*Sindrya explains a bit about the path she took. But her explanation seems unclear; she hesitates whenever she's about to give you directions. After a while, she shakes her head and says to you, very firmly:*\\n\\nWhatever you do, don't go into the central room. Don't step through the doorway marked with a pyramid.","content.75.6000":"*Sindrya's heart aches as she imagines you wandering in the darkness of the pyramid*\\n\\n*Above all, her heart aches as she imagines the lifeless bodies of her comrades. Even the ones that never made it out of the pyramid... Like Sindrya's fiancé. She lost them so fast... What was it if not a fateful series of choices? If only she could go back in time, a few seconds... Just a few seconds... That's all she'd need*\\n\\n*Alas, the seconds cruelly accumulate, turning into hours, then weeks. Sindrya's wound becomes ever more painful as the tragedy gets older, like a puddle that inexorably spreads on the ground, eroding the surface bit by bit, leaving indelible marks*\\n\\n*It's like a darkness that constantly paralyzes every fiber of her being. Like a memory that would never fade. She would've needed just a few seconds, but she'll never have that magic, that trump card... that deliverance*","content.75.6001":"*Captivated by your arrogance, the Kween dangles a set of keys, one of which is a lovely golden hue and looks like it goes to the palace*\\n\\nYou'we fwee to do things youw way. Just wemembew who holds the keys. I'll wemind you ouw bowdews awe closed and we don't accept visitows.\\n\\n*It's clear that the Kween has her reasons for not trusting outsiders. With war on the horizon and all the disasters plaguing the island, there's no getting around her arrogant demeanor with you. She must be testing your trust*","content.75.6002":"I used up what I had while dlafting my lettel, but you'll find some at the village malket. Given the cilcumstances, please help youlself.\\n\\nI didn't know Hel Majesty would ask you fol such a thing...","content.75.6003":"*The Kween carefully examines the items you brought her. She seems to be thinking, then she looks at you with a smirk*\\n\\nJust a minute. You've bwought me black ink. And this papew is too simple... It doesn't suit my puwposes at all.\\nI need something mowe \"pewsonal\". As fow the ink, I want owange, fit fow the finest cawwots in my... I mean, ouw vegetable gawden.","content.75.6004":"There's some in my gawden. But the Viziew would nevew let you in.","content.75.6005":"*With an authoritarian air, the Kween gets impatient*\\n\\nDon't wowwy about my weasons - I simply need it. You don't need to undewstand evewything. All you need to know is that a cewtain cawwot is requiwed to make ink, a pwemium cawwot. We usually gwow them in the woyal gawden, but we also have a field in the village.\\n\\nA Wabbit guawds the fields and won't let you just take some. He's distwustful, but he's also pwetty thick, so you should be able to bwibe him with a black cawwot by telling him it's magical.\\n\\nAs fow the papew, you should easily find some. Say you'we thewe on my behalf.","content.75.6006":"To know one's subjects is to know the futuwe. You have all the infowmation you need. Now, go!\\n\\n*You can't explain it, but you're suddenly overcome{[1*]?:} with doubt. You sense she isn't telling you everything... You'd better go find out more about the infamous Kween*","content.75.6007":"Ah... So, you seek papew that would suit the Kween... You bwought hew Lenald papew and ink, is that wight? You fell wight{[1*]?:} into hew twap... She was testing you to see if you wewe{[1*]?:} sent by the Lenalds.\\n\\n*The steward strokes his beard. He seems older, based on his white hair and the cane he uses, but he seems quite sharp as well. He says he'll return shortly, then goes to a storeroom. A few minutes later, he comes back out with a few pieces of high-quality, cawwot-scented paper*\\n\\nHewe you go, young adventuwew{[1*]?:}. Can I pwovide you with anything else? ","content.75.6008":"Come now, I know you helped ouw Wa to wetake the thwone. I'm suwe that was no easy feat. And wight now, he could suwely use the suppowt...","content.75.6009":"*The old Wabbit seems glad that you're asking him*\\n\\nYou know the Wa was tawgeted by an assassin, yes? To be bwief, he isn't out of twouble just yet.\\n\\nI imagine you've heawd of the Viziew? He's the leadew of the Webels, a gwoup of Wabbits whose sole puwpose is to assassinate the Wa. To pwevent a twagedy, the Kween locked hew husband inside the thwone woom. Accowding to hew, the Wa's safety must be ensuwed by any means. Of couwse, hew distwust is faiw.\\n\\nShe believes the people need theiw Wa, and a coup would be a weal disastew.","content.75.6010":"The Wa Wabbit's cwown and sceptew awe passed down fwom one genewation to the next, but Ogwest's Chaos killed the fowmew Wa unexpectedly and he had no successow. So thewe was a powew stwuggle among the Wabbits...\\n\\nAftew almost thwee decades of chaos, a new Wa Wabbit appeawed, by the name of Cywus. To legitimize his weign, Cywus decided to fowce the Lenalds off the island once mowe. This kicked off a new waw, which lasted close to a hundwed yeaws. And it was duwing his ewa that the tunnels wewe closed off, as the expewimentations had gotten out of contwol.","content.75.6011":"The waw lasted much longew than expected because of Lin Shi, whose mawtial pwowess enabled the Lenalds to win many battles. The fighting dwagged on long enough fow the Wabbits to weopen the tunnels, and the expewimentations to cweate Zwombbit supewsoldiews.\\n\\nAt one point, the Wabbits wewe about to win a cewtain battle, but the Lenalds had a secwet weapon: a white Dofus which they used as a last wesowt. Thanks to the Dofus Keepew, they wewe able to tuwn the tide and fowce a peace tweaty between the two peoples.","content.75.6012":"It was a newve-wacking time, and that's an undewstatement... The Wabbits enduwed hungew, suffewing, and despaiw. Do you know what it's like to be bown in a countwy at waw?\\n\\nOvew time, a gwoup of Webels fowmed with the goal of stopping the Wa in his belligewence. Many Wabbits wanted the waw to end, and even aftew the peace tweaty, they feawed that waw would wesume. They owchestwated many attempts, but none wewe successful.\\n\\nThe Wa at the time was gwowing old, so he named his son to succeed him, as twadition dictates. That is the cuwwent Wa.","content.75.6013":"He's the son of Cywus, a Wa they considew illegitimate. The pwoblem wemains. Especially to the Webels, the cuwwent Wa is a glutton who gwew up in luxuwy and plenty while avewage people suffewed.\\n\\nHe's nevew been able to lead his people – only wuling by feaw and angew thwough the powew of his Cawwot Dofus.","content.75.6014":"Fow one simple weason: thanks to the Kween. Theiw mawwiage was political, and it eased a gweat deal of tension. It was the Kween who acted as wegent when the Wa was in exile. The Wa consumes wesouwces iwwesponsibly... But the Kween is closew to the Wabbit people, at least seemingly.\\n\\nAt any wate, the Wabbits wewe a lot bettew off because of that mawwiage. The Black Wabbits wemained devoted to their Wa, and the Wabbits wespected the Kween as she successfully ended ouw famine.\\n\\nEvewyone dewived some benefit, until the appeawance of the Muvegitants and the desewt cweatuwes.","content.75.6015":"I'm not hewe to expwess my opinion, adventuwew{[1*]?:}. I mewely sewve the leadews, whoevew they awe. ","content.75.6016":"I ovewheawd youw talks with the Kween, and I wead the lettew Liz sent the Kween. I get the sense you sincewely want to help this island, without needing any glowy ow powew fwom it. Kind of like Liz, in the end. I think the two of you wepwesent a new hope fow ouw two peoples.\\n\\nI've extensively studied Twelvian histowy... The futuwe can only be built with help fwom people like youwself. I think following youw path is in the best intewest of the Wa, the Kween, the Loyal Lenald, and all of ouw peoples.","content.75.6017":"Unfowtunately, I can't help you any fuwthew. My wole will be to wecowd the coming events... May they favow you.","content.75.6018":"*The Loyal Lenald digs his heels in at such a request, shocked yet intrigued, before coming back to his senses*\\n\\nHave you lost youl mind...? Oh... My apologies, I misundelstood youl lequest. Leave it to me. That's the kind of task a gleat Lenald walliol couldn't lefuse.\\n\\n*After a few moments, you have a small flask containing a darkish orange liquid. This should satisfy the Kween*","content.75.6019":"*The Kween pouts, not terribly impressed. It seems she had anticipated this might happen. She folds her hands in a dignified manner before speaking*\\n\\nBwave adventuwew{[1*]?:}. You ovewcame a gweat evil.","content.75.6020":"Keep youw voice down, you fool{[1*]?:}! I'll tell you evewything.\\n\\nIndeed, the Wabbits of the Wesistance wewe loyal to me. They sought to get wid of the Wa Wabbit so I could continue to wule. My husband can be a weal nuisance when he wants to be...","content.75.6021":"*The Kween seems disappointed, very plainly refuting your accusation*\\n\\nI nevew wanted the Viziew to assassinate my husband. I couldn't beaw to shawe my tewwitowy with the Viziew. You see... The Viziew was clevew and methodical. Aftew I mawwied the cuwwent Wa, I soon wealized he was bumbling and tempewamental. But most of all, he was incompetent.","content.75.6022":"*The Kween nods*\\n\\nThe Viziew was quite useful to me. He posed a thweat to the Wa... I discweetly thwawted his assassination attempts ovew the yeaws. Thanks to the Viziew, I pewsuaded the Wa to go into exile, ow to shut himself away in his thwone woom whewe he can't do anything. But the Viziew stawted to cause pwoblems fow me... He was a bit smawter than I expected.\\n\\nThank you fow getting wid of him fow me.","content.75.6023":"*The Kween replies without batting an eye*\\n\\nThat's twue. You awe a diswuptive element. You could unsettle the balance of Wabbit powew. Honestly, I wouldn't tewwibly mind if you disappeawed at the same time.","content.75.6024":"My{[1*]?:} deaw, didn't you heaw me?\\n\\nIf peace is westowed to my kingdom, my idiot husband won't have any weason to stay locked up in his palace...","content.75.6025":"*The Kween tilts her head back in exasperation*\\n\\nIt's not in youw intewest to have me as an enemy... You think you can fowce me, Kween and wegent of the Wabbits, to do anything against my will? You think you can blackmail me? I need only deny youw vewsion of events. If it's youw wowd against mine, I know who will pwevail...","content.75.6026":"*For the first time, you see the Kween falter*\\n\\nWhat an idiot! I should nevew have twusted him...","content.75.6027":"Alwight, alwight, you win. Here.\\n\\n*The Kween takes a cawwot-shaped golden key from her keyring, then weakly tosses it to you*\\n\\nI wouldn't wecommend telling my husband the twuth about me. You seem to cawe about the peoples of this island... In that case, it's in youw best intewest to leave me alone. You can't in good conscience leave that buffoon Wa Wabbit in chawge of this island. He'll let all his subjects stawve to death again...","content.75.6028":"And how!\\n\\nDo you have any idea what it's like to be bown in a waw-town countwy? To go to sleep without eating and wake up hungwy? I invested many wesouwces fow the good of my people...\\n\\nIt's cwitical that I wemain in powew.","content.75.6029":"What's the diffewence? Would you wathew I continue wobbing the Wabbit folk as my husband did?\\n\\nYou'we limited{[1*]?:}, just like evewyone else. Considew this a wawning - you win this time, but don't you dawe get in my way.","content.75.6030":"What do you want now? Leave me be, I've much wowk to do.","content.75.6031":"Who dawes entew my... Hang on, I wecognize you!","content.75.6032":"*The Wa giggles stupidly on his thwone*\\n\\nThat's quite a lead-in... Yes, I have the Ivowy Dofus. And it's my undewstanding you wewe involved in the disappeawance of my Cawwot Dofus.","content.75.6033":"Imagine my suwpwise when I wegained my thwone.\\n\\nI made quite the face when I leawned that my most pwecious tweasuwe had been puwloined...","content.75.6034":"Well, no mattew. I have a much mowe powewful welic now. The Ivowy Dofus will sewve me well in pwotecting my people from wecent thweats.\\n\\n*The Wa sits atop his oversized thwone*","content.75.6035":"Come now, ouw awmy can handle a few cawnivowous leek-men. They'we so savouwy cooked in a pie... With cawwots, of couwse.\\n\\nNo, I'm talking about something mowe impowtant. The Muvegitants awe on the main island, anyway, so it's mowe the Lenalds' pwoblem than it is ouws.","content.75.6036":"That's wight. They thweaten ouw tewwitowy, and they'we getting stwongew as time goes on. I'll nevew suwwendew this Dofus - it's the key to safeguawding Wabbitkind!\\n\\n*It's true that before now, you weren't particularly concerned{[1*]?:} about that desert suddenly appearing on the outskirts of Wabbit Island*","content.75.6037":"You'd make an awful{[1*]?:} stwategist. You'we supposed to save youw ace in the hole fow just the wight moment.\\n\\n*The Wa smiles, visibly satisfied*","content.75.6038":"Nevew!\\n\\nI don't twust those Lenalds... Ow my own kind, fow that mattew! I know my own Kween conspiwes against me. The Ivowy Dofus is added secuwity. I will not suwwendew my life ow my thwone!","content.75.6039":"*The Wa Wabbit's face changes dramatically when you mention his father. You can't tell if his expression is one of fear or anger... But clearly you've hit a nerve*\\n\\nHe was wown out in his old age. He disappeawed aftew passing me the thwone... No one knows what happened to him.\\n\\n*He straightens up suddenly*\\n\\nBut I don't think that's any of youw business! Everyone seems to wesent me, but what's the wowst I've done, huh? All the Wabbits plotting against me, all the Lenalds wanting to go to waw again... And now, even you!","content.75.6040":"That's enough! You've bothewed me enough as it is. If you want to make youwself useful, go get wid of that pywamid.","content.75.6041":"*The Kween picks up the paper and ink, then smiles as she meets your gaze*\\n\\nThat's mowe like it. Thanks fow youw help.\\n\\n*A silence sets in*","content.75.6042":"I'm awawe you wanted to see my husband. Alas, the Wa is shut away in his palace. It's my duty to pwotect him fwom outside thweats.\\n\\n*You've heard this line before... You hesitate for a moment, during which the Kween takes the opportunity to raise her voice and add:*\\n\\nAs I undewstand it, you questioned ouw stewawd, fowcing him to pwovide answews about ouw situation, ouw people...","content.75.6043":"You still wish to see the Wa Wabbit? Even though you know he's undew thweat fwom the Viziew, the Webel leadew, at this vewy moment?\\n\\n*The Kween continues with her pressing questions*\\n\\nIf I wewe to open the doow to the Wa's thwone, who knows what could happen to my poow husband? ","content.75.6044":"How dawe you waise youw voice to the Kween? This is the last stwaw. So long as the Webel thweat exists, I shall nevew let you entew the thwone woom.\\n\\n*She holds your gaze, seemingly waiting for something. It seems she'll need more persuading yet*","content.75.6045":"I sweaw it.\\n\\n*The Kween smirks. The thought of snatching her keyring crosses your mind, but causing a diplomatic incident is the last thing you need right now*","content.75.6046":"Wait... Fiwst I'll have to give you the key to the gawden. Wait hewe a moment, will you? And don't move, ow else we no longew have a deal.\\n\\n*The Kween enters the fortress. She's gone at least a quarter of an hour. You wait at the edge of the lawn. After a while, a Guawd runs out of the fortress carrying a small bag. A few minutes later, the Kween leaves in turn*\\n\\nOh deaw, I'd fowgotten the gawden was unlocked. My memowy plays twicks on me...","content.75.6047":"I have so much wowk wight now - I have to take cawe of my people all by myself. I need to manage the line of defense against the desewt cweatuwes, administew the whole tewwitowy... Do you see?","content.75.6048":"I just said I've too many othew things to deal with. I'm much too busy pwotecting my tewwitowy and my people. You take cawe of the Webels and I'll have time to take cawe of youw thing with the Lenalds.","content.75.6049":"*Liz warily tilts her head towards the Dofus for a moment*\\n\\n*She suddenly looks to you with a blink*\\n\\nI... I leally don't know what to tell you, adventulel{[1*]?:}. I inhelited this Dofus flom my fathel, and I filmly believe that it's authentic.\\n\\nUnfoltunately, I have no folmal ploof to suppolt that belief - I was simply boln into my lole as its gualdian.","content.75.6050":"By Inali, don't tell me that the agleement between oul peoples was based on a lie by the Wa...\\n\\nDon't you know anyone who could shale theil expeltise on the Dofus you've acquiled?","content.75.6051":"May the Gods plotect you, adventulel{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6052":"*Despite his friendly demeanor, you sense a note of contempt in Otomai's smile*\\n\\nHo ho! I see you're starting to take an interest in the legendary Primordial Dofus! So go ahead, ask me anything!\\n\\nIt's so adorable, it seems like only yesterday you were just a young incarnate{[1*]?:} {[1*]?:} with immense potential.","content.75.6053":"Er, excuse me, young Twelvian{[1]?:}.\\n\\nI tend to be a bit too paternalistic at times... You were saying?","content.75.6054":"*Otomai raises an eyebrow, perplexed*\\n\\nIt's strange... Your Dofus isn't emitting any energy, but I'm quite certain it's real. My scientomage's instinct is never wrong about these things.","content.75.6055":"In my opinion, only an extremely great power could accomplish something like that. I don't even know if it's technically possible.","content.75.6056":"Aha, yes! That's no small thing! It could be a lead - there are a number of Huppermage artifacts with various abilities.\\n\\nI believe the secret of your Dofus's power could be found there. You should go to Tal Kasha to learn more.","content.75.6057":"My knowledge of Huppermagic is very limited... You'd be better off talking to someone who understands it better than I.","content.75.6058":"Ha ha ha, you flatter me, my friend{[1*]?:}...\\n\\nEven if I lived forever, I would still be utterly ignorant on a myriad of topics. It's better to spend the time we have on the things we choose deliberately. We should never be ashamed of those choices or regret having made them, because every step we take towards greater knowledge will benefit us sooner or later.\\n\\nI'm sorry I can't help you this time, but feel free to come back and see me if you need to.","content.75.6059":"*The Grand Master remains stoic*\\n\\nA most unusual choice of topic. I'm listening.","content.75.6060":"Stealing the magic of a Dofus is a colossal task that even the Gods would struggle to achieve... I have trouble believing that Lady Jhessica's murderer could have managed such a feat.\\n\\nCome to think of it, though, it's not inconceivable that she could have been aided by the immense powers of the artifacts in the pyramid.","content.75.6061":"Lady Jhessica is a bottomless well of knowledge, but I don't know how far she might have got along in her research before... the incident.\\n\\nAll I know is that the Huppermages have a tradition of installing magic mirrors in some of their complexes. They typically use them to perform various experiments with refraction of light rays.\\n\\nAs far back as I can remember, Lady Jhessica had an extremely powerful mirror in her possession... although what its powers were, I don't know. A clear clue as to its potential for manipulating light energy is that Lady Jhessica herself dubbed it the \"Mirror of Light and Darkness\". I imagine it had some particular use in her search for Prosperus Elementor.","content.75.6062":"It's a possibility that we'd be remiss to ignore. Tal Kasha may have used it during some contact with the Dofus, however brief.","content.75.6063":"I wouldn't wish it on you - I'm afraid that this task will require courage and skill that no mere mortal can hope to achieve.","content.75.6064":"*The Ouginak seems disturbed by her intense thoughts*\\n\\nSo you're back.","content.75.6065":"Hmm... The pyramid is far too dangerous to enter - even the Sandyoptera instinctively understand that it's a dangerous place.\\n\\nThe only ones I've seen even slightly approach it were a group of Wabbit guawds, one of whom didn't even have clothes the right size for him. I couldn't see exactly what they were doing, but it didn't last long, and the poorly-dressed one caught up to them a few minutes later. It's a wonder he could walk at all with such enormous trousers on.","content.75.6066":"If I understand correctly, you want to go to the room at the very center of the pyramid.\\n\\nHaven't you been listening to anything I've told you? Are you prepared{[1*]?:} to sacrifice your own existence for such a futile cause?","content.75.6067":"*Sindrya remains rigid, and you feel like her mournful look has become a lot worse since you suggested that she might be worried about you*\\n\\nHmph. I suppose everyone has the right to die a heroic death. Do whatever you want.","content.75.6068":"...","content.75.6069":"I... I don't want someone's death on my conscience. I know you'd be going there no matter what, but... I can't just leave you like this.\\n\\nListen, there's just one thing I want you to do to put my mind at ease. Please train rigorously, and make sure you don't get stuck in there. I'd hate myself if lost another acquaintance in that cursed pyramid.","content.75.6070":"*Sindrya crosses her arms and looks away*\\n\\nYou're even more stubborn than I thought.","content.75.6071":"...","content.75.6072":"*As you leave, you hear a strange gurgling behind you. Hearing that from her is such a shock that you turn around immediately with a baffled expression*","content.75.6073":"*You recount your experience in the pyramid. Sindrya seems shaken by your words. After a brief pause, it is her turn to speak*\\n\\nI already half-expected it, but at least now I really know the truth. I had some faint hope that my friends might still be alive... At least now I won't have to keep running after a mirage.","content.75.6074":"I'll be all right. My companions are gone, in any case. All I can do now is tell my employers where the pyramid is located, and after that, it's their problem.\\n\\n*Sindrya looks over to the pyramid, her eyes filled with pain*\\n\\nWell, I'd better get back to work... I'll finish up this ship and go back to my people. After all, Alia and Bordegann are counting on me to get back home safely...","content.75.6075":"I wasn't able to save my companions, but at least I can help this young couple to escape from that hell. And now that you've found the spice, maybe you'll find a way to make things better on the island. Others must be spared the misfortune that befell me.\\n\\n*The Ouginak looks at you, still as sad and distant as ever, yet seemingly relieved of a burden. She takes a deep breath and raises her shoulders, suddenly looking a bit more relaxed. You sense that she must have made a decision, and that the future looks clearer to her now*\\n\\nIt's in your hands now, adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6076":"*The scientist stands up as best he can, his eyes squinting in what could be pain or fatigue*\\n\\nHow wondewful! Please, set it down hewe...\\n\\n*Patwick tries to pick up a few books to make room on his desk, but it's a struggle for him. You step in quickly to help him, then set the small chest of spice on the table*","content.75.6077":"I'm quite suwe of it, this is definitely spice. It seems evewy bit as extwaowdinawy as the wepowts descwibed it...\\n\\nI'll get to wowk wight away. Thanks to you, I'll be able to advance in my wowk... Youw effowts will not be in vain, I pwomise you.","content.75.6078":"If wowst comes to wowst, I'll consume pawt of the spice myself to benefit fwom its life-pwolonging effects.\\n\\nAs I told you befowe, I'm vewy sick, and my days awe numbewed... But I pwomise you I won't die until I've wectified the situation!","content.75.6079":"Even though it was on the Kween's owdews, the expewiments on the Muvegitants wewe my wesponsibility. Not to mention that in my youth, I had also pawticipated in the expewiments on the Zwombbits with Womewo...\\n\\nAnd you know, if I hadn't tried to cweate vegetables that wewe mowe nutwitious and easiew to gwow, the Sandyoptewa wouldn't have mutated like that eithew.","content.75.6080":"I've figuwed out why the Sandyoptewa mutate so much with evewy cycle - it's because of theiw food! Muvegitants make up most of theiw diet.\\n\\nAnyway. To wetuwn to youw question... I'll have all etewnity to west. And I've wasted enough time alweady making tewwible mistakes. I only hope I'll have enough time to set evewything wight... And not leave a new uncontwollable expewiment to futuwe genewations.","content.75.6081":"I must meet with Tom Eyto. Once we've got to know each othew, I'll include him in the weseawch pwocess. We'll make his comwades see weason.\\n\\nOnce the Muvegitants awe conscious of the situation, pewhaps all thwee peoples can unite against the Sandyoptewa... To achieve that, you must do whatevew it takes to convince the Lenalds and the Wabbits not to stawt theiw waw.","content.75.6082":"Halt! I fowbid you to take any pwemium cawwots.","content.75.6083":"... Hmph! What do you expect me to do with a black cawwot?","content.75.6084":"Weally? My wowd! Just my luck!\\n\\nI'll gladly give you a pwemium cawwot fow that!","content.75.6085":"All wight... I suwwendew!\\n\\n*The Wa Wabbit plops sheepishly down on his throne. To your eyes, he looks like a child who realizes he's just thrown a tantrum, but can't bring himself to admit it. You also wonder why he hasn't used the Ivory Dofus he stole from the Lenalds*\\n\\nIf I'd known that my own guawds would tuwn against me...","content.75.6086":"You don't undewstand! The thweat of the Muvegitants and the Sandyoptewa...","content.75.6087":"My wowd, I had no idea that Patwick was still wowking... You say he cweated the Muvegitants? On the Kween's owdews?","content.75.6088":"But she gowged hewself too!\\n\\n*The Wa Wabbit struggles to control his anger*\\n\\nWegawdless, without my Cawwot Dofus, I cannot wule my kingdom. And I will nevew suwwendew the Ivowy Dofus. Without that symbol of powew, my claim to the thwone will nevew be seen as legitimate! My people would not wespect me!","content.75.6089":"The othew leadews would nevew agwee to negotiate with me. Fow that mattew, I don't want to negotiate with them eithew. You'we wasting youw time!","content.75.6090":"All wight, you win! We will at least twy to meet to discuss mattews.\\n\\n*The Wa Wabbit quickly writes out several missives inviting the various peoples to an extraordinary council to discuss the recent upheavals on the island*\\n\\nEvewyone will think it's a twap. Good luck twying to convince the Loyal Lenald!","content.75.6091":"Just a moment... It says hele that the council will be held in the Wa's foltless. I'm not willing to tlavel to Wabbit tellitoly.\\n\\nMy answel is a lesounding no!","content.75.6092":"Hmm... Liz celtainly is a leckless one. She's plepaled to take such selious lisks to leach hel objectives... Vely well, then... In that case, I'll pay the council a visit.\\n\\nI can't let the voice of our deity place helself in danger, so I'll plotect hel myself!","content.75.6093":"*Liz reads the letter calmly*\\n\\nTo be honest, I'm not sule it's a good idea. But my desile to see the Lenald people living in peace is mole impoltant than the lisk of making things wolse. And aftel all, you ale the chosen one{[1*]?:} of the Lenald people.\\n\\nYou can count on me, adventulel!{[1*]?:}","content.75.6094":"*The old scientist struggles to remove the seal on the envelope. He finally gets it open and quickly reads over the letter*\\n\\nVewy well, I think it'll be essential that I be thewe to shawe my expewtise. Can you infowm Tom Eyto?\\n\\n*Patwick nods to himself, apparently remembering that he had something to tell you*\\n\\nI met him, you see. I was an incwedible expewience to speak with a Muvegitant. Now I wemembew my expewiments on him... It's all so vewy cleaw now! In the vast sea of my many ewwows, he wepwesents a new hope. It seems my pewsistence finally paid off!","content.75.6095":"Yes, I've met Patwick... So he's my creator. When he came to see me a few days ago, it all came back to me. I remembered the little songs he used to hum to himself while tending to the plants in this greenhouse.\\n\\nAnd now I remember his tender and affectionate words.\\n\\nOf course, I also remember the pain of his absence... Yes, one day he was no longer there. The other vegetables had left me, and Patwick had too. I think those were the earliest events that I perceived with my awakening consciousness...\\n\\nI agree to represent the Muvegitants at the council. We have a right to exist too!","content.75.6096":"I'm not sure it's a good idea. Bordegann and I are outsiders here... The Wabbit and Lenald people are so different from one another.\\n\\nI'm really worried I won't be able to restore peace between them. Worse yet, I might make some stupid mistake that would make the situation even worse!","content.75.6097":"All right, then, I'll do it. I trust you. Together, we'll make them listen to reason!","content.75.6098":"I really have no confidence in this whole council idea. I've been chased away by Wabbits in the past when I crossed into their territory to ask for help. If you ask me, it's better to leave them alone.\\n\\nOutsiders like us might just aggravate the situation by trying to reason with them.","content.75.6099":"Flattery will get you nowhere, my friend{[1*]?:}. But I still owe you a favor, since you helped me fight the Sandyoptera. So if you insist, I'll go with you for the council. Let's bring peace to Wabbit Island!","content.75.6100":"You're wasting your time with me. You know how I feel about the issue... I'm not interested in getting involved in things that don't concern me. All I care about is getting off this damned island as soon as I can.","content.75.6101":"I don't need their help. It's simply not my role to participate in this council. But all the same... I wish you good luck. Make them listen to reason.","content.75.6102":"You absolutely must find some way to bweak the deadlock. Wesolve one situation, and the west will follow. You must wecovew the Ivowy Dofus – that Dofus is how this whole thing got stawted.","content.75.6103":"I'm counting on you. Make some sowt of deal with the Wa. And do whatevew it takes – even if you have to twick him!","content.75.6104":"Ah, what a pleasuwe to see some fawmiliaw faces again... Who would have thought I might still end up playing a wole in the island's political intwigue?","content.75.6105":"Alas, it's impossible. The Cawwot Dofus wewe magically cweated by a fowmew Wa Wabbit. The mowe wecent Was have been unable to cweate any.\\n\\nCouldn't you just go hunt down Count Hawebourg?","content.75.6106":"*You sense that you're approaching the finish line. You have an idea in mind that you just can't let go of. You try to consider it from every angle to see if there isn't some plausible way to approach it. After all, you've already done so much for this island! The old scientist thoughtfully strokes his beard*\\n\\nPewhaps I could cwaft a fake Cawwot Dofus. I have all the wight tools to make one...","content.75.6107":"*Patwick seems to do a quick calculation in his head before continuing*\\n\\nI weckon that may be the only solution. You'll have to bawgain with the Wa Wabbit. Bwing me back some ingwedients, and I can cweate a fake DOFUS that should be able to twick him.\\n\\nYou'll find me in my labowatowy!","content.75.6108":"*Patwick thanks you for bringing him the ingredients. He sets to work for a few hours, then returns with a Cawwot Dofus. It's so perfect and smooth that you'd swear it was the real thing... You're sure it will fool the Wa Wabbit*","content.75.6109":"*The priestess of Inali turns to face you. She holds the Ivory Dofus in her hands. The Dofus shines with a faint glow, and you are hypnotized by its mysterious color*\\n\\n[#name]... This means so much to me. Thank you.\\n\\nHow wondelful that oul peoples ale now wolking to build peace. And how wondelful that the Ivoly Dofus is back in oul possession. This time, I will be sule not to fail in my duty.","content.75.6110":"All of this was made possible thlough youl effolts.\\n\\n*The priestess turns to face the grave of her father, the former guardian of the Ivory Dofus. You see a familiar four-letter name on the tombstone. A name very similar to Liz's own. You decide to take a moment of silence to reflect on the memory of this proud Lenald who was able to unite the two peoples once before. You have the feeling that you're carrying on his legacy*","content.75.6111":"Adventulel{[1*]?:}... You've managed to bling peace to oul island. Pelhaps...\\n*Liz hesitates for a moment*\\n\\nPelhaps if you used this Dofus, you could bling gleat joy and peace to the entile wolld.\\n\\n*Liz hands you the Dofus with great respect*","content.75.6112":"I tlied asking Inali what we should do, but she hasn't answeled my call. I'll nevel know if this is what oul goddess would have wanted. But this Dofus... it embodies the hopes and dleams of the Lenald people.\\n\\nYou ale oul new{[1*]?:} helo{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nI suppose you'le the one who leplesents our hopes now.","content.75.6113":"*Liz places the Dofus in your hands, then bids you a respectful farewell. This Dofus has been a source of great conflict, but also holds the promise of a lasting peace between the peoples. It embodies the hopes of the Lenald people... and now it's in your hands*\\n\\nI'm sule you have many adventules ahead of you. Falewell, [#name], and I hope we'll meet again one day. I plomise that I will watch ovel the Lenald people.","content.75.6114":"Ah, you've letulned! You will always be welcome{[1*]?:} hele, adventulel{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6115":"Perfect timing! I have something to show you. I don't think you'll be disappointed.","content.75.6116":"*Otomai walks over to a hidden chest near the fire. He takes two objects out of it. One is a notebook, and the other is something you can't quite identify. It looks like a large stone marked with unintelligible inscriptions*\\n\\nDuring one of my explorations on Zinit, I found these two artifacts. I'd like to know what you think of them.","content.75.6117":"I happen to go back every so often. I want to keep this old ship in working order. I enjoy delving into nooks and crannies, digging up new pieces to tinker with.\\n\\nThat visit was different from usual. I stumbled on a secret room. There was a door, heavily protected and hidden in a wall. After many attempts, I managed to force it open, but there was only a small chest inside. It contained a journal, as well as this stele.","content.75.6118":"It's a magical stele and a notebook. The stele uses technologies I've never studied.","content.75.6119":"*Otomai looks you right in the eyes, smiling*\\n\\nI haven't told you the best part yet. I studied the notebook and translated part of it. It's written entirely in the Eliatrope language. Seems to me it was used as a logbook by its previous owner.\\nI'll let you make up your own mind.","content.75.6120":"*Otomai smiles smugly again*\\n\\nSo, what did you think?","content.75.6121":"That's right.\\n\\nThe author also mentions a \"patriarch\", the \"council\", a \"great wandering\", and his \"brothers\". If what this says is true, it provides invaluable information on Eliatropes.\\n\\nAlso, he signs his notes with \"Qilby\". I haven't found it in any other piece of writing, so perhaps it's the author's name.","content.75.6122":"Well... It seems the Eliatropes still have things to show us through relics about their time in our world.","content.75.6123":"I called{[1*]?:} you because the stele doesn't seem to be working. It won't respond to any of my appeals even though it's charged up with Wakfu. It seems the passage of time hasn't helped matters.\\n\\nI think we could use Qilby's notes to try and activate it ourselves. Clearly all he had left was the Stasis theory. I don't know where I could find an adequate source to stabilize such a large amount of Wakfu, but since you've traveled all over, I thought you might have an idea?","content.75.6124":"Hm... Well, it's a good start... The hope of a new world habitable by Twelvians is certainly a great promise. New ecosystems or new technologies could be discovered there, who knows?\\n\\nWould you accompany me there to solve the mystery of the stele? Any help would be welcome, and I know you're not scared of an adventure! Our priority is to be cautious. Even the Eliatropes weren't able to activate the stele. It might contain a power much too great to be released carelessly. We don't even know where it will take us.","content.75.6125":"Let me stop you right there. I wasn't promoted to colonel in the elite Foggernaut navy because I did free favors for runt{[1*]?:}s. What can you offer me in return?","content.75.6126":"*Frida rubs her chin. It seems like she's about to ask you for something that won't be easy to get*\\n\\n*Suddenly, she snaps her fingers. Her face lights up with a brilliant idea in mind, and she eyes you*\\n\\nI'm someone who likes variety, you know. I'll do the favor you want, but in return, you'll go get a list of items for me.","content.75.6127":"So, what do you need?","content.75.6128":"Oh... But... Is that all?\\n\\n*Frida starts giggling*\\n\\nI guess I assumed you would ask me for something a lot more complicated! I see adventurers are more modest these days. It's almost wasteful to send you all over the world for such a rudimentary favor.","content.75.6129":"Help yourself. I don't need that much anyway...\\n\\n*After thinking for a moment, she gives you a magnanimous look*\\n\\nIn my great mercy, I wish to be lenient with you. You can do your experiments down there if you like, so long as you don't damage the mine. I'll have my Foggernauts stop while you're there.","content.75.6130":"By the Twelve! It's a miracle you made it back in one piece. On the other side, the stele fractured not long after you left. I tried to get it working again, but I'm thinking it's broken.","content.75.6131":"*Otomai takes a moment to think*\\n\\nI haven't heard much about projection artifacts. For as long as I can remember, certain types of magic have been employed to protect their users.\\n\\nMaybe the stele has that power! After all, it brought you back to our world right when Toross would have killed you.","content.75.6132":"Regardless, we can't answer these questions with any certainty if we don't look into how to repair it.","content.75.6133":"*Otomai sighs, then looks off into the distance, taking a few moments to think*\\n\\nI know all about great troubles turning the world upside down, you know... My instincts as a scientomage tell me I must go back, but... I have to admit you're right.\\n\\nShouldn't we just drop this and never bring it up again, for the whole World of Twelve's sake?","content.75.6134":"*Otomai chuckles. Without saying anything, he makes it clear that he appreciates your help*\\n\\nLet's seal this stele together and put an end to this whole thing.","content.75.6135":"Good! I'll have everyone get back to work. In the meantime, I'm expecting something from you.","content.75.6136":"Well, I'm training to be just as strong as master Goultard! I look up to him so much, and I wanna be a great warrior like him!","content.75.6137":"... Well, there is one other thing, but if I tell you, d'you promise not to laugh? I think my master would think it's a silly objective, since he's so strong.","content.75.6138":"Ever since I was little, I've watched Gladiatrool fights on jellivision. That's the combat arena at the Trool Fair, in case you didn't know. They look so cool in their costumes...\\n\\nAnyway, I've been dreaming ever since of becoming a champion one day! Then I'll be a strong enough warrior to even beat Ogrest!","content.75.6139":"I've never been there yet - too busy training... But they say there's tons of balloons and attractions, yummy stuff to eat, and you can even win gifts! Plus, there's fighting too!","content.75.6140":"OK, you go ahead first. But I'll catch up to you eventually, y'know! And once I finally get there, maybe I'll let you team up with me in the arena.\\n\\nYou'd better make sure you're even stronger{[1*]?:} by then, 'cause I sure will be! ","content.75.6141":"Haha... At my age and with my nose for business, it's hardly surprising! You can start building a little nest egg as a mercenary, then grow it further with a few smart transactions at the Marketplace.","content.75.6142":"It'd be far too easy if I told you all my tricks! Don't rush yourself, and calmly follow the teachings of my god. You know, even my fortune pales in comparison to the Great Miser's!","content.75.6143":"Even more than you think. They say that his divine dimension is made entirely of gold as far as the eye can see, and filled with gigantic chests that could hold all the kamas in the world!","content.75.6144":"As far as I know, no one has been able to go there to confirm those legends. But many Twelvians dream of being able to see Enurado's great mountains of gold with their own eyes... or to steal them. But I'm afraid that neither Sram nor Eugor can hope to pierce the defenses of that golden paradise!","content.75.6145":"Ha ha! If that ever happens, bring me back a little souvenir! It doesn't seem likely, but you seem to have potential. I'm willing to bet a coin on your future exploits! Who knows? Maybe Enutrof himself will reward your bravery!","content.75.6146":"Thanks for the compliment! Care for a taste? It's a treechnid-smoked piwi fricassee.\\n\\nIt's one of my specialties. Trust me, you'll love it!","content.75.6147":"Ha ha ha, of course! Well, I won't deny that sometimes I have to take a few risks. And yes, I've been responsible for a few culinary disasters... But so far, none of my dishes have ever killed anyone!","content.75.6148":"Not to worry!\\n\\nWhen you're an experienced cook, it's easy to create new flavors with these exotic ingredients. I can assure you that this recipe is entirely safe, and you'll even be asking for seconds!","content.75.6149":"So? Not bad, huh?","content.75.6150":"I told you so! If your adventures ever take you to Emelka, I recommend the innkeeper's gobball stew. I'm telling you, it's an absolute masterpiece!","content.75.6151":"That happens to me a lot. In fact, just a few days ago, I was serving an adventurer in a swimsuit who was just back from Bilbiza.\\n\\nHe told me about a dimension made completely out of jelly, and he asked me to whip up a dessert with the samples he'd brought back with him.","content.75.6152":"Yep, jellies. They look a bit like blops with their soft, transparent bodies. Don't ask me how a jelly can be alive, I'm just a simple cook!","content.75.6153":"Who knows? I think he called it the Jellith Dimension. I definitely plan to go there one day. Imagine the incredible deserts I could create with those jellies! I can't wait to get into the kitchen!","content.75.6154":"That's right, friend{[1*]?:}, you caught me! I'm originally from Amakna. They put me in charge of the Astrub Fields, to take care of the workers and make sure the local residents have good food on their plates!","content.75.6155":"Never been there{[1*]?:}? It's definitely way off in the countryside, but it's a great place to do your own thing. It's also the closest nation to Astrub! The air is pure, even when it smells a bit like moogrr, the food is good and the people are warm and welcoming! I've heard some rumors that paint a less rosy picture, but...","content.75.6156":"My dad told me in a letter that old Joe is having trouble with his moogrrs. I didn't understand everything he was blabbing about, but it smells like a dungheap to me. It seems that earthquakes are more frequent, the harvests are no good, and plants have even started attacking the farmers! By Bettie, I've never seen so many problems in our quiet little corner of Amakna!","content.75.6157":"Certainly! And just to keep things interesting, Riktus bandits have started showing up nearby. Ah well, I suppose every nation's got its problems! If you ever feel like giving the locals a helping hand, I'd suggest having a look at the mercenary boards. ","content.75.6160":"Hahaha! It's true - when there's a brawl to be joined, I'm usually at the front of the line! With some training and a few centuries of fighting, you'll eventually be as good as me. But no need to worry about that!","content.75.6161":"Really? I tend to forget that we're not forged of the same metal...\\n\\nWell, you'd better get to it right away, in that case! No time to lose! My first lesson: If you find yourself facing a stronger opponent and your muscles aren't enough, use your head!","content.75.6162":"I've smacked my knuckles into more faces than I can remember. I think it was Rushu who gave me the most trouble. You wouldn't know it to look at him, but when he really goes all-out, he can be a real pain to fight against!","content.75.6163":"Yep, in person! He didn't much appreciate me taking out my frustration on his henchmen in the Shustuft Crust... I don't recommend going there on vacation - the demon dimension doesn't have that many nice places to visit.\\n\\nThat being said, there are plenty of monsters to smash, if that's what interests you!","content.75.6164":"Ah, well... I'm a bit of a special case... But it seems that a scientist was recently able to open a portal to that dimension on a deserted island. The Shusnitch Reef, near Brakmar. You'll have to get stronger if you don't want to get burned by those fiery beasts!","content.75.6165":"Hee hee... Yes, when you're lucky enough to live as long as I have, you wind up accumulating quite an assortment of items. It's important to put the Pals' fortune to work for the economy! But don't worry, it doesn't all go to books and knick-knacks. It's thanks to our fortune that Astrub has been able to start rebuilding, and I'm pleased to see our efforts bearing fruit.","content.75.6166":"Well, you know, we don't do it solely from the goodness of our hearts... Pappy and I see it as an investment in the future! *rubs hands eagerly* ","content.75.6167":"I do have to admit, I've got a penchant for impulse purchases. Every time I go to the stands at the Kelba Market, I always come home with a huge pile of merchandise!","content.75.6168":"Right, I'm sorry, you were only recently incarnated. Kelba is one of the most renowned markets in the World of Twelve. Good old Hadibal Toot knows how to get me buying anything and everything in his shop!","content.75.6169":"The island is right between Astrub and Amakna, and it's even connected to Amakna by a bridge. I've heard that Riktus bandits have recently been blocking access to the bridge, though. I'd recommend that you take the zaap portal or hop on a boat to get there!","content.75.6170":"You're sure to find something you like, even though nothing beats a piece of equipment lovingly hand-crafted by a skilled artisan! If you plan to go there, I must warn you of a danger lurking on the island...","content.75.6171":"Hard to say... The Riktus are a rot at the Nation of Amakna's core, and there's nothing to say he's one of them. He's a bandit who only attacks the Kelba Market specifically. They call him the \"Black Crow\" because of his costume and his mount... and together, they're terrorizing the region's merchants! Be careful not to wind up in his talons, as he's said to be quite a fearsome fighter.","content.75.6172":"Oh, you're not a customer{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:}, but... So be it. And what makes you say I have the answer to your question?","content.75.6173":"A keen observation, indeed... I'll answer you if you promise to come back to my workshop... this time as a customer!{[1*]?:}","content.75.6174":"Very well. It's a way to access my god's dimension: Ecaflipus. Or part of it, at least - it's actually far larger, but only an elite few are chosen to have access to the rest of his domain.","content.75.6175":"The Big Tease supposedly created the Ecaflipus arenas in a moment of boredom, to allow Twelvians to face off against each other in joy, good humor, and large quantities of blood. I've heard rumors that he occasionally organizes bets on the fights. Needless to say, all of that is far too brutal to interest someone of my station...","content.75.6176":"Looking at your gear, I'm hardly surprised... Simply touch the statue and you'll be teleported{[1*]?:} there. But for Ecaflip's sake, please do something about your style! We'll see about that the next time you visit.","content.75.6177":"Of course! Our world has suffered enough as it is. It's our duty to preserve what we can, to allow it to rebuild after this catastrophe...","content.75.6178":"Ah... *sighs* \\nYou adventurers{[1*]?:} are all the same... Don't look at it as a chore, think of it as a quest in its own right! Developing an ecosystem comes with its own joys, disappointments, and rewards. It's the god Osamodas's favorite pastime! ","content.75.6179":"Ah, so I've piqued your curiosity, heh heh! Let me tell you a story that my grandmother shared with me when I was little... A tale from time immemorial, when Osamodas and the other gods shaped the World of Ten and allowed life to develop there.","content.75.6180":"Unfortunately, the first creatures that appeared weren't all viable - a few of them eradicated all the others with no sense of balance. And though the Celestial Tamer respects the principle of survival of the fittest, he nevertheless decided to create a dimension to test and protect his creations before sending them into the new world. That way, they'd have a chance to contribute to the diversity of the Krosmoz.","content.75.6181":"That's no surprise - lots of people deny its existence! Personally, I believe in it. Those who have passed this myth down through the generations call that divine land Osamosa. It's said to lie on the back of one of Osamodas's dragons, whose iridescent scales shine brilliantly in the vastness of Ingloriom. It must be a magnificent sight.","content.75.6182":"It's said that Osamosa is where the Master of Beasts runs all of his experiments. The ecosystem in that dimension is apparently so unique that the creatures which stay there develop incredible vitality and abilities. My grandmother used to say that all living creatures in this world started out in the gardens of Osamosa before being incarnated in the World of Twelve.","content.75.6183":"Oh, really? An{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}, are you? Are you sure{[1*]?:} you don't need any more riches? I've heard a rumor that could be quite lucrative... But since you don't seem to be interested{[1*]?:}, I'll just hire someone else!","content.75.6184":"Alrighty, then! *chuckles*\\nHave you heard of the Mineral Tower? It's a mysterious rock formation that supposedly emerged from the waves a few years back. They say it's inhabited by a terrible witch who's come back from the dead...","content.75.6185":"Well, you're not wrong. But the monsters prowling around there are made of minerals with unique properties that are worth their weight in gold! It's even said that if you use them to craft equipment, the resulting gear will have very strong magic powers.","content.75.6186":"But it's the truth! My sources are reliable! Listen, here's what I'll propose. You bring me back the ores from those monsters, and I'll sell them on to my network of crafters. Then we'll share the profits: 95% for me, 5% for you.","content.75.6187":"Come on, I was only testing you! You're obviously a shrewd one, heh heh... How about 10% for you? No? All right, then, 15%, but that's my last - uh - Hey! Wait! If we work together, we could dominate the marketplace! Come back!","content.75.6188":"There are countless unsavory places in the World of Twelve. I was sent out long ago to investigate cursed locations for restless souls. I don't mind telling you that I would have preferred working on my tan in Bilbiza than becoming an exorcist priest! But someone's got to do the work to help those poor souls return to the cycle of incarnation.","content.75.6189":"I'm too old for all that now, but you do seem quite eager for action. With a bit of training, you could likely free Monk Island of its curse...","content.75.6190":"Many years ago, the island was a charming place. The monks brewed their beer, and tourists could visit the grounds and pay tribute to the departed in the cemetery.  But all that changed when the Nun's ghost appeared... The monks lost their lives or their minds, and this place became a sinister monument to a bygone era.","content.75.6191":"I was asked to exorcise her, but she was too strong. I just barely avoided falling under her control and becoming one of her servants. She wanted to make me the top priest in her new cult! Escaping with my life cost me my underwear and a big part of my dignity... But it was still better than dying in that cemetery!","content.75.6192":"No, you heard me right. Those fanatical monks tore off my underwear while trying to keep me from leaving the abbey! Those degenerates started worshipping it like it was a gift from the gods... I suppose that having been picked by the Nun made me some kind of chosen one in their eyes. They've even renamed the place \"The Undieworld\" in honor of that so-called relic.","content.75.6193":"That's ancient history now. Still, don't expect me to set foot on that island again! If you really think you can manage to purify the place, I give you my blessing. But make sure your underwear is on tight - you never know what might happen.","content.75.6194":"*You approach the Hullcatz. He seems to be purring to himself as he scans the horizon*\\n\\nFelix, where in the world could you be?","content.75.6195":"Hmmm? Ah...\\n\\n*The Hullcatz turns back to you with a faint purr*\\n\\nI've known many sailors who weighed anchor and set sail in search of freedom and adventure. Felix was one of them. Alas, there's no shortage of tragic endings for those who underestimate the sea.","content.75.6196":"Yes, the waters have been unsteady lately.\\n\\nEven so, stories of mysterious disappearances were already quite common in the World of Twelve, even before the cataclysm. Legends of cursed islands and ferocious monsters... Or worse.","content.75.6197":"*The Hullcatz chuckles warmly, touched by your sunny determination. But then he catches himself and adopts a more serious attitude. His usual purring also drops a note deeper*\\n\\nYou sound just like Felix... Always in search of the truth, and the thrill of discovery. The last mystery he went after got the better of him. Do you think you've got what it takes to solve this puzzle in his place?","content.75.6198":"Since the dawn of time, they say that an island appears very briefly on the horizon. And what do you think became of the unlucky sailors who have explored it? They all immediately disappeared, along with the island...\\n\\nAs if the island and those sailors had never existed.","content.75.6199":"Where do you suppose it goes when it's not here in our world? I've heard lots of stories about that island that's as elusive as the sea fog. Too many for it to be just a silly rumor.\\n\\nBe careful{[1*]?:}. Sometimes nature is our worst enemy...\\n\\n*A final purr, more nostalgic this time, marks the end of his story. The Hullcatz turns back to the sea, as though to avoid missing the moment of his friend's return*","content.75.6200":"Thank you for your consideration, adventurer{[1*]?:}, but this is only the beginning. I'm training hard for an even grander objective! The time will soon come for the shadow vigilante to bring order to the heavens.","content.75.6201":"They say that the worst scoundrels in the Krosmoz gather in a place that can't be reached by ordinary mortals. To tear out the evil at its root, I'll have to go to the dimension that's associated with crime in all its forms: Srambad.","content.75.6202":"Yes! I was saved by the gods to serve this single purpose - a divine mission that I intend to carry out, no matter what. Don't try to join me in my quest for redemption, for it's a task I must accomplish alone.","content.75.6203":"Not yet... But that's just one more obstacle to overcome! For now, I'm concentrating on bringing order to these sewers. Shreddie and his Grambos are up to something, I'm sure of it. Once I've dealt with this situation, I'll focus on the question of traveling between dimensions.","content.75.6204":"Oh, these? They're the proof of my Ouginak education! My many travels have been a part of that too... You learn quickly with only one good eye. I'm just glad it was my prey who wound up as a fur coat that day! Haha!","content.75.6205":"It's a hard life in the Ouginak tribes! I'm from Ohwymi, a desert island east of here. We're trained from childhood to become warriors or hunters. Since life is tough there, we have to earn our meals, find water, and do everything we can to be useful to the pack. Otherwise, only death awaits us.","content.75.6206":"It's a trial from our god, and we are all honored to follow his teachings! The weak have no place in my pack, unlike my cousin Tovak's. Regardless, I quickly grew accustomed to this life, and even found myself needing more. That's why I set out for adventure... but I'm sure you know that feeling well!","content.75.6207":"I was looking for traces of ancient Ouginak tribes from the Dofus Era. According to my clan's oral tradition, our ancestors were nomads. So I traveled to Brakmar to visit the Sidimote Moors, which was one of the main places in their journey. But those moors are just vast fields of ruins now, disfigured by magma and infested with skeletons that have come back to life!","content.75.6208":"There's danger in Bonta too, but it's sneakier there since the environment looks less hostile overall. Centuries ago, the Cania Plains were home to Ouginak tribes. I was tracking down a lead there when an enormous blibli got the jump on me! It proved a valiant foe, and I still wear its hide on my back as a souvenir of that battle. That trophy and my scars are the only things I've kept from those days.","content.75.6209":"I have to say, I'm fine with having chosen Astrub as the place to hang up my boots and tend to my wounds. Life is peaceful here, and if I ever get that urge for adventure again, I can always pack up and leave!","content.75.6210":"Yes indeedy! But that's not the only activity I've got up to over the years. I did all kinds of little jobs in Bonta before setting off for adventure. I've dragged my shovel to every corner of the World of Twelve as a treasure hunter, so I know it like the back of my hand! ","content.75.6211":"Exactly. You've never heard of the Strouds? Our family is very influential in this nation! If you ever make your way to the windy village, you should drop in on my uncle Baal and tell him I sent you. He may not look it, but he's an excellent host! Oh, and not to brag, but I'm a bit of a minor celebrity there...","content.75.6212":"Oh yeah! My team and I lit up all the gobbowl stadiums when I was young! Those were great times, but it wasn't such a great way to make money... So I traded in my gobbowl ball for a shovel and hit the road. If you've never seen a gobbowl match, you really must visit the stadium!","content.75.6213":"It's hard to say... The party atmosphere in Bilbiza is really something special! I'd sum up my experience on the island as being full of music, dancing, cocktails, and the occasional blackout... Come to think of it, that would also be a perfect summary of my adventure in Pandalucia! I think I drank enough bamboo milk on that trip for an entire lifetime, ha ha ha!","content.75.6214":"It's a sun-drenched valley, a fertile land that's home to most of the Pandawa people. People come from all four corners of the world to celebrate with rich traditional meals and cool pints of bamboo milk. In a word, it's the joyful land of happy travelers!","content.75.6215":"Oh, it's my pleasure - just one scrapper helping another! If you'd like to make a few kamas to help fund your adventures, I may have some work for you. Feel free to come by and see me once in a while.","content.75.6216":"My son? What do you want to know? That immature boy went off to study ruins in Bonta! No, he doesn't tell me what he's up to.\\n\\nOf course, I'm in no hurry to see him again any time soon... He'd make fun of my appearance.\\n\\n*An ever-so-slightly bitter smile crosses Jenry Hones's face*","content.75.6217":"Yes. The Honeses have traveled a lot, you see. We've braved many dangers and solved many mysteries...\\n\\n*Jenry Hones Sr. looks wistfully to the sky for a brief moment, then pulls himself together*\\n\\nAnyway. The last time we saw each other, he was studying multiple leads at once... He told me he wanted to go to Bonta, and more specifically to the Cania and Kara regions.","content.75.6218":"Something about a university... And something else... They were... Crocodyls, I think... Come to think of it, Crocoburio is closely linked to the history of Bonta.\\n\\n*Jenry Hones pushes his glasses up, then turns to you with an accusatory tone*\\n\\nSay... You're awfully curious{[1*]?:} about all this...","content.75.6219":"Absolutely! This forest area is very modest compared to the Sadida Kingdom, but I'm quite proud of it all the same! A lot of people say it's dangerous to walk around here, but as long as you don't damage the trees, the Treechnids should leave you alone.","content.75.6220":"No, my family settled in Astrub long before I was born. But I've been there a few times to meet my cousins, or to take part in a few... not-so-pleasant ceremonies. Our last meeting plunged the entire Sadida people into a period of deep mourning...","content.75.6221":"*though still as radiant as ever, Maui's face loses its typical joy, replaced by a look of profound pain*\\n\\nOur beloved queen has... returned to the divine meadows of Sadida. She was still so young, always listening to the people and concerned for their well-being... Our tears fed the streams on that day. I like to believe that our prayers guided her soul to help her sprout anew and illuminate the world, when the time comes.","content.75.6222":"Thanks a lot. Even though it's sometimes hard to accept, it's the cycle of life. Wishing for our queen to return would go against everything we believe in as Sadidas. This is how things are, and we'll just keep moving forward. The queen planted the seeds of peace and prosperity for our people. We have full confidence in our king to continue her efforts and harvest the fruit that they bear!","content.75.6223":"*smiles again*\\n\\nBut enough of that depressing talk! If you get the chance, you should go to the Sadida Kingdom. Everyone should see our tree of life at least once in their lives. After all, it's surely the biggest tree in the entire world! But I should warn you that the kingdom's wildlife is much tougher than what you'll find in my forest.","content.75.6224":"Er, yes, the digs are going fine. Was it my father who's been talking to you about me?","content.75.6225":"Ah, [#name]! Perfect timing. I was just looking into a lead about a tribe from the Primitive Era.","content.75.6226":"Absolutely. I suppose it was my father who told you I was working on that. For a long time, they were considered primitive and savage beings... But over a thousand years ago, crocodyls nearly took over the entire World of Twelve.\\n\\n*Jenry stands up straight and gives you an intense stare. He can't tell how much you know about the crocodyl people*\\n\\nIt's rather difficult to find any information about them since Ogrest's Chaos.","content.75.6227":"Well, yes... I discovered a stele not far from here, in Cania. It describes the birth of Crocoburio, the son of Grougalorasalar, a great crocodyl warrior who terrorized Bonta.\\n\\nIt's a story that dates back many centuries. It's always thrilling to try and figure out what's truth and what's fiction!","content.75.6228":"Interesting! So you've learned more about Crocoburio... He must have been an incredible warrior. I wonder if he just had superior strength, or if he had some sort of special power.\\n\\nIn any case, since there aren't many crocodyls around here these days, I think we can deduce that the birth of this supernatural creature wasn't enough to restore the might of the Jade Empire.","content.75.6229":"It was a crocodyl empire that existed during the Primitive Era. Legend says that the founder of that empire had a weapon of extraordinary power.\\n\\n*Jenry looks up at the sky and mumbles something briefly, then looks back at you*\\n\\nHe wound up being brutally annihilated after a few centuries, but I'm not sure how or why... So? Admit it, these stories are pretty fascinating!","content.75.6230":"Oh, that... I've found better fishing spots in my travels, but I'm past the days of dragging my old bones out to the middle of the big blue! I may not get many nibbles, but I'm enjoying my well-deserved retirement. Tranquil... and alone.","content.75.6231":"You don't quit easy, do ya? Well... I might have a coupla stories to tell ya. Like the time when my li'l' dinghy got caught in a storm and I washed up on Moon Island. I had to survive on my own for a few months, hidin' from the scorchin' sun in the shade of the kokonut trees. ","content.75.6232":"Yeah. I ate kokonuts to avoid dehydration, plus whatever fish I could catch, though I had to move around a lot on account of the Crocodyls always tryin' to kill me. For a while, I reckoned survivin' in the forest'd be easier, but I changed my mind when I nearly landed in the local Kanniballs' cook pot!","content.75.6233":"Ya got that right! The Kanniballs worship a god that looks like a monkey - the one the island's named after, I guess. The totems an' all that are to honor that divine ape... Those crazy fanatics wanted to sacrifice me in his name! Seems they even got some other Hullcatz before me... I was better off toasting my buns on the scaly folks' island, tell you what...","content.75.6234":"An exploration ship finally came up to shore to drop off some adventurers. They almost attacked me on sight - and to be fair, with my shaggy fur all caked with dried blood, I prob'ly looked more like a monster than a Hullcatz! They brought me back to Astrub, an' it's been good times ever since.","content.75.6235":"*The Hullcatz gazes pensively at the statue. You approach him and hear him mumbling to himself. Perhaps he knows something about this city's history*","content.75.6236":"Hmm? Oh! Greetingzh! I wazh jusht thinking that this shtatue izhn't kept up very well. The plaque hazh become quite illegible over time. A real shame...","content.75.6237":"What the... You've never heard of Brutash? He'zh the founder of the city!\\n\\nThey shay thish place wazh nothing more than a makeshift campground in the Primitive Era. But then the camp became a village, and it kept growing until it wazh almosht azh big as the other great cities! In no time at all, the city of mershenaries wazh born.","content.75.6238":"That was eshpecially true back then. The beer flowed freely when the mershenariezh came back from their missionzh.\\n\\nOne day, Brutash shaid, \"The godzh invented water sho we could wash our feet with it. If you want to quench your thirsht, there are plenty of other drinksh to choozhe from.\"\\n\\nWhat a great man... a true visionary!","content.75.6239":"It'sh tradition! Over the yearzh and azh the conflictsh rolled on, the city's rezhidents gradually turned away from the art of war. Merchantsh and artizhanzh came pouring in from all over the World of Twelve!\\n\\nThat'sh how the city became what it izh today: a key economic hub and a training area for up-and-coming adventurerzh.","content.75.6240":"That'sh why I'm sho shad to shee our heritage decaying over time. There are only the ancientsh and a few old Hullcatzh like me left to tell you all thezhe shtoriezh!\\n\\nIf you're intereshted in learning about the city, you should find shome other folksh who can tell you more about it!\\n\\n*The Hullcatz turns politely away*","content.75.6241":"It's true we still haven't really gotten to the bottom of this story. According to my information, there is at least one other stele in the region. But I don't know where it is...\\n\\n*Jenry puts his hand thoughtfully to his chin*\\n\\nThose steles were written in the Dofus Era, so they could be at the bottom of the ocean by now.","content.75.6242":"Well, well, well! Did you manage to find the missing stele? Tell me all about it!","content.75.6243":"Incredible... I'd heard rumors of its existence, but it seems that Crocoburio really did inherit Crocobur hundreds of years ago.\\n\\n*Jenry Hones's eyes light up, and he places his hand on your shoulder*\\n\\nWe have to find out what became of Crocoburio, whatever it takes. Then we'll be able to track down his sword!","content.75.6244":"Did you know that 70% of archaosology is done in the library?\\n\\nIf you ask me, you should talk to the Bonta archivist, Master Hoot. He can tell you about any books about the life and death of Crocoburio. You'll find him at Bonta Guard HQ.","content.75.6245":"So Croulaklakoss was able to defeat Grougalorasalar... And Crocoburio died too at the gates of Bonta.\\n\\nSince this tale dates back a good eight centuries or so, Crocoburio's tomb must be in the old Bontarian cemetery. As luck would have it, I've already studied the Bontarian ruins. I've got a pretty good idea of where that cemetery may be located!","content.75.6246":"There's only one way to find out!\\n\\nIf there's anything left of that cemetery, it should be to the southeast of the current city of Bonta. It's surely lost under the sea at this point. You go on ahead - I'll find a boat and catch up to you.","content.75.6247":"There you are, [#name]! My intuition was correct. There's no doubt about it - we've found Crocoburio's tomb!\\n\\n*You look around. The archaosologist's words echo and blur in the dark, dank vault. Jenry pulls out a Louie Gee Mushroom to cast some light around you, and you notice some bones lying in a corner of the cave*\\n\\nWho would have guessed there was a cave beneath his tombstone? Hard to understand how it could have survived Ogrest's Chaos...","content.75.6248":"Evidently, these are indeed his bones. There's also this stele written in Crocodyl... I've taken the liberty of translating it.\\n\\nAh... and to think, Lebbocq was so sure he was way ahead of me...\\n\\n*Jenry smiles proudly*","content.75.6249":"Let's start with the bones.\\n\\nIt's clearly a crocodyl skeleton, about... Six to nine hundred years old, looks like. That would line up with Crocoburio.\\n\\nBut if the Cania stele is correct... I don't remember all the details, but I think I recall a passage that said Crocoburio was very tall. What do you think?","content.75.6250":"That's true. Now, about the sword.\\n\\n*Jenry crouches over the sword, thrust into the ground beside the crocodyl skeleton*\\n\\nIf this is Crocobur, I'm not sensing any power. I think it's just a rusty old replica... If the legends are true, the sword should hold exceptional power.","content.75.6251":"I appreciate that possibility, but I'm still sticking with my intuition that this isn't the real Crocobur. Look.\\n\\n*Jenry points out a few vulgarities at the base of the crossguard and on the pommel*\\n\\nI'd say it was designed to honor Crocoburio in his final resting place. A sword of incomparable power wouldn't have been abandoned in some dark cave, right?","content.75.6252":"What I can say is that this stele is much more recent. It's from before Ogrest's Chaos, that's for certain. Still, it must be...\\n\\n*Jenry runs one hand around the edge of the stele, then walks partway around it, rubbing his chin thoughtfully*\\n\\nAbout three centuries old.","content.75.6253":"The content is quite strange as well. It talks about prophecy and resurrection...\\n\\n*Jenry turns back to you to hear your response*","content.75.6254":"I suppose it's possible. As part of my research on Crocoburio, I learned that a number of tricksters had tried to pass themselves off as Crocoburio or one of his descendants.\\n\\nI was even able to locate one of those imposters. He was a slightly crazy Crocodyl who had settled in the Cania Swamps a few years back.\\n\\nClearly, Crocoburio's name alone carries great meaning.","content.75.6255":"Yes. But if that's true, no one knows what's become of Crocoburio since then.","content.75.6256":"I'm afraid we don't have any satisfactory conclusion.\\n\\nPerhaps Crocoburio was revived, then headed off somewhere else. Perhaps Crocobur was lost. We certainly know that Ogrest's Chaos played a role in the Crocodyls' disappearance.\\n\\nWe've learned that the old legends of Bonta were true. But we won't learn anything else about that nation.","content.75.6257":"Come on! We've made a historic discovery! If my father could only see this...\\n\\n*Jenry seems happy. He's obviously excited to share his discovery with the others. You still don't fully grasp the thrill of archaosology... at least, not yet*","content.75.6258":"I discovered a stele not far from here, in Cania. It describes the birth of Crocoburio, the son of Grougalorasalar, a great crocodyl warrior who terrorized Bonta.\\n\\nIf this story interests{[1*]?:} you, I'd encourage you to read it! We'll talk more about it later.","content.75.6259":"Our research on the crocodyls has been deadlocked since we found the Cania stele. According to my information, there is at least one other stele in the region. But I don't know where it is...\\n\\n*Jenry puts his hand thoughtfully to his chin*\\n\\nThose steles were written in the Dofus Era, so they could be at the bottom of the ocean by now.","content.75.6260":"In that case, I should inform you that there are several sea routes to Bonta. One of them is southeast of here, and the other to the southwest.","content.75.6261":"We unearthed a lead about the legendary sword Crocobur. Unfortunately, it was lost...\\n\\nWe have to find out what became of Crocoburio, whatever it takes. Then we'll be able to track down his sword!\\n\\nIf you ask me, you should talk to the Bonta archivist, Master Hoot. He can tell you about any books about the life and death of Crocoburio. You'll find him at Bonta Guard HQ.","content.75.6262":"Crocoburio's tomb must be in the old Bontarian cemetery. As luck would have it, I've already studied the Bontarian ruins. I've got a pretty good idea of where that cemetery may be located!\\n\\nIf there's anything left of it, it should be to the southeast of the current city of Bonta. It's surely lost under the sea at this point. You go on ahead - I'll find a boat and catch up to you.","content.75.6263":"You're back! Say, have you got my little daily gift...?","content.75.6264":"Thank you very much! Feel free to come back tomorrow. I've still got a mountain of gifts to prepare with Father Kwismas.","content.75.6265":"Psst! How would you like to help save Kwismas? Father Kwismas gave me a shopping list to prepare gifts for all the Twelvians, but I need a little help. Needless to say, you'll get a nice reward for each ingredient you bring me.","content.75.6266":"Hello... Have you come to help the Guild of Hunters?","content.75.6267":"I DON'T KNOW WHO YOU ARE, SQUIRT,{[1*]?:}, BUT IF I WANTED TO INVADE THE WORLD OF TWELVE, I WOULDN'T HAVE STARTED BY SETTING UP STATUES. I WOULD'VE JUST DESTROYED EVERYTHING!\\n\\n*Rushu bursts into laughter. The sound is so loud that your organs shake*","content.75.6268":"*Rushu seems taken aback by your power. The Vestiges of the old Demon Kings that appeared thanks to the strange key you crafted may have helped you get the upper hand in this fight... but it's your unwavering determination that has put the King of the Demons on his heels*\\n\\n*With another raging blow, you send Rushu to the ground. The Shushus all around you hold their tongues. None dares interfere in this situation. You walk slowly towards the Lord of the Shadows, still gasping for breath after your intense battle. A heavy silence surrounds you. You grab Rushu by the beard and force him to look at you*","content.75.6269":"*The Lord of the Shadows responds in a much quieter voice than you've grown accustomed to{[1*]?:}*\\n\\nI don't know what you're talking about, mortal{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6270":"*Rushu pulls his beard free with a turn of his hand*\\n\\nI TOLD YOU, I DON'T KNOW!\\n\\nLIKE I SAID, IF I EVER INVADE THE WORLD OF TWELVE, IT WON'T BE WITH A BUNCH OF DAMN STATUES!","content.75.6271":"*You hold Rushu's hateful stare for a moment, then realize something. You can't see inside his mind, but his way of doing things seems very linear. The Lord of the Shadows just wants to destroy everything. He will betray and lie to achieve his goals, but is he capable of subtlety?*\\n\\n*You stop short, chilled to the bone by a terrifying revelation. You think back to Sthulhu, and remember him telling you to never trust a demon... then chuckling. His sinister laugh echoes in your head as you let out a flustered gasp*","content.75.6272":"*Rushu pauses to catch his breath, stunned by your brutal confrontation*\\n\\nDON'T SPEAK TO ME OF BROTHERHOOD! YOU KNOW NOTHING OF MY FAMILY AFFAIRS.\\n\\nYOU DARE USE THEIR POWER AGAINST ME... FACE ME IN A FAIR FIGHT AND I'LL SMASH YOU TO BITS!","content.75.6273":"*You hear Rushu screaming and yelling threats from behind you. He seems to be sticking to his overall theme of destroying the world*","content.75.6274":"Hmmm...\\n\\n*The young woman lets out a guilty-sounding groan*","content.75.6275":"*Ahr Khayuh gives you a shy smile without answering, then casts an admiring glance at Sthulhu. She's clearly caught in his grip. An indescribable feeling comes over you*\\n\\nSorry... It's nothing personal.","content.75.6276":"*Jacqueline seems to be listening closely*\\n\\nYes? What did you want to tell me?","content.75.6277":"*You briefly recount your adventures and explain how Juspark helped{[1*]?:} you to locate the hideout*\\n\\nOh, you had help from Juspark and Farle? Hmmm...\\n\\n*The young woman nods - it seems you're close to your goal. Apparently, she'll be able to continue helping the local animals once they've been freed of the Bearkneck's evil influence*","content.75.6278":"*The young woman gives a serious nod, encouraging you to continue*","content.75.6279":"I'm relieved to hear that.\\n\\nWell done, adventurer{[1*]?:}! I was sure that all my efforts to preserve the ice floe and the Plantiguards would be in vain. It really seems just about impossible...","content.75.6280":"I still have a lot of work to do if I want to restore some semblance of ecological balance in this area, and I'm the only one who can do it...","content.75.6281":"No thanks, it'll be fine, I'm used to it. I managed all by myself for a very long time, you know...\\n\\n*Jacqueline's coldness once you're no longer of use to her surprises you. She seems quite proud of her accomplishments. You decide to leave*","content.75.6282":"Ah ha! Perfect timing, I just made a fresh pot of makoffee.\\n\\n*Juspark hands you a cup of piping hot makoffee*\\n\\nIt'll cheer me up to talk with you a bit. Plus, considering how damn cold it is here...","content.75.6283":"*You recount your adventures in exhaustive detail. Juspark goes through the full range of emotions. At the end of your story, she sighs and gives a sympathetic pout. She places a hand on your shoulder with an exaggerated gesture*\\n\\nI'm really sorry you had to go through all that.","content.75.6284":"Come on, you're not the type to lose heart that easily! Chin up! Besides, we never stop learning in life.\\n\\nWe don't know where those strange phenomena are coming from yet, but now we've got a good lead, right?","content.75.6285":"Really? Have you already forgotten what I told you?\\n\\n*Juspark leans towards you, pointedly raising one index finger*\\n\\nI thought the Shushus were behind it... But you correctly realized that it wasn't them. So we've been able to narrow down the possibilities!","content.75.6286":"You know what? I think you should take a little time off to rest.\\n\\nYou've earned a vacation after your trip to the Shustuft Crust, right? Step away for a while, then start over from the beginning. It might be useful for you. We often see things more clearly when we're not right in the middle of them.","content.75.6287":"Hmm... okey-doke. I can offer you some little cookies. What do you say? They're made from pingwin eggs, flowerflake flour, and fish. And just a touch of salt to bring the flavors out. Wondering how I got hold of salt around here? Well... I collected some tears from Morsnivel the Tearful. I boiled them up, and next thing you know, yummy salt at the bottom of the pot! Let me know what you think.\\n\\n*You wonder how she managed to make the flowerflake flour*","content.75.6288":"*You describe your altercation with the supreme Demon King. Juspark gets straight to the point, as usual*\\n\\nLittle Rushu seems awfully simple-minded. I expected better from him.","content.75.6289":"Ah, ah! He might also want to keep them so he can destroy them later. After all, he's a master destroyer. Maybe it's a bit like a snack that he's keeping in his back pocket for later?\\n\\nI don't know if such a cruel creature could really feel any attachment for a brotherhood he exterminated.","content.75.6290":"*The young woman nods politely, then holds up a finger* \\n\\nEven so, you can be proud{[1*]?:} of yourself. You've stood up to the most powerful demons in existence.","content.75.6291":"By the way, if you happen to acquire any other Dofus, you must refrain from using them against Ogrest.\\n\\nI know you regularly go to calm him down a bit in order to slow the rising waters, but if the fight ever went sideways, there'd be a risk that the World of Twelve could quite simply be destroyed.","content.75.6292":"It seems there's not much left I can teach you! Soon, the student shall surpass the master.","content.75.6293":"Incredible, you got to meet Kali and Goultard! Although, about Goultard... are you sure{[1*]?:} it was him? After all, you were in a pretty strange dimension...","content.75.6294":"We're talking about a demon that died millennia ago. It'll be tricky to figure out what's true and what's false. After all, the defining feature of his power was that you can't tell what's real and what's not.","content.75.6295":"You mean Arlemia? Yes, I remember. With her dad.\\n\\nThis whole situation almost seems like proof that Twelvians and Shushus can actually live together.","content.75.6296":"Life is all about evolving and changing your point of view. You're no longer the same person as when you started your voyage. The same is possible for Shushus.\\n\\n*The young woman sighs*\\n\\nOf course, it would take quite a while to make some of them listen to reason.","content.75.6297":"Grr... I'm getting angry again just thinking about it! Those liars will get what's coming to them!","content.75.6298":"Yeah, that's exactly right!\\n\\n*Juspark flashes a big smile at you*","content.75.6299":"I haven't see her, but from what you've told me, it seems like she's totally under his control.\\n\\n[#name]... It's hard to help people who don't want to be helped. You've done nothing wrong, you just followed the call of adventure with the fate of the world at heart. Anyone who's interfering with you doesn't deserve much from us... So just move on, and let her wax rhapsodic about her Shushus if she wants.","content.75.6300":"Who knows? Sthulhu might also be one of Rushu's brothers that we thought were lost. Then his art of manipulation would be justified...\\n\\n*The young woman realizes that this isn't really what you wanted to hear. She grabs both your arms and gently rests her forehead against yours for a few seconds, then steps back*\\n\\nAll right, that's enough. You're working too hard. You need to rest so you can see things more clearly. How many times have you started this year over?","content.75.6301":"You, along with lots of other protectors, ensure that life goes on and that everyone can have a future. Be proud{[1*]?:} of that, and never forget that I'm here for you. Agreed?\\n\\n*You thank Juspark with a nod*","content.75.6302":"What do you mean, mortal{[1*]?:}? I don't understand your question...","content.75.6303":"*The demon mulls over your question. He seems hesitant to respond*\\n\\nI have a few places in mind... But I'm almost certain they're not what you're looking for. You'll probably be disappointed{[1*]?:}...","content.75.6304":"All right, let's go. You'll see there's nothing interesting anyway.","content.75.6305":"*You feel the stone structure calling to you. It seems like some sort of ancient Zaap. You don't see any energy, nor any portal. Could this be the portal that Wolfram mentioned? You feel sure of it*","content.75.6306":"*You suddenly have very clear memories. You see and hear things that don't belong to you, as if you were a{[1*]?:} mere visitor{[1*]?:} trapped{[1*]?:} inside a physical envelope other than your own. Gradually, a strange certainty takes root in you, the certainty that makes dreamers think everything is normal despite the pearly sky, the undulating ground, and the unlikely silhouettes*","content.75.6307":"*All you see now is a fog of colors and vague sensations. Your whole body is burning, and you feel like you can no longer resist the strange phenomenon that's overcoming you*\\n\\n*You feel like you're being pushed and pulled at the same time*","content.75.6308":"*You realize that the memory phenomenon is rejecting you... or that you're strongly rejecting it. You realize that the entire Krosmoz, all of its worlds and all of its dimensions, have been overtaken by alternate consciousnesses. You, on the other hand, are unaffected by the phenomenon. You are an exception, and the phenomenon is trying to force you to comply, or to make you disappear*","content.75.6309":"*You draw on all your strength to completely reject the phenomenon. You are struck with a thunderbolt of sudden clarity. You have changed the world many times over through the temporal scars*\\n\\n*At the end of each year, you travel back to the past, to early in the year 977. Everything you have changed through your own direct actions will remain that way*\\n\\n*If you cut down a tree in your first visit to 977, it will stay cut down when you come back the next time in Javian 977, and everyone will act as though it's always been cut down*\\n\\n*Replant it, and it will grow all year long. When you come back to 977 for the third time, it will be a mid-sized tree. And on your fourth visit, it will be full-grown*\\n\\n*None of what you've done is supposed to have caused strange memories in the inhabitants of the World of Twelve... Memories of alternate worlds where they were happier or sadder*","content.75.6310":"*Suddenly, you see yourself. You see yourself from... the Zaap. Apparently, you are writhing in pain on the ground, and white smoke is emerging from your body*\\n\\n*Even if you concentrate and try to resist, you only succeed in aggravating the situation*","content.75.6311":"*You completely give in to the situation and relax every muscle in your body*\\n\\n*A hole opens beneath your corporal shell, and you fall away from the island. You fall into the infinite depths of the dimension. An endless void surrounds you. But your eyes stay riveted to the island, as seen from the portal's perspective*\\n\\n*The hole in the ground closes, and you see yourself arriving*\\n\\n*You walk toward the portal. Six points of energy surround you, and you proceed with a determined air toward the portal, toward your own point of view. At the moment when the two perspectives collide, you return to your senses*","content.75.6312":"*You're on the ground on the little island. All the pain has disappeared. Your fall through the void has stopped. The portal is now silent, like your surroundings*\\n\\n*You now understand what you need in order to pass through this portal*","content.75.6313":"*The Bworks don't look particularly welcoming. You have no reason to disturb them, so you decide to continue on your way*","content.75.6314":"*Exhausted{[1*]?:} by your trip through this putrid swamp, you struggle to shoo away the moskitos that surround you, then look at the great lump in front of you*\\n\\n*You realize that it's actually a Bworkette who's been around a few years and certainly accumulated a few pounds. You're alone{[1*]?:} in this fake Bwork village, surrounded{[1*]?:} by potential enemies... First contact will irreversibly set the tone*\\n\\n*You quickly think over your options, and decide that your first priority is to find out whether they even speak the same language as you*","content.75.6315":"Another Not Bwork? You shipwrecked?\\n\\n*The Bworkette looks you over as though evaluating a pack animal for purchase. She breaks out in a grotesque laugh, spraying your face with spittle in the process*\\n\\n*Several Bworks surround you, but they don't seem hostile despite their imposing frames. At most, they seem startled and surprised to see someone show up like this*","content.75.6316":"You not bad. My sisters take you to paddock with others.\\n\\n*You raise an eyebrow, surprised{[1*]?:} and upset{[1*]?:} by this turn of events*","content.75.6317":"*The clan chief - or is she just an esteemed elder? - snaps her fingers, ignoring you completely. She settles comfortably into her makeshift throne, with a diabolical smile on her swollen face*\\n\\nTake Not Bwork away. Okay to use force, me in no mood.","content.75.6318":"*You knock out the final Bwork, still gripping their makeshift clothing tightly enough to hold it more or less upright. Catching your breath, you realize that they're all females...*","content.75.6319":"*You detect a spark of interest shining brightly in her eyes. You suspect that if she were physically capable of it, she would have even... sat up a little straighter in her seat. But instead, she chooses to scream at you, spraying a new blast of colorful spittle at your face*\\n\\nYou warrior?","content.75.6320":"Me want you Not Bwork in herd with other Not Bworks!","content.75.6321":"We try find fertile Not Bwork for me daughter. Her name Zulnara. You got potential. But... You needa prove more than that.","content.75.6322":"Zulnara great warrior! You eyes pop out happy when you see her!","content.75.6323":"Me no understand. You warrior. Good match for Bworkette girl.","content.75.6324":"*The Bwork chief burps noisily in annoyance. She growls and starts lecturing you. She's less articulate than usual in her anger*\\n\\nYou awful curious for Not Bwork who... no want herd! No want go! Go to herd!\\n\\n*Through her rage, you sense that she has considerable strength, and you allow your expression to show that you're impressed.{[1*]?:} The chief gets hold of herself and speaks more calmly*\\n\\nYou can go yourself. Me, Bworkana, accept you in Bwork swamp.","content.75.6325":"If my theory is correct, these ruins may be linked to this island's greatest mystery: its ability to slip away from everyone who tried to find it through the mist. \\n\\nI believe that this ancient device has protected the island and made it invisible to the rest of the world for decades... even centuries! I can't wait to verify my hypothesis...","content.75.6326":"*The impressive Bworkana looks down at you. She chews on something noisily for a moment, then spits a huge loogie right next to you*\\n\\nWhat you want, Not Bwork?","content.75.6327":"Bworkette Burgille explain. You defended us, defended important herd. You brave and loyal warrior. You can marry Zulnara!","content.75.6328":"Not so simple.\\n\\n*Bworkana lets out a huge burp, and you have to focus your mind to avoid fainting from the rank odor she exhales. Even the moskitos that have been pestering you fall to the ground, groggy and inert*\\n\\nZulnara have final word. You prove good match for Zulnara. Most important, you need pass intelligence test.","content.75.6329":"If Zulnara want you, give you ancient artifact.","content.75.6330":"Artifact belong to scaly Not Bwork before Bworks come. Scaly build big temple with powerful artifact.","content.75.6331":"*The elder continues*\\n\\nZulnara very smart. You hafta prove intelligence with test.\\n\\n*She suddenly falls silent and gives you a determined stare. Several Bworkettes gather around, curious*","content.75.6333":"So, how do you feel? I was really afraid you wouldn't make it this time!\\n\\nI'm sorry, I'm absolutely useless in a fight... ","content.75.6334":"*The Bworkettes seem surprised and look at one another, whispering indistinctly back and forth. You see disappointment in Bworkana's eyes. Are they expecting you to provide a demonstration of your intellect? The silence continues, and you decide to do something to impress them*","content.75.6335":"*A bitter smile appears on the archaosologist's face*\\n\\nNot willingly, but yes. He forced me to help decode the Eliatrope archives in this place. They call it the Heart, and it seems that the whole island is controlled from here.\\n\\nWe were right. All the sources of the island's energy converge at its center.","content.75.6336":"*You weren't sure{[1*]?:} it would work... but you can sense that the Bworkettes are increasingly impressed. Even Bworkana is stunned, with her mouth hanging open*","content.75.6337":"*The archaosologist shakes his head apologetically*\\n\\nI can't confirm it, but... after what's just happened, I'm certain that Nox sees absolutely everything that happens on the island. I don't know if it's through his Grambos or his machines, but he watched every move we made since we arrived here. He must have been waiting for us to do his dirty work for him!","content.75.6338":"Not Bwork big genius and great inventor. Worthy of chief Zulnara.","content.75.6339":"Zulnara in Bwork war hall. You can go in to prove worth. Good luck!\\n\\n*Bworkana gives you a big, toothy smile, a striking and unforgettable spectacle*","content.75.6340":"He's a terrifying foe. But... I think you're right. We can't just let him do whatever he likes and not react. This island is only a first step, and who knows what he'll be capable of with what he's just acquired...","content.75.6341":"*A disturbing atmosphere settles over the island's heart as Milo adjusts his glasses*\\n\\nShortly before you arrived, we found some archives that mentioned research on Stasis. It seems there's a lab a bit further along in the complex... I imagine that Nox was able to extract something from there to support his work on that form of energy.","content.75.6342":"Not Bwork ask questions.","content.75.6343":"Be careful{[1*]?:}. Nox may have booby-trapped the place.\\n\\n*You flash Milo a confident smile*\\n\\nFor my part, I'll keep looking through the archives. With a little luck, maybe I'll find something to thwart his plans... or at least learn more about that mysterious island.","content.75.6344":"Bworkana not chief no more.","content.75.6345":"Island be upset recently. Bworkana sense big times soon rattle tribe. Metal creatures tough, but greenskins' determination even tougher.","content.75.6346":"Men weak. Only good for mating. We get rid of male Bworks before we come here. But not much mating, now there no male Bworks.","content.75.6347":"*Bworkana smiles, then slaps her hands loudly on her thighs*\\n\\nLotsa good mating with Not Bworks from herd!\\n\\n*A shadow crosses Bworkana's hideous face*\\n\\nBut no new Bworks for clan.","content.75.6348":"... I just can't figure him out. Everything about him screams absolute evil, and yet... I still sense fragments of the Twelvian he used to be. He implied that I reminded him of his former self... But what exactly did he mean?","content.75.6349":"*You reflect that no moskito has tried to bite you since you came{[1*]?:} back to the temple*\\n\\n*The Bwork warrior scrutinizes you with a determined stare. Her dark and intense glare, as strong as Sufokian makoffee, gives you an indescribable feeling in the pit of your stomach. You guess from her powerful presence that this must be Zulnara, chief of the Bworkana Clan*\\n\\n*She holds a large Shushu sword that she wields effortlessly, and you realize that she must be a fearsome fighter. Yet a question nags at you: Wasn't she supposed to wield Crocobur? You decide to try a pacifist approach first*","content.75.6350":"*Zulnara seems surprised for a moment, then bursts out laughing. It's a much softer, more \"Twelvian\" laugh than the mwarf-arf-arf you'd usually hear from a Bwork. She answers with a huge grin on her face*\\n\\nDon't worry, I know Twelvian grammar. You can speak normally to me. So you're my mother's new{[1*]?:} chosen{[1*]?:} one{[1*]?:}? I've heard about your impressive feats. It seems you're quite skilled in the art of combat.","content.75.6351":"*The fighter gives a proud nod. She exudes a striking air of confidence and superiority that affects you strongly*\\n\\nI hope we'll have an interesting duel, then. If you win, you can leave with the Crocodyl artifact, and perhaps my hand. If you lose, that just means you're useless and weak. That should be enough of a punishment for you.","content.75.6352":"Oh, no need to be so formal. And we can start right away, if you like. Unless you'd like to chat a bit?","content.75.6353":"*Zulnara is intrigued that you want to ask her something*\\n\\nI was only kidding... If you have any questions, I'd rather you ask them after the fight. If you're still in any condition to speak, that is.","content.75.6354":"*Knocked to the ground, Zulnara struggles to catch her breath. You calmly reach out and help her to her feet. She's back to her normal self and looks at you gratefully*\\n\\nThank you, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I'm sorry, I... I kind of lost control for a minute there. Alraune can be temperamental at times.","content.75.6355":"*The fighter is surprised, then smiles at your repartee*\\n\\nYou are skilled in the verbal arts. A skill that has always interested me. But of course, I have few opportunities to practice it as chief of this clan. My brethren tend to use a... rudimentary vocabulary.","content.75.6356":"It's not my sword, strictly speaking. But please, let's sit down and talk.\\n\\n*You both sit down cross-legged and facing each other. Zulnara seems quite close to you. How strange to think that just a moment ago, you were locked in an intense battle... You're quite surprised{[1*]?:} at how calm you are*\\n\\n*You have to admit that the Bworkette has an aura of confidence and superiority that reassures you and pulls you along in her wake*\\n\\nAlraune, would you like to introduce yourself?","content.75.6357":"Meh, I don't like talking much... Especially not to that{[1*]?:} Twelvian{[1*]?:} who defeated us...","content.75.6358":"Come on now, don't be shy!","content.75.6359":"Grmbl...","content.75.6360":"*Zulnara scratches a place under the guard*","content.75.6361":"No, stop it! I'm begging you! I surrender...\\n\\n*The Bwork chief stops the torture. Alraune coughs, a bit embarrassed, then recovers her calm attitude*\\n\\nSo... I guess you're getting to know the Shushus pretty well by now, huh?","content.75.6362":"That's often the case with Shushus. Listen...\\n\\n*Alraune visibly hesitates, unable to look you in the eye. Zulnara gently tightens her grip, as though to prod her to speak*\\n\\nI'm... sorry for attacking you like that. I was worried about Zulnara, so I decided I had to step in to protect her.","content.75.6363":"I know it may be hard for a{[1*]?:} Twelvian{[1*]?:} to hear, but I promise I didn't do it solely to hurt you.","content.75.6364":"*The proud fighter nods, seeming to understand your reticence*\\n\\nAlraune is different. She's been part of our Bwork clan for decades. Her pact makes us stronger. Alas, not strong enough to defeat the clockmaker's machines and the Starvannahs...","content.75.6365":"Their leader is a vengeful Crocodyl spirit that manipulates them through magic. When we arrived in these lands, our clan fought a war against the Crocodyls who lived here. Bworkana and her clan eventually exterminated them...\\n\\nSince then, that spirit has tormented us. We've trapped it in a kind of prison, but the attacks continue.","content.75.6366":"They appeared about two years ago. We fought a pitched battle, but gradually lost our village at the center of the island... along with many of our people. Then that wicked clockmaker corrupted the soil and dried up certain parts of our once-lush island. Nothing grows or lives there any more.","content.75.6367":"Ha ha, way to state the obvious!","content.75.6368":"Calm down, Alraune! The{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} is right. We're a fearsome clan, but we're weakened.\\n\\n*The Bwork chief's aura is still as strong as ever. She speaks with confidence*\\n\\nWe need to change the course of the war... And to do that, we need to find powerful allies.","content.75.6369":"*Zulnara seems to sense your uncertainty and lowers her head as a sign of respect*\\n\\nIt's all right if you refuse, of course. We caused some of these evils ourselves. But from what I know, this island is home to many secrets.\\n\\nThat clockmaker mustn't get his hands on them. You are a{[1*]?:} powerful{[1*]?:} and strategic adventurer{[1*]?:}. You understand that it would be a problem for your world if that monster developed new powers...","content.75.6370":"*She finally relaxes and flashes you her usual smile, then rises and extends a hand*\\n\\nFinally! I was worried you'd refuse. With you by our side, we can look forward to some incredible battles! As promised, I'll give you the key to the herd, and the Crocodyl artifact that was kept in the temple...","content.75.6371":"*Zulnara goes to search behind the throne and pulls out a fairly large object, a sort of blue sphere pulsing ever so slightly with mystical energy*","content.75.6372":"You look surprised{[1*]?:}... This mysterious object has always been in the temple. It seems the Crocodyls worshipped it in the past. If you're able to harness its power, it could be useful to you in the war we're preparing to wage.","content.75.6373":"*The Bwork chief places a friendly hand on your shoulder, with a renewed look of pride*\\n\\nI'm pleased to have a{[1*]?:} warrior{[1*]?:} like you by our side. I look forward to fighting alongside you again!\\n\\nIf you have any questions, you know where to find me.","content.75.6374":"Ah, perfect timing, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I was just thinking back on our fight. It would be good form to give it another try.","content.75.6375":"*The archaosologist works cautiously with the console, eyes locked on the screen which is covered with Eliatrope symbols*","content.75.6376":"So it seems that an explosion of Wakfu demolished our world millennia ago... That would explain the disappearance of the Eliatrope people! \\n\\nThen we appeared through the intervention of the gods, and prospered due to the harmony brought by the Dofus much later on...","content.75.6377":"Really? Who's that?\\n\\n*He's still completely absorbed in the console... which might annoy you if you weren't so captivated{[1*]?:} by the mysteries of this place yourself*","content.75.6378":"In Zinit?\\n\\n*The archaosologist is so stunned that he's torn from his technological trance*\\n\\nAre you insinuating that... the two places are linked? ","content.75.6379":"Hang on a moment... That's a lot of information.\\n\\n*Milo removes his glasses and pinches his nose*\\n\\nIf I understand you right, the Eliatropes supposedly left their home planet and crossed the universe aboard Zinit, which is actually their spaceship?","content.75.6380":"And the technology in the lab is the same or very similar to what's found in the ship? I suppose Qilby is the missing link in all this.\\n\\nThis explains so many things... but raises just as many questions!","content.75.6381":"I've always admired the Eliatropes and their technology... But this creation goes beyond anything I could have imagined!\\n\\n*The archaosologist gestures broadly at the whole room, then points at the screens nearest him*\\n\\nMisty Isle is completely artificial, powered by Wakfu circuits that feed the various ecosystems. Everything is controlled from here, even though it's been working fully autonomously for centuries or even millennia!","content.75.6382":"The archives mention specimens from other systems. At first, I thought it was a way of referring to the different sectors of the island...\\n\\nBut in light of what you've just told me, I wonder if they actually come from other planets in the Krosmoz!","content.75.6383":"So these capsules allowed the island's flora and fauna to survive their krosmic voyage... Do you understand what this means? There is life on other worlds!","content.75.6384":"*Milo is pacing around the room, no longer listening to you at all*\\n\\nI simply must tell the others about this! No... Better I should keep it to myself, to give Sufokia an advantage... But on the other hand, this is so incredible, Arlemia will never believe me! I won't be dismissed as easily if I have someone else to back me up...","content.75.6385":"*Milo suddenly stops, then gives an embarrassed cough*\\n\\nSorry, I got carried away again... There is one small problem I needed to tell you about. We don't have access to all of the archives. Some of it is locked for reading. I only have access to the island's functional data.","content.75.6386":"*Milo adjusts his glasses as he takes the strange object you've handed him*\\n\\nYou think we can insert this into the...","content.75.6387":"I suppose it can't hurt to try.\\n\\n*The archaosologist firmly inserts the key into the corresponding port. The machine purrs and vibrates for a moment before making a confirmation sound*\\n\\nIt... It worked! We've unlocked new data areas!","content.75.6388":"Let's see... There's a ton of stuff in here! Most of it is reports on the state of the ecosystem and the climate...\\n\\nAh! There's a section on error reports and system alerts. This might be interesting for us. I'll let you do the honors!","content.75.6389":"*You hold out the document to the archaosologist, who frowns and stares at it intensely*","content.75.6390":"*Milo shakes his head no*\\n\\nAs things are, I can't. It's as though it were written in another language, and only its intended recipient had the key to translate it. When you think about it, it's strange... Why is this document protected and not the others? I don't suppose you've found anything to help give me a little insight?","content.75.6391":"No. That won't work; it's a completely different kind of protection. Though I suppose I could use it as a base, if that's the best we have to work with...\\n\\n*The archaosologist frowns, looking unsure*\\n\\nNothing else?","content.75.6392":"I see. I suppose it would be awfully nosy of us to open it anyway...","content.75.6393":"... So.\\n\\n*The archaosologist crosses his arms with a chastened expression, then breaks into a mischievous smile* \\n\\nWe're going to do it anyway, right?","content.75.6394":"Glad to see we're on the same page!\\n\\nI can't promise anything, but I'll try to break through this protection. It's going to take some time, though.","content.75.6395":"I'm listening.","content.75.6396":"She was the previous chief, and she is still our beloved elder. You must have noticed for yourself how much of a matriarch's role she plays here. Even though I'm the official chief, I don't have the heart to change the clan's name yet.","content.75.6397":"I've always known her. She was previously held by my mother, Bworkana. But as far back as I can remember, I'd sneak into the armory to talk to her in secret. She's my best friend and my closest confidant...","content.75.6398":"Awww, you're making me blush!","content.75.6399":"The pact that our clan made with Alraune to increase our power also made us sterile. I'm the only birth in nearly a century - a real miracle for our people.","content.75.6400":"I don't know. No one knows the answer to that. The Bworkettes in the clan think it was a miracle.\\n\\n*Your gaze falls on Alraune. She pretends to be looking somewhere else. It seems the answer must be a bit more complicated than that. Maybe her pact wasn't entirely infallible... You think about the situation and wonder if Alraune might have temporarily weakened the pact to find a new successor for Bworkana*\\n\\n*Of course, you doubt that the Shushu would be willing to confirm this hypothesis for you*","content.75.6401":"Yeah. I was imprisoned there for a while... Pretty humiliating for a major demon like me. A lot of us Shushus wound up trapped inside weapons when Rushu launched his invasion. I could tell you my whole story, but I assume it wouldn't interest you much.","content.75.6402":"Hmph, you're just a{[1*]?:} kid{[1*]?:}, as far as I'm concerned. You're strong{[1*]?:}, sure, but don't expect to earn my respect that easily. I won't go along with you just because you let a bunch of demons take you for a ride.","content.75.6403":"Alraune's words can be as cutting as her blade, but she's had a painful past.","content.75.6404":"Hey! Who gave you permission to tell anyone about that?\\n\\nUgh... Fine, I admit it. Before going underground to follow Rushu, I used to work for Vaal'Enthia. When Rushu killed her, I swore to get revenge, but... all the Shushus just disgusted me.\\n\\n*You try not to betray any kind of reaction*\\n\\nI'd kill them all if I could. The blood of their masters was still warm after they were savagely murdered by Rushu, but they still went to cower behind the Demon King with their tails between their legs.\\nJust disgusting, if you ask me.","content.75.6405":"I hope I'll have an opportunity to avenge my mistress Vaal'Enthia. I dream of sinking my teeth into the monster who hurt her.\\n\\n*You try to avoid blinking in order to stay completely immobile*\\n\\nI'm just the protective type, you know? That's why I got so angry when you hurt Zulnara! Don't try that again, by the way.","content.75.6406":"I was born a good thirty years after the Crocodyls disappeared, so I didn't see anything in person. But I have written a journal that recounts the facts as I understood them after talking with different Bworkettes in the clan.\\n\\n*The proud warrior gives you a sidelong look*\\n\\nI can give it to you, if you want...","content.75.6407":"And hey, if you have any feedback you want to give me about my writing style...\\n\\n*Zulnara is acting a bit shy all of a sudden. She seems interested in writing. You realize that behind her tough warrior's exterior is a sensitive soul*\\n\\n*You briefly wonder how old Zulnara is. She could be quite a bit older than you... yet there's a certain charming innocence about her*","content.75.6408":"Yes. I learned from books that washed up with wrecked ships... And with Alraune's help, of course. As a half-Bwork, half-Twelvian, I never knew my father, and I always wanted to learn more about that part of myself.\\n\\nBut anyway.\\n\\n*hands you the journal*","content.75.6409":"C'mon, you've just got to tell me what you thought of it!\\n\\n*You both go into her room and start a passionate discussion of her book. The minutes pass. Then the minutes turn into hours. You point at certain passages in the journal that struck you as especially important. Zulnara moves closer, your shoulders touch and your faces draw closer together as she hangs on your every word, having finally met someone with a decent education. At least enough of one for her to learn something*\\n\\n*You notice a strange feeling. The feeling of seeing someone open their heart for the first time in their whole life. It's here, it's now, it's happening right this second*","content.75.6410":"*Zulnara is the chief of an aging clan of Bworkettes, at war with a terrifying clockmaker and his destructive machines*\\n\\n*Zulnara is the last child with Bwork blood born to this clan, a symbol of hope for their common heritage*\\n\\n*Zulnara has probably spent her entire life training without any friends her own age, with a demon as her only confidant*\\n\\n*Maybe today, just for a few minutes, Zulnara can allow herself to be someone who's interested in writing and history* ","content.75.6411":"*Your eyes meet for a moment*\\n\\n[#name]...","content.75.6412":"Thank you.\\n\\n*Zulnara gently places her hand on your arm, then gives you a faint smile*\\n\\nI've never had a conversation like this in my life. It's really nice...","content.75.6413":"I feel safe with you. You're strong{[1*]?:}, intelligent{[1*]?:}, cultured{[1*]?:}... And our conversations are really exciting. I know this is kind of blunt, but I'd like to... think about a future with you, if that works for you.\\n\\n*Her hand remains on your arm*","content.75.6414":"I know, but I want to be with you anyway.","content.75.6415":"I see. I understand.\\n\\n*Zulnara takes her hand away and gives a big sigh. A weight seems to have been lifted from her shoulders*\\n\\nYou're right. You're a {[1*]?woman:man} who believes strongly in fulfilling your duty. And to be honest... I really like that about you.\\n\\n*An awkward silence falls*","content.75.6416":"But, uh... if you maybe want to spend a little time with me anyway...","content.75.6417":"*You never would have thought it possible, but you decide to stay with Zulnara for a while. After all, why turn away from her at this point? You quickly stop thinking and focus on the present moment*\\n\\n*You soon discover that the warrior has many scars on her half-Bwork, half-Twelvian body. She tries to make up for her lack of experience with her usual fervor*","content.75.6418":"*If you had to describe this moment, you might compare it to a sort of dance in which each partner is trying to take control, trying to get the upper hand. Sometimes you find yourselves completely out of sync, and it takes a moment to get back on the same wavelength*\\n\\n*The hours race past in Zulnara's room, but you barely notice the time passing*","content.75.6419":"Thank you, [#name]. I'm so lucky to have met you. Our paths will separate, but I'll remember your courage and your... impressive fighting skills.","content.75.6420":"*You weren't expecting to find good old Lebbocq in such a rough spot. You take a good look at him: His face is haggard, with dark bags under his eyes. It looks like he hasn't slept for the past couple of days*\\n\\n[#name]. It's nice to see a familiar face in this strange land...","content.75.6421":"It's a long story. I was on the trail of an ancient Crocodyl relic... These swamps were inhabited by Crocodyls in the past, you see! I've found multiple traces of their presence.","content.75.6422":"All the evidence I've seen suggests that the Crocodyls have disappeared from the island. Based on my initial examinations, the traces date back no more than a century.\\n\\n*You recognize the spark of archaosology in Lebbocq's shining eyes*","content.75.6423":"So it would seem. I found a big building built by the Crocodyls, but it was full of Bworkettes.\\n\\nI was examining the stones when they grabbed me and dragged me here without waiting for an explanation. Fortunately, they haven't tried anything with me yet...","content.75.6424":"*Lebbocq grabs the bars, suddenly gripped by panic*\\nWhat's happening is exactly what you think. You've got to get me out of here as fast as you can!","content.75.6425":"*The archaosologist looks down and shakes his head in dismay. He soon looks up at you again, looking a bit reassured despite everything, and hesitantly confides in you*\\n\\nThank you, [#name]. I'm really dying to get out of here. I have to discover the mysteries of this area... especially with the fabulous treasures to be had when I do!","content.75.6426":"Yesterday, I overheard some guards talking among themselves...\\n\\n Bworkana's daughter, Zulnara, has an incredibly powerful sword that can perform miracles. My theory is that she's got her hands on Crocobur, the legendary lost sword of the Crocodyls.","content.75.6427":"It won't be that simple. It's in the big Crocodyl building I was examining... Considering that they attacked me as soon as I got anywhere near it, I'd say it's a very important place for the Bworks. Some kind of war hall, perhaps.\\n\\nI need to get out of here, but it will be hard to learn anything more about the Crocodyls as long as that clan is getting in our way.","content.75.6428":"I agree. But how do you intend to go about it? If the Bworks see you, they'll throw you in here for sure!","content.75.6429":"*You explain that you've impressed the clan chief and that she considers you a good match for her daughter Zulnara. As Eminerell Lebbocq mentioned, the Bwork princess seems to have a mysterious magic sword that could quite possibly be Crocobur, the lost sword of the Crocodyls. Could it be possible to manipulate Bworkana in order to meet Zulnara?*\\n\\nWell, then. That's an opportunity you won't want to miss... I mean, you could use that to infiltrate their clan!","content.75.6430":"Well, for one thing, all I've seen are Bworkettes.\\n\\n*Eminerell pauses, looking thoughtful*\\n\\nOther than that, I don't really know. I didn't have time to examine the Bworks all that much. If I had access to their distinctive signs and symbols, I'm sure I could tell you more.","content.75.6431":"Wait! Don't... Don't leave me here...","content.75.6432":"This prison is such a miserable place... I prefer the dungeons in Brakmar - it's a much more comfortable experience.","content.75.6433":"*Lebbocq carefully inspects the cloths, each marked with some sort of emblem*\\n\\nWait... This symbol... This belongs to the Gisgoul Bwork clan, I'm sure of it! I thought they'd disappeared.","content.75.6434":"It used to be a territory in the Brakmar region, which is how I happen to know a bit about it. With Ogrest's Chaos, Gisgoul became a separate island in its own right, a bit like Forfut.\\n\\n*Lebbocq looks straight at you with a keenly focused expression*\\n\\nGisgoul was the home of the Bworker clan during the Dofus Era. It was also inhabited by another clan of Brakmarian Bworks, after Ogrest's Chaos. To my knowledge, the two clans tried to coexist, but no one has been to the island in over a century... so who knows what's happened since then?","content.75.6435":"As far as I'm concerned, there's no doubt about it. That's why they have this emblem.","content.75.6436":"*Lebbocq turns the statuette over and over in his hands, looking thoughtful*\\n\\nIt's a fertility statuette. I'm almost certain of it.","content.75.6437":"It's an icon representing a fertility goddess. It's a pretty common good luck charm among primitive cultures. These statuettes are supposed to help the bearer to have children more easily.","content.75.6438":"Hmm, that is strange. And that would explain why they're using that herd to have children anyhow.\\n\\n*Lebbocq shudders as another prisoner embarks on a long fit of awkward coughing*","content.75.6439":"*Lebbocq grabs the gems and looks them over with great interest*\\n\\nWhere did you find this?","content.75.6440":"I think your intuition is right on. I've seen this mineral in the past.\\n\\nIt's often used in Shushu-summoning rituals.","content.75.6441":"Right, exactly. Based on that, we can guess that this clan has a connection with one or more Shushus... A rather unsettling prospect.\\n\\nI wonder if they've made a pact with demons. That would explain their supernatural strength.","content.75.6442":"I'm not a demonologist. If you know someone, this might be the time to go and talk to them!","content.75.6443":"Well, it seems we've got a better understanding of this whole story now. I've got a few theories... But to earn their trust, we'll have to make a big move. Find some way of showing them that you're very loyal to their cause.\\n\\n*You suddenly hear noises outside. It sounds like a number of Bworkettes are running around and shouting directions. A few seconds later, you hear a huge racket*","content.75.6444":"If the Bworkettes are being attacked, you could earn some points by coming to their defense. Think of the magic sword... We've got to earn their trust!\\n\\n*This all seems to be happening at just the right moment. But you're more concerned about surviving than winning the Bwork clan's trust*","content.75.6445":"It seems that the fight is over, and the invaders won't be coming back.\\n\\nYou should go and see Bworkana to find out if you've earned her trust. Don't forget... You've got to get your hands on Crocobur, whatever it takes. That sword is far too powerful to be left in the Bworks' hands. Do whatever you can to get it away from Zulnara!","content.75.6446":"*Lebbocq first looks surprised, then concerned*\\n\\nI'm really sorry to hear that. It seems there was no trace of Crocobur here after all. I'm surprised... Have you had a chance to learn anything more about the Crocodyls?","content.75.6447":"So the Crocodyls were exterminated by the Bworks. It's interesting that this story is about Crocoburio himself. The sword could still be here on the island!\\nFor now, can you please get me out of this cell?","content.75.6448":"Let me know once you learn more.\\n\\nFor now, can you please get me out of this cell?","content.75.6449":"*The young man pauses to think for a moment*\\n\\nMilo probably knows more about that. I think he's somewhere around the center of the island...","content.75.6450":"*The Brakmarian tells you he's going to meet up with his fellow Archaosologists on the island. He finally steps out into the open air, looking reassured. As for you, you've formed a strange alliance with Bworkana and Zulnara's clan of Bworkettes. A powerful Shushu is involved in the clan's affairs, and you sense that there must be some kind of secret waiting to be revealed around the Crocodyls who were exterminated in the past*\\n\\n*For now, you tirelessly return to your quest*","content.75.6451":"*The screen displays sequences of Eliatrope characters that Milo translates as you struggle to even recognize them. A cursor blinks, seemingly awaiting an instruction*","content.75.6452":"*A list of events fills the screens. There are so many that it would be impossible to read them all. Every system check and anomaly has been logged over the centuries*","content.75.6453":"*You boldly enter your commands into the console. Yet the volume of data doesn't really seem to have decreased as a result. You sense Milo's baffled look over your shoulder, a sort of subtle pressure that rattles your previously unshakable confidence in your chaotic approach*","content.75.6454":"*The first few occurrences date back thousands of years. They mainly describe the deployment and fine-tuning of a system to regulate the island's energy. Wakfu leaks, mutations in the plant life causing it to grow at uncontrollable speeds, drought-parched soil... The day-to-day lives of Misty Isle's creators seem to have been quite busy*","content.75.6455":"*You try to organize the reports based on their coordinates on the island. It's an interesting idea that allows you to identify two sets of errors that stand out from the rest*","content.75.6456":"*These coordinates seem to correspond to the lab's location. The error has to do with a malfunction in two cryo capsules that led to the awakening of two specimens of the Zurikat species. \\n\\nIt seems they then broke out of their capsules and escaped from the complex. That would explain what you saw in the lab. The date of the event was nearly a century ago*","content.75.6457":"*This one is much more alarming than the first. It describes the appearance of an enormous unidentified Stasis source. The recommended solution is a complete lockdown of the affected area. \\n\\nFrom what you can glean here, the location is indeed sealed off, and the source is still present at least fifty years later*","content.75.6458":"*Guided by a sudden intuition, you type in your date of birth. After all, you're the chosen{[1*]?:} one from the prophecy! The screen makes a confirmation sound, then announces that the island has been awaiting your arrival for millennia, and grants you full power over its secrets and its fate. \\n\\nYou're filled with a surge of euphoria... then come back to reality as you realize that all of this was just in your imagination and had no actual effect on the machine*","content.75.6459":"*The screen quivers for a moment, followed by a sudden electric shock to punish your clumsy approach. Violence obviously won't be the answer this time*","content.75.6460":"*You turn your gaze to the archaosologist, who stares right back at you. You sense a certain discomfort taking hold during the long pause that follows. You finally return your attention to the machine, feeling guilty for having thought about that option even for a moment*","content.75.6461":"*You get right to the point and ask your question directly to the machine. It makes a brief crackling noise, followed by a long silence accompanied only by a flashing cursor on the screen. As though it were thinking deeply about the existential question that it's just been asked. \\n\\nAfter all, this machine seems to control everything here, so it should certainly be able to answer you*","content.75.6462":"*You stare intensely at the screen for a long moment, arms crossed. After what seems like an eternity, you realize that the machine wasn't thinking - your instruction simply had no effect*","content.75.6463":"*The first few occurrences describe the arrival of unidentified individuals on the island. You readily deduce that this must be a reference to you and the archaosologists. Going a bit further down the list, a mass of unsettling errors captures your attention*","content.75.6464":"*Numerous error reports describe a critical imbalance in the Wakfu flux in a particular area, leading to its eventual exhaustion. There's no doubt that this was the northern part of the island - the target of Nox's plan. This imbalance seems to have caused the massive Wakfu leak occurring in the canyon*","content.75.6465":"*The analyses reveal that the system can no longer regulate itself, resulting in a slow but inexorable draining of its Wakfu. A terrible finding that suggests the island is doomed, even without the mad Xelor's influence*","content.75.6466":"*Milo thinks for a moment, then points at the console*\\n\\nTry sorting by severity and in chronological order. That should get us the main events that have happened since the island's creation.","content.75.6467":"*New entries appear alongside the ones you've already looked over. The most important event is listed first, and describes a gigantic Wakfu explosion that struck the world millennia ago. \\n\\nLuckily, the Wakfu shield that hides the island from the rest of the world was able to absorb most of the cataclysm's impact, but at the cost of a permanently weakened infrastructure*","content.75.6468":"*Subsequent entries describe significant movements in the Wakfu surrounding the island, under the influence of unknown entities. \\n\\nFollowing this event, it seems that a number of souls were incarnated into the world. You easily interpret this as the intervention of the Ten in what would later become the World of Twelve*","content.75.6469":"*The system detected a strange pulse that sent a shudder through the Wakfu around it. A wave of energy that calmed the turmoil and infused the energy flux with a kind of... harmony. That must have been when the Primordial Dofus appeared*","content.75.6470":"The Grambos are an interesting life form... But at least we're safe here.","content.75.6471":"Yes. It's still so lush, so beautiful... It's almost inconceivable that it's already too late to save it. But Nox has definitely broken the delicate balance that keeps this island in place. Without its creators, I don't see how we can hope to change its grim fate in any way.","content.75.6472":"The appearance of a Stasis source? Yes, me too... Could there be another lab at that location? It's true, that's the most promising lead we've got right now. Can you show me the coordinates again? Hmmm...","content.75.6473":"I think I know exactly where that location is. When the other archaosologists and I arrived on the island, we spread out into different areas. I started exploring the forest, and I came across a Crocodyl structure up in the highlands.","content.75.6474":"It looked like some sort of temple. The entrance was sealed, and that's not my specialty anyway. I also heard the cries of a Dazzlosaurus nearby, which motivated me to get away from there in a hurry! \\nRegardless, I'm quite certain of it: That's definitely the location indicated by the Heart.","content.75.6475":"*The archaosologist thoughtfully rests his hand on his chin for a moment*\\n\\nAs I said, I'm not an expert in this civilization. But I think it's Crocodyl runes blocking the way. \\n\\nI expect Jenry could help you? Of course, the ideal option would be to have one of those Crocodyls to call on...","content.75.6476":"*Milo raises his eyebrows*\\n\\nReally?! Well, in that case, I suppose that solves the problem. I'll leave it to you to explore the place with Jenry. \\n\\nAs for me, I'm going to keep looking at this data a little longer. Then I'll head back to the archaosologists' camp and you can tell me what you've learned!","content.75.6477":"*nods*\\n\\nI know you don't make promises lightly! Good luck!","content.75.6478":"*The subject clearly makes the archaosologist uncomfortable, as he adjusts his cap and looks away*\\n\\nOh, she's doing better... I think. We try to spend time together when I've got a free moment, but our interactions are still a little touchy. It's hard to get past years of resentment, even with the best intentions in the world.","content.75.6479":"*Milo's expression grows sad - clearly you've hit him where it hurts*\\n\\nListen, [#name], I appreciate everything you'd done for me and my family, but this is the best I can do right now. Give me a little time before judging me too severely. I know I'm not a perfect father, but what we discover here will be of great help to future generations!","content.75.6480":"... She does love flowers. People often say that you should express your feelings in the language of flowers. I suppose that's a good way to help re-establish contact... I'll think about it.","content.75.6481":"*The archaosologist spots you and gives you a friendly smile*\\n\\n[#name]! Nice to see you again.","content.75.6482":"Incredible... It seems to contain an astronomical amount of energy! \\n\\n*Milo looks over your discovery from every possible angle*\\n\\nIt looks like some sort of... energy cell!","content.75.6483":"Here, just look.\\n\\n*The archaosologist points to the ends of the artifact*\\n\\nThese two opposite points serve as poles to balance the energy charges that flow through it. The inside of the... \"egg\" must function as the site of a Wakfu reaction, subject to intrinsic stimulation of an accumulation process involving...","content.75.6484":"It's a battery. Or the Eliatrope equivalent, I suppose. \\n\\n*He looks at the central device of the ruins nearby*\\n\\nBut I don't think there's anywhere it'll fit in these ruins. Besides, where there's a battery, there must be a generator, or at least a machine to be powered!","content.75.6485":"Really? Can you describe it to me in detail?","content.75.6486":"*The Grambo bows when she sees you*\\n\\nWelcome to the headquarters of the United Grambo Workers. What can I do for you, noble adventurer{[1*]?:}?","content.75.6487":"Exactly! I founded this resistance movement to take revenge for Meccanox's mistreatment. We want to pay him back and fight for our fundamental freedoms.\\n\\n*The Grambos around you approve, whispering in agreement*","content.75.6488":"We want one day off a year!\\n\\n*The Grambos approve in unison*","content.75.6489":"We want bonuses for night work!\\n\\n*A few Grambos whisper that they don't understand what you're talking about. Others raise their fists in support, maybe out of habit*","content.75.6490":"And we want salt on the stones during meals!\\n\\n*All the Grambos shout in approval. This seems to be a particularly unifying point*","content.75.6491":"We've put a plan in motion to throw a wrench in his gears. I'm sure that with your help, we'll be able to force his hand. The aim is to show him that we're strong and responsible!\\n\\n*You think about what these Grambos might make you do for a moment. It may not be worth the risk. Demonstrating the Grambos' strength and responsibility is a perfectly fine idea. But it doesn't seem to square with the fact that they're asking for your help*\\n\\n*On the other hand, doing them a favor could help you learn more about this island*","content.75.6492":"*Julpi clenches her fist, clearly pleased with your support*\\n\\nWith an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} of your caliber, there's no stopping us! My plan is worthy of a great Gobbowl master. I've been devising and preparing it for a few months now...","content.75.6493":"We need planks and citronanas. This is an essential step in our plan. Then... we'll need mystical leather and coarse fiber.\\n\\nAnd finally, we'll need infernal tiramisoup.","content.75.6494":"*The Grambos scurry around you, carefully collecting the citronanas*\\n\\nThank you so much, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Our plan will be foolproof with this!","content.75.6495":"Be patient... Our plan will still take a long time to take shape. We still need to do some surveying.","content.75.6496":"Well, that's magnificent!\\n\\n*Julpi checks your resources a bit, as if to assess their quality, and then nods before giving them to another Grambo. The Grambo leaves in a hurry, carrying the pile of fabric with difficulty*","content.75.6497":"Not yet... We have a lot of things to get ready.","content.75.6498":"*The Grambo sniffs your shushued fish and starts drooling with excitement*\\n\\nI've never smelled anything so delicious! What a shame I have to part with it for the sake of the plan.","content.75.6499":"Soon. We haven't gotten everything together yet...","content.75.6500":"*Julpi nods seriously. She takes out a crude map of the area and places it on the floor. The Grambos gather around you. You look at the map, which looks like a child's squiggles... You squint in an attempt to understand what they're supposed to be*\\n\\n*The resistance leader starts looking serious, as if she were an experienced professor emeritus*\\n\\nUm, right. We'll start by explaining the plan...","content.75.6501":"The village we're in is fortified with wooden fences. Machines are all around us, and the clockmaker keeps a constant watch on us with his Noxines. We don't have much leeway if we want our demands to be met. We need to hit hard and fast.\\n\\n*The Grambos nod and whisper that they are prepared to carry out the plan, whatever it takes*","content.75.6502":"Our plan will be possible thanks to the adventurer{[1*]?:}'s contribution. The resources that were brought here are essential in all phases of this plan. First, we need to disguise the adventurer{[1*]?:} as a Grambo, like us...\\n\\n*Julpi nods, and two Grambos pull out a Grambo costume... tailor made just for you. You recognize the fabric you brought with you*","content.75.6503":"*The Grambos confer with each other, stunned. They don't understand your comment. Julpi clears her throat*\\n\\nSorry, I'll continue.\\n\\nThe main part of the plan of action is to make Meccanox slip on a citronana. To do this, our survey team determined that our supervisor should take a daily bio break in the early evening. He always goes to the tributary of the river, east of the village, right next to the boat.\\n\\n*Julpi points to a spot on the map that is indeed next to the boat*","content.75.6504":"Yes, I admit it's a rather rough plan. But I've thought up a contingency plan.\\n\\nSince the citronanas are so obvious, we're going to put planks over them so he can't see them... And we're going to nail them to the ground so they won't blow away in the wind.","content.75.6505":"Uh... Well...\\n\\n*The Grambos look at each other again, clearly shocked by your lack of intellect. Julpi pulls herself together and points to several red circles on the map*\\n\\nTo make sure he steps on them, we've positioned the tiramisoups in strategic spots. He'll be drawn in by the delicious smell...","content.75.6506":"What? Speak for yourself, adventurer{[1*]?:}! Do you know how much time we spent coming up with this plan?\\n\\n*You are interrupted by a noise. The Grambos freeze in silence and then drag you behind a rock. They throw the makeshift Grambo costume at you and then crowd together*","content.75.6507":"*The Grambo still seems disoriented by the events*\\n\\nPatrohix...","content.75.6508":"He's our master, the clockmaker... Nox...","content.75.6509":"I never should have gone against the order of things. We are nothing but insignificant creatures against the clockmaker's omnipotence... We should just keep taking pleasure in robbing adventurers and archaeologists. What was I thinking, making this foolish plan?\\n\\n*A few Grambos leave for work, while others gather around the pile of ashes and bow their heads. The mood is gloomy*","content.75.6510":"But yes, you're right, noble adventurer{[1*]?:}. We'll continue the revolution and come up with another plan! Our UGW shall prevail!","content.75.6511":"*A few minutes have passed, and most of the Grambos already seem to have forgotten about Patrohix. You look at the little pile of ashes next to which the Grambos are complaining they'll have to clean up and reposition the stools around the fire*","content.75.6512":"He was an old comrade. He worked hard and helped our young recruits integrate.\\n\\n*You hope the Grambos won't know how to react, but it hurts you deeply to see such a tragedy so quickly forgotten by comrades. You think that, at least among Twelvians, you wouldn't risk seeing such a lack of empathy from people who live side by side all year round*","content.75.6513":"We'll need you again, adventurer{[1*]?:}!","content.75.6514":"Oh, really? But you've got that Grambo costume that suits you so well... You're completely unrecognizable.","content.75.6515":"*The Grambo seems lost in thought. He examines his considerable collection of lenses. You decide not to bother him*","content.75.6516":"And here's the result. It's so hard to manage such an impetuous group!","content.75.6517":"The cemetery is full of people who just can't be replaced. All that matters is our productivity. If we don't produce enough, how do you suggest we survive?\\n\\nIt's easy to give me lessons in management. It's clear that you're not the one feeding and housing these Grambos.","content.75.6518":"Let me enlighten you. The world of work isn't so easy. I can't please everyone. It's sad, but that's the way it is. If people stopped complaining and just mined faster, at least Patrohix would still be alive.\\n\\nI prefer to be realistic and choose my battles.","content.75.6519":"I know that, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Don't worry. I'm sure we can come to an agreement. You see, my plan was to negotiate a significant improvement in the Grambos' conditions with our master, the clockmaker.","content.75.6520":"Yes. He's our master, Nox.\\n\\n*Meccanox scowls*\\n\\nHis power defies imagination. Trust me, we'd best stop it with these childish revolutions and take what we can get... A bit of salt for the stones twice a year and a weekly meal break are already major social improvements.","content.75.6521":"*You think about it. Yes, the Grambos of the UGW are making revolution all over the place and relying on outside help to save them. But this Meccanox seems to be a tough customer, despite what he claims. Does he really believe what he's saying, or is he trying to float from compromise to compromise without getting his feet wet?*\\n\\n*You think back to what Meccanox told you about Nox. He seems dangerous... He also reminds you of an old enemy: Count Harebourg. Could they be connected?*","content.75.6522":"*The Grambo seems to think for a moment, staring at you*\\n\\nHmmm... Yes, that could be a good idea.","content.75.6523":"Very well. Meet me north of the camp. There you can ask me anything you like.\\n\\nOh, and adventurer{[1*]?:}... You'd do well not to cause too much havoc on this island. I say that for your own good, obviously.","content.75.6524":"*The Grambo bows when she sees you*\\n\\n*You return the greeting, but you decide not to bother her. You don't know whether you're{[1*]?:} welcome{[1*]?:} here... You think you'd better move on*","content.75.6525":"*The Grambo bows when she sees you, whispering a few hurried words to you*\\n\\nWe shouldn't talk here... The machines might punish us. Meet me at the extraction site HQ.","content.75.6526":"*You go up to the Zurikat. He recognizes you and stares at you. He seems to be waiting for something*","content.75.6527":"*The Zurikat looks melancholic as he fidgets with his brother's necklace*\\n\\nTimo troun. Te Utuafare...","content.75.6528":"Koutak! Spikalabouk!\\n\\n*The Zurikat seems genuinely pleased to see you*","content.75.6529":"The area is teeming with that strange blue mineral. Unfortunately, it's also teeming with monsters... It's rare to find rich sources of Wakfu in nature. What a fabulous discovery!","content.75.6530":"This island keeps getting more intriguing. Who would've thought it had this kind of technology hidden in its depths?","content.75.6531":"The others told me everything. This island just never ceases to surprise! We must save what we can, no matter what!","content.75.6532":"*Laura mumbles, her eyes riveted on a crude map she made of the island*\\n\\nWhat an exciting region...","content.75.6533":"*Laura covers her mouth to suppress a gasp of surprise*\\n\\nNo... Do... Do you think it's a...?\\n\\n*All of the archaosologists come out of Laura's makeshift tent, drawn by her shout. You form a circle with them and you hold out your Dofus so that everyone can examine it*","content.75.6534":"I thought that Dofus was in Ogrest's possession, along with all the other Primordial Dofus. Or so the legend goes.","content.75.6535":"I've read plenty of stories from the Dofus Era. In some documents, dragon eggs are said to be ubiquitous, which explains why so many of them were available at markets back then. Others thought that Dofus could be duplicated under certain conditions, but that there was always an original one protected by a guardian.","content.75.6536":"Ha ha! That's quite possible. The legends surrounding these Dofus have always worked out well for all kinds of crooks... Their disappearance during Ogrest's Chaos caused many alchemists to attempt to create all kinds of counterfeit ones.\\n\\n*The Ouginak's eyes gleam with greed*\\n\\nYou wouldn't believe the price some of my acquaintances would pay for a genuine dragon egg...","content.75.6537":"*The archaosologist stares at you for a few moments, and you sense in her gaze that she is seriously considering your offer, before shaking her head and raising her hands*\\n\\nI give up. I've seen{[1*]?:} you at work on this island. All the kamas in the world wouldn't be enough to make up for the danger of having you as an enemy{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6538":"*The archaosologist who had been silent since your return suddenly speaks up*\\n\\nBut there is an explanation for the appearance of this Dofus. Remember the Crocodyl's words: Only the black fire that springs from an ocean of ebony tears can undo what has been forged by dragon fire.","content.75.6539":"The ebony tears are what catches my attention. Legend has it that the Primordial Dofus came into being through a dragon's love for Sadida's dolls.\\n\\nWhat if love weren't the only emotion that could produce this phenomenon?","content.75.6540":"You said it yourself: We don't know a thing about the magic of the Dofus. Crocatzin was that dragon's grandson. His death and the annihilation of his entire people may have been what triggered the appearance of this Dofus... Love is a strong emotion, as are grief and hatred. At least, that's my theory.","content.75.6541":"When I think that Crocobur is no more... Are you sure that destroying it with the Dofus's energy was the right thing to do?","content.75.6542":"I knew it! I should have come myself! Destroy Crocobur?! What were you thinking?!","content.75.6543":"Easy for you to say! I'm accountable to Brakmarian employers. They helped pay for this expedition, and they don't forgive failure!\\n\\nWhen I think about all I had to endure at the hands of those darn Bworks just to get my hands on that sword...","content.75.6544":"Aha! \\n\\n*The archaosologist points an accusing finger at Lebbocq*\\n\\nI knew it! A Brakmarian like you can never be trusted! You should be ashamed, tarnishing our profession with your little schemes!","content.75.6545":"He's right. You can air your dirty laundry later! We need a plan to enable [#name] to fight the clockmaker. Ever since you opened the way to the Heart, he's locked himself inside his clock, and his army is guarding the entrance.","content.75.6546":"True, we're not fighters. But we shouldn't be underestimated.\\n\\nEveryone has a weak point, and the clockmaker is no exception. If we pool our skills, we could exploit it. And there's no way we'll let you be the{[1*]?:} only{[1*]?:} one taking such risks.","content.75.6547":"Yes. But I suggest you get some rest. Recent events have been pretty exhausting.\\n\\nCome back and see me when you're ready{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6548":"I don't know if we can really call it a plan. These machines are as impressive as they are formidable, but they have a major design flaw that Amelia managed to identify while conducting her sabotage.","content.75.6549":"These machines aren't energy self-sufficient. To deliver this kind of firepower, they constantly drain the island's underground flows of Wakfu. That's why the desolation is spreading further into other territories.","content.75.6550":"Many of these machines will be disabled at the same time, yes.\\n\\nThanks to Arlemia's expertise, we've managed to design effective prototypes. Milo thinks he can jury-rig energy scramblers from the monsters' components.\\n\\nHowever, we won't be able to affect the whole area in the time we have.","content.75.6551":"It's all still quite theoretical.\\n\\nNevertheless, I think I can make one or two in the time I have. Maybe three, if Lebbocq helps me with his mechanical knowledge.","content.75.6552":"Pffft... I suppose I don't really have a choice. I can't stand the idea of letting that demented Xelor act with impunity either.\\n\\n*The fierce determination in his eyes betrays Lebbocq's motivation*","content.75.6553":"I've written down what we'll need right here.\\n\\n*Milo holds out a hastily scribbled note*\\n\\nThere's still the question of their placement. For them to be effective, the scramblers need to be positioned at key points where Wakfu flows across the artificial island.","content.75.6554":"I think I can help you with that part! After our discovery of the pipes and the fight with Imagorila, I tried to find out how far this network extended.\\n\\nIf you give me some time, I should be able to determine the optimal locations to restrict these flows.","content.75.6555":"That won't be enough.\\n\\nEven if we manage to affect a large part of the Desolation, many machines are still connected to the Great Clock, which will automatically take over and power them. I was able to observe it by doing a few tests before I got caught.","content.75.6556":"Assessing danger is like second nature when you're used to walking on the edge of legality... While you prepare the scramblers, I'm going to sabotage a few machines.\\n\\nDo you think you can convince the rebel Grambos to help me with this task? They seem to like you, [#name].","content.75.6557":"If we're going to include the Grambos in the plan anyway, why not do the same with the Starvannahs?\\n\\nThey too have every interest in preventing Nox from destroying their island. I can help you talk to them if needed.","content.75.6558":"How lovely of you, coming up with a Gavid vs. Doliath plan. But let me remind you that there's already a whole tribe on the island, armed to the teeth, ready to do the clockmaker in for us!","content.75.6559":"NO! Ahem... No, that's okay. You go ahead.","content.75.6560":"Hah! I wonder how the clockmaker will look when his only working machines are caught in between the Starvannahs and the enraged Bworkettes.","content.75.6561":"*Laura makes eye contact with all the archaosologists, who nod in return*\\n\\nYes. We're ready!","content.75.6562":"Perfect, thanks! I don't know what Xelors have with this kind of item, but it seems to play a central role in many of their mechanisms.\\n\\nI intend to study it and make miniature versions that can set the rhythm of the energy discharges of each scrambler.","content.75.6563":"*The archaosologist takes one and inspects it thoroughly before pointing out a nearby location*\\n\\nCan you put them here? Their design is simply remarkable. I'd never have been able to jury-rig a device that can handle such an intense flow of Wakfu myself. There's something quite satisfying about turning your opponent's ingenuity against them!","content.75.6564":"This makeshift camp is much cozier than the squalid Bwork prison.\\n\\n*The archaosologist shivers slightly*","content.75.6565":"Argh! You could have been gentler with these pieces of scrap metal... Just look at it!\\n\\n*The archaosologist points his hammer at the many rust marks and indentations left over from your victory*\\n\\nHow do you expect me to do a decent job with this junk?","content.75.6566":"*Lebbocq strikes the metal with his hammer and then stands still*\\n\\n... So. On closer inspection, I should still be able to make a fair structure out of it. Was this metal forged using ores from the Desolation? It's stronger than I thought, yet still fairly flexible... I know some Brakmarians who'd be interested in such an alloy!","content.75.6567":"*Lebbocq puffs out his chest, now full of renewed energy*\\n\\nYou can count on me! I didn't think the few years I spent as a scrap dealer to pay for my studies would ever come in handy.","content.75.6568":"These little spikes? Honestly, I was expecting something more impressive when Amelia and Milo described mechanical components that could absorb Wakfu! I'll have to coordinate with Milo to make sure the energy flows smoothly through our creations. But I should warn you: It won't be a walk in the park.","content.75.6569":"*The Zurikat tilts his head to one side*\\n\\nToukra joupe snouk?","content.75.6570":"*The archaosologist holds you by the shoulder*\\n\\nLeave it. I'll take care of it. I knew I'd be more useful here than at the camp! Let's take a look...\\n\\n*Jenry takes out his notepad and starts drawing the Nox head before pointing at you and clearing his throat*\\n\\nAye rau xourous. Toukra foulkone itou?","content.75.6571":"*Brossar seems to understand what the archaosologist is saying, so he points to the drawing and then to his neck, before making an equivocal gesture and pointing at you*\\n\\nXourous zloup kaput?\\n\\n*He then nods before pointing to his hut and tapping the handle of his paintbrush on the ground*\\n\\nKoutak somonone ula snouk. ","content.75.6572":"I think he's willing to help us fight Nox! He says they owe you.\\n\\nAnd it seems that Timo still has a few demonic powers.","content.75.6573":"*Brossar smiles and bows*\\n\\nPross.","content.75.6574":"It may take a bit of time, but no problem. ","content.75.6575":"*A fierce smile comes over the Bwork's face*\\n\\nHa ha! Hear that, Alraune? The time for vengeance is here at last!","content.75.6576":"I'm not sure I understand everything about these scramblers... But I think I've got the gist of it. Basically, we charge in, attacking the machines from the rear, which will also be attacked from the other side by the Starvannahs. This is all so we can clear a path to the clock and you can fight Nox.","content.75.6577":"I'd have preferred to fight the Xelor myself, but you've earned that right by proving your strength...\\n\\n*Zulnara tightens her grip on Alraune's guard*\\n\\nWe'd be honored to have your back!\\n\\n*The declaration is met with a long silence*","content.75.6578":"Yeah! What's wrong? Are you sulking because we're not going to give Nox the coup de grace? But you know our rules! [#name] has earned that right. Don't force me to make you spit it out...\\n\\n*Zulnara brings her hand close to a specific part of the guard*","content.75.6579":"Stop that right now! No, it's not for that. ","content.75.6580":"*The demon's eye examines you intently, making you feel deeply uneasy*\\n\\nIt's that smell... {[1*]?She:He} reeks of demon blood, or I don't know a thing.","content.75.6581":"*The Bworkette and the Shushu look at each other*\\n\\nTo tell you the truth, we kind of suspected. Alraune did sense a familiar presence, but it wasn't clear enough for her to be certain. Should I take it you killed that demon?","content.75.6582":"*The sword's single eye widens*\\n\\nDid you say Bulak? The Bulak? He's no mere major demon... He's a warlord! I fought alongside him during the invasion of the 1,000 Shushus... but I'm one of those who got caught and sealed away in items. I didn't know he'd survived!","content.75.6583":"Hah! I'm not going to feel sorry for him. He was a nasty brute, although I do respect his fondness for cunning and convoluted schemes. He was the kind of man who dreamed of replacing Rushu, and he let everyone know it. He didn't lift a finger to help me when I got caught, preferring to run off with some minor demons.","content.75.6584":"*Zulnara, who had been deep in thought until now, suddenly speaks up*\\n\\nI don't understand. Why did they prefer to die in dishonor so as to summon this demon? It had no impact on the conflict at the time, and nobody ever saw it.","content.75.6585":"After all, they were the ones who went looking for trouble first! It was a good meal for me, so I didn't see any harm in exterminating them...","content.75.6586":"*The Bworkette takes the scroll respectfully*\\n\\nThank you, [#name]. My mother wouldn't understand how precious this testimony is. You can count on us in the battle ahead. Past ones can wait until I pick up the pen again.","content.75.6587":"Oh, sweet!\\n\\n*The Grambo peels a citronana and starts chewing on it*\\n\\nSo? What'sha plan?","content.75.6588":"*Julpi swallows before thinking hard*\\n\\nHmm, no, not really. What do you want us to do?","content.75.6589":"*The Grambo is so surprised that she drops the rest of her citronana on the floor, mouth wide open*\\n\\nBut... If we touch Lord Nox's machines, he'll...","content.75.6590":"Just keep a low profile. With all this chaos, I'm sure the clockmaker will blame everything on us, so you won't have to worry about a thing. In any case, if our plan goes off without a hitch, you'll all be free!","content.75.6591":"Free? What does that mean? \\n\\n*You notice that your little discussion is starting to intrigue the Grambos around you. They come closer, repeating this word that is apparently absent from their vocabulary, as if the sound of it was inexplicably appealing to them. Maybe it's time to motivate the troops*","content.75.6592":"*Julpi's eyes go as wide as saucers*\\n\\nYou're lying, adventurer{[1*]?:}! Such a thing isn't possible...","content.75.6593":"Freedom... I like that word! But after whipping Meccanox, what will we do if we're out of work?\\n\\n*The Grambos seem to be hanging on your every word, as if you were a storyteller telling them a captivating legend*","content.75.6594":"*Your proposals are met with a long, tense silence*","content.75.6595":"*The Grambos cry out in joy. Some faint at the idea of gaining free will. Their brains are unable to rationalize this complex feeling*\\n\\nAdventurer{[1*]?:}, what you're proposing sounds far better than one day off a year! You can count on us!","content.75.6596":"I don't know why, but I get the feeling it's going to be a long day...","content.75.6597":"Just give me a moment...\\n\\n*Laura marks the map in three different spots*\\n\\nThere. If I'm not mistaken, these three spots will be the most effective in disrupting the island's energy flows. ","content.75.6598":"That's good timing, as we just finished them! It's pretty crude, but they should last for the whole operation.","content.75.6599":"How they work is really simple. You put them in the appropriate places, press the button to deploy them... and cross your fingers that they won't blow up in your face.","content.75.6600":"Noooo... At least in theory.","content.75.6601":"He means we have no idea. Sorry, but you'll just have to deal with it!","content.75.6602":"*The Grambo smiles at you*\\n\\nOur movement has never had so many supporters! You really are amazing, adventurer{[1*]?:}. This is all thanks to you!","content.75.6603":"Indeed, there's not much doubt about the nature of this structure. It must be one of the machines we've been looking for! I'm intrigued by this container, though. Did the machine look active to you?","content.75.6605":"Just as I thought. It must lack an energy source to power the ruins where we are.","content.75.6606":"Incredible... It seems to contain an astronomical amount of energy! \\n\\n*Milo looks over your discovery from every possible angle*\\n\\nIt looks like some sort of... energy cell!","content.75.6607":"Here, just look.\\n\\n*The archaosologist points to the ends of the artifact*\\n\\nThese two opposite points serve as poles to balance the energy charges that flow through it. The inside of the... \"egg\" must function as the site of a Wakfu reaction, subject to intrinsic stimulation of an accumulation process involving...","content.75.6608":"It's a battery. Or the Eliatrope equivalent, I suppose.\\n \\n*Milo reluctantly gives you the artifact back*\\n\\nAll you need to do is take it to that machine, and we'll see what happens.","content.75.6609":"Really? Can you describe it to me in detail?","content.75.6610":"Indeed, there's not much doubt about the nature of this structure. It must be one of the machines we've been looking for! \\n\\n*Milo reluctantly gives you the artifact back*\\n\\nAll you need to do is take the energy cell to it, and we'll see what happens.","content.75.6611":"I was waiting for you to get back! One of the diodes turned on, projecting an Eliatrope rune! I knew it was you who was behind the change.","content.75.6612":"It's still too early to validate my whole theory. I managed to translate a few engravings that weren't affected by the passage of time. It looks like the link between the machine and the base represented by these runes is called \"resonance\".","content.75.6613":"Yes, this is getting exciting! I wonder what will happen once you've reactivated all the resonances... I'll be relying on you again for the next part!","content.75.6614":"It doesn't matter... You wish to defy time and play in my room? *sinister laugh*","content.75.6615":"*As you approach the strange house, you notice a small creature. It looks peaceful, looking at you with interest. You stop, not quite sure{[1*]?:} how to proceed*","content.75.6616":"Joupe snouk. Jutru snouk. Somonone ulu mir touk.\\n\\n*The little animal seems to be speaking to you in an unknown language, but you don't understand. Your expression is one of incomprehension, which he seems to understand. He lets out a small sigh before trying again, emphasizing each word and staring into your eyes*\\n\\nJoupe... snouk.","content.75.6617":"*The Zurikat goes back into the shack and comes out with two sheets of paper. One is a drawing of some kind of fruit, and the other is of a fish*\\n\\nPloss. Snouky splotch!","content.75.6618":"*The Zurikat takes hold of the fish between his two hands and inhales the smell eagerly. He goes back inside the hut with it. You hesitate to go inside, but for once, you show restraint and just stay a few yards from the doorway. But your curiosity gets the better of you, and you watch the Zurikat from the outside*","content.75.6619":"*With baffling skill, the little Zurikat cuts the fish up with a cleaver. He removes the bones, dices the meat, and adds it to a pot that was already on the fire. He smells it before adding a few finely chopped herbs, along with salt and roots. He then gets to work stirring the pot, still with a surprising level of skill*\\n\\n*You wait a good 15 minutes. The smell of fish soup and herbs begins to tickle your nostrils*","content.75.6620":"*The Zurikat takes out a ladle and an earthenware bowl. He serves two generous ladles into the bowl, filling it two-thirds full, and then heads toward you. You take a few steps back and look at the arid savannah landscape, but the little creature doesn't seem to care. He holds out the bowl of soup with both hands*\\n\\nAtela egale fla zia. Ekoudas timota zia.","content.75.6621":"*The creature extends his arms a little further, bringing the bowl of soup closer to your chest. You grasp it delicately. The Zurikat places the bowl in your hands and stares at you. It looks like he's waiting for you to take a sip*","content.75.6622":"*The little creature swallows loudly*","content.75.6623":"*The soup is hot and tasty. Many aromas flood your mouth. You are incredibly happy{[1*]?:} to taste such good soup. You raise your eyebrows and reveal a contented expression*\\n\\n*Even though you're already a{[1*]?:} great{[1*]?:} cook{[1*]?:}, you're impressed by the Zurikat's simple, delicious dish. You've prepared enough dishes in your lifetime to know that he's got great know-how*","content.75.6624":"*The soup is hot and tasty. Many aromas flood your mouth. You are incredibly happy{[1*]?:} to taste such good soup. You raise your eyebrows and reveal a contented expression*\\n\\n*You're already a{[1*]?:} fairly good cook{[1*]?:}. You've cooked little meals before, but this Zurikat seems to be more of an expert than you are. Ashamed{[1*]?:}, you inwardly admit that this harmless little creature is better than you are*","content.75.6625":"*The soup is hot and tasty. Many aromas flood your mouth. You are incredibly happy{[1*]?:} to taste such good soup. You raise your eyebrows and reveal a contented expression*\\n\\n*You've never cooked a thing in your life. This delicious soup fills you with joy, and you find yourself thinking that maybe you should start taking lessons, especially if such a small creature can make such tasty soup*","content.75.6626":"*The Zurikat's eyes light up, and you suppose it's the way he smiles*\\n\\nJaniu slopaktim.\\n\\n*He points to your bowl and exclaims*\\n\\nHoltu ploss. Ekoudas timota zia.","content.75.6627":"*The creature picks up your empty bowl, satisfied*\\n\\nSnouky splotch?","content.75.6628":"*The Zurikat picks it up. It looks like this is what he was expecting. He goes back inside the hut, and you suppose he's going to make you a dessert... So, the Zurikat cuts the fruit into halves, peels one half, and squeezes it into a bowl. He adds a kind of earthy paste, which he mixes with the fruit. It doesn't look appetizing*\\n\\n*He adds the contents of some kind of vial, and ocher smoke billows from the mixture. This can't be good at all*","content.75.6629":"Ji faltom.\\n\\n*Using a whisk, he beats the mixture vigorously. Then he goes to the other end of the hut. You stand back to watch what he's doing. He hangs two sheets side by side on his wall and grabs a gigantic brush, which he dips in the mixture. He then paints on the sheets... It looks like there won't be any dessert after all*","content.75.6630":"*The little animal draws at an impressive speed, quickly emerging from the hut to show you the results. In the first drawing, you recognize a portrait of the Zurikat himself: a small creature holding a brush larger than himself. You find the second drawing more interesting. On closer inspection, it looks like... You*\\n\\nJi faltom delp ossums jarepek.","content.75.6631":"*The situation seems insane to you. This defenseless little animal has cooked you a nice little meal before painting a striking portrait of you in just a few minutes. He seems to want to communicate with you... But what could he mean?*\\n\\n*You delicately take the drawing of yourself. The Zurikat puts his hand on his chest, then on his self-portrait, before saying one word clearly*\\n\\nBrossar.","content.75.6632":"[#name].\\n\\n*The Zurikat struggles to pronounce your name before jumping up and down happily. You're amazed{[1*]?:} this creature has managed to establish contact with you, first by offering you soup, then by drawing you. His approach has paid off*","content.75.6633":"Somonone ulu mir touk.","content.75.6634":"*Brossar seems to think for a moment. He goes back inside the hut and shows you two drawings. The first one looks quite old, and the sheet is yellowed and stained. It shows a lady wearing a cyan dress with gray hair*","content.75.6635":"*The creature looks very sad and sighs deeply before showing you another drawing. It's a man with big glasses, blue hair like his shirt, and an adventurer's hat. This person looks familiar*","content.75.6636":"*The drawing is so well done that you have no trouble recognizing your old companion with whom you explored the Bonta ruins and tried to unravel the mysteries of Crocoburio. When you say his name, the Zurikat is startled, as he recognizes it*","content.75.6637":"*Thankfully, Brossar guesses what you mean and gives you one final drawing. You take it in your hands. It consists of several symbols*","content.75.6638":"*Brossar shrugs and points to the drawing he's made for you. Looks like you'll have to try to figure out what it means...*","content.75.6639":"*mumbles while sketching various observations in his notebook*\\n\\nThis savannah is truly fascinating! The symbols on the trees and rocks in this biome seem to have been painted by an intelligent people. Is it a language? Ritual symbolism? I'd like to investigate that mystery... once I've solved the one that brought me to this island in the first place!","content.75.6640":"Yes, I can imagine. It's a long story, how I came to this island...  Actually, I came with the other archaosologists. Have you already met them?","content.75.6641":"It doesn't matter! I've made some fascinating discoveries! Listen to this. My father and Lebbocq won't believe it. This island contains evidence of Crocodyls... Crocodyls once lived on this island! Perhaps they even still live here!","content.75.6642":"*Jenry smiles at you with pride and enthusiasm*\\n\\nDo you remember when we explored the ruins in Bonta?","content.75.6643":"Over a thousand years ago, Crocodyls nearly took over the entire World of Twelve.\\n\\nWe found steles in Cania detailing the mythical tale of Crocoburio, the son of Grougalorasalar, one of the primordial dragons. It's said that Crocoburio wielded a sword of unimaginable power named Crocobur, and that he terrorized Bonta!\\n\\nThat is, until Croulaklakoss defeated the black dragon... And Crocoburio died too at the gates of Bonta. The sword Crocobur was lost at that point.\\n\\nThis tale dates back a good eight centuries or so.\\n\\nWe found a stele dating back three centuries claiming that Crocobur had come back to life... And it's true. He came back to life and led his people here, to this island! I imagine their exodus took place during Ogrest's Chaos.","content.75.6644":"Look inside this cavern. You can see a few rudimentary Crocodyl tools...\\n\\nThere are also some skeletons that clearly belong to their species. It looks like some sort of rudimentary, hastily built tomb. I'd say it dates back 50 years or so.","content.75.6645":"That is the question.\\n\\n*Jenry places a hand on your shoulder*\\n\\nWe need to find that blade. The fate of the world could depend on it... With the strength it contains, you might just be able to put an end to Ogrest's Chaos!","content.75.6646":"Hmm... Our interests align, however! We need to learn more about this area. All I've found so far is some sort of creature, er... A Zurikat called Brossar.","content.75.6647":"Well, well, well! I find it hard to believe that Brossar is so smart. He realized you were looking for me and decided to show you the way.","content.75.6648":"I was wandering the savannah, being chased by monsters, when I saw his hut. Strangely enough, the other monsters didn't want to go near it.\\n\\nWe tried to establish a dialogue. It took a bit of time and perseverance... But I managed to get across that I was looking for Crocodyls. He pointed out this dolmen. I didn't really understand what the symbols meant...\\n\\n*He shows you the drawing Brossar made for him: a drawing similar to yours*","content.75.6649":"*Jenry still looks thoughtful*","content.75.6650":"As it happens, [#name], I haven't the slightest idea.","content.75.6651":"I see. I guess I found the right dolmen by chance. Brossar did point me in the right direction...\\n\\n*You briefly consider that the Zurikat didn't do you this kindness, and you frown, which Jenry doesn't notice*\\n\\nI'd like to study this paint. It may be linked to the Crocodyls. Could you help me investigate it?","content.75.6652":"Yes. I think I've found everything I needed to find here.\\n\\nMeet me in the Zurikat's hut, and I'll try to ask him some questions in the meantime. He seems to know a lot about the region.","content.75.6653":"Well, well, well! It's the same paint as...\\n\\n*Jenry sniffs at a scale*\\n\\nYes, it's from the fruit you brought our friend. The smell is the same as on our drawings, something quite unique and honeyed.","content.75.6654":"Snouky splotch.","content.75.6655":"*The Zurikat takes the half of the fruit left on the table*\\n\\nSnouky.\\n\\n*Then he puts the fruit down and takes some kind of vial in his hand. You recognize the vial as the one he poured into the paint preparation. You don't know where it comes from, but it seems to be an essential ingredient in this paint*\\n\\nSplotch.\\n\\n*Finally, the Zurikat points to the orange line on the scale Jenry is holding*\\n\\nSnouky splotch.","content.75.6656":"We're well on our way.","content.75.6657":"Snouky.\\n\\n*The Zurikat puts down the vial and picks up the fruit*","content.75.6658":"Nice one, [#name]! Your powers of deduction are sharper than ever.\\n\\nUnfortunately, that doesn't get us very far. This strange paint grows on the region's trees. We can't establish a link with the Crocodyls.","content.75.6659":"Oh! That's just like you. I can't let you have that pleasure. You see, while you were carrying out that important mission, I was also making progress with my research...\\n\\nI managed to find out more about Brossar.\\n\\n*Jenry points to a new drawing you haven't seen yet*","content.75.6660":"So? What do you think?","content.75.6661":"Timo.\\n\\n*The Zurikat's voice seems tinged with a certain sadness as he says this word. Or rather... this name. You realize that it's not Brossar, but another Zurikat*","content.75.6662":"I think this Timo is a member of Brossar's family. For some unknown reason, he's not here, but far south of here.\\n\\n*You look at the drawing again. Timo's face looks distorted, and he seems to be holding some kind of skull*","content.75.6663":"It's possible. What's got me wondering is this skull. Doesn't it look like a Crocodyl skull? That's our trail! Maybe we can find out more about Crocobur by speaking to Timo.\\n\\n*Jenry has managed to put the topic of Crocobur back on the table*","content.75.6664":"A dungeon? How exciting! I'm sure it will be quite interesting... Imagine if we got our hands on Crocobur after an epic fight!","content.75.6665":"What's wrong with you all of a sudden? We've survived many adventures together. You look really serious. I'm perfectly capable of going with you.\\n\\n*It's true that you're in the grip{[1*]?:} of an inexplicable adrenaline rush. There's something about this drawing that makes you shudder. You don't know what kind of powers Timo possesses*\\n\\n*Jenry would have trouble following you. What's more, you're beginning to find his ambition to get his hands on Crocobur at all costs rather disturbing*","content.75.6666":"Alright, then... But you're forbidden from getting your hands on the legendary sword without me!","content.75.6667":"*You tell of your terrible fight with the Zurikat possessed by a vengeful Crocodyl spirit, the fact that it is being held in place by a powerful seal, and that it actually controls the region's monsters*\\n\\nSo, you managed to speak to the spirit possessing him... I guess it has something to do with that kind of skull he has on his scepter. You were right, [#name]. That fight must have been no mean feat.","content.75.6668":"I see. Exorcising this evil spirit would free Timo.\\n\\nWe don't have an immediate solution, do we? I wonder if we have an expert on Nolifis and its ghosts in our group of archaosologists...\\n\\n*Jenry seems to be racking his brains to solve Timo's problem*","content.75.6669":"Yes...\\n\\nYou were right, [#name]. I'm so caught up in my excitement to find Crocobur, that fabulous treasure... So much so that I'm losing sight of what's essential. The most important thing is to proceed with caution. We need to look at the facts rationally.\\n\\nI'll try to keep that in mind.","content.75.6670":"Very well. This thing can wait!","content.75.6671":"Timo troun...\\n\\n*You realize that he recognizes this medallion. You decide to hand it over*","content.75.6672":"*The little creature takes it delicately. His eyes are teary... This sight pains you greatly. You failed to free Timo, and you barely learned anything useful about the Crocodyls. This vengeful spirit must have some answers, but you'll find it hard to trust him... It's frustrating*\\n\\nHuglasp.\\n\\n*Brossar stares at you and tightly clutches the medallion*","content.75.6673":"*Without saying a word, the Zurikat opens a trapdoor hidden under his rug. He pulls out a chest. He opens the chest and takes out a large bluish orb, which he holds out to you. You realize he is thanking you for entrusting him with this memento of his brother and has decided to give you this in return*","content.75.6674":"*You take the sphere, and a kind of energy washes over you*\\n\\nI wonder what it is... Perhaps you should ask Milo, as he might have some idea about it!","content.75.6675":"Yes, he's a very smart creature. I managed to take a look inside. I think he's collected a lot of things from ships that have run aground in the region: jars, crates, tools...\\n\\nAfter all, many a sailor has been trapped by the Misty Isle.","content.75.6676":"My father's father studied the Bwork clans years and years ago. While searching for... I don't know what, near Brakmar, he saw the Misty Isle with his own eyes. That was well over 70 years ago. Not many people believed him, apart from a few Brakmarian fishermen who had also spotted the island.\\n\\nThe island disappeared a few days later... Many sailors sailed in the direction my grandfather pointed out. Some of them vanished, but most returned without having found any island whatsoever.","content.75.6677":"Yes! And as it happens, it looks like we've still got a lot of mysteries to unravel on this island. This really smart Zurikat will help us get to the truth of the matter!","content.75.6678":"*The Grambos' master examines his vast array of magnifying glasses for a moment and then turns to you again, looking confident*\\n\\nOh, hello, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I was waiting for you... I hope you don't mind if we speak as equals.\\n\\n*You glance at the crate on which Meccanox is standing to overlook you*","content.75.6679":"*The Grambos' master examines his vast array of magnifying glasses for a moment and then turns to you again, looking confident*\\n\\nSo? How's that coming along?","content.75.6680":"*Meccanox sweats profusely when he sees you. You move toward him, boiling with rage, and his face reveals his surprise and panic* \\n\\nI-I... Well, adventurer{[1*]?:}, you're back already...","content.75.6681":"*The Grambo is packing some things into a kind of suitcase in a real hurry. He looks at his lenses in an inexplicable state of panic*\\n\\nHow am I going to escape with all this? I won't be able to leave on the Noxine-Express...\\n\\n*Suddenly, he jumps and turns around, seeing you with your arms crossed in front of him* ","content.75.6682":"*Meccanox pouts. He looks fearful when he sees you, but he tries to regain his composure* \\n\\nOh, hello, adventurer{[1*]?:}... How nice to see you again...","content.75.6683":"That's great.\\n\\n*The Grambo examines you. He's totally motionless. Is he... thinking about something?*\\n\\nI've had an absolutely great idea. You want to help the Grambos, right?","content.75.6684":"I don't have to tell you that the Grambos' cause is at the heart of the concerns of our group: the Clockmaking and Vehicle Corporation. The CVC group represents the future of the World of Twelve. And that's why we're always looking for ways to improve our associates' wellbeing.","content.75.6685":"They exaggerate so much... Do you really think they don't like it here? They're more than happy to follow our project, believe me.\\n\\n*You doubt these words for a moment. It all sounds like slavery, pure and simple. Meccanox seems to realize this and goes on*\\n\\nWell... Yes, it's true, conditions aren't fantastic. But you've seen that the clockmaker's patience has its limits. I'm trying to protect them...","content.75.6686":"*Meccanox remains silent for a few seconds, not seeming to realize what you're getting at, then he clears his throat*\\n\\nWe'll be freed when we've finished carrying out Lord Nox's plan. I have to make tough choices in an attempt to please our boss. Unfortunately, we're running out of resources.","content.75.6687":"In management, compromise is everything.","content.75.6688":"*Here you are: This negotiation should set the stage for your future relationship. You think you shouldn't show your hand too quickly. If you say you want to catch Nox and potentially wring his neck, Meccanox might warn him, and your plan could be foiled*\\n\\n*You consider taking advantage of this situation to learn more about Nox without getting noticed. Helping the Grambos could be a plus*","content.75.6689":"Yes, you could say that. I helped him with a few projects... A few systems here and there, nothing fancy compared to the genius of our master.","content.75.6690":"Yes, that sounds reasonable. But I need... a lot of help.","content.75.6691":"*You just killed two birds with one stone: Solving the Grambos' problems would enable you to learn more about Nox's plans, and Meccanox would be extremely grateful to you. Meccanox replies immediately*\\n\\nIn that case, I've got a few missions for you... But don't forget, it's in your interest to go unnoticed.","content.75.6692":"There are several problems.\\n\\nFirst of all, there's a Grambo expedition that didn't come back from the extraction cavern... I don't know why. They might be in danger.","content.75.6693":"Ah, hey{[1*]?:} there{[1*]?:}, {[1*]?gal:guy}. What can I do to help y'out?","content.75.6694":"I see... Thank you.\\n\\nMy employees' safety is essential to me, and it will always take priority... That said, what's happening with their delivery? Did they manage to collect the Fragmonnites?","content.75.6695":"That's annoying. I'm not exactly in tune with the project anymore, without those materials...","content.75.6696":"Ah, you again. What can I do to help y'out?","content.75.6697":"Ahem. It's a really interesting material. I know the Desolation is a rather empty land, but it used to be filled with lakes and aquatic fauna. The fauna has since been wiped out.","content.75.6698":"Ahem.\\n\\nFragmonnites are fossil remains of this fauna. They have extraordinary properties: high resistance and unparalleled conductivity. It's now a basic material for some of our machines.\\n\\nOnce crushed and reduced to sand, they can be turned into absolutely perfect glass. With our new lenses, we'll be able to carry out many innovative projects.","content.75.6699":"I'll be fine with 30 of 'em.","content.75.6700":"*Helmatoot looks you up and down before holding out one hand, gazing deeply into your eyes. It looks like she's trying to make you realize something indirectly*","content.75.6701":"*The Grambo grabs your hand and begins to apply pressure at regular intervals. She seems to be concentrating really hard, humming numbers out loud. After a moment, you notice that she's just alternating a sequence of two different fingers. You decide to copy her to lighten the mood*\\n\\n*As soon as the first pressure is applied, she lets you go*\\n\\nSo you're part of the UGW too... I'm fascinated.","content.75.6702":"Don't worry: I'm on your side. Anyway, I imagine Julpi has already told you about me.","content.75.6703":"Hahahaha, I knew it... but I'm going to introduce myself anyway. I'm Helmatoot, and I make sure the work is done properly in the forest.","content.75.6704":"And what's more, I'm one of the most important members of the group!","content.75.6705":"Speaking of questions, I've got one for you!\\n\\n*Helmatoot looks left and right, then up and down. Once that is done, she lifts her feet one by one to check that there's nothing underneath them*\\n\\nThere's no one around, so I need to talk to you.","content.75.6706":"For some time now, I've been hearing strange things when I listen to the other Grambos around here talking among themselves. None of it sounds good, and I'm afraid they'll blow my cover if I get involved.\\n\\nI think they want to breed combat Ferociraptors to take control of the island.","content.75.6707":"I don't know where, but they found Ferociraptor eggs somewhere in the forest. I spied on them for several days to find out where they were incubating them. If they ever manage to hatch them, it could be catastrophic.\\n\\n*The Grambo raises her hands to the sky*\\n\\nWhy did it have to be such big criminal masterminds who came across them?! Every time I talk to them about it, they cleverly change the subject.","content.75.6708":"In your great kindness, I see you're trying to reassure me about the situation. I'm grateful to you, but it's my duty as a high-class Grambo to preserve calm and order on the island while trying to overthrow the rule with the rest of the United Grambo Workers.","content.75.6709":"I think the smartest thing to do would be for you to pay them a visit and help them hatch their eggs.","content.75.6710":"Wait! Listen to the rest of my plan. I've been thinking about it for a long time.\\n\\nIn fact, when the eggs hatch, you'll go right up to the Ferociraptors and let them think you're their mommy. Then you can order them around and avoid disaster.","content.75.6711":"Not at all. What if Lord Meccanox discovered them and became their mother? He would use them to attack us.","content.75.6712":"*Helmatoot looks at you in silence. After a moment, she continues*\\n\\nBasically, my idea is to help them hatch their eggs and take control of the dinosaurs.","content.75.6713":"Grambo's honor!\\n\\n*The Grambo points to a trapdoor*\\n\\nThey meet here regularly. This is Lord Meccanox's egg reserve. There must be some reason why they've put their eggs there, but I don't know...","content.75.6714":"Thank you very much, adventurer{[1*]?:}. You've made up for my Grambo comrades' mistake. I'm most grateful.","content.75.6715":"Our group is trying to specialize in the transportation sector. We're developing many high-quality, environmentally friendly vehicles.","content.75.6716":"Don't underestimate our ability to create a revolution in the field of teleportation.\\n\\nBesides, you should try out our Noxine-Express network! Noxines will take you all over the island. Well, uhh... It looks like there's a calibration error with the region's Noxine-Express. Do you think you could investigate it?","content.75.6717":"Perfect!\\n\\n*Meccanox looks at you warily, seemingly expecting something from you. You must ask him another question about Nox... You seem to have won the Grambo boss's trust, so it seems appropriate to show your hand a little more*","content.75.6718":"*The Grambo looks a bit embarrassed and coughs a little before replying*\\n\\nThe clockmaker acts alone. We Grambos are at his service, of course, but we're not much of a strike force.\\n\\n*A single Xelor with formidable machines, sure... But he seems to be within your reach. You think that for an adventurer of your caliber, you could ask Nox for an explanation and get away with it, even if it gets a little rough*","content.75.6719":"Can I enlighten you, adventurer{[1*]?:}?","content.75.6720":"*Meccanox says nothing. You may have played your cards a bit fast. You decide to backpedal a little to see if Meccanox is on the same wavelength as you*","content.75.6721":"*Meccanox crosses his hands in a conciliatory gesture*\\n\\nSure, I understand. I'll tell you more, if you really want...\\n\\nLet's say Nox is looking for particular things. An... energy source.","content.75.6722":"Nox discovered there were several on this island. These energy sources could be useful for his plan.\\n\\nWe found one just a few hours ago... I could use your help.","content.75.6723":"Our master has already collected one and is using it to power the machine factory.\\n\\n*Meccanox stares at you intently, his hands still crossed calmly. He begins to speak more softly*\\n\\nWe mustn't let Nox get the second one...","content.75.6724":"B-But...","content.75.6725":"*You grab hold of Meccanox's collar and lift him out of his cursed crate to bring him up to your height*\\n\\nNo, please! I'll tell you anything you want!\\n\\n*You notice that Meccanox seems terrified*","content.75.6726":"Owie!\\n\\nAlright, everything's in the factory... You'll find all the information you need in the big box at the back. That's also where the energy source is... I swear!","content.75.6727":"S-Stop! I'll tell you everything!\\n\\nMany Nox machines are guarding this place.\\n\\nThere's a secret to opening the box... You have to assemble... I mean, you have to place monsters on special trapdoors.","content.75.6728":"Yeah, uh... It's like a code. You need two Noximpetuses, two Noxilts, and two Noxus IV.\\n\\n*You frown and bring your face closer to the trembling Grambo*\\n\\nI swear! I promise you on everything I hold dear!","content.75.6729":"*The Grambo is packing some things into a kind of suitcase in a real hurry. He looks at his lenses in an inexplicable state of panic*\\n\\nHow am I going to escape with all this? I won't be able to leave on the Noxine-Express...\\n\\n*Suddenly, he jumps and turns around, seeing you with your arms crossed in front of him*\\n\\nOoooh no...","content.75.6730":"I-I can explain everything...","content.75.6731":"A... Adventurer{[1*]?:}...","content.75.6732":"Please, listen... ","content.75.6733":"*Meccanox shouts back*\\n\\nI had to! I'm in between Nox and you. If I antagonize Nox, he'll make me suffer the consequences. And the same goes for you. You're both the same!\\n\\nYou Twelvians really think you're gods. You're playing hardball with us... It isn't right! Do you think I chose to grovel at the clockmaker's feet?","content.75.6734":"I don't have it anymore. It was stolen from me. I wanted to get it and put it in a safe place just after you left{[1*]?:} for the dungeon. When we reached the control room, it was there... But by the time I'd activated the controls to disconnect it properly, it had disappeared.\\n\\n*The Grambo sighs wearily*","content.75.6735":"*Suddenly, you hear a Noxine-Express behind you. Amelia Hartlyss steps out, carrying a large cloth bag on her back, and she stands beside you*","content.75.6736":"At your service. I took the liberty of following Meccanox back to that control room when you left{[1*]?:} for the dungeon.\\n\\nI thought it would be a way of thanking you for helping me out of the abyss.\\n\\n*Amelia hands you the bag. You take it and find a large blue orb inside*","content.75.6737":"If you're in any doubt about what it is, you should show it to the archaosologists. In particular, Milo should be able to help you...","content.75.6738":"Maybe you're right.\\n\\nEspecially as I made a tidy profit by getting a bunch of gadgets from those Grambos...","content.75.6739":"*Meccanox wants to protest but can't. He looks completely exhausted*\\n\\nPfff...","content.75.6740":"Consistent?\\n\\n*You clout Meccanox, who falls to the ground*","content.75.6741":"*You and Amelia move away. Once Meccanox can't hear you, Amelia speaks*\\n\\nYou hit him so Nox wouldn't do it for you.","content.75.6742":"True.\\n\\nHave a good trip. I'll try to find the archaosologists. We'll probably meet again.","content.75.6743":"*When you fell into the pit, you didn't expect to run into Amelia Hartlyss... She shrugs as she approaches you*\\n\\nA friendly face at last... Mind you, I didn't expect to see you so soon.","content.75.6744":"Like you, I'm trying to make life hard for that darn Xelor. But he's very smart and very well protected...","content.75.6745":"Yes. Have you already met the other archaosologists? I came separately when the island appeared... I don't really want to run into them, you know? It's a Riktus problem. We've lost face since certain events.\\n\\nAnd while I've got you here, stop repairing the Noxine-Expresses I keep going to the trouble of sabotaging!","content.75.6746":"Bingo. You know how expensive these things are. I've been bothering them for a while now, trying to find out more, but the clockmaker is covering his tracks well. I figured he must have some valuable gadgets to steal.\\n\\nWell, for the moment, we seem to be stuck here...","content.75.6747":"I would have tried to warn you sooner, but there was always a Noximpetus to pelt me whenever I approached you.\\n\\n*Think that with the noise they're making, you're surprised{[1*]?:} you didn't hear Amelia being shot at earlier. Yes, that's surprising... Perhaps it's more plausible that she didn't try so hard to warn you*","content.75.6748":"This door is locked, but luckily, the control levers are on our side. All we have to do is pull both levers at the same time to get through the door.\\n\\n*You're still as impressed{[1*]?:} with Amelia's knowledge. She means business when it comes to unlocking doors*","content.75.6749":"Aaaah...\\n\\n*The demon inhales deeply, his fists opening and closing while his titanic muscles flex beneath his skin*\\n\\nHow good it is to be whole again... But Bulak is starving!","content.75.6750":"Don't be such a sore{[1*]?:} loser{[1*]?:}! Without the part of my soul locked up in that darn sword, I wasn't really myself.\\n\\nTo thank you for twice freeing me from my prison, I'll even let you get out of here. Let it not be said that Bulak doesn't honor his pacts!","content.75.6751":"*Bulak's incandescent gaze seems to pierce your soul*\\n\\nHow arrogant.\\n\\nDon't think you can compete with me just because you've defeated a tiny fraction of my powers in this pitiful prison of flesh... I'll break you, just like I destroyed those scaly people by feeding on their souls.","content.75.6752":"*Fiery flames erupt from Bulak's breath*\\n\\nMy patience is very nearly at its limit, [#breedName]. The idea of making you into my first meal is becoming more and more delicious...","content.75.6753":"*This was clearly one provocation too many. The demon bursts into flames with an unbearable smell of sulfur*\\n\\nTHAT'S ENOUGH! I'LL REPAINT MY TEMPLE WALLS WITH YOUR BLOOD!","content.75.6754":"*The Shushu's breathing is nothing more than a rasping wheeze now, and although his gaze has just as much fighting spirit in it, he can't hide the scars of your confrontation*\\n\\n*You come away from this fight victorious{[1*]?:}. You must be used to Shushus by now, even if Bulak was extremely powerful and devastating. Crocobur really helped{[1*]?:} you out*\\n\\nHaaa... Ha ha... HA HA HA!!  It's been so long since I had a fight like that! How thrilling! My blood's rushing!","content.75.6755":"*The demon stops smiling*\\n\\nI haven't played my last trump card. Crocatzin locked me up with his last breath, but part of my soul escaped. Locked up in this... thing, I witnessed something he didn't know while he was alive!","content.75.6756":"*The demon's smile widens*\\n\\nOh no, adventurer{[1*]?:}. I'm not lying this time.\\n\\n*Bulak raises one arm toward the wall of flames at the back of the temple*","content.75.6757":"*The Grambo stares at you as if he doesn't recognize you. Suddenly, you notice a spark in his blank gaze, and he starts to hop up and down*\\n\\nSo, have you brought something to incubate the egg?","content.75.6758":"Who are you again?","content.75.6759":"*You approach the Hullcatz. He seems to be purring to himself as he scans the horizon*\\n\\nI should try going on an adventure myself.","content.75.6760":"*The Hullcatz grabs the journal. His hands slide over the leather. Not a meow or a purr leaves his lips. He stares at the cover for several seconds, then nods*\\n\\nFelix... So, you found the Misty Isle after all.","content.75.6761":"No, no... I...\\n\\n*The Hullcatz's hands grip the journal's cover*\\n\\nCan I tell you a story about Felix? ","content.75.6762":"Well, he was a rare kind of adventurer. He loved adventure, of course. But you know what? He was determined to make his mark on history, to discover unknown places. To carry the torch, as he used to say.\\n\\nHe would eventually carry it for real... One day, Felix hoisted some kind of bonfire over his boat. Needless to say, it could've ended very badly! I remember jumping onto his boat and tossing the sail that had caught fire into the sea. Ah... I was so worried.","content.75.6763":"Yes, he was always in good company. He made friends wherever he went.\\n\\nWhen we returned to shore, he managed to turn things to mockery. Everyone laughed and made fun of his fake embarrassment. Even I did. He had a talent for storytelling. Everyone wanted to hear him share his next adventure or misadventure.\\n\\nHe arrived one day without saying hello. He left at night without saying goodbye.\\n\\nBut yes. We loved him. He was part of our lives...\\n\\n*The Hullcatz gives the journal back to you*","content.75.6764":"On second thought, I don't want the journal. I have thousands of memories of my friend in my heart... I don't need to know all the twists and turns of his journey. The stories belong to him alone. I can remember the Twelvian who stepped off his boat with his friends, glad to return to Astrub after a long voyage, with epic tales on his lips.\\n\\nAnd that's how it should be.","content.75.6765":"Welcome to my timeless theater, where scenes of life zoom by... Reliving my tragic demise keeps me focused on my objective.\\n\\n*The Xelor looks down, his voice turning melancholy*\\n\\nIt's kind of like turning back time.","content.75.6766":"*The Golem stays still. Maybe there's something in the room that would activate it*","content.75.6767":"Do you want to start the fight?","content.75.6768":"Do you want to start the fight?","content.75.6769":"Do you want to start the fight?","content.75.6770":"Do you want to start the fight?","content.75.6771":"Do you want to start the fight?","content.75.6772":"[#name]! Now, that's a surprise! Well, as you might've guessed, I'm no fighter. But I won't be kicked around either!\\n\\n*Laura twirls her pick in a questionable fashion*\\n\\nI think I'll fare better than my fellow archaosologists!","content.75.6773":"As you can see, the perils of this island weren't enough to scare me away! I'm not a fighter. But I won't be kicked around either!\\n\\n*Laura twirls her pick in a questionable fashion*\\n\\nI think I'll fare better than my fellow archaosologists!","content.75.6774":"When the various nations heard about this island appearing, they began squabbling to find out who would set foot on it first. Ironically, volunteers weren't flocking to bear the risks of such a journey. Then again, the legends surrounding this isle were less than reassuring!","content.75.6775":"You can say that again! Regardless, I'm the one who handled the administrative formalities allowing us to form this delegation. Having a representative from each nation has calmed the waters somewhat. ","content.75.6776":"It's not so bad if you know how to deal with politicians. Anyway, that's how the four of us ended up here! What about you? What are you doing here? I thought only the people in our expedition were mad enough to set foot on this myth of an island!","content.75.6777":"*Laura smiles and then laughs outright*\\n\\nHaha, I'm sorry. That was a dumb question. Of course, it's only natural for an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} of your skill to be interested{[1*]?:} in an island like this one! In fact, you could be very useful to me indeed.","content.75.6778":"*Laura points at the bluish minerals nearby*\\n\\nThe leaders of Amakna have asked me to identify the island's natural resources, with the possibility of exploiting them. The problem is, whenever I use my pick, the monsters start chasing me down!","content.75.6779":"I'm desperate to analyze a sample... You must've encountered the nearby creatures on the way here. They appear to be petrifying by the minute. I was hoping to determine if it was the same type of mineral.","content.75.6780":"*Laura's face is beaming*\\n\\nIs that so? You'll be taking a big thorn out of my side if you bring me samples of ore and those monsters! Be careful, though: They're tough, like they came straight from the Primitive Era! That's why I call them primounts. Has a nice ring to it, eh?","content.75.6781":"While I have you... I'd like to get a few samples of the plants in the area. The monsters seem to be herbivores, so perhaps their troubles stem from their food source. You don't mind?","content.75.6782":"It couldn't have been easy to collect all this ore, so thank you! At first glance, it seems pretty unique to me. Wakfu isn't supposed to stiffen like this... I'm going to need a little time to examine these samples!","content.75.6783":"Thanks! This material attached to their epidermis is what I find most intriguing. Have the monsters' bones calcified? Or is it the presence of that strange mineral in the area? Hopefully analyzing them will provide some answers.","content.75.6784":"This plant is the primounts' primary food source. Its leaves are packed with Wakfu, a pattern that seems to recur in the surrounding area... I need to do a few tests to be sure, but if they consume too much of it, this would certainly impact their metabolism.","content.75.6785":"You sure don't leave anything to chance! However, I'm not sure the primounts have gone all the way to the forest to feed... I've never seen them chewing on rozen. That being said, this luminous plant could be used by miners to light the tunnels! It's an interesting find.","content.75.6786":"First, the plants you brought. I'm not a botanist, so my knowledge in this area is limited. However, it's reasonable to assume these specimens are very primitive. Their structure is simple, and they don't resemble anything I've seen before, at any rate!","content.75.6787":"That is one possibility. As for the rocks, I confirmed that they have the same origin! The primounts' petrification is therefore not the result of a unique physical feature. This mineral behaves similarly to a parasite, slowly eating away at its host, presumably by draining its Wakfu.","content.75.6788":"I can't say so definitively. At least, I don't think it's developed consciousness, if that's what you're driving at. Nevertheless, it's certainly no ordinary mineral. Such rapid growth doesn't correspond to any geological data known to our world.","content.75.6789":"It may sound crazy, but I think this logic-defying rock came from space. From a comet, to be more precise! \\n\\nIn fact, that's not the only valid explanation. But I'm seeing structural similarities with comet remains found in the World of Twelve. And after all, many legends tell of artifacts that were forged using metals from the stars!","content.75.6790":"I can only imagine! Finally, if the parasitic rock is clinging to the primounts, it must be because of their diet. The high concentration of Wakfu in the primaniolas is collected by this rock, which explains their accelerated development!","content.75.6791":"I think that symbiotic link explains why they get aggressive when the rock is attacked. Since they don't present a mortal danger to you, could you come with me to the dig site I explored? Sadly, someone had apparently gotten there first, and I didn't have time to uncover what the place was hiding.","content.75.6792":"This skeleton must have belonged to a budding archaosologist or adventurer who got trapped on the island years ago. Hope I don't end up like him!","content.75.6794":"The poor wretch... It's up to us to continue his work! I agree that this part of the wall is definitely weaker. But we'll still need a really good pick to bring it down. Do you have the materials to craft one?","content.75.6795":"Not much more, unfortunately. Like I said, the concentration of Wakfu is such that an average Twelvian would lose consciousness in a few minutes. \\n\\nBut I saw the guardian: some kind of huge, violent primate. I even named him: Imagorila!","content.75.6796":"You know what? I might have an idea...\\n\\n*The archaosologist rifles through her gear and pulls out an amulet shaped like a shield and adorned with a pearl. It looks very old and worn*","content.75.6797":"I found this amulet connected to the goddess Feca while on an expedition. It seemed to have lost its power, but I've kept it as a good-luck charm for years. I think it could be restored to offer protection again.","content.75.6798":"That's right: I need you to get me some resources to restore the two parts of the artifact. \\n\\nFirst off, I don't think you'll like this, but... I need some Ogrest's tears. The amulet's magic comes from the pearl in its center, and we have to recharge it using that. ","content.75.6799":"The other part will be easier to get. I'll need primount tails so I can collect the fur from them and braid a new cord for the amulet. If we're lucky, that'll be enough to restore its powers.","content.75.6800":"Hopefully this artifact can shield you from the Wakfu fumes. Our curiosity will soon be satisfied!","content.75.6801":"Perfect! Hopefully, it'll counter the harmful effects of this cave. Wait just a minute...\\n\\n*Laura starts braiding a new cord for the amulet, patiently and meticulously*","content.75.6802":"*You wait patiently, watching the archaosologist as she applies the Ogrest's tears on the gem, which glimmers intermittently. After a few moments, the stone shines with a comforting glow*\\n\\nThere we go! Here, you can borrow it!","content.75.6803":"*Laura nods, looking satisfied*\\n\\nThere's nothing more I can do for you now. I'll wait outside while you deal with the guardian, and then I'll join you.","content.75.6804":"That was a close one! I'm impressed. Every time I see you, you're stronger{[1*]?:} than the last time!","content.75.6805":"Much better, thanks! If you hadn't been around, I would've passed out in the cavern... But look, it worked out!","content.75.6806":"You think so? It doesn't seem to be a real egg, anyway. I'm guessing Milo will know more... This is his specialty, after all. If you haven't run into him, he should be in the forest now. He was intrigued by the ruins there.","content.75.6807":"Really? Well, in that case, I'll give it to you. After everything you've done to help me with my research, you've earned it! I'm going to continue looking for similar places in the region.","content.75.6808":"The story of this island is turning out to be far more complex than we imagined. The fates of its multiple tribes have intertwined to form an archaosological puzzle. It's downright thrilling!","content.75.6809":"*The archaosologist stays quiet for a while, processing everything*\\n\\nWell... I already knew this island was special, but I had no idea just how special it was! The threat from that Xelor seems serious... I agree that we have to stop him. You can count on me!","content.75.6810":"*Her eyes light up, her interest piqued*\\n\\nIs that so? No, I haven't ventured into that part of the island yet. If it really is a temple, it could be the place we're looking for! ","content.75.6811":"Ogrest's Chaos! It would've been too easy... \\n\\n*The archaosologist begins contemplating the matter until your eyes meet and you see a look of understanding in his*\\n\\nDon't tell me...","content.75.6812":"That evil spirit is out of control... Who knows what he'll be capable of once he's free...? ","content.75.6813":"Well... With a little time, I might be able to decipher the inscriptions!","content.75.6814":"Hmm... I can't really argue with that. I feel somewhat bitter since we failed to reunite him with his brother... If you think it's the right solution, I trust you. ","content.75.6815":"I'll wait for you in front of the temple. With any luck, I'll have found a solution by the time you get there!","content.75.6816":"This temple gives off an evil energy... I don't know what's behind those runes, but my instincts are screaming to be on my guard.","content.75.6817":"It's even worse inside... The atmosphere is heavy, and the air is unbreathable! You look like you'd have an easier time handling it... \\n\\nI'll let you explore the environment first{[1*]?:}. Meanwhile, I'll keep an eye on our new friend.","content.75.6818":"A Shushu! I knew the Crocodyls used some bloody rituals... but sacrificing themselves to summon a demon?! I... I've got to finish translating this text!","content.75.6819":"So, you fought the demonarch?\\n\\n*The demon chokes out a strained laugh*\\n\\nBwahaha... Just my luck... Looks like I wasn't that fortunate to run into you after all.","content.75.6820":"*The demon chuckles laboriously. It seems he's badly weakened*\\n\\nIf you want... It doesn't matter anymore.","content.75.6821":"It's because of that damned Crocodyl... I promised his people that I'd give them the strength to defeat their enemies. I had already been the Jade Bloodlord once, so why not give it another go? But the truth was, I had no interest in reprising that whole song and dance.","content.75.6822":"All I cared about was escaping Rushu's clutches. His tortures are among the worst ever devised! When the scalies opened the portal, I was able to escape from my prison. \\n\\nMoving through the planes has consequences, and I found myself weakened. So I seized control of their leader's body to feast on the blood of his subjects.","content.75.6823":"Have you finished questioning me? If so, then just finish me off... Let's get this over with!","content.75.6824":"I was so weak that I was struggling to even control this frail, tiny body. I fed on the blood of other creatures on the island to gradually regain my strength. Parts of my memories and my identity had faded away during the separation from my soul. I was like a wild beast.","content.75.6825":"*The demon lets out a groan*\\n\\nHe got lucky. If I hadn't been weakened by the journey, my control would have been complete! But in spite of everything, he managed to turn Crocobur against him and seal a part of my soul within it. That mistake cost me dearly, but a fragment of my soul survived to take up residence in another living being. It was this curious rodent who was watching the whole thing!","content.75.6826":"We are artisans of destruction, but that doesn't mean we can't have our own identity and aspirations! Regardless, I eventually drew some unwanted attention, and those Bwork witches flushed me out and imprisoned me with their powerful magic. I don't know why, but my powers of influence had no effect on them.","content.75.6827":"You know the rest. Some of my powers came back, and I was able to extend my grip over the animals in the area. And the whole time, I pretended to be a Crocodyl spirit in hopes that someone would be stupid enough to set me free! Ha ha...","content.75.6828":"Heh heh... Not directly, but I saw it when I escaped into the rodent's body. I think the artifact's appearance is linked to Crocatzin's death. But why? I couldn't care less. I just wanted to use it to spread more destruction!","content.75.6829":"All's fair in love and war. The only law I respect is survival of the fittest!\\n\\n*The demon twitches slightly, as though to adjust his position before springing into action*","content.75.6830":"*The demon hurls a chain at you that wraps around Crocobur, then tears it out of your hands in a powerful motion*\\n\\nHA! As though I'd ever say that!","content.75.6831":"I never had any intention of fighting... \\n\\n*Bulak swings the sword in a windmill arc before jamming it into the palm of his other hand*","content.75.6832":"*The demon's image blurs, and it takes you a moment to realize he's being absorbed by the sword*\\n\\nI am immortal, and I can wait a few more decades until you're no longer part of the equation... Time marches inexorably forward, and one day, someone else will find me and set me free once more.","content.75.6833":"*All that remains of the Shushu is a shadow as his final words ring in the air*\\n\\nIt's either that, or death. You have far too many battles ahead of you to try and do without this sword... You will need my strength to defeat the clockmaker... and many other adversaries as well...\\n\\n*Crocobur falls to the ground with a deafening clatter*","content.75.6834":"*As you approach Crocatzin's skeleton, a wisp of smoke appears and takes on the form of a Crocodyl Ghostof. He looks at you with great interest and speaks to you. You understand everything he says, which surprises you for a moment*\\n\\nAdventurer{[1*]?:}... You have defeated a great evil and liberated my people from the grip of a treacherous demon. In blood I vanished, and in blood I appear before you to thank you this day.","content.75.6835":"*The Crocodyl bows silently in expression of his profound gratitude*","content.75.6836":"That's right. I am the last king of the Crocodyls... and one of Crocoburio's sons. My story is told in my journal, where my last words are also written... However, it seems that fate has seen fit to let me manifest once more.","content.75.6837":"The years after my death are nothing but indistinct nightmares. But I do remember my final moments quite clearly. I was sure that all was lost that day. The demon's grip on my body was unrelenting - I couldn't do a thing about it. Not a single thing.","content.75.6838":"Then, for one brief moment, a force buried deep within me suddenly awakened. I was able to temporarily regain control of my body. I decided to take advantage of that unexpected opportunity to end my own life and take the demon down with me. It seems that my failure has caused you no end of trouble...","content.75.6839":"It's all explained in my final words, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Our people had their back against the wall, and it only seemed right to protect them... What a fool I was to believe that demon's promises...","content.75.6840":"You were right to take him out. I saw you use demonic energy, adventurer{[1*]?:}. But you were not corrupted{[1*]?:}...","content.75.6841":"Vestiges? Rushu? I'm not sure I fully understand...","content.75.6842":"In that case, you are worthy and respectable. We Crocodyls could never resist the allure of great power, and for that we paid the ultimate price. Our people have now completely disappeared.","content.75.6843":"This demon is responsible for what happened, but he was only acting in accordance with his nature. The real causes of this disaster are our people's pride and my own weakness. The Jade Bloodlord's empire was already just a legend when I came into the world. Ogrest's Chaos dealt the final killing blow to our people's past glory, leaving us as orphans of an inhabitable land. ","content.75.6844":"Can you blame my people for seeking in me the strength of Crocoburio and Crocobur? Can you be angry at them for seeking to regain the glory of their ancestors?\\nAnother people would surely have emigrated somewhere else when the greenskins arrived... But I couldn't find the words to convince my people to renounce everything they aspired to.","content.75.6845":"Only after my hands were drenched in their blood did I decide to use it to save others. But as you know, all I really did was condemn them to darkness. Bulak used us and reduced all of our hopes to dust. Our families, our lives, our future...\\n\\n*You can see profound suffering in Crocatzin's face*","content.75.6846":"It troubles my very soul to talk about it... I shall have no rest as long as it exists. Please, finish what I started. Kill him once and for all.","content.75.6847":"This sword is a gift from Grougalorasalar, the primordial ebony dragon, to his son Crocoburio. It was the key to many of our great successes... and became the instrument of our demise.\\n\\nIt was by Crocobur's blade that the last of the Crocodyls died. It was forged in the fire of another dragon, so it should be quite indestructible.","content.75.6848":"There is a solution, however: Only the black fire that springs from an ocean of ebony tears can undo what has been forged by dragon fire... \\nThe power of the Dofus could destroy Crocobur once and for all, utterly annihilating the spirit trapped inside... Although the process is not without its risks.","content.75.6849":"Wait, [#name]! Think of what we could accomplish with that sword. We spent so much time searching for it... We can't just destroy it on a whim!\\n\\n*Absorbed{[1*]?:} in your discussion with the Crocodyl, you had almost forgotten the archaosologist was there*","content.75.6850":"*You set your hand on Jenry's shoulder, but the archaosologist seems repulsed by your decision*\\n\\nYou were the{[1*]?:} first{[1*]?:} to take advantage{[1*]?:} of a powerful form of demonic magic. The vestiges, as you call them. I know that Crocatzin suffered greatly at that demon's hands... But think of all the good we could do with that blade! Think of the historical value of our discovery!","content.75.6851":"At least keep it long enough to defeat the clockmaker! Besides, who says the Dofus will come out unscathed if you use it to destroy the relic?\\n\\n*The archaosologist gives you a determined stare, and you hold his gaze*","content.75.6852":"*The archaosologist stares at you a moment longer before giving in*\\n\\nWell... I'm still convinced that it's a mistake, but I respect your decision. You're a{[1*]?:} great{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}, and I'm just a simple archaosologist.","content.75.6853":"I understand that it's not an easy decision. You show compassion and wisdom in sacrificing Crocobur. With that choice, my people will find eternal rest.","content.75.6854":"*When the two artifacts collide, a devastating blast of energy is unleashed. The pain radiates through your arms, feeling ready to snap under the pressure. Bolts of black lightning surround you, accompanied by deafening cracks that roar like an almost unreal rumble of thunder*","content.75.6855":"*You persist despite your agony and apply just a little more force on the Dofus, causing its energy to surge. Finally, a minuscule crack appears in the metal, then rapidly snakes along the blade. A new scream joins in the cacophony all around you, and you recognize it all too well: It's Bulak's scream*","content.75.6856":"*Filled with the vengeful fury of an entire sacrificed people, you smash the blade down again until an enormous crack resonates through the temple, followed by a bone-chilling silence. You've done it. You raise one trembling hand to confirm it. Crocobur and Bulak are no more, disintegrated by the energy of the Dofus, which now appears to have fallen inert*","content.75.6857":"Yes, you've done it. You've untangled the threads of destiny that had condemned my people to eternal suffering. We are greatly in your debt, adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6858":"Yes, we will return to the darkness... \\n\\n*The ghost seems strangely absent for a moment*\\n\\nFather, is that your voice I hear? I've made you wait so long out there beyond Externam... We will soon be reunited...","content.75.6859":"*The Crocodyl's silhouette dissipates, leaving you alone with Jenry in this ghoulish temple*","content.75.6860":"*Jenry stares at you with an indecipherable expression*","content.75.6861":"*The archaosologist points at the Zurikat, still passed out on the floor*\\n\\nYou should deal with him first... He's still breathing, so all you need to do now is bring him back to his brother. I'll wait for you at the camp.","content.75.6862":"Timo! \\n\\n*The little creature cries out, then rushes over to his brother to confirm that he's truly alive. His eyes fill with tears, then he looks up at you with an expression of boundless gratitude*\\n\\nJi faltom huglasp!","content.75.6863":"*The Zurikat tightly embraces his brother, who eventually opens his eyes with a tormented look. After a few long seconds, he realizes that this is his brother, despite how much older he's gotten, and cries out in turn before hugging him back*","content.75.6864":"*Laura gives you a mischievous smile*\\n\\nOh no, that's not my kind of thing at all! See you soon, [#name]!","content.75.6866":"...\\n\\n*The archaosologist sinks into a deep silence*","content.75.6867":"Awesome, gimme those citronanas!","content.75.6868":"Goodbye.","content.75.6869":"*The archaosologist shoots you a teasing look*\\n\\nSo, you managed to hook up with the Bwork chief? Not bad. I wonder if they have any valuable artifacts. I'm guessing not much, apart from smelly socks...","content.75.6870":"*The archaosologist smiles shyly when she sees you*\\n\\nThere you are, [#name]! This place is more hospitable than it looks... I just wonder why the Grambos are keeping explosive powder so close to their fire.","content.75.6871":"*The young woman eyes you silently*\\n\\nI didn't miss the archaosologists. They're always snooping around caves and ruins!","content.75.6872":"I hope you've got a good reason for disturbing me!","content.75.6873":"Exquisite, succulent, delicate, and... nice and bloody!\\n\\n*slurp*","content.75.6874":"Hmm? What can I do for you, my friend{[1*]?:}?","content.75.6875":"Oh, I see. If he's sent you to pick up meals, I'm afraid I can't give you any at the moment...","content.75.6876":"Here's the monster of the day. Bring me some of its meat, and we can cook a dish together.","content.75.6877":"Marvelous. I'll let you use my kitchen workshop to see what you're capable of.","content.75.6879":"Marvelous! I will reward you based on the quality of your dish.","content.75.6880":"A Iop gourmet? Ha ha, well, I certainly do like to stuff my face from time to time! But I'm probably not the person you're looking for.","content.75.6881":"I only know one Iop like that: Karn. What a character...\\n\\nI heard he was passing through Astrub. Knowing him, you can probably find him hanging out with the hunters.","content.75.6882":"No trouble at all, friend{[1*]?:}. But be careful!\\n\\nHe's... not the easiest person to deal with.","content.75.6883":"A contest? Hmm... No, that doesn't ring a bell.\\n\\nBut there was that fellow who came to see me recently. He showed up in my kitchen looking for the best cook in the area!","content.75.6884":"Well, I answered the call! He certainly wasn't the most agreeable customer, but he paid well.","content.75.6885":"Kid{[1*]?:}, if I had to remember the name of every customer I serve, I'd have no room to remember my recipes! All I can tell you is that he was a Iop, or my name's not E.Z. Yeast!","content.75.6886":"Hmm, let's see... He was a redhead, with a proud and courageous attitude!\\n\\nDefinitely what you'd call a colorful character.","content.75.6887":"*The Iop cuts you off*\\n\\nI hope you've got a good reason for interrupting my meal! This dish is excellent... Such high-quality cooking deserves respect!\\n\\n*The Iop grips his cleaver firmly and points it at you*","content.75.6888":"Yes, that's me. I am Karn, master hunter and refined gourmet!\\n\\n*The Iop sizes you up from head to toe*\\n\\nAnd you are...?","content.75.6889":"*Karn bursts out laughing*\\n\\nWell, what do you know, another hero! Adventurers like you are a kama a dozen in Astrub!","content.75.6890":"*Karn interrupts you again*\\n\\nNever mind. Why were you looking for me?","content.75.6891":"That's right.","content.75.6892":"Yes. I may have been a bit harsh at first. But you see, I have a rather keen sense of honor. Even though... I'm very difficult to satisfy.\\n\\nI've been traveling the world for years. I've hunted the most terrifying and reclusive monsters in these lands to taste the finest meats that life has to offer! I've become more powerful in the course of my journey, and my standards have changed accordingly!","content.75.6893":"So far, only one cook around here has met my high standards! Pascal Liko, an old seafaring tomcat. A proper chef! The only trouble is, he doesn't seem able to bring me many dishes. ","content.75.6894":"I don't really know, but I don't think his age is doing him any favors.","content.75.6895":"Well, kid{[1*]?:}, if you can bring me some dishes that are worthy of old Pa-Liko, you'll be handsomely rewarded{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nI've accumulated quite a bit of wealth and unique collector's items in my travels. You won't be disappointed{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6896":"You want to bring him my dishes?","content.75.6897":"I don't care about rewards. Instead of bringing him my dishes, how would you like for me to teach you some Pa-Liko cooking techniques? As I get older, I worry that I won't be able to pass on my knowledge before I go dotty. I'd like to leave a legacy.","content.75.6898":"You see, Pa-Liko cuisine requires ingredients of the highest quality, gathered with great care and precision. The meat I use is particularly tasty. That's why Karn enjoys my dishes so much.","content.75.6899":"Well, that's precisely the problem. The meat has to be collected from very specific creatures, sometimes as dangerous as they are hard to get to. My supplies are all out, and I have less and less strength these days to go out monster hunting.","content.75.6900":"Well, if that's not a problem for you, then I'm prepared to teach you my art. Each day, I'll send you out to hunt a monster to collect its meat, and then we'll cook up a nice dish together. As you gain more experience, I can teach you some more sophisticated recipes.\\nWhat do you say{[1*]?:}?","content.75.6901":"Well, if that's not a problem for you, then I'm prepared to teach you my art. Each day, I'll send you out to hunt a monster to collect its meat, and then we'll cook up a nice dish together. As you gain more experience, I can teach you some more sophisticated recipes.\\nWhat do you say?","content.75.6902":"*Mishell straightens up and looks at you pensively. Her face takes on a satisfied expression*\\n\\nPerfect timing. I was just looking for a{[1*]?:} flunky{[1*]?:} for a little \"investigation\" mission.","content.75.6903":"What a cheek!\\n\\nAll right, let me rephrase that to be more to Your Highness's liking. Dearest{[1*]?:} chosen one{[1*]?:} of the prophecy, I humbly request your assistance for an investigation of the utmost importance.","content.75.6904":"*Mishell gives a sardonic smile, as though she were stewing up a nasty plan*\\n\\nI see you're learning from the strongest... and that's to your credit! You wouldn't leave an old friend in the lurch, would you?","content.75.6905":"*Mishell's face grows tense, as though she were disturbed by what she's about to tell you*\\n\\nI can hear my friends' voices... and their cries. I hear them begging Osamodas himself to come help them.","content.75.6906":"I don't normally intervene in Twelvians' affairs. I keep my distance from all that, even when they affect other species in the world.\\n\\nBut this time... No, this time is different. The situation is out of control.","content.75.6907":"All I can tell you is that there's a real massacre going on in the Sadida Kingdom.\\n\\nIt would be crazy of me to ask a{[1*]?:} simple adventurer{[1*]?:} to solve a mystery like this on their own, but...\\n\\nI'd like you to investigate the causes of the problem.","content.75.6908":"You really don't listen at all, do you?\\n\\nI just told you that I don't intervene in Twelvian activities! Besides, I'm not the one they asked for help.\\n\\nBut I'm sufficiently worried about their fate to ask you to look into it for me.","content.75.6909":"Not much, except for the pleasure of helping out your dear friend Mishell, who gave you a hand{[1*]?:} when you first arrived on the Wild Beach.\\n\\nA bit of advice: You'll always find it beneficial to maintain good relationships, especially with... strong and powerful people. But hey, your call.","content.75.6910":"*As you approach the camp, you see a broad-shouldered adventurer armed with an enormous knife and a pensive expression*\\n\\nA nice, fresh boowolf steak... Some kokomilk... High-quality spices... A bit of vanilla rice...\\n\\nWhat else could I add?","content.75.6911":"*You recognize Karn, the Iop gourmet from Astrub that you and Pascal Liko cooked dishes for. The Iop turns towards you briefly as you approach, then returns indifferently to his recipe. The warrior doesn't seem to recognize you*\\n\\nSimmer the preparation and cook the meat separately... Don't forget to season the sauce sparingly.","content.75.6912":"*The Iop turns towards you briefly as you approach, then returns indifferently to his recipe. You don't recognize this strapping young man*\\n\\nSimmer the preparation and cook the meat separately... Don't forget to season the sauce sparingly.","content.75.6913":"I gave you a chance to leave peacefully.\\n\\n*The tone becomes threatening*\\n\\nI hope an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} of your ilk has a good reason to bother me while I'm cooking.","content.75.6914":"I am Karn, the famous hunter-eater.\\n\\nAs for the boowolves, don't bother giving me your \"defender of wildlife\" speech. I'm simply helping the Sadida Kingdom... in my own way.\\n\\nI take a problem off the Sadidas' hands and turn it into a delectable feast. We both come out as winners in the end.","content.75.6915":"What do you take me for, some sort of unscrupulous eco-terrorist?\\n\\nThe current context may not inspire much confidence, but I do have a certain sense of honor.","content.75.6916":"I only eat enough to satisfy my hunger, but I doubt you can offer me a better alternative. So I'd advise you to stay out of my way. You might lose one of those juicy legs.","content.75.6917":"*Normally relaxed and distracted, Goultard seems to shiver at the mention of Karn's name*\\n\\nKarn... Yes, perhaps. But let's not waste too much time on the subject. I don't really have much to say about him.","content.75.6918":"Nervous? Me? You really don't know me, do you?\\n\\nLet's just say there are some things I prefer to keep to myself... If you follow me.","content.75.6919":"*The valiant warrior lets out a long sigh. He knows you won't drop the subject. But you notice that he can't seem to look you in the eye when he talks about Karn*\\n\\nYes, I suppose you could say I've met him...\\n\\nI had heard talk of a strong and powerful Iop, roaming the world in search of power.","content.75.6920":"Well... I decided to pay him a visit.\\n\\nWhen I saw him, I immediately sensed an aura of power emanating from him. He was so impressed by my divine nature that I decided to give him one of my hairs as a souvenir.","content.75.6921":"He started to get very... intrusive. I could feel his admiration gradually turning into something else.\\n\\nOver time, he became consumed with a passion so strong that he slowly descended into a kind of insatiable madness. I sensed that he was hungry, and that he coveted my powers.\\n\\nAnd so at that point, I left him.","content.75.6922":"*Goultard regains his focus*\\n\\nI suppose you're not bringing him up just so you can hear my story. What do you want from him, little one{[1*]?:}?","content.75.6923":"You won't be able to stop him until you can offer him a better option. He's quite relentless and single-minded when he's hungry...\\n\\n*Goultard runs his hand through his thick mane and pulls out a single brilliant hair*","content.75.6924":"Take that and show it to him. He'll be more willing to listen. Maybe you can find some common ground with him.\\n\\nIf you really want to earn his trust, you should bring him something exceptional to sink his teeth into...","content.75.6925":"Back to lecture me some more?\\n\\n*The Iop shakes his head*\\n\\nDon't waste your time or mine. Why not come and savor this feast with me instead?\\n\\nI never say no to a bit of company around the table.","content.75.6926":"You're really starting to get on my nerves, adventurer{[1*]?:}. Don't you see the situation you're putting yourself into? You've got a lot of nerve to try and stand in my way.\\n\\nI suppose you've got some sort of... argument you want to make?","content.75.6927":"*At a glance, Karn instinctively recognizes the item you present to him. He leans his face in dangerously close to the hair*\\n\\nAh yes, Goultard...\\n\\nHe never came back to see me, and he's stopped responding to my calls.","content.75.6928":"I knew you had something delicious hidden away. And I can sense you've got other interesting things on you as well...\\n\\nGo on then, I'm listening. What have you got to offer me?","content.75.6929":"That's very decent of you. I suppose I can reconsider my position if you bring me back something to satisfy my appetite.\\n\\nBut I should warn you: I'm not easy to please. If you think you can manage it, then by all means, go wild. I'd even be willing to invite you back to my table.","content.75.6930":"*Karn smells the fresh meats that you've brought him*\\n\\nThis is a real royal feast you're giving me here. It must have been quite a fight to get hold of such high-quality meat... although I doubt it'll be enough.\\n\\nYou'll need to be more ambitious{[1*]?:}, little{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.6931":"*A sneering grin appears on the Iop's face*\\n\\nYou really know how to kick off a conversation. Get straight to the point this time. I can already tell you want something.\\n\\nJust a minute... You're giving off quite the delicious scent. I can smell it from here. What have you brought me?","content.75.6932":"*Karn takes the bloody meat in his hands, savoring every detail of its odor and appearance*\\n\\nThat scent... I'd swear I was smelling an ultra-powerful alpha boowolf.","content.75.6933":"My mouth's already watering at the thought of cooking this little morsel. But I'll be patient and wait until sunset to treat myself.\\n\\nVery well, adventurer{[1*]?:}, you've held up your end of the bargain. I'm very satisfied with what you've given me. Now it's my turn to do something for you.\\n\\nWould you like to join me in savoring your loot?","content.75.6934":"I'm going out to hunt another beast... One even more powerful than the one you brought me.\\n\\nI've been living this life for a long time now. Hunt, eat, and grow stronger and more powerful with every meal!","content.75.6935":"The World of Twelve is filled with divine, powerful and magical creatures. Some of my favorites are the dragons created by Osamodas himself. That god is really full of pleasant surprises.\\n\\nI'm going back out to hunt some more of those appetizing beasts. Would you perhaps like to join me? It would be a nice opportunity for you to put on some muscle. No offense, but you look a bit fragile.","content.75.6936":"Well, I've got an idea... I've seen a few before, on a sort of floating island. I've tried fighting them, but without much success. I'll spare you the details of the fight...","content.75.6937":"Indeed! There's nothing left for me to do here... You took{[1*]?:} care of the problem by killing the moowolf.","content.75.6938":"All right, we'll have to take a boat. We can't use mine; it's still being repaired after my altercation with the dragons... So we'll improvise.\\n\\nI'm a very resourceful hunter. Don't worry.","content.75.6939":"*Karn gives you a sideways glance. He seems to be acting very coldly towards you*\\n\\nSo, you came{[1*]?:} back to see me.","content.75.6940":"I mean... That's really none of your business, is it?\\n\\nI can't say you're too skilled{[1*]?:} at covering my back like I asked you to.\\n\\nI'll go back to hunting alone now. It's nothing against you; it's just... I think you're too fragile to hang around with me.","content.75.6941":"Oh! An{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} who wants to give me some cooking lessons. Very interesting.\\n\\nLet's see what you can deliver.","content.75.6942":"Not bad! That gives it a slight woody touch.\\n\\nThe mushrooms pair well with the Kokomilk.","content.75.6943":"Our{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} is one smart{[1*]?:} cookie{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nIt's never wrong to add nuts to a dish. Besides, the protein will help me bulk up. Great idea!","content.75.6944":"That's an understandable choice.\\n\\nI don't usually add any salt to my cooking. I like the flavor of authenticity.","content.75.6945":"*Karn yanks your arm to stop you from adding the Funkus to the preparation*\\n\\nWhat were you trying to accomplish doing that?! You almost ruined my recipe. If you didn't want to leave here alive{[1*]?:}, all you had to do was ask.","content.75.6946":"I see... A person of taste.\\n\\nWe should do things together more often. I'll leave you my apron!","content.75.6947":"Not bad... You have high-end tastes.\\n\\nToo bad wealth doesn't guarantee quality, although it's not a bad choice.","content.75.6948":"You had me fooled. I genuinely thought you'd switched sides.","content.75.6949":"Yes... and I found it very funny. Why put on that whole charade?","content.75.6950":"I see! First you maintain a good relationship with him. Then you avoid bloodshed by helping little Mishell in distress.\\n\\nThat's very clever of you. ","content.75.6951":"*The Osamodas girl laughs warmly*\\n\\nYou took me literally. You're a fast learner.","content.75.6952":"I'd already been following your investigation from afar...\\n\\nMy dragon friends will go stay elsewhere, in a secure location. Karn had been eyeing them for a while. He was already beaten by Thalos-Kyarrelmne, but that wicked hunter has more tricks up his sleeve.\\n\\nGood thing you didn't let him kill my friend.","content.75.6953":"You know, you did a lot more than I expected by fixing the situation with the Sadida Kingdom, earning Karn's trust so he would reveal his next hunts, and neutralizing him before he could harm my friend.\\n\\nThanks a lot for your help.","content.75.6954":"I can be grateful sometimes. You earned it.\\n\\nAt first, I thought I was dealing with an{[1*]?e:} inept, occasionally crazy adventurer{[1*]?:}. In the end, you were able to alter my friends' fate. You proved to be useful{[1*]?:} after all!","content.75.6955":"There are creatures in this world that must be protected. We simply cannot afford to lose them.\\n\\nI'd like to honor you by revealing one of my biggest secrets, if that's all right!","content.75.6956":"*The hunter turns to you and sizes you up, her hand on her rifle. She seems ready to draw it at the slightest wrong word from you*\\n\\n*Despite everything, you feel that sincere dialogue is possible among skilled warriors*","content.75.6957":"Can't you tell?\\n\\n*Otomai's aging disciple shakes her head disdainfully*\\n\\nI'm one of Otomai's disciples, and I help the Guild of Hunters. I collect samples from local animal species to study them.","content.75.6958":"Yes, quite a while. I came here at the same time as a boat carrying an expedition of adventurers.\\n\\nThe island was still lost in the fog.","content.75.6959":"Sadly, landing on an invisible island isn't easy... Our ship was wrecked on the rocks.","content.75.6960":"*You notice that the woman is gradually opening up to you, although she remains somewhat tense*\\n\\nAccording to legend, the island appeared once every... century, thereabout. It briefly appeared on the horizon and then disappeared into a thick cloud of fog.\\n\\nMany expeditions tried to approach the island, but none came back. I soon realized why...\\n\\n*Khida crosses her arms, seemingly recalling the tragic moment when she reached the Misty Isle*","content.75.6961":"Actually, the island became visible as soon as we got close enough. We ended up sailing straight toward the reefs. You can only imagine our surprise.\\n\\n*She moves a lock of hair out of her face, looking worried*\\n\\nThe next day, I woke up on the shore. I never saw anyone again...","content.75.6962":"*Khida takes the journal and reads a few pages at random*\\n\\nHow about that... I knew the adventurer who wrote these pages. Felix...","content.75.6963":"Yes. We already had a few adventures together.\\n\\nWe were actually on the same ship when we came here. He met a tragic end, just like his friends...","content.75.6964":"I knew Felix well. He was fearless.\\n\\n*A slight smirk appears on Khida's lips*\\n\\nHe set up a little guild with Sylvenor. They were both cofounders.","content.75.6965":"She was a disciple of Cra. I think they had a little something going on.\\n\\nAnyway, everything was going well for them. They recruited a few members to their guild, overcame a few dangers, and brought back some loot...\\n\\nBut alas, the World of Twelve can be a cruel place.","content.75.6966":"No, there's no need. It's not as if I knew them that well.","content.75.6967":"I'm sure Felix would have wanted this journal to end up in the bag of an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} of your ilk... Someone who can uncover the real secrets of this island.\\n\\n*The disciple smiles sadly at you. It's as if something is awakening within her... Some kind of fulfillment. Revealing information about her expedition might just have helped her, in a way*","content.75.6968":"*You tell the story of your journey to the Misty Isle. The monsters you faced, the energy batteries... You explain that deep within the island lies an ancient laboratory full of secrets. You don't leave out the story of Crocatzin and Bulak or that of your Ebony Dofus*\\n\\n*Khida stays silent and listens to you with a weary look. She occasionally drinks some cold tea from her flask*\\n\\n*She doesn't really look you in the eye when you talk to her... The disciple prefers to look in every direction, as if to remain attentive to her surroundings*","content.75.6969":"I see.\\n\\n*The woman looks you in the eyes, seeming indifferent*\\n\\nThank you for telling me.","content.75.6970":"It was a bit too complex of a story for me. I'm not sure I understand everything about the Crocodyls' stories.\\n\\nDespite everything, I'm glad you were able to avenge my expedition. But hey... That won't bring them back.","content.75.6971":"No, adventurer{[1*]?:}. There's nothing else you can do. Just...\\n\\n*The woman places one hand on her hip, looking stern*\\n\\nMake sure you keep a little flame of their spirit lit in your heart, wherever you may go. Remember Felix, Sylvenor... and the mysterious creators of the island. The ones who, in their quest for creation and learning, caused so many tragedies over the years.","content.75.6972":"*The disciple rolls her eyes, shaking her head in a way that is both annoyed and amused*\\n\\nWhat a young woman. Make sure you're on the right side of her lance. She's the greatest warrior I know by far. And I've met many great ones, you included...","content.75.6973":"Listen, adventurer{[1*]?:}. That girl has a special power. Back when I knew her in Otomai's Disciples, I saw her in action... Trust me, you really don't want to cross her.\\n\\n*You think about this slightly eccentric young girl. Could she actually be hiding great power? You take a second to imagine her taking down Ogrest, Rushu, and Goultard*","content.75.6974":"Oh, yes... I've lost count of how many times I've saved their lives. Those idiots rush straight into the greatest dangers on the island without looking anywhere besides their darn notebooks.\\n\\nLuckily, you and the Ouginak came to take over. I was beginning to get tired of hunting monsters for them.","content.75.6975":"She's a good fighter and quickly grasps the ins and outs of any situation, unlike the other four. Anyway...\\n\\nI ended up losing sight of one of them among the Bworkettes, the red one there. I don't know what's become of him.","content.75.6976":"A young brunette eventually arrived, not long after you did. We discussed the situation. At least she's got a good head on her shoulders...\\n\\nIf only she could help them a bit.","content.75.6977":"Are you talking about Karn? Yes, I know him a bit. He's been around for a long time. He did much searching for the Misty Isle in the past, thinking it had some quality meat for him to eat.","content.75.6978":"No. He's hard to miss... He's got a large underwater pet and a spine-chilling laugh.\\n\\nIf you want my opinion, it won't be long before he shows up on this island, now that it's appeared.","content.75.6979":"He's an excellent hunter... We could do business together. I know more than one member of the Guild of Hunters who's used his services.","content.75.6992":"Well, I wouldn't say no to a makoffee...","content.75.6993":"*You sit down away from the others with Arlemia. The Grambos' cave is warm and bright, and the tasty smell of grilled sausage and makoffee fills your nostrils. With a cup of hot makoffee in her hands, the young archaosologist leans against the wall, her dull eyes scanning the scene*\\n\\nThis place is quite different from the Void Spiral. The last time we saw each other...","content.75.6994":"*You remember the desolate, empty, devastated area. A vision of the past and the future. The ultimate fate of all living beings, everything we build, and everything we leave behind. Nothing really lasts forever*\\n\\n*Infinite desolation. Eternal inertia*\\n\\n*No thought, no potential. Game over*\\n\\nI wanted to escape the World of Twelve, but all I found were sad rocks and dark clouds.","content.75.6995":"I think... I believe it's so I can make a fresh start.","content.75.6996":"I've always felt like I wasn't from here. I still feel the need to leave...","content.75.6997":"My head is filled with these strange memories.\\n\\nI have visions of a peaceful world. I'm in a happy home. Twelvians and Shushus live in harmony in my village.","content.75.6998":"Now I know I have roots in the World of Twelve.\\n\\nThat's where I spent my childhood, even if it was... well, what it was.","content.75.6999":"Precisely.\\n\\n*Arlemia takes a sip of makoffee, then looks at you*\\n\\nBut anyway, I've kind of hit a dead end. The Shustuft Crust is a dangerous place. I can't traverse it alone. I was lucky enough to explore the Void Spiral... I bumped into you pretty quickly.","content.75.7000":"Actually... I'm a strong believer in fate. And you?","content.75.7001":"*The young woman nods. A surreptitious smile flashes across her face*\\n\\nI guess for an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} as distinguished as you, there's not a doubt in your mind.","content.75.7002":"*The young woman considers your answer before moving closer to you*\\n\\nWell, that surprises me. But I find it interesting.\\n\\nI saw you as a{[1*]?:} distinguished adventurer{[1*]?:} who thinks that everything is already written. In the end, you are also embarking on a path full of uncertainty.","content.75.7003":"*The young woman rubs her nose a bit. She replies... neutrally*\\n\\nI see.","content.75.7004":"If only you could see these memories, like I do... Moments so clear, so precise...\\n\\nI feel like I'm on a path that's already been laid out. I want to reach them, and I know that I will. Besides... something put you on my path.","content.75.7005":"I think people are first and foremost paths, roads. We inevitably cross paths and walk part of the way together.\\n\\nMy view of fate isn't so much a great book in which everything is already written, but rather one of vectors... We each have our own directions.","content.75.7006":"Yes, so we can separate more easily later. I think that's what we'd all like: to get closer, to be on the same wavelength for a while, and then to slowly drift apart.","content.75.7007":"*The archaosologist remains stony-faced, now accustomed to your being involved{[1*]?:} in her family matters*\\n\\nI don't know. I think that if we both change enough, we might get closer more quickly. But that means making choices about our respective paths.","content.75.7008":"Getting closer...\\n\\n*Arlemia takes another sip from her cup, but longer than the previous ones*\\n\\nIt only seemed natural to come here. I felt drawn to something here... And I can feel this thing is very close by.","content.75.7009":"*Arlemia looks at you as if you have the answer to her question. \"Something\" drew her to this island... You wonder what it could be*","content.75.7010":"*The young woman shakes her head, clearly unmoved by your suggestion*\\n\\n*Arlemia looks at you as if you have the answer to her question. \"Something\" drew her to this island... You wonder what it could be*","content.75.7011":"*The archaosologist's eyes darken when she sees the ashen Dofus*\\n\\nYes... I can feel something calling out to me. In the fathomless depths...","content.75.7012":"I can feel it. This item... It's as if it's always been in a corner of my mind somewhere. I'm not even... surprised to see it. It's an odd sensation.\\n\\n*The archaosologist pulls herself together and regains some sense of clarity*\\n\\nSorry, I was lost in thought.","content.75.7013":"I get the feeling there's something essential you need to do with this Dofus.","content.75.7014":"Yes, but... You don't understand.\\n\\nThis Dofus is a paradox. You need it as much as it needs you. You must find a way to get closer so that you can make your way forward together.\\n\\n*The archaosologist smiles, her cup of makoffee still in her hand*\\n\\nRemember the vectors.","content.75.7015":"Everyone follows their own path. This Dofus is no exception. You must take a step toward it... I'm quite sure of it.","content.75.7016":"I think so, yes. The darkness is a place where everything merges, distances become more tenuous, and barriers become more blurred.\\n\\nI suggest you try isolating yourself in a dark place marked by despair.","content.75.7017":"Well... Let's take stock.\\n\\n*You slightly regret bringing the young archaosologist along on this adventure, especially since you just wanted to have a nice chat with her. But it seems she has a lead that could help you unlock its potential. It's a breakthrough that you can't afford to turn down*","content.75.7018":"Well... I know it must be confusing for you, but I don't really know how else to explain it.\\n\\nWe should talk about it more after defeating Nox. The plan needs to be executed quickly, after all.\\n\\n*You slightly regret bringing the young archaosologist here, especially since you just wanted to have a nice chat with her. You thank her for the chat and the makoffee*","content.75.7019":"When I came back from the Void Spiral, I studied the different forms of darkness. I read terrifying things... and I came across writings that were as dark as what they described.","content.75.7020":"When we were in that other dimension, there was the energy of nothingness. It's a rather hard concept to explain...\\n\\nI don't think you can use it to get closer to the Ebony Dofus.","content.75.7021":"I recommend that you look for a dark place where gruesome events took place. Given the island's history, I don't think you'll have much trouble coming up with a few ideas.\\n\\n*The young woman stands up*\\n\\nWe've got time... and I've had my makoffee. I'll go with you!","content.75.7022":"*The archaosologist has already taken a few steps away from you. She turns sideways, waiting for you. It looks like you'll have to do some more archaosology... But perhaps the reward will be worth it*","content.75.7023":"By boat, of course. There are a few merchants who pass by the Misty Isle. I suspect they've been doing business with a few Grambos... After all, the raw materials for their machines don't come free.","content.75.7024":"I came because I sensed something special about this island. Some kind of... calling.","content.75.7025":"When I arrived, I soon came across Khida. She's a warrior who protected me from the island's dangers and guided me to the other archaosologists.\\n\\nI think I found them when they moved into the Grambos' HQ.","content.75.7026":"That goes without saying.\\n\\n*The woman shoots you a teasing smirk*\\n\\nI'll try to be more careful next time. I can't just rely on you forever.","content.75.7027":"As you might expect, he's in his tunnel... He's trying to uncover the island's mysteries.","content.75.7028":"Hey... I can hear you, you know.","content.75.7029":"Mm-hmm. Let's stop talking about that. I don't want to create a bad atmosphere at HQ because of my problems with my dad, however legitimate they might be.\\n\\nEspecially since he hasn't tried to contact me in years.\\n\\n*The coldest of the archaosologists crosses her arms, her eyebrows furrowed. It looks like she'll struggle to forgive her father for not putting enough effort into their relationship. Meanwhile, Milo attentively turns back to his book. You hear him mumbling complex theories as if to suggest that he wasn't paying attention to his daughter's cutting remarks*","content.75.7030":"Oh yes, I forgot to give you one.\\n\\n*Arlemia comes extremely close to you and reaches into your bag. You take a step back, surprised{[1*]?:} by how close she suddenly is. She forcefully puts something inside and then pulls her hand out, still remaining fairly close*","content.75.7031":"I put a blocker in your bag. With that, it will look to the Nox machines as if you're shrouded in darkness, as long as you remain far enough away. I'd say it works up to at least a few feet away. It'll let...\\n\\n*The archaosologist stares at you and frowns*\\n\\nYou okay?","content.75.7032":"I put a blocker in your bag. With that, it will look to the Nox machines as if you're shrouded in darkness, as long as you remain far enough away. I'd say it works up to at least a few feet away. It'll let you go unnoticed on the island. It works pretty well for one person.","content.75.7033":"With a sophisticated magnifying glass system, I think.\\n\\n*You think about the large magnifying glasses Meccanox was working on... They reminded you of the observatory in the Xelorium*","content.75.7034":"That's the whole point. Right, you can go back to saving the world now.","content.75.7035":"*Arlemia puts her hands on her hips with her mouth slightly open*\\n\\nI don't really know how to react.","content.75.7036":"Look, uh...","content.75.7037":"Uh... no.","content.75.7038":"Welcome to my timeless theater, where scenes of life zoom by... Reliving my tragic demise keeps me focused on my objective.\\n\\n*The Xelor looks down, his voice turning melancholy*\\n\\nIt's kind of like turning back time.","content.75.7039":"Time is a mystical concept that most Twelvians are unfamiliar with. Even we Xelors don't fully understand time.\\n\\nEvery tick just leads to another tock. Every tock is inevitably followed by a tick.\\n\\nBehind this simplicity lies a brutal, relentless truth. A constantly growing pain. After all, every second takes us a little further from our perfect world.","content.75.7040":"*The Xelor's tone becomes a bit more threatening*\\n\\nI did warn{[1*]?:} you, adventurer{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nI wanted you to leave this island while there was still time. I don't like unnecessary sacrifices.","content.75.7041":"*Nox sighs wearily*\\n\\nNo matter... You'll just be another cog in my big machine.\\n\\nYou seem to have a lot of Wakfu for a{[1*]?:} mere adventurer{[1*]?:}... Know that it will greatly feed the cube.","content.75.7042":"Stop... Stop looking at me like that! I don't need your pity!","content.75.7043":"You're just an obstacle in my way. I'll show you what happens to the unfortunate people who get in the way of my machinery!","content.75.7044":"*Your allies have assembled at HQ. You give one last briefing on the phases of the plan. The mood is solemn*\\n\\n*With the plan laid out, a silence falls over HQ. You sense great apprehension among everyone in the room. It's clear that you must rally your troops with your exceptional charisma... But how will you go about it?*","content.75.7045":"I have to say, you're a damn{[1*]?:} good{[1*]?:} warrior{[1*]?:}... You've gotten{[1*]?:} so strong{[1*]?:} after all this time.","content.75.7046":"That's nothing. Zulnara and Timo are way more confident than I am. Honestly, it was kind of presumptuous of me to even join them... But still, if I helped them, that's great.\\n\\nI was able to get some gear along the way, so it's all good.","content.75.7047":"Gosh, you're rarin' to go, [#name]! Such fancy footwork!\\n\\n*The Bwork chief flashes a big grin before elbowing you hard in the chest*\\n\\nAlraune and I have crossed swords with the clockmaker, and he was ridiculously tough, even for us. So, nice work. You've earned eternal glory!","content.75.7048":"Come on, don't pretend to be a weakling now!\\n\\nYou managed to wield Alraune, after all. That's proof enough that you're stronger than a Crackler's toe.","content.75.7049":"*You still have a pretty hard time trusting Shushus. It wasn't long ago that Bulak had you wrapped{[1*]?:} around his little finger - not to mention Sthulhu. Your wounds of betrayal are still fresh. Then again, Alraune did save{[1*]?:} you there... You don't know where you stand on this*\\n\\n*The demon finally breaks the silence*\\n\\nI'll admit that you're skilled{[1*]?:}, wielding that Shushu sword...","content.75.7050":"Naturally. What did you expect?\\n\\n*The Shushu looks at you knowingly. Will you blindly trust all Shushus from now on? No. But you should base your decision on the facts. The fact is, you only managed to defeat Nox with the Shushu's help*\\n\\nAdmit it, you enjoyed facing me, right? You'd like to cross swords again, wouldn't ya?\\n\\n*... Even so, that doesn't mean you have to be friends*","content.75.7051":"Well... We suffered losses against the machines, but overall, most of our allies are doing well. The plan went smoothly, and we quickly gained the upper hand.","content.75.7052":"When Zulnara, Timo, and I saw that we were gaining the upper hand against the machines, we decided it was better to come and help you with the clockmaker.\\n\\nAnd the rest you already know.","content.75.7053":"You can say that again. You looked completely worn out... It seems you passed{[1*]?:} out after delivering the final blow with your sword.","content.75.7054":"He teleported us to the beach and took off with all his machines. His clock is still there, but the Bworks have all returned... And they didn't find anything inside.\\n\\nI doubt we'll see him again anytime soon.","content.75.7055":"... Voyager{[1*]?:}.","content.75.7056":"The impassive Xelor's eyes scan the horizon*","content.75.7057":"Yes and no.\\n\\nWhat I found in the heart of the island is... interesting. My research will help me achieve the next stage of my plan. ","content.75.7058":"The cube called me here. I thought there would be enough Wakfu to fully sustain it, but the Wakfu on this island is unusual...\\n\\nIts resonance is more complex, as if the energy were... frozen.","content.75.7059":"*The mad Xelor ignores your question*\\n\\nThat's strange. I thought the cube would have a more important reason for urging me to come here.\\n\\nWhatever.\\n\\nI got my hands on some useful research, anyway.","content.75.7060":"I'm leaving now. I have to find some things...\\n\\nIf I had to eliminate you, it would cost me too much Wakfu. And besides, this island is already doomed.\\n\\nIt's smarter for my plan if I leave today.","content.75.7061":"You're quite resourceful, Voyager{[1*]?:}. I didn't expect you to know so much about the fate of this island.","content.75.7062":"No matter. You won't be able to get in my way anymore.\\n\\nDon't try following me... You and I don't have the time to interfere with each other's plans.","content.75.7063":"*The Xelor's face is expressionless, but his voice breaks slightly. Despite the horrors he is capable of, this person still touches you*\\n\\nThey don't know how lucky they are. They're oblivious to the infinite joy surrounding them. As if in a dream.","content.75.7064":"Sadly so, Voyager{[1*]?:}. It is too late. Far too late.\\n\\nHad we met{[1*]?:} sooner, perhaps then...","content.75.7065":"You've been a tough opponent, Voyager{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nI hope we don't see each other again. I would hate to wipe out the existence of a{[1*]?:} prisoner{[1*]?:} of time such{[1*]?:} as you.","content.75.7066":"I wonder what makes you say that...","content.75.7067":"*The Xelor laughs maniacally*\\n\\nYou say having too much confidence will be the end of me... But your hunches will be the end of you, Voyager{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nRemember, you're an anomaly. One day or another, the World of Twelve will correct it.","content.75.7068":"*The Xelor disappears as soon as his warning is given. The area is shrouded in silence. The night, peaceful and quiet, envelops you in a terrifying premonition. You try to remain calm and focus on the main thing: that the clockmaker is gone for good this time*\\n\\n*Milo and Arlemia approach you, visibly upset*","content.75.7069":"Yes, indeed. We were just discussing...\\n\\nHey, you okay? You look like you've seen a ghost.","content.75.7070":"What? Oh no...\\n\\nArlemia, run and take cover!","content.75.7071":"*The two archaosologists are obviously in shock*\\n\\nHow can you be so sure{[1*]?:}?","content.75.7072":"I see.\\n\\nWe should go after him and stop him from doing harm once and for all!","content.75.7073":"You're proposing that we forget him? He's very dangerous... Just think how much harm he could do to the World of Twelve!","content.75.7074":"I'm positive there's a way. If we archaosologists get to work on it... We're bound to solve the problem in no time!","content.75.7075":"You're the one who seems calm. You were all about his destruction before the battle... What changed?","content.75.7076":"Come on, we're already deeply involved in this case. Tell us what you found in the clock.","content.75.7077":"It's... It's awful! The implications are terrifying! We have to assemble the team right away... And...","content.75.7078":"What do you mean?","content.75.7079":"*The father and his daughter are wary of your statements. As you suspected, it's going to be hard to explain to them that you have an advanced understanding of time travel*\\n\\nI don't really get it. He's only trying to go back a few minutes in time?","content.75.7080":"Yeah...\\n\\n*You can tell from Arlemia's expression that she isn't entirely convinced by what you're saying*\\n\\n*You consider that if Nox's plan was going to change the world too much anyway, Pandora would've taken care of it a long time ago*","content.75.7081":"If that's true, why'd you go to town on the clockmaker?\\n\\n*Amelia, who has apparently been listening to you, jumps out from behind a bush to question you*","content.75.7082":"I see. You've gotten{[1*]?:} smarter{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nYou managed to come up with a new plan within a few minutes in the clock. Not bad.","content.75.7083":"Well. Looks like it's all over, then.","content.75.7084":"*You've won another great battle in your eternal struggle to preserve the World of Twelve, and a Dofus is added to your collection. Nevertheless, a number of questions remain unanswered...*\\n\\n*Where did the clockmaker come from, and what exactly is he trying to do? What is the mysterious cube he used?*\\n\\n*He called{[1*]?:} you an \"anomaly\"... What did he mean by that?*\\n\\n*On top of that, something odd keeps running through your head. You can't say what, but you're missing something*","content.75.7085":"*The young woman eyes you silently*\\n\\nSo, do you feel anything here?","content.75.7086":"I see.\\n\\n*The woman scans the eerie temple for a moment before going on*\\n\\nThis is where the Dofus came from. The area might not produce the expected resonance.\\n\\nSee any other areas of distress around here?","content.75.7087":"Seems like this is the jail that Timo was held in.\\n\\nDo the residual emotions in this place bring anything out in the Dofus?","content.75.7088":"Maybe this place isn't negatively charged enough. Let's move on.","content.75.7089":"This place is repulsive... I don't want to stay here long. Let me know right away if the Dofus reacts.","content.75.7090":"Are you kidding?\\n\\n*Arlemia frowns, clearly stunned by the ramifications of your confession*\\n\\nWell, let's be going.","content.75.7091":"*As soon as you enter the laboratory, darkness starts radiating from your Dofus. You hold it up in the middle of the room*\\n\\nFinally a proper reaction. My hunch was right. Even after all these years, a great despair is trapped in this place...","content.75.7092":"*Despite the flood of negative emotions contained in the laboratory, the Ebony Dofus stops reacting. It seems like a few glimmers of hope were still in the scholar's mind when he came here. Perhaps he could've even been saved*\\n\\nA brick wall, then.","content.75.7093":"Don't give up just yet. There's one place we haven't visited yet.\\n\\nNox's clock is still here, you know. We should take a look inside. Who knows? Maybe a Grambo had a crisis in there...","content.75.7094":"*You have no idea how you ended{[1*]?:} up in this strange pit of darkness*\\n\\n*You sense an odd fluctuation. A disembodied voice speaks to you in your mind*\\n\\nSurrender to the darkness... for eternity.","content.75.7095":"*You fight to escape the clutches of this fathomless abyss, but there seems to be no use. The darkness is everywhere. That's right; you remember now. Nothing exists anymore*\\n\\n*You fall to the ground*\\n\\n*When you hit the ground, you feel something break*\\n\\n*Everything around you stops forever*","content.75.7096":"*Time, space, reason, heart*\\n*Time, space, unison, fear*\\n*Time, space, separation, lethargy*\\n\\nYour mind is unraveling, as you struggle to preserve a modicum of intelligence... But your thoughts are changing*\\n\\n*You forget your name. You forget your life. You forget your age*\\n\\n*You forget the things you never wanted to forget. Your purpose... Your reason for living... Your friends... Your loved ones... Your quests... Your home... Everything*","content.75.7097":"Be one with the silence.","content.75.7098":"Be one with the shadows.","content.75.7099":"Be one... with the ebony.","content.75.7100":"Hey, will you be okay?","content.75.7101":"Wake up, adventurer{[1*]?:}.","content.75.7102":"Come on, get up!","content.75.7103":"*You struggle to get back on your feet... And you wake up. Your head is spinning. Apart from that, you're actually thinking clearly... It seems you haven't forgotten who you are*\\n\\nI see you've come to your senses...","content.75.7104":"You're a prisoner{[1*]?:} of the Ebony Dofus's power, and that Dofus was created from the loss of our people.\\n\\nA few fragments of my mind were absorbed by the Dofus when I died... and when it appeared. Because of this, I can protect you from the darkness trying to engulf you.","content.75.7105":"Yes, you're right. The Dofus has been out of control since it was used to destroy Crocobur... But an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} of your caliber should be able to stabilize it.","content.75.7106":"This island is a tangled web. Each territory has its own energy...","content.75.7107":"All the Wakfu found on the Misty Isle is unusual. By balancing things with a good amount of Stasis, you should be able to rebalance the Ebony Dofus.","content.75.7108":"Adventurer{[1*]?:}, listen when I talk to you. This is serious.","content.75.7109":"Thanks to the Ebony Dofus, the toughest enemies you've fought on the island are back. These are ordinary ghosts, though extremely realistic. Remember to fight them at a certain amount of Stasis...\\n\\n*You internally commend the effort to set up this side quest, which is doing its best to justify redoing the Misty Isle dungeons at Stasis 3*","content.75.7110":"Once that's done, you should attack the greatest source of despair ever to walk on the Misty Isle: Nox.","content.75.7111":"Yes, I feel the darkness is clearing too.","content.75.7112":"It looks like the Dofus is on course to connect with you.\\n\\nI guess there's nothing left for me to do here. The presence that called me has vanished...","content.75.7113":"Bah. We've just been butting heads since I got here. I think we're still too distant.\\n\\nMaybe one day.","content.75.7115":"Welcome to Astrub, young adventurer{[1*]?:}!\\n\\n*The old woman looks at you fondly*","content.75.7116":"*Mammy Pal nods, lost in thought for a few seconds*\\n\\nIn that case, can you take this Haven Bag to my friend Goultard? He is outside the city.\\n\\nI would go there myself, but... My poor legs... And my old back...","content.75.7117":"*The old woman hands you a bag*\\n\\nThank you. That's very kind.\\n\\nI have a feeling you are going to accomplish great things, young {[1*]?lady:man}...","content.75.7118":"My friend is south of here. He's a big redhead. He's hard to miss... Goultard is always fighting with his apprentice!","content.75.7119":"Hello, little{[1*]?:} one! All well and good? I haven't seen you{[1*]?:} before, I don't think...\\n\\n*The proud warrior looks at you with a puzzled look before bursting out laughing*\\n\\nYou look like you've got some potential in you, for a{[1*]?:} simple incarnate{[1*]?:}! You want to train with us?","content.75.7120":"*You hand Goultard the Haven Bag that Mammy Pal gave you*\\n\\nThat old thing? What do you want me to do with that?","content.75.7121":"Mammy is never going to leave me in peace! I already told her I have no need for this Haven Bag...\\n\\nYou know what? You can keep it. You may still find it useful for organizing your things.","content.75.7122":"Who is {[1*]?she:he}?\\n\\n*Goultard's young disciple looks at you nonchalantly. At least he's not lacking in bravery*\\n\\nYou! Do you know how to fight? You want to train with us?","content.75.7123":"It takes time to recover from reincarnation. That being said, I can see you have a lot of potential!","content.75.7124":"*The legendary warrior thinks for a moment*\\n\\nNow that I think about it, the Bow Meows are wreaking havoc around here. Both of you, go clean Grandmeow's house for me! The poor lady has been unable to get back into her house for days now.","content.75.7125":"Master Goultard, that's a terrible mission!","content.75.7126":"Daldal, an adventurer's missions are not always epic. The main thing is to help those in need.\\n\\nAnd then, who knows? Maybe something surprising will happen!","content.75.7127":"Now if you want to learn how to train and ride your dragoturkey, meet me in the paddock.","content.75.7128":"All right, off you go to Grandmeow's house! You've got lots of bow meows to hunt!","content.75.7129":"Hahaha! Come on, Daldal, quit pouting!","content.75.7130":"It's... It's not fair, Master Goultard!\\n\\nYou didn't leave any Nekark for me! Not even one tentacule!","content.75.7131":"It's a TENTACLE, you Iop head!\\n\\nBut seriously...\\n\\nDecent work, you two! Thanks to you, the Fishermen's Hamlet will finally be a nice, quiet place again.","content.75.7132":"*The Gemlin reacts excitedly. It hops up on your shoulder and gives Goultard a friendly wave*\\n\\nHey, it's a Gemlin! That's an interesting creature. It should help you to focus your powers. Nice find, kid!{[1*]?:}","content.75.7133":"I'll resume personal training with Daldal.\\n\\nDon't take this the wrong way, but... Managing two full-time disciples at the same time is kind of a pain!","content.75.7134":"Aw, don't give me that look! I've cooked up a little series of missions for you.\\n\\nYou want to become the{[1*]?:} greatest{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} that the World of Twelve has ever known, don't you?","content.75.7135":"The Astrub Knight disappeared while on a mission. It seems he was trying to learn more about some mysterious cult... Something to do with Grambos...\\n\\nI think it's a mission you can probably handle. But you'll have to go into the city.\\n\\nTalk to Pappy Pal, he might know more about it.","content.75.7136":"You could also do a tour of the Astrub dungeons.\\n\\nAny self-respecting adventurer has to go through the Gobball dungeon and the Tofu dungeon at least once! You'll have a hard time getting through them alone, but if you can find some other adventurers, you'll level up really quick in there!","content.75.7137":"There are three low-level dungeons in Astrub: the Gobball dungeon, the Tofu dungeon, and the Larva dungeon.\\n\\nOh, and I've marked on your map where Otomai's Disciple is located... If you lend him a hand, you'll make super fast progress and acquire some really useful equipment!\\n\\nThat's pretty good for a start, but Astrub's also bursting with other minor quests you can take on if you feel like it!","content.75.7138":"*You recount your adventures during your time in Astrub. Goultard doesn't seem impressed, but does show a certain amount of respect*\\n\\nNot bad, kid!{[1*]?:}{[1*]?:} Sounds like my advice paid off.","content.75.7139":"In that case, I've got a little gift for you!","content.75.7140":"Even better: I've got some important advice for you! Wherever your path leads you, remember that a good warrior always uses their head.","content.75.7141":"*The legendary warrior sets a hand on your shoulder*\\n\\nI've also told my friend Melmac that you'll be needing a proper dragoturkey. You want to roam the world, battle through dungeons and complete the ultimate quest by defeating Ogrest, right? Well, that'll all go a lot faster with a mount to ride!","content.75.7142":"Now run off and see Melmac, and make me proud!\\n\\nJust don't forget your training, or Daldal will catch up to you in no time!","content.75.7143":"Well, aren't you the{[1*]?:} brash{[1*]?:} one... Kind of annoying, if you ask me! But I suppose it can't hurt to help you out. Go to the mercenary reserve over there, they'll have something for you!","content.75.7144":"*The renowned handyman sputters in frustration*\\n\\nOf all the dad-gummed, rack-a-frackin'...! It's getting more chaotic in Astrub every day. Thanks for handling them... I'll work on getting things straightened out.","content.75.7145":"Looksh like a shplendid day ahead, doezhn't it?\\n\\n*The fishercat turns to Goultard and Percedal*\\n\\nIf only thozhe damned Iopsh would turn it down a notch...","content.75.7146":"This used to be such a peaceful village. Nice and quiet, you know?\\n\\nBut recently, all these bow meows have started showing up.\\n\\nIf you ask me, it's because of those Iops stirring up trouble over there.","content.75.7147":"It's a rough time for sailing right now. I've seen several Nekarks prowling around nearby.\\n\\nThe seas of the World of Twelve have never been so hard to navigate.","content.75.7148":"Perfect timing, my friend.{[1*]?:} Some rats have settled in at the sawmill nearby...","content.75.7149":"They're disturbing the fresh air in the forest. If you're up for dealing with them, I'd really appreciate it!","content.75.7150":"Already? Wow, that was fast! Thank you.\\n\\nOur lumberjacks will be able to resume their partnership with Wikan Dewitt!","content.75.7151":"Members of Ogrest's Cult are wreaking havoc in my cemetery...\\n\\nWhatever they're doing, it seems they're using Chaos Plants to do it.","content.75.7152":"I don't know, kid{[1*]?:}. Ogrest has caused so many calamities...\\n\\n*The old man is overcome with a brief coughing fit*\\n\\nMany of the tombstones in this cemetery are in memory of mortals who lost their lives because of that accursed ogre.","content.75.7153":"Thank you, adventurer.{[1*]?:} May the residents of this cemetery continue to rest in peace.\\n\\n*Père Lachaise coughs violently*\\n\\nOof... I have a feeling I'll be joining them before long...","content.75.7154":"I'll have you know that these sewers used to be the height of cleanliness!\\n\\nBut that was before those larvae came in and messed everything up...","content.75.7155":"Besides the dungeon to the west of the sewers, there's also a larva nest to the north. Just an endless stream of larvae coming out of there. There must be a Nanny Larva inside...\\n\\nIf only a brave adventurer could get rid of them for us!","content.75.7156":"It's true, the air is more breathable now... And the ground's not as sticky.\\n\\nThanks, adventurer!{[1*]?:}","content.75.7157":"The World of Twelve must not fall!","content.75.7158":"But haven't you noticed?\\n\\nAn evil darkness is spreading throughout the World of Twelve. Nobody knows where this evil energy comes from or how to stop it.","content.75.7159":"It's a sort of dark mist. It corrupts earth, plants, and creatures...\\n\\nIn its wake, the very air becomes saturated with evil.","content.75.7160":"A number of monsters have been possessed by this evil energy and are wreaking havoc and destruction.\\n\\nOgrest, the Black Crow, and Vampyro - who were already formidable enough - have lost all reason, and now they're attacking anything that moves.\\n\\nIf this darkness keeps on spreading, then all life will become corrupted.","content.75.7161":"That's the whole point. We founded the Neo Raid to rise up against this disaster!","content.75.7162":"Adventurers, guards, farmers, and restaurateurs alike have come from all over the World of Twelve to unite under a single banner of hope and reconquest.\\n\\nFighting darkness with light, the Neo Raid advances day by day to contain the spread of the darkness.","content.75.7163":"The Neo Raid is still looking for adventurers to swell their ranks.\\n\\nPerhaps you'll be their next recruit? Go talk to Neo Jonk about it! Take the canoon beside me to reach the Neo HQ.","content.75.7164":"The Neo Canoon just next to me will take you to the Neo HQ.\\n\\nThe Neo Vessel is always moving around, so this is the only way to get to it.","content.75.7166":"You need to go to Astrub right now. The Royal Gobball is wreaking havoc in Tainela!\\n\\n*The colossus shouts out a few more orders and then turns to you, looking serious*\\n\\nWho are you? A new recruit?","content.75.7167":"*Jonk looks at you more closely. He eventually raises an eyebrow*\\n\\nHow about that... It looks like you just incarnated, but you've got huge potential! I can sense so much Wakfu in you...\\n\\nYes... You might be the glimmer of hope the World of Twelve needs to keep it from falling.","content.75.7168":"The World of Twelve is being plagued by a powerful, evil form of corruption... Luckily, Twelvians have rallied to fight this threat.\\n\\nTogether, we form the Neo Raid.","content.75.7169":"If you've got any questions, I'll gladly answer them.","content.75.7170":"Hey, you.\\n\\nHow about a little quest?","content.75.7173":"The darkness appeared one fine day, out of nowhere. An evil energy so powerful that it broke so many minds.\\n\\nNations' governors, adventurers, heroes... None of them could stop the darkness from spreading.","content.75.7174":"Yes. More specifically, the darkness is spreading because of a ghost... The same one who's a prisoner deep within the HQ.\\n\\nIt attacked me, but it met its match! I managed to beat it, but it wasn't easy.","content.75.7175":"The specter has been held prisoner ever since our fight. I asked some monks to make sure he'd stay put.\\n\\nOne thing led to another, and everyone willing to fight the darkness rallied around me. I took command of the troops... And that's how the Neo Raid came to be.","content.75.7176":"We tried to kill it every way we could, but it's impossible. Eventually, it regenerates.\\n\\nAll we know is that it hates the light.","content.75.7177":"We're keeping the ghost prisoner here in the Neo HQ. But it's so powerful that it's taking up a large part of our strength.\\n\\nThe rest of the Neo Raid is trying to purge the darkness that has already spread across the rest of the World of Twelve.","content.75.7178":"We need reinforcements in the field.\\n\\nAdventurers, harvesters, guards, merchants... Anyone will do!","content.75.7179":"We've located the most corrupted places. There, the corruption is so dense that it's impossible to enter without immediately losing your mind.\\n\\nFirst, you'll need to perform rituals by bringing resources to the Neo Urn. Each ritual will let you enter a new dungeon to try to defeat the terrible Neo Boss!","content.75.7180":"First, if you join us, we'll give you a blessing that will help you earn more loot.\\n\\nWe'll also give you a Neo Pet, a loyal sidekick who's as formidable as it is lovable. You can evolve it during your adventure.","content.75.7181":"There are other rewards in store. They'll be yours if you show bravery by exterminating the Neo Bosses.\\n\\nEvery Neo Boss you defeat will increase the speed at which you progress. Come see me after you've defeated one, and I'll increase the experience you earn, with a little extra gift.\\n\\nFinally, feel free to pay the Neo Hunter a visit, because she'll give you daily and weekly quests with even more rewards for you to win.","content.75.7182":"Excellent! Sign this document, and you'll become a member of the Neo Raid.\\n\\n*The commander holds out a contract some 100 pages long... written in tiny letters*","content.75.7183":"*The contract consists of thousands of extremely precise and laborious clauses. Since everything is written so small, you have to make a huge effort to read it. You soon start to tire, especially as the whole Neo Raid is waiting. Nobody's ever read the contract, after all*\\n\\n*After reading the countless points of the contract for several hours, you come to the conclusion that, unfortunately, you haven't understood a word of it. It would take several more weeks of reading to properly immerse yourself in all its clauses. Sadly, time is running out*","content.75.7184":"There. Now you're a member of the Neo Raid! Welcome!","content.75.7185":"Hey, it's starting to sink in! I have no doubt you'll make a great recruit.\\n\\nHere is your Neo Pet. Go to the Neo Table to identify the different Neo Bosses you have to defeat, then come see me every time you defeat a new Neo Boss so I can give you some rewards!","content.75.7186":"The Neo Raid is rising!\\n\\nAh, there you are, [#name]. How's your quest going?","content.75.7187":"You bravely managed to defeat your first Neo Boss, [#name].\\n\\nThere's still a long way to go... But thanks to your efforts, your Neo Blessing will let you progress faster and earn more experience in combat!\\n\\nRemember that the World of Twelve must not fall!","content.75.7188":"That's already two Neo Bosses purged thanks to you!\\n\\nThanks to the special power of the Neo Raid, your experience will increase even faster from now on. But stay alert. This is only the beginning of your adventure.","content.75.7189":"So, you managed to defeat three Neo Bosses. At this rate, perhaps...\\n\\n*The giant stops mid-sentence and sizes you up with a dark expression*\\n\\nNo matter. We're counting on you, [#name]. And as usual, your experience will increase faster from now on!","content.75.7190":"That's four Neo Bosses for you now! Well done, [#name].\\n\\nAs usual, I'll make your Neo Blessing stronger. But you deserve something special this time!\\n\\nI'll evolve your Neo Pet so it'll become more powerful. With its help, your journey will be a little easier. Keep on embodying our hope!","content.75.7191":"Five Neo Bosses have been defeated... Well, I must admit that I'm starting to get impressed by your performance.\\n\\nBut it's still far from over. Don't lose focus!\\n\\nI'm going to increase the power of your Neo Blessing some more. Come back soon, [#name]!","content.75.7192":"Now that you've exterminated this sixth Neo Boss, there's no doubt you can go all the way in the quest.\\n\\nYour Neo Blessing has reached a new level too!\\n\\nYour progress is essential to saving the World of Twelve. Remember that we're all behind you.","content.75.7193":"Seven! So, you've managed to defeat more than half of the Neo Bosses.\\n\\nNow things are about to get really tough...\\n\\nThe next time you beat one, I'll make your Neo Pet stronger. In the meantime, you'll get even more experience than usual!","content.75.7194":"With this eighth Neo Boss you've slain, there's never been greater hope.\\n\\nYou truly are a{[1*]?:} skilled{[1*]?:} Neo Hero{[1*]?:}. Just like your Neo Pet! It deserves to evolve a bit, in fact.\\n\\nRight, good luck for the final sprint!","content.75.7195":"Nine... That's nine Neo Bosses destroyed.\\n\\nWell done. The World of Twelve has a lot to thank you for again. But we still need your help if we're to complete this quest.\\n\\nI don't want to put pressure on you, but time is running out! For your trouble, I'm going to increase the power of your Neo Blessing some more.","content.75.7196":"If someone had told me one day that you'd defeat 10 Neo Bosses... well, I'd have believed it, because I've always had high expectations of you!\\n\\nCongratulations! There are only three left to defeat, and I'm sure they won't be the easiest of opponents.\\n\\nYour Neo Blessing has been made stronger again. And you'll need it for the final sprint!","content.75.7197":"We should consider changing our slogan to \"The darkness is spreading, and [#name] is rising\".\\n\\nWell done, [#name]. Eleven Neo Bosses have been defeated thanks to you. I'll make your Neo Blessing stronger again!\\n\\nThe next time you defeat a Neo Boss, I'll evolve your Neo Pet into its ultimate form. You're almost there!","content.75.7198":"Twelve, like the World of Twelve!\\n\\nWe owe you a lot, [#name]. You've done more than anyone else to save the entire Krosmoz from an unprecedented threat.\\n\\nBut I know you weren't alone{[1*]?:} in your quest, and that your Neo Pet also played a decisive role. That's why I'm giving it its ultimate form. All our hope now lies with you two... You need to defeat the final Neo Boss. Time is of the essence, and with every passing minute, the barrier holding back the ghost grows weaker. Well, [#name], the whole Neo Raid is behind you!","content.75.7199":"So, it's true? You defeated all 13 Neo Bosses?\\n\\n*Jonk places a hand on your shoulder*\\n\\n[#name]... You're the{[1*]?:} greatest{[1*]?:} warrior{[1*]?:} the Neo Raid has ever known. You should be proud{[1*]?:}! As a reward, you have the infinite gratitude of the World of Twelve!","content.75.7200":"I don't know how to rid us of that damn ghost... It's getting more and more powerful by the minute.\\n\\n*Neo Jonk gives you a worried look*\\n\\nI don't know what else to tell you... But make sure you're ready. One day, it'll manage to break free, and we'll need you. You're our greatest asset.","content.75.7201":"Stop there! Access to this area is restricted.","content.75.7203":"We need you to fight this ghost once and for all.","content.75.7204":"...\\n\\n*An imposing dragon stands before you. He is made of water as pure as the Ohwymi spring and as loud as the torrents of Mount Zinit*\\n\\n*You wonder if he's going to eat you or ignore you*","content.75.7205":"Ah, there you are, [#name]! I was just waiting for an{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} to help me with an extremely important mission...\\n\\nPay no attention to Aguabrial. He won't hurt you.","content.75.7206":"I felt a disturbance in the World of Twelve.\\n\\nIt would seem an uprising has begun. A long-lost area will soon reappear...","content.75.7207":"Well...\\n\\n*Otomai thinks for a moment*\\n\\nSupposedly there are clues throughout the world to find this area. But for now, it cannot be reached. I can't say more than that for now.","content.75.7208":"I think there is a connection between this place and the Primordial Dragons.\\n\\n*Your mentor snaps his fingers*\\n\\nAnd who knows? Maybe we will find a special power there that could help us defeat Ogrest... and, in so doing, claim the six Primordial Dofus!","content.75.7209":"For now, Aguabrial seems to have lost his ability to reason. His wise and venerable mind has been reduced to a sort of primitive state... What do you say? Would you help bring him to his senses?","content.75.7210":"*Aguabrial remains silent, staring into emptiness*","content.75.7211":"If you are referring to the events preceding your clash with the Last Voyager, I doubt that has anything to do with it. All the other Primordial Dragons are in the same state.","content.75.7212":"The World of Twelve is still beset by chaos and the unexpected... But this unexpectedness leads to surprises and opportunities!\\n\\nEnvironmental quests are part of this. Try to participate in these random events, and perhaps Aguabrial will remember what was once his true nature.","content.75.7213":"Ah, [#name]. There you are. Any news?","content.75.7214":"It could be said you've done what you could, but Aguabrial doesn't appear to have come to his senses, however. I'll let you know if I receive any news.","content.75.7215":"As you wish, but you've been warned. Proceed at your own risk.","content.75.7216":"Everything is under control. Our men are on it. At least, I think they are...","content.75.7217":"It's confidential and far too dangerous.","content.75.7218":"*Neo Jonk looks down, resigned*\\n\\nThe ghost broke free. Our Neo Monks were unable to prevent it from escaping, and...","content.75.7219":"*Staring into emptiness, Neo Jonk appears to be reliving a traumatic scene*\\n\\nHe destroyed everything. I had never seen such power. Screams of panic, flames shooting here, then there... It was chaos.","content.75.7220":"Our men made a valiant effort, but in vain. In the end, the Neo HQ crashed here. Ever since, we've been trying to hold back the ghost. If we fail to stop it here, I fear grave consequences. We need you.","content.75.7221":"Rest assured{[1*]?:} that you'll be assisted{[1*]?:} by our men. You are our only hope. When darkness spreads...","content.75.7222":"*Aguabrial remains silent, staring into emptiness*","content.75.7223":"Allow me to introduce our new flagship product, straight from Bilbiza: Multijely!\\n\\n*He shows you jellies of various different colors*\\n\\nWith Multijely, you can explore every corner of the Krosmoz in search of unimaginable challenges! In some fights, your abilities will be restricted. In others, you'll fight as some of the greatest heroes of the Krosmoz!\\n\\nEach Multijely lets you open an imaginary portal. Once inside, you'll take on a fearsome opponent. And the crowd will be watching it all on our live broadcast!","content.75.7224":"*The slightly overenthusiastic Pandawa drapes an arm over your shoulder. A pungent odor assaults your nostrils as the roaring crowd chants your name*\\n\\nWelcome to the Trool Fair's ultimate attraction! Choose a boss from the list, and a portal will appear!","content.75.7225":"*The ancestral dragon looks you over calmly. You hear a whisper in your mind: Bosses have emerged from their dungeons to invade the World of Twelve... Will you take on the challenge?*","content.75.7226":"I have a message for you from Otomai. He'd like to hear what you're up to. Pay him a visit on the Celestial Island. He'd also like to talk to you about a certain specific place...","content.75.7227":"It's been several days now. I even went to the Astrub Mountains on Mammy Pal's advice, but to no avail...\\n\\nLuckily, Goultard told me he had run into you. Are your first steps in Astrub going well so far?","content.75.7228":"I'm glad your adventures are going well!\\n\\nI wanted to tell you about a place where wildlife and plant life are one and the same: the Haven Place. You can set it up to cultivate resources... and even raise all kinds of creatures there!\\n\\nYou seem to be an{[1*]?:} accomplished{[1*]?:} adventurer{[1*]?:} now... I'll give you access to it.","content.75.7229":"Great, I hope you'll like the place!\\n\\nFeel free to go check it out right away to learn all about what you can do in the Haven Place. You'll see that nature has been working to reclaim it, so it'll need to be cleared out a bit.","content.75.7230":"*You <b>notice</b> a fisherman pacing back and forth. He seems troubled by something and is muttering to himself*","content.75.7231":"*He finally notices you*\\n\\nHey! You there! Come here. Can't believe it. Come over 'ere, I said! What's that over there?\\n\\n*The fisherman points intently at his boat*","content.75.7232":"Yes! A boat! A boat fer fishin' fish. Fish! Been doin' this fer 40 year an' never seen nothin' like it... So I were just headin' out to sea this mornin', like every mornin'. I pull in the net, like always, and there's this old man in the net. An' stark naked at that!\\n\\n*His eyebrows furrow*\\n\\nAn' ya can stop lookin' at me like that all suspicious. It's true! Go see fer yourself if ya don't believe me.","content.75.7233":"No, he's not doin' well at all. How could he be doin' well? My fish ain't fresh now! With a naked guy in my net, how can I sell my fish? Who'd want to buy my catch after it's been cuddled by some briny boowolf?","content.75.7234":"*An Enutrof is sitting curled up in a corner of the hold. The fisherman seems to have had the decency to give him some clothes before leaving him alone. He raises his head upon hearing your footsteps on the creaking boards. He wears a blank look, and his lips are cracked from the salty sea*\\n\\nI... Where... Wh... What am I doing here?","content.75.7235":"Yes? No? Well, I think. I don't know. It's all a jumble. I don't really remember. I... \\n\\n*The Enutrof freezes for a few seconds, mouth half-open*\\n\\nI think I've forgotten everything. My name, where I'm from... everything. Absolutely everything! EVERYTHING!","content.75.7236":"*He runs his hand through his hair and quickly feels his body*\\n\\nNo, I don't think so. How have I managed to lose my memory? What if I never get it back? I can't stay like this. I need to go back home! Please... Help me. I'll give you anything you want, everything I have! ","content.75.7237":"*The old man begs you*\\n\\nI'd be forever grateful...","content.75.7238":"Thank you! Thank you! Whatever happens from now on, I promise to repay you a hundredfold for the help you give me!","content.75.7239":"Who do you take me for? I've mapped more seas and oceans than you've ever seen in your life. I swear by the Kralove, drawing is in my blood.\\n\\nThere's none better than me! However, why should I draw for you?","content.75.7240":"It feels good to be able to breathe again! ","content.75.7241":"Hard to say. It's still all muddled.\\n\\n*The Enutrof closes his eyes to concentrate. His eyebrows furrow, and his eyelids flutter*\\n\\nI remember feelings, shapes. I was somewhere hot, very hot!","content.75.7242":"I can't remember. It was a strange shape. A symbol or something like that.","content.75.7243":"It's a bit fuzzy. I can't quite picture it. At most, I could describe parts of it, but trying to draw it is another story...","content.75.7244":"Ha ha! You really think I'm scared of a freshwater deckhand like you? Explain the situation to me instead of making a fool of yourself.","content.75.7245":"I see. I see. This is a very unique case.\\n\\nI don't have what I need for drawing here. Come to my place when you have time. I'll see what I can do for you.","content.75.7246":"There you are at last! Did you wait for low tide to get here? I almost thought you'd never come and that you were just messing with me!","content.75.7247":"*He takes some paper, spits a bit of ink in a glass pot and turns to you*\\n\\nRight, let's start. I'm listening.","content.75.7248":"*Black Ink hands you a piece of paper with his drawing on it*\\n\\nThere, how's that for talent?!","content.75.7249":"That's the exact symbol I was picturing! I'm certain of it.","content.75.7250":"*The Enutrof concentrates, then shakes his head*\\n\\nNo, still nothing...","content.75.7251":"But isn't it obvious? Or are you saying that my drawing is so bad that you can't recognize it instantly?","content.75.7252":"It's the Hoodlums' emblem.","content.75.7253":"It's the Hoodlums' emblem...","content.75.7254":"What? You've not even heard of them? You really need everything explained, don't you?! They're a group of activists found all over the world. They fight to save the planet in their own special way. They've been targeting Bonta and its vices in recent years.\\n\\nTheir members tend to hide in the shadows before striking hard and then disappearing again. I heard they had taken over the tunnels near the capital.","content.75.7255":"I don't know if I want to continue with all this. What if the real me was actually a terrible person? I can't undo the harm I've done, but I can now live a peaceful life and do good wherever I go. ","content.75.7256":"You're right. I need to know for sure. Let's go!","content.75.7257":"I have a bad feeling about this. The pennants in this place bear the symbol we're looking for, but something's not right.","content.75.7258":"*The Old Amnesiac looks at one of the pennants*\\n\\nI feel like that's it... but not quite. I'm not getting the same feelings as I remember. The zeppelin at the end of that rope doesn't mean anything to me. Flying, moving around, breathing in fresh air... that's the opposite of the oppressive feeling I get when I look at this symbol. ","content.75.7259":"*The Old Amnesiac turns to the barrel of weapons next to him*\\n\\nWeapons! There were weapons there. I remember now! ","content.75.7260":"Not these specific ones. Weapons of all kinds. A lot of...\\n\\n*His face turns dark*\\n\\nWeapons and blood. Lots of blood.","content.75.7261":"I don't think that's my thing. But I think I witnessed it. I definitely think I was in serious trouble before losing my memory. I'm also pretty sure I wasn't alone.\\n\\nThat probably means people are in danger! ","content.75.7262":"So you're only interested{[1*]?:} in the money? People are probably suffering right now, and all you can think of is filling your pockets?","content.75.7263":"[#name]! I've had time to think about the situation.","content.75.7264":"A little bit. I think I remember someone important. ","content.75.7265":"Not really. I have a feeling of disgust when I think of this person.\\n\\n*You sense he's revolted by this memory. Could it be someone evil?*","content.75.7266":"Hey...\\n\\n*The Enutrof turns back to you with a serious look*\\n\\nWhat kind of person do you think I was? The further I go, the more scared I become of my past.","content.75.7267":"Do you think it's normal that some people are fundamentally good and others bad?","content.75.7268":"But what if that past is too difficult to accept?","content.75.7269":"You're right. I must get a grip! \\n\\n*The Old Amnesiac slaps both cheeks sharply, and his eyes light up with determination*","content.75.7270":"I can only remember his general appearance, his build, and what he wears. But I can't recall his name or face. One thing I'm certain of is that people suffered because of this person. ","content.75.7271":"Well, okay. You can use all the clothes available here and my mannequin. I'll do a sketch for you. \\n\\nTake the opportunity to do some thrifting while you're here. It would be a shame to leave empty-handed. I'll even give you a bulk discount if you take multiple items! ","content.75.7272":"*The Owl leafs through his files, searches through different piles of paper, and rummages in his drawers. He examines every wanted notice he finds*\\n\\nI don't recognize that person at all... hoo. Not among wanted people and not among the victims either. If you give me this portrait, I can create a wanted notice and share it with my colleagues.","content.75.7273":"*The Owl makes a quick copy of the wanted notice, folds it carefully in four, and then hands it to you discreetly*\\n\\nAn unscrupulous representative of the profession would tell you to show this wanted notice to those involved in questionable business practices... such as the Rogues in Sufokia. However, it would be a significant risk without any guarantee of results. Thankfully, I'm not one of those representatives. Hoo! ","content.75.7274":"What makes you say that?","content.75.7275":"We guarantee our clients' anonymity. We simply cannot afford to give out information to the first person who comes asking for it.","content.75.7276":"Our shop is the result of many long years exploring the world to find rare and unique items. None of the products you see here could possibly come from the black market! ","content.75.7277":"Even if that were so, I've got nothing to say to you. Such allegations are harmful to our business!","content.75.7278":"KABROK!!","content.75.7279":"*The antique dealer at the other end of the room turns to you*\\n\\nWHAT?","content.75.7280":"These people here want to talk to you! ","content.75.7281":"I'm coming...\\n\\n*He approaches, shuffling his slippers across the floor*\\n\\nWhat is it?","content.75.7282":"Tell them what you know, or they'll never leave us alone.","content.75.7283":"Aligias... I have actually heard of him. However, I've never done business with him directly. I heard he hunts for collector's items, but I can't tell you more than that. \\nTo be honest, I've always tried to avoid him. I've heard strange rumors about him. Antiquities aren't his only passion, and because his other passions don't align with mine, I'd rather keep my distance. \\nFor these reasons, I don't want to discuss the matter any further.","content.75.7287":"*The Old Amnesiac seems lost in thought*","content.75.7288":"I had a strange feeling coming into this room. Those creature heads, the crackling fire. It's warm, yet I have cold sweats.","content.75.7289":"Not really. My throat tightens and I have trouble breathing when looking at them.\\n\\n*The Old Amnesiac freezes briefly*\\n\\nI remember now. I was in a cave with a huge creature! Something that makes your blood run cold. I thought I was going to die. I can't really picture it very well. It... it was terrifying!","content.75.7290":"(...)","content.75.7291":"Yes.","content.75.7292":"*The Enutrof turns to the fireplace*\\n\\nWhat I'm sure about is that the cave was like a furnace. The fire from this fireplace is nothing in comparison. The heat was suffocating in there. ","content.75.7293":"*Kabrok moves toward you*\\n\\nI heard your conversation. There's a cave in Brakmar matching that description. It's full of lava waterfalls. The atmosphere is suffocating, and more importantly, it's teeming with creatures called stalagmotes. It even seems that these creatures are led by a giant stalagmote that will attack anyone who dares approach. It's so big that no one has ever managed to see the whole thing. ","content.75.7294":"Neither. As I said earlier, I'd rather not talk about that. If you have any other questions about my items, and only about my items, I'll gladly help.","content.75.7295":"If that creature is still there, I don't think we could make it out of there in one piece. It's like nothing else we've come up against before.","content.75.7296":"Okay, I'll go with you.","content.75.7300":"*The old man stands up straight, staring into space*","content.75.7301":"I'm torn. I can't tell if my memories are real anymore. Nothing makes any sense. We're running all over the world without finding anything. That creature had nothing to do with my memories. \\n\\nThe further I go, the more I grow... and the less I understand.","content.75.7302":"What others? What are you talking about?","content.75.7303":"Personally, I'd rather try and find the answers more quickly. I'd love to be a respectable person who cares about other people's fates. But deep down, it's my own situation that concerns me the most. What did I do in my life to end up like this? How much suffering did I endure? Do I really want to go through all that again? Recovering one's memory is a bit like being reborn. I'll have to relive all of my memories, both good and bad.","content.75.7304":"You're not angry with me for making you run all over the place with no results?","content.75.7305":"Oh yes, I definitely promise! ","content.75.7306":"Alright!","content.75.7307":"I forgot to tell you: This cave is much too natural. The one in my memories is... How can I put it? It's more human. More artificial. It also seemed recent, and all fitted out. ","content.75.7308":"Either on his own, or with outside support.","content.75.7309":"Do you think there are criminal masons out there? Be honest.","content.75.7310":"What kind of information are you looking for?","content.75.7311":"I'll have a look in my notebook here.\\n\\n*The guardian pulls out an enormous book with thousands of pages and drops it on the table with a dull thud*","content.75.7312":"Yes, I keep notes on all my current prisoners. \\n\\n*The guardian opens to the first page*\\n\\nSo... Not him.","content.75.7313":"Not him.","content.75.7314":"Not her.","content.75.7315":"Not him.","content.75.7316":"Not him.","content.75.7317":"Not her either.","content.75.7318":"Not him.","content.75.7319":"Him, maybe... Or maybe not.","content.75.7320":"Him? No, he died yesterday.","content.75.7321":"Not him either.","content.75.7322":"Oh yes, of course! I'm sorry! \\n\\n*He raises his hands in an apologetic gesture, allowing the notebook to fall shut*\\n\\nOh darn, now where was I? Probably around... here! \\n\\nNot him.","content.75.7323":"Not him.","content.75.7324":"Not him.","content.75.7325":"Not her either.","content.75.7326":"Not him.","content.75.7327":"Him, maybe.","content.75.7328":"Him? Oh, that's the guy who died yesterday again.","content.75.7329":"Not him either.","content.75.7330":"Him... Who is he? \\n\\n*He peers over your shoulder at a cell*\\n\\nNoooo...","content.75.7331":"Not him.","content.75.7332":"Not her.","content.75.7333":"Not her.","content.75.7334":"Not him.","content.75.7335":"And not him, either.\\n\\nNone of my prisoners fit that description.","content.75.7336":"Hmmm. There was one former prisoner who belonged to a group specializing in terraforming operations. He was caught digging tunnels to try and rob the Astrub Bank. Their group is pretty well known in the underworld. They're often hired on for illegal projects and such.","content.75.7339":"Unfortunately, no. He arrived with no identity and later died in his cell. He said he was a member of the Elite Riktus clan.","content.75.7340":"*The guardian snatches the portrait sketch from your hand*\\n\\nIs he a prisoner?","content.75.7341":"I can look in my notebook for any notes or information on the subject, if you like.","content.75.7342":"*The guardian opens his notebook back up to the first page*\\n\\nLet's continue! \\n\\nSo... Not him.","content.75.7343":"Not him.","content.75.7344":"Not her.","content.75.7345":"Not him.","content.75.7346":"Not him.","content.75.7347":"Not her either.","content.75.7348":"Not him.","content.75.7349":"Him, maybe.","content.75.7350":"Him? Nope, still dead.","content.75.7351":"Not him either.","content.75.7352":"*He stands up suddenly, letting his notebook flip shut*\\n\\nWait! I'm almost done!","content.75.7353":"No problem, I remember where I was. Just a moment.\\n\\n*He opens his notebook at a random place*\\n\\nSo... Not him.","content.75.7354":"Not him.","content.75.7355":"Not him.","content.75.7356":"Not her either.","content.75.7357":"Not him.","content.75.7358":"Him... Maybe not, actually.","content.75.7359":"Ah!","content.75.7360":"It's that guy who died yesterday again!","content.75.7361":"Not him either.","content.75.7362":"Him... Ah, that's the guy from a minute ago.","content.75.7363":"Not him.","content.75.7364":"Not her.","content.75.7365":"Not her.","content.75.7366":"Not him.","content.75.7367":"And not him, either.\\n\\nSorry, I don't have anything under that name.","content.75.7368":"Is everything okay? Anything else I can do for you?","content.75.7369":"*The Enutrof remains quiet before the dragon*","content.75.7370":"That's it, [#name]! I remember everything! It was here. It all happened in this cave. The horrors, the massacres... all of it! There's a room behind that dragon. We must get in there at all costs. I'll explain later.","content.75.7371":"Let's take him on!","content.75.7372":"What do you mean, no?","content.75.7373":"Yes.","content.75.7374":"Trust me. We'll draw him into a fight, and as soon as the opportunity arises, quickly slip into the room behind him.","content.75.7375":"Like I said, trust me! I've got my memory back, and I have an idea of how to get through it. The fact that I'm standing here now, after being on the other side before my amnesia... That proves that I've already made it through once, somehow.","content.75.7376":"I've got an additional advantage. I remember everything. I know it'll work. Just let me know when you feel ready{[1*]?:}.","content.75.7377":"Alright, ready{[1*]?:} to fight?","content.75.7378":"I'm so terribly sorry...","content.75.7379":"I know, but it was impossible.","content.75.7380":"Time was short, so I couldn't stand around explaining things to you when the dragon might have spotted us. My objective was to bring you here.","content.75.7381":"Not exactly. I was already dead before we got here. ","content.75.7382":"Yes. When I lost my memory, my soul was unable to become fully disembodied, nor to be reincarnated either. I found myself trapped, with no idea of what to do or where to go.","content.75.7383":"Yes. In spite of everything, I still thought I was perfectly alive. I was so convinced of it that my soul was indistinguishable from my real self.","content.75.7384":"About that... There's one last thing I have to tell you. \\n\\nThe person we've been looking for all this time, Aligias... is me.","content.75.7385":"No. I was the victim of my own actions. Everything I had done over the years came back to bite me. ","content.75.7386":"No! Just let me explain. ","content.75.7387":"I don't have any explanation for it. I'm well aware my actions are inexcusable. Some things simply can't be explained. I grew up with a sociopathic father... and I learned from him. It always just seemed normal to me. Some people grow up in hunter tribes and can kill their game with no emotion, while others, raised in a different setting, are incapable of it.","content.75.7388":"Wait! If my past and my story don't interest you, then at least let me tell you what happened at the end. Why that dragon is here, and why I wanted to bring you here anyway after getting my memory back.","content.75.7389":"Yes. When I died, my soul briefly interacted with the dragon's.","content.75.7390":"All the terrible things I did. All those people who died because of me, over all those years, generated vast amounts of despair. Touched by all that accumulated despair, the dragon, Ignemikhal, produced an egg... his egg, the Crimson Dofus. Its creation generated such a powerful source of energy that no one here could withstand it. We were all swept away in the blink of an eye, without really realizing anything had happened. ","content.75.7391":"I do need to go back to what I've done, though. Just for a moment, to put things in context. For years, if not my whole life, I was always hurting people. I couldn't tell you how many people suffered and died because of me. My acts alone caused boundless despair, not only in my victims, but in their families as well. It just kept building up more and more.","content.75.7392":"That despair I was talking about is what eventually led to the end of it all. The dragon you saw is the fire dragon, Ignemikhal. Dragons are highly sensitive beings. Year after year, he sensed people's distress, to the point that he started traveling around to check up on what I was doing.","content.75.7393":"I was getting to that. Once he was confronted with the problem, that was the last straw. All that accumulated despair produced an egg... his egg, the Crimson Dofus. Its creation generated such a powerful source of energy that no one here could withstand it. We were all swept away in the blink of an eye, without really realizing anything had happened. ","content.75.7394":"My goal wasn't really to show you all that. I just needed you to see it so you'd believe me. ","content.75.7395":"Not at all! As I said, my soul was able to communicate with Ignemikhal's, and I felt all the despair I had caused. I was able to experience all the suffering I had inflicted on people.","content.75.7396":"I can never erase what's been done. But someone like you might be able to counterbalance my existence. I want you to use the power of the Dofus created by my atrocities to help people in need. You're a good person. You're the exact opposite of me.","content.75.7397":"Thank you. I'll let you carry the weight of their lives, the power of their souls, and the bright sparkle of their dreams. Use it wisely! ","content.75.7398":"Adventurer{[1*]?:}! This Dofus is not meant for you to hold.\\n\\nProve your merit. Defeat your enemies once again. Bring me the fruits of your efforts. Then perhaps I shall deem you worthy.","content.75.7399":"Have you come{[1*]?:} to bring me the fruits of your efforts?","content.75.7400":"*The dragon rises up to his full height*\\n\\nYou have my trust. Just be sure you don't betray it. If the use of my power brings anyone to harm, I shall personally put an end to it.","content.75.7401":"*Black Ink looks you up and down. He doesn't seem pleased to see you*\\n\\nYou're one of those [#breedName] types. I said no to them... Ah, well. Never mind. You're the{[1*]?:} only{[1*]?:} one who's shown up{[1*]?:}.\\n\\nAnd I've been waiting a month already...","content.75.7402":"Tell me about it! Kids these days are nothing like they used to be. Twelvians always have their noses glued to newspapers.\\n\\nIn my day, we went out, we chatted, all that stuff. All that media has killed communication. Anyway, where was I?","content.75.7403":"I've heard of an island that's never been explored before!\\n\\nSailors have seen a sort of rocky outcrop on the horizon, just a few days' sail from Haven Port.","content.75.7404":"According to the few sailors who've gotten close, the island has a lush jungle, rivers running through it, and wild, hostile creatures. With some kind of...\\n\\nUm... I mean, they're all just rumors. There's no danger, so don't worry! I'm sure it's uninhabited!","content.75.7405":"So, coming or not?","content.75.7406":"I had heard that Hoodfella had been attacked over an emblem for some reason, but I didn't expect the perpetrators to show up in person.","content.75.7407":"Mainly, I have a powerful network. And I know how to cover my behind.\\n\\nIf you want information, let me go.","content.75.7408":"*Remington seems perplexed. He stares at each of you in turn, his confidence gradually waning*\\n\\nYou... Are you serious?","content.75.7409":"*Remington waits a few seconds before replying*\\n\\nIf that's what you want, fine. But first, give me your word. Both of you.\\n\\n*You and the Old Amnesiac exchange a glance, then a nod*","content.75.7410":"T... Tell me exactly what you want to know.","content.75.7411":"*The Rogue squints curiously* \\n\\nHis name is Aligias. I had never seen him before in real life. Let's just say he's got one hell of a reputation.","content.75.7412":"He's got different activities he's into... Various kinds of smuggling operations. He keeps a low profile, as long as no one gets in his way. ","content.75.7413":"And if they do get in his way?","content.75.7414":"*sweating nervously*\\n\\nI... I've heard his favorite hobbies are kidnapping and torture. A lot of people have disappeared in the past few months and... I mean... It could be connected, right? That's just what I've heard, is all! Maybe it's all made up! ","content.75.7415":"And the smuggling operations?","content.75.7416":"He... He likes older items... high-value antiquities.","content.75.7417":"A little bit... I think I was one of his victims... but by some unknown miracle, I managed to escape. I have vague memories of mutilated people screaming in pain, with someone laughing maniacally nearby... presumably him. I'm sure of it now. There were other people with me, and those people are in danger! ","content.75.7418":"We know his appearance and his name, but that doesn't tell us where to look. ","content.75.7419":"If you want information, let me go with the book.","content.75.7420":"*Remington waits a few seconds before replying*\\n\\nIf that's what you want, fine. But first, give me your word. Both of you.\\n\\n*You and the Old Amnesiac exchange a glance, then a nod*","content.75.7421":"He... He likes older items, high-value antiquities.","content.75.7422":"And... What about my book?","content.75.7424":"Aaaar!!! Ahoy there, sailor! Is ye on the hunt for treasure 'mong the shipwrecks too? I be the one that gives the orders 'round 'ere. 'Tis me the only one who knows where it be, squit... squit... squit...","content.75.7425":"Aaaar!!! What be ye blabberin' about, sailor?! This here island been inhabited fer a long time...","content.75.7426":"By Bonnie lying over the ocean! Ye must have gotten the wrong{[1*]?:} island.","content.75.7427":"*The captain's face becomes serious*\\n\\nThis here island 'tis but a memory doomed to disappear soon. But as long as ye be rememberin' your adventures here, this here island will never truly disappear... And besides, maybe a new island will appear on the 'orizon soon.","content.75.7428":"Squirrrrt... Even on me way 'ere from Ereboria, I spotted a new island!","content.75.7429":"I sent a few sailors to take a look, but they never returned. But I made a little drawing anyway, so I could find it again one day. There be a mountain there, sailor! A jungle too!","content.75.7430":"I hid it somewhere on this here island.","content.75.7431":"Ahaha! Finally, here we are on a completely new island!","content.75.7432":"*Black Ink seems annoyed*\\n\\nYou're right. I left a container near the boat. We'll need to collect resources to repair the bridge. But with all these pirates everywhere, I'd say it's only a matter of time before the bridge is destroyed again.","content.76.20":"Thanks, I'll make sure I learn it all!","content.76.32":"Pick the flowers.","content.76.33":"Harvest the fruit.","content.76.34":"Harvest the seeds.","content.76.35":"What is this? I don't even-","content.76.36":"No, the fields are much more fertile.","content.76.37":"Of course, the earth is welcoming.","content.76.38":"Yes, but rocky land is best of all.","content.76.39":"I don't even... What is this?","content.76.40":"Turn them into various types of flour.","content.76.41":"Turn them into Bowmeow-pops.","content.76.42":"Turn them into juice.","content.76.43":"What is this? I don't even-","content.76.44":"Here we go! Erm... I mean, thank you, sir!","content.76.48":"...","content.76.62":"Cuttings.","content.76.63":"Wood.","content.76.64":"Planks.","content.76.65":"Nothing, the trees grow back by themselves.","content.76.66":"Prune the cuttings.","content.76.67":"Pick the fruit.","content.76.68":"Pick the berries.","content.76.69":"Drop a log.","content.76.70":"A sawmill.","content.76.71":"A planker.","content.76.72":"An anvil.","content.76.73":"A refiner.","content.76.74":"Handymen.","content.76.75":"Jewelers.","content.76.76":"Boarders.","content.76.77":"No one.","content.76.81":"Thanks, I love your work.","content.76.82":"Nothing right now. Bye.","content.76.90":"No, only in the areas where these creatures are present.","content.76.91":"Yes, to have more control over the ecosystem.","content.76.92":"No, he can only harvest resources and introduce creatures.","content.76.93":"Yes, everything from boots to hats.","content.76.94":"Of course, and he can even combine species.","content.76.95":"Chefs use the meats, and skins go to the unfortunate.","content.76.96":"Chefs use the meats, and leather dealers use the skins.","content.76.97":"Makdo Pull uses the meats, and Lupene Jaguar-Tail uses the skins.","content.76.98":"No one.","content.76.99":"Thanks!","content.76.100":"Thanks. See you later!","content.76.101":"Thanks. See you later!","content.76.111":"Trapper.","content.76.112":"Miner.","content.76.113":"Miller.","content.76.114":"Farmer.","content.76.115":"They're crusty.","content.76.116":"They are the only things to give you back HP.","content.76.117":"You can use them to teleport.","content.76.118":"They make you look younger.","content.76.119":"Any time.","content.76.120":"Only during battles.","content.76.121":"Only when not in battle.","content.76.122":"Public holidays.","content.76.123":"An oven.","content.76.124":"A sloven.","content.76.125":"An anvil.","content.76.126":"A pastrier.","content.76.127":"Thanks!","content.76.157":"Thanks. See you later.","content.76.162":"I'm feeling a bit lost...","content.76.163":"You're a Clan Member, aren't you? I'd like to know more about your territory.","content.76.164":"Nothing, thanks.","content.76.166":"No thank you, sir. Mine fit me like a glove.","content.76.173":"Of course, even in water.","content.76.174":"In any type of grass.","content.76.175":"In a good quality pan.","content.76.176":"No, only in certain special soils.","content.76.180":"Nothing right now. Bye.","content.76.181":"Thanks, I'll go and learn the basics. See you later.","content.76.188":"Ores.","content.76.189":"Ores and precious stones.","content.76.190":"Mines.","content.76.191":"Dust.","content.76.192":"...","content.76.193":"Salt.","content.76.194":"Iron tablets.","content.76.195":"Gold-fish.","content.76.196":"None.","content.76.197":"...","content.76.198":"Blacksmith.","content.76.199":"Weapons master and kama minter.","content.76.200":"Handyman.","content.76.201":"Jeweler.","content.76.202":"...","content.76.203":"Thank you! The mines are all mine!","content.76.231":"Cool, thanks!","content.76.232":"...","content.76.233":"A distillery to turn them into juice.","content.76.234":"A flowermill to turn them into bread.","content.76.235":"A mortar to grind them into powder.","content.76.236":"A needle and thread, to turn them into a necklace.","content.76.237":"...","content.76.238":"Cut the stems and leaves and harvest the seeds.","content.76.239":"Cut the roots and harvest the bulbs.","content.76.240":"Trim stray hairs and admire your handiwork in its blade.","content.76.241":"Pick the petals and harvest love.","content.76.248":"Seeds of doubt.","content.76.249":"Wild plants and flowers.","content.76.250":"Various herbs.","content.76.251":"Better buds than the ones he has.","content.76.255":"Really sorry, I thought you were someone else. See you soon.","content.76.258":"Thanks. See you later.","content.76.259":"Thanks!","content.76.260":"...","content.76.261":"Handymen.","content.76.262":"Chefs.","content.76.263":"Boarders.","content.76.264":"Fishmongers.","content.76.265":"...","content.76.266":"Yes.","content.76.267":"No, he might get a fish, an item, or nothing at all.","content.76.268":"Yes, but he has to confront the fish.","content.76.269":"Yes, but he has to pay part of his catches to the territory's Clan Member.","content.76.270":"...","content.76.271":"On shoals of fish, in freshwater only.","content.76.272":"On shoals of fish, in freshwater or seawater.","content.76.273":"On shields belonging to adventurers only.","content.76.274":"On shawls belonging to old women only.","content.76.283":"I don't want to disturb you. Goodbye.","content.76.286":"I'll read it and come back. Thanks!","content.76.287":"One of those hooks that lets you fish for another fish.","content.76.288":"A bit of meat attached to the end of the line to attract rare fish.","content.76.289":"A harpoon.","content.76.290":"One of his fingers.","content.76.291":"...","content.76.292":"For their beauty tips.","content.76.293":"Because the resources they harvest are useful for nearly all the crafting professions.","content.76.294":"Because they know Fertilizator the Magnificent's address.","content.76.295":"Because they're good gardeners.","content.76.296":"...","content.76.326":"I give up, it's the smart choice.","content.76.327":"You won't be seeing me behind bars anytime soon. Goodbye!","content.76.328":"Okay.","content.76.329":"1 kama? I've got nothing on me, Poopy.","content.76.333":"Come on, two of Enutrof's disciples should be able to come to some arrangement...","content.76.335":"Excellent! Thanks, Pappy!","content.76.336":"Cool! I'm on it...","content.76.338":"Ahh! You should have said so earlier! Thank you.","content.76.339":"Uh...","content.76.340":"Oh yeah, right. Just a little misunderstanding on my part, heh heh.","content.76.341":"I'll remember! See you soon, you old Snoofle.","content.76.342":"Ooooh... Okay.","content.76.345":"But... But... That's incredible! How did you know?","content.76.346":"Uh... No thanks, violence is for Trools.","content.76.350":"Uhh... Actually, I didn't want anything...","content.76.353":"I would like to learn more about the ecosystem.","content.76.360":"Thanks for sharing your wisdom. I'm going to learn all the secret techniques.","content.76.361":"Not yet. I'll be back soon.","content.76.368":"No, only in the areas where these creatures are present.","content.76.369":"Yes, to have more control over the ecosystem.","content.76.370":"That depends on Osamodas' mood.","content.76.371":"No, he can only harvest resources and introduce creatures.","content.76.372":"Yes, everything from boots to hats.","content.76.373":"Of course, and he can even combine species.","content.76.374":"Chefs use the meats, and skins go to the unfortunate.","content.76.375":"Chefs use the meats, and leather dealers use the skins.","content.76.376":"Makdo Pull uses the meats, and Lupene Jaguar-Tail uses the skins.","content.76.377":"No one.","content.76.378":"Cool! But, uh... Would you cut it out with the stupid nicknames?","content.76.379":"Thanks, I'll read it right away.","content.76.381":"Okay, I'll pay more attention this time.","content.76.382":"Yeah, totally... Your brother Mimi is a bit odd, isn't he?","content.76.383":"Yeah, totally... Your brother's a bit... odd, isn't he?","content.76.384":"What have you got in this basket, then? Cheese?","content.76.385":"I want to become a great warrior!","content.76.386":"I would like to learn the secrets of the ecosystem.","content.76.391":"I guess it's worth a try...","content.76.393":"In that case... \"Charge!\"","content.76.394":"Seeds?","content.76.396":"But, after a while, wouldn't there be too many Wodents?","content.76.397":"Will do, thank you.","content.76.398":"Crozolilies?","content.76.400":"But, if you eat all the Wodents, soon there won't be any left!","content.76.401":"Thanks for the advice.","content.76.403":"What a lovely story.","content.76.404":"Appetizing...","content.76.405":"Thanks.","content.76.406":"Thanks.","content.76.408":"Waaaoow! Thanks for everything, Master Kano. Goodbye!","content.76.411":"Yeah! And, as all the young people say these days... Here it is!","content.76.412":"Uh... What do I have to do with the ore again?","content.76.413":"Um... I think I'm missing some ingredients...","content.76.414":"Aha! my precious kama, think again!","content.76.415":"Yeah! Or else... two of Enutrof's disciples should be able to come to some kind of arrangement...","content.76.424":"Don't worry about it. It happens to me all the time.","content.76.425":"Let's stop talking about that.","content.76.426":"Really? Well, if you insist. Thanks!","content.76.428":"Thanks, I hope I'll find what I'm looking for.","content.76.433":"Apart from your territory, what else is worth seeing in the region?","content.76.434":"Another thing...","content.76.435":"See you soon.","content.76.436":"What else do I need to know about the great Amakna?","content.76.437":"That sounds tempting.","content.76.439":"Another thing...","content.76.440":"See you soon.","content.76.446":"Sokay, I'd like to go down.","content.76.447":"Oh, did you build this bridge, then?","content.76.448":"2 kamas okay with you?","content.76.449":"Will you let me pass for 20 kamas?","content.76.450":"If you want my gold, you'll have to take it from my cold, dead hands!","content.76.451":"I'm going to turn back, I don't want to distract you from your bridge any longer.","content.76.452":"Get your dirty hands o...","content.76.453":"But but but...","content.76.454":"But... I hardly have anything!","content.76.455":"You're welcome, you dirty lout.","content.76.456":"Come and get it, then, you foul brute!","content.76.457":"En garde!","content.76.459":"Hello, I...","content.76.463":"How about 2 kamas?","content.76.464":"Of course, but...","content.76.466":"Uh, thanks... Wait, be careful?","content.76.469":"Thank you for the information. Goodbye.","content.76.470":"I won't put up a fight this time. Here's 40 kamas.","content.76.471":"Unfortunately, I don't have enough on me.","content.76.472":"You still haven't learned your lesson, have you? I'm 